              "wiki_body": "thumb #1714807 thumb #1616698 thumb #48860 thumb #1003866 thumb #1263881 \r\n\r\n[b]Cetaceans[/b] are any member of the infraorder Cetacea, aquatic [[mammal|mammals]] which are mostly [[marine]].  This infraorder includes two extant parvorders - [[toothed_whale|odontoceti]] and [[baleen_whale|mysteceti]] - which share a common ancestor by means of an extinct parvorder, [[archaeoceti]].  Cetacea as an infraorder is related most to the [[hippopotamid|hippopotamuses]] and fall under the order Artiodactyla accordingly, having diverged from even-toed ungulates 53 to 45 million years ago.  Members of this infraorder vary in shape and size, from small porpoises to great blue whales.  A summary of their taxonomy is listed below.\r\n\r\nh4. Taxonomy:\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[cetacean]]\r\n*** [[baleen_whale]]\r\n**** [[fin_whale]]\r\n**** [[gray_whale]]\r\n**** [[humpback_whale]]\r\n**** [[minke_whale]]\r\n**** [[right_whale]]\r\n**** [[sei_whale]]\r\n**** [[bryde's_whale]]\r\n**** [[bowhead_whale]]\r\n**** [[blue_whale]]\r\n*** [[toothed_whale]]\r\n**** [[beaked_whale]]\r\n***** [[bottlenose_whale]]\r\n**** [[well-nosed_dolphin]]\r\n**** [[physeteroid]]\r\n***** [[sperm_whale]]\r\n**** [[delphinoid]]\r\n***** [[oceanic_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[striped_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[pilot_whale]]\r\n****** [[hourglass_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[commerson's_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[bottlenose_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[dusky_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[humpback_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[hector's_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[atlantic_spotted_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[orca]]\r\n****** [[common_dolphin]]\r\n******* [[short-beaked_common_dolphin]]\r\n******* [[long-beaked_common_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[white-sided_dolphin]]\r\n******* [[pacific_white-sided_dolphin]]\r\n******* [[atlantic_white-sided_dolphin]]\r\n***** [[monodontid]]\r\n****** [[beluga]]\r\n****** [[narwhal]]\r\n***** [[river_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[amazon_river_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[baiji]] - Chinese river dolphin\r\n****** [[la_plata_dolphin]]\r\n****** [[south_asian_river_dolphin]]\r\n***** [[porpoise]]\r\n****** [[harbour_porpoise]]\r\n*** [[archaeoceti]]\r\n**** [[ambulocetid]]\r\n***** [[ambulocetus]]\r\n**** [[protocetid]]\r\n***** [[maiacetus]]\r\n**** [[pakicetid]]\r\n***** [[pakicetus]]\r\n**** [[basilosaurid]]\r\n***** [[basilosaurus]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related:\r\n* [[werecetacean]]\r\n** [[wereorca]]\r\n* [[cetacean_taur]]\r\n** [[orca_taur]]\r\n* [[cetacean_humanoid]]\r\n** [[orca_humanoid]]\r\n\r\nh4. More information:\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cetacea\r\n\r\nh4. Other rankings\r\n\r\n* [b][[tag group:species]][/b]\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[afrosoricid]] - Golden mole and tenrec.\r\n** [[bovid]] - Buffalo, cattle, yak, etc.\r\n** [[camelid]] - Alpaca, camel, llama, etc.\r\n** [[canid]] - Dog, fox, wolf, etc.\r\n** [[caprine]] - Goat, ibex, sheep, etc.\r\n** [[cervid]] - Elk, moose, reindeer, etc.\r\n** cetacean - Dolphin, porpoise, whale, etc.\r\n** [[equine]] - Donkey, horse, zebra, etc.\r\n** [[eulipotyphlan]] - Hedgehog, mole, shrew, etc.\r\n** [[euplerid]] - Fanaloka, fossa, vontsira, etc.\r\n** [[felid]] - Cat, lion, tiger, etc.\r\n** [[giraffid]] - Giraffe, okapi, etc.\r\n** [[herpestid]] - Mongoose\r\n** [[hyaenid]] - Hyenas\r\n** [[lagomorph]] - Rabbit, hare, pika, etc.\r\n** [[marsupial]] - Kangaroo, koala, opossum, etc.\r\n** [[mephitid]] - Skunks and stink badgers.\r\n** [[monotreme]] - Echidna and platypus\r\n** [[mustelid]] - Ferret, otter, weasel, etc.\r\n** [[pinniped]] - Sea lion, seal, walrus, etc.\r\n** [[primate]] - Ape, lemur, monkey, etc. (excludes [[human]])\r\n** [[proboscidean]] - Elephant, mammoth, mastodon, etc.\r\n** [[procyonid]] - Kinkajou, raccoon, ring-tailed cat, etc.\r\n** [[suina]] - Boar, pig, warthog, etc.\r\n** [[rodent]] - Mouse, rat, squirrel, etc.\r\n** [[ursid]] - Grizzly bear, panda, polar bear, etc.\r\n** [[viverrid]] - Civet, genet, linsang, etc.\r\n** [[xenarthran]] - Anteater, armadillo, and sloth."
            }
