                  "wiki_body": "[i]Hirundinids[/i], members of [i]Hirundinidae[/i], are a family of birds that include the [[swallow_(bird)|swallows]] and the martins.\r\n\r\nHighly adapted to aerial feeding, they have a very distinctive appearance, possessing an evolutionarily conservative body shape that is slender and streamlined with long, pointed [[wings]]. These were to adapt to hunting [[insect|insects]] in [[flying|flight]], allowing maneuverability and frequent gliding as well as general efficient flight. Typical [i]Hirundinids[/i] possess short and wide [[beak|beaks]], containing strong jaws and a wide gape, as well as relatively long eyes. They also tend to have long, [[forked tail|deeply forked]] [[tail feathers]], often utilized in maneuvering and possibly sexual display.\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* [[martin_(bird)]]\r\n* [[swallow_(bird)]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[avian]]\r\n** [[bird]]\r\n*** hirundinid"
                }
