                "wiki_body": "[b]Cardinals[/b] are New World [[passerine]] birds belonging to the family [i]Cardinalidae[/i]. Cardinals are most commonly recognized by their crimson plumage, but blue, yellow, and black species also exist. They are also known as cardinal-grosbeaks and cardinal-buntings. True cardinals belong to the genus [i]Cardinalis[/i], which includes three bird species all native to North America. \r\n\r\nh4. Species Overlap\r\n\r\nNot all cardinals belong to the family [i]Cardinalidae[/i]. Certain South American species belong to the Tanager family [i][[tanager|Thraupidae]][/i] including the genus [i]Paroaria[/i] which contains the [[cardinal-tanager|cardinal-tanagers]] and the yellow cardinal ([i]Gubernatrix cristata[/i]). Other members that were once part of Thraupidae, and still carry the tanager common name have since moved to [i]Cardinalidae[/i].\r\n\r\nh4. Genera, and species\r\n\r\n* Amaurospiza (genus) - Seedeaters\r\n** [[blackish-blue_seedeater]] ([i]A. moesta[/i])\r\n** [[blue_seedeater]] ([i]A. concolor[/i])\r\n** [[carrizal_seedeater]] ([i]A. carrizalensis[/i])\r\n* Cardinalis (genus) - True cardinals\r\n** [[desert_cardinal]]\r\n** [[northern_cardinal]]\r\n** [[vermilion_cardinal]]\r\n* Caryothraustes (genus) - Grosbeaks\r\n* Chlorothraupis (genus) - Related to ant tanagers, formerly part of the family [i]Thraupidae[/i].\r\n* Cyanocompsa (genus) - Buntings and grosbeaks\r\n** [[blue_bunting]] ([i]C. parellina[/i])\r\n* Cyanoloxia (genus)\r\n** [[glaucous-blue grosbeak]] ([i]C. glaucocaerulea[/i]) - Also known as the [b]indigo grosbeak[/b].\r\n* Granatellus (genus) - Chats, formerly included in the family [i]Parulidae[/i].\r\n** [[red-breasted_chat]] ([i]G. venustus[/i])\r\n** [[gray-throated_chat]] ([i]G. sallaei[/i])\r\n** [[rose-breasted_chat]] ([i]G. pelzelni[/i])\r\n* [[ant_tanager|habia]] (genus) - Ant tanagers, formerly part of the family [i]Thraupidae[/i]. \r\n* [[passerina]] (genus) - Buntings (includes one species of grosb