                  "wiki_body": "Thumb #275452\r\n\r\nThe [b]eagle[/b] is any of several large, soaring birds of prey belonging to the hawk family [I][[accipitrid|Accipitridae]][/I], noted for their size, strength, and powers of flight and vision: formerly common in America, the widespread use of pesticides (DDT in particular), environmental pollution, and hunting left eagles mostly confined to Alaska and a few isolated populations.  Conservation measures have seen eagle populations rebounding for decades; one such species, the [[bald eagle]], was removed from the U.S. federal government's list of endangered species in July of 1995.\r\n\r\nh5. Species\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=True eagles and relatives]\r\n* [[Aquilinae]]\r\n** [[true_eagle|Aquila]] (genus) - True eagles\r\n*** [[african_hawk-eagle]] (A. spilogaster)\r\n*** [[bonelli's_eagle]] (A. fasciata)\r\n*** [[cassin's_hawk-eagle]] (A. africana)\r\n*** [[eastern_imperial_eagle]] (A. heliaca)\r\n*** [[golden_eagle]] (A. chrysaetos)\r\n*** [[gurney's_eagle]] (A. gurneyi)\r\n*** [[spanish_imperial_eagle]] (A. adalberti)\r\n*** [[steppe_eagle]] (A. nipalensis)\r\n*** [[tawny_eagle]] (A. rapax)\r\n*** [[verreaux's_eagle]] (A. verreauxii)\r\n*** [[wedge-tailed_eagle]] (A. audax)\r\n** Hieraaetus (genus)\r\n*** [[ayres's_hawk-eagle]] (H. ayresii) - Also known as [b]Ayres' eagle[/b].\r\n*** [[booted_eagle]] (H. pennatus)\r\n*** [[little_eagle]] (H. morphnoides)\r\n*** [[pygmy_eagle]] (H. weiskei)\r\n*** [[wahlberg's_eagle]] (H. wahlbergi)\r\n** Nisaetus (genus, Incomplete) - Old World hawk-eagles\r\n** Spizaetus (genus, Incomplete) - New World hawk-eagles\r\n** [[spotted_eagle]] (Clanga)\r\n*** [[greater_spotted_eagle]] (C. clanga)\r\n*** [[indian_spotted_eagle]] (C. hastata)\r\n*** [[lesser_spotted_eagle]] (C. pomarina)\r\n** Other\r\n*** [[black_eagle]] (Ictinaetus malaiensis)\r\n*** [[crowned_eagle]] (Stephanoaetus coronatus)\r\n*** [[long-crested_eagle]] (Lophaetus occipitalis)\r\n*** [[martial_eagle]] (Polemaetus b