                "wiki_body": "[b]Accipiter[/b] is a genus of birds of prey in the subfamily Accipitrinae. All species in this genus are known as [[true_hawk|true hawks]]. Most species are known as [[goshawk|goshawks]] or [[sparrowhawk|sparrowhawks]].\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* [[bicolored_hawk]] (Accipiter bicolor)\r\n* [[chilean_hawk]] (Accipiter chilensis)\r\n* [[cooper's_hawk]] (Accipiter cooperii) - Also known as big blue darter, chicken hawk, flying cross, hen hawk, quail hawk, striker, and swift hawk.\r\n* [[goshawk]]\r\n** [[african_goshawk]] (Accipiter tachiro)\r\n** [[black-mantled_goshawk]] (Accipiter melanochlamys)\r\n** [[brown_goshawk]] (Accipiter fasciatus)\r\n** [[crested_goshawk]] (Accipiter trivirgatus)\r\n** [[fiji_goshawk]] (Accipiter rufitorques)\r\n** [[grey-bellied_hawk]] (Accipiter poliogaster) - Also known as the grey-bellied goshawk.\r\n** [[grey_goshawk]] (Accipiter novaehollandiae) - There is a white bodied variant known as white goshawk.\r\n** [[grey-headed_goshawk]] (Accipiter poliocephalus)\r\n** [[henst's_goshawk]] (Accipiter henstii)\r\n** [[imitator_goshawk]] (Accipiter imitator) - Also known as imitator sparrowhawk.\r\n** [[meyer's_goshawk]] (Accipiter meyerianus)\r\n** [[moluccan_goshawk]] (Accipiter henicogrammus) - Also known as Halmaheran goshawk.\r\n** [[new_britain_goshawk]] (Accipiter princeps)\r\n** [[northern_goshawk]] (Accipiter gentilis)\r\n** [[pied_goshawk]] (Accipiter albogularis)\r\n** [[red-chested_goshawk]] (Accipiter toussenelii)\r\n** [[shikra]] (Accipiter badius) - Also known as the little banded goshawk.\r\n** [[slaty-mantled_goshawk]] (Accipiter luteoschistaceus)\r\n** [[sulawesi_goshawk]] (Accipiter griseiceps)\r\n** [[variable_goshawk]] (Accipiter hiogaster)\r\n** [[white-bellied_goshawk]] (Accipiter haplochrous) - Also known as the New Caledonia goshawk or New Caledonia sparrowhawk.\r\n* [[gundlach's_hawk]] (Accipiter gundlachi)\r\n* [[semicollared_hawk]] (Accipiter collaris) - Considered the sister species of the tiny hawk.\r\n* [[sharp-shinned_hawk]] (Accipiter striatus)\r\n** [[plain-breasted_hawk]] (Accipiter ventralis)\r\n** [[rufous-thighed_hawk]] (Accipiter erythronemius)\r\n** [[white-breasted_hawk]] (Accipiter chionogaster)\r\n* [[sparrowhawk]]\r\n** [[besra]] (Accipiter virgatus) - Also known as the besra sparrowhawk.\r\n** [[black_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter melanoleucus) - Also known as the black goshawk or great sparrowhawk.\r\n** [[chestnut-flanked_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter castanilius)\r\n** [[chinese_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter soloensis) - Also known as the Chinese goshawk, and grey frog hawk.\r\n** [[collared_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter cirrocephalus)\r\n** [[dwarf_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter nanus) - Also known as the small sparrowhawk.\r\n** [[eurasian_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter nisus) - Also known as the northern sparrowhawk.\r\n** [[frances's_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter francesiae)\r\n** [[japanese_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter gularis)\r\n** [[levant_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter brevipes)\r\n** [[little_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter minullus)\r\n** [[madagascan_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter madagascariensis)\r\n** [[new_britain_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter brachyurus)\r\n** [[nicobar_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter butleri)\r\n** [[ovambo_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter ovampensis) - Also known as Ovampo sparrowhawk, or Hilgert's sparrowhawk.\r\n** [[red-thighed_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter erythropus) - Also known as the red-legged sparrowhawk or the western little sparrowhawk.\r\n** [[rufous-breasted_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter rufiventris) - Also known as the rufous-chested sparrowhawk and as the red-breasted sparrowhawk.\r\n** [[rufous-necked_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter erythrauchen)\r\n** [[spot-tailed_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter trinotatus) - Also known as spot-tailed goshawk.\r\n** [[vinous-breasted_sparrowhawk]] (Accipiter rhodogaster)\r\n* [[tiny_hawk]] (Accipiter superciliosus)\r\n\r\nh4. External links\r\n\r\n* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accipiter\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[avian]]\r\n** [[bird