              "wiki_preview": "An [b]alcid[/b], also known as an [b]auk[/b], is a member of the [i]Alcidae[/i] family of [[bird|bir...",
              "wiki_body": "An [b]alcid[/b], also known as an [b]auk[/b], is a member of the [i]Alcidae[/i] family of [[bird|birds]].\r\n\r\nAuks are superficially similar to [[penguins]], tending to have black-and-white color schemes, upright postures, and some of their general habits. Nevertheless, they are not closely related, and are believed to be an example of convergent evolution. All currently living auks are notable for their ability to [[swimming|\"fly\" under water]] as well as in the air. Although they are excellent swimmers and divers, their walking appears clumsy. \r\n\r\nAlthough not to the extent of penguins, auks have largely sacrificed flight, and also mobility on land, in exchange for swimming ability; their [[wings]] are a compromise between the best possible design for diving and the bare minimum needed for flying.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[penguin]]\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* [[auklet]]\r\n* [[great auk]]\r\n* [[guillemot]]\r\n* [[little auk]]\r\n* [[murrelet]]\r\n* [[puffin]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[avian]]\r\n** [[bird]]\r\n*** alcid"
            }
