            "wiki_body": "thumb #840318 thumb #665341 thumb #3201853\nThe [b]Avali[/b] are an avian species that superficially resembling a cross between a large rabbit and a velociraptor, Avali stand bipedally, with digitigrade poise. They are covered from head to toe in feathers of varying length, possess two large wings with rudimentary digits at the wrist/hand enabling them to manipulate objects dexterously, while also possessing 4 long, rabbit-like ears. They prefer to gather and work together in packs.\n\nThe Avali can be identified with these traits: oval shaped heads; [[big_eyes|large eyes]]; [[4_ears|four ears]]; [[3_fingers|three fingers]], [[3_toes|tri-pronged talons]]; large [[feathered_wings|wing]] feathers [[winged_arms|connected to their arms]]; and long cartilage whip like tail. They are canonically typically between 60cm (2 feet) and 120cm (3 feet, 11 inches) tall.\n\nThe Avali were created by [[Cutesune]] (previously under the name RyuujinZERO): <http://community.playstarbound.com/members/ryuujinzero.40227/>.\n\nMore can be read about the Avali on the official \"Avali Wiki\":[https://avali.fandom.com/wiki/The_Official_Avali_Wiki]. A not-yet-canon rewrite of the lore can be found at <https://avali.wikidot.com>. A non-canon but extremely comprehensive PDF by [[toddavali|Todd]] can be found hosted at <https://avali.nexus>. An archive of the original lore that is no longer canon can be found at <https://avali.weebly.com>.\n\nNote: There are some avali-like species that are not avali: [[Teshari]], [[Resomi]], and [[Sur'ri]]. When tagging, note the existence of these."
