            "wiki_body": "thumb #1882960 thumb #1737031 thumb #1797079 thumb #1628378\n\n[b]Ambient birds[/b] are small subtle [[bird|birds]] found off in the distance in an image. Removing an ambient bird would do little to change the feel of an image. They're mostly just there to make the world feel a little more alive. If the main character is interacting with or touching the bird in question, it's probably not an ambient bird.\n\nh4. General guidelines\n\n* Ambient creatures [b][u]do not[/u][/b] count as characters.\n* Do not use ambient creature tags to describe ambient animal sounds. Use [[animal_noises]] [[ambient_noises]] for sounds and ambient creature tags for visible creatures.\n* Not all flying creatures are [[bird|birds]], or even avians for that matter. [[Bat|Bats]] are mammals. Flying [[dragon|dragons]] such as [[wyvern|wyverns]] aren't birds. \n** Use the [[ambient_flier]] tag to generally describe any ambient creature that is flying, including ambient birds.\n* Unless a non-ambient bird is also depicted, [[bird]] [color=red]SHOULD NOT[/color] be tagged.\n\nh4. Species\n\n* [[ambient_duck]]\n* [[ambient_owl]]\n* [[ambient_penguin]]\n* [[ambient_pigeon]] - This should probably exist.\n* [[ambient_seagull]] - This should probably exist.\n\nh4. Related tags\n\n* [[ambient_silhouette]] - For ambient creatures with almost no details apart from their shape.\n* [[detailed_ambient_creature]] - For ambient creatures that are more detailed than a silhouette (contain more colors, body textures, etc).  \n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[ambient_arthropod]]\n** [[ambient_arachnid]]\n*** [[ambient_spider]]\n** [[ambient_insect]]\n*** [[ambient_ant]]\n*** [[ambient_bee]]\n*** [[ambient_beetle]]\n*** [[ambient_butterfly]]\n*** [[ambient_dragonfly]]\n*** [[ambient_firefly]]\n*** [[ambient_fly]]\n*** [[ambient_ladybug]]\n*** [[ambient_moth]]\n** [[ambient_myriapod]]\n* [[ambient_bat]]\n* [b]ambient_bird[/b]\n** [[ambient_owl]]\n* [[ambient_fairy]]\n* [[ambient_human]]\n* [[ambie