            "wiki_body": "[i]Trogonids[/i], members of [i]Trogonidae[/i], are a family of [[bird|birds]].\r\n\r\n[i]Trogons[/i] have soft, often colourful, [[feathers]] with distinctive and heavy [[sexual dimorphism]] between [[male]] and [[female]] [i]Trogonids[/i]. They are the only animal with a heterodactyl toe arrangement, which is similar to [[zygodactyl]] but with the inner toe reversed. [i]Trogons[/i] are fairly uniform in appearance, having compact bodies and [[long tail|long tails]], especially quetzals, and short necks. Their legs and feet are weak and short, and they are essentially unable to walk beyond a very occasional shuffle, being incapable of even turning around on a branch without using their wings. They nest in holes dug into [[tree|trees]] or [[termite]] mounds.\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* [[quetzal]]\r\n** [[resplendant_quetzal]]\r\n* [[trogon]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[avian]]\r\n** [[bird]]\r\n*** trogonid"
