            "wiki_body": "The [b]shoebill[/b], also known as [b]whalehead[/b], is a very large [[stork]]-like [[bird]].\r\n\r\n\r\nIts signature feature, as well as its namesake, is its huge, bulbous [[beak|bill]], which is [[yellow beak|a pale yellow]] or [[tan beak|a light tan]] often with erratic [[grey markings|greyish markings]]. Its bill is the third longest bill among living birds after [[pelican|pelicans]] and large storks, and can best pelicans in bill circumference. Their [[bird feet|dark coloured legs]] are fairly [[long legs|long]], and their feet are exceptionally large, likely assisting the species to stand on aquatic vegetation while hunting. The [[feathers|plumage]] of adults tends to be blue-grey with darker grey flight feathers. Juveniles have similar colors, but are darker grey with a small amounts of brown.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[avian]]\r\n** [[bird]]\r\n*** shoebill"
