            "wiki_body": "[b]Kiwis[/b] are flightless [[bird|birds]], about the size of a chicken, native to [[New Zealand]] (and the origin of the term \"kiwi\" for New Zealanders). They possess a long [[beak]] and large three-toed feet, and their feathers appear to be fur at first glance. While they do have wings, they are very small and invisible underneath their feathers.\r\n\r\nKiwis are [[ratite|ratites]], and thus related to [[ostrich|ostriches]], [[emu|emus]], and [[cassowary|cassowaries]].\r\n\r\nNot to be confused with the little brown hairy [[kiwifruit]]."
