                "wiki_body": "[b]Domestic sheep[/b], otherwise known as [i]Ovis aries[/i] though casually are referred to as just \"[b]sheep[/b]\", are [[quadruped|quadrupedal]] [[caprine|caprines]]. Although the term \"sheep\" applies to many species in the genus [i][[sheep|Ovis]][/i], casual usage of said term is used to almost always refer to domesticated sheep. Domesticated sheep are also the largest species of sheep.\r\n\r\nDomesticated sheep more than likely descended from from the [[mouflon]], a Eurasian species of [[wild sheep]], and are one of the earliest animals [[human|humans]] domesticated for its use in agriculture. They are raised for several resources, mainly for their [[wool|fleece]], [[meat]], and [[milk]], with sheep wool being the most widely used animal fiber.\r\n\r\nDomesticated sheep play a key role in various facets of human cultures, often appearing in and being represented within language, symbology, and various culture's [[mythology|mythologies]]. Domestic sheep are often utilized in both ancient and modern animal sacrifices.\r\n\r\nh4. Breeds\r\n\r\n* [[barbados_blackbelly]]\r\n* [[bluefaced_leicester]]\r\n* [[border_leicester]]\r\n* [[cheviot_sheep]]\r\n* [[clun_forest_sheep]]\r\n* [[corriedale]]\r\n* [[dorset_down]]\r\n* [[greyface_dartmoor]]\r\n* [[hampshire_down]]\r\n* [[herdwick]]\r\n* [[hill_radnor]]\r\n* [[icelandic_sheep]]\r\n* [[jacob_sheep]]\r\n* [[kerry_hill_sheep]]\r\n* [[lincoln_sheep]]\r\n* [[merino_sheep]]\r\n* [[navajo-churro]]\r\n* [[oxford_down]]\r\n* [[rough_fell]]\r\n* [[scottish_blackface]]\r\n* [[shropshire_sheep]]\r\n* [[southdown_sheep]]\r\n* [[valais_blacknose]]\r\n* [[welsh_mountain_sheep]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[caprine]]\r\n*** [[goat]]\r\n**** [[domestic_goat]]\r\n*** [[sheep]]\r\n**** domestic_sheep"
