                        "wiki_preview": "thumb #2775679 thumb #1148155 thumb #783354\r\n\r\nA [b]herding dog[/b], also known as a shepherd dog or...",
                        "wiki_body": "thumb #2775679 thumb #1148155 thumb #783354\r\n\r\nA [b]herding dog[/b], also known as a shepherd dog or working dog, is a type of dog that was bred for herding and has a variety of breeds all made for the same purpose. The best way to describe what they look like would be to show you so if you are unaware of what a herding dog looks like [ \"[b]Click here[/b]\":https://www.google.com/search?q=herding+dog&client=opera&hs=Rph&source=lnms&tbm=isch&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjo_drx37TrAhUsw1kKHdLBB2YQ_AUoAXoECA4QAw&biw=1474&bih=794 ]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Other info]\r\nh3. Herding Dogs\r\n A list of herding dogs\r\n[section=Herding Dogs]\r\n1. Australian Cattle Dog\r\n2. Australian Shepherd\r\n3. Bearded Collie\r\n4. Beauceron\r\n5. Belgian Malinois\r\n6. Belgian Sheepdog\r\n7. Belgian Tervuren\r\n8. Bergamasco\r\n9. Berger Blacnc Sussie\r\n10. Berger Picard\r\n11. Border Collie\r\n12. Bouvier Des Flandres\r\n13. Briard\r\n14. Canaan Dog\r\n15. Cardigan Welsh Corgi\r\n16. Finnish Lapphund\r\n17. German Shepherd\r\n18. Icelandic Sheepdog\r\n19. Norwegian Buhund\r\n20. Old English Sheepdog\r\n21. Pembroke Welsh Corgi\r\n22. Polish Lowland Sheepdog\r\n23. Puli\r\n24. Pyrenean Shepherd\r\n25. Shetland Sheepdog\r\n26. Swedish Vallhund\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh3. Related Tags \r\nA detailed section about the related tags \r\n[section=Related]\r\n** [[bearded_collie|Beared Collie]] - The Beardie is a medium-size dog with a rectangular body and a shaggy coat that can be black, blue, brown or fawn, with or without white markings. A Beardie's eyes are the same tone as his coat color, so black and brown dogs have brown eyes while blue dogs have grayish-blue eyes.\r\n\r\nthumb #2374552\r\n\r\n** [[berger_blanc_suisse|Berger Blanc Sussie]] - The skull and muzzle of the dog are equal in length, parallel to one another and join at a moderate stop. The coat is slightly longer and heavier at the neck, especially in males. Thecolor of the coat is white 99.98% of the time, with dark pigmentation on the nose, eye rims, nails, etc.\r\n\r\n\r\n** [[berger_picard|Berger Picard]] - The Berger Picard is a medium-sized, well-muscled dog, slightly longer than tall with a tousled yet elegant appearance. Their ears are naturally erect, high-set and quite wide at the base. Their eyebrows are thick, but do not shield their dark frank eyes. They are known for their smile. Their natural tail normally reaches to the hock and is carried with a slight J-curve at the tip. Their coat colors fall into two colors, fawn and brindle with a range of shade variations\r\n\r\n** [[beauceron|Beauceron]] - The beauceron is a large breed of dog with a coat that is short but also thick with a dense undercoat.\r\n\r\nthumb #1929174\r\n\r\n** [[bergamasco_shepherd|Bergamasco Shepherd]] - The Bergamasco's characteristic feature is its unique coat, made up of three types of hair. The coat forms flocks (strands of hair weaved together creating flat layers of felted hair) or loose mats, which cover the dog's body and legs.\r\n\r\n** [[german_shepherd|German Shepherd]] - German Shepherds are strong, agile, well-muscled dogs that are longer than they are tall. They have a loping stride that easily covers ground to satisfy working demands. They have a long muzzle, square head and erect, pointed ears. Their back and hind legs are slightly angled and they have long, bushy tails.\r\n\r\nthumb #893096\r\n\r\n** [[welsh_corgi|Welsh Corgi]] - They are double-coated with a thick undercoat and longer topcoat. Their coat can be red, sable, black, or fawn colored with white markings.\r\n\r\nthumb #1999842\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n* Meta-generalizations : \"shephard_dog\":https://e621.net/wiki_pages/show_or_new?title=shephard_dog [ misspelling of shepherd dog ]  \"shepard_dog\":https://e621.net/wiki_pages/show_or_new?title=shepard_dog [ misspelling of shepherd dog ] \"shepherd_dog\":https://e621.net/wiki_pages/show_or_new?title=shepherd_dog & \"pastroal_dog\":https://e621.net/wiki_pages/show_or_new?title=pastoral_dog\r\n\r\n"
