                        "wiki_preview": "The [b]Saluki[/b] is a standardised breed of dog, developed from sighthounds – dogs that hunt primar...",
                        "wiki_body": "The [b]Saluki[/b] is a standardised breed of dog, developed from sighthounds – dogs that hunt primarily by sight rather than scent – used by nomadic tribes to run down game animals. It is closely related to the [[Afghan Hound]], and is deep-chested, and long-legged, but with much shorter fur than the Afghan Hound.\r\n\r\nThe Saluki has incredible running speed. While the [[Greyhound]] is credited as being the fastest dog for up to 800 meters, the Saluki and [[Whippet]] are thought to be faster for longer distances. Its heavily padded feet allow for remarkable stamina as they are able to better absorb impact on its body.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[afghan hound]]\r\n* [[canine]]\r\n* [[dog]]"
