                    "wiki_body": "[b]Poodles[/b] are a group of formal [[domestic_dog]] breeds, the Standard Poodle, Miniature Poodle and Toy Poodle (the three are listed in decreasing order of size). The origin of the breed is still discussed, with a prominent dispute over whether the poodle descends from Germany as a type of water dog, or from the French Barbet.\r\n\r\nPoodles are the national dog of France, and are ranked as the second most intelligent breed behind only the [[border_collie|border collie]]. They are well known for their [[curly_hair|curly fur]]. Although they were once primarily hunting dogs, they are popular as show dogs nowadays."
