                    "wiki_body": "The pit bull has become a collective name for the dog breeds of the [[american_pit_bull_terrier|American Pit Bull Terrier]], the [[american_staffordshire_terrier| American Staffordshire Terrier]], and the [[american_bully|American Bully]]. Between these, they share traits of having very short fur, a mid-sized frame, a muscular body, a ridge down the top of the head, shrivels on the forehead, a boxy snout, short to medium flews, round eyes with visible irises, and ears being either half pricked, rose eared, button eared, or cropped.\n\nIt is sometimes confused with [[bull_terrier|Bull Terriers]], [[cane_corso|Cane Corsos]], [[dogo_argentino|Dogo Argentinos]], [[english_bulldog|English Bulldogs]], and [[boxer_(dog)|Boxers]], so remember to tag accordingly."
