                    "wiki_body": "The [b]Tamaskan Dog[/b] is a breed of [[domestic dog]] originating from Finland but curated in the UK, that has been selectively bred to resemble a [[wolf]] or [[wolfdog]], while having the better temperament of a domestic dog. Although their exact origins are uncertain, these mixbreed dogs were primarily arctic breed crosses of [[Alaskan Husky]], [[Alaskan Malamute]], [[Canadian Eskimo Dog]], [[German Shepherd]], Labrador Husky, and [[Siberian Husky]].\r\n\r\nThe Tamaskan Dog is primarily used as a [[nordic_sled_dog|sled dog]], being smaller than the Alaskan Malamute, but larger than many other typical sled dogs. They are described as having the temperament of a good family dog and being accepting of other dogs. Breeding lines are closely controlled and as such, there are fairly few health problems in the breed."
