                    "wiki_body": "thumb #2413130 thumb #3460691 thumb #14621 thumb #3381\r\n\r\n\"[b]Wolf[/b]\" ([i]Canis lupus[/i]) refers to the grey/gray wolf (also known as the timber wolf) and its many subspecies.  The gray wolf is the largest wild member of the Canidae family with a range across the northern hemisphere. Wolves share a common ancestry with the [[domestic_dog|domestic dog]] ([i]Canis lupus familiaris[/i]) but for the sake of tagging both dogs and wolves will be treated as distinct members of the Canidae family. \r\n\r\nSome extant subspecies, such as the [[red_wolf]] ([i]C. l. rufus[/i]), the eastern wolf ([i]C. l. lycaon[/i]) are currently debated for taxonomic placement, proposed as the species [i]C. rufus[/i] and [i]C. lycaon[/i], respectively.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, some extinct subspecies such as the Florida black wolf ([i]C. l. floridanus[/i]) and Mississippi Valley wolf ([i]C. l. gregoryi[/i]) are currently proposed and debated as a subspecies of the red wolf, [i]C. rufus[/i].\r\n\r\nThe domestic dog ([i]C. l. familiaris[/i]) is currently proposed and debated as belonging to its own species, [i]C. familiaris[/i].\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[canine]]\r\n*** [[canis]]\r\n**** [b]wolf[/b]\r\n***** [[eurasian_wolf]]\r\n***** [[arabian_wolf]]\r\n***** [[iberian_wolf]]\r\n***** [[mexican_wolf]]\r\n***** [[japanese_wolf]]\r\n***** [[alaskan_tundra_wolf]]\r\n***** [[italian_wolf]]\r\n***** [[tundra_wolf]]\r\n***** [[arctic_wolf]]\r\n***** [[eastern_wolf]][sup]1[/sup]\r\n***** [[red_wolf]][sup]2[/sup]\r\n***** [[mississippi_valley_wolf]][sup]3[/sup]\r\n***** [[florida_black_wolf]][sup]4[/sup]\r\n**** [[jackal]]\r\n***** [[golden_jackal]]\r\n***** no longer classified as [i]Canis[/i]; now [i]Lupulella[/i]:\r\n****** [[side-striped_jackal]]\r\n****** [[black-backed_jackal]]\r\n**** [[african_golden_wolf]]\r\n***** [[egyptian_wolf]]\r\n**** [[coyote]]\r\n**** [[dire_wolf]]\r\n**** [[ethiopian_wolf]]\r\n\r\n[sup][sup]1[/sup]Proposed as the species [i]Canis lycaon[/i] but currently debated.[/sup]\r\n[sup][sup]2[/sup]Proposed as the species [i]Canis rufus[/i] but currently debated.[/sup]\r\n[sup][sup]3[/sup]Proposed as the species [i]C. r. gregoryi[/i] but currently debated.[/sup]\r\n[sup][sup]4[/sup]Proposed as the species [i]C. r. floridanus[/i] but currently debated.[/sup]\r\n\r\nSimilar species:\r\n\r\n* [i]Canis[/i]:\r\n** [[dire_wolf]]\r\n** [[ethiopian_wolf]]\r\n** [[african_golden_wolf]]\r\n*** [[egyptian_wolf]]\r\n\r\n* [i]Chrysocyon[/i]:\r\n** [[maned_wolf]]\r\n\r\n[b]More information:[/b]\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolf\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subspecies_of_Canis_lupus"
                  }
