                    "wiki_body": "thumb #2408032 thumb #2145204 thumb #2660513\r\n\r\nThis is an informal group for three [[canid]] species colloquially called jackals: the [[black-backed_jackal]], the [[side-striped_jackal]] of sub-Saharan Africa and the [[golden_jackal]] of Eurasia.  Of these, only the black-backed jackal and side-striped jackal are closely related, with the golden jackal more related to the wolf, coyote, and ethiopian wolf.\r\n\r\nFor the sake of convenience, the [[anubian_jackal]] is also implicated to this informal group.\r\n\r\nh4. Species:\r\n* [[black-backed_jackal]] ([i]Lupulella mesomelas[/i])\r\n* [[side-striped_jackal]] ([i]Lupulella adustus[/i])\r\n* [[golden_jackal]] ([i]Canis aureus[/i])\r\n\r\nh4. Fictional:\r\n* [[anubian_jackal]]\r\n\r\nh4. More information:\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jackal"
