                  "wiki_body": "thumb #1433473thumb #3353351thumb #2219613\r\n\r\nThe coyote, also known as the American jackal or the prairie wolf, is a species of [[canine]] found throughout North and Central America.\r\n\r\nThey have large [[prick ears]] and a [[fluffy tail]] [[dipstick_tail|tipped]] with black. They have [[countershade_fur|countershaded fur]] in shades of [[tan_fur|tan]] and [[grey_fur|grey]] in a pattern similar to [[wolf|wolves]].\r\n\r\nCoyotes are often associated with American [[desert]] settings as well as [[American mythology]].\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Associated Tags]\r\nh6. Anatomy\r\n* [[canine_genitalia]]\r\n** [[canine_penis]]\r\n*** [[knot]]\r\n** [[canine_pussy]]\r\n* [[snout]]\r\n* [[prick_ears]]\r\n* [[fur]]\r\n* [[digitigrade]]\r\n* [[paws]]\r\n* [[pawpads]]\r\n* [[tail]]\r\n** [[fluffy_tail]]\r\n\r\nh6. Color and Markings\r\n* [[tan_fur]]\r\n* [[grey_fur]]\r\n* [[countershade_fur]]\r\n* [[dipstick_tail]]\r\n* [[black_tipped_tail]]\r\n\r\nh6. Other\r\n* [[american_mythology]]\r\n* [[desert]]\r\n* [[western]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Implication Tree\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[canid]]\r\n*** [[canine]]\r\n**** [[canis]]\r\n***** [[coyote]]"
