                    "wiki_body": "[color=species][b][i]Vulpes[/i][/b][/color] is a genus of the sub-family Caninae. The members of this genus are colloquially referred to as [b]true [[fox|foxes]][/b], meaning they form a proper clade. This is opposed to the \"false foxes\" of [i]Lycalopex[/i], known as \"[[South American fox|South American foxes]]\" or \"zorros\". \r\n\r\nNot counting subspecies or coat variations, there are twelve members of the genus, [i]Vulpes vulpes[/i] being the type species when the genus was defined by Carl Linnaeus in 1758.\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Species]\r\n* [[Bengal fox]] - [i]Vulpes bengalensis[/i] (George Kearsley Shaw, 1800)\r\n* [[Blanford's fox]] - [i]Vulpes cana[/i] (William Thomas Blanford, 1877)\r\n* [[Cape fox]] - [i]Vulpes chama[/i] (Andrew Smith, 1833)\r\n* [[corsac fox]] - [i]Vulpes corsac[/i] (Calrl Linnaeus, 1768)\r\n* [[Tibetan sand fox]] - [i]Vulpes ferrilata[/i] (Brian Houghton Hodgson, 1842)\r\n* [[Arctic fox]] - [i]Vulpes lagopus[/i] (Carl Linnaeus, 1758)\r\n* [[kit fox]] - [i]Vulpes macrotis[/i] (Clinton Hart Merriam, 1888)\r\n* [[pale fox]] - [i]Vulpes pallida[/i] (Philipp Jakob Cretzschmar, 1827)\r\n* [[Ruppell's fox|Rüppell's fox]] - [i]Vulpes reuppellii[/i] (Heinrich Rudolf Schinz, 1825)\r\n* [[swift fox]] - [i]Vulpes velox[/i] (Thomas Say, 1823)\r\n* [[red fox]] - [i]Vulpes vulpes[/i] (Carl Linnaeus, 1758)\r\n** [[Arabian red fox]] - [i]Vulpes vulpes[/i] (Michael R. Oldfield Thomas, 1902)\r\n** [[Ezo red fox]] - [i]Vulpes vulpes schrencki[/i] (Kyukichi Kishida, 1924)\r\n** [[Japanese red fox]] - [i]Vulpes vulpes japonica[/i] (John Edward Grey, 1869)\r\n* [[fennec fox]] - [i]Vulpes zerda[/i] (Eberhart A.W. von Zimmermann, 1780)\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n"
