                    "wiki_preview": "The [b]arctic fox[/b] ([i]Vulpes lagopus[/i]) is a species of [[fox]] common in Arctic regions.  The...",
                    "wiki_body": "The [b]arctic fox[/b] ([i]Vulpes lagopus[/i]) is a species of [[fox]] common in Arctic regions.  They are distinguished from other foxes by their small ears and size. White morph arctic foxes have a coat that changes from white in winter to brown in summer, while blue morph arctic foxes maintain a dark coloration all year.  They are classified as Least Concern on the IUCN Red List of Threatened Species.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. For more information:\r\n* \"Arctic Fox (Wikipedia)\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic_fox"
