                "wiki_preview": "The [b]maned wolf[/b] ([i]Chrysocyon brachyurus[/i]) is the largest [[canid]] of South America. Its ...",
                "wiki_body": "The [b]maned wolf[/b] ([i]Chrysocyon brachyurus[/i]) is the largest [[canid]] of South America. Its markings resemble those of foxes, but it is neither a [[fox]] nor a [[wolf]]. It is the only species in the genus [i]Chrysocyon[/i] (meaning \"golden dog\").\r\n\r\nIt is omnivorous, and though it specializes in preying on small and medium-sized animals, including small mammals (typically [[rodent|rodents]] and [[rabbit|rabbits]]), [[bird|birds]], and even [[fish]], a large portion of its diet is vegetable matter. It particularly favors the \"wolf apple\", a tomato-like fruit named for the maned wolf's preference of the fruit.\r\n\r\nManed wolves are ecologically flexible and are even able to survive in human-disturbed areas. Unlike other large canids such as the grey wolf, [[African wild dog]], or [[dhole]], the maned wolf does not form packs.\r\n\r\nThey are a species threatened by habitat loss and being run over by automobiles. Feral and [[domestic_dog|domestic dogs]] pass on diseases to them, and have been known to attack them.\r\n"
              }
