            "wiki_body": "The [b]dire wolf[/b] ([i]Aenocyon dirus[/i]) is an extinct species of prehistoric canine and was an avid competitor against the also extinct [[saber-toothed cat|saber-toothed tiger]]. Despite the name, it was not a wolf.\n\nIn 2024 [[Colossal Biosciences]], the same company behind the [[woolly mouse]], claimed to \"de-extinct\" the dire wolf. Through minor genetic modification of [[grey_wolf]] DNA, \"three cubs with supposed dire wolf traits\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romulus,_Remus,_and_Khaleesi were born. Despite the claims, they are genetically grey wolves, and are not an actual reemergence of the extinct Aenocyon genus.\n\nh4. External links\n* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dire_wolf\nh4. See also\n* [[canine]]\n** [b]dire wolf[/b] ([i]Aenocyon dirus[/i])\n** [[canis]]\n*** [[coyote]]\n*** [[jackal]]\n*** [[wolf]] ([i]Canis lupus[/i])"
