            "wiki_body": "A species created by [[Discreet_user]]. They resemble glowing foxes, and are a type of Kyri, which are beings made of light.\r\n\r\nFyre foxes mostly live in their home planet. Very few if any actually leave their planet to go to others. Their home planet is tidal locked (eternal sunset) allowing them to constantly be charged with light, which is how they get their glow. They all live in communal temples, adults travel out to procreate in nature, because they all live together there's so much shedding that you need a broom to keep it clean. They're able to use light to cook food or heat buildings. It is possible for one to become drained somehow, even when drained they still glow at least a little bit. Their young also glow, but just barely, think of a young dalmatian not getting it's spots yet.\r\n\r\nThe most well-known member of this species is [[mylar_(discreet_user)|Mylar Bezier]]."
