              "wiki_body": "thumb #1353658 thumb #1506786 thumb #788118 thumb #692964\r\n\r\n[b]Cervids[/b]: hooved ruminants of the [i]Cervidae[/i] (deer) family and the even-toed ungulates (artiodactyla), known for their [[antlers]] (or [[tusks]], in some species).  Cervids come in many shapes and sizes and are widespread through most of the world with three known subfamilies: Capreolinae (new-world deer), Cervinae (old-world deer), and Hydropotinae (water deer).\r\n\r\nh4. Subfamilies, genera, and species\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[cervid|cervidae]]\r\n*** [[cervine|cervinae]]\r\n**** rusa\r\n***** [[javan_rusa_deer]]\r\n***** [[sri_lankan_sambar]]\r\n***** [[visayan_spotted_deer]]\r\n**** cervus\r\n***** [[sika_deer]]\r\n***** [[elk]]\r\n***** [[red_deer]]\r\n***** [[kashmir_stag]]\r\n***** [[thorold's_deer]]\r\n**** panolia\r\n***** [[eld's_deer]]\r\n**** rucervus\r\n***** [[schomburgk's_deer]]\r\n***** [[barasingha]]\r\n****** [[southern_swamp_deer]] ([i]R. d. branderi[/i])\r\n****** [[eastern_swamp_deer]] ([i]R. d. ranjitsinhi[/i])\r\n****** [[western_swamp_deer]] ([i]R. d. duvauceli[/i])\r\n**** axis\r\n***** [[chital]]\r\n**** dama\r\n***** [[fallow_deer]]\r\n**** elaphurus\r\n***** [[père_david's_deer]]\r\n**** hyelaphus\r\n***** [[hog_deer]]\r\n**** [[megaloceros]]\r\n***** [[irish_elk]]\r\n**** [[muntjac|muntiacus]]\r\n***** [[indian_muntjac]]\r\n***** [[giant_muntjac]]\r\n**** [[tufted_deer]]\r\n*** [[capreoline|capreolinae]]\r\n**** rangifer\r\n***** [[reindeer]]\r\n**** blastocerus\r\n***** [[marsh_deer]]\r\n**** hippocamelus\r\n***** [[taruca]]\r\n***** [[south_andean_deer]]\r\n**** [[roe_deer|capreolus]]\r\n***** [[eastern_roe_deer]]\r\n***** [[western_roe_deer]]\r\n**** [[pudú]]\r\n***** [[southern_pudú]]\r\n***** [[northern_pudú]]\r\n**** odocoileus\r\n***** [[mule_deer]]\r\n***** [[white-tailed_deer]]\r\n****** [[key_deer]] ([i]O. v. clavium[/i])\r\n**** alces\r\n***** [[moose]]\r\n**** [[brocket_deer|mazama]]\r\n***** [[dwarf_brocket]]\r\n*****