                "wiki_preview": "A [b]pony[/b] is a member of any breed of [[horse|horses]] ([i]Equus ferus caballo[/i]) that are sma...",
                "wiki_body": "A [b]pony[/b] is a member of any breed of [[horse|horses]] ([i]Equus ferus caballo[/i]) that are small in size as adults.  Most ponies tend toward stockiness, with shorter than average legs, wider bodies, and heavier [[bone]] structure, although there are exceptions.  They often have thicker manes, tails, and coats than other horses.  Not all small horses are necessarily ponies; the smallest breed of horse, the miniature horse, is generally not categorized as a pony.\n\nThey should not be confused with other [[equine]] species as defined by the e621 Wiki.  Ponies are differentiated from [[unicorn|unicorns]] by the lack of a [[horn]] and from [[pegasus|pegasi]] by the lack of [[wings]].\n\nIn My Little Pony: Friendship is magic, they are referred to as [[earth_pony|Earth ponies]].\n\nFor the series, see [[my_little_pony|My Little Pony]].\n\nh4. Breeds:\n* [[equine|equinae]]\n** equus (genus)\n*** [[horse|(domestic) horse]] (E. f. caballus)\n**** pony\n***** [[shetland_pony]]\n\nh3. For more information:\n\n* \"Pony (Wikipedia)\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pony"
