            "wiki_body": "Gorillas constitute the eponymous genus Gorilla, the largest extant genus of [[primate]]'s by size. They are ground-dwelling, predominantly herbivorous [[ape]]'s that inhabit the forests of central Africa. The DNA of gorillas is highly similar to that of a [[human]], from 95–99% depending on what is counted, and they are the next closest living relatives to humans after the [[bonobo]] and common [[chimpanzee]].\r\n\r\n"
