                    "wiki_body": "thumb #2043602\r\n\r\n[b]Calico cats[/b] are domestic cats with a [[piebald|piebald coat]]; in other words, they show off a coat of [[white fur]] with patches of two other colors.  Outside of North America, the pattern is more usually called tortoiseshell-and-white.  Calicos are almost exclusively female except in a rare few genetic variations.\r\n\r\nThe line between calico and [[tortoiseshell_cat|tortoiseshell]] is blurry, but is generally accepted that calicos have over 50% white spotting and \"patchier\" patterns rather than \"brindled\".\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[feline]]\r\n*** [[domestic_cat]]\r\n**** [b]calico_cat[/b]\r\n\r\nh4.More Information\r\n\"Calico Cat (Wikipedia)\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calico_cat"
