                  "wiki_body": "thumb #636642 thumb #1775317\r\n\r\nThe wildcat is a \"species complex\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Species_complex involving the [[European wildcat]] [i](F. sylvestris)[/i] and the [[African wildcat]] [i](F. lybica)[/i].  The European wildcat resides in forests of Europe and the Caucasus and has long fur, a bushy tail, and is generally dark in color.  The African wildcat instead inhabits the semi-arid landscapes and steppes of Africa, Arabia, and western and central Asia.  Contrary to the European wildcat, the African wildcat is sandy grey in color with short fur and a tapering tail.\r\n\r\nThough other species common names involve the wildcat term, they are not part of the species complex and should not receive the tag.\r\n\r\nh4. Taxonomy:\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[felid]]\r\n*** [[feline]]\r\n****  [[felis]]\r\n***** [[wildcat]] (species complex)\r\n****** [[african_wildcat]] [i](F. lybica)[/i]\r\n****** [[european_wildcat]] [i](F. sylvestris)[/i]\r\n\r\nh4. More information:\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wildcat"
