                "wiki_preview": "thumb #1374655 thumb #2337027 thumb #1382020 thumb #1300227\n\nA type of feline that is best known for...",
                "wiki_body": "thumb #1374655 thumb #2337027 thumb #1382020 thumb #1300227\n\nA type of feline that is best known for its swift speed.  Despite its size, the cheetah is not actually a 'big cat,' or member of the pantherinae subfamily.  Their closest living relatives are the [[cougar]] and [[jaguarundi]].  It's thought that the Cheetah evolved in North America millions of years ago.\n\nThese felines are generally slender with a [[yellow fur|yellow]], [[orange fur|orange]], or [[tan fur|tan]] coat and [[black spots|black]] or [[brown spots]]. \n\nThese spots are small simple spots, except on [[king cheetah|king cheetahs]], where the [[spots]] are larger and less tidy.  Cheetahs generally have a rather distinctive marking:  a black line running from the inner corner of the eye down and around the sides of the muzzle, called a 'tear mark.'\n\n[[King Cheetah|King Cheetahs]] are one distinct color mutation that cheetahs exhibit.  [[Melanistic]] and [[albino]] animals have also been reported.  Most unusually, some rare spotless cheetahs have been seen, exhibiting only a small splatter of brown fur and tiny spots along the lower back.  This cheetah is called a white cheetah, or a tabby/ticked cheetah, referring to the genetics that resulted in this pattern.\n\nCheetahs are carnivores.\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[mammal]]\n** [[feline]]\n*** [b]cheetah[/b]\n**** [[king_cheetah]]"
