            "canada_lynx": [
              {
                "tag": "canada_lynx",
                "kor": "",
                "count": 661,
                "wiki_preview": "thumb #1756966 thumb #1214819 thumb #1093306\r\n\r\n* [[Mammal]] > [[Felid]] > [[Feline]] > [[Lynx]] > [...",
                "wiki_body": "thumb #1756966 thumb #1214819 thumb #1093306\r\n\r\n* [[Mammal]] > [[Felid]] > [[Feline]] > [[Lynx]] > [[Canada_Lynx]]\r\n\r\nh4. About...\r\n\r\nA species of lynx native to North America, largely found in, and around, the Rocky Mountains.\r\n\r\nIt is a medium sized cat, that typically has a silvery brown coat of fur, with [[white_countershading]]. They usually have [[cheek_tuft]]s, distinct [[ear_tuft]]s and particularly large paws. It's winter coat of [[grey_fur]] is very long and fluffy, and generally lacks a distinct pattern.  However, in summer, it's shorter coat usually becomes [[brown_fur]] that sometimes allows [[spots]] to be visible. It has a [[short_tail]] that usually has a black tip. Interestingly, the hind legs are usually longer than the forelegs.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with...\r\n\r\nThere are several other animals in the lynx genus that all bear a similarity to the Canada Lynx.  They are the [[Eurasian_lynx]], the [[Iberian_lynx]] and the [[Bobcat]].  The [[caracal]] also shares the lynx's tufted ears.\r\n\r\nh4. Species:\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[feline]]\r\n*** [[lynx]]\r\n**** [[eurasian_lynx]]\r\n**** [[iberian_lynx]]\r\n**** canada_lynx\r\n**** [[bobcat]]\r\n\r\nh4. More information:\r\n* \"Canada Lynx on Wikipedia\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canada_lynx"
              }
            ],
            "eurasian_lynx": [
              {
                "tag": "eurasian_lynx",
