                "count": 423,
                "wiki_preview": "thumb #721008 thumb #4516113 thumb #1105800 thumb #4956840\n\nThe [b]Eurasian Lynx (Lynx Lynx) [/b]is ...",
                "wiki_body": "thumb #721008 thumb #4516113 thumb #1105800 thumb #4956840\n\nThe [b]Eurasian Lynx (Lynx Lynx) [/b]is the largest of the four extant species in the medium-sized [[felid]] genus [[Lynx]].\n\nIt inhabits the north of Eurasia, its range extending as far south as Iran and Iraq. Eurasian Lynxes fare well at high altitude, inhabiting elevations up to 5500m (18000ft). Eurasian Lynxes are opportunistic hunters, though they prefer large ungulates. \n\nThe Eurasian Lynx has a [[spotted fur|spotted]] reddish-brown to golden fur in with [[white fur|white coloration]] on its neck, chin and underparts changing into a thicker [[grey fur|silver-grey fur]] in the winter. Some animals feature brown forehead and back [[markings]]. It has a [[short tail]] with a black tip, black [[ear tuft|ear tufts]], [[inner ear fluff]] and [[cheek tuft|cheek tufts]]. \nh4. Species:\n* [[mammal]]\n** [[feline]]\n*** [[lynx]]\n**** eurasian_lynx\n**** [[iberian_lynx]]\n**** [[canada_lynx]]\n**** [[bobcat]]\nh4. More information:\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eurasian_lynx"
