              "wiki_body": "The [b]domestic goat[/b], often casually referred to as simply [b]goat[/b], is the domesticated member of the [i][[goat|Capra]][/i] genus. There are over 300 distinct breeds of domestic goats; domestic goats are one of the oldest domesticated animals in the world, similar to the [[domestic sheep]]. Over the ages, breeds have been used to cultivate [[milk|milks]], [[meat|meats]], [[wool|fleeces]], and [[pelt|skins]].\r\n\r\nThere are many differing terms for domestic goats depending on things such as age and gender. Female goats are referred to as [i]does[/i] or [i]nannies[/i], intact males are called [i]bucks[/i] or [i]billies[/i], castrated males are known as [i]wethers[/i], and juveniles are coined [i]kids[/i].\r\n\r\nDomesticated goats play a key role in various facets of human cultures, often appearing in and being represented within language, symbology, and various culture's [[mythology|mythologies]].\r\n\r\nh4. Breeds\r\n\r\n* [[alpine_goat]]\r\n* [[angora_goat]]\r\n* [[arapawa_goat]]\r\n* [[barbari_goat]]\r\n* [[boer_goat]]\r\n* [[cashmere_goat]]\r\n** [[changthangi]]\r\n* [[icelandic_goat]]\r\n* [[kamori_goat]]\r\n* [[kiko_goat]]\r\n* [[nigerian_dwarf_goat]]\r\n* [[nubian_goat]]\r\n* [[oberhasli_goat]]\r\n* [[pygmy_goat]]\r\n* [[saanen_goat]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[caprine]]\r\n*** [[goat]]\r\n**** [b]domestic_goat[/b]\r\n*** [[sheep]]\r\n**** [[domestic_sheep]]"
