            "wiki_body": "Apes are Old World anthropoid mammals, more specifically a group of tailless catarrhine primates, belonging to the biological superfamily Hominoidea. The apes are native to Africa and Southeast Asia. Apes are the largest [[primate]]s and the [[orangutan]] is the largest living arboreal animal.\r\n\r\nMembers of the ape family are split into two subgroups:\r\n\r\n* Hylobatidae; consisting of four genera and sixteen species of gibbon, including the lar gibbon and siamang. Commonly referred to as the [i]lesser apes[/i].\r\n\r\n* Hominidae, comprised of [[bonobo]]s, [[chimpanzee]]s, [[orangutan]]s, [[gorilla]]s, and [[human]]s. Commonly referred to as the [i]great apes[/i].\r\n"
