                "wiki_body": "[i]Orthopterids[/i], members of the order [i]Orthoptera[/i], are an order of [[insect|insects]]. Most are easily recognizable by their hind legs, abilities to jump, and the 'songs' they produce.\r\n\r\nOrthopterans have general cylindrical bodies, with elongated hindlegs and musculature adapted for jumping. They have [[mandibles|mandibulate mouthparts]] for biting and chewing and large [[compound eyes]]. They have [[4 wings|two pairs]] of [[wings]], which are held overlapping their long, thin [[abdomen|abdomens]] at rest. They produce sounds, known as \"stridulation\", by rubbing their wings against each other or their legs. These sounds are often used by males to attract mates, but also can be used to deter other males from their territories.\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* [b]orthopterid[/b]\r\n** [[ensiferid]]\r\n*** [[cricket]]\r\n**** [[gryllid]] (True crickets)\r\n***** [[field_cricket]]\r\n****** [[european_field_cricket]]\r\n****** [[fall_field_cricket]]\r\n****** [[jamaican_field_cricket]]\r\n***** [[house_cricket]]\r\n**** Other types\r\n***** [[ant_cricket]]\r\n***** [[weta]]\r\n****** [[camel_cricket]] (Cave crickets)\r\n***** [[dune_cricket]] (Schizodactylidae)\r\n***** [[jerusalem_cricket]]\r\n***** [[katydid]] (Bush crickets, Tettigoniidae)\r\n***** [[mole_cricket]] (Gryllotalpidae)\r\n** [[caeliferid]] - Grasshoppers, locusts, and groundhoppers\r\n*** [[grasshopper]]\r\n**** [[bladder_grasshopper]]\r\n**** [[gaudy_grasshopper]]\r\n**** [[locust]]\r\n*** [[groundhopper]]\r\n*** [[pygmy_mole_cricket]] (Tridactylidae, more closely related to a grasshopper than a cricket)\r\n\r\nh4. General anatomy\r\n\r\n* [[antennae]]\r\n** [[long_antennae]]\r\n* [[arthropod_abdomen]]\r\n* [[compound_eyes]]\r\n* [[exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[long_legs]]\r\n* [[mandibles]]\r\n* [[wings]]\r\n** [[4_wings]]\r\n** [[insect_wings]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[arthropod]]\r\n** [[insect]]\r\n*** [b]orthopterid[/b]"
              }
