              "wiki_body": "Baboons are six extant species of [[old world monkey]] belonging to the genus Papio. They are most closely related to [[mandrill | mandrills]], [[macaque | macaques]] and [[gelada | geladas]], the last of which were for a time also considered a species of baboon. They are some of the largest monkeys in the world, with elongated dog-like muzzles and [[fur]] that is usually brown, tan, or grey. All species of baboon are native to Africa, though the [[hamadryas_baboon]] is also found in the Arabian Peninsula.\r\n\r\nTheir most widely recognizable feature is their [[hairless butt | hairless butts]], which are adapted for comfortable sitting and in which female baboons experience swelling during mating. Their butts are often depicted as brightly colored in art and media.\r\n\r\nh4.Species\r\n* [[hamadryas baboon]]\r\n* [[olive baboon]]\r\n* [[yellow baboon]]\r\n* [[chacma baboon]]\r\n* [[kinda baboon]]\r\n\r\nh4.See Also\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[primate]]\r\n*** [[monkey]]\r\n**** baboon"
