              "wiki_preview": "thumb #1407843 thumb #1358794 thumb #1134175\r\n\r\nThe family otherwise known as the elephant family.  ...",
              "wiki_body": "thumb #1407843 thumb #1358794 thumb #1134175\r\n\r\nThe family otherwise known as the elephant family.  Unlike the term \"[[elephant]]\" which is most commonly used to refer to only extant members of this family, \"elephantid\" is used to refer to any member of the elephantid family, including prehistoric members like the [[mammoth]] and [[stegotetrabelodon]].  It does not refer to other non-elephantid-family [[proboscidean]] members (e.g. [[mastodon]], [[gomphotherium]]), however, so that term (and tag) should be used instead.\r\n\r\nThese animals are mostly known for their hulking size, tough skin, tusks, and trunk.  Only two genera of this family are extant -- [i]Loxodonta[/i] (African elephants) and [i]Elephas[/i] (Asian elephants).  The remaining members are extinct.  A summary of their taxonomy is listed below.\r\n\r\nh4. Subfamilies, genera and species:\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[proboscidean|proboscidea]]\r\n*** [[elephantid|elephantidae]]\r\n**** stegotetrabelodontinae\r\n***** [[stegotetrabelodon]]\r\n**** elephantinae\r\n***** [[mammoth]]\r\n***** [[african_elephant]] (Loxodonta)\r\n****** [[african_bush_elephant]] (L. africana)\r\n****** [[african_forest_elephant]] (L. cyclotis)\r\n***** ([i]Elephas[/i])\r\n****** [[asian_elephant]] (E. maximus)\r\n******* [[indian_elephant]] (E. m. indicus)\r\n\r\nh4. More information:\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephantidae"
            }
