              "wiki_preview": "thumb #245281 thumb #214906 thumb #214894\r\n\r\nThe Anteater, animals of the suborder [i]Vermilingua[/i...",
              "wiki_body": "thumb #245281 thumb #214906 thumb #214894\r\n\r\nThe Anteater, animals of the suborder [i]Vermilingua[/i] (\"worm tongue\") and member of the order [i][[pilosan|Pilosa]][/i] alongside [[sloth|sloths]], are a species of [[mammal]] commonly known for eating [[ant|ants]] and [[termite|termites]].\r\n\r\nThe species s a whole are well known for their elongated, toothless [[snout|snouts]] and long, thin [[tongue|tongues]]. They use their large, curved [[claws|foreclaws]] to tear open ant and termite mounds and for defense, while their dense and long [[fur]] protects them from attacks from the insects. All species (except the [[giant anteater]]) have a long [[prehensile tail]].\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* [[giant_anteater]]\r\n* [[silky_anteater]]\r\n* [[tamandua]]\r\n\r\nh4. General anatomy\r\n\r\n* [[long_claws]]\r\n* [[long_snout]]\r\n* [[long_tongue]]\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with:\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[aardvark]]\r\n** [[marsupial]]\r\n*** [[numbat]] - alternate names \"banded anteater\" and \"marsupial anteater\", though not a true anteater\r\n** [[monotreme]]\r\n*** [[echidna]] - alternate name \"spiny anteater\", though not a true anteater\r\n** [[pangolin]] - alternate name \"scaly anteater\", though not a true anteater\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[pilosan]]\r\n*** anteater"
            }
