              "count": 113,
              "wiki_preview": "thumb #214898 thumb #214908 thumb #288060\r\n\r\nThe tamandua are a species of two [[anteater|anteaters]...",
              "wiki_body": "thumb #214898 thumb #214908 thumb #288060\r\n\r\nThe tamandua are a species of two [[anteater|anteaters]], northern and southern tamandua. They, like others of the species, have elongated muzzles and long, [[prehensile tail|prehensile tails]] they use to aid in their semi-arboreal ([[tree]]) lifestyles in the [i]Central[/i] and [i]Southern Americas[/i].\r\n\r\nTheir [[fur|pelts]] are yellowish-white to tan in color, often with a black banding upon their sides. Though not easy to distinguish, northern tamanduas have black V shapes on their backs and a \"vest\" marking over their torsos, while southern tamanduas tend to be lighter in color and may lack the \"vest\".\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[anteater]]\r\n*** [[giant_anteater]]\r\n*** [[silky_anteater]]\r\n*** tamandua"
