              "wiki_body": "thumb #3049333 thumb #2775679 thumb #2741820 thumb #1948225 thumb #3217562 thumb #393907\nthumb #2598967 thumb #50113 thumb #4536751 thumb #2819907 thumb #3557633\n\nWritten from the \"Mammal Classification\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mammal_classification on Wikipedia\n\n[b]Mammals[/b] are a class of \"vertebrate\":https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vertebrate \"animals\":https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal characterized by the presence of [[fur]] [i](except for certain [[marine]] mammals)[/i], a \"neocortex\":https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neocortex and mammary glands ([[nipples]], [[teats]], [[udders]]...), whose [[female]] representatives feed their juveniles from a specialized cutaneous-glandular secretion called [[milk]] [i](they are then said to nurse)[/i].\n\nh3.Advice for Tagging\nThink about these questions: [i]If this character was in real life...[/i]\n\n* Does it have a skeleton in its body?\n* Would it have nipples/teats/udders? [i](regardless of gender)[/i]\n* Would it be able to feed its young with its nipples/teats/udders if they produced milk? [i](regardless of gender)[/i]\n\n✓ If you can answer \"[b]Yes[/b]\" to [b][u]all[/u][/b] these [b][u]questions[/u][/b]: [b][u]Use[/u] this tag[/b].\n\n✕ If you answer \"[b]No[/b]\" to [b]at least one[/b] question: [b]Do [u]NOT[/u] use this tag[/b].\n[i]It's probably [b]not[/b] a mammal[/i]...\n\nh2.Short List of Mammal Species\n* [[canine|Canines]]: Like [[domestic_dog|dogs]], [[fox|foxes]], [[wolf|wolves]]...\n* [[caprine|Caprines]]: Like [[goat|goats]], [[sheep]]...\n* [[equine|Equines]]: Like [[horse|horses]], [[unicorn|unicorns]], [[zebra|zebras]]...\n* [[feline|Felines]]: Like [[domestic_cat|cats]], [[lion|lions]], [[tiger|tigers]]...\n* [[human|Humans]] [i](Pretty logic... We're all mammals)[/i]\n* [[Lagomorph|Lagomorphs]]: Like [[rabbit|rabbits]], [[hare|hares]], [[pika|pikas]]...\n* [[primate|Primates]]: Like [[chimpanzee|chimpanzees]], [[gorilla|gorillas]], [[monkey|mon