              "wiki_body": "thumb #2924069 thumb #4619962 thumb #2210064 thumb #2081932 thumb #3051185\n[sup]humans depicted in a variety of art styles[/sup]\n\n[b][i]Humans[/i][/b], or Homo Sapiens — a [[bipedal]], sentient [[mammal|mammalian]] species of the [[ape|Great Apes]] family of [[primate|primates]]. On e621, `human` is a species tag, [b][i]and[/i][/b] a [[tag_group:body_types|\"form\"/body type]] tag — meaning that characters that are canonically non-human, but physically indistinguishable from humans, with NO visible non-human features, should be tagged as human.\n\n[quote]\n\nh4. Tagging Notes\n\n* As noted above, canonically non-human characters may be tagged as `human` if they are visually indistinct from humans in any meaningful physical way, this includes:\n** [[android|androids]] with no obviously robotic features (e.g. the androids from [[Dragon Ball Z]])\n** [[alien|aliens]] that are almost entirely human in appearance, regardless of skin colour (e.g. the [[Chiss]] From [[Star Wars]] or the [[Tamaranean]] from [[DC comics]])\n*** Note that such characters may be tagged as `alien` as well as `human`, due to their human form.\n** [[vampire|vampires]] (if lacking vampire features other than [[fangs]]), and [[ghost|ghosts]] of humans should be tagged as human and as their respective supernatural creature\n** human characters that have unnatural skin tones (e.g. human characters from [[Equestria Girls]], [[Kris]] from [[Deltarune]] and [[Frisk]] from [[Undertale]])\n\n* This tag also applies to [[anon]] characters when they are intended to be placeholders for a human, despite often lacking facial features, and unnatural grey or paper-white skin\n* If a character has obviously non-human features, such as antennae, horns, antlers, or [[humanoid pointy ears]], they should be tagged as [[humanoid]], not human\n\n[/quote]\n\nh3. Tags About Humans\n\n[section=\"Meta\" Tags]\n\n* [[human only]] — posts which only depict humans\n* [[human focus]] — posts that are centred on a human character, but feature a humanoid, anthro or feral character\n* [[humanized]] — a character that is typically anthro, feral, or humanoid, is depicted in human form\n* [[faceless human]] — a human character with an obscured or off-screen face\n* [[human pov]] — a [[first person view]] from the perspective of a human\n* [[human edit]] — a post where a previously non-human character has been edited to be human\n\n\n[/section]\n\n[section=Sex/Gender]\n* [[ambiguous human]]\n* [[female human]]\n* [[male human]]\n* [[intersex human]]\n\n[/section]\n[section=Age]\n\nh6. Physical Age\n* [[mature human]] — an older adult human, can be generalized as ages 40-60\n* [[young human]]  — a human that is an infant, child, or adolescent, ages 0-17\n* [[elderly human]] — a human that is [[old|elderly]], generalized as age 60+\n\nh6. Age Differences\n* [[older human]] — a human that is older than another character within the scene\n* [[younger human]] — a human that is younger than another character within the scene\n\n[/section]\n[section=Body Type/Physical Description]\n* [[athletic human]]\n* [[muscular human]]\n* [[slightly chubby human]]\n* [[overweight human]]\n* [[obese human]]\n* [[morbidly obese human]]\n\n* [[larger human]]\n* [[smaller human]]\n[/section]\n\n[section=Interspecies Interactions]\n\nThese tags are typically used to describe [[interspecies|sexual or romantic interactions]] between characters of different forms\n\n* [[human on anthro]]\n* [[human on feral]]\n* [[human on human]]\n* [[human on humanoid]]\n* [[human on taur]]\n\nh6. Sex/Gender\n[sup]Note: the character being described by their gender is usually intended to be of a different form/species[/sup]\n\n* [[ambiguous on human]]\n* [[female on human]]\n* [[intersex on human]]\n* [[male on human]]\n\n\n\n[/section]\n\n[section=Sexual Tags]\n\n[i]Note, this section is incomplete[/i]\n\n* [[human penetrated]]\n* [[human penetrating]]\n** [[human penetrating anthro]]\n** [[human penetra