                  "count": 52570,
                  "wiki_preview": "A [b]hedgehog[/b] is any of the spiny mammals of the subfamily [i]Erinaceinae[/i] and the order [i]E...",
                  "wiki_body": "A [b]hedgehog[/b] is any of the spiny mammals of the subfamily [i]Erinaceinae[/i] and the order [i]Erinaceomorpha[/i]. There are 17 species of hedgehog in five genera, found through parts of Europe, Asia, Africa, and New Zealand. There are no hedgehogs native to Australia, and no living species native to the Americas. Hedgehogs share distant ancestry with shrews (order [i]Soricidae[/i]), with gymnures possibly being the intermediate link, and have changed little over the last 15 million years. Like many of the first mammals they have adapted to a nocturnal, insectivorous way of life.\r\n\r\n[[Sonic the Hedgehog]], from [[Sonic (series)|the popular Sega franchise of the same name]], is indeed, an [[anthro|anthropomorphic]] hedgehog."
