              "wiki_body": "thumb #1645567\r\n\r\n[i]Mephitids[/i], also known as the [i]Mephitidae[/i], are a family of mammals comprising the [[skunk|skunks]] and stink badgers. Skunks were formerly classified as a subfamily of the [i][[mustelid|Mustelidae]][/i] (the [[weasel]] family); however, recent genetic evidence has caused skunks to be treated as a separate family. Similarly, the stink badgers had been classified with [[badger|badgers]], but genetic evidence shows they share a more recent common ancestor with skunks, so they are now included in the skunk family.\r\n\r\n[i]Mephitids[/i] are noted for the great development of their anal scent glands, which they use to deter predators in a variety of ways depending on the species. They can vary in size form and weight, but often have moderately elongated bodies with relatively short, [[muscular thighs|muscled legs]] and long front [[claws]] for digging. They are most commonly covered in black and white [[fur|pelts]], however some skunks are brown or grey and a few are cream-colored. All are [[stripes|striped]], even from birth. They may have a single thick stripe across back and tail, two thinner stripes, or a series of white [[spots]] and broken stripes. Some also have stripes on their legs.\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* mephitid\r\n** [[skunk]]\r\n*** [[hog-nosed_skunk]]\r\n**** [[american_hog-nosed_skunk]]\r\n**** [[humboldt's_hog-nosed_skunk]]\r\n**** [[molina's_hog-nosed_skunk]]\r\n**** [[striped_hog-nosed_skunk]]\r\n*** [[hooded_skunk]]\r\n*** [[spotted_skunk]]\r\n**** [[eastern_spotted_skunk]]\r\n****  [[pygmy_spotted_skunk]]\r\n**** [[southern_spotted_skunk]]\r\n**** [[western_spotted_skunk]]\r\n*** [[striped_skunk]]\r\n** [[stink_badger]]\r\n*** [[palawan_stink_badger]] (pantot)\r\n*** [[sunda_stink_badger]] (teledu)\r\n\r\nh4. General anatomy\r\n\r\n* [[claws]]\r\n* [[countershading]]\r\n** [[reverse_countershading]]\r\n* [[fur]]\r\n* [[long_tail]]\r\n* [[spots]]\r\n* [[stripes]]\r\n* [[skunk_spray]]\r\n\r\nh4. Other rankings\r\n\r\n* [b][[tag group:species]][/b]\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[afrosoricid]] - Golden mole and tenrec.\r\n** [[bovine]] - Buffalo, cattle, yak, etc.\r\n** [[camelid]] - Alpaca, camel, llama, etc.\r\n** [[canine]] - Dog, fox, wolf, etc.\r\n** [[caprine]] - Goat, ibex, sheep, etc.\r\n** [[cervine]] - Elk, moose, reindeer, etc.\r\n** [[cetacean]] - Dolphin, porpoise, whale, etc.\r\n** [[equine]] - Donkey, horse, zebra, etc.\r\n** [[eulipotyphlan]] - Hedgehog, mole, shrew, etc.\r\n** [[euplerid]] - Fanaloka, fossa, vontsira, etc.\r\n** [[feline]] - Cat, lion, tiger, etc.\r\n** [[giraffid]] - Giraffe, okapi, etc.\r\n** [[herpestid]] - Mongoose\r\n** [[lagomorph]] - Rabbit, hare, pika, etc.\r\n** [[marsupial]] - Kangaroo, koala, opossum, etc.\r\n** mephitid - Skunks and stink badgers.\r\n** [[monotreme]] - Echidna and platypus\r\n** [[mustelid]] - Ferret, otter, weasel, etc.\r\n** [[pinniped]] - Sea lion, seal, walrus, etc.\r\n** [[porcine]] - Boar, pig, warthog, etc.\r\n** [[primate]] - Ape, lemur, monkey, etc. (excludes [[human]])\r\n** [[proboscidean]] - Elephant, mammoth, mastodon, etc.\r\n** [[procyonid]] - Kinkajou, raccoon, ring-tailed cat, etc.\r\n** [[rodent]] - Mouse, rat, squirrel, etc.\r\n** [[ursine]] - Grizzly bear, panda, polar bear, etc.\r\n** [[viverrid]] - Civet, genet, linsang, etc.\r\n** [[xenarthran]] - Anteater, armadillo, and sloth."
