                  "wiki_body": "Strepsirrhini or Strepsirhini (/ˌstrɛpsəˈraɪni/; STREP-sə-RY-nee) is a suborder of primates that includes the lemuriform primates, which consist of the lemurs of Madagascar, galagos (\"bushbabies\") and pottos from Africa, and the lorises from India and southeast Asia. Collectively they are referred to as strepsirrhines. Also belonging to the suborder are the extinct adapiform primates which thrived during the Eocene in Europe, North America, and Asia, but disappeared from most of the Northern Hemisphere as the climate cooled. Adapiforms are sometimes referred to as being \"lemur-like,” although the diversity of both lemurs and adapiforms does not support this comparison.\r\nSource: Wikipedia"
