                "wiki_body": "thumb #986871 thumb #301118\r\n\r\nA Kangaroo is a [[marsupial]] from the family Macropodidae. In common use the term is used to describe the largest species from this family, especially those of the genus Macropus, Red Kangaroo, Antilopine Kangaroo, Eastern Grey Kangaroo and Western Grey Kangaroo. Kangaroos and kangaroo characters are commonly associated with [[Australia]], where they are the national animal, and a cultural symbol.\r\n\r\nWhen tagging sex, it's important to note that [[anatomically_correct]] [[male]] kangaroos have an anal vent/[[cloaca]] that doubles as their [[sheath]], so unless there are two separate holes to denote this it would be incorrect to tag [[andromorph]].\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n* [[balancing on tail]]\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[marsupial]]\r\n*** kangaroo"
