                "wiki_body": "thumb #1900455\r\n\r\nAn [b]echidna[/b] is one of four species of [b]monotreme[/b] native to Australia and New Guinea.  All are insect-eaters with long snouts and possess spines on their backs. As monotremes, they lay eggs instead of giving birth to live young.\r\n\r\nThe [[short-beaked_echidna|short-beaked echidna]] or spiney anteater ([i]Tachyglossus aculeatus[/i]) is among the most wide-spread of [[mammal|mammals]] in Australia and shares New Guinea with the three long-beaked species.\r\n\r\nEchidnas derive their name from \"Echidna, the Mother of All Monsters,\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echidna_%28mythology%29 from Greek myth.\r\n\r\n[b]Tagging:[/b] In practice, the majority of \"echidnas\" are characters from the [[sonic (series)]] fandom and bear little resemblance to the actual animal.\r\n\r\nthumb #934619 thumb #930591 thumb #161160\r\n\r\nh4.See also: \r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[monotreme]] \r\n*** echidna \r\n*** [[platypus]]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4.More Information:\r\n\"Echidna (Wikipedia)\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echidna"
