              "wiki_body": "thumb #1246129 thumb #1426262 thumb #1659865 thumb #1659866 thumb #718116\n\n[i]Proboscidea[/i], also known as [i]Proboscideans[/i], are an order [[mammal|mammals]] containing the still living species of [[elephant|elephants]] as well as extinct species such as the [[mammoth]].\n\nAll [i]Proboscideans[/i] are enormous in size, and often have [[tusks]] and long, muscular, prehensile [[trunk|trunks]]. Some species, mainly early [i]Proboscideans[/i], often have less developed trunks and tusks, or rarely even lack them.\n\nh4. Families, genera, and species\n\n* [[mammal]]\n** [[proboscidean]]\n*** amebelodontidae\n**** [[platybelodon]]\n*** gomphotheriidae\n**** [[stegomastodon]]\n*** palaeomastodontidae\n**** [[palaeomastodon]]\n*** deinotheriidae\n**** [[deinotherium]]\n*** mammutidae\n**** [[mastodon]]\n*** gomphotheriidae\n**** [[gomphotherium]]\n*** [[elephantid|elephantidae]]\n**** [[mammoth]]\n**** [[stegotetrabelodon]]\n**** [[african_elephant]]\n***** [[african_bush_elephant]]\n***** [[african_forest_elephant]]\n**** [[asian_elephant]]\n***** [[indian_elephant]]\n\nh4. Related\n\n* [[proboscidean_taur]]\n** [[elephant_taur]]\n* [[proboscidean_humanoid]]\n** [[elephant_humanoid]]\n\nh4. General anatomy\n* [[tail_tuft]]\n* [[trunk]]\n* [[tusks]]\n\nh4. More information\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proboscidea\n\nh4. Other rankings\n\n* [b][[tag group:species]][/b]\n* [[mammal]]\n** [[afrosoricid]] - Golden mole and tenrec.\n** [[bovine]] - Buffalo, cattle, yak, etc.\n** [[camelid]] - Alpaca, camel, llama, etc.\n** [[canine]] - Dog, fox, wolf, etc.\n** [[caprine]] - Goat, ibex, sheep, etc.\n** [[cervine]] - Elk, moose, reindeer, etc.\n** [[cetacean]] - Dolphin, porpoise, whale, etc.\n** [[equine]] - Donkey, horse, zebra, etc.\n** [[eulipotyphlan]] - Hedgehog, mole, shrew, etc.\n** [[euplerid]] - Fanaloka, fossa, vontsira, etc.\n** [[feline]] - Cat, lion, tiger, etc.\n** [[giraffid]] - Giraffe, okapi, etc.\n** [[herpestid]] - Mongoos