                "wiki_body": "thumb #223602 thumb #101767 thumb #100856 thumb #49564\r\n\r\nDasyuromorphia, an order of carnivorous Australian [[marsupial|marsupials]].  This order includes the [[quoll]], the [[numbat]], and the well-known [[tasmanian_devil]] and extinct [[thylacine]].  There are four families in this order, though two are extinct.  Of the extant families, the [[numbat]] family (Myrmecobiidae) contains only a single member while the Dasyuridae family contains about 70.  Families, genera, and species are listed below.\r\n\r\nh4. Families, genera, and species:\r\n* [[marsupial]]\r\n** [[dasyuromorph|dasyuromorphia]] (order)\r\n*** myrmecobiidae\r\n**** [[numbat]]\r\n*** dasyuridae\r\n**** [[tasmanian_devil]]\r\n**** [[quoll]]\r\n***** [[tiger_quoll]]\r\n*** thylacinidae\r\n**** [[thylacine]]\r\n\r\nh4. More information:\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dasyuromorphia"
