                "wiki_preview": "thumb #576026 thumb #1235108 thumb #751507\r\n\r\n[b]Viverridae[/b] is a family of small to medium-sized...",
                "wiki_body": "thumb #576026 thumb #1235108 thumb #751507\r\n\r\n[b]Viverridae[/b] is a family of small to medium-sized mammals, the [i]viverrids[/i]. They are [i]Feliforms[/i], a suborder of mammals that are either [[feline]] or feline-like, comprising of animals like [[herpestid|herpestids]] and [[hyena]]. Viverrid's fit into the latter category, as while they are not felines they are very feline-like, and in fact are the most primitive of feliforms.\r\n\r\nMost species have relatively small heads with short, erect ears, a relatively long, pointed [[snout|muzzle]], and tufts of [[whiskers|facial vibrissae]] between the lower jaw bones. Most species have [[stripes]], [[spots]], or bands on their bodies, and their tails are often [[ringtail|ringed]] with contrasting colors. Most have glands near their [[anus|anuses]] that produce a strong-smelling musk; in some species the odor is sufficiently potent to ward off predators. The secretion from these glands often is used as a perfume base and medicine. Male viverrids also have a [[baculum]], or [[bone]], within their [[penis|penises]].\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* [[binturong]]\r\n* [[civet]]\r\n** [[african_civet]]\r\n** [[malay_civet]]\r\n** [[palm_civet]]\r\n*** [[asian_palm_civet]]\r\n*** [[masked_palm_civet]]\r\n* [[genet]]\r\n** [[aquatic_genet]]\r\n** [[cape_genet]]\r\n** [[common_genet]]\r\n** [[crested_genet]]\r\n* [[linsang]]\r\n** [[banded_linsang]]\r\n** [[spotted_linsang]]\r\n\r\nh4. General anatomy\r\n\r\n* [[barbed_tongue]]\r\n* [[claws]]\r\n* [[fur]]\r\n** [[spotted_fur]]\r\n** [[striped_fur]]\r\n* [[long_tail]]\r\n** [[ringtail]]\r\n** [[spotted_tail]]\r\n** [[striped_tail]]\r\n* [[whiskers]]\r\n\r\nh4. Other rankings\r\n\r\n* [b][[tag group:species]][/b]\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[afrosoricid]] - Golden mole and tenrec.\r\n** [[bovine]] - Buffalo, cattle, yak, etc.\r\n** [[camelid]] - Alpaca, camel, llama, etc.\r\n** [[canine]] - Dog, fox, wolf, etc.\r\n** [[caprine]] - Goat, ibex, sheep, etc.\r\n** [[cervine]] - Elk, moose, reindeer, etc.\r\n** [[cetacean]] - Dolphin, porpoise, whale, etc.\r\n** [[equine]] - Donkey, horse, zebra, etc.\r\n** [[eulipotyphlan]] - Hedgehog, mole, shrew, etc.\r\n** [[euplerid]] - Fanaloka, fossa, vontsira, etc.\r\n** [[feline]] - Cat, lion, tiger, etc.\r\n** [[giraffid]] - Giraffe, okapi, etc.\r\n** [[herpestid]] - Mongoose\r\n** [[lagomorph]] - Rabbit, hare, pika, etc.\r\n** [[marsupial]] - Kangaroo, koala, opossum, etc.\r\n** [[mephitid]] - Skunks and stink badgers.\r\n** [[monotreme]] - Echidna and platypus\r\n** [[mustelid]] - Ferret, otter, weasel, etc.\r\n** [[pinniped]] - Sea lion, seal, walrus, etc.\r\n** [[porcine]] - Boar, pig, warthog, etc.\r\n** [[primate]] - Ape, lemur, monkey, etc. (excludes [[human]])\r\n** [[proboscidean]] - Elephant, mammoth, mastodon, etc.\r\n** [[procyonid]] - Kinkajou, raccoon, ring-tailed cat, etc.\r\n** [[rodent]] - Mouse, rat, squirrel, etc.\r\n** [[ursine]] - Grizzly bear, panda, polar bear, etc.\r\n** viverrid - Civet, genet, linsang, etc.\r\n** [[xenarthran]] - Anteater, armadillo, and sloth."
