                "wiki_body": "thumb #1430428 thumb #1283872 thumb #1276968\r\n\r\n[b]Phalangeriformes[/b] are a suborder of long-tailed [[marsupial|marsupials]] typically referred to as [b]possums[/b].  Other common names associated with this suborder include glider and cuscus, both types of possums.  They are generally nocturnal and arboreal, adjusting well to urban sprawl.  Their diets range from general herbivore and omnivore to specialized browser (leaf-eating), insectivore, and nectarivore (nectar-consuming) depending on species.\r\n\r\nDespite some naming similarity, there are no opossums in this suborder. In fact, [[american_opossum|opossums form an entirely different order]].\r\n\r\nh4. Families, genera, and species\r\n\r\n* [[marsupial]]\r\n** diprodontia (order)\r\n*** [b]phalangeriformes[/b] (suborder)\r\n**** [[acrobatid]]\r\n***** [[feather-tailed_possum]]\r\n***** [[feathertail_glider]]\r\n**** phalangeridae\r\n***** [[brushtail_possum]]\r\n****** [[common_brushtail_possum]]\r\n***** [[cuscus]]\r\n****** [[spilocuscus]]\r\n**** tarsipedidae\r\n***** [[honey_possum]]\r\n**** [[petaurid]]\r\n***** [[striped_possum]]\r\n***** [[sugar_glider]]\r\n**** [[pseudocheirid|pseudocheiridae]]\r\n***** [[common_ringtail_possum]]\r\n****** [[western_ringtail_possum]] ([i]P. p. occidentalis[/i])\r\n***** [[greater_glider]]\r\n***** [[green_ringtail_possum]]\r\n***** [[herbert_river_ringtail_possum]]\r\n***** [[lemur-like_ringtail_possum]]\r\n**** burramyidae\r\n***** [[pygmy_possum]]\r\n\r\nh4. More information\r\n\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phalangeriformes"
