                "wiki_preview": "thumb #561997 thumb #773149\r\n\r\n[b][i]Sauropoda[/i][/b], or [i]Sauropods[/i] are [[quadruped|quadrupe...",
                "wiki_body": "thumb #561997 thumb #773149\r\n\r\n[b][i]Sauropoda[/i][/b], or [i]Sauropods[/i] are [[quadruped|quadrupedal]], herbivorous, [i]Saurischian[/i] [[dinosaur|dinosaurs]] of the clade [i]Sauropoda[/i]. Many sauropods are considered to be one of the largest species of dinosaur discovered, let alone one of the largest animals to live on the planet. They have iconically large necks, some found to be over 50 feet in length, giving them the common nickname of \"long-neck\". Other notable qualities they tend to share are their long tails, thick and flat bottomed limbs similar to an [[elephant|elephant's]], and their herding tendencies.\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* [[Apatosaurus]]\r\n* [[Argentinosaurus]]\r\n* [[Brachiosaurus]]\r\n* [[Brontosaurus]]\r\n* [[Diplodocus]]\r\n* [[Mamenchisaurus]]\r\n* [[Puertasaurus]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[Dinosaur]]\r\n** [[Ankylosaurian]]\r\n** [[Ceratopsian]]\r\n** Sauropod\r\n** [[Stegosaurian]]\r\n** [[Theropod]]"
