              "wiki_preview": "thumb #988444 thumb #1768686 thumb #449304\r\n\r\nPlesiosaurs (plesiosauria) were an order or clade of [...",
              "wiki_body": "thumb #988444 thumb #1768686 thumb #449304\r\n\r\nPlesiosaurs (plesiosauria) were an order or clade of [[marine]] [[reptile|reptiles]] existing during the same time as dinosaurs, but were not dinosaurs themselves.  They first appeared during the late triassic period and thrived during the jurassic period, eventually replacing [[ichthyosaur|ichthyosaurs]] as top marine predator through the late cretaceous period.  Plesiosaurs went extinct during the \"Cretaceous–Paleogene extinction event\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cretaceous–Paleogene_extinction_event (K-Pg or K-T event).\r\n\r\nPlesiosaurs are often characterized by long, stiff necks and flippers in place of legs.  However, it should be noted that many did not have long necks ([[pliosaur|pliosaurs]]) so it may be worth looking species up if one is uncertain.\r\n\r\nh4. Families and species:\r\n* [[plesiosaur]]\r\n** [[plesiosaurus]]\r\n** [[cryptoclidid]]\r\n*** [[cryptoclidus]]\r\n** [[elasmosaurid]]\r\n*** [[elasmosaurus]]\r\n*** [[alexeyisaurus]]\r\n** [[pliosaur]]\r\n*** [[pliosaurus]]\r\n*** [[liopleurodon]]\r\n\r\nh4. More information:\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plesiosauria"
