        "arachnid": {
          "_Self (arachnid)": [
            {
              "tag": "arachnid",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 15532,
              "wiki_preview": "thumb #1989482 thumb #1818702 thumb #10084\n\n[i]Arachnids[/i], members of [i]Arachnida[/i], are a lar...",
              "wiki_body": "thumb #1989482 thumb #1818702 thumb #10084\n\n[i]Arachnids[/i], members of [i]Arachnida[/i], are a large class of [[arthropod|arthropods]], with most adults possessing [[multi leg|multiple legs]], [[multi eye|multiple eyes]], facial appendages such as [[chelicerae]] and [[pedipalps]], and generally large and/or elongated [[arthropod_abdomen|abdomens]]. The most well known arachnids are [[spider|spiders]] and [[scorpion|scorpions]]. If the arachnid isn't contributing to the scene, consider using [[ambient_arachnid]] [i]instead[/i].\n\nNearly all adult arachnids have 8 legs, differentiating them from general [[insect|insects]] who typically have 6. Also, unlike insects, they lack [[antennae]] as well as [[wings]]. Their bodies are covered in a tough [[exoskeleton]], some being covered in [[fur]] or hairs known as urticating hairs, used as a form of defensive irritant. Almost all arachnids are terrestrial, though a few live within freshwater and marine environments. Quite a few arachnids utilize various, similar defensive and hunting mechanisms, often related to piercing the skin of the predator or their prey with [[claws]], [[pincers]], [[stinger|stingers]], or [[fangs]]. A lot of arachnids utilize this piercing alongside a form of [[venom]]. All arachnids produce silk, and about half of the arachnid species use the silk to weave [[arthropod webbing|webs]] to catch prey.\n\nh4. Families, genera, and species\n\n* [[arthropod]]\n** arachnid\n*** [[acarine]]\n**** [[mite]]\n***** [[acariform]]\n****** [[pyroglyphid]]\n******* [[dust_mite]]\n****** [[sarcoptiform]]\n******* [[itch_mite]]\n****** [[trombidiform]]\n******* [[chigger]]\n******* [[demodex]]\n***** [[mesostigmata]]\n****** [[varroid]]\n**** [[parasitiform]]\n***** [[mesostigmata]]\n***** [[tick_(arachnid)]]\n*** [[camel_spider]]\n*** [[harvestmen]]\n*** [[hooded_tickspider]]\n*** [[horseshoe_crab]]\n*** [[pseudoscorpion]]\n*** [[scorpion]]\n**** [[brontoscorpio]]\n**** [[buthid]]\n***** [[deathstalker_scorpion]]\n***** [[indian_red_scorpion]]\n**** [[hemiscorpiid]]\n***** [[flat_rock_scorpion]]\n**** [[iurid]]\n***** [[hairy_scorpion]]\n**** [[pulmonoscorpius]]\n**** [[scorpionid]]\n***** [[emperor_scorpion]]\n***** [[nebo_(scorpion)]]\n****** [[common_black_scorpion]]\n***** [[giant_forest_scorpion]]\n****** [[asian_forest_scorpion]]\n**** [[vaejovid]]\n***** [[vaejovis]]\n****** [[bryson's_striped_scorpion]]\n*** [[spider]]\n**** [[araneomorph]]\n***** [[diving_bell_spider]]\n***** [[huntsman_spider]]\n***** [[jumping_spider]]\n****** [[peacock_spider]]\n****** [[vampire_spider]]\n****** [[zebra_spider]]\n***** [[orb-weaver_spider]]\n****** [[golden_silk_orb-weaver]]\n****** [[spiny_orb-weaver]]\n******* [[crab-like_orb-weaver]]\n******* [[curved_spiny_spider]]\n***** [[recluse_spider]]\n****** [[brown_recluse]]\n***** [[spitting_spider]]\n***** [[theridiid]]\n****** [[hawaiian_happy-face_spider]]\n****** [[steatoda]]\n******* [[cupboard_spider]]\n****** [[widow_spider]]\n******* [[black_widow_spider]]\n******** [[european_black_widow]]\n******** [[katipo]]\n******** [[northern_widow_spider]]\n******** [[redback_spider]]\n******* [[brown_widow_spider]]\n******* [[red_widow_spider]]\n******* [[white_widow_spider]]\n***** [[thomisid]]\n****** [[flower_crab_spider]]\n******* [[goldenrod_crab_spider]]\n***** [[wandering_spider]]\n****** [[brazilian_wandering_spider]]\n***** [[wolf_spider]]\n**** [[jumping_spider]]\n**** [[mygalomorph]]\n***** [[atracid]]\n***** [[atypical_tarantula]]\n***** [[tarantula]]\n****** [[brachypelma]]\n****** [[cyriopagopus]]\n******* [[cobalt_blue_tarantula]]\n****** [[goliath_birdeater]]\n****** [[ornamental_spider]]\n******* [[gooty_sapphire]]\n****** [[pinktoe_tarantula]]\n**** [[trapdoor_spider]]\n*** [[vinegaroon]]\n*** [[whip_spider]]\n\nh4. Related\n\n* [[ambient_spider]]\n* [[arthropod_humanoid]]\n** [[arachnid_humanoid]]\n*** [[scorpion_humanoid]]\n*** [[spider_humanoid]]\n**** [[tarantula_humanoid]]\n* [[art