        "draconcopode": {
          "_Self (draconcopode)": [
            {
              "tag": "draconcopode",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 13480,
              "wiki_preview": "thumb #945460 thumb #2473023 thumb #1728991 thumb #1281251\r\nthumb #3059066 thumb #4212463 thumb #166...",
              "wiki_body": "thumb #945460 thumb #2473023 thumb #1728991 thumb #1281251\r\nthumb #3059066 thumb #4212463 thumb #1666041 thumb #3890206\r\n\r\nLiterally \"snake-footed\"; an [[apode]] creature that moves around on a [[snake]] tail or similar, excluding [[feral]] [[snake|snakes]]. This can describe anything from a snake with a human head to a [[naga]] or a [[lamia]]. It also covers other slithering body-types that don't fit neatly under either naga or lamia, including \"half-feral\" types that may use forelimbs when moving. \r\n\r\nNot to be confused with [[anguiped]], which is for creatures that have literal snakes instead of feet."
            }
          ],
          "naga": [
            {
              "tag": "naga",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 7832,
              "wiki_preview": "thumb #528538 thumb #2373650 thumb #1728991 thumb #4134914 thumb #1134936\r\nthumb #4081684 thumb #413...",
              "wiki_body": "thumb #528538 thumb #2373650 thumb #1728991 thumb #4134914 thumb #1134936\r\nthumb #4081684 thumb #4132778 thumb #696673 thumb #3989500 thumb #2305232\r\n\r\nAn [[apode]] creature with an [[anthro]] upper body that moves around on a \"snake-like\" lower body of the same species. The term typically refers to the [[snake_naga|\"snake with arms\"]] kind of naga, where it's essentially just an all-snake [[lamia]] (not unlike what a [[horse_taur]] is to [[centaur|centaurs]]). By extension, it may also be used to refer to non-snake species, such as [[dragon_lamia|dragons]], that are made to have the same body shape, but [i]wouldn't count as lamias given how they are not [[split_form]][/i].\r\n\r\nNote that both \"[b]naga[/b]\" and \"[b]lamia[/b]\" have served to designate a wide variety of somewhat snake-like creatures in various fantasy universes, regardless of the etymology. While the definition given to those two words for tagging purposes is essentially arbitrary, care should be taken to avoid tagging as [[naga]] fantasy species that do not match the above definition, even though they may be called that in-universe. The [[naga_(warcraft)|nagas from Warcraft]], for example, have their own tag, even though their usual body shape qualifies for the definition of [[naga]] so long as enough of it is visible to tell. Likewise, [[cock_naga]] (related to [[snake penis]]), despite the name, does not meet that definition, as it describes a creature that is [[conjoined]] and doesn't actually move on its own, which is problematic given the implications of [[draconcopode]] and, by extension, [[apode]].\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[animal_humanoid]]\r\n** [[snake_humanoid]]\r\n* [[serpentine]]\r\n** [[draconcopode]]\r\n*** [[lamia]]\r\n*** [b]naga[/b]\r\n**** [[dragon_naga]]\r\n**** [[snake_naga]]\r\n**** [[pokemon_naga]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[scalie]]\r\n* [[taur]]"
            }
          ]
        },
