        "columbid": {
          "_Self (columbid)": [
            {
              "tag": "columbid",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 2439,
              "wiki_preview": "[b][i]Columbids[/i][/b], members of the family [i]Columbidae[/i] and the order [i]Columbiformes[/i],...",
              "wiki_body": "[b][i]Columbids[/i][/b], members of the family [i]Columbidae[/i] and the order [i]Columbiformes[/i], are a family of stout bodied birds consisting of [[dove|doves]] and [[pigeon|pigeons]] who play a big part in various cultures worldwide. They are likely the most common birds in the world.\r\n\r\nPigeons and doves exhibit considerable variation in size, however their general build tends to follow similar characteristics. [i]Columbids[/i] overall are compact-bodied, with short legs and short necks, and short slender [[beak|bills]] that in some species feature [[cere (feature)|fleshy ceres]]. Most [i]Columbid[/i] plumage tends to be dull in color, however there are a few exceptions with extravagant and vibrant feathers. While in motion, they tend to bob their heads, which is most likely done in order to keep their vision constant.\r\n\r\nDepending on the species, [i]Columbids[/i] play distinct and specific roles within a variety of cultures. Doves are often used and seen as symbolic in [[religion|religious contexts]], often being associated with purity, love, and peace. Pigeons on the other hand, in many modern portrayals, are often associated with [[ill|disease]], compact [[city]] life, and animal pests in general, similar to (and often compared with) the modern portrayal of the [[rat]].\r\n\r\nh4. General anatomy\r\n\r\n* [[beak]]\r\n** [[small_beak]]\r\n* [[cere_(anatomy)]]\r\n* [[feathers]]\r\n** [[feathered_wings]]\r\n** [[tail_feathers]]\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* [[dodo]]\r\n* [[dove]]\r\n** [[diamond_dove]]\r\n** [[mourning_dove]]\r\n** [[turtle_dove]]\r\n** [[zebra_dove]]\r\n** [[zenaida_dove]]\r\n* [[pigeon]]\r\n** [[common_pigeon]]\r\n** [[crowned_pigeon]]\r\n*** [[victoria_crowned_pigeon]]\r\n** [[domestic_pigeon]]\r\n*** [[fancy_pigeon]]\r\n**** [[fantail_pigeon]]\r\n**** [[lahore_pigeon]]\r\n**** [[lucerne_gold_collar]]\r\n*** [[homing_pigeon]]\r\n** [[nicobar_pigeon]]\r\n** [[passenger_pigeon]]\r\n** [[speckled_pigeon]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[avian]]\r\n** [[bird]]\r\n*** [b]columbid[/b]"
            }
