            "wiki_body": "thumb #807078 thumb #736113 thumb #2903086 thumb #2329102\r\n\"[b]◀[u]Bulbapedia[/u]▶[/b]\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Charizard_(Pokémon)?wprov=sfti1#\r\n\r\n[color=species][b]Charizard[/b][/color] (Japanese: [color=species][b]リザードン [i]Rizādon[/i] \"Lizardon\"[/b][/color]) is a dual-type [color=#EE8130]Fire[/color]/[color=#A98FF3]Flying[/color] Pokémon. \r\n\r\nIt evolves from Charmeleon starting at level 36. It is the final form of Charmander. It can Mega Evolve into two forms: [[Mega Charizard X]] using Charizardite X and [[Mega Charizard Y]] using Charizardite Y. \r\n\r\nCharizard is a draconic, bipedal Pokémon. It is primarily orange with a cream underside from the chest to the tip of its tail, which burns with a sizable flame. Charizard has a long neck, small blue eyes, raised nostrils, and two blunt horns protruding from the back of its rectangular head. There are two fangs visible in the upper jaw when its mouth is closed. Two large wings with teal undersides sprout from its back, and a horn-like appendage juts out from the third joint of each wing. Charizard's arms are short and skinny compared to its robust belly, and each limb has three white claws. It has stocky legs and cream-colored soles under its feet. \r\n\r\nCharizard is close to the [[feral]]/[[anthro]] split, and can be difficult to tag. As a rule of thumb, the canon form is [[feral]] but any amount of anthrofication (such as shorter neck, see the first thumb as an example) will usually push it into [[anthro]] instead. [[Semi-anthro]] subtag often applies.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n* [[biped]]\r\n* [[dragon]] - often resembles dragons, despite not being dragon type\r\n* [[flaming_tail]]\r\n* [[membranous_wings]]\r\n* [[orange_body]]\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]]\r\n** #0004 [[Charmander]]\r\n** #0005 [[Charmeleon]]\r\n** [b]#0006 Charizard[/b]\r\n*** [[Mega Charizard]]\r\n**** [[Mega Charizard X]]\r\n**** [[Mega Charizard Y]]\r\n*** [[Gigantamax Charizard]]\r\n* [i][[Chilicola charizard]][/i] — species of [i]Chilicola[/i] [[bee]] named after Charizard"
