            "wiki_body": "thumb #833578 thumb #635305 thumb #628902 thumb #579127\n\nMewtwo is a Psychic-type Legendary Pokémon introduced in Generation I. Mewtwo's appearance is loosely based on Mew, with a less feline look. Its body is purple and it has three fingers on each hand. Mewtwo projects a faint purple aura when at full power. It is an [[artificial lifeform]] created by [[Team Rocket]], though its exact backstory is different across the various Pokémon canons.\n\nMewtwo is the antagonist of the first Pokémon movie, where he has a masculine voice and is referred to as male. He attempts to take over the world due to his hatred of humans, but ultimately chooses peace. A different Mewtwo also appears in [i]Genesect and the Legend Awakened[/i]; it has a feminine voice, but its gender is never stated.\n\nThough it technically doesn't evolve, Mewtwo has two Mega Evolutions, which appear in the Pokemon X and Y games. \n\nh4. See Also:\n\n* [[pokémon]]\n** [[legendary_pokémon]]\n*** [b]Generation I[/b]\n**** Legendary birds\n***** [[articuno]]\n***** [[zapdos]]\n***** [[moltres]]\n**** Mew duo\n***** mewtwo\n****** [[mega_mewtwo]]\n******* [[mega_mewtwo_x]] (Generation VI)\n******* [[mega_mewtwo_y]] (Generation VI)\n****** [[shadow_mewtwo]] (Pokkén)\n***** [[mew]]"
