            "wiki_body": "thumb #399342 thumb #1694289 thumb #595347 thumb #4530688\r\n\r\nAn [[apode]], [[split form]] creature with the bottom half of a [[snake]]. The top half, while traditionally [[humanoid]], can be any [[anthro]] non-snake species (an all-snake [[lamia]] would just be a [[naga]], as it would not be split-form).\r\n\r\nNote that both \"[b]naga[/b]\" and \"[b]lamia[/b]\" have served to designate a wide variety of somewhat snake-like creatures in various fantasy universes, regardless of the etymology. While the definition given to those two words for tagging purposes is essentually arbitrary, care should be taken to avoid tagging as [[lamia]] fantasy species that do not match the above definition, even though they may be called that in-universe.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[serpentine]]\r\n** [b]lamia[/b]\r\n** [[naga]]\r\n* [[animal_humanoid]]\r\n** [[snake_humanoid]]\r\n* [[monster_girl]]\r\n* [[split_form]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n\r\n* [[Scalie]]\r\n* [[Taur]]"
