            "wiki_body": "Species that became extinct after about 5,000 years ago, most of them falling victim to human activity.\n\n[section=Incomplete list]\nOnly species who have a tag with at least one image are listed here.\n\n* [[woolly mammoth]] (2nd millennium BCE)\n* [[elephant bird]] (11th century)\n* [[moa (bird)]] (c. 1445)\n* [[haast's eagle]] (shortly after the Moa)\n* [[aurochs]] (1627)\n* [[dodo]] (1662)\n* [[steller's sea cow]] (1768)\n* [[mauritius blue pigeon]] (c. 1830)\n* [[great auk]] (1862)\n* [[quagga]] (1883)\n* [[sea mink]] (1894)\n* [[japanese wolf]] (1905)\n* [[passenger pigeon]] (1914)\n* [[carolina parakeet]] (1918)\n* [[bubal hartebeest]] (1925)\n* [[thylacine]] (1936)\n* [[kaua'i 'o'o]] (1987)\n* [[pyrenean ibex]] (2000, again in 2003 after unsuccessful cloning)\n* [[japanese river otter]] (2012)\n* [[chinese paddlefish]] (2022)\n\nBelow are believed to be extinct but unconfirmed.\n* [[baiji]] (last seen 2002)\n[/section]"
