            "wiki_body": "thumb #2391467   thumb #94908   thumb #3521596\r\n\"[b]◀[u]Bulbapedia[/u]▶[/b]\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Squirtle_(Pokémon)?wprov=sfti1#\r\n\r\n[color=species][b]Squirtle[/b][/color] (Japanese: [color=species][b]ゼニガメ [i]Zenigame[/i][/b][/color], lit. \"coin turtle\") is a [color=#6390F0]Water[/color]-type [[Pokémon (species)|Pokémon]]. It evolves into [[Wartortle]], and is in the [i]Monster[/i] and [i]Water 1[/i] egg groups.\r\n\r\nIt is the Water starter of Kanto.\r\n\r\nSquirtle is a small Pokémon that resembles a light blue turtle. While it typically walks on its two short legs, it has been shown to run on all fours in [i][[Super Smash Bros|Super Smash Bros. Brawl]][/i]. It has large brown eyes and a slightly hooked upper lip. Each of its hands and feet have three pointed digits. The end of its long tail curls inward. Its body is encased by a tough shell that forms and hardens after birth. This shell is brown on the top, pale yellow on the bottom, and has a thick white ridge between the two halves. \r\n\r\nShiny Squirtle has green shell.\r\n\r\nAs it is a bipedal tortoise-like creature (not to mention that its head shape is much closer to human than animal), Squirtle is [[anthro]] in its canon form. The [[semi-anthro]] subtag often applies.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[biped]]\r\n* [[shell]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]]\r\n** [b]#0007 Squirtle[/b]\r\n*** [[Squirtle Squad]]\r\n** #0008 [[Wartortle]]\r\n** #0009 [[Blastoise]]\r\n*** [[Mega Blastoise]]\r\n*** [[Gigantamax Blastoise]]\r\n* [i][[Mauremys]][/i]\r\n** [[Japanese pond turtle]] ([i]Mauremys japonica[/i]) — In Japan, [i]銭亀 zenigame[/i] is commonspeak for baby turtles of this species.\r\n* [[Squirtle (Leo)]] — Character from [i][[Leo (film)|Leo]][/i] (2023) named after the species."
