            "wiki_body": "thumb #2045448\r\n\r\nSource: https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Toxtricity_(Pok%C3%A9mon)\r\n\r\n[b]Toxtricity[/b] (Japanese: [i]ストリンダー Sutorindā[/i]) is a dual-type Electric/Poison [[Pokémon (species)|Pokémon]] introduced in Generation VIII. Both Toxtricity and its pre-evolved form [[Toxel]] are the only Pokémon with this type combination.\r\n\r\nToxel evolves into Toxtricity at level 30. Toxtricity has two forms. Which form Toxel evolves into depends on its nature:\r\n\r\n* Toxel becomes [[Amped Toxtricity]] if its Nature is Hardy, Brave, Adamant, Naughty, Docile, Impish, Lax, Hasty, Jolly, Naive, Rash, Sassy, or Quirky.\r\n* Toxel becomes [[Low Key Toxtricity]] if its Nature is Lonely, Bold, Relaxed, Timid, Serious, Modest, Mild, Quiet, Bashful, Calm, Gentle, or Careful.\r\n\r\nAmped Toxtricity can learn Venoshock and Shift Gear, whereas Low Key Toxtricity can learn Venom Drench and Magnetic Flux. The rest of Toxtricity's moves are able to be learned by either form.\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokémon_(species)]]\r\n** [[toxel]]\r\n*** toxtricity\r\n**** [[amped_toxtricity]]\r\n**** [[low_key_toxtricity]]"
