            "wiki_preview": "thumb #1927191 thumb #4864346\r\n\r\n[b]Alcremie[/b] ([i]マホイップ[/i], Mawhip) is a Fairy-type [[pokémon_(s...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1927191 thumb #4864346\r\n\r\n[b]Alcremie[/b] ([i]マホイップ[/i], Mawhip) is a Fairy-type [[pokémon_(species)|Pokémon]] introduced in Generation VIII. It evolves from [[Milcery]] when the player gives it a sweet to hold and then spins on the spot in the overworld for a few seconds. This evolution method is a reference to how [[whipped cream]], which Alcremie resembles, is made. \r\n\r\nAlcremie has 63 different forms, along with a [[gigantamax_pokémon|Gigantamax]] form, which is the signature Pokémon of Gym Leader [[opal_(pokémon)|Opal]]. It also has seven [[shiny_pokémon|shiny]] variations, which only differ in what sweet they have on them. Which form of Alcremie the Milcery becomes depends on the time of day, how long the player spins, whether they spin clockwise or counterclockwise, and which sweet they give to Milcery. Alcremie has the most alternate forms out of any Pokémon, beating the previous holder of the title, [[Unown]], which only has 28 forms.\r\n\r\nThese forms are combinatory, each being a pairing of one of nine different creams (with the shiny form acting as a sort of tenth) and one of seven different sweets. The cream determines the overall coloration of the body, while the sweet determines the adornments on the head and the eye color. In order to not have a ridiculous number of very long tags (and a few other reasons), the cream and sweet are tagged separately here.\r\n\r\nh4. Creams\r\n\r\n* [[vanilla_cream_alcremie]]\r\n* [[ruby_cream_alcremie]]\r\n* [[matcha_cream_alcremie]]\r\n* [[mint_cream_alcremie]]\r\n* [[lemon_cream_alcremie]]\r\n* [[salted_cream_alcremie]]\r\n* [[ruby_swirl_alcremie]]\r\n* [[caramel_swirl_alcremie]]\r\n* [[rainbow_swirl_alcremie]]\r\n* ([[shiny_pokemon]])\r\n\r\nh4. Sweets\r\n\r\n* [[strawberry_sweet_alcremie]]\r\n* [[berry_sweet_alcremie]]\r\n* [[love_sweet_alcremie]]\r\n* [[star_sweet_alcremie]]\r\n* [[clover_sweet_alcremie]]\r\n* [[flower_sweet_alcremie]]\r\n* [[ribbon_sweet_alcremie]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[pokémon_(species)]]\r\n** [[milcery]] \r\n*** alcremie\r\n**** [[gigantamax_alcremie]]"
