            "wiki_body": "Source: <https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Pyroar_(Pok%C3%A9mon)>\r\n\r\n[b]Pyroar[/b] (Japanese: カエンジシ Kaenjishi) is a dual-type Fire/Normal [[Pokémon (species)|Pokémon]]. Both Pyroar and its pre-evolved form [[Litleo]] are the only Pokémon with this type combination.\r\n\r\nPyroar is a [[quadruped]], leonine Pokémon. It is mostly dark [[brown_fur|brown]] with light brown legs, tail tip, chest, and face. Pyroar's irises are tinted [[blue_eyes|azure]] with black pupils, and its nose is the same dark [[brown_nose|brown]] as the main area of its body.\r\n\r\nPyroar's other body features are dependent on gender. The [[male|males]] are visibly taller and bulkier than the [[female|females]], as with real [[lion|lions]], although the Pokédex does not make the distinction and instead classifies them under the same height and weight. A male Pyroar has a large, dominantly red [[mane]] with gold streaks forming a pattern resembling the [i]Daimonji[/i] symbol 大. The shape also resembles the symbol for fire 火. In addition to this, the tuft on the end of their tail has a noticeable split, and the fur ruffs on their back legs spread out. In contrast, a female has a long, gold and red mane extending from its forehead to the whole length of its body which, unlike the male's mane, does not obscure its ears. The female's tail tuft and back legs do not have spread-apart tips like those of the males. Additionally, though the male Pyroar has a chevron-shaped nose in its official artwork and in [i]Pokémon Battle Trozei[/i], all other merchandise, game, and anime artwork shows it with a triangular shaped nose, similar to that of the female.\r\n\r\nLitleo and Pyroar are notable for their unique gender ratio; only one in every eight Litleo/Pyroar is male. This contrasts the universal ratio for all starter Pokémon, where seven of every eight individuals are male.\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokémon]]\r\n** [[litleo]]\r\n*** pyroar"
