            "wiki_body": "thumb #376680   thumb #1697313   thumb #5104302\n\nA [color=species][b]mouth creature[/b][/color] is an [[organ creature]] whose body [i]OR[/i] [[for_a_head|head]] consists predominantly of one or more mouths.\n* Naturally, a mouth creature must have an orifice that can be visually identified as a mouth, and some part of the body that can be identified as a \"face\".\n** [[goo creature|Goo creatures]] are often depicted as being able to take insertions in arbitrary locations, but this doesn't mean every orifice is a mouth.\n** Certain species (such as a feral [[annelid]]) may have a bodily form that lacks a distinct head, and therefore a distinct \"face\".\n** Certain body parts may have a mouth attached (such as [[nipple mouth|nipple mouths]]), but this alone does not mean the body part is a \"face\".\n\nh4.See also:\n* [[ear creature]]\n* [[eye creature]]\n* [[eyeless]]\n* [[multi mouth]]\n* [[nose creature]]\n* [[tongue creature]]\n* [[tooth creature]]"
