            "wiki_body": "thumb #1669947 thumb #1663784 thumb #1685740\r\n\r\nSource:\r\nhttps://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Azurill\r\n\r\n[b]Azurill[/b] (Japanese: ルリリ [i]Ruriri[/i]) is a dual-type Normal/Fairy [[baby Pokémon]] introduced in Generation III. Prior to Generation VI, it was a pure Normal-type [[Pokémon]].It evolves into [[Marill]] when leveled up with high friendship, which evolves into [[Azumarill]] starting at level 18.\r\n\r\nAzurill, along with [[Wailmer]] and [[Kecleon]], was one of the first Generation III Pokémon revealed, in early March 2001.\r\n\r\nAzurill is a round, blue mouse Pokémon. It has circular ears with pink insides. There are two white dots on its cheeks, and it has black eyes. Its thin, black, zigzagging tail has a large blue ball at the end.It often sits on its tail and has no arms.\r\n\r\nThe ball is bouncy and packed with the nutrients it needs to be able to grow. The ball can also be used as a flotation device. It can be seen bouncing and playing on this rubbery tail. The tail can also be spun around like a lasso. When the tail is thrown, the body can go as far as 33 feet (10 meters). Though Azurill is typically docile, it swings the big ball on its tail to smash into opponents bigger than itself when angered. It lives at the water's edge.\r\n(The above content is from the bulbapedia.)\r\n\r\nShiny Azurill is green instead of blue.\r\n\r\nAccording to the bulbapedia,Azurill has circular ears with pink insides,so Azurill should be tagged as [[pink_inner_ear]] instead of [[red_inner_ear]],unless the inner ears drawn as red deliberately.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n* [[armless]]\r\n* [[black_eyes]]/[[blue_eyes]]\r\n* [[black_tail]]\r\n* [[blue_body]](Original)\r\n* [[blue_ears]](Original)\r\n* [[blue_fur]](Original)\r\n* [[blue_tail]](Original)\r\n* [[featureless_feet]]\r\n* [[green_body]](Shiny)\r\n* [[green_ears]](Shiny)\r\n* [[green_fur]](Shiny)\r\n* [[green_tail]](Shiny)\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n* [[noseless]]\r\n* [[pink_inner_ear]]\r\n* [[rodent]]\r\n* [[round_ears]]\r\n* [[tail_orb]] \r\n* [[two_tone_tail]]\r\n* [[white_cheeks]]\r\n* [[white_spots]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokémon_(species)]]\r\n** [b]azurill[/b]\r\n*** [[marill]]\r\n**** [[azumarill]]"
