            "wiki_preview": "[b]Icterids[/b], members of [i]Icteridae[/i], are a family of small to medium-sized, often colorful ...",
            "wiki_body": "[b]Icterids[/b], members of [i]Icteridae[/i], are a family of small to medium-sized, often colorful [[passerine]] birds. This group includes the New World blackbirds, New World orioles, the bobolink, meadowlarks, grackles, cowbirds, oropendolas, and caciques. Despite the similar names, the New World groups are only distantly related to the Old World [[common blackbird]] (a [[thrush (bird)|thrush]]) or the Old World orioles, [[oriolid|Oriolids]].\r\n\r\n[i]Icterids[/i] are variable in size, and often display considerable [[sexual dimorphism]], with brighter coloration and extremely unique size differences in [[male|males]] being typical. Most [i]Icterids[/i] have black as a predominant plumage color, often enlivened by yellow, orange or red. The name, meaning \"jaundiced ones\" (from the prominent yellow feathers of many species) comes from the Ancient Greek [i]ikteros[/i], via the Latin [i]ictericus[/i].\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* [[cacique_(bird)]]\r\n* [[cowbird]]\r\n* [[grackle]]\r\n** [[greater_antillean_grackle]]\r\n* [[meadowlark]]\r\n* [[new_world_blackbird]]\r\n** [[bobolink]]\r\n** [[red-winged_blackbird]]\r\n** [[rusty_blackbird]]\r\n** [[yellow-headed_blackbird]]\r\n* [[new_world_oriole]]\r\n** [[baltimore_oriole]]\r\n** [[montserrat_oriole]]\r\n* [[oropendola]]\r\n** [[chestnut-headed_oropendola]]\r\n\r\n[section=Taxon]\r\n\r\n* [b]icteridae[/b]\r\n** [[cacique_(bird)]]\r\n*** [i]Amblycercus[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[yellow-billed_cacique]]\r\n*** [i]Cacicus[/i] (genus) - Contains most cacique, and a few oropendola species.\r\n*** [i]Cassiculus[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[mexican_cacique]] - Also known as yellow-winged cacique.\r\n** [[cowbird]]\r\n*** [i]Molothrus[/i] (genus)\r\n** [[grackle]]\r\n*** [i]Hypopyrrhus[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[red-bellied_grackle]] ([i]H. pyrohypogaster[/i])\r\n*** [i]Lampropsar[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[velvet-fronted_grackle]] ([i]L. tanagrinus[/i])\r\n*** [i]Macroagelaius[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[mountain_grackle]]\r\n*** [i]Quiscalus[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[common_grackle]]\r\n**** [[greater_antillean_grackle]]\r\n**** [[great-tailed_grackle]]\r\n** [[marshbird]]\r\n*** [i]Pseudoleistes[/i] (genus)\r\n** [[meadowlark]]\r\n*** [i]Leistes[/i] (genus) - Group of red breasted meadowlarks.\r\n**** [[red-breasted_meadowlark]]\r\n*** [i]Sturnella[/i] (genus) - Group of yellow breasted meadowlarks.\r\n**** [[eastern_meadowlark]]\r\n**** [[western_meadowlark]]\r\n** [[new_world_blackbird]]\r\n*** [i]Agelaius[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[red-winged_blackbird]]\r\n*** [i]Agelasticus[/i] (genus)\r\n*** [i]Agelaioides[/i] (genus) - Baywings, related to cowbirds\r\n**** [[baywing]]\r\n***** [[greyish_baywing]] ([i]A. badius[/i])\r\n***** [[pale_baywing]] ([i]A. fringillarius[/i])\r\n*** [i]Amblyramphus[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[scarlet-headed_blackbird]] ([i]A. holosericeus[/i])\r\n*** [i]Anumara[/i] (genus)\r\n*** [i]Chrysomus[/i] (genus)\r\n*** [i]Curaeus[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[austral_blackbird]] ([i]C. Curaeus[/i])\r\n*** [i]Dives[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[cuban_blackbird]] ([i]D. atroviolacea[/i])\r\n*** [i]Dolichonyx[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[bobolink]]\r\n*** [i]Euphagus[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[brewer's_blackbird]]\r\n**** [[rusty_blackbird]]\r\n*** [i]Gnorimopsar[/i] (genus)\r\n*** [i]Gymnomystax[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[oriole_blackbird]]\r\n*** [i]Nesopsar[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[jamaican_blackbird]]\r\n*** [i]Oreopsar[/i] (genus)\r\n*** [i]Xanthopsar[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[saffron-cowled_blackbird]]\r\n*** [i]Xanthocephalus[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[yellow-headed_blackbird]]\r\n** [[new_world_oriole]]\r\n*** [i]Icterus[/i]\r\n**** [[baltimore_oriole]] ([i]I. galbula[/i])\r\n**** [[montserrat_oriole]] ([i]I. oberi[/i])\r\n** [[oropendola]]\r\n*** [i]Cacicus[/i] (genus)\r\n**** [[band-tailed_oropendola]] ([i]C. latirostris[/i])\r\n**** [[casqued_oropendola]] ([i]C. oseryi[/i])\r\n*** [i]Psarocolius[/i]\r\n**** [[chestnut-headed_oropendola]] ([i]P. wagleri[/i])\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with