              "wiki_body": "thumb #1341948 thumb #2093303 thumb #120046\r\n\r\n[b]Lizards[/b] are a widespread group of squamate reptiles, with over 6000 species, ranging across all continents except Antarctica as well as most oceanic island chains. The group, traditionally recognized as the suborder Lacertilia, is defined as all extant members of the Lepidosauria (reptiles with overlapping scales), which are neither sphenodonts \r\n nor snakes – they form an evolutionary grade. While the snakes are recognized as falling phylogenetically within the anguimorph lizards from which they evolved, the Sphenodonts are the sister group to the Squamates, the larger monophyletic group, which includes both the lizards and the snakes.\r\n\r\nh4. Species (Incomplete)\r\n\r\n* [[gecko]]\r\n* [[girdled_lizard]]\r\n* [[helodermatid]]\r\n* [[iguanomorph]] (Iguanomorpha)\r\n** [[acrodont]]\r\n*** [[agamid]] (Dragon lizards)\r\n*** [[chameleon]]\r\n** [[pleurodont]]\r\n*** [[collared_lizard]] (Crotaphytidae)\r\n**** [[leopard_lizard]]\r\n*** [[dactyloid]] (Anoles)\r\n*** [[helmeted_lizard]]\r\n*** [[iguanid]] (Iguanas)\r\n*** [[phrynosomatid]]\r\n* [[monitor_lizard]]\r\n* [[skink]]\r\n* [[tegu]]    \r\n\r\nh4. Fictional Species\r\n\r\n* [[argon_lizard]]\r\n** [[great_argon_lizard]]\r\n* [[lizard_taur]]\r\n\r\nh4. External links\r\n\r\n* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lizard\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[reptile]]\r\n** [b]lizard[/b]\r\n** [[snake]]\r\n* [[scalie]]"
