                  "wiki_body": "[b]Pit vipers[/b] are venomous snakes in the subfamily Crotalinae in the family [[viper|Viperidae]]. They are named as such for the heat-sensing pit organ located between the eye and the nostril on both sides of the head.\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* [[ground_pit_viper]]\r\n** [[american_ground_pit_viper]] (Agkistrodon)\r\n*** [[american_copperhead]] (A. contortrix)\r\n*** [[cottonmouth]] (A. piscivorus)\r\n** [[asian_ground_pit_viper]] (Gloydius)\r\n*** [[japanese_mamushi]] (G. blomhoffii)\r\n*** [[siberian_pit_viper]] (G. halys)\r\n** [[bushmaster]] (Lachesis)\r\n** [[humpnosed_viper]] (Hypnale)\r\n** [[malayan_ground_pit_viper]] (Calloselasma)\r\n* [[hog-nosed_pit_viper]] (Porthidium)\r\n* [[hundred-pace viper]] (Deinagkistrodon)\r\n* [[lancehead]]\r\n** [[american_lancehead]] (Bothrops, include Bothrocophias_andianus)\r\n* [[jumping_pit_viper]] (Atropoides)\r\n* [[mexican_horned_pit_viper]] (Ophryacus)\r\n* [[mountain_pit_viper]]\r\n** [[american_mountain_pit_viper]] (Cerrophidion) - montane pit vipers\r\n** [[asian_mountain_pit_viper]] (Ovophis)\r\n** [[mount_kinabalu_pit_viper]] (Garthius)\r\n** [[cloud_montane_pit_viper]] (Mixcoatlus)\r\n* [[palm_pit_viper]]\r\n** [[american_palm_pit_viper]] (Bothriechis)\r\n* [[protobothrops]]\r\n* [[rattlesnake]] (Crotalus)\r\n** [[baja_rattlesnake]] (Crotalus enyo)\r\n** [[black-tailed_rattlesnake]] (Crotalus molossus)\r\n** [[diamondback_rattlesnake]]\r\n*** [[eastern_diamondback_snake]] (Crotalus adamanteus)\r\n*** [[red_diamond_rattlesnake]] (Crotalus ruber) - Red diamond rattlesnake, Western diamondback snake, and Western rattlesnake are similar in appearance.\r\n*** [[western_diamondback_snake]] (Crotalus atrox)\r\n*** [[western_rattlesnake]] (Crotalus oreganus)\r\n** [[mexican_lance-headed_rattlesnake]] (Crotalus polystictus)\r\n** [[mohave_rattlesnake]] (Crotalus scutulatus)\r\n** [[rock_rattlesnake]] (Crotalus lepidus)\r\n** [[sidewinder]] (Crotalus cerastes)\r\n** [[south_american_ra