          "frog": {
            "_Self (frog)": [
              {
                "tag": "frog",
                "kor": "",
                "count": 11775,
                "wiki_preview": "thumb #1317507 thumb #848626 thumb #591382\r\n\r\n[b]Frogs[/b], members of the order [i]Anura[/i], are a...",
                "wiki_body": "thumb #1317507 thumb #848626 thumb #591382\r\n\r\n[b]Frogs[/b], members of the order [i]Anura[/i], are a group of diverse [[amphibian|amphibians]]. Frogs are widely distributed around the world, but are most commonly found in and are the most diverse in [[rainforest|tropical rainforests]]. With around 4,800 recorded species, they make up around 85% of extant amphibian species. Warty frog species, while often referred to as [[toad (frog)|toads]], are simply informally distinct. The difference does not exist in taxonomy or evolutionary history.\r\n\r\nAdult frogs are generally stout and wide in body shape, and they are [[quadruped|quadrupedal]] with limbs that can fold in under their bodies. Their eyes protrude from their heads and their [[tongue|tongues]] are cleft. They also notably lack tails. Their skin colors can vary depending on the species, with some providing camouflage, while others are bright, vivid colors to ward off predators. Adults live in fresh water and on dry land, with some living [[underground]] or in [[tree|trees]]. Frogs usually start off and develop from [[larva]] known as [[tadpole|tadpoles]], who hatch from [[egg|eggs]] typically laid [[underwater]]. Their larval forms come with tails as well as [[gills]], useful for their temporary dwelling in bodies of water. After growth, they metamorphose into adults frogs.\r\n\r\nFrog skins allow for things to pass through it, such as water, which can make dehydration quite easy. Due to this, they either live in very moist environments or have special adaptations to allow for their survival in dry areas. Frogs are well known for their wide varieties of vocalizations such as croaks, especially during breeding seasons.\r\n\r\nh4. Families, genera, and species\r\n\r\n* [[amphibian]]\r\n** [[frog]]\r\n*** [[archaeobatrachian]]\r\n**** [[fire-bellied_toad]]\r\n**** [[leiopelmatid]]\r\n**** [[painted_frog]]\r\n**** [[tailed_frog]]\r\n*** eleutherodactylid\r\n**** [[eleutherodactylus]]\r\n***** [[common_coquí]]\r\n*** [[glass_frog]]\r\n*** [[litter_frog]]\r\n*** mantellid\r\n**** [[mantella]]\r\n***** [[painted_mantella]]\r\n*** [[parsley_frog]]\r\n*** [[pipid]]\r\n**** [[surinam_toad]]\r\n*** [[poison_dart_frog]]\r\n**** [[blue_poison_dart_frog]]\r\n**** [[dyeing_dart_frog]]\r\n**** [[green-and-black_poison_dart_frog]]\r\n**** [[red-backed_poison_frog]]\r\n**** [[reticulated_poison_frog]]\r\n**** [[strawberry_poison-dart_frog]]\r\n**** [[yellow-banded_poison_dart_frog]]\r\n*** [[rain_frog]]\r\n**** [[desert_rain_frog]]\r\n*** [[ranid]]\r\n**** [[wood frog]]\r\n*** [[toad_(frog)]] (informal group)\r\n**** [[burrowing_toad]]\r\n**** [[fire-bellied_toad]]\r\n**** [[spadefoot_toad]]\r\n**** [[surinam_toad]]\r\n**** [[true_toad]]\r\n***** [[beaked_toad]]\r\n****** [[cane_toad]]\r\n**** [[colorado_river_toad]]\r\n**** [[kihansi_spray_toad]]\r\n**** [[wyoming_toad]]\r\n*** [[tree_frog]]\r\n**** [[amazon_milk_frog]]\r\n**** [[red-eyed_treefrog]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related\r\n\r\n* [[tadpole]]\r\n\r\nh4. General anatomy\r\n\r\n* [[horizontal_pupils]]\r\n* [[long_tongue]]\r\n* [[shiny_skin]]\r\n* [[webbed_feet]]"
              }
