            "wiki_body": "thumb #1230829 thumb #1230831 thumb #2157742\n\nThese [[Lizardman|Lizardmen]] are a race of anthropomorphic saurian reptiles from the setting of [[Warhammer_Fantasy|Warhammer Fantasy]] and its sequel setting, [[Warhammer_Age_Of_Sigmar|Warhammer: Age of Sigmar]], where they are renamed \"The Seraphon.\"\n\n[section,expanded=Lizardmen sub-species]\n* [[Slann]] - Toad-like Lizardmen who are powerful mages and rulers of Lizardman society.\n* [[Saurus]] - Large and ferocious Lizardmen who serve as the warrior-caste.\n* [[Skink_(warhammer_fantasy)|Skink]] - Small and intelligent Lizardmen who serve as artisans, administrators, scribes and translators. In times of war, they serve as light infantry and skirmishers (with those gifted with magic serving as priests; casting powerful and destructive spells against their foes)\n* [[Kroxigor]] - Hulking and dimwitted Lizardmen who serve as laborers and shock infantry.  \n[/section]\n\n[section,expanded=Lizardmen Mounts]\n* [[Carnosaur]]\n* [[Ancient Salamander]]\n* [[Terradon]]\n[/section]\n\n[section,expanded=List of Lizardman characters]\n* [[Kroq Gar]] & [[Grymloq]] - A mighty Saurus Oldblood and [[Carnosaur]], respectively. \n* [[Tehenhauin]] - The skink Prophet of Sotek.\n* [[Nakai the Wanderer]] - The Eldest and Largest of the Kroxigors.\n* [[Gor-Rok]] - A mighty saurus warrior, also known as \"The Great White Lizard.\"\n* [[Tiqtak'to]] - Current Master of Skies of the Temple-City of Hexoatl, the greatest of the Terradon Riders. Also known as the \"Eye in the Heavens.\"\n[/section]"
