              "wiki_body": "thumb #1816936 thumb #1063420 thumb #14484 thumb #176825\r\n\r\nThe largest family of rodents, including old-world rats and mice.  Murids are widespread throughout the world, though they are native to Eurasia and Africa.  Note that this means that new-world rodents like [[cricetid|hamsters, voles, and new-world rats and mice]] are part of an entirely different family and thus should not be tagged with [[murid]] or any tag under it.\r\n\r\nThis family can be divided further into five subfamilies: [[deomyine|deomyinae]], [[gerbil|gerbillinae]], [[maned_rat|lophiomyinae]], [[togo_mouse|leimacomyinae]] and [[murine|murinae]].\r\n\r\nh4. Subfamilies, genera, and species:\r\n* [[murid|muridae]]\r\n** [[maned_rat|lophiomyinae]] (maned rats)\r\n** [[togo_mouse|leimacomyinae]] (togo mice)\r\n** [[gerbil|gerbillinae]] (gerbils)\r\n** [[deomyine|deomyinae]]\r\n*** [[spiny_mouse]]\r\n*** [[link_rat]]\r\n*** [[rudd's_mouse]]\r\n** [[murine|murinae]] (old-world rats and mice)\r\n*** [[striped_grass_mouse]]\r\n**** [[barbary_striped_grass_mouse]]\r\n*** [i]Apodemus[/i]\r\n**** [[wood_mouse]]\r\n*** [[mouse]] ([i]Mus[/i])\r\n**** [[house_mouse]] ([i]M. musculus[/i])\r\n**** [[fancy_mouse]] ([i]M. m. domesticus[/i])\r\n*** [[rat]] ([i]Rattus[/i])\r\n**** [[black_rat_(species)|black_rat]] ([i]R. rattus[/i])\r\n**** [[brown_rat]] ([i]R. norvegicus[/i])\r\n**** [[fancy_rat]] ([i]R. n. domestica[/i])\r\n***** [[dumbo_rat]]\r\n***** [[blue_rat]]\r\n***** [[hairless_rat]]\r\n\r\nh4. More information:\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muridae"
