              "wiki_preview": "[i]Sciurids[/i], members of [i]Sciuridae[/i] and also known collectively as [b]squirrels[/b], are a ...",
              "wiki_body": "[i]Sciurids[/i], members of [i]Sciuridae[/i] and also known collectively as [b]squirrels[/b], are a family of well known and iconic [[rodent|rodents]]. Known collectively as the \"squirrel family\", it includes animals such as the [[tree squirrel|tree squirrels]] and [[ground squirrel|ground squirrels]].\r\n\r\nGenerally being small in stature, the typical [i]Sciurid[/i] tend to be slender, have [[long tail|long]], [[fluffy tail|bushy tails]], soft [[fur|pelts]], and characteristic [[buckteeth|rodent incisors]]. Most squirrels have long hind limbs and versatile [[claws]] for grasping and climbing, seen most especially in the Tree squirrels, who can also unusually descend [[tree|trees]] head-first. Squirrels have an excellent sense of vision thanks to their enlarged eyes, especially important for the tree-dwelling squirrels.\r\n\r\nh4. General anatomy\r\n\r\n* [[buckteeth]]\r\n* [[curled_tail]]\r\n* [[fluffy_tail]]\r\n* [[fur]]\r\n** [[fur_tuft]]\r\n* [[long_tail]]\r\n* [[whiskers]]\r\n\r\nh4. Subfamilies, genera, and species:\r\n\r\n* Sciurinae\r\n** [[flying squirrel|Pteromyini]] (flying squirrel)\r\n** [i][[pine squirrel|Tamiasciurus]][/i] (pine squirrel)\r\n*** [[american red squirrel]] ([i]T. hudsonicus[/i])\r\n*** [[douglas squirrel]] ([i]T. douglasii[/i])\r\n*** [[mearns's squirrel]] ([i]T. mearnsi[/i])\r\n** [i]Sciurus[/i]\r\n*** [[eurasian red squirrel]] ([i]S. vulgaris[/i])\r\n*** [[fox squirrel]] ([i]S. niger[/i])\r\n*** [[eastern grey squirrel]] ([i]S. carolinensis[/i])\r\n*** [[western grey squirrel]] ([i]S. griseus[/i])\r\n* [[giant squirrel|Ratufinae]] (giant squirrel)\r\n** [i]Ratufa[/i]\r\n*** [[black giant squirrel]] ([i]R. bicolor[/i])\r\n*** [[indian giant squirrel]] ([i]R. indica[/i])\r\n* Xerinae\r\n** [[ground squirrel|Marmotini]] (ground squirrel)\r\n*** [i]Eutamias[/i]\r\n*** [i]Neotamias[/i]\r\n*** [i]Tamias[/i]\r\n**** eastern chipmunk ([i]T. striatus[/i])\r\n*** [i][[prairie dog|Cynomys]][/i] (prairie dog)\r\n*** [i][[marmot|Marmota]][/i] (marmot)\r\n**** [[groundhog]] ([i]M. monax[/i])\r\n**** [[yellow-bellied marmot]] ([i]M. flaviventris[/i])\r\n\r\nh4. Informal groups:\r\n\r\n* [[tree squirrel]]\r\n* [[grey squirrel]]\r\n* [[chipmunk]]\r\n\r\nh6. Fictional\r\n\r\n* [[saber-toothed_squirrel]]\r\n** [[scratazon]]\r\n* [[sciurid_humanoid]]\r\n** [[chipmunk_humanoid]]\r\n** [[prairie_dog_humanoid]]\r\n** [[squirrel_humanoid]]\r\n* [[weresquirrel]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[rodent]]\r\n*** sciurid"
