                "wiki_body": "thumb #1411461 thumb #2771591 thumb #838934\r\n\r\nThe [b]red squirrel[/b] or [b]Eurasian red squirrel[/b] ([b][i]Sciurus vulgaris[/i][/b]) is a species of [[tree squirrel]] in the genus [i]Sciurus[/i] common throughout Europe and Asia. The red squirrel is an arboreal and primarily herbivorous [[rodent]].\r\n\r\nA lighter, redder overall coat colour[sup]*[/sup], along with the [[ear tuft|ear-tufts]] (in adults) and smaller size, distinguish the red squirrel from the [[eastern grey squirrel]].\r\n\r\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_squirrel\r\n\r\n[sup]*[/sup] See: [[red fur]], [[orange fur]], [[brown fur]]"
