              "wiki_body": "thumb #1935363\r\n\r\nSimilar to the [[kangaroo mouse]], the term \"kangaroo rat\" refers to a genus of small New-World bipedal rodents, [i]Dipodomys[/i], found in in western North America.  Despite superficial similarities it is not related to [[murid]] rodents (such as [[mouse|mice]] or [[rat|rats]]) or [[dipodid]] rodents (such as [[jerboa|jerboas]]) and is part of its own family, [[heteromyid|Heteromyidae]].  They share the subfamily of [[dipodomyine|dipodomyinae]] with the [[kangaroo mouse|kangaroo mice]].\r\n\r\nh4. Species:\r\n* [[heteromyid|heteromyidae]]\r\n** [[dipodomyine|dipodomyinae]]\r\n*** [i][[kangaroo rat|Dipodops]][/i]\r\n**** [[agile kangaroo rat]] [i](D. agilis)[/i]\r\n**** [[california kangaroo rat]] [i](D. californicus)[/i]\r\n**** [[gulf coast kangaroo rat]] [i](D. compactus)[/i]\r\n**** [[desert kangaroo rat]] [i](D. deserti)[/i]\r\n**** [[texas kangaroo rat]] [i](D. elator)[/i]\r\n**** [[big-eared kangaroo rat]] [i](D. elephantinus)[/i]\r\n**** [[san quintin kangaroo rat]] [i](D. gravipes)[/i]\r\n**** [[heerman's kangaroo rat]] [i](D. heermanni)[/i]\r\n**** [[giant kangaroo rat]] [i](D. ingens)[/i]\r\n**** [[merriam's kangaroo rat]] [i](D. merriami)[/i]\r\n**** [[chisel-toothed kangaroo rat]] [i](D. microps)[/i]\r\n**** [[nelson's kangaroo rat]] [i](D. nelsoni)[/i]\r\n**** [[fresno kangaroo rat]] [i](D. nitratoides)[/i]\r\n**** [[ord's kangaroo rat]] [i](D. ordii)[/i]\r\n**** [[panamint kangaroo rat]] [i](D. panamintinus)[/i]\r\n**** [[phillips's kangaroo rat]] [i](D. phillipsii)[/i]\r\n**** [[dulzura kangaroo rat]] [i](D. simulans)[/i]\r\n**** [[banner-tailed kangaroo rat]] [i](D. spectabilis)[/i]\r\n**** [[stephens's kangaroo rat]] [i](D. stephensi)[/i]\r\n**** [[narrow-faced kangaroo rat]] [i](D. venustus)[/i]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. More information:\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kangaroo_rat"
