            "wiki_body": "An [b]arthropod[/b] is an invertebrate animal having an [[exoskeleton]] (external skeleton), a segmented body, and jointed appendages. Arthropods form the phylum Arthropoda, and include the insects, arachnids, and crustaceans. If the arthropod isn't contributing to the scene, consider using [[ambient_arthropod]] [i]instead[/i].\n\nh3. Chelicerates\n\n* [[arachnid]]\n** [[camel_spider]]\n** [[scorpion]]\n** [[spider]]\n*** [[tarantula]]\n** [[tick_(arachnid)|tick]]\n** [[vinegaroon]]\n* [[horseshoe_crab]]\n\nh3. [[crustacean|Crustaceans]]\n\n* [[barnacle]]\n* [[crab]]\n* [[crawfish]]\n* [[hermit_crab]]\n* [[isopod]]\n* [[lobster]]\n* [[shrimp]]\n\nh3. [[myriapod|Myriapods]]\n\n* [[myriapod]]\n** [[millipede]]\n** [[centipede]]\n\nh3. [[trilobite|Trilobites]]\n\nh3. Hexapods\n\nh4. [[insect|Insects]] (incomplete)\n\n* [[ant]]\n** [[army_ant]]\n** [[fire_ant]]\n** [[honeypot_ant]]\n* [[antlion]]\n* [[bee]]\n* [[beetle]]\n** [[firefly]]\n** [[ladybug]]\n** [[rhinoceros_beetle]]\n** [[scarab]]\n** [[stag_beetle]]\n* [[cicada]]\n** [[treehopper]]\n* [[cockroach]]\n* [[earwig]]\n* [[flea]]\n* [[dipteran|fly]]\n** [[bee_fly]]\n** [[blow_fly]]\n** [[botfly]]\n** [[crane_fly]]\n** [[horsefly]]\n* [[lepidopteran]] - winged insects with proboscises; butterflies, moths, etc.\n** [[butterfly]]\n*** [[marpesia_furcula]]\n** [[moth]]\n*** [[pellucid_hawk_moth]] \n* [[mantidfly]]\n* [[mantis]]\n** [[european_dwarf_mantis]]\n** [[flower_mantis]]\n*** [[devil's_flower_mantis]]\n*** [[orchid_mantis]]\n** [[glass_mantis]]\n** [[stick_mantis]]\n* [[mosquito]]\n* odonata - insects with long abdomens and 2 pairs of wings; dragonfly, damselfly, etc\n** [[damselfly]]\n** [[dragonfly]]\n* orthoptera - insects with cylindrical bodies and elongated hindlegs; grasshoppers, crickets, etc.\n** [[cricket]]\n** [[grasshopper]]\n** [[locust]]\n* [[phasmid]] (stick-bug)\n* [[silverfish]]\n* [[snakefly]]\n* [[termite]]\n* [[wasp]]\n** [[hornet]]\n\n* [[insectoid]]\n\nh4. [[spr