            "wiki_preview": "Sloths, seperated in 2 families depending on how many [[claw|claws]] they have, are [[mammal|mammals...",
            "wiki_body": "Sloths, seperated in 2 families depending on how many [[claw|claws]] they have, are [[mammal|mammals]] in the order [[pilosan|pilosa]] well known for their slow movements and reactions. This slowness is due to how their metabolisms evolved in order to conserve energy. They are also known for their long limbs, hanging from trees, occasional [[green fur]] from algae or fungus growth, and their ability to swim. They tend to have shaggy and unkempt fur due to their hanging habits and slowness.\r\n\r\nh5. Species\r\n\r\n* [[ground_sloth]]\r\n** [[giant_ground_sloth]]\r\n** [[megalonyx]]\r\n* [[three-toed_sloth]]\r\n* [[two-toed_sloth]]\r\n\r\nh5. Fictional\r\n* [[ice_age]]\r\n** [[granny (ice age)|granny]]\r\n** [[sid (ice_age)|sid]]\r\n* [[my_little_pony]]\r\n** [[friendship_is_magic]]\r\n*** [[lola the sloth]]\r\n* [[zootopia]]\r\n** [[flash_slothmore]]\r\n** [[priscilla_tripletoe]]\r\n\r\nh6. Mythology and Folklore\r\n\r\n* [[mapinguari_(cryptid)|mapinguari]]\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with:\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[primate]]\r\n*** [[ape|apes]]\r\n*** [[monkey|monkeys]]\r\n** [[bear]]\r\n*** [[sloth bear|sloth_bears]], though similar in name, are not sloths.\r\n\r\nh4. Related\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[pilosan]]\r\n*** sloth\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[seven_deadly_sins]]\r\n** [[sloth_(sin)|sloth]]"
