            "wiki_body": "[b]Pooka[/b] can refer to two distinct species from separate video games: in the Vanillaware game [[Odin Sphere]], originally for the Playstation 2, Pookas are humans suffering under a curse that has turned them into a race of semi-anthropomorphic rabbits.\nIn the Namco arcade classic [[Dig Dug]], they're those red and yellow things that kind of look like they're wearing goggles.\n\nThe name Pooka is traditionally derived from the creature of Celtic Folklore called the púca in Irish Gaelic, which is a shape-changing spirit that often takes the form of animals, including rabbits. Another derivative is the English [i]Puck[/i], of Shakespearean fame.\n\nFor the Dig Dug species, use [[pooka_(dig_dug)]] instead."
