            "wiki_body": "thumb #210946 thumb #2548253 thumb #2477634 thumb #1383671\n\nDragonborn is a race of draconic humanoids originating from the pen and paper role-playing game, [i][[Dungeons and Dragons]][/i].\n\nThe dragonborn of [i]Dungeons & Dragons[/i] typically sport approximately human-sized heights, [[non-mammal breasts]] for the females, [[tailless|no tails]], and head spines resembling [[dreadlocks]].\n\nThey started off life in the [i]D&D[/i] series as good-aligned and non-draconic humanoids who, upon rebirth, willingly took on draconic traits as a show of devotion to their patron god Bahamut. They became a playable race beginning with 4th edition, though whose origins are unknown and varied. But when taking magical creation and lack of tails out of the picture, a dragonborn becomes near-interchangeable from a [[half-dragon]].\n\nh4. Not to be confused with\n\n* The [[Dovahkiin]], the hero of [i][[The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim]][/i], often referred to as \"(the) Dragonborn\".\n* A [[kobold]] or [[lizardfolk]], with the former race essentially being made up of [[short|shorter]] draconic humanoids and the latter race usually having little to no relation to the [[dragon]] species.\n\nh4. See also\n\n* \"Forgotten Realms page about the Dragonborn race\":https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dragonborn"
