            "wiki_body": "thumb #1499773\r\n\r\n[b]Kenku[/b] are an avian race from [i][[Dungeons_and_Dragons|Dungeons & Dragons]][/i]. Commonly based on corvids and standing around 5 feet, kenku were robbed of their ability of flight and speech by an ancient god. Kenku have the ability of mimicry, able to piece together voices and sounds they have heard to communicate.\r\n\r\nKenku first appeared in the [i]Fiend Folio[/i] sourcebook for the first edition of [i]Dungeons & Dragons[/i] and have made numerous appearances since then. In 2012, kenku became an official playable race in the 411th issue of [i]Dragon[/i] magazine for the fifth edition of [i]Dungeons & Dragons[/i].\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n* [[aarakocra_(dnd)|Aarakocra]], another avian race from [i]Dungeons & Dragons[/i], but these are capable of flight, speech, and can be based on other species of bird.\r\n* [[Tengu]], a loose inspiration of kenku.\r\n\r\n"
