            "wiki_body": "The [b]Manakete[/b] are a race of [[humanoid]] [[dragon]]s featured in the [[Fire Emblem]] series by [[nintendo|Nintendo]] and Intelligent Systems.\n\nThese shape-shifting beings take up human form, but store their dragon energy inside a magical artifact known as a \"dragonstone\", which they can use to take their original form as [[feral]] dragons. Manaketes are frequently depicted as the survivors of a past [[genocide]], though the details vary by continuity.\n\nManaketes are extremely long-lived, with lifespans measured in millennia. Their physical development is similarly slowed, such that even at 1000 years of age they have the physical appearance of [[child|children]]. The species is infamous for being populated almost entirely by [[loli]] characters who are [[adult_(lore)|technically adults]].\n\nThe dragons in [i][[fire_emblem_three_houses|Three Houses]][/i] and the dragon [[laguz]] in [i][[fire_emblem_path_of_radiance|Path of Radiance]][/i] and [i][[fire_emblem_radiant_dawn|Radiant Dawn]][/i] are functionally identical to manaketes, though they do not require stones to transform.\n\nNotable manaketes include [[tiki_(fire_emblem)|Tiki]] (the original) and [[Nowi]] (the most infamous)."
