              "wiki_preview": "A hybrid is the offspring of two different species of animal. This tag applies to mainly odd combina...",
              "wiki_body": "A hybrid is the offspring of two different species of animal. This tag applies to mainly odd combinations of distantly related species.\r\n\r\nNote that this tag does not apply to [[human|humans]]. 'Hybrid humans' are covered by body type tags such as [[animal humanoid]], [[taur]], and [[anthro]].\r\n\r\nh4. Real-world examples\r\n\r\n* [[wolfdog]]\r\n* [[mule]]\r\n* [[liger]]\r\n* [[tigon]]\r\n\r\nh4. Fictional hybrids\r\n\r\nIn order to find the specific species of hybrid you want, search for the component animal tags along with the hybrid tag. Using fictional species tags such as `cabbit`, `folf`, and `wolingo` are not allowed, and will not work if you try to search for them. Try to make sure the fictional species can be discerned from the image before you tag. Sometimes the hybrid parts will be obscured from view.\r\n\r\nNote: Winged versions of various species do not typically get treated as hybrids.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[chimera]], creatures that have mixed parts from multiple distinct species, for example a fox with butterfly wings\r\n* [[transformation]], mid-transformation forms are not tagged as hybrid\r\n* [[Hybrid (fortnite)|Hybrid]], a draconic humanoid character from [[Fortnite]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag group:species#hybridfauna|tag group:species: Hybrid]]\r\n** [[tag group:fictional species#hybridother|tag group:fictional species: Fictional Animal Hybrids]]\r\n* [[chimera]] - An animal made up of distinct parts of other animals, such as a [[gryphon]], often created through magic.\r\n* [[interspecies]] - A relationship between characters of different species.\r\n** [[interspecies_pregnancy]] - The process from which gives rise to a hybrid.\r\n* [[taur]] - A character with an anthropomorphic head and body, and a lower half with four (or more) legs. Resembles a [[centaur]]."
