            "wiki_body": "thumb #118921 thumb #3776654 thumb #81327 thumb #4408222\n\nA [b]gryphon[/b] or [b]griffin[/b] is a [[mythological_avian|mythological avian]] creature traditionally consisting of a mix between an [[eagle]] and a [[lion]]. In general, a gryphon is a [[feral]] [[quadruped]] with bird-like features such as [[feathers]], a [[beak]], or [[feathered_wings|wings]] and a cat-like mammalian body with a [[butt]] and distinct shoulders. A [[tail_tuft|leonine tail]] or [[tail_feathers|tail feathers]] and [[prick_ears|prick ears]] are common. Gryphons are often but not always depicted with mammalian genitalia ([[sheath]]/[[balls]]/[[vulva]]) and an [[anus]]. [[Anthro]] gryphons have these characteristics but are bipedal. An anthro [[bird]] can usually be distinguished from an anthro gryphon by having no cat-like features."
