              "wiki_body": "[b]Scalie[/b], or [b]scaly[/b], is a generic term invented by the furry fandom for [[reptile|reptiles]] and other species (with actual scales or not) that have reptilian features, such as [[dragon|dragons]].\r\n\r\nA common point of confusion with scalies is that they are any species with scaly skin. There are several notable exceptions to this idea, as the tag only requires reptilian features, not scales. For creatures with scales, just use the [[scales]] tag instead.\r\n\r\nExamples of species with scales that are not scalie:\r\n* most [[fish]] (including the [[shark]])\r\n* [[bird|birds]] (scales are found on their feet)\r\n* [[pangolin|pangolins]]\r\n* [[armadillo|armadillos]]\r\n\r\nExamples of scalie species commonly seen without scales:\r\n* [[leopard_gecko|leopard geckos]], [[bearded_dragon|bearded dragons]], and several species of [[snake]] can be found in scaleless varieties\r\n* [[feathered dinosaur]]\r\n* [[pterosaur]] (in place of scales, they had pycnofibers, which usually look like fur in artwork)\r\n* [[softshell turtle]]\r\n* [[furred snake]] - completely fictional, but popular enough to note\r\n* [[salamander]] - while not technically a reptile, these are typically considered part of the scalie group due to their strong resemblance to lizards.\r\n\r\nh5. Some species that are considered scalies are\r\n* Any [[reptile]]\r\n* Some [[amphibian|amphibians]] ([[frog|frogs]] are generally excluded)\r\n* Mythological reptilian species\r\n** [[chimera (mythology)]]\r\n** [[cockatrice]]\r\n** [[dragon]]\r\n** [[kirin]]\r\n** [[leviathan]]\r\n** [[lizardman]] (not to be confused with a regular {{anthro lizard}})\r\n** [[naga]]\r\n** [[questing beast]]\r\n** Some [[cryptid|cryptids]]\r\n*** [[loch ness monster]]\r\n*** [[chupacabra]] (sometimes)\r\n** Some [[yōkai]]\r\n*** [[kappa]]\r\n*** [[tsuchinoko]]\r\n* Fictional reptilian species\r\n** [[argonian]]\r\n** [[deathclaw]]\r\n** [[dragonborn (dnd)]]\r\n** [[iksar]]\r\n** [[kig-yar]]\r\n** [[kobold]] (not to be confused with the canine-like [[japanese_kobold|Japanese kobold]], nor the [[kobold_(warcraft)|rat-like kobold]] from [i][[Warcraft]][/i])\r\n** [[koopa]]\r\n** [[night stalker (fallout)]]\r\n** [[viper (x-com)]]\r\n** [[yoshi]]\r\n\r\nh4. See other rankings:\r\n* [[tag group:species]]\r\n\r\n* [[amphibian]]\r\n* [[arthropod]]\r\n* [[avian]]\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n* [[marine]]\r\n* [[mollusk]]"
