              "wiki_preview": "thumb #2528233 thumb #4363760 thumb #634954\r\nSalamanders in classical mythology and heraldry are [[l...",
              "wiki_body": "thumb #2528233 thumb #4363760 thumb #634954\r\nSalamanders in classical mythology and heraldry are [[lizard]]-like or [[dragon]]-like creatures with an affinity for [[fire]], often depicted as living within fire. Modern depictions of the mythological salamander tend to depict it as a [[lizard]] or small [[dragon]] either with a flame at the tip of its [[tail]], a [[flaming mane]], or even made completely of fire. The most popular depiction of this species is seen in the [[Pokemon]] evolutionary line of [[Charmander]], [[Charmeleon]], and [[Charizard]].\r\n\r\nMythological salamanders may additionally be tagged as [[western dragon]], [[lizard]], or [[salamander]] if it closely resembles those species. Please do not tag all mythological salamanders as [[salamander]] unless the character actually looks like a real salamander, as that tag is reserved for the real-world amphibian species.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with:\r\n* [[fire salamander]] - a real-world species of salamander.\r\n\r\nh4. See more:\r\n* \"Cultural depictions of salamanders\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultural_depictions_of_salamanders on Wikipedia."
