                  "wiki_body": "In mythology, [b]firebirds[/b] are legendary, often sacred, birds associated with the element of fire as the name suggests.\r\n\r\nThey are commonly seen [[breathing fire]], or with [[flaming wings]] and/or [[flaming tail|tails]]. They are most often associated with rebirth and reincarnation, often turning into [[ashes]] and [[transformation|reforming into a new being]]. They are also often associated with [[rainbow|rainbows]], sometimes creating [[rainbow arch|a rainbow trail]], and often carry [[rainbow feathers|rainbow plumage]].\r\n\r\nh4. Common anatomy\r\n\r\n* [[fire]]\r\n** [[breathing_fire]]\r\n** [[flaming_tail]]\r\n** [[flaming_wings]]\r\n* [[multicolored_feathers]]\r\n** [[rainbow_feathers]]\r\n* [[multicolored_wings]]\r\n** [[rainbow_wings]]\r\n* [[rainbow]]\r\n** [[rainbow_arch]]\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n\r\n* [[mythological_fenghuang]]\r\n* [[phoenix]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[avian]]\r\n** [[bird]]\r\n* [[cryptid]]\r\n* [[elemental]]\r\n** [[fire_elemental]]\r\n* [[mythology]]\r\n** [[chinese_mythology]]\r\n** [[egyptian_mythology]]\r\n** [[greek_mythology]]"
