              "wiki_preview": "Clams are [[bivalve|bivalves]] characterised by [i]commonly[/i] burying themselves in soft substrate...",
              "wiki_body": "Clams are [[bivalve|bivalves]] characterised by [i]commonly[/i] burying themselves in soft substrate (such as [[sand]] or [[mud]]) by means of digger \"foot\".\r\n\r\nTheir shells are mostly symmetrical, being either smooth or marked with grooves. They also may vary in shape, being compact, elliptical, rectangular; and  rarely more wavy rather than symmetrical ([[giant_clam|giant clams]]).\r\n\r\nA typical characteristic of clams is the presence of developed siphons, which promotes water circulation. They may sometimes be seen poking out of the shell or emerging from the ground if the creature is buried.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[oyster]]\r\n* [[scallop]]\r\n* [[seashell]]\r\n\r\n\r\n"
