              "wiki_body": "[i]Echinozoa[/i] are a subphylum of generally globose, flattened, or aberrant [[echinoderms]] which lack the characteristic arms of [[crinoid|crinoids]] and [[asterozoan|Asterozoans]], opting instead for derived [[tube_feet|tube feet]] and [[spikes_(anatomy)|spines]] in their skin. The characteristic pentaradial symmetry of most other echinoderms is highly modified in this group, with [[holothurian|Holothuria]] containing the most derived, nearly-bilateral body plans."
