              "wiki_body": "thumb #1238871 thumb #1568377 thumb #1345340 thumb #451198\r\n\r\nMarsupials are any member of the infraclass Marsupialia.  These animals are characterized by giving birth before full fetal development and raising their young in a maternal pouch until fully developed.  They represent the clade originating from the last common ancestor of the extant metatheria (animals which are most related to marsupials than to placental mammals, including extinct non-marsupial relatives).  Popular representatives include the [[red_kangaroo]], the [[koala]], and the [[virginia_opossum]].  A sample of their taxonomy is listed below.\r\n\r\nh4. Taxonomy\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[marsupial]]\r\n*** [[marsupial_mole|notoryctemorphia]] (marsupial_mole)\r\n*** [[monito_del_monte|microbiotheria]] (monito_del_monte)\r\n*** diprodontia (order)\r\n**** [[macropod|macropodiformes]] (suborder)\r\n***** macropodidae\r\n****** [[red_kangaroo]]\r\n****** [[western_grey_kangaroo]] ([i]M. fuliginosus[/i])\r\n****** [[eastern_grey_kangaroo]] ([i]M. giganteus[/i])\r\n****** [[antilopine_kangaroo]]\r\n****** [[tree-kangaroo]]\r\n****** [[wallaby]]\r\n****** [[quokka]]\r\n***** potoroidae\r\n****** [[bettong]]\r\n****** [[potoroo]]\r\n**** [[possum|phalangeriformes]] (suborder)\r\n***** [[acrobatid]]\r\n****** [[feather-tailed_possum]]\r\n****** [[feathertail_glider]]\r\n***** phalangeridae\r\n****** [[brushtail_possum]]\r\n******* [[common_brushtail_possum]]\r\n****** [[cuscus]]\r\n******* [[spilocuscus]]\r\n***** tarsipedidae\r\n****** [[honey_possum]]\r\n***** [[petaurid]]\r\n****** [[striped_possum]]\r\n****** [[sugar_glider]]\r\n***** [[pseudocheirid|pseudocheiridae]]\r\n****** [[common_ringtail_possum]]\r\n******* [[western_ringtail_possum]] ([i]P. p. occidentalis[/i])\r\n****** [[greater_glider]]\r\n****** [[green_ringtail_possum]]\r\n****** [[herbert_river_ringtail_possum]]\r\n****** [[lemur-like_ringtail_possum]]\r\n***** burramyidae\r\n****** [[pygmy_possum]]\r\n**** [[vombatiform|vombatiformes]] (suborder)\r\n***** [[koala]]\r\n***** [[wombat]]\r\n***** thylacoleonidae\r\n****** [[thylacoleo]]\r\n*** [[dasyuromorph|dasyuromorphia]] (order)\r\n**** myrmecobiidae\r\n***** [[numbat]]\r\n**** dasyuridae\r\n***** [[tasmanian_devil]]\r\n***** [[quoll]]\r\n****** [[tiger_quoll]]\r\n**** thylacinidae\r\n***** [[thylacine]]\r\n*** [[didelphid|didelphimorphia]] (order)\r\n**** didelphidae\r\n***** [[marmosops]]\r\n***** [[bushy-tailed_opossum]]\r\n***** [[virginia_opossum]]\r\n***** [[water_opossum]]\r\n***** [[marmosa]]\r\n****** [[woolly_mouse_opossum]]\r\n***** [[monodelphis]]\r\n****** [[southern_red-sided_opossum]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related:\r\n* [[weremarsupial]]\r\n** [[weremacropod]]\r\n* [[marsupial_humanoid]]\r\n** [[didelphid_humanoid]]\r\n** [[macropod_humanoid]]\r\n** [[vombatiform_humanoid]]\r\n*** [[koala_humanoid]]\r\n* [[marsupial_taur]]\r\n** [[macropod_taur]]\r\n\r\nh4. More information:\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsupial\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metatheria\r\n\r\nh4. Other rankings\r\n\r\n* [b][[tag group:species]][/b]\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[afrosoricid]] - Golden mole and tenrec.\r\n** [[bovine]] - Buffalo, cattle, yak, etc.\r\n** [[camelid]] - Alpaca, camel, llama, etc.\r\n** [[canid]] - Dog, fox, wolf, etc.\r\n** [[caprine]] - Goat, ibex, sheep, etc.\r\n** [[cervine]] - Elk, moose, reindeer, etc.\r\n** [[cetacean]] - Dolphin, porpoise, whale, etc.\r\n** [[equine]] - Donkey, horse, zebra, etc.\r\n** [[eulipotyphlan]] - Hedgehog, mole, shrew, etc.\r\n** [[euplerid]] - Fanaloka, fossa, vontsira, etc.\r\n** [[felid]] - Cat, lion, tiger, etc.\r\n** [[giraffid]] - Giraffe, okapi, etc.\r\n** [[herpestid]] - Mongoose\r\n** [[hyaenid]] - Hyenas\r\n** [[lagomorph]] - Rabbit, hare, pika, etc.\r\n** marsupial - Kangaroo, koala, opossum, etc.\r\n** [[mephitid]] - Skunks and stink badgers.\r\n** [[monotreme]] - Echidna and platypus\r\n** [[mustelid]] - Ferret, otter, weasel, etc.\r\n** [[pinniped]] - Sea lion, sea