              "count": 4072,
              "wiki_preview": "thumb #631966 thumb #346880 thumb #186073\r\n\r\nUse this for bipedal monsters with a [[humanoid]] form....",
              "wiki_body": "thumb #631966 thumb #346880 thumb #186073\r\n\r\nUse this for bipedal monsters with a [[humanoid]] form. Classic examples include old-school movie characters such as [[Nosferatu]] and [[Frankenstein's monster]]. This often involves animations and images with a [[creepy]] or otherwise [[violence|violent]] atmosphere.\r\n\r\nDon't use this if a character has a basic form way unlike a [[Human|human being]] (examples being creatures with multiple heads, a bunch of legs, etc). Alternate labels such as '[[alien]]' and just '[[monster]]' probably imply instead. It's also not applicable to characters that can be described as '[[cute]]'. If a creature looks broadly non-threatening, somewhat human-like, and so on, use other labels such as '[[Monster_girl_(genre)|monster girl]]' and simply '[[humanoid]]'. \r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[Creepy]]\r\n* [[Monster]]\r\n* [[Nightmare_fuel]]\r\n* [[Not_furry]]\r\n* [[Undead]]\r\n* [[Vampire]]\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with:\r\n\r\n* [[Uncanny_valley]], which is more subtle"
