                "wiki_body": "[b]Feline humanoids[/b] are characters who appear mostly [[human]], but possess features of \"small cat\" species — almost always including feline ears and a feline tail.\r\n\r\nIn addition to ears and tails, they may have other feline features, such as [[whiskers]], [[sharp teeth]], [[fangs]], [[slit pupils]], and/or [[claws]]. They may have paw-like hands, patches of fur on their skin, hair patterned after feline markings, they may have markings on their skin (such as stripes or spots), or they may even appear to have a thin layer of fur covering their entire body.\r\n\r\n[quote]h5. Tagging Notes\r\n\r\n* If a character has full-body markings/appears to be covered in fur, and has an animal-nose, as common with feline characters drawn in the [[kemono]] style, they should be tagged as [[anthro]], not as animal humanoid\r\n** A character with a snout should always be tagged as [[anthro]], not [[animal humanoid]]\r\n* Animal humanoids should never be tagged [[anthro]] or [[human]]\r\n* If the ears seem fake, use [[fake cat ears]] instead[/quote]\r\n\r\nh4. Types of Feline Humanoids\r\n\r\n* [[cat humanoid]]\r\n* [[caracal humanoid]]\r\n* [[cheetah humanoid]]\r\n* [[cougar humanoid]]\r\n* [[sand cat humanoid]]\r\n* [[serval humanoid]]\r\n* [[lynx humanoid]]\r\n* [[leopardus humanoid]] (not to be confused with \"leopard humanoid\")\r\n** [[ocelot humanoid]]\r\n** [[margay humanoid]]\r\n\r\nh4.See Also\r\n\r\n* [[felid humanoid]] - umbrella tag for all humanoids under the [i]Felidae[/i] \r\n* [[humanoid]]\r\n** [[animal humanoid]]\r\n* [[anthro]]\r\n* [[feral]]\r\n* [[human]]\r\n* [[not_furry]]\r\n* [[taur]]"
