              "wiki_body": "thumb #788089 thumb #974654 thumb #4103388 thumb #1708223 thumb #2737184 thumb #1134645\n\nThe [[tag_group:body_types|body type]] of a multi-limbed character whose lower body is that of a legged [[feral]] creature, and the upper body of an [[anthro]], [[human]], or [[humanoid]]. Based on the [[centaur]], a creature from [[Greek mythology]]. \n\n\n[quote]\n\nh4. Tagging Notes\n* Taur may also include characters that appear similar to taurs but have [[flippers]] in place of legs/ paws.\n\n* Please note that taurs are their own category and shouldn't be tagged as [[anthro]], [[feral]], [[human]], or [[humanoid]] ([[animal_humanoid]]).\n\n* Not to be confused with: [[draconcopode]], [[merfolk]], [[minotaur]], [[naga]], [[lamia]], [[satyr]].\n\n[/quote]\n\n\nh4. Tags About Taurs\n\n[section=Types Of Taur]\n\n** [[bipedal_taur]] - A taur whose lower body is a biped feral.\n** [[feral_taur]] - A taur whose lower body is a complete specimen of its derivative species.\n** [[humanoid_taur]] - A taur whose upper body is human or humanoid.\n** [[long_taur]] - A taur who has multiple lower bodies connected in a chain.\n** [[long_neck_taur]] - A taur whose body halves join thru a long neck.\n** [[multi_taur]] - A taur who has multiple separate lower bodies connected to a single upper body or vice versa.\n** [[rear_taur]] - A taur whose upper body joins at the lower body's hips.\n\n[/section]\n\n[section=Taur Species]\n\n[section=Non-fictional Species:]\n\n** [[amphibian_taur]]\n*** [[frog_taur]]\n*** [[salamander_taur]]\n\n+++\n\n** [[arthropod_taur]]\n*** [[insect_taur]]\n*** [[myriapod taur]]\n*** [[scorpion_taur]]\n*** [[spider_taur]]\n\n+++\n\n** [[avian_taur]]\n*** [[bird_taur]]\n\n+++\n\n** [[mammal_taur]]\n*** [[ailurid_taur]]\n**** [[red_panda_taur]]\n*** [[bat_taur]]\n*** [[bovid_taur]]\n**** [[antelope_taur]]\n**** [[bovine_taur]]\n**** [[caprine_taur]]\n*** [[camelid_taur]]\n*** [[canid_taur]]\n**** [[canine_taur]]\n***** [[dog_taur]]\n*****