            "wiki_preview": "Images or animations in which it isn't clear what species a character is intended to be. While the t...",
            "wiki_body": "Images or animations in which it isn't clear what species a character is intended to be. While the tag is intended to be temporary, replaced with the appropriate species tag once the truth is found out, there are a certain number of artists who draw fantasy creatures that they themselves are not sure what to call (or \"generic furry characters\"), particularly for one-off images or animations, without having any specific species in mind. There are also characters who are specifically designed to be one-of-a-kind or who officially have an \"unknown\" species (e.g. [[chip (sonic)]]).\r\n\r\nIf the species of the character is hard to identify due to a lack of recognizable features visible in the image, such as the case of extreme close-ups for example, use [[ambiguous_species]] instead.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[anon]]\r\n** [[anonymous_character]]\r\n* [[ambiguous_gender]]\r\n* [[source_request]]\r\n* [[tagme]]\r\n* [[translation request]]\r\n* [[species_request]]\r\n* [[unknown_artist]]\r\n** [[unknown_artist_signature]]\r\n* [[unknown_character]]\r\n* [b]unknown_species[/b]"
