            "tag": "boss_monster_(undertale)",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 23622,
            "wiki_preview": "Boss Monsters are a species in [[Undertale]]. They are creatures whose [[Soul_(Undertale)|souls]] ca...",
            "wiki_body": "Boss Monsters are a species in [[Undertale]]. They are creatures whose [[Soul_(Undertale)|souls]] can temporarily exist outside of their body after [[death]], and they only age when their offspring does, unique traits compared to other monsters in the game. \r\n\r\nAll currently known Boss Monsters are members of the same royal family, the Dreemurr family: [[asgore_dreemurr|Asgore]], [[Toriel]], and [[asriel dreemurr|Asriel]]. They display a mix of [[caprine]] and [[leonine|lion]]-like features such as [[fangs]], [[paws]], droopy ears, and [[horn|horns]] when matured. Similar to real life [[lion|lions]], they appear to display [[sexual dimorphism]], with males often having [[mane|manes]]. They also appear to have unique [[magic|magical powers]] of sorts, often dealing with or themed around [[fire|flames or fire]], a possible nod to and deconstruction of the tropes surrounding [[caprine demon|satanic and demonic caprines]].\r\n\r\nWhile all Boss Monsters are encountered as bosses ingame, [b][i]not all bosses are Boss Monsters[/i][/b]. Boss Monster refers to the unique, caprine-like species seen in the universe of Undertale, not all monsters who happen to be bosses. While deliberately very similar in appearance to Asriel, it is unknown if [[deltarune|Deltarune's]] [[Ralsei]] is also a Boss Monster, and therefore they should not be tagged as such.\r\n\r\nIn the unofficial fan game [[Undertale Yellow]], two other Boss Monsters are observed: [[Chujin Ketsukane]] and his daughter [[kanako_ketsukane|Kanako]]. Unlike the Dreemurr family, the Ketsukane family have fox-like features, including tails and long snouts, and seem to be based on mythological [[fox_spirit|kitsune]]. Despite being a part of the same family, [[ceroba_ketsukane|Ceroba]] is not a Boss Monster.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[caprine]]\r\n* [[video_games]]\r\n** [[deltarune]]\r\n** [[undertale]]\r\n*** [[asgore]]\r\n*** [[asriel_dreemurr]]\r\n*** [[toriel]]"
