            "wiki_body": "thumb #1584341 thumb #1205335 thumb #1902445 thumb #1206425\r\n\r\nThis tag refers to the [i][[Lilo and Stitch|Lilo & Stitch]][/i] franchise's [b]genetic experiments[/b]; the 629 genetically engineered [[alien]] characters created by Dr. [[Jumba Jookiba]], of which [[Stitch (Lilo and Stitch)|Stitch]] is the most famous. Should also be used for any [[fan character|fan characters]] created as one such experiment, as well as [[alternate species|interpretations of non-experiment characters as one of these creatures]], such as [[Lilo Pelekai]] (see [[lilo_pelekai_(experiment)]] for instances of her in particular as an experiment).\r\n\r\nExperiments—whose designs have some basis in Earth creatures—tend to have pudgy limbs, almond-shaped [[black eyes|black]] or single-colored eyes, oblong heads, claws, [[rabbit]]-like ears, [[canine]] noses, markings on their bodies, and a unique [[countershading]] style on their torsos and faces (especially around the eyes which may be rimmed above by eyebrows like with their creator). Several of them also have [[antennae (anatomy)|antennae]] and [[multi limbs|multiple limbs]], which may be retractable. That said, not every experiment has each and every one of these design traits (e.g. [[Mr. Stenchy]] has eyes with visible irises and white sclera, [[Clip (Lilo and Stitch)|Clip]] has no countershading, and neither of them have noses or ears).\r\n\r\nh4.Tagged canon experiments\r\nWhile all of the first 626 experiments were named in [i]Leroy & Stitch[/i] (2006), only experiments who appeared in the franchise and have unique character tags here are listed in the sectioned tables below. A full list (divided by series) of experiments can be seen on either \"Fandom\":https://liloandstitch.fandom.com/wiki/Experiments or \"TV Tropes\":http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Characters/LiloAndStitchExperiments.\r\n\r\nExperiments who only appeared in the [i][[Stitch!]][/i] anime need to be tagged with the [[stitch!]] tag. (Note the exclamation point to avoid tagging Stitch by mistake if he doesn't appear.) These such experiments have their numbers [u]underlined[/u] in the lists below.\r\n\r\n[section=0-Series (\"Oh-Series\")]\r\nJumba's test batch, which includes many household helpers.\r\n[ltable]\r\nNo.|Name|Tag [sup]if necessary[/sup]|Notes\r\n[u]000[/u] |Cyber |[[cyber_(stitch!)]] |From the [i][[Stitch!]][/i] anime, \"Experiment Zero\" is technically unnumbered and doesn't belong in any experiment series; he's only placed here for convenience.\r\n001 |Shrink |[[shrink_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n002 |[[Doubledip]] | | \r\n007 |Gigi (a.k.a. \"Yapper\") |[[gigi_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n[u]009[/u] |Pop |[[pop_(stitch!)]] | \r\n010 |Felix |[[felix_(lilo_and_stitch)]] |Also called \"Oscar\" depending on his programming.\r\n014 |Kernel |[[kernel_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n020 |Slick |[[slick_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n[u]022[/u] |[[Hertz Donut]] | | \r\n025 |Topper |[[topper_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n029 |Checkers |[[checkers_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n031 |[[Gotchu]] | | \r\n032 |[[Fibber]] | | \r\n033 |[[Hammerface]] (a.k.a. \"Hammerhead\")| | \r\n036 |Poki |[[poki_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n040 |Backhoe |[[backhoe_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n044 |Forehead |[[forehead_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n[u]047[/u] |Lorider |[[lorider_(stitch!)]] | \r\n051 |[[Hocker]] | | \r\n052 |Coco |[[coco_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | From a [i]Disney Adventures[/i] comic.\r\n054 |Fudgy |[[fudgy_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n062 |Frenchfry |[[frenchfry_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n[u]074[/u] |[[Welko]] | | \r\n077 |[[Zawp]] | | \r\n086 |Clink |[[clink_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n089 |Skip |[[skip_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | |\r\n[/ltable]\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=1-Series (\"One-Series\")]\r\nCivic disturbances.\r\n[ltable]\r\nNo.|Name|Tag [sup]if necessary[/sup]|Notes\r\n102 |[[Stopgo]] | | \r\n103 |Stamen |[[stamen_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n110 |Squeak |[[squeak_(lilo_and_stitch)]] | \r\n111 |Mulch |[[mulch_(lilo_and_stitch)]] |