            "wiki_preview": "A vampire is an [[undead]] that feeds on the blood of the living. When an especially cruel person di...",
            "wiki_body": "A vampire is an [[undead]] that feeds on the blood of the living. When an especially cruel person dies, they can sometimes be offered a pact wherein they can escape hell by returning as a vampire to spread misery and pain. A condion of this is that they must feed on the blood of living people. Vampires can, through a ritual, cause a victim they feel close to-a lover, a son or daughter, a dear friend- become a vampire; and can raise their victims as lesser vampires, which are little better than [[zombie]]s. However, it is not unheard of for vampires to have been raised unwillingly, by irresponsible sires or foolish [[Necromancer]]s; vampires are themselves often necromancers. \r\n\r\nVampires have the ability to command [[bat|bats]] and [[wolf|wolves]] by thought, discorporate into vapour, shapechange into animals, control the minds of humans by eye contact, and fly unaided. Vampires can be warded away by garlic and crucifixes; and need permission to enter a home that doesn't belong to them. A spike or stake of wood of a fruit-bearing tree or silver stabbed into the heart can kill weak or lesser vampires; for greater vampires, the stake simply paralyzes them. The head must be removed, and the holes in the neck must be stuffed with rose flowers; the two parts must then be burned and scattered in a river."
