            "wiki_body": "A [[humanoid]] with wings. \r\nUsually tagged in combination with more specific species such as [[angel]] or [[harpy]], but can be tagged by itself for generic winged humanoids.\r\n\r\n[sub]\"Biologically improbable due to human bone and muscle structure, and if they're intended for actual flight, you may have to write off several laws of physics as well.\" - TV Tropes[/sub]\r\n\r\nMake sure to tag the related humanoid in addition to this tag, unless this refers to a generic humanoid that has wings.\r\n\r\nh4. Body parted humanoids\r\n* [[horned_humanoid]]\r\n* [b]winged_humanoid[/b]\r\n* [[tailed_humanoid]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related humanoids\r\n\r\n* [[angel_humanoid]]\r\n* [[avian_humanoid]]\r\n** [[bird_humanoid]]\r\n* [[demon_humanoid]]\r\n* [[fairy_humanoid]]\r\n* [[harpy_humanoid]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related species\r\n\r\n* [[angel]] and [[demon]] - Not always humanoid. \r\n* [[fairy]]\r\n* [[harpy]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[biped]]\r\n* [[wings]]\r\n** [[feathered_wings]]\r\n** [[membranous_wings]]"
