            "wiki_body": "[quote]\nh3. Tag Under Debate\nThe future of this tag is under debate. See topic #54387 for discussion.\n[/quote]\n\nA succubus (plural: [[succubi]]) is a female [[demon]] that feeds on lustful emotions, semen, and ultimately the souls of human men by seducing them. They take the form of beautiful women of loose morals. Succubi can sometimes be encountered by men who suffer from sleep paralysis.\n\nIts male counterpart is an [[incubus]]. The offspring of a succubus and an incubus is a cambion.\n\n\nh3. Succubus properties\nThe [i]succubus[/i] tag can sometime be used to describe the attitude of a character about sex.\n\n* saying to be a succubus\n* [[seductive]]\n* [[hypnosis]] for sex\n* [[petted_silly]] or [[fucked_silly]]\n* [[energy_drain]]\n* result of completely [[exhausted]] partner\n\n\nh3. Classical succubus appearance\n[section,expanded]\nthumb #5391250 thumb #2790931 thumb #2763094\n\nThey usually have a human face, [[horn|horns]], and a [[spade tail]]. They can have different skin colors and sometimes [[membranous wings]].\n\nh5. Related tags:\n* [[demon_humanoid]]\n* [[female]]\n* [[horn]]\n* [[tail]]\n** [[spade_tail]]\n\nh4. Not to be confused with\n* [[demon|Demons]] with either sufficiently visible [[snout]], [[fur]], [[furry_tail]], [[spikes_(anatomy)|spikes]] on the body, or any other animal/[[monster|monstrous]] characteristic other than horn, tail, wings or other skin color.\n* An [[anthro]] [[goat]], or another anthro with fur and horns\n\nh5. Examples of [b]NOT succubus[/b]\nthumb #2943138 thumb #4881265 thumb #3121119 thumb #2208254 thumb #2482624\n\n[/section]\n\n\nh3. See also\n* topic #54387 - should succubus be alias to [[demon]] or not ?"
