            "wiki_body": "thumb #249084 thumb #544798 thumb #2961923 thumb #4316368 \r\n\r\n[b]Gargoyles[/b] are [[monster|monsters]] inspired by the \"architecture of the same name\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gargoyle. They are said to be [[rock|stone]] [[statue|statues]] during the [[day]] [i](due to [[petrification]])[/i] and [[transformation|come to life]] during the [[night]].\r\n\r\nThese creatures are typically depicted with [[demonic]] features, which include [[bat wings]], [[claws]], [[demon]] [[horn|horns]], and a [[tail]] (which may or may not be [[spade tail|spaded]]). The color of their bodies can vary, but is very often [[grey body|grey]] like rock when they are petrified.\r\n\r\nThey also tend to be shown [[crouching]] or [[perching|perched]] at the top of tall buildings (such as [[cathedral|cathedrals]]).\r\n\r\nThese monsters are prominently featured in the animated TV series [i][[Gargoyles]][/i], the [i][[Gargoyle's Quest]][/i] duology, and [i][[Demon's Crest]][/i].\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[anthro]]\r\n* [[clawed_fingers]] / [[finger_claws]]\r\n* [[crouching]]\r\n* [[humanoid]] \r\n* [[living_statue]] – For when a gargoyle has a stony body even while active.\r\n* [[monster]]\r\n* [[perching]]\r\n* [[petrification]] – Noun of the “stone [[transformation]]”.\r\n* [[sculpture]] / [[statue]]\r\n* [[stone]]\r\n* [[stone_body]] – When a gargoyle's body is entirely in stone.\r\n* [[wings]]"
