            "wiki_body": "[color=species][b]MalO[/b][/color], plural [color=species][b]MalOs[/b][/color], are a fictional species established by the author [color=artist]LurkD[/color] in their [i][[SCP Foundation]][/i] story [i]SCP-1471 — MalO ver1.0.0[/i], and the reception of said story by fans. In general, MalO are [[anthro|anthropomorphic]] [[canine|canines]] with a [[skull head]] or [[exposed skull]]. They also have dark colored [[hair]], [[fur]], and ears (often black and/or grey), and [[empty eyes|empty]] [[white eyes]] set in dark eye sockets or [[black sclera|sclera]], but appearances may vary.\r\n\r\nThe design of MalOs originated in [[2011]] with the concept of a [[zombie]] [[werewolf]] with loose incorporation of the \"[i]gjenganger[/i]\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gjenganger of [[Scandinavian folklore]]; specifically with [[Breynz (Tarangryph)|Breynz]], an original character belonging to cosplayer [color=artist]Tarangryph[/color] who commissioned a fursuit from [[Qarrezel]]. On October 29th, 2011, Tarangryph photographed herself dressed as Breynz at a hotel anticipating MCM London Expo, a picture titled \"“Don't open the door...”\":https://www.furaffinity.net/view/6770853/ \r\n\r\nCirca [[2013]], LurkD found and was inspired by “Don't open the door...” to write an SCP entry around it; from this they produced [i]SCP-1471 — MalO ver1.0.0[/i], coining the name MalO for [[SCP-1471-A]]. After being posted February 23rd, 2023, the use of MalOs as a species name can be found as early as March 1st in [[Fantem]]'s tale \"[i]Capone[/i]\":https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/capone, the potentially first fanwork of LurkD's story. Due to rise in SCP-1471-A's popularity, especially in the [i]SCP Foundation[/i]'s Furry demographic, and encouraged by the canonical prospect of multiple SCP-1471-As, multiple [[fan character|fan characters]] have been made and cemented an interpretation of MalO as a species. \r\n\r\nDue to [[SCP-1471]] being specified as a \"[[MalO 1.0|version 1.0.0]]\", explorations of MalO subspecies in the form of older and newer versions have been made; such as [[MalO 0.9]] and [[MalO 1.1]] (both created by [[Keadonger]]) or [[MalO 2.0]] (by SCP_1471_TTV).\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=MalOs]\r\n\r\n* \"[[Capone (Fantem)|Capone]]\" — © [[Fantem]]\r\n* \"[[Cassandra (Fantem)|Cassandra]]\" — © Fantem\r\n* \"[[Malc0m]]\" — © [[Keadonger]]\r\n* [[MalO v2.0]] — © SCP_1471_TTV\r\n* \"[[SAMI (whisperfoot)|SAMI]]\" — © [[whisperfoot]]\r\n* [[SCP-1471-A (CumminHam)|SCP-1471-A]] — © [[CumminHam]]\r\n* [[SCP-1471-A (da.nilkaz)|SCP-1471-A]] — © [[da.nilkaz]]\r\n* [[SCP-1471-A (Furromantic)|SCP-1471-A]] — © [[Furromantic]]\r\n* [[SCP-1471-A-37]] \"Marsh\" — © [[victordantes]]\r\n* [[SCP-1471-A-52]] \"Sabrina\" — © [[hawtlava]]\r\n* [[SCP-1471-A-96]] \"Yuki\" — © YukiTheMalO\r\n* [[SCP-1471-A-1088]] \"Mel0dy\" — © CoyoteJeeper7\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4.External Links\r\n* \"DeviantArt\":https://www.deviantart.com\r\n** \"Don't open the door...\":https://www.deviantart.com/tarangryph/art/Don-t-open-the-door-266339027\r\n** \"Genganger\":https://www.deviantart.com/qarrezel/art/Genganger-253977442\r\n* \"FurAffinity\":https://www.furaffinity.net\r\n** \"London Expo - Don't open the door...\":https://www.furaffinity.net/view/6770853/\r\n* \"SCP Foundation Wikidot\":https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com\r\n** \"SCP-1471 — MalO ver1.0.0\":https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-1471\r\n** \"Capone\":https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/capone"
