            "wiki_body": "thumb #283394 thumb #890864 thumb #1033423\r\n\r\n[b]Fennekin[/b] (Japanese: フォッコ Fokko) is a Fire-type [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] from [[generation_6_pokemon|Generation VI]]. It is the fourth Pokémon in the [i]Pokémon X and Y[/i] games.\r\n\r\nAlongside [[Chespin]] and [[Froakie]], it is part of the [[Starter trio]] of the Kalos region.\r\n\r\n[b]Fennekin[/b] evolves from level 16 into [[Braixen]], which evolves from level 36 into [[Delphox]].\r\n\r\nh4.Biology\r\n\r\n[b]Fennekin[/b] is a small Pokémon that – as its name suggests – looks like a [[fennec]]. It is mainly covered in yellow fur, which is longer on its hips. It has a white muzzle with a tuft of fur on each cheek, large orange eyes and a pointed black nose. \r\n\r\nThis Pokémon has two pointed teeth on its upper jaw, visible when [b]Fennekin[/b] opens its mouth. Tufts of orange fur are tucked inside its large ears. It has small, slender paws with no visible toes, also its tail is fluffy with an orange tip.\r\n\r\n[b]Fennekin[/b] is inspired by the fennec. It also shares similarities with the [[kitsune]], a mythical [[fox]] from Japanese folklore that can generate fire from its tail or mouth and is often associated with \"witchcraft\":https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Witchcraft\r\n\r\nIt releases hot air from its ears, which can reach temperatures of over 200 degrees Celsius [i](≈ 392 degrees Fahrenheit)[/i]... [b]Fennekin[/b] uses this ability to intimidate its opponents.\r\n\r\nIt can also be a little temperamental, but is very loyal to its trainer.\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|pokémon]]\r\n** fennekin\r\n*** [[braixen]]\r\n**** [[delphox]]"
