            "wiki_body": "thumb #13697 thumb #54081\r\n\r\nThe [b]fox spirit[/b] ([i]狐狸精[/i]) or [b]nine-tailed fox[/b] ([i]九尾狐[/i]) is a mythical [[fox]] entity originating from [[Chinese mythology]] and later seen commonly in multiple forms within [[East Asian mythology]]. In East Asian folklore, they are depicted as [[spirit]] possessed fox-like creatures, capable of utilizing [[magic|magical powers]]. These fox creatures are depicted as mischievous tricksters, often having abilities such as the ability to disguise themselves.\r\n\r\nNote that, for a post to be appropriately tagged with this tag ([b]if not already tagged via other implications[/b]), the post must [i]explicitly depict a mythical, eastern asian, and/or magical fox spirit being[/i]. This is [b]NOT[/b] to be used on posts simply involving normal foxes and/or foxes that happen to have multiple tails; {{fox}} and/or {{fox multi_tail}} are more appropriate.\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Species\r\n* [[kitsune]]\r\n* [[huli_jing]]\r\n* [[kumiho]]\r\n* [[nogitsune]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[asian_mythology]]\r\n** [[east_asian_mythology]]\r\n*** fox_spirit\r\n* [[fox]]\r\n* [[kitsunebi]]\r\n* [[yōkai]]"
