            "wiki_body": "thumb #1338427 thumb #1368598\r\nIn Greek and Roman mythology, harpies were an all-female species in the form of a bird with a human face. \r\n\r\nNowadays harpies are common in fantasy literature and games. They're also heavily featured in the [[monster_girl_(genre)|monster girl]] genre. While most are still female, other genders are not completely unheard of.\r\n\r\nHarpies are [[humanoid]] by default. Most designs should be tagged as [[harpy humanoid]] instead.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[winged_humanoid]]\r\n* [[wings]]\r\n** [[winged_arms]]\r\n** [[feather_hands]]\r\n** [[realistic_wings]]\r\n* [[animal_legs]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[siren]]\r\n* [[sphinx]]\r\n* [[centaur]]\r\n* [[gryphon]]\r\n* [[chimera_(mythology)]]"
