            "wiki_preview": "thumb #3965237 thumb #4068412 thumb #2223174\r\n\r\n[b]Samurott[/b] (Japanese: ダイケンキ Daikenki) is a Wate...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #3965237 thumb #4068412 thumb #2223174\r\n\r\n[b]Samurott[/b] (Japanese: ダイケンキ Daikenki) is a Water-type [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] introduced in [[generation_5_pokemon|Generation V]].\r\n\r\nIt evolves from [[Dewott]] starting at level 36. It is the final form of [[Oshawott]].\r\n\r\n[i](In Hisui, [b]Samurott[/b] has a dual-type Water/Dark regional form. It evolves from Dewott starting at level 36. It is the final form of Oshawott in the Hisui region.)[/i]\r\n\r\n[b]Samurott[/b] is a quadrupedal Pokémon resembling a river [[otter]] or [[sea lion]]. Its head, dorsal coat, and limbs are royal blue, and its underbelly is a dull bluish-gray. It has pointed canine teeth, and a red nose, and its eyes have white sclera and circular red irises. Long white [[whiskers]] resembling [[mustache|mustaches]] extend from its snout and lower jaw.\r\n[i](These whiskers look like a [[beard]])[/i]\r\n\r\n[b]Samurott[/b] possesses three black claws on each limb, and a fin-like tail resembling a war fan. Its head, limbs, and tail are adorned with cream-colored armor resembling seashells. The armor on its head resembles a spiked conch shell. \r\n\r\nThis helmet-like armor is bulbous in the back, and tapers into a spear-like horn in the front. Segmented armor resembling bracers covers each of this Pokémon's limbs. \r\nThe forelimbs' bracers contain shell swords called seamitars. The two lower segments of these bracers serve as scabbards for these seamitars, and the upper segment and spike are the seamitars' blade and handle, respectively.\r\n\r\n[i]([[shiny_pokemon|Shiny]] [b]Samurott[/b] is darker shade of blue.)[/i]\r\n\r\n[i](Also, this Pokémon is [[feral]] in its canon form.)[/i]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[blue_body]]\r\n* [[horn]]\r\n* [[quadruped]]\r\n* [[tail_fin]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|pokémon]]\r\n** [[oshawott]]\r\n*** [[dewott]]\r\n**** samurott\r\n**** [[hisuian_samurott]], a regional form introduced in [i]Pokémon Legends: Arceus[/i]\r\n* \"Bulbapedia: Samurott\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Samurott"
