            "wiki_preview": "thumb #1000233 thumb #3306380 thumb #2987942 thumb #1621288\r\n\r\n[b]Grovyle[/b] (Japanese: ジュプトル Jupti...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1000233 thumb #3306380 thumb #2987942 thumb #1621288\r\n\r\n[b]Grovyle[/b] (Japanese: ジュプトル Juptile) is a Grass-type Pokémon introduced in [[generation_3_pokemon|Generation III]].\r\n\r\nIt evolves from [[Treecko]] starting at level 16 and evolves into [[Sceptile]] starting at level 36.\r\n\r\n[b]Grovyle[/b] is a bipedal [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] similar in appearance to a \"theropod\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theropoda. It is primarily green with a red underside. There is a belt-like green stripe across its belly.\r\nThis Pokémon's hands have two clawed fingers and powerful legs with birdlike feet. Its well-developed muscles make it an expert climber and allow it to leap quickly from branch to branch. \r\n\r\n[b]Grovyle[/b] has three long leaves on its wrists, a large leaf on top of its head, and two tails that have a leafy appearance. This leafy appearance allows it to be camouflaged in the forests where it lives.\r\n\r\n(In the [i][[Pokémon Mystery Dungeon]]: Explorers[/i] spin-off, a special [b]Grovyle[/b] nammed [b]\"[[Grovyle_the_thief|Grovyle the Thief]]\"[/b] appears in the game; his distinctive feature is that he has a brown satchel)\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|pokémon]]\r\n** [[treecko]]\r\n*** grovyle\r\n**** [[sceptile]]\r\n***** [[mega_sceptile]]"
