            "kor": "",
            "count": 1845,
            "wiki_preview": "This tag should only be used for the fantasy species known as a [b]troll[/b]. Trolls are generally d...",
            "wiki_body": "This tag should only be used for the fantasy species known as a [b]troll[/b]. Trolls are generally depicted as [[humanoid|humanoids]] with regenerative abilities, often seen as allies to [[orc|Orcs]] and enemies to [[human|Humans]].\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[shitpost]] - Images or animations deliberately intended to harass or annoy a person or group of people on the Internet, taken from the term 'trolling', a form of fishing in which a wide net is cast and dragged behind a fishing boat, in the hopes of catching as many fish as possible. Similarly, troll images tend to be incredibly generalized, so as to offend the maximum number of victims. \r\n\r\n* [[trolling]] - A troll may refer to a character trolling another. Likewise, such images may also contain the [[trollface]].\r\n\r\nExamples of troll tags on e621 include [[the_truth]], and [[uncanny_valley]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[troll_(homestuck)]] - The gray-skinned race from the webcomic [[homestuck]]."
