            "wiki_preview": "thumb #166532 thumb #310622 thumb #1458084 thumb #988048 \r\n\r\nBasically, creatures that possess both ...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #166532 thumb #310622 thumb #1458084 thumb #988048 \r\n\r\nBasically, creatures that possess both fungal and animal or humanoid characteristics.\r\n\r\nThese can be divided in three categories:\r\n\r\n(1) Fungi -usually mushrooms- with animal or humanoid features (eyes, mouth, limbs etc). \r\n\r\n(2-a) Animals or humanoids with remarkable fungal structures (hypha, mushroom, mildew etc). \r\n\r\n(2-b) Animals or humanoids and fungi physically integrated into them acting as a single being.\r\n\r\n\r\nh4.Observations:\r\n\r\n* The simple presence of fungi growing over the character's body usually isn't enough to make the tag applicable (especially seen in case of [[flora fauna]] or [[undead]]).\r\n\r\n* Some features may denote the integration of the fungal parts into the character's bodily structure such as: shared colors, luminescence or texture; an average (or higher) number of these parts and the presence of a single type of them.\r\n\r\nh4.Related tags:\r\n* [[fungus]]\r\n* [[mushroom]]\r\n* [[matango]]\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n* [[flora_fauna]]\r\n* [[mineral_fauna]]\r\n* [[food_creature]]"
