            "wiki_preview": "thumb #437118 thumb #3279363 thumb #2865125\r\n\r\n[b]Mudkip[/b] (Japanese: ミズゴロウ Mizugorou) is a Water-...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #437118 thumb #3279363 thumb #2865125\r\n\r\n[b]Mudkip[/b] (Japanese: ミズゴロウ Mizugorou) is a Water-type Pokémon introduced in [[generation_3_pokemon|Generation III]].\r\n\r\nIt evolves into [[Marshtomp]] starting at level 16, which evolves into [[Swampert]] starting at level 36.\r\n\r\nAlong with [[Treecko]] and [[Torchic]], [b]Mudkip[/b] is one of three [[starter_trio|starter Pokémon]] of Hoenn available at the beginning of [i]Pokémon Ruby, Sapphire, Emerald, Omega Ruby, and Alpha Sapphire[/i].\r\n\r\n[b]Mudkip[/b] is a small, amphibious, quadrupedal Pokémon. It has a blue body with a light blue underside. This Pokémon has a large head with a blue fin on top and a light-blue tail fin. It has black, beady eyes and orange, star-shaped gills on its cheeks.\r\n\r\nBy using the fin on its head, it can detect changes in air and water currents as well as bodies of water. Its fin can also point in a certain direction, as seen in the anime. Despite its small size, [b]Mudkip[/b] is a very strong Pokémon. \r\n\r\n[b]Mudkip[/b] is more commonly found in captivity, though it can be found in swamps and other wetlands. In the wild, it sleeps by burying itself in the mud soil at the water's edge or bottom of a river.\r\n\r\nThey are also classified as the Mud Fish Pokémon.\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|pokémon]]\r\n** mudkip\r\n*** [[marshtomp]]\r\n**** [[swampert]]\r\n***** [[mega_swampert]]"
