            "wiki_body": "thumb #3074322 thumb #2462737 thumb #4776962\r\n\r\nA non-living object in the shape or likeness of a living one. Living versions should be tagged as [[animate inanimate]] instead.\r\n\r\nDue to their nature, they don't increase the post's character count with their presence. (eg.: A post depicting a child and their doll should not be tagged as [[duo]] as there is only one character present in the post).\r\n\r\nRegardless of this, their presence warrants that their name be tagged as well if their likeness was based on a named character or the inanimate itself alone has canonically been given a name of their own.\r\n\r\nh4. Inanimate concepts\r\n* [[doll]]\r\n* [[plushie]]\r\n* [[snowman]]\r\n* [[statue]]\r\n* Objects shaped like creatures. For instance a [[wall clock]] with cat ears.\r\n* Objects with facial features that would not fall under a print tag such as [[head print]]."
