            "wiki_body": "thumb #237058 thumb #70786 thumb #34729\r\n\r\nThe Thylacine, also known as the Tasmanian Tiger or Tasmanian Wolf, was the largest known carnivorous marsupial. Its two common names came from its striped lower back and its [[canid]]-like characteristics.\r\n\r\nThe last known living specimen of the species died in captivity on September 7, 1938 due to neglect. Numerous unconfirmed sightings have been reported after its extinction date, however, leaving many to believe that the Thylacine may still exist.\r\n\r\nh5. Not to be confused with [[Tasmanian devil]].\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n\r\n* [[mammal]]\r\n** [[marsupial]]\r\n*** thylacine"
