            "wiki_body": "thumb #1348277 thumb #2499777 thumb #1167689 thumb #2049374\r\nA cartoon style prevalent during the Silent Age of Animation between the mid 1920's and 1930's. Inkblot characters are commonly known for their simplistic design, inky black bodies, [[dot eyes]], white faces and tubular limbs which ends in bulbus hands and feet. They are also well known for always wearing white [[gloves]].\r\n\r\nh2.Examples\r\nFamous names from the time period are [[Mickey Mouse]], [[Popeye]], [[Betty Boop]] and [[Felix the Cat]].\r\nThe Warner siblings ([[Yakko_warner|Yakko]], [[wakko_warner|Wakko]] and [[dot_warner|Dot]]) from [[Animaniacs]] were also based on this style.\r\nRecent examples of this style includes [[Bendy]] from [[Bendy and the Ink Machine]] and many characters from [[cuphead_(game)|Cuphead]]."
