            "wiki_preview": "thumb #1600835 thumb #3359804 thumb #562299 thumb #4340362\r\n\r\nSource: <https://bulbapedia.bulbagarde...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1600835 thumb #3359804 thumb #562299 thumb #4340362\r\n\r\nSource: <https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Oshawott_(Pokémon)>\r\n\r\n[b]Oshawott[/b] (Japanese: ミジュマル Mijumaru) is a Water-type [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] introduced in [[generation_5_pokemon|Generation V]].\r\n\r\nIt evolves into [[Dewott]] starting at level 17, which evolves into [[Samurott]] starting at level 36.\r\n\r\n[i](In Hisui, it evolves into Dewott starting at level 17, which evolves into [[Hisuian Samurott]] starting at level 36.)[/i]\r\n\r\nAlong with [[Snivy]] and [[Tepig]], [b]Oshawott[/b] is one of the three [[starter_trio|starter Pokémon]] of Unova available at the beginning of [i]Pokémon Black, White, Black 2, and White 2[/i].\r\n\r\n[b]Oshawott[/b] is also one of the three starter Pokémon of Hisui in [[pokemon_legends_arceus|Pokémon Legends: Arceus]], alongside [[Rowlet]] and [[Cyndaquil]].\r\n\r\n[b]Oshawott[/b] is a bipedal sea [[otter]]-like Pokémon. It has a spherical white head with small, triangular dark-blue ears on the sides. Its eyes are dark, and its dark-orange nose is shaped like a horizontal oval. Several freckles cover its cheeks which may be premature whiskers, and two pointed teeth can be seen when it opens its mouth. \r\n\r\nThe light blue fur on its body forms bubble shapes around its neck. Its arms are white and rounded, while its feet are dark blue with three toes each. It also possesses a rudder-like dark blue tail. It carries a pale yellow seashell called a \"scalchop\" on its belly.\r\n\r\nThis shell is made of the same material as its claws and is used for both battles and cracking hard berries. This Pokémon wields the shell like a knife. It uses the scalchop to block the moves of its enemies before slashing back at them in swift retaliation. \r\n\r\n[b]Oshawott[/b] learned to how maintain its scalchop with riverbed stones by copying the humans it observes using whetstones. If the scalchop is heavily damaged or lost, Oshawott can grow a new one from its navel.\r\n\r\n[i]([[shiny_pokemon|Shiny]] [b]Oshawott[/b]'s torso is sky blue; difficult to tell apart from the normal color.)[/i]\r\n\r\nOshawot is [[anthro]] (with [[semi-anthro]] subtag) in its canon form, but the species is often depicted as further [[anthrofied]].\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with:\r\n\r\n* [[lutrine]] (a.k.a otter)\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[biped]]\r\n* [[seashell]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|pokémon]]\r\n** oshawott\r\n*** [[dewott]]\r\n**** [[samurott]]\r\n**** [[hisuian_samurott]]"
