            "wiki_body": "thumb #2359315\n\nA Greek and Roman forest deity, with lower body of a goat and upper body of a human with the exception of usually carrying goat horns and/or ears. Often associated with the Greek god Pan.\n\nh4. Not to be confused with\n\n* [[faun_(spyro)]] - A species from the [[Spyro the Dragon]] universe of the same name. While the original model of this species more closely resembles a traditional faun, the redesigned version, and most artist depictions are fully [[anthro]]. Depictions of this species more typically resemble a [[cervid]] than a [[goat]].\n\nh4. Related tags\n\n* [[animal_legs]]\n* [[biped]]\n* [[hooves]]\n* [[horn]]\n** [[2_horns]]\n** [[head_horn]]\n* [[split_form]]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[satyr]]\n"
