            "wiki_body": "thumb #2079659 thumb #4686772 thumb #3926473\r\n\r\n[b]Rillaboom[/b] (Japanese: [b]ゴリランダー[/b] [i]Gorirander[/i]) is a Grass-type [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] introduced in [[Generation_8_pokemon|Generation VIII]].\r\n\r\nIt is the final form of [[Grookey]] and it evolves from [[Thwackey]] starting at level 35.\r\n\r\n[b]Rillaboom[/b] is a [[biped|bipedal]] Pokémon with a resemblance to an [[ape]] or a [[gorilla]]. Its body is mainly mud-colored. It has a large orange snout with a dark brown nose, which is also present on its ears and around its orange eyes with white pupils. \r\n\r\nIts forehead is light brown, as are its torso, [[abs]], hands and [[feet]]. It also has [[butterfly]]-shaped [[markings]] on each shoulder of the same color. \r\nThis Pokémon has thick [[leaf_hair|leafy hair]] coming out of the back of its head, with a single [[vine]] in front of its face (like a frezzy strand). \r\nIt also has a \"[[belt]]\" and \"[[cuffs]]\" made of [[leaf|leaves]]... \r\n\r\n[b]Rillaboom[/b] always carries a large [[drum]] on its back, which it puts in front of itself in battle. This drum is created from a [[tree stump]] from which four thick [[branch]]es protrude...\r\n\r\nThis Pokémon's appearance is inspired by a popular representation of a [[drummer]], particularly a [[taiko]] player. Also, its behavior may refer to the fact that gorillas beat their [[chest]]s rhythmically to show social [[dominant|dominance]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|pokémon_(species)]]\r\n** [[grookey]]\r\n*** [[thwackey]]\r\n**** [b]rillaboom[/b]\r\n** [[cinderace]]\r\n** [[inteleon]]"
