            "tag": "chesnaught",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 847,
            "wiki_preview": "thumb #799360 thumb #403957 thumb #2836552\r\n\r\n[b]Chesnaught[/b] (Japanese: ブリガロン Brigarron) is a dua...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #799360 thumb #403957 thumb #2836552\r\n\r\n[b]Chesnaught[/b] (Japanese: ブリガロン Brigarron) is a dual-type Grass/Fighting [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] introduced in [[generation_6_pokemon|Generation VI]].\r\n\r\nIt evolves from [[Quilladin]] starting at level 36 and it's the final evolution of [[Chespin]].\r\n\r\nh4.Biology\r\n\r\n[b]Chesnaught[/b] is a bipedal, mammal-like Pokémon that shares similarities with plants. The white fur on its belly rises to its face, where it gives the illusion of a [[beard]]. It has a small red nose with a tuft of brown fur on its snout. \r\n\r\nOn top of its head, this Pokémon wears a beige armor plate that acts as a [[helmet]]. Its back is mostly covered by a beige, dome-shaped [[carapace]] that serves as [[armor]], similar to a chestnut, with four spines down its back. This carapace is bordered by a small red stripe and then a larger green border. Two further spines protrude from each of its shoulders, which are connected by a green [[breastplate]]. \r\n\r\nIts body is the same color as its carapace. Its upper arms and tail are covered in green armor, with two small spines on each arm. It has three brown claws on each paw.\r\n\r\nLike its two previous evolutions, [b]Chesnaught[/b] was inspired by the [[hedgehog]] and a \"chestnut\":https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chestnut\r\nIt was probably also inspired by other mammals who have a armor...\r\n\r\nIt is also inspired by a [[knight]], and more generally by various pieces of armor such as the \"brigandine\":https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brigandine , the \"barbute\":https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbute or from a more modern point of view, a \"bulletproof vest\":https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bulletproof_vest\r\n\r\nWhat's more, when considered alongside other [[starter_trio|starter Pokémon]] ([[Delphox]] and [[Greninja]]) of the Région inspirée de la France, it seems to be inspired by the warrior character class or by the Tank class in RPG, its Fighting type and its chivalrous appearance and heavy armor.\r\n\r\n[b]Chesnaught[/b] is renowned for having a body as tough as a tank. It can turn over a truck weighing over fifty tons. Finally, when it strikes its defensive pose with its muscular arms in front of its head, this big Pokémon can withstand a bomb blast.\r\n\r\nIts [[shiny_pokemon|Shiny]] counterpart has dark green plating and is overall much darker in color.\r\n\r\n[b]Chesnaught[/b] is always depicted as an [[anthro]] and often as [[anthrofied]]. Finally, this Starter is very often represented as a [[male]].\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[biped]]\r\n* [[chest_tuft]]\r\n* [[green_body]]\r\n* [[shell]]\r\n* [[spikes]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|pokémon]]\r\n** [[chespin]]\r\n*** [[quilladin]]\r\n**** chesnaught\r\n* \"Bulbapedia: Chesnaught\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Chesnaught"
          },
