            "wiki_preview": "thumb #1600834 thumb #2602231 thumb #2877110 thumb #2456311\n\nSource: <https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1600834 thumb #2602231 thumb #2877110 thumb #2456311\n\nSource: <https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Tepig_(Pokémon)>\n\n[b]Tepig[/b] (Japanese: ポカブ Pokabu) is a Fire-type [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] introduced in [[generation_5_pokemon|Generation V]].\n\nIt evolves into [[Pignite]] starting at level 17, which evolves into [[Emboar]] starting at level 36.\n\nAlong with [[Snivy]] and [[Oshawott]], [b]Tepig[/b] is one of the three [[starter_trio|starter Pokémon]] of Unova available at the beginning of [i]Pokémon Black, White, Black 2, and White 2[/i]. It is also one of the starter Pokémon available in the upcoming game \"[i]Pokémon Legends: Z-A[/i]\":http://e621.net/wiki_pages/pokemon_legends_z-a, this time alongside [[Chikorita]] and [[Totodile]].\n\n[b]Tepig[/b] is a quadrupedal, [[porcine|pig]]-like Pokémon that is primarily orange. It has oval eyes, a red nose, and a thick yellow stripe on its snout. The upper portion of its head is dark brown, and its long, pointed ears are positioned closely together. \nThis Pokémon has short legs, and its front feet are dark brown. A dark brown band covers its lower back and rear. Its curly tail is tipped with a ruddy red sphere.\n\n[b]Tepig[/b] is a nimble Pokémon capable of blowing fire from its snout. It can use its speed to both dodge and confound enemies before striking back. Instead of flames, it will spout thick, black smoke when ill. This Pokémon is a well-known ravenous glutton for food. \n[b]Tepig[/b] will roast berries before eating them but occasionally gets overexcited and burns them.\n\nThey are also classified as the Fire Pig Pokémon.\n\nh4.Fun Fact:\n\nThere's a furry artist called [[tepigfan101|Tepig Fan 101]] who [i]- as his name suggests -[/i] owns a fursona and the majority of his posts are about [b]Tepig[/b].\n\nh4. See Also:\n\n* [[pokemon_(species)|pokémon]]\n** tepig\n*** [[pignite]]\n**** [[emboar]]"
