            "wiki_preview": "A fictional race that inhabits the Star Trek Universe.  Caitians are a warp capable race and are par...",
            "wiki_body": "A fictional race that inhabits the Star Trek Universe.  Caitians are a warp capable race and are part of the United Federation of Planets.  They are a feline-like humanoid species and are known to serve in all branches of the Federation.\r\n\r\nThe most prominent Caitians are Lieutenant M'Ress, who appeared in [i]Star Trek the Animated Series[/i] (1973-1974) as a semi-regular cast member, and Commander T'Ana, MD, who appears in [i]Star Trek: Lower Decks[/i] (2020-) as a more prominent supporting character. However, there have been other less prominent Caitians in the Star Trek Universe featured in the movies.\r\n\r\nIn [i]Star Trek IV: The Voyage Home[/i] a Caitian admiral can be seen in attendance at the court martial of James T. Kirk.  A second Caitian, a Commodore, can be seen attending the court martial as well.  In the 2013 re-boot sequel [i]Star Trek: Into Darkness[/i], two Catians (twins) are portrayed as having spent the night with James T. Kirk.\r\n\r\nh1.Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[star_trek_the_animated_series]]\r\n* [[m'ress]]\r\n* [[dr._t'ana]]\r\n* [[alien]]\r\n\r\nh1.Notable Caitians\r\n\r\n* [[M'Ress]]\r\n* [[Dr._T'Ana]]"
