            "wiki_body": "thumb #3807500 thumb #3981696 thumb #4251612 thumb #3819480\r\n\r\n[b]Quaquaval[/b] ([b]ウェーニバル[/b] [i]Wanival[/i]) is a dual-type Water/Fighting [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] introduced in [[generation_9_pokemon|Generation IX]]. This Pokémon is classified as the `Dancer Pokémon`.\r\n\r\nIt evolves from [[Quaxwell]] (starting at level 36) and it is the final form of [[Quaxly]].\r\n\r\nCurrently, it's the latest Pokémon [[starter_trio|Starter]].\r\n\r\nh4.Physical appearance:\r\n[b]Quaquaval[/b] is a [[biped|bipedal]] Pokémon with a [[humanoid]] appearance and features reminiscent of both a [[duck]] and a [[peacock]]. Its [[blue_feathers|indigo plumage]] seems to form a dancer outfit, particularly on its [[legs]] where it takes the form of [[pants]]. The tips of its [[feathers]] are lighter, more turquoise, and it seems to wear a [[headdress]] with [[red feathers]] at the edge of the [[beak]]. \r\n\r\nIt has large [[webbed feet]] and [[red claws]]. It has numerous [[feathers]] composed of [[water]] around this Pokémon, arranged in an arc when it fights, like the plumage of a peacock doing a \"cartwheel\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cartwheel_(gymnastics).\r\n\r\n[b]Quaquaval[/b] seems inspired by a Brazilian [[samba]] dancer. In fact, it continually performs dance steps in combat, and its cry is highly musical.\r\n\r\nh4.Related tags:\r\n* [[avian]]\r\n* [[biped]]\r\n* [[beak]]\r\n* [[blue_body]]\r\n* [[blue_eyes]]\r\n* [[blue_hair]]\r\n* [[feathered_wings]]\r\n* [[feathers]]\r\n* [[multicolored_body]]\r\n* [[tail]]\r\n* [[tail_feathers]]\r\n* [[webbed feet]] \r\n* [[white_body]]\r\n* [[white_feathers]]\r\n* [[winged_arms]]\r\n* [[wings]]\r\n* [[yellow_beak]]\r\n* [[yellow_feat]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon_(species)]]\r\n** [[Quaxly]]\r\n*** [[Quaxwell]]\r\n**** [b]Quaquaval[/b]"
