            "tag": "torchic",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 660,
            "wiki_preview": "thumb #1706038 thumb #1485232 thumb #1522076\r\n\r\nSource: <https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Tor...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1706038 thumb #1485232 thumb #1522076\r\n\r\nSource: <https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Torchic_(Pokémon)>\r\n\r\n[b]Torchic[/b] (Japanese: アチャモ Achamo) is a Fire-type Pokémon introduced in [[generation_3_pokemon|Generation III]].\r\n\r\nIt evolves into [[Combusken]] starting at level 16, which evolves into [[Blaziken]] starting at level 36.\r\n\r\nAlong with [[Treecko]] and [[Mudkip]], [b]Torchic[/b] is one of three [[starter_trio|Starter Pokémon]] of Hoenn available at the beginning of [i]Pokémon Ruby, Sapphire, Emerald, Omega Ruby, and Alpha Sapphire[/i].\r\n\r\n[b]Torchic[/b] is a small, chick [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] with stubby, downy, yellow wings. Its body is covered with orange feathers and a fluffy coat of down. There is an orange and yellow crest on its head that resembles a flame. Its two thin legs and short beak are a light brownish yellow, and the feet have three toes in front and one in the back. A male Torchic will have a small black speck on its rear that is not present in females.\r\n\r\nWithin Torchic's belly, this Pokémon has a flame sac filled with a burning fire. This internal flame causes this Pokémon to feel warm if hugged. The warmth feels similar to a warm water bottle. As long as this Pokémon is alive, the internal flame will burn continuously. When attacked, it will shoot fireballs of 1,800 °F (1,000 °C) at its foes, leaving them scorched black. It dislikes darkness, as it cannot see its surroundings. Torchic will follow its Trainer with unsteady steps. While Torchic is rarely found in the wild, it is known to inhabit grasslands.\r\n\r\nThey are also classified as the Chick Pokémon.\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|pokémon]]\r\n** torchic\r\n*** [[combusken]]\r\n**** [[blaziken]]\r\n***** [[mega_blaziken]]\r\n"
