            "wiki_preview": "[b]Ambient bats[/b] are small subtle [[bat|bats]] found off in the distance in an image. Removing an...",
            "wiki_body": "[b]Ambient bats[/b] are small subtle [[bat|bats]] found off in the distance in an image. Removing an ambient bat might make an image a little less \"creepy\", but won't change much overall.  They're mostly just there to make the world feel a little more spooky. If the main character is interacting with or touching the bat in question, it's probably not an ambient bat. Unless a non-ambient bat is also depicted, [[bat]] [color=red]SHOULD NOT[/color] be tagged.\n\n\nh4. Not to be confused with\n\n* Decorative, or symbolic depictions of bats. See [[bat_(shape)]] and [[bat_decoration]]. If you see a string attached, it is not an ambient bat.\n\nh4. Related tags\n\n* [[ambient_flier]]\n* [[ambient_silhouette]]\n* [[hanging_from_branch]]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[ambient_arthropod]]\n** [[ambient_arachnid]]\n*** [[ambient_spider]]\n** [[ambient_insect]]\n*** [[ambient_ant]]\n*** [[ambient_bee]]\n*** [[ambient_beetle]]\n*** [[ambient_butterfly]]\n*** [[ambient_dragonfly]]\n*** [[ambient_firefly]]\n*** [[ambient_fly]]\n*** [[ambient_ladybug]]\n*** [[ambient_moth]]\n** [[ambient_myriapod]]\n* [b]ambient_bat[/b]\n* [[ambient_bird]]\n** [[ambient_owl]]\n* [[ambient_fairy]]\n* [[ambient_sealife]]\n** [[ambient_barnacle]]\n** [[ambient_coral]]\n** [[ambient_crustacean]]\n** [[ambient_fish]]\n** [[ambient_jellyfish]]\n** [[ambient_starfish]]\n* [[ambient_wildlife]]\n** [[ambient_cervine]]\n** [[ambient_dragon]]\n** [[ambient_frog]]\n** [[ambient_pterosaur]]"
