            "wiki_preview": "thumb #831852\r\n\r\nJapanese kobolds are a species of small, canine-faced creatures featured in Japanes...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #831852\r\n\r\nJapanese kobolds are a species of small, canine-faced creatures featured in Japanese media like the [i][[Suikoden]][/i] series. The two most prominent examples are [[polt_(monster_musume)|Polt]] from [i][[Monster Musume]][/i] and [[illfang_the_kobold_king|Illfang]] from [i][[Sword Art Online]][/i]. The name is borrowed from the German word “kobold”, which was a mischievous [[goblin]]-like sprite in Germanic folklore. The Japanese qualifier is used here to distinguish them from the unrelated reptilian [[kobold|kobolds]] popularized by [i][[Dungeons and Dragons|Dungeons & Dragons]][/i].\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n* [[kobold]] - The species most commonly associated with the name “kobold,” these are short anthropomorphic reptilians that first appeared in [i]Dungeons & Dragons[/i].\r\n* [[kobold_(warcraft)]] - Another unrelated species that borrowed its name from German folklore, these are anthropomorphic rodents from the [i][[Warcraft]][/i] franchise.\r\n\r\n\r\n"
