            "kor": "",
            "count": 449,
            "wiki_preview": "thumb #160489\r\n\r\nA [b]wolpertinger[/b] (also called wolperdinger or woiperdinger) is a mythological ...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #160489\r\n\r\nA [b]wolpertinger[/b] (also called wolperdinger or woiperdinger) is a mythological hybrid animal from Germany.\r\n\r\nIt has a body comprising various animal parts — generally wings, antlers, tails and fangs, all attached to the body of a small mammal. The most common depiction of the creature portrays it as a [[lagomorph]] with the antlers of a [[cervine|deer]] as well as [[feathered wings]] and [[fangs]]. Often the wings themselves come from [[pheasant|pheasants]], and on occasion it can possess the [[bird feet|legs of one]].\r\n\r\nWhile similar to the [[jackalope]] and [[skvader]], they are not the same. Jackalope lack wings, while skvader lack fangs and horns.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[jackalope]]\r\n* [[skvader]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[cryptid]]\r\n* [[hybrid]]\r\n** [[chimera]]\r\n* [[lagomorph]]\r\n* [[mythology]]\r\n** [[european_mythology]]\r\n*** [[german_mythology]]"
