            "wiki_body": "thumb #4319011 thumb #3309711 thumb #3197644\r\n\r\n[b]Quaxly[/b] ([b]クワッス [/b][i]Kuwassu[/i]) is a Water-type [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]], and along with [[Sprigatito]] and [[Fuecoco]] is one of the three [[starter_trio|starter Pokémon]] from [i]Pokémon Scarlet[/i] and [i]Pokémon Violet[/i]. Classified as the `Duckling Pokémon`,[b] Quaxly[/b] are known for being earnest and tidy.\r\n\r\n[b]Quaxly[/b] was first revealed to the public as the third [[generation_9_pokemon|Generation IX Pokémon]] starter during the \"Pokémon Presents\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Pokémon_Presents \"video presentation on February 27, 2022\":https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xoiwcdqMlCA.\r\n\r\nh4.Physical appearance:\r\n\r\n[b]Quaxly[/b] is a [[biped|bipedal]] Pokémon who looks like a small [[duck]]. Its two [[wings]] and almost its entire body are covered in immaculate [[white_feathers|white plumage]]. It has two legs with light-[[blue_feet|blue]] [[webbed feet]]. This color is also found on the thick [[crest]] that this Pokémon has on its head, giving the impression that this little duck has a [[haircut]].\r\nThis \"hairstyle\" takes the form of a [[beret]] or [[bachi]], with a wisp running forward, and a white, rounded W-shaped [[pattern]] on the front.\r\nOn its face, it has a [[yellow beak]] and two large eyes with dark [[blue_eyes|blue irises]] and [[white pupils]].\r\n\r\n[b]Quaxly[/b] draws its inspiration from ducks, and more broadly from [[seabird|seabirds]]. The light blue color of its legs and crest seem to be a reference to the [[blue-footed booby]], a seabird species known for its blue legs.\r\n\r\nh4.Related tags:\r\n* [[avian]]\r\n* [[bird]]\r\n* [[beak]]\r\n* [[blue_body]]\r\n* [[blue_eyes]]\r\n* [[blue_hair]]\r\n* [[blue_skin]]\r\n* [[feathered_wings]]\r\n* [[feathers]]\r\n* [[membrane_(anatomy)]]\r\n* [[multicolored_body]]\r\n* [[webbed feet]] \r\n* [[white_body]]\r\n* [[white_feathers]]\r\n* [[white_wings]]\r\n* [[wings]]\r\n* [[yellow_beak]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon_(species)]]\r\n** [b]Quaxly[/b]\r\n*** [[Quaxwell]]\r\n**** [[Quaquaval]]"
