            "wiki_preview": "thumb #498180 thumb #3490181 thumb #498168\r\n\r\n[b]Gieeg[/b], or [b]Geeg[/b], is the name given to the...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #498180 thumb #3490181 thumb #498168\r\n\r\n[b]Gieeg[/b], or [b]Geeg[/b], is the name given to the species of [[alien|aliens]] that [[giygas|Giegue]], the main antagonist of [i][[earthbound_(series)|MOTHER 1/EarthBound Beginnings]][/i], is part of. Even though Giegue is the only one of his kind to make a full appearance in the games, the race's existence is implied in [i]MOTHER's[/i] backstory which has been expanded upon in fan-projects, such as [i][[mother:_cognitive_dissonance|Mother: Cognitive Dissonance]][/i].\r\n\r\nThey have a [[humanoid]] body shape, with generally [[tall]] and [[slim]] proportions, while their faces are commonly depicted as more [[anthro|animal-like]], sporting a distinct [[snout]]. Their most distinguishable features are their [[tapering_tail|tapered]], [[long_tail|long tails]] and a pair of pointy horn-/ear-like extensions on top of their heads. The shape and alignment of the latter vary from one individual to another and they are sometimes depicted with small, curled up [[antennae_(anatomy)|antennae]] at the tip. Most Gieegs have [[white_skin|white skin]] and no hair or fur. Their eyes can have many different colors and are either depicted in one solid color, often with a faint pupil, or with [[black_sclera|black scleras]] and thin irises.\r\n\r\nThe exact origin of the species is uncertain, though it seems to be of extrasolar nature, judging by the size of Giegue's mothership. As seen by their experiments on other lifeforms, their sense of curiosity and ambition are very similar to that of humans, however, compared to them, Gieegs are more stoic, preferring to keep emotions shallow and struggling with feeling empathy. They are also very potent PSI-users and are often seen communicating via telepathy. In fact, almost all of the PSI on Earth can be traced back to their technology."
