            "count": 322,
            "wiki_preview": "thumb #4302247\r\n[b]Ogerpon[/b] (Japanese: オーガポン Ogerpon) is a Grass-type [[Legendary Pokémon]] intro...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #4302247\r\n[b]Ogerpon[/b] (Japanese: オーガポン Ogerpon) is a Grass-type [[Legendary Pokémon]] introduced in [[generation_9_pokemon|Generation IX]]. \r\n\r\nIt has a green torso with white flowers and yellow dots and long black legs with two toes on each foot. Between it's toes are sprouts with two leaves. A leafy cloak-like structure extends from it's head, the neck of which appears to be a large, thorny vine. Two thorns stick out prominently from the top, resembling two large horns, a large leaf growing out behind them. This \"cloak\" moves as if Ogerpon has arms underneath it, but Ogerpon has neither arms nor shoulders. The \"cloak\" is actually a prehensile extension of its head that allows it to grab and manipulate objects via the large \"sleeves\" (as well as giving space to store it's masks). Underneath the mask it usually wears, Ogerpon has an orange face, and yellow eyes with white star-shaped pupils. In battle, it wields a large, spiky cudgel wrapped in ivy. Ogerpon is a female-only species with no male counterpart. Ogerpon has a curious and mischievous personality. It enjoys spending time with humans while wearing a mask to blend in. It has been alive for hundreds of years.\r\n\r\nOgerpon has four forms determined by which mask it wears, changing the colors of the cloak.\r\n - [[Teal Mask Ogerpon]]'s cloak is green.\r\n - [[Wellspring Mask Ogerpon]]'s cloak is white and blue.\r\n - [[Hearthflame Mask Ogerpon]]'s cloak is yellow and red.\r\n - [[Cornerstone Mask Ogerpon]]'s cloak is black and gray.\r\n\r\nIt has a 100% female gender ratio in-game.\r\n\r\n[b]Source:[/b]\r\nhttps://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Ogerpon_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
