            "wiki_body": "thumb #1245151 thumb #146264 thumb #1398366\r\n\r\nA mythological creature, often known as the \"Sea Horse\". However, unlike real world sea horses, this creature has the head and forelimbs of a horse, while the rear half of it's body is some nature of fish.\r\n\r\nThe feet may be some nature of fins or claws instead of hooves.\r\n\r\nA similar creature is the [[capricorn]], which is composed of a goat rather than a horse.\r\n\r\nIn Greek Mythology, there ere also several other fish-tailed animals, including leokampoi (lions), taurokampoi (bulls) and pardalokampoi (leopards).  However, these creatures to not have tags here, and are better served with the [[merfolk]] tag. \r\n\r\n"
