            "count": 247,
            "wiki_preview": "(From the WikiFur page:) The Jogauni are a fictional race of tribal elemental canines created by Lus...",
            "wiki_body": "(From the WikiFur page:) The Jogauni are a fictional race of tribal elemental canines created by Luskwood Creatures.\r\n\r\nThere are eight tribes, representing Shadow (Chayam), Light (Ujyalo), Metal (Phalama), Wood (Katha), Fire (Ago), Water (Pani), Air (Hava) and Earth (Mato). They have opposing and complementary tribes.\r\n\r\nThe elements they are bound to are not necessarily the usual representation of Western elementals (such as fire, water, earth and sky) but are loosely based on Nepali legends.\r\n\r\nAs they exist in Second Life, there is also a \"quest\" attached to the avatars.\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[tag group:fictional species]]"
          },
          {
            "tag": "warframe_(species)",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 243,
            "wiki_preview": "[quote][i]\"The true nature of the Warframes and their Tenno connection is a secret lost to the Old W...",
            "wiki_body": "[quote][i]\"The true nature of the Warframes and their Tenno connection is a secret lost to the Old War. Together, they represent our best hope in turning the tide of the machine war. Warframes are unique from Dax and other Infantry, deploying dangerous and esoteric Void energy, and equipped with often mundane physical weapons – this is key to fighting an enemy that had turned our technology against us.\"[/i] —\"Warframes\" Fragment[/quote]\n[quote][i]A mysterious weaponized armor controlled solely by the Tenno. Through the Warframe, Tenno can cheat death, channel the forbidden Void energies and face scores of enemies without fatigue. Due to apparent resistances of their Bio-Metal exoskeletons, Warframes can be safely deployed to Infestation Outbreaks, should they occur. In-depth information of the Warframe mandate is forbidden to all but the Seven.[/i]\n—Warframe Technology Fragment[/quote]\n\nWarframes are the biomechanical warriors controlled by the [[Tenno]] in the titular game, [[Warframe]].\n\nWarframes vary greatly in aesthetics, but are consistently [[eyeless]] and appear to be [[mouthless]], despite accounts in-lore of Warframes consuming flesh, or other substances. [spoiler]While some Warframes can act of their own will, the majority seen within the game are almost completely inanimate without the influence of the Tenno to control them via transference.\n[/spoiler]\n\nCurrently there are 61 Warframes, not counting alternate skins or primes.\n[section=List of Warframes]\n* [[Ash_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Ash_Prime_(warframe)]]\n** [[Ash_Koga]] [i]Designed by IgnusDei.[/i]\n* [[Atlas_(Warframe)]]\n** Atlas_Prime\n*** Atlas_Karst [i]Designed by LigerInzuka[/i]\n* [[Banshee_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Banshee_Prime]]\n** [[Banshee_Soprana]] [i]Sleek and stylish, with headphones and thigh-highs.[/i]\n* [[Baruuk_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Baruuk_Prime]]\n* [[Caliban_(Warframe)]]\n* [[Chroma_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Chroma_Prime]]\n** [[Chroma_Dynasty]]\n** [[Chroma_Zunlong]]\n* [[Citrine_(Warframe)]]\n* [[Dagath_(Warframe)]]\n* [[Dante_(Warframe)]]\n* [[Ember_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Ember_Prime]]\n** [[Ember_Heirloom]] [i]Designed by Vik / Cleo Naturin[/i]\n** [[Ember_Vermillion]]\n** [[Ember_Pyraxis]]\n***  [i]Ember is the first warframe to receive three separate deluxe skins.[/i]\n* [[Equinox_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Equinox_Prime]]\n** [[Equinox_Antonym]]\n* [[Excalibur_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Proto-Excalibur]]\n*** [[Arthur_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Excalibur_Prime]]\n*** [[Excalibur_Umbra]]\n** [[Excalibur_Zato]] [i]Designed by LigerInzuka[/i]\n* [[Frost_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Frost_Prime]]\n** [[Frost_Harka]]\n** [[Frost_Heirloom]]\n* [[Gara_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Gara_Prime]]\n** [[Gara_Kaleida]]\n* [[Garuda_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Garuda_Prime]]\n* [[Gauss_(Warframe)]]\n* [[Grendel_(Warframe)]]\n* [[Gyre_(Warframe)]]\n* [[Harrow_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Harrow_Prime]]\n** [[Harrow_Reliquary]]\n* [[Hildryn_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Hildryn_Prime]]\n** [[Hildryn_Einheri]]\n* [[Hydroid_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Hydroid_Prime]]\n** [[Hydroid_Rakkam]] [i]Designed by LigerInzuka[/i]\n* [[Inaros_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Inaros_Ramses]]\n* [[Ivara_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Ivara_prime_(Warframe)]] [i]Styled after a jellyfish[/i]\n** [[Ivara_Skathi]]\n* [[Jade_(Warframe)]]\n* [[Khora_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Khora_Prime]]\n** [[Khora_Urushu]] [i]Designed by LigerInzuka[/i]\n* [[Kullervo_(Warframe)]]\n* [[Lavos_(Warframe)]]\n* [[Limbo_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Limbo_Prime]]\n* [[Loki_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Loki_prime]]\n*** [[Archon_Boreal]]\n*** [[Knave_Specter]]\n* [[Mag_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Mag_prime]]\n** [[Mag_Pneuma]]\n*** [[Aoi_(Warframe)]]\n*** [[Archon_Nira]]\n* [[Mesa_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Mesa_Prime]]\n* [[Mirage_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Mirage_Prime]]\n** [[Mirage_Oneiro]] [i]Designed by Vik / Cleo Naturin[/i]\n* [[Nekros_(Warframe)]]\n* [[Nezha_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Nezha_Prime]]\n** [[Nezha_Empyrean]] [i]Designed by LigerInzuka[/i]\n* [[Nidus_(Warframe)]]\n** [[Nidus_Phryke]] [i]Designed by LigerInzuka[/i]\n* [[N