            "wiki_preview": "thumb #34933 thumb #1663928 thumb #4911957 thumb #4001048\r\n\r\n[b]Tropius[/b] ([b]トロピウス[/b] [i]Tropius...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #34933 thumb #1663928 thumb #4911957 thumb #4001048\r\n\r\n[b]Tropius[/b] ([b]トロピウス[/b] [i]Tropius[/i]) is a dual-type Grass/Flying [[Pokemon (species)|Pokémon]].\r\n\r\nIt has no [[evolution|evolutions]], and is in the `Monster` and `Grass` egg groups.\r\n\r\n[b]Tropius[/b] is a large [[sauropod]]-like Pokémon, with a [[brown body]] wrapped in green [[leaf|leaves]] on its chest and head. It also has large green [[leaf (anatomy)|leaves as part of its anatomy]] on its back, which enable it to [[flying|fly]] and create [[sugar]] through [[photosynthesis]]. \r\nDespite this dinosaur is big and pretty bulky, it is surprisingly agile in the [[wind|air]].\r\n\r\nIts [[long neck]] is enables it to reach tall [[tree|trees]] to [[feeding|feed]] on its favorite [[fruit]]... Also, when he began to eat this fruit continuously, it began to grow on its chin/throat.\r\n\r\nThese \"[[banana]]-shaped fruits\" can be picked and eaten by other Pokémon or even by [[human|humans]], and they grow twice a year thanks to the rapid sugar production in Tropius' leaves. His toes are the same color as these fruits. It lives in tropical jungles.\r\n\r\nIn its canon form, it is a [[feral]]. The species is occasionally depicted as [[Anthrofied]] and [[Pokemorph|Pokémorph]].\r\n\r\n[[Shiny pokemon|Shiny]] [b]Tropius[/b] has bright [[green wings]] and yellow tint to its body.\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n* [[elemental_creature]]\r\n* [[flora_fauna]]\r\n* [[food]]\r\n* [[fruit]]\r\n* [[leaf]]\r\n* [[quadruped]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[Pokemon|Pokémon]]\r\n* \"Bulbapedia: Tropius\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Tropius"
