            "wiki_preview": "thumb #75794 thumb #3986985 thumb #2531015\r\n\r\n[b]Torterra[/b] (Japanese: [i]ドダイトス[/i], Dodaitose) is...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #75794 thumb #3986985 thumb #2531015\r\n\r\n[b]Torterra[/b] (Japanese: [i]ドダイトス[/i], Dodaitose) is a dual-type Grass/Ground [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] introduced in [[generation_4_pokemon|Generation IV]], being the fully evolved form of Sinnoh's grass starter [[Turtwig]]. Torterra is a [[quadruped|quadrupedal]], bulky, [[reptile|reptilian]] Pokémon, heavily resembling and based on a [[tortoise]].\r\n\r\nThe large [[shell]] covering their hide seems to hold its own mini ecosystem or [[grass|grassy]] field. This small field consists of a single oak-like [[tree]], pointed [[boulder|boulders]] resembling [[mountain|mountain peaks]], and patches of [[dirt|soil]]. All of this is surrounded on the shell by a white \"rim\", leading into a diamond-like shape upon the front of their shell. Torterra's body is segmented or sectioned, being green on the top with [[brown countershading]]. Their mouth is [[jagged mouth|jagged]] and ends in a [[brown beak]], similar to a [[snapping turtle|snapping turtle's]], and their cheeks are adorned with grey [[spikes]]. Surrounding their [[red eyes]] are [[dark circles|dark, blackened circles]]. Like their torso, their legs are bulky, and come with [[4 toes|four toes]] in the [[anisodactyl]] style ending in grey toes\r\n\r\n[quote][i]Torterra's large and clean shell supports the lives of many small Pokémon, which occasionally gather and build their nests upon the shell. Some are born and spend their entire life there. Torterra migrate in search of water, creating the illusion of \"moving forests\". However, it is typically immobile.[/i] - \"Bulbapedia, [i]Torterra biology[/i]\": <https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Torterra_(Pokémon)#Biology>[/quote]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]]\r\n*** [[turtwig]]\r\n**** [[grotle]]\r\n***** torterra"
