            "kor": "",
            "count": 206,
            "wiki_preview": "Amoeba (also spelled [i]ameba[/i] or [i]amœba[/i]) are eukaryotic, generally [[unicellular_organism_...",
            "wiki_body": "Amoeba (also spelled [i]ameba[/i] or [i]amœba[/i]) are eukaryotic, generally [[unicellular_organism_(organism)|unicellular organisms]] falling under various different species, of which are not all directly related. They are characterised primarily by [[blob|bloblike]] or amorphous cell shapes, an ability to [[absorption_vore|absorb]] or [[swallowing|engulf]] prey with their shapeless bodies, and generally able to [[mitosis|mitose]] and [[splitting|split]]. Plurally, amoeba may be written as [i]amoebae[/i] or [i]amoebas[/i].\r\n\r\n* See also:\r\n** [[slime_mold|slime moulds]], which include the sometimes gigantic, branching single celled [[myxogastrian|myxogastria]];\r\n** [[protist_(organism)]], a wastebasket taxon which generally includes many amoeboid organisms;\r\n** [[amoeboid_(ratchet_and_clank)|Amoeboid (Ratchet And Clank)]], a fictional alien which embodies many of the hallmark amoeba-like traits\r\n** [[reuniclus|Reuniclus]], a Pokémon which is loosely based on various [[algae]] and amoeba.\r\n* Not to be confused with:\r\n** [[slime]]\r\n** [[goo_creature|goo creature]], which sometimes display amoeba-like traits, and may ambiguously be tagged as amoebas.\r\n** [[bacteria_(organism)|bacteria]], which are prokaryotes, and may serve as a food source or symbiotic with amoebae. This tag is frequently used alongside the [[amoeba_(organism)|amoeba]] tag."
