            "count": 193,
            "wiki_preview": "thumb #3807495 thumb #4072326 thumb #3780807 thumb #3704143\r\n\r\n[b]Skeledirge[/b] ([b]ラウドボーン[/b] [i]L...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #3807495 thumb #4072326 thumb #3780807 thumb #3704143\r\n\r\n[b]Skeledirge[/b] ([b]ラウドボーン[/b] [i]Laudbon[/i]) is a dual-type Fire/Ghost [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] introduced in [[generation_9_pokemon|Generation IX]]. This time, this Pokémon is classified as the `Singer Pokémon`.\r\n\r\nIt evolves from [[Crocalor]] starting at level 36 and it is the final form of [[Fuecoco]].\r\n\r\nh4.Physical appearance:\r\n\r\n[b]Skeledirge[/b] is a large, mainly red [[alligator]], with a [[white back]], [[white_belly|belly]], top of [[white_snout|snout]], part of the [[white_legs|legs]] and [[white_tail_tip|tip of tail]]. It has several lines all over its body and numerous [[pattern|patterns]] on its face, such as: four small squares (■) and two red triangles (▼) on its snout, as well as two more triangles around each of its eyes. \r\nThis Pokémon also has two yellow triangles on the front of its [[muzzle]], replacing its [[nostrills]]. \r\n\r\nIts eyes have a slightly [[frown|furious look]], with its [[eyebrows]] [[furrowed_brow|slightly furrowed]]. [b]Skeledirge[/b] also has two large [[flame|flames]] coming out of either side of its mouth, encircling its head before stopping at the back of its neck. A small [[bird]] of flames levitates above its nose.\r\n\r\n[b]Skeledirge[/b] may have been inspired by the [[harmony]] that reigns between birds and alligators: the former peck the rest of the [[food]] directly onto the alligator's [[teeth]], while the latter do not attack them.\r\n\r\n[b]Skeledirge[/b] is said to possess a soul-soothing [[song]], and the firebird on its snout is said to be a [[soul]] that has taken [[possession]] of a fireball. This bird is a soul now soothed by the Pokémon's song, so they live in harmony and collaboration.\r\n\r\nAlso, the [[skeleton]] [[crocodile]]'s head could be inspired by the [[make-up]] worn during the \"Dia de Los Muertos\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day_of_the_Dead [i](Day of the Dead)[/i], a popular holiday in Mexico, the country from which [[Fuecoco]]'s [[evolutionary family]] draws its inspiration!\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon_(species)]]\r\n** [[Fuecoco]]\r\n*** [[Crocalor]]\r\n**** [b]Skeledirge[/b]"
