            "wiki_body": "thumb #3133781 thumb #4684774 thumb #3207188\r\n\r\nSource: <https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Arcanine_(Pokémon)>\r\n\r\n[b]Hisuian Arcanine[/b] is a [[regional_form_(pokémon)|regional form]] of [[Arcanine]] found in the Hisui region from [i][[pokemon_legends_arceus|Pokémon Legends: Arceus]][/i]. While its Kantonian counterpart is pure Fire-type, Hisuian Growlithe is Fire/Rock-type.\r\n\r\nIt is the fully-evolved form of [[hisuian_growlithe|Hisuian Growlithe]].\r\n\r\n[b]Hisuian Arcanine[/b] has a slightly different look due to the volcanic activity of the environment it lives in. Its body fur is red-orange while its muzzle, mane, tail, eyebrows, and tufts of fur behind its elbows and around its ankles are gray, and the insides of its ears are light gray. The gray fur is made out of igneous rock components. Its cheek mane, ankle fur, and tail form into curls. Its elbow fur resemble wings. It has a large horn in the center of its head and three small horns between its head and ears. Its mane form into curled clumps at the back of its neck and large rectangular clumps on the sides and bottom of its neck. The rectangular clumps have light red-orange markings on them.\r\n\r\nIt uses its fangs while engulfed in flames to snap at foes. Despite how deceivingly bulky this Pokémon is, it moves around nimbly like a dancer. This allows it to lead opponents in a merry chase while avoiding them at the same time.\r\n\r\nA special [b]Hisuian Arcanine[/b] is worshipped by the Hisui people due to it being one of the 10 ancient Pokémon who received a blessing from Arceus. It is one of the Noble Pokémon who resides in Cobalt Coastlands watched by a Warden.\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n\r\n* [[Pokemon|pokémon]]\r\n** [[growlithe]]\r\n** [[hisuian_growlithe]]\r\n*** [[arcanine]]\r\n*** [[hisuian_arcanine]]\r\n* [[Regional_form_(pokemon)|regional_form_(pokémon)]]"
