            "wiki_body": "thumb #4692047 thumb #1599958 thumb #4657037\r\n\r\n[b]Skiddo[/b] (Japanese: [b]メェークル[/b] [i]Meecle[/i]) is a Grass-type [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] introduced in [[generation_6_pokemon|Generation VI]]. It is in the `Field` egg group.\r\n\r\nIt evolves into [[Gogoat]] starting at level 32.\r\n\r\n[b]Skiddo[/b] is a [[quadruped]] Pokémon with a [[goat]]-like appearance and a [[brown_body|body]] covered mostly in thick [[brown fur]]. It has a [[white face]] with a vertical brown stripe, a round [[black nose]], [[black eyes]], a small [[beard]] and small round ears. It also has a pair of pointed [[black horn]]s on the top of its head that point to the side. Its lower legs are white and it has [[orange_hooves|orange cloven hooves]]. \r\nThis Pokémon has a leafy [[mane]] around its neck that extends down its back to its [[tail]], which is made up of three small [[leaf|leaves]].\r\n\r\n[b]Skiddo[/b] is inspired by a goat, or more likely by its [[horn]]s, the \"bharal\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bharal. It is also inspired by a two-wheeled [[vehicle]]: it can be driven and its horns are reminiscent of [[bicycle]] \"handlebars\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bicycle_handlebar. The leaves growing from its body are inspired by the Greek myth of \"Pan\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pan_(god), the half-man, half-goat god of nature. \r\nThey may also recall the \"Julbock\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yule_goat, a straw goat from northern Europe.\r\n\r\nThanks to its photosynthesizing leaves, this Pokémon doesn't need to be fed as long as it can use the energy of the sun. It is docile by nature, and is believed to be one of the first Pokémon domesticated by humans. The anime also shows that [b]Skiddo[/b]'s milk can be used to make dairy products.\r\n\r\nIn [i]Pokémon X and Y[/i], [b]Skiddo[/b] can be used as a \"Poké Ride\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Poké_Ride.\r\n\r\nFinally, its [[shiny_pokemon|Shiny]] counterpart has pale fur and pink hooves.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[brown_fur]]\r\n* [[hooves]]\r\n* [[horn]]\r\n* [[quadruped]] - In its [[feral]] version; but if it is [[anthro]] use: [[biped]] \r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[pokemon_(species)|pokémon]]\r\n** [b]skiddo[/b]\r\n*** [[gogoat]]"
