              "wiki_body": "An umbrella tag for all species, or contains elements of known species classified as [[Pokemon|Pokémon]] from the franchise of the same name.\n\nh4. Tagging notes\n\nThe best advice for using this tag is to let the implication handle it by tagging the applicable Pokémon species tag.\n\nh4. Good examples\n\nthumb #1268334 thumb #1258647 thumb #600563 thumb #2274408 thumb #1319757  thumb #1250938 thumb #1313780\n\n* a picture of a [[Pikachu]]\n* a picture of an [[Alolan Vulpix]] or other [[regional_form_(pokémon)|regional form]]\n* a picture of a [[Mega Lucario]], [[Primal Groudon]], or other [[mega evolution]] or primal reversion \n* a picture of a character with a fantasy Pokémon party \n* a picture of a Pokémon [[fan character]] or [[Pokemorph|Pokémorph]]\n* a picture of a [[pokemon_costume|Pokémon costume]]\n* a picture including a stuffed animal of a Pokémon species. (But not the [[substitute_doll|\"Substitute\" doll]]!)\n\nThis is not an exhaustive list, but simply some examples of when this tag should apply.\n\nh4. Bad examples\n\nthumb #837022 thumb #965893 thumb #603419 \n\n* a picture of an original character with [[Pokeball|Pokéball]] boxers/other themed clothing that does not depict actual Pokémon\n* a picture of an original character with a vague symbol (such as a Pokéball) as an item or symbol\n* an original character dressed up as a Pokémon Trainer or other kind of [[cosplay]] without any Pokémon shown\n\nIn short, don't put this on posts that show only vague symbols from the franchise, use it only when Pokémon themselves are depicted.  For symbols, trainer cosplay, and so on, use the umbrella [[Pokemon|Pokémon]] tag.\n\nh4. Species tagging\n\nDespite being called Pocket Monsters, most Pokémon do not look monstrous enough to be tagged as [[monster]]. Moreover, while Pokémon species may also be tagged with certain physical traits/classes, they should not also be tagged with the specific species of animal they are based on. So for example, the Pokémon [[Blaziken]] (see below), could be tagged with Avian since it has bird-like features such as talons, feathers, and a beak; but it should never also be tagged with [[Chicken]].\n\nthumb #2365716\n\nh4. Species list\n\n[section=Generation I (0001-0151)]\n\n* [[bulbasaur]] -\t(0001)\n** [[ivysaur]] -\t \t(0002)\n*** [[venusaur]] -\t(0003)\n* [[charmander]] -\t(0004)\n** [[charmeleon]] - \t(0005)\n*** [[charizard]] - \t(0006)\n* [[squirtle]] - \t(0007)\n** [[wartortle]] -\t(0008)\n*** [[blastoise]] - \t(0009)\n* [[caterpie]] -\t\t(0010)\n** [[metapod]] -\t\t(0011)\n*** [[butterfree]] - \t(0012)\n* [[weedle]] -\t\t(0013)\n** [[kakuna]] -\t\t(0014)\n*** [[beedrill]] -\t(0015)\n* [[pidgey]] -\t\t(0016)\n** [[pidgeotto]] -\t(0017)\n*** [[pidgeot]] -\t(0018)\n* [[rattata]] -\t\t(0019)\n** [[raticate]] -\t(0020)\n* [[spearow]] -\t\t(0021)\n** [[fearow]] -\t\t(0022)\n* [[ekans]] -\t\t(0023)\n** [[arbok]] -\t\t(0024)\n* [[pikachu]] -\t\t(0025)\n** [[raichu]] -\t\t(0026)\n* [[sandshrew]] -\t(0027)\n** [[sandslash]] -\t(0028)\n* [[nidoran♀]] -\t\t(0029)\n** [[nidorina]] -\t(0030)\n*** [[nidoqueen]] - \t(0031)\n* [[nidoran♂]] -\t\t(0032)\n** [[nidorino]] -\t(0033)\n*** [[nidoking]] -\t(0034)\n* [[clefairy]] -\t\t(0035)\n** [[clefable]] -\t(0036)\n* [[vulpix]] -\t\t(0037)\n** [[ninetales]] -\t(0038)\n* [[jigglypuff]] -\t(0039)\n** [[wigglytuff]] - \t(0040)\n* [[zubat]] -\t\t(0041)\n** [[golbat]] -\t\t(0042)\n* [[oddish]] -\t\t(0043)\n** [[gloom_(pokemon)|gloom_(pokémon)]] -\t\t(0044)\n*** [[vileplume]] - \t(0045)\n* [[paras]] -\t\t(0046)\n** [[parasect]] -\t(0047)\n* [[venonat]] -\t\t(0048)\n** [[venomoth]] -\t(0049)\n* [[diglett]] -\t\t(0050)\n** [[dugtrio]] -\t\t(0051)\n* [[meowth]] -\t\t(0052)\n** [[persian_(pokemon)|persian_(pokémon)]] -\t\t(0053)\n* [[psyduck]] -\t\t(0054)\n** [[golduck]] -\t\t(0055)\n* [[mankey]] -\t\t(0056)\n** [[primeape]] -\t(0057)\n* [[growlithe]] -\t(0058)\n** [[arcanine]] -\t(0059)\n* [[poliwag]] -\t\t(0060)\n** [[poliwhirl]] -\