              "wiki_body": "thumb #668353 thumb #509970 thumb #639936\n\n[b]Eeveelution[/b] (Japanese: イーブイズ [i]EVs[/i]), is a term used to describe the many evolutions of the [[pokemon|Pokémon]] [[Eevee]]. Originating as an unofficial term used by fans, it was first officially used in the context of a game in [i][[pokemon_ranger|Pokémon Ranger]]: Shadows of Almia[/i]. A less-common related term is [b]Veevee[/b] (ブイブイ), used in English media beginning in Generation VII, and most prominently by the character [[penny_(pokemon)|Penny]] in Generation IX.\n\n[b]This tag does not include eevee itself[/b]\n\nDue to Eevee having unstable genetic formations, Eevee has [i]currently[/i] eight stages of evolutions/Eeveelutions. They are listed below: \n\n* The Water type, [[Vaporeon]], using a Water Stone.\n* The Fire type, [[Flareon]], using a Fire Stone.\n* The Electric type, [[Jolteon]], using a Thunder Stone.\n* The Psychic type, [[Espeon]], leveling up with high friendship during daytime.\n* The Dark type, [[Umbreon]], leveling up with high friendship at night.\n* The Grass type, [[Leafeon]], leveling up near the mossy stone, or in Sword and Shield, using a Leaf Stone.\n* The Ice type, [[Glaceon]], leveling up near the icy stone, or in Sword and Shield, using an Ice Stone.\n* The Fairy type, [[Sylveon]], gaining two affection hearts in Pokémon Amie (having high friendship in Generation VIII onward), learning a Fairy-type move, and leveling up.\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[pokemon_(species)]]\n** [[eevee]]\n*** eeveelution\n**** [[vaporeon]]\n**** [[jolteon]]\n**** [[flareon]]\n**** [[espeon]]\n**** [[glaceon]]\n**** [[leafeon]]\n**** [[umbreon]]\n**** [[sylveon]]\n\n"
