                "wiki_preview": "Some [[pokémon_(species)|Pokémon]] have adapted to the distinctive microclimates of certain regions,...",
                "wiki_body": "Some [[pokémon_(species)|Pokémon]] have adapted to the distinctive microclimates of certain regions, taking on different forms than they have in others. These Pokémon are called [b]regional forms[/b] (referred to as [b]regional variants[/b] in [[generation 7 pokemon|Generation VII]]). Originally observed in the \"Alola region\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Alola but later found in \"Galar\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Galar and \"Paldea\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Paldea, they live like native Pokémon. [b]Regional variant[/b] Pokémon can have different appearances and types, and their ways of living can also differ from that of the forms previously known.\r\n\r\n[[Alolan form|Alolan forms]] are all of [[Generation 1 Pokemon|Generation I Pokémon]]. Unlike Alolan Forms, there are [[Galarian form|Galarian]], [[Hisuian form|Hisuian]], and [[Paldean form|Paldean Forms]] of Pokémon from beyond Generation I, and several Galarian and Hisuian Forms have an evolution that their regular form does not.\r\n\r\nSimilarly to [[mega_evolution|Mega Evolutions]], [b]regional forms[/b] [b][u]should NOT be tagged as their base form[/u][/b], unless both are present in the image.\r\n\r\n[section=Extra information]\r\n\r\nThe explanation is that some Pokémon have adapted to the distinctive microclimates of a region, which makes sense, but it can also be seen as a creative means for [i]Game Freak Inc.[/i] to retool classic franchise characters with new Pokémon types, and abilities better suited for gameplay for the Pokémon roster for that specific region.\r\n\r\nThe pre-evolutions of [[Raichu]], [[Exeggutor]], [[Marowak]], [[Weezing]], [[Mr. Mime]], [[Typhlosion]], [[Samurott]], [[Lilligant]], [[Braviary]], [[Sliggoo]], [[Avalugg]], and [[Decidueye]]  do [b][u]not[/u][/b] themselves have regional forms.\r\n\r\nAlolan Forms all consist of [[generation_1_pokemon|Generation I Pokémon]]. Unlike Alolan Forms, there are Galarian, Hisuian, and Paldean Forms of Pokémon from beyond Generation I, and one Paldean Form and several Galarian and Hisuian Forms have an evolution that their regular form does not.\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Tagging guidelines\r\n\r\n* Regional forms should not be tagged as their default species tag. Use the regional form species tag instead.\r\n\r\nh4.Examples\r\nthumb #3598986 ▷ This post should [b][u]NOT[/u][/b] be tagged \"[[Vulpix]]\" but [b]\"[[Alolan Vulpix]]\"[/b]\r\n\r\nthumb #3352787\r\nBut here, since both forms of Vulpix (\"Kanto\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Kanto and Alolan form) are present on the same post...\r\n\r\nThis post should therefore be tagged with [b]\"[[Vulpix]]\"[/b] [b][u]AND[/u][/b] [b]\"[u][[Alolan Vulpix]][/u]\"[/b]\r\n[section=Alolan forms (Generation VII)]\r\n* [[Alolan Rattata]]\r\n** [[Alolan Raticate]]\r\n* [[Alolan Raichu]]\r\n* [[Alolan Sandshrew]]\r\n** [[Alolan Sandslash]]\r\n* [[Alolan Vulpix]]\r\n** [[Alolan Ninetales]]\r\n* [[Alolan Diglett]]\r\n** [[Alolan Dugtrio]]\r\n* [[Alolan Meowth]]\r\n** [[Alolan Persian]]\r\n* [[Alolan Geodude]]\r\n** [[Alolan Graveler]]\r\n*** [[Alolan Golem]]\r\n* [[Alolan Grimer]]\r\n** [[Alolan Muk]]\r\n* [[Alolan Exeggutor]]\r\n* [[Alolan Marowak]]\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Galarian forms (Generation VIII)]\r\nh5. Base game\r\n* [[Galarian Meowth]] (Evolves into [[Perrserker]])\r\n* [[Galarian Ponyta]]\r\n** [[Galarian Rapidash]]\r\n* [[Galarian Farfetch'd]] (Evolves into [[Sirfetch'd]])\r\n* [[Galarian Weezing]]\r\n* [[Galarian Mr. Mime]] (Evolves into [[Mr. Rime]])\r\n* [[Galarian Corsola]] (Evolves into [[Cursola]])\r\n* [[Galarian Zigzagoon]]\r\n** [[Galarian Linoone]] (Evolves into [[Obstagoon]])\r\n* [[Galarian Darumaka]]\r\n** [[Galarian Darmanitan]]\r\n* [[Galarian Yamask]] (Evolves into [[Runerigus]])\r\n* [[Galarian Stunfisk]]\r\n\r\nh5. [i]The Isle of Armor[/i]\r\n* [[Galarian Slowpoke]]\r\n** [[Galarian Slowbro]]\r\n\r\nh5. [i]The Crown Tundra[/i]\r\n* [[Galarian Slowking]]\r\n* [[Galarian Articuno]]\r\n* [[Galarian Zapdos]]\r\n* [[Galarian Moltres]]\r\n[/section]\r\n[section=Hisuian forms (Pokemon Legends: Arceus)]\r\n* [[Hisuian Growlithe]]\r\n** [[Hisuian Arcanine]]\r\n* [[Hisuian Voltorb]]\r\n** [[Hisuian Electrode]]\r\n* [[Hisuian Qwilfish]] (evolves into [[Overqwil]])\r\n* [[Hisuian Sneasel]] (evolves into [[Sneasler]])\r\n* [[Hisuian Typhlosion]]\r\n* [[Hisuian Samurott]]\r\n* [[Hisuian Lilligant]]\r\n* [[Hisuian Zorua]]\r\n** [[Hisuian Zoroark]]\r\n* [[Hisuian Braviary]]\r\n* [[Hisuian Decidueye]]\r\n* [[Hisuian Sligoo]]\r\n** [[Hisuian Goodra]]\r\n* [[Hisuian Avalugg]]\r\n[/section]\r\n[section=Paldean forms (Generation IX)]\r\n* [[Paldean Wooper]] (evolves into [[Clodsire]])\r\n* [[Paldean Tauros]]\r\n** [[Paldean Tauros (Aqua Breed)]]\r\n** [[Paldean Tauros (Blaze Breed)]]\r\n** [[Paldean Tauros (Combat Breed)]]\r\n[/section]"
              }
