              "wiki_preview": "A fossil is a trace or piece of an organism from the past, such as a skeleton, shell, or leaf, prese...",
              "wiki_body": "A fossil is a trace or piece of an organism from the past, such as a skeleton, shell, or leaf, preserved in the earth.\r\n\r\nIn the [[Pokémon]] world, Fossils of prehistoric [[pokémon_(species)|Pokémon]] are items which can be revived into living Pokémon using techniques developed by the Devon Corporation and a research laboratory on Cinnabar Island. The two institutions purportedly developed their techniques independently of each other at around the same time. There are also other scientists around the Pokémon world who can revive Fossils using these techniques.\r\n\r\nPokémon revived from Fossils are commonly called [b]Fossil Pokémon[/b]. The majority of Fossil Pokémon are part Rock-type (with the exceptions of [[Dracozolt]], [[Arctozolt]], [[Dracovish]], and [[Arctovish]]).\r\n\r\nNote: Gen II, Gen VII and Gen IX did not introduce any new Fossil Pokémon.\r\n\r\nh5. Fossil Pokémon:\r\nh6. Gen I\r\n* [[Omanyte]] ([[Helix Fossil]])\r\n** [[Omastar]]\r\n* [[Kabuto]] ([[Dome Fossil]])\r\n** [[Kabutops]]\r\n* [[Aerodactyl]] ([[Old Amber]])\r\n** [[Mega Aerodactyl]]\r\nh6. Gen III\r\n* [[Lileep]] ([[Root Fossil]])\r\n** [[Cradily]]\r\n* [[Anorith]] ([[Claw Fossil]])\r\n** [[Armaldo]]\r\nh6. Gen IV\r\n* [[Cranidos]] ([[Skull Fossil]])\r\n** [[Rampardos]]\r\n* [[Shieldon]] ([[Armor Fossil]])\r\n** [[Bastiodon]]\r\nh6. Gen V\r\n* [[Tirtouga]] ([[Cover Fossil]])\r\n** [[Carracosta]]\r\n* [[Archen]] ([[Plume Fossil]])\r\n** [[Archeops]]\r\nh6. Gen VI\r\n* [[Tyrunt]] ([[Jaw Fossil]])\r\n** [[Tyrantrum]]\r\n* [[Amaura]] ([[Sail Fossil]])\r\n** [[Aurorus]]\r\n\r\nh6. Gen VIII\r\n* [[Dracozolt]] ([[Bird Fossil]] + [[Drake Fossil]])\r\n* [[Arctozolt]] ([[Bird Fossil]] + [[Dino Fossil]])\r\n* [[Dracovish]] ([[Fish Fossil]] + [[Drake Fossil]])\r\n* [[Arctovish]] ([[Fish Fossil]] + [[Dino Fossill]])\r\n\r\nh4. Further reading:\r\n\"Bulbapedia Fossil page\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Fossil"
            }
