                "wiki_preview": "Introduced in [[generation_9_pokemon|Generation IX]] ([i]Pokémon Scarlet and Violet[/i]), Paradox Po...",
                "wiki_body": "Introduced in [[generation_9_pokemon|Generation IX]] ([i]Pokémon Scarlet and Violet[/i]), Paradox Pokémon are a group of [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] who appear to be past ([i]Scarlet[/i] only) and future ([i]Violet[/i] only) relatives of contemporary Pokémon. They were brought to the present day from their respective time periods with a time machine built by [[Professor Sada]] ([i]Scarlet[/i])/[[Professor Turo]] ([i]Violet[/i]).\r\n\r\nThough they appear to be alternate forms of existing Pokémon, they are considered to be distinct Pokémon within the Pokédex and should not be tagged as the species of their present-day relative.\r\n\r\nh3. [[ancient_pokemon|Ancient Pokémon]] ([i]Scarlet[/i])\r\n* [[Great Tusk]] ([[Donphan]])\r\n* [[Brute Bonnet]] ([[Amoonguss]])\r\n* [[Sandy Shocks]] ([[Magneton]])\r\n* [[Scream Tail]] ([[Jigglypuff]])\r\n* [[Flutter Mane]] ([[Misdreavus]])\r\n* [[Slither Wing]] ([[Volcarona]])\r\n* [[Roaring Moon]] ([[Mega Salamence]])\r\n* [[Koraidon]] aka \"Winged King\" ([[Cyclizar]])\r\n* [[Walking Wake]] ([[Suicune]])\r\n* [[Gouging Fire]] ([[Entei]])\r\n* [[Raging Bolt]] ([[Raikou]])\r\n\r\nh3. [[future_pokemon|Future Pokémon]] ([i]Violet[/i])\r\n* [[Iron Treads]] ([[Donphan]])\r\n* [[Iron Moth]] ([[Volcarona]])\r\n* [[Iron Hands]] ([[Hariyama]])\r\n* [[Iron Jugulis]] ([[Hydreigon]])\r\n* [[Iron Thorns]] ([[Tyranitar]])\r\n* [[Iron Bundle]] ([[Delibird]])\r\n* [[Iron Valiant]] ([[Gardevoir]]/[[Gallade]])\r\n* [[Miraidon]] aka \"Iron Serpent\" ([[Cyclizar]])\r\n* [[Iron Leaves]] ([[Virizion]])\r\n* [[Iron Boulder]] ([[Terrakion]])\r\n* [[Iron Crown]] ([[Cobalion]])"
              }
