                "wiki_preview": "[b]Ancient Pokémon[/b] are a category of [[paradox_pokemon|Paradox Pokémon]] introduced in [i]Pokémo...",
                "wiki_body": "[b]Ancient Pokémon[/b] are a category of [[paradox_pokemon|Paradox Pokémon]] introduced in [i]Pokémon Scarlet[/i]. They are past relatives of present-day Pokémon brought to the current time by [[Professor Sada]]'s time machine. Ancient Pokémon tend to be far larger and have  a more menacing and naturalistic appearance compared to their present-day equivalents.\r\n\r\nThough they appear to be alternate forms of existing Pokémon, they are considered to be distinct Pokémon within the Pokédex and should not be tagged as the species of their present-day relative. They should not be confused with [[fossil_pokemon|Fossil Pokémon]] or the trio of [[generation_3_pokemon|Generation 3]] [[legendary_pokemon|Legendary Pokémon]] referred to as \"super-ancient Pokémon\" ([[Groudon]], [[Kyogre]], and [[Rayquaza]]).\r\n\r\nh3. List of Ancient Pokémon \r\n* [[Great Tusk]] ([[Donphan]])\r\n* [[Brute Bonnet]] ([[Amoonguss]])\r\n* [[Sandy Shocks]] ([[Magneton]])\r\n* [[Scream Tail]] ([[Jigglypuff]])\r\n* [[Flutter Mane]] ([[Misdreavus]])\r\n* [[Slither Wing]] ([[Volcarona]])\r\n* [[Roaring Moon]] ([[Mega Salamence]])\r\n* [[Koraidon]] aka \"Winged King\" ([[Cyclizar]])\r\n* [[Walking Wake]] ([[Suicune]])\r\n* [[Gouging Fire]] ([[Entei]])\r\n* [[Raging Bolt]] ([[Raikou]])"
              }
