            "wiki_preview": "thumb #1661232 thumb #5581411 thumb #5585712 thumb #1618483 thumb #3708551\n[i][b]\"thee who doth turn...",
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1661232 thumb #5581411 thumb #5585712 thumb #1618483 thumb #3708551\n[i][b]\"thee who doth turn mortal men a many...into furry.\"[/b][/i]\n\n[b]Renamon[/b] (Japanese: レナモン Renamon) is an [[anthro]] [[canine]] species with fox like attributes from the [[Digimon]] franchise. Renamon is typically covered in [[yellow fur]] with white or tan countershading down the front, and including the dipstick markings on the tail and ears. Other notable traits include the fox like ears, and muzzle, [[big_tuft|thick tufts]] of fur on the shoulders, and arms, and purple [[double tomoe]] [[thigh markings]]. The default model of this species also [[clothed|wears clothing]] in the form of purple [[bridal gauntlets]].\n\nthumb #5245158  thumb #3835647 thumb #5448550  \n\nThe designer and illustrator of Renamon was watabane kenji (lead artist of the Digimon franchise) under the creative supervision of Chiaki J. Konaka (head scriptwriter of Digimon Tamers, 2001). Its conceptualization integrated elements from Japanese folklore, particularly the kitsune and yokais, evident in symbolic motifs such as the [[yin-yang]], [[tomoe_(symbol)]]  (swirling patterns), and themes drawn from Shinto and Buddhist traditions.\n\n\nThe Digimon Reference Book describes Renamon’s species as follows: “A Beast Man Digimon with the appearance of a golden Fox. The relationship Renamon has with humans is directly apparent; it is said that depending on how it was raised during its time as a Baby, it can evolve into a Renamon of particularly high intelligence. It is always calm, cool, and collected, as well as disciplined enough not to lose that composure in any situation. Its slender, tall appearance stands out when compared with other Child levels, and rather than emphasizing on power in battle, it instead makes sport of the enemy with various techniques that utilize its speed. Its Signature Move is a transformation art in which it copies the opponent's appearance and re-covers itself in that texture (Kohenkyo). Its Special Move is throwing sharpened leaves at the opponent (Koyousetsu).”\n\nthumb #5582590  thumb #1618485 thumb #2406798\n\nAdditionally, Renamon possesses a variant influenced by the Antibody X, which amplifies its mystical abilities. This form enhances its spiritual powers, manifested through a visible aura, and grants mastery of dark arts to manipulate the environment, conjure energy-based attacks, and cast illusions.\n\nthumb #2266114 thumb #5025645 thumb #2845889\n\nRenamon was also the Digimon partner to [[Rika Nonaka]] in the Digimon Tamers (2001) series and related media. Despite this relationship, Renamon is treated as a species tag, which makes it ineligible for character specific tags such as [[crossgender]]. This is not true for Digimon [[fan_character|fan characters]] using the Renamon species, which would be based on the specific character traits for that character.\n\nthumb #4513217  thumb #4609789  thumb #4911462\n\nDuring its design phase, the character was initially slated to be named Lunamon (a name later assigned to another Digimon), referencing its lunar symbolism; a theme retained in its evolution sequences to Taomon and Sakuyamon in the anime. However, the final name Renamon was derived from the French word “Renard” (fox), combined with the suffix \"mon\". Konaka has also noted that the name subtly alludes to renaissance (\"rebirth\"), symbolizing the character’s emotional growth throughout the series.\n\nthumb #5537970 thumb #3445703 thumb #4261856 thumb #4486296  thumb #13700\n\nIn interviews, Chiaki Konaka emphasized that Renamon’s androgynous design was deliberate, aiming to subvert archetypal feminine character tropes. He described Renamon as a \"gender-neutral ally\" crafted to transcend traditional gender roles, balancing Rika’s logical detachment with her gradual emotional development. This approach reflects Konaka’s broader narrative interest in challenging societal norms through nonconforming personas.\n\nthumb #781584\n\nh4. Related tags\n\n* [[anthro]] - Unless drawn to be more feral, the default model for Renamon is anthro.\n* [[biped]]\n* [[bridal_gauntlets]]\n* [[countershading]]\n** [[countershade_fur]]\n** [[countershade_torso]]\n** [[white_countershading]]\n* [[fur]]\n** [[yellow_fur]]\n** [[white_fur]]\n* [[fur_markings]]\n** [[double tomoe]]\n** [[thigh_markings]] \n** [[purple_markings]] \n* [[shoulder_tuft]]\n\nh4. External links\n\n* https://digimon.fandom.com/wiki/Renamon\n* https://digimon.fandom.com/wiki/Renamon_(Tamers)\n* https://wikimon.net/Renamon\n* https://digimon.net/reference_en/detail.php?directory_name=renamon\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[relemon]]\n** [[viximon]]\n*** [b]renamon[/b]\n*** [[renamon_x]] - A renamon that carries the X-antibody.\n**** Champion forms\n***** [[kyubimon]]\n***** [[youkomon]]\n**** Ultimate forms\n***** [[taomon]]\n***** [[doumon]]\n**** Mega forms\n***** [[sakuyamon]]\n***** [[kuzuhamon]]  \n"
