            "wiki_body": "In-development designs for [[pokemon|Pokémon]], generally obtained either from early ROMs (a la the Pokémon Gold and Silver Spaceworld '97 demo) or from internal leaks.\r\n\r\nBeta Pokémon generally fit into two distinct categories: [b]completely unused monsters[/b], or [b]prototype versions of finalized monsters[/b].\r\n* Unused Pokémon generally have original names that are transliterations of in-game text (e.g. [[Warabbit]] and [[rinrin_(pokemon_gold_beta)|Rinrin]]).\r\n* Prototype Pokémon may be tagged as their \"release\" name with an additional prefix (e.g. [[Beta Octillery]], [[Beta Girafarig]]).\r\n* Some prototype Pokémon may be identified as closely related to a finalized pokémon, but nevertheless have a different name (compare [[Fiyoko]] to [[Torchic]].)\r\n** In the interest of separating beta Pokémon from finalized Pokémon, [i]prototype Pokémon should not be tagged as their finalized form![/i] [[Fiyoko]] is not [[Torchic]], [[Beta Octillery]] is not [[Octillery]], etc.\r\n\r\nFake designs may occasionally be disseminated along with genuine beta designs when enthusiasts are picking through files for art and data. If a design is proven to be fake, it should instead be tagged as [[fakemon]]."
