            "wiki_body": "thumb #16870   thumb #182439   thumb #1773845   thumb #2493160   thumb #4896776   thumb #5301875   thumb #5504756\n\n[color=species][b]Tōchūkasō[/b][/color] ([color=species][b]冬虫夏草[/b][/color]) is a species of [[parasite|parasitic]] [[fungus]] from the [i][[pokemon|Pokémon]][/i] series that parasitizes the species [[Paras]] and [[Parasect]].\n\nAn agaric fungus, the [[spores|spore]]-bearing anatomy of tōchūkasō takes the form of a [[mushroom]]. These tōchūkasō mushrooms are generally [[red mushroom|red]] with [[yellow spots]], but over the years have appeared in shades of [[pink mushroom|pink]], [[purple mushroom|purple]], or [[orange mushroom|orange]]. With a near-identical appearance, the tiny mushroom and big mushroom items are likely instances of tōchūkasō mushrooms. The tōchūkasō mushrooms and their spores can be consumable by humans and Pokémon. They have been used in herbal medicine and potions in places like the Kanto region and [[China]] (or the Pokémon world's counterpart). Tōchūkasō can be toxic, at least when hosted by Parases and Parasects, using them for poisonous attacks.\n\nTōchūkasō is noted for its symbiosis with the Paras–Parasect line. Spores contaminate [[egg|eggs]] upon their laying and hatchlings are infected shortly after emerging. For the Paras stage of the life cycle, two small mushrooms sprout from the Pokémon's back, on the second segment of the [[arthropod_abdomen|abdomen]]. Tōchūkasō grows with its host and, upon [[evolution_(transformation)|evolution]], overwhelms the Parasect: the fungus forms one giant mushroom with streaked spots that comprises most of the Pokémon's volume. Pokémon researchers are of the understanding that a Parasect's actions are dictated not by the host's [[brain]], but by the overwhelming infection. Tōchūkasō and its influenced hosts prefer dark, damp places to grow in, and Parases and Parasects parasitize [[tree]] [[roots]] (thus making tōchūkasō a hyperparasite). \n\nThe fungus' namesake is the [[real world]] species of [i]Ophiocordyceps sinensis[/i], (the \"caterpillar fungus\", more literally translated as \"winter worm summer grass\"), however it does not bear any visual or ecological resemblance aside from being an entomopathogenic fungus.\n\nh4. See also\n* [[fungus]]\n** [[fungi fauna]]\n** morphology\n*** [[mushroom]]\n** taxonomy\n*** [i][[Cordyceps]][/i]\n*** [i][[Ophiocordyceps]][/i]\n* [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]]\n** [[generation 1 pokemon|Generation 1 Pokémon]] \n*** #0046 [[Paras]]\n*** #0047 [[Parasect]]\n\nh4. External links\n* Bulbapedia — \"Tochukaso\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Tochukaso\n* Wikipedia — \"[i]Ophiocordyceps sinensis[/i]\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ophiocordyceps_sinensis"
