              "wiki_body": "[b]Note:[/b] This page is a stub. You can help out by continuing to fill it out other aliens we have missed from the list.\n\nAn extraterrestrial creature not in traditional myths and not native to the planet [[Earth]].\n\nIf an alien looks more human and less bestial or [[monster|monstrous]], add the [b][[alien humanoid]][/b] tag instead.\n\nKeep in mind that this tag should only be added if the creature looks like an alien by [[tag what you see|twys]]. Do not tag this by outside information.\n\nh5. Disambiguation\n\n[[Xenomorph|Xenomorphs]] are aliens from the [i]Alien[/i] franchise, commonly referred to simply as Alien. For these specific kinds of aliens, please use the [[Xenomorph]] tag.\n\nh3. Known alien species and characters:\n\nh5. Unsorted:\n* [[Prawn (District 9)|Prawns]] of the film [i][[District 9]][/i], which includes [[Christopher Johnson]].\n* [[Zanburg]] species made by the artist [[Petaroh]].\n* [[Elma]], a character in the franchise [i][[Tenchi Muyo|Tenchi Muyo GXP]][/i].\n* [[Ryo-Ohki]], a [[Cabbit (Tenchi Muyo)|cabbit]] in the franchise [i][[Tenchi Muyo]][/i].\n* [[Cthulhu]] of the Lovecraft series. Also arguably a [[God]].\n* [[Irken]] of the [i][[Invader Zim]][/i] franchise, which includes [[Zim]] himself.\n* [[M'Ress]] and [[Dr. T'ana]] of the [[Caitian]] of the [i][[Star Trek]][/i] franchise.\n* [[Gem (species)|Gems]] of the animated series [i][[Steven Universe]][/i].\n* [[Na'vi]] of [i][[James Cameron's Avatar]][/i] universe, which includes [[Neytiri]] and (post-body transfer) [[Jake Sully]].\n* The [[Lombax]] from [[Ratchet and Clank]]\n* [[Rocket Raccoon]] and [[Blackjack O'Hare]] are aliens that look like mammals.\n\n\nh5. [i][[Alien (franchise)|Alien]][/i] and [i][[Predator (franchise)|Predator]][/i] franchises\n* [[engineer_(alien)|Engineer]]\n* [[Facehugger]]\n* [[Neomorph]]\n* [[Trilobite (Prometheus)|Trilobite]]\n* [[Xenomorph]]\n* [[Yautja]]\n\nh5. [i][[Animorphs]][/i] franchise.\n* [[Andalite]] species\n* [[Yeerk]] species\n* [[Hork-Bajir]] species\n* [[Taxxon]] species\n\nh5. [i][[Ben 10]][/i] franchise\nSince there are numerous alien species in this franchise, only the first ten Omnitrix alien species are listed here. A full species list can be seen on the [i]Ben 10[/i] wiki page.\n\n* [[Pyronite]] species, which includes [[Heatblast]].\n* [[Vulpimancer]] species, which includes [[Wildmutt]].\n* [[Petrosapien]] species, which includes [[Diamondhead]].\n* [[Kineceleran]] species, which includes [[XLR8]].\n* [[Galvan]] species, which includes [[Grey Matter]].\n* [[Tetramand]] species, which includes [[Four Arms (Ben 10)|Four Arms]].\n* [[Lepidopterran]] species, which includes [[Stinkfly]].\n* [[Piscciss Volann]] species, which includes [[Ripjaws]].\n* [[Galvanic Mechamorph]] species, which includes [[Upgrade (Ben 10)|Upgrade]].\n* [[Ectonurite]] species, which includes [[Ghostfreak]].\n\nh5. Conspiracy theories\n* [[Roswell Grey]], as in the classic imagery of such from supposed [[real]] world encounters. Have a penchant for vivisection.\n* Nordics, another allegedly \"real\" race of aliens who resemble blonde humans. Since they look like Norsemen, they were named after them. These are the fun ones, as they supposedly conduct experiments involving crossbreeding with normal humans.\n* Reptillians, the third allegedly \"real\" race of aliens. Usually used to lampoon conspiracy theories (ie, \"The President is a lizardman from Mars!\")\n\nh5. [i][[Dragon Ball]][/i] franchise\n* [[Frieza]]'s [[Frieza Race|race]]\n* [[Majin]], such as [[Majin Buu|Buu]] and [[Majin Android 21|Android 21]]\n* [[Namekian]]s, such as [[Piccolo]]\n* [[Saiyan]]s, such as [[Goku]] and [[Vegeta]]\n* The Gods of Destruction and anthro-looking aliens such as [[Beerus]], [[Champa]] and [[Bergamo]]\n\nh5. [i][[EarthBound_(series)|EarthBound/MOTHER]][/i] franchise\n* [[gieeg|Geeg]] species, which includes [[giygas|Giegue]].\n* [[Mook]] species.\n* [[Mr. Saturn]] species, recurring characters and the series' mascot.\n* [[Starman]] species.\n* [[Wooly Shambler]] species.\n\nh5. [i][[Futurama]][/i] franchise\n* [[decapodian (futurama)|Decapodian]] species, which includes [[Doctor Zoidberg]].\n* [[Omicronian]] species, which includes [[Lrrr (futurama)|Lrrr]].\n* [[neptunian_(futurama)|Neptunian]] species, which includes [[Elzar (futurama)|Elzar]].\n* [[nibblonian|Nibblonian]] species, which includes [[Nibbler]].\n\nh5. [i][[Halo (series)|Halo]][/i] franchise (the [[Covenant (Halo)|Covenant]])\n* [[Sangheili]] (Elites), which includes the [[Arbiter]].\n* [[Unggoy]] (Grunts)\n* [[Jiralhanae]] (Brutes)\n* [[Kig-Yar]] (Jackals)\n\nh5. [i][[Lilo and Stitch|Lilo & Stitch]][/i] franchise\n* [[Kweltikwan]] species, which includes Dr. [[Jumba Jookiba]].\n* Dr. Jumba Jookiba's [[experiment (Lilo and Stitch)|genetic experiments]], which includes [[Stitch]] himself. (Note that each experiment are actually of their own artificial species.)\n* [[Plorgonarian]] species, which includes Wendy [[Pleakley]].\n* [[Gantu]] of an unknown species that resemble large, anthro sharks.\n* The [[Grand Councilwoman]] of an unknown species.\n* [[Dr. Hämsterviel|Dr. Jacques von Hämsterviel]] of an unknown, [[gerbil]]-like ([[hamster]]-like according to him) species.\n\nh5. [i][[Mass Effect]][/i] franchise\n* [[Turian]] species, which includes [[Garrus Vakarian]].\n* [[Krogan]] species, which includes [[Urdnot Wrex]].\n* [[Quarian]] species, which includes [[Tali'zorah]].\n* [[Asari]] species, which includes [[Liara T'soni]].\n* [[Prothean]] species, which includes [[Javik]].\n* [[Hanar]] race.\n\nh5. [i][[Starcraft]][/i] franchise\n* [[Zerg]]\n* [[Protoss]]\n\nh5. [i][[Star Wars]][/i] franchise\n* [[Wookiee]] species, which includes [[Chewbacca]].\n* [[Yoda]] and [[Grogu]] (\"The Child\"/\"Baby Yoda\") of [[Yoda's species|an unknown species]].\n* [[Gungan]] species, which includes [[Jar Jar Binks]].\n* [[twi'lek|Twi'lek]] species.\n* [[Hutt]] species, which includes [[Jabba the Hutt]].\n* [[M