              "count": 561,
              "wiki_preview": "thumb #3312156\r\n[b]Togruta[/b] (/'təʊgɹʌtʌː/) — a [[humanoid]] [[alien]] species from the [i][[Star ...",
              "wiki_body": "thumb #3312156\r\n[b]Togruta[/b] (/'təʊgɹʌtʌː/) — a [[humanoid]] [[alien]] species from the [i][[Star Wars]][/i] franchise\r\n\r\nThe Togruta are a [[biped|bipedal]] [[mammal|mammalian]] species from Shili, a planet in the Expansion Region with colorful grasslands and mountainous valleys. They're generally similar to [[human|humans]] in exception to their notable complexions and pronounced protrusions from the skull. \r\n\r\nIn place of [[hair]], they have a pair of hollow [[horns]] called \"[[montrals]]\" growing upwards and three tail-like appendages called \"[[lekku_(anatomy)|lekku]]\" dangling down (two that protrude from the skull, one on either side that drapes over their chest; and one hanging down their back from the rear base of their skull), both of which grow in length as the Togruta matures. [[Sexual dimorphism]] in the species leads for montrals to grow larger and more angular in the [[male|males]], and the lekku to grow longer in [[female|females]]. As montrals are connected to an extrasensory organ, Togruta can [[echolocation|echolocate]] movement within 25 meters. \r\n\r\nSkin colors varies from [[red skin|red]]; [[orange skin|orange]]; [[yellow skin|yellow]]; [[green skin|green]], with all possessing highly variable [[white markings]] on the face; limbs; and majority of the lekku and montrals, the lattermost of which further have [[blue markings]]. Additionally, Togruta possess multiple stomachs and (in Legends continuity) are carnivorous."
            }
