            "wiki_body": "thumb #547825 thumb #364237 thumb #619052\r\n\r\nBeings with both biological and synthetic (e.g. mechanical, electronic, robotic, etc.) parts. Although they also fit the description, [[robot|robots]] (and by extension [[android|androids]]) with organic components installed, as well as [[amputee|amputees]] with regular non-mechanical/electronic prosthetics such as [[glass eye|glass eyes]], [[hook hand|hook hands]], and [[pegleg|peglegs]], are generally not considered cyborgs.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[machine]]\r\n** [b]cyborg[/b]\r\n*** [[prosthetic]]\r\n**** [[cybernetics]]\r\n***** [[bionics]]\r\n\r\nForum discussion:\r\n\r\n* forum #141131 - Cyborgs, Androids, and Robots. Oh my! (Oct. 2014)\r\n* forum #145008 - Calling all robot, android, mecha, etc. experts! (wiki project) (Dec. 2014)"
