          "tag": "zombie",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 4042,
          "wiki_preview": "A [b]zombie[/b] is [[corpse]] that has [[resurrection|risen from the dead]]. Most are created throug...",
          "wiki_body": "A [b]zombie[/b] is [[corpse]] that has [[resurrection|risen from the dead]]. Most are created through viral experimentation, radiation, or supernatural forces. In some cases, someone who has died will re-animate no matter how they have died.\r\n\r\nZombies have been made famous through film, television, comic books, novels, video games, and so much more. As zombies are already dead, you can't really \"kill\" them so to speak. Shooting them in the head will destroy them. Keep in mind that they don't feel pain. Don't try kicking them in the balls. It doesn't work. Stay safe. Stay alive. \r\n\r\nThere is some confusion between \"zombies\" and \"[[Ghoul]]s\". In some cases, the terms can be used interchangeably.\r\n\r\nNote that zombies are a supplementary species; Meaning that tagging a character with this tag alone would be insufficient. You should also tag their primary species along with this tag one.\r\n\r\nh4.Common traits\r\nThe following tags are usually associated with zombies but not always:\r\n* [[rotting_flesh]]\r\n* [[exposed_bone]]\r\n* [[blank_stare]]\r\n* [[amputee]]\r\n* [[torn_clothing]]\r\n* [[hard_vore]]\r\n* [[gore]]\r\n\r\nh4.See also\r\n* [[undead]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "feathered_dinosaur",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 3943,
          "wiki_preview": "thumb #978909 thumb #341111 thumb #845222\r\n\r\nA tag for dinosaurs possessing [[feathers]], whether th...",
          "wiki_body": "thumb #978909 thumb #341111 thumb #845222\r\n\r\nA tag for dinosaurs possessing [[feathers]], whether they be a [[feathered crest|crest of feathers upon their heads]], [[tail feathers]], [[winged arms|winged claws/arms]] and/or completely feathered bodies, [[feathered wings]], or all of the above.\r\n\r\nOriginally, dinosaurs with feathers were unheard of in the scientific field. However, during a historical period known as the \"dinosaur renaissance\" scientists realized dinosaur's relationship with birds, and eventually came to the conclusion that birds are the modern descendants of [[theropod|theropods]].\r\n\r\nWith this now being relatively common knowledge, more reconstructions and imaginings of dinosaurs have been including dinosaurs with feathers. Fossils have also been discovered with evidence of feathered dinosaurs, one of the most well known being the fossils of [[archaeopteryx]].\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[avian|avians]] or [[bird|birds]]; while birds technically can be considered the modern version of feathered dinosaurs, for tagging purposes they are not referred to as such.\r\n\r\nh4. Related\r\n\r\n* [[dinosaur]]\r\n** [[theropod]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n\r\n* [[feathers]]\r\n** [[feathered dragon]]"
        },
