          "prick_ears": [
            {
              "tag": "prick_ears",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 20766,
              "wiki_body": "[b]Prick ears[/b], known by several names such as [b]erect ears[/b] or [b]perked ears[/b], are a type of ear.\r\nAs the name(s) implies, the ear is \"pricked\" or \"erect\", tapering at a pointed end. They are always upwards pointing and upright. These ears are traditionally seen on [[wolf|wolfish looking]] [[domestic dog|dog breeds]] as well as various [[canid|canids]].\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[cropped_ears]], in which the whole or part of their external ears (pinnae/auricles) are surgically removed for cosmetic purposes. Cropped ears can be most commonly seen in certain breeds like [[boxer_(dog)|Boxers]], [[Pit Bull|Pit Bulls]], [[Pinscher|Pinschers]] and [[Schnauzer|Schnauzers]].\r\n* [[ear_tuft]]\r\n* [[humanoid_pointy_ears]], which can be seen as the [[humanoid]] equivalent of prick ears.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:feral_anatomy]]\r\n\r\n* [[canid]]\r\n** [[canine]]\r\n*** [[canis]]\r\n**** [[domestic_dog]]\r\n**** [[jackal]]\r\n**** [[wolf]]\r\n*** [[fox]]\r\n\r\n* [[floppy_ears]]\r\n* [[long_ears]]"
            }
