        "floppy_ears": {
          "_Self (floppy_ears)": [
            {
              "tag": "floppy_ears",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 60561,
              "wiki_body": "[i]\"Ears that droop down\"[/i] — this can be subdivided into lop ears and button ears (but not all ears may cleanly fall into these categories).\r\n\r\nh5. [[Lop Ears]]\r\n\r\nthumb #2807793 thumb #3914364 thumb #2738560\r\n\r\nEars that hang down from the point where they connect to the head, covering the ear canal. They are typically long and fall to the sides of the head. Rabbits, dogs and goats, among other species, may be seen with lop ears.\r\n\r\nh5. [[Button Ears]]\r\n\r\nthumb #2527784 thumb #3461720 thumb #3896772\r\n\r\nEars with tips that fold over and droop down, these are mostly seen in specific dog breeds but may also be drawn on pigs, or other canines.\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[big ears]]\r\n* [[long ears]]\r\n* [[fluffy ears]]\r\n"
            }
          ],
          "lop_ears": [
            {
              "tag": "lop_ears",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 8816,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #2878828 thumb #2807793 thumb #3914364 thumb #2738560\r\n\r\nFloppy ears that naturally hang down from the point where they connect to the head, covering the ear canal. \r\n\r\nLop ears may fall to the sides or back of the head, and are typically long. While the term \"lop\" is often associated with rabbits - dogs, goats and other species may be seen with lop ears.\r\n\r\nThis should not be tagged if the character's ears are being pushed down or tied back.\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[floppy ears]]\r\n** [[button ears]]\r\n* [[long ears]]\r\n* [[big ears]]\r\n* [[fluffy ears]]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n"
            }
          ]
