            {
              "tag": "spear",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 10067,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #3787519 thumb #3768353 thumb #3556954 thumb #3718156 thumb #2731538\r\n\r\nThe original [[polearm]]. The spear is as simple as it gets: a shaft - usually of wood - with a pointed head on the end. It's primary purpose is to let the user [[stab]] an opponent from a safer distance. It can also be [[throwing|thrown]], to strike opponent from even farther away.\r\n\r\nThe spear is very probably the single most used weapon in the history of warfare - every single polearm variant, as well as the [[bayonet]], evolved from the spear.\r\n\r\nh4.Types\r\n* [[pike]] - A spear with a longer shaft.\r\n* [[lance]] - A spear made for mounted [[cavalry]].\r\n* [[javelin]] - A throwing spear.\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[bardiche]] \r\n* [[glaive]]\r\n* [[halberd]]\r\n* [[harpoon]]\r\n* [[lance_(weapon)]]\r\n* [[naginata]]\r\n* [[poleaxe]]\r\n* [[scythe]]\r\n* [[trident]] \r\n* [[swordstaff]]"
