            {
              "tag": "fake_ears",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 8943,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #2493844 thumb #3223005 thumb #2941903 thumb #3164043\r\n\r\n[b]Fake ears[/b] describes a set of \"wearable ears\", which resemble those of various animals. Fake ears are most often attached to a [[hairband]], and are frequently worn as a part of a costume - which may include other fake animal parts, such as gloves or a tail, and sometimes themed or [[animal print]] clothing. Fake ears may also be a part of other headgear, such as a hat, hood, or pair of headphones. Two of the most popular varieties of fake ears are [[fake cat ears]] and [[fake rabbit ears]].\r\n\r\n[quote]\r\n\r\nh5. Important Notes:\r\n\r\n* If there is no visible hairband or clothing that the ears are connected to, and the exact connection between the ears and head is obscured as well, [i]use your best judgment[/i]. \r\n** Fake ears will usually be of a different colour than the rest of the character's body, fur or scales \r\n* [[not furry|\"Non-furry\"]] characters - humans, and non-animal humanoids wearing fake ears are [b]still non-furry[/b]. \r\n** The species of what the ears are intended to resemble [b][i]should not be tagged[/i][/b] - a post with a human wearing fake rabbit ears does not get tagged as \"rabbit\", and they are not a [[rabbit humanoid]].\r\n\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\nh5. Types of Fake Ears\r\n* [[fake cat ears]]\r\n* [[fake cow ears]]\r\n* [[fake dog ears]]\r\n* [[fake equine ears]]\r\n* [[fake fox ears]]\r\n* [[fake human ears]]\r\n* [[fake pokemon ears]]\r\n* [[fake rabbit ears]]\r\n* [[fake tiger ears]]\r\n* [[fake wolf ears]]\r\n* [[ironic fake ears]]\r\n\r\nh5. Other \"Fake Parts\"\r\n* [[fake antennae]]\r\n* [[fake halo]]\r\n* [[fake horns]]\r\n** [[fake cow horns]]\r\n* [[fake tail]]\r\n* [[fake wings]]\r\n\r\nh5. Related Tags\r\n* [[animal print]]\r\n* [[costume]]\r\n** [[cosplay]]\r\n* [[hairband]]\r\n* [[humanoid]]\r\n** [[animal humanoid]]\r\n"
