            "tag": "pear-shaped_figure",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 4449,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #2561510 thumb #3866278 thumb #3637943 thumb #2418880 thumb #819459 thumb #2420737 thumb #3177528\n\nA [b]pear-shaped figure[/b] describes a character with [[wide hips]] paired with a narrower upper body and shoulders. They will have comparatively lower fat-mass around their torso/waist and commonly have thicker thighs and/or a larger butt. If the character has breasts, they will usually have [[small breasts|small]] to [[medium breasts|medium-sized breasts]], or, more loosely, breasts that are noticeably smaller in comparison to the size of the characters lower body and hips. This figure resembles a [[pear]], and is a commonly used term in fashion and beauty circles. \n\nThis tag can be applied to a range of similarly pear-shaped bodies (see examples above). A character doesn't [i]need[/i] to be chubby or overweight to be pear-shaped, but this figure is more common with chubby/overweight characters.\n\nh5. Features:\n\n* [[Thick Thighs]] | [[Huge Thighs]]\n* [[Wide Hips]] | [[Huge Hips]]\n* [[Belly]]\n* [[Butt]]\n* [[Slightly Chubby]]\n* [[Overweight]]\n\n[quote]\n\nh5. Tagging Notes\n\n[i][color=red][b]What isn't a Pear-Shaped Figure:[/b][/color][/i]\n\n* [b]Do not[/b] add this tag to characters who merely have wide hips or big butts (consider [[bottom heavy]] instead)\n* [b]Do not[/b] add this tag if the character's lower body only appears larger due to their pose or perspective (ie. a [[low-angle view]]), or [[butt shot]]/[[butt focus]] images where the character has no distinct figure)\n* Characters with pear shaped figures will [b]never[/b] have [[broad shoulders]] or [[hyper breasts]], and [i]rarely[/i] have [[huge breasts]]. \n* A character tagged as pear-shaped figure should [b]never[/b] be tagged as [[hourglass figure]] or [[voluptuous]], these are different body shapes.\n[/quote]\n\nh5. Pear Shaped Vs. Bottom Heavy:\n\n[section= Both tags describe characters with lower bodies that are wider than their upper bodies, however...]\n\n* pear-shaped is intended to be subtler, more realistic or natural\n** a pear shaped figure should always have a \"flow\" of curving out from a narrower upper body, to wider midsection/waist, to wide hips and thick thighs\n\nthumb #2818162 thumb #3320593 thumb #2363241 thumb #2718177\n\n* [[bottom heavy]] is broader, and often applies to exaggerated figures, sometimes with disproportionately wide lower bodies and very small upper bodies\n** bottom heavy figures usually have huge or hyper hips, thighs, and butt \n** bottom heavy can apply to [[semi-anthro]] characters, pear-shaped should not be used for semi-anthro or feral characters\n\nFor characters with [[toony]] proportions, and nearly spherical exaggerated lower bodies that resemble pears, see [[hyper pear]].\n\n[/section]\n\nh4. Related Tags:\n* [[short stack]] / [[Teapot_(Body_type)|teapot]]: These characters may have pear-shaped figures\n\nh4. See Also:\n* [[bottom heavy]]\n* [[curvy figure]]\n** [[hourglass figure]]: A character with shoulders and hips of equal width, and a narrow waist\n** [[voluptuous]]\n* [[Tag Group:Figures]]"
          },
          {
            "tag": "pearl_necklace",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 3235,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #2093200\r\n\r\nA [[necklace]] made of [[pearl_(gem)|pearls]] strung together, usually all white or off white. Pearl necklaces may be worn in multiple rows or with a second necklace, they are usually drawn tightly worn around the neck, but conversely, are sometimes shown hanging far down from the wearers neck. \r\n\r\nWearing a pearl necklace has several cultural associations, it may signify a character being wealthy (especially when worn with a fancy [[dress]] or [[evening gown]]), a \"professional woman\" (when worn with [[business attire]]), and most of all, have a heavy association with being worn by [[mature female|middle aged]] and [[elderly female|elderly]] women in media. \r\n\r\n[quote]h5. Not to be confused with:\r\n\r\n* [b][[Bead Necklace]][/b]\r\n** While visually similar, bead necklaces often have \"smaller spheres\" strung together\r\n\r\n* [b][[Prayer Beads]][/b]\r\n** Often shown worn as a necklace, these typically have far larger spheres, and are often either clearly made of wood and/or brightly coloured, unlike pearl necklaces.\r\n\r\n* [b][[Rosary]][/b]\r\n** Catholic prayer beads often worn as a necklace, but are clearly not pearls, often have a [[cross]] pendant\r\n\r\n* [b][[Cum on Neck]][/b]\r\n** A sexual act that is referred to in slang as a \"pearl necklace\"[/quote]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also: \r\n* [[pearl (gem)]]\r\n* [[necklace]]\r\n* [[jewelry]]"
          },
