            "kor": "",
            "count": 123,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #881495   thumb #1770779   thumb #2131477   thumb #3171393   thumb #3840463   thumb #4535779\r\n\r\nAn [color=general][b]insult of endearment[/b][/color] is an [[insult]] used as a [[term of endearment]]. \r\n\r\nAt face value, the words are abrasive, but careful attention to context indicates it was made either in jest, instead being used to convey playfulness or affection and lacking serious hurtful intent. A multi-word insult of endearment may consist of a traditional term of endearment mixed with an insulting adjective, in which case it is more apparent. May also be juxtaposed to an explicit declaration of positivity, such as \"[[I love you]]\".\r\n\r\nUsing insults of endearment are a signature of a [[flustered]] [[tsundere]]. Often overlaps with [[teasing]], [[humiliation]], and [[kinkshaming]], with it being hard to discern during [[bullying]] or [[degradation]]. In extreme cases, the insulting word may be an appropriated [[slur]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[baka]] — the archetypal Japanese insult of endearment.\r\n* [[dialogue]]\r\n** [[talking_to_another]]\r\n** [[talking_to_partner]]\r\n** [[talking_to_viewer]]\r\n* [[insult]] — the negative connotation.\r\n* [[teasing]]\r\n* [[term_of_endearment]] — the positive intonation.\r\n* [[tsundere]] — practitioner of insults of endearment.\r\n\r\n"
