              "wiki_body": "A character with their eyes closed. If you can not see the other eye, assume it is closed as well.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[one eye closed]] - when only one eye is closed (unintentionally).\r\n* [[half-closed eyes]] - when both eyes are closed halfway.\r\n* [[wink]] - when a character is intentionally closing one eye.\r\n\r\n* [[looking at viewer]]\r\n* [[looking away]]\r\n* [[looking back]]\r\n* [[looking down]]\r\n* [[looking up]]"
            }
          ],
          "eyes_always_closed": [
            {
              "tag": "eyes_always_closed",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 393,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #1815910\r\n\r\nCharacters with [i]eyes always closed[/i], often seen in [[anime]] and [[manga]], are a character feature and a general character trope. Similar to [[eyes closed|fully closed eyes]], the character has permanent (or almost always permanent) horizontal lines where their eyes normally would be. However, unlike closed eyes, the character still looks and behaves as if their eyes are open, implying either an incredibly heavy [[squint]] with minimal strain or eyes that are [[eyes mostly closed|almost fully closed]]. This trope is often used to denote wisdom or other similar character traits, often referred to as [i]kitsune no me[/i] ([i]キツネの目[/i], \"fox eyes\" or \"shifty eyes\") in Japanese media.\r\n\r\nThe tag is not to be used if the character just appears with plain closed eyes as if they were [[blinking]], [[sleeping]], etc. The base eyes closed tag would instead apply, due to a lack of in context cues to indicate the use of said eyes. This also does not apply if the character's eyes are shown half or just slightly open, with [[half-closed eyes|eyes half closed]] or [[eyes mostly closed|mostly closed eyes]] being more appropriate instead.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[eyes_mostly_closed]]\r\n* [[horizontal_pupils]]\r\n* [[squint]]"
            }
          ],
