              "wiki_body": "thumb #5461498 thumb #5405329 thumb #5176552\n\nA protruding portion of a character's face, consisting of its nose, mouth, and jaw. In many animals, the equivalent structure is called a muzzle, rostrum, or proboscis. \n\nThis does not apply to flat-faced characters, common among humanoids and even a few anthro characters.\n\nh4. Related tags:\n\n* [[blocky_snout]] - [[loona_(helluva_boss)|Loona]] from [i][[Helluva Boss]][/i] and [[legoshi_(beastars)|Legoshi]] from [i][[Beastars]][/i] are both examples for this type of snout.\n* [[long_snout]]\n* [[rounded_snout]] - This is common with [[toony]] characters.\n* [[scaled_snout]]\n* [[short_snout]]\n* [[snout_overhang]]\n* [[tapering_snout]]\n\nh4. Snout actions:\n\n* [[snout_fuck]]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[beak]]\n* [[long_mouth]]\n* [[muzzle_(object)]]\n** [[muzzled]]\n* [[proboscis_(anatomy)]]\n** [[invertebrate_proboscis]]\n** [[trunk_(anatomy)]]"
