            "wiki_body": "thumb #1469431 thumb #869133 thumb #1320644 thumb #1405845\r\n\r\nTagged for posts that cannot be considered even remotely furry. \r\n\r\nDo not use if the post contains a mix of furry and non-furry characters.\r\n\r\nNote that furry refers to the fandom, not to actual fur. For example, furless animals such as birds and reptiles still count as 'furry'. The term is used in a loose sense, and includes frequently debated things such as [[animal_humanoid|kemonomimi]] and [i][[My Little Pony]][/i].\r\n\r\nThe following lists contain some examples of what is and isn't furry, but the lists are not all-inclusive.\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Non-furry:]\r\n\r\n* [b][[human]][/b] characters are the most obvious.\r\n** [b][[humanized]][/b] characters that would normally be considered furry, such as those from [i][[Equestria Girls]][/i]\r\n* [b][[humanoid]][/b] races such as [[elf]], [[orc]], [[troll]], [[goblin]], [[gargoyle]], [[ogre]], [[cyclops]], and [[gnome]]\r\n* human-like [[alien|aliens]], [[angel|angels]], [[demon|demons]], [[monster|monsters]]\r\n* [[mechanical]] characters such as [[robot|robots]] ([[android]], [[mecha]], etc.)\r\n* [[golem|golems]], [[flora_fauna|plants]], [[goo_creature|goo creatures]], [[tentacles]] (particularly when they are only interacting with human characters)\r\n* [[zero pictured]] - A pretty landscape, a toaster, a car, and other miscellaneous things\r\n\r\n[b]Bold[/b] - in all cases\r\nRegular - in many cases, excluding things like \"an [[angel]] [[fox]]\" or \"a [[robot]] [[dragon]]\" [/section]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Furry:]\r\n\r\n* [[anthro]], [[feral]], [[centaur]], [[minotaur]], [[naga]], [[scalie]]\r\n* [[animal humanoid]] (kemonomimi) - Humanoids with minor animal characteristics. This includes some [[monster_girl_(genre)|monster girls]], such as harpies.\r\n* [[chimera]] if they have animal parts.\r\n* [[photomorph]] of real-life humans into furry is considered furry (note that real photos are generally discouraged)\r\n* [[robot|robots]] and [[animatronic|animatronics]] that are modeled to look like feral or anthro animals.\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with:\r\n* [[not_furry_focus]], which is used when the main focus is not furry but there are still furries present\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n* [[human_focus]]\r\n* [[human_only]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[anthro]]\r\n* [[feral]]\r\n* [[humanoid]]\r\n** [[animal_humanoid]]\r\n** [[humanoid_focus]]\r\n* [[taur]]\r\n\r\nh4. Tagging projects:\r\n\r\n* {{not_furry ~anthro ~feral}} should return no hits, usually in need of clean-up"
