            "kor": "글램퍼",
            "count": 1208,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #4356 thumb #5210 thumb #4022 thumb #11937 thumb #5295 thumb #59102\r\n\r\n[b]Glamfur[/b] was an art trend popular in the early 2000s, primarily with teenage artists on sites such as [[DeviantART]], [[FurAffinity]] and [[Livejournal]], as well as being popular on VCL before its closure.\r\n\r\nThe style often features [[unusual anatomy]] and stylistic choices such as large foreheads. Fashion inspiration is taken from several [[alternative fashion]] styles, such as [[goth]] (particularly [[mall goth]] and [[cybergoth]]), [[visual kei]], and [[emo]]. Body modifications, both the extreme and mundane, are also common.\r\n\r\nCommon thematic elements include [[crossdressing]] and LGBT+ themes, [[medical]] imagery, [[gore]] and other common horror traits, and mental illness.\r\n\r\nSome notable artists for the style include [[Zeriara]], [[Chival]], [[vera_(artist)|Vera]], [[Leelee Lenox]] and [[Psychodjinn]]. The [[Langurhali]] species, created by Vera in 2004, are also associated with the trend.\r\n\r\nthumb #4163975 thumb #4613979 thumb #4129541\r\n\r\nIn the 2020s, a sort of \"resurgence\" has occurred, bringing [[sparkledog]]s and [[scene_(fashion)|scene fashion]] into the mix while maintaining the elements of the original glamfur style.\r\n\r\nh5. External links\r\n* \"Glamfur Zine\":https://twitter.com/glamfurzine\r\n* \"What is Glamfur?\":https://glamfur.livejournal.com/10310.html on LiveJournal\r\n* \"Glamfur Archive\":https://www.tumblr.com/glamfurarchive on Tumblr\r\n* \"Glamfur FurAffinity club\":https://www.furaffinity.net/user/glamfur/\r\n* \"Vixen Controlled Archive\":https://vixencontrolled.net (An archive of VCL)"
