            "count": 1186,
            "wiki_body": "Compound eyes, commonly seen in [[Arthropod|Arthropods]] such as [[insect|insects]] and [[crustacean|crustaceans]], may consist of thousands of individual photoreceptor lenses which in themselves form the compound eyes. Compound eyes, when compared to simple eyes, can have enhanced abilities such as possessing large viewing angles and the ability to detect fast movement.\r\n\r\nCompound eyes are also present occasionally in [[worm|worms]] and [[bivalve|bivalves]].\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with:\r\n* [[multi_eye]], as compound eyes are individual lenses and rods making up the surface of a single eye and aren't multiple eyes inherently.\r\n\r\nh4. Related:\r\n* [[arthropod]]\r\n** [[insect]]\r\n* [[crustacean]]\r\n* [[mollusc]]\r\n** [[bivalve]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:feral_anatomy]]\r\n* [[eyestalks]]\r\n* \"wikipedia entry\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye#Compound_eyes\r\n** \"wikipedia entry on arthropod eyes\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arthropod_eye\r\n** \"wikipedia entry on mollusc eyes\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mollusc_eye"
