          {
            "tag": "circle_eyes",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 125,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #693005 thumb #1948721 thumb #2070877 thumb #3105833 thumb #4014224\r\n\r\n[b]Circle eyes[/b] (🇯🇵:丸目 [i]maru-me[/i]), or [b]zero eyes[/b] (🇯🇵:○目 [i]zero-me[/i]), is an artistic trope pertaining to a character's eyes for some expressions, originating from manga and anime. \r\n\r\nCircle eyes are generally solid [[white sclera|white]] with [[no pupils]] or irises, with a black outline around it. They do not have to be perfect circles, nor do they have to be those colors as they could potentially be the color of what the character's sclera or iris normally are. The outline may vary in thickness and neatness, with sloppier lines often indicative of distress. It may also be disrupted to allow for [[tears]]. Along with other facial features, circle eyes may be used to express when a character feels overwhelmed; shocked; startled; scared; or foolish upon a realization. It may also be used to convey a wild or distant look for angry, monstrous, crazy, or disassociating characters.\r\n\r\nDiscretion should be used when tagging characters whose eyes are naturally solid and does not have any pupils or irises, or have been drawn in a [[simple eyes|simplified]] art style.\r\n\r\nh4.See also\r\n\r\nh6.Tags \r\n* [[empty eyes]]\r\n* [[hollow eyes]]\r\n* [[simple eyes]]\r\n* [[wide eyed]]\r\n\r\nh6.External sources\r\n* Japanese With Anime — \"Circle Eyes\":https://www.japanesewithanime.com/2020/04/circle-eyes.html\r\n* TvTropes — \"Blank White Eyes\":https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BlankWhiteEyes"
          },
