              "wiki_body": "thumb #3140696 thumb #1359980 thumb #3036204 thumb #1723799  thumb #1749460\r\n\r\n[b]Huge thighs[/b] describe characters with [i]very[/i] large thighs - ranging from head-turning but entirely realistic (sometimes [i]surprisingly[/i] realistic), to exaggerated but believable. Characters with huge thighs will usually have equally [[huge hips]]; they may be [[overweight]] or [[obese]], have a [[curvy figure]] or be considered [[voluptuous]]. Less commonly, huge thighs might be the result of the character having [[big muscles]]. \r\n\r\n[quote]\r\n\r\nh5. Tagging Notes \r\n[i]As this tag is the grey area between completely realistic \"thick thighs\", and the entirely fantastical world of \"hyper thighs\", it can be hard to determine when to tag huge thighs over thick or hyper. Some helpful rules of thumb:[/i]\r\n\r\n* Huge thighs should generally have an upper limit of twice the width of the character's waist, if [b]one[/b] of the character's thighs is more than twice as wide as the character's waist, \"hyper thighs\" may be more appropriate\r\n* A character with huge thighs will rarely, if ever, have a thigh gap, when standing normally, their upper thighs will touch. If the character's thighs are small enough to have a thigh gap, \"thick thighs\" is likely more appropriate\r\n* [b]Proportions are important[/b], if the character is overweight/obese, or a [[short stack]]/[[teapot_(body_type)|teapot]], thighs that might be considered \"hyper\" on a slimmer figure can be safely tagged as \"huge thighs\"\r\n\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n\r\n* [[thick thighs]]\r\n** [b]huge thighs[/b]\r\n** [[hyper thighs]]"
