              "count": 97559,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #3757751 thumb #3097094 thumb #2682073\n\n[b]Armor[/b] is any type of protective covering that prevents damage or, at the very least, mitigate it. Be it from impact to hazardous conditions. Coverage varies from vitals only to full body. Armor is often segmented into individual pieces, allowing the wearer to move around.\n\nNote that armor is considered 'clothing' when tagging [[nude]], [[fully clothed]], etc.\n\n[section,expanded=Types]\n* [[Brigandine]] (Metal plating sewn or riveted underneath cloth or leather)\n* [[Chainmail]] (Metal ring mesh)\n* [[Lamellar Armor]] (Laced together rectangular plates)\n* [[Laminar Armor]] (Rows of overlapping plate bands)\n* [[Living Armor]] (A living creature worn as armor)\n* [[Ornamental Armor]] (Armor made for fashion rather than protection)\n* [[Plate Armor]] (Large fully-encasing plating)\n* [[Plate Mail]] (Chainmail with embedded plates)\n* [[Power Armor]] (Mechanically assisted armor)\n* [[Scale Armor]] (Cloth or leather backing covered in scale plates)\n* [[Splint Armor]] (Cloth or leather backing covered in rows of plate strips)\n* [[Studded Armor]] (Cloth or leather armor studded with metal rivets)\n[/section]\n\n[section,expanded=Styles]\n* [[Battle Armor]] ([[Saiyan]]/[[Frieza]] Force armor)\n* [[Bikini Armor]] ([[Bikini]]-shaped armor)\n* [[Boob Armor]] (Armor with [[breasts]])\n* [[Feral Armor]] (Armor designed for [[feral]]s)\n* [[Full Armor]]\n* [[Futuristic Armor]]\n* [[Improvised Armor]]\n* [[Mandalorian Armor]]\n* [[Medieval Armor]]\n* [[Ornate Armor]] / [[Detailed Armor]]\n* [[Print Armor]]\n* [[Protogen Armor]]\n* [[Riot Gear]]\n* [[Samurai Armor]] / [[Japanese Armor]]\n* [[Segmented Armor]]\n* [[Skimpy Armor]] (Revealing armor)\n* [[Spiked Armor]]\n* [[Tribal Armor]]\n* [[Unconvincing Armor]] (Armor with little to no protective value)\n[/section]\n\n[section,expanded=Materials]\n* [[Diamond Armor]]\n* [b][[Metal Armor]][/b]\n** [[Bronze Armor]]\n** [[Gold Armor]]\n** [[Silv