          "unconvincing_armor": {
            "_Self (unconvincing_armor)": [
              {
                "tag": "unconvincing_armor",
                "kor": "",
                "count": 6326,
                "wiki_body": "thumb #64400 thumb #64200 thumb #14553 thumb #7876 thumb #4620083\r\n\r\nA suit of [[armor]] that - even when complete and worn as intended - doesn't appear to adequately protect the wearer.\r\n\r\nSuch armor doesn't seem reasonably protective against plausible dangers to the character when in peril, without suspension of disbelief. Ignore information from outside sources, like invisible magic, lore, or game mechanics, per [[tag what you see]].\r\n\r\nFor example, any \"armor\" that fails to properly cover the torso and/or abdomen qualifies, as both of those body parts contain vital organs like the [[lung| lungs]], [[heart (organ)| heart]], and [[intestines]]. Often, this armor doesn't cover any more than the wearer's shoulders, [[breasts]], and [[genitals]]...if it even covers [i]that[/i] much. (In which case, consider [[ineffective_clothing]] as well.)\r\n\r\nIn essence, anyone using such armor in real combat is very likely to become a casualty in short order.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[armor]]\r\n** [[chainmail_bikini]]\r\n* [[convincing_weapon]]\r\n* [[ineffective_clothing]] - When a character wears [[clothing]] that doesn't adequately cover their more private areas ([[genitals]], [[butt]], and/or [[breasts]]/[[nipples]]) when worn normally, but is still intended to be a \"complete\" set of attire.\r\n* [[mostly_nude]] - When a character is wearing [[clothing]] that doesn't cover anything around the torso region (including groin).\r\n* [[skimpy]]\r\n* [[full_armor]] - The polar opposite of this tag."
              }
