              "wiki_body": "thumb #2682073 thumb #1250734 thumb #274741\r\n\r\n[b]Power Armor[/b] (also known as [b]battlesuit[/b], [b]powersuit[/b], [b]mech suit[/b], or  [b]robot suit[/b]) is a wearable mobile [[machine]] with an on-board power supply and a combination of technologies that allow for limb movement with increased strength, endurance, speed and provide additional features.\r\n\r\nAnd it protects you. I mean, it wouldn't be power [i][[armor]][/i] if it didn't.\r\n\r\nh4.Not to be confused\r\n* [[Mecha]] - The key difference here is if the operator inside is still [i]wearing[/i] the machine (as in their limbs are inside the machine's limbs) as opposed to driving/piloting it (the limbs are entirely robot operated inside).\r\n* [[Exosuit]] - Although both serve the same function of enhancing the wearer's performance via mechanical assistance, exosuits have little to no armor plating. Leaving the wearer exposed.\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n* [[exosuit]] - When you strip the armor plating away leaving only exoskeleton frame.\r\n* [[futuristic armor]]\r\n* [[machine]]\r\n** [[mecha]]\r\n** [b]power armor[/b]"
