        "disembodied_hand": {
          "_Self (disembodied_hand)": [
            {
              "tag": "disembodied_hand",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 46796,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #5094837 thumb #3598747\nA hand, or arm that visibly doesn't attach to, or associate with a body within the scene. The hand may be coming from offscreen.\n\nh4. Not to be confused with\n\n* [[detached_hand]] - A hand that can be detached, and reattached.\n* [[floating_hands]] - Hands that are still associated with a body visible in the scene. \n* [[severed_hand]] - Amputated hands do not count towards this tag.\n\nh4. Categories\n\n* [[ghost_hands]] - Translucent / magical hands fall under this term.\n\nh4. Character tagging\n\nDisembodied hands count as characters.\n\nTwo hands generally equates to one character, but sometimes the hand position will suggest multiple different characters. Check thumb positions. If the artist is nice, they will color code the hands.\n\nThese values assume one full bodied character as the focus.\n\n- 1-2 hands - Usually [[duo]], but might be [[trio]]. \n- 3 hands - Usually [[trio]], but might just be a [[group]].\n- 4 hands or more - Always [[group]], and might be a [[trio]].\n\nOther disembodied parts do not count as separate characters if they can be associated with one or more disembodied hands.\n\n* Almost always [[solo_focus]], but sometimes [[duo_focus]], or [[trio_focus]] will apply.\n* Except for very unusual circumstances, a disembodied hand will never be in focus compared to a figure with more details showing, or more important details (a [[headshot portrait]] is more important than a handshot)\n* Often seen with a [[disembodied_penis]]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[disembodied]]\n** [[disembodied_head]]\n** [[disembodied_mouth]]\n** [b]disembodied_hand[/b]\n** [[disembodied_penis]]\n** [[disembodied_balls]]\n** [[disembodied_leg]]\n** [[disembodied_foot]]\n* [[disembodied_tail]]\n\n* [[first_person_view]]\n* [[hands_everywhere]]\n\nh4. Forum discussion\n\n* forum #134072 - Disembodied hands: ambiguous_gender or no further mention? (Jul. 2014)\n* forum #150900 - Tag Implication: disembodied_hand -> ambiguous_gender (Jan. 2015) "
            }
