            "wiki_body": "thumb #1243025 thumb #361449 thumb #871385 thumb #519842\r\n\r\nThe character is [[standing]] with one foot in contact with the ground, and the other raised off the ground with the foot supporting no weight.\r\n\r\nDo not use this tag for movement related postures such as [[walking]] or [[running]]. These postures are better tagged as [[raised foot]] to avoid the `standing` implication. \r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[one_leg_up]] - This tag includes leg positions that would be considered raised from a standing position. This usually means that some part of the leg is elevated at or above the character's waistline. It is not exclusive to standing positions.\r\n* [[raised_foot]] - A depiction of a leg with a foot raised off the ground, but not usually raised higher than the waist if in a standing posture.\r\n\r\nh4. Related poses\r\n\r\n* [[lord_of_the_dance_pose]]\r\n* [[step_pose]]\r\n* [[tree_pose]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:pose]]\r\n\r\n* [[on_one_knee]]"
          },
          {
            "tag": "winged_arms",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 12215,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #609185 thumb #181193 thumb #227773\r\n\r\n[[Wings]] hybridized with arms, they have fully fledged opposable hands and arms with wingspan. [i]Wing arms[/i] generally replace the arms of [[biped|bipedal]] characters. They are commonly [[feathered wings]] or sometimes [[membranous wings]].\r\n\r\nA character with [i]wing arms[/i] is probably not [[feral]] because proper hands skew toward [[anthro]] or [[humanoid]] whereas ferals rarely have hands outside of [[dinosaur|dinosaurs]] like [[dromaeosaurid|raptors]].\r\n\r\nh4.Do not confuse with\r\n\r\n[b]No wings[/b] - Winged_arms implicates the [[wings]] tag. Do not tag if the character does not have credible wings. [i]Wing arms[/i] do not need to convince us of their ability to maintain flight or aid in gliding, but they must have some recognizable wing features along the arm.\r\n\r\n[b]Separate wings[/b] - Do not tag for normal, handless wings and normal, wingless arms appearing on the same character. Just tag [type]_[[wings]].\r\n\r\n[b]Claws, digits, \"partial hands\"[/b] - Do not tag for wings with incomplete, non-opposable hands. For wings with [[claws]] (and perhaps some digits) but not complete hands, consider tagging [[wing_claws]] instead. This is commonly seen on [[chiropteran|bats]] and fantasy scalies with [[membranous wings]].\r\n\r\n[b]No hands[/b] - An anthro or humanoid with no hands but convincingly flight-capable wings does not have [i]winged arms[/i] but should qualify for the [[realistic_wings]] tag instead. This tag can overlap with [[wing claws]].\r\n\r\n[b][[Feather hands]][/b] - Some [[feathered wings]] or wingless, feathery arms are drawn with extraordinarily flexible and strong feathers used as substitutes for fingers. They are usually unnaturally bent, perhaps holding or at least touching something, or may just look like palms with feather-shaped fingers. We tag this [[feather_hands]]. This tag was not meant to overlap with [i]winged arms[/i].\r\n\r\nh4.Related\r\n\r\n* wings\r\n** [[feather_hands]]\r\n** [[realistic_wings]]\r\n\r\nh4.See also\r\n\r\n* [[wings]]\r\n** [[butt_wings]]\r\n** [[head_wings]]\r\n** [[tail_wings]]\r\n** winged_arms"
          },
          {
            "tag": "muscular_arms",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 12002,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #2896838 thumb #2880558 thumb #3148094 thumb #3111105\r\n\r\n[b]Muscular Arms[/b] describes characters with [b][i]particularly[/i][/b] well defined arms, [i]regardless[/i] of the overall definition to, or shape of, the character's body. \r\n\r\n[quote]\r\n\r\nh5. Tagging Notes:\r\n\r\nh6. [b] Ideally, rather than the tag being applied to most [[muscular]] characters, who will inherently have muscular arms, this tag is more usefully applied to...[/b]\r\n\r\n* Characters who are not overly muscular enough to warrant the [[muscular]] tag:\r\n** [[Athletic]] bodied characters with particularly muscular arms\r\n** [[Slightly chubby|Chubby]], or [[overweight]] characters, with toned, muscular arms contrasting their overall \"softness\" or \"fatness\", these may fall under [[musclegut]]\r\n** [[Curvy figure|Curvy figured]] female characters with minimal muscular definition besides their arms\r\n* Muscular characters with arm muscles that are visibly more toned or larger than the muscles of the rest of their body\r\n* An image where a muscular character's arms are a visual focus or particularly noticeable (such as the second example above)\r\n\r\n[b] Muscular arms [i]should not be confused with[/i] [[thick arms]][/b]\r\n\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[muscular]]\r\n* [[muscular legs]]\r\n"
