            "wiki_body": "thumb #526730 thumb #2438434 thumb #2447778\r\n\r\nA character depicted with only one leg featuring little or no bending at the knee. This tag suggests that their other leg is [[bent_leg|bent]], but it is often unknown what state the other leg is.\r\n\r\nThis tag currently isn't used for standing positions or similar vertical positions in which the legs are pointing downward underneath the character. For these situations, the standing posture tags ([[straight_leg]], [[straight_legs]]) should be used instead. \r\n\r\nFor more than one leg in an extended position, use [[extended legs]] instead.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[lying]] - especially while [[on_side|on the side]] with [[raised_leg|leg raised]].\r\n* [[splits]] - Sometimes this tag counts as being straight instead of extended.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[bent_leg]]\r\n* [[extended_arm]]"
