          {
            "tag": "raised_leg",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 63003,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1676548 thumb #2664101 thumb #2331966\r\n\r\nPosts in which a single leg is raised up or away from the body, usually revealing genitalia. A raised hind leg could be a [[hiked leg]] when a character does it to [[peeing|urinate]]. It can also occur while engaged in [[sex]].\r\n\r\n* If both legs are raised e.g. if on back or in [[missionary position]], consider using [[legs_up]] instead.\r\n\r\nA raised leg is characterized by a foot that is elevated off the ground, and both the foot and knee should be raised to the same level or above that character's waist. For [[standing]] and related positions, the foot should still be elevated, but the leg positions should be extended out from under the character. A leg positioned directly underneath a character becomes [[one calf up]] instead. The [[raised foot]] tag is generally applicable to [[on one leg]] positions.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[knee_pulled_up]]\r\n* [[on_one_leg]] - Raised status for standing positions is treated differently than other positions. Positions that don't meet the definition of [[one leg up]] should probably be tagged as [[raised foot]] instead.\r\n\r\n[section=Posture examples]\r\n\r\nh5. [[Lying]]\r\n\r\n- Lying [[on front]] postures almost always should be tagged as [[one_calf_up]] / [[calves_up]] instead of `raised_leg`.\r\n\r\nthumb #2151965 thumb #3179759 thumb #3185452 thumb #2960013 thumb #2857291\r\n\r\nh5. [[Reclining]] / [[Sitting]]\r\n\r\nthumb #3320679 thumb #3064444 thumb #128012 thumb #2274646\r\n\r\nh5. [[Standing]]\r\n\r\n- Standing postures are restricted by how high the leg is elevated relative to a character's waist. Keep this in mind when deciding whether to tag as `raised_leg` or `raised_foot`.\r\n\r\nh6. Bipeds\r\n\r\nthumb #3379954 thumb #1467777  thumb #1480362 thumb #1681445 thumb #2702294\r\n\r\nh4. Feral anatomy\r\n\r\n- Raised leg generally apply to the hindlegs only. Raised foot may apply to any leg on a quadruped.\r\n- Upright postures involving both forelegs, or both hindlegs should be tagged as [[on_fore_legs]], and [[on_hind_legs]] respectively instead of typical raised tags.\r\n\r\nh5. Hindlegs ([[raised_hindleg]])\r\n\r\n thumb #2802736 thumb #3266220 thumb #2788537 thumb #2014124\r\n\r\nh5. Forelegs ([[raised_foreleg]])\r\n\r\n- Left example could pass as a `raised_leg`, and the right example as a `raised_foot`.\r\n\r\nthumb #2726300 thumb #2633996\r\n\r\nh5. Both\r\n\r\n- Treat forelegs as independent from hindlegs when checking raised status. These should not be tagged as [[legs_up]].\r\n\r\nthumb #3242041 thumb #2992047\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n- It is recommended to know the differences between these tags. These tags are different in the postures that they contain, and they do not tend to overlap with `raised_leg`.\r\n\r\n* [[legs_up]]\r\n* [[raised_calf]]\r\n* [[raised_foot]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Related poses\r\n\r\n* [[climbing_on]]\r\n* [[hiked_leg]]\r\n* [[leg_glider_position]]\r\n* [[one_leg_up]]\r\n** [[vertical_splits]]\r\n* [[step_pose]]\r\n* [[step_position]]\r\n\r\nh4. Interactions\r\n\r\n* [[holding_raised_leg]]\r\n* [[raised_leg_grab]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[legs_up]]\r\n* [[on one leg]]\r\n* [[raised_foot]]"
