            "kor": "",
            "count": 385,
            "wiki_body": "A [b]headscarf[/b] or [b]head scarf[/b] are scarves covering most or all of the top of a person's, usually women, hair and her head, leaving the face uncovered. A headscarf is formed of a triangular or square cloth folded into a triangle piece of fabric, with which the head is covered. Apart from the [[shemagh]] of the Middle East, headscarves worn by men are much less common and usually for practical purposes.\r\n\r\nh4. Tags About Scarfs\r\n\r\n* [[scarf]]\r\n\r\n[section=Tags About Scarfs]\r\n\r\n[section=Scarf Colors]\r\nh4. Scarf [[tag_group:colors|Colors]]\r\n\r\n* [[black_scarf]]\r\n* [[blue_scarf]]\r\n* [[brown_scarf]]\r\n* [[green_scarf]]\r\n* [[grey_scarf]]\r\n* [[orange_scarf]]\r\n* [[pink_scarf]]\r\n* [[purple_scarf]]\r\n* [[red_scarf]]\r\n* [[tan_scarf]]\r\n* [[white_scarf]]\r\n* [[yellow_scarf]]\r\n\r\n* [[monotone_scarf]]\r\n* [[multicolored_scarf]]\r\n** [[rainbow_scarf]]\r\n** [[two_tone_scarf]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=General]\r\n* [[cum_on_scarf]]\r\n* [b]headscarf[/b]\r\n* [[pattern_scarf]]\r\n** [[checkered_scarf]]\r\n** [[plaid_scarf]]\r\n** [[spotted_scarf]]\r\n** [[striped_scarf]]\r\n* [[pseudo_scarf]]\r\n** [[tail_scarf]]\r\n** [[tentacle_scarf]]\r\n** [[tongue_scarf]]\r\n* [[scarf_only]]\r\n* [[shared_scarf]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[tag_group:clothes]]\r\n* [[clothing]]\r\n** [[headwear]]\r\n*** [[headdress]]\r\n*** [b]headscarf[/b]"
