          {
            "tag": "legendary_trio",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 442,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #92256 thumb #547792 thumb #293483\r\n\r\n\"[b]Legendary trio[/b]\" is a popular, fanmade term in the [i][[Pokémon]][/i] fandom meant to refer to the main series' regions' [[Legendary Pokémon]], specifically a connected \"trio\". Each region has at least one, and these trios are connected together in origin and design. Two members of the trio are often game version exclusive and often are the version's \"mascot\", playing important roles in the plot and appearing on the game's box art. The third member often is made into a version mascot later on in a \"sister\" expansion game, with expanded upon lore. Some trios have a \"trio master\" who often oversee and lead them. Some trio masters aren't a member of the trio itself but are an outside creature instead.\r\n\r\nSome legendary trios often start out as [[legendary duo|legendary duos]] before the eventual third member is revealed. However, despite being connected as a trio, legendary duos turned into trios often have closer dynamics/relationships together than with their third member.\r\n\r\nThis tag requires the entirety of a trio in one post, interacting or not.\r\n\r\n[section=Kanto region legendary trio(s)]\r\n* [[legendary_birds]]\r\n** [[articuno]]\r\n** [[zapdos]]\r\n** [[moltres]]\r\n[/section]\r\n[section=Johto region legendary trio(s)]\r\n* [[legendary_beasts]]\r\n** [[raikou]]\r\n** [[entei]]\r\n** [[suicune]]\r\n[/section]\r\n[section=Hoenn region legendary trio(s)]\r\n* [[legendary_titans]]\r\n** [[regirock]]\r\n** [[regice]]\r\n** [[registeel]]\r\n* [[weather_trio]]\r\n** [[kyogre]]\r\n*** [[primal_kyogre]]\r\n** [[groudon]]\r\n*** [[primal_groudon]]\r\n** [[rayquaza]]\r\n*** [[mega_rayquaza]]\r\n[/section]\r\n[section=Sinnoh region legendary trio(s)]\r\n* [[lake_guardians]]\r\n** [[uxie]]\r\n** [[mesprit]]\r\n** [[azelf]]\r\n* [[creation_trio]]\r\n** [[dialga]]\r\n** [[palkia]]\r\n** [[giratina]]\r\n*** [[giratina_(altered_form)]]\r\n*** [[giratina_(origin_form)]]\r\n[/section]\r\n[section=Unova region legendary trio(s)]\r\n* [[forces_of_nature_trio]]\r\n** [[tornadus]]\r\n*** [[tornadus_(incarnate_form)]]\r\n*** [[tornadus_(therian_form) ]]\r\n** [[thundurus]]\r\n*** [[thundurus_(incarnate_form)]]\r\n*** [[thundurus_(therian_form) ]]\r\n** [[landorus]]\r\n*** [[landorus_(incarnate_form)]]\r\n*** [[landorus_(therian_form) ]]\r\n* [[tao_trio]]\r\n** [[reshiram]]\r\n** [[zekrom]]\r\n** [[kyurem]]\r\n*** [[black_kyurem]]\r\n*** [[white_kyurem]]\r\n[/section]\r\n[section=Kalos region legendary trio(s)]\r\n* [[aura_trio]]\r\n** [[xerneas]]\r\n*** [[xerneas_(active_mode)]]\r\n*** [[xerneas_(neutral_mode)]]\r\n** [[yveltal]]\r\n** [[zygarde]]\r\n*** [[zygarde_10%_forme]]\r\n*** [[zygarde_50%_forme]]\r\n*** [[zygarde_cell]]\r\n*** [[zygarde_complete_forme]]\r\n*** [[zygarde_core]]\r\n[/section]\r\n[section=Alola region legendary trio(s)]\r\n* [[light_trio]]\r\n** [[cosmog]]\r\n*** [[cosmoem]]\r\n**** [[solgaleo]]\r\n**** [[lunala]]\r\n** [[necrozma]]\r\n*** [[dusk_mane_necrozma]]\r\n*** [[dawn_wings_necrozma]]\r\n*** [[ultra_necrozma]]\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Related\r\n\r\n* [[guardian_tapu]]\r\n* [[legendary_duo]]\r\n* [[swords_of_justice]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[evolutionary_family]]\r\n* [[pokémon]]\r\n** [[pokémon_(species)]]\r\n*** [[legendary_pokémon]]\r\n** [[starter_trio]]"
