            "wiki_body": "An image that consists of five event / action states, otherwise known as frames. A panel of a comic usually counts as a single frame. A frame may have borders, or be without borders; frames may sometimes overlap.\r\n\r\nThis tag focuses primarily on [[comic]], and [[sequence]] themes at the moment. It might end up applying to unrelated images too, but the complexities of that have yet to be figured out. Sequences specifically have their own [[five_frame_sequence|concept tag]]. It is difficult to judge whether the sequence tag is a sub-concept to `five_frame_image`, or just a closely related theme. Sequences can realistically appear as part of a larger scoped image. \r\n\r\nA sequence with five, or more frames is also considered a [[multi_frame_sequence]].\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Layouts]\r\n\r\nTODO: Create\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[comic]]\r\n* [[sequence]]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Frame count tags]\r\n\r\n[i]The more image frames there are, the longer, and more complex the layout tends to be.[/i]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Basic frame counts (2-8)]\r\n\r\n* [[two_panel_image]]\r\n* [[three_frame_image]]\r\n* [[four_frame_image]]\r\n* [b]five_frame_image[/b]\r\n* [[six_frame_image]]\r\n* [[seven_frame_image]]\r\n* [[eight_frame_image]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=High frame counts (9-15+)]\r\n\r\n* [[nine_frame_image]]\r\n* [[ten_frame_image]]\r\n* [[eleven_frame_image]]\r\n* [[twelve_frame_image]]\r\n* [[thirteen_frame_image]]\r\n* [[fourteen_frame_image]]\r\n* [[max_frame_image]] - 15 or more frames\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Grid layouts]\r\n\r\n[i]Layout concepts apply to the entire layout.[/i]\r\n\r\n* [[grid_layout]]\r\n* [[staggered_grid_layout]]\r\n\r\n[i]Partial layout concepts apply to only a section. Currently regular grids are tagged through the respective grid count tags.[/i]\r\n\r\n* [[staggered_grid]]\r\n\r\n[section=Grid frame counts]\r\n\r\n[i]These tags do not apply to staggered grids.[/