          {
            "tag": "seven_frame_image",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 734,
            "wiki_body": "An image that consists of seven event / action states, otherwise known as frames. A panel of a comic usually counts as a single frame. A frame may have borders, or be without borders; frames may sometimes overlap.\r\n\r\nThis tag focuses primarily on [[comic]], and [[sequence]] themes at the moment. It might end up applying to unrelated images too, but the complexities of that have yet to be figured out. Sequences specifically have their own [[seven_frame_sequence|concept tag]]. It is difficult to judge whether the sequence tag is a sub-concept to `seven_frame_image`, or just a closely related theme. Sequences can realistically appear as part of a larger scoped image.\r\n\r\nA sequence with five, or more frames is also considered a [[multi_frame_sequence]].\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Layouts]\r\n\r\nTODO: Create\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[comic]]\r\n* [[sequence]]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Frame count tags]\r\n\r\n[i]The more image frames there are, the longer, and more complex the layout tends to be.[/i]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Basic frame counts (2-8)]\r\n\r\n* [[two_panel_image]]\r\n* [[three_frame_image]]\r\n* [[four_frame_image]]\r\n* [[five_frame_image]]\r\n* [[six_frame_image]]\r\n* [b]seven_frame_image[/b]\r\n* [[eight_frame_image]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=High frame counts (9-15+)]\r\n\r\n* [[nine_frame_image]]\r\n* [[ten_frame_image]]\r\n* [[eleven_frame_image]]\r\n* [[twelve_frame_image]]\r\n* [[thirteen_frame_image]]\r\n* [[fourteen_frame_image]]\r\n* [[max_frame_image]] - 15 or more frames\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Grid layouts]\r\n\r\n[i]Layout concepts apply to the entire layout.[/i]\r\n\r\n* [[grid_layout]]\r\n* [[staggered_grid_layout]]\r\n\r\n[i]Partial layout concepts apply to only a section. Currently regular grids are tagged through the respective grid count tags.[/i]\r\n\r\n* [[staggered_grid]]\r\n\r\n[section=Grid frame counts]\r\n\r\n[i]These tags do not apply to staggered grids.[/i]\r\n\r\n* [[four_frame_grid]]\r\n* [[six_frame_grid]]\r\n* [[eight_frame_grid]]\r\n* [[nine_frame_grid]]\r\n* [[ten_frame_grid]]\r\n* [[twelve_frame_grid]]\r\n* [[fourteen_frame_grid]]\r\n* [[max_frame_grid]] - 15 or more frames\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Staggered grid frame counts]\r\n\r\n[i]These tags do not apply to regular grids.[/i]\r\n\r\n* [[four_frame_staggered_grid]]\r\n* [[six_frame_staggered_grid]]\r\n* [[eight_frame_staggered_grid]]\r\n* [[nine_frame_staggered_grid]]\r\n* [[ten_frame_staggered_grid]]\r\n* [[twelve_frame_staggered_grid]]\r\n* [[fourteen_frame_staggered_grid]]\r\n* [[max_frame_staggered_grid]] - 15 or more frames\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n[section=Sequence layouts]\r\n\r\n* [[basic_sequence]]\r\n** [[linear_sequence]]\r\n\r\n* [[before_and_after]] - Two frame\r\n* [[three_frame_sequence]]\r\n* [[four_frame_sequence]]\r\n* [[multi_frame_sequence]]\r\n** [[five_frame_sequence]]\r\n** [[six_frame_sequence]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Row layout tags]\r\n\r\n[i]These tags define the image layout in terms of how many horizontal segments can be logically formed within the layout. This is not necessarily how many rows it has, but rather how many row-like segments there are.[/i]\r\n\r\nh4. Base forms\r\n\r\n[i]The most basic structure the image layout can form described as the number of row-like segments within the layout. The higher the number, the more complex the layout tends to be.[/i]\r\n\r\n* [[base_one_layout]]\r\n* [[base_two_layout]]\r\n* [[base_three_layout]]\r\n* [[base_four_layout]]\r\n* [[base_five_layout]]\r\n* [[base_six_layout]]\r\n\r\nh4. Strict row layouts\r\n\r\n[i]These tags maintain a strict definition of what is defined as a row, disallowing rows to be subdivided into column segments. These are subset concepts of their respective base layout tag.[/i]\r\n\r\n* [[one_row_layout]]\r\n* [[two_row_layout]]\r\n* [[three_row_layout]]\r\n* [[four_row_layout]]\r\n* [[five_row_layout]]\r\n* [[six_row_layout]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Layout element tags]\r\n\r\n[i]Tags in this group may apply to any part of a layout. Please do not confuse `_layout` with `_(layout)`[/i]\r\n\r\n* [[blockage_(layout)]]\r\n** [[horizontal_blockage]]\r\n** [[vertical_blockage]]\r\n* [[staggered_grid]]\r\n* [[staggering_(layout)]]\r\n** [[horizontal_staggering]]\r\n** [[vertical_staggering]]\r\n\r\n[/section]"
