              "count": 1605890,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #2460744 thumb #1085052 thumb #92521 \n\nThe [b]tail[/b] is a feature of most vertebrate animals located at the rear end of the torso. It is a flexible extension of the spinal column that serves a variety of purposes, acting as a counterbalance in [[felid|felids]], a communication signal in [[canid|canids]] and as a fly swatter in [[horse|horses]]. \n\nh4. Tail Tags:\n\nThis is a non-exhaustive list of tags used for tails.\n\n[section=Tail Colors]\nTags describing tail colors\n\nh5. [[tag group:colors|Color]] appearing\n\n* [[black_tail]]\n* [[blue_tail]]\n* [[brown_tail]]\n* [[green_tail]]\n* [[grey_tail]]\n* [[orange_tail]]\n* [[pink_tail]]\n* [[purple_tail]]\n* [[red_tail]]\n* [[tan_tail]]\n* [[white_tail]]\n* [[yellow_tail]]\n\nh5. Color number\n\n* [[monotone_tail]] - only one distinct color.\n* [[two_tone_tail]] - only two distinct colors.\n* [[multicolored_tail]] - at least two distinct colors.\n* [[multi_tone_tail]] - more than two distinct colors.\n** [[rainbow_tail]] - a rainbow of colors\n\nh5. Special coloration\n\n* [[countershade_tail]]\n* [[tail_markings]]\n** [[banded_tail]]\n** [[dipstick_tail]]\n** [[ringtail|ringed_tail]]\n** [[spotted_tail]]\n** [[striped_tail]]\n\n[/section]\n\n[section=Tail Appearance]\n\nh5. Global Size\n\n* [[small_tail]]\n* [[big_tail]]\n* [[huge_tail]]\n* [[hyper_tail]]\n\nh5. Proportions\n\n* [[short_tail]]\n* [[long_tail]]\n* [[thin_tail]]\n* [[thick_tail]]\n* [[thin_tail]]\n* [[line_tail]] \n* [[nub_tail]] \n\nh5. Shape\n\n* [[crooked_tail]] - A tail featuring sharp bends or changes in direction.\n* [[curled_tail]] - A tail with a smooth and strong curve that curls inwards (like pigs tail). It is treated separate from curved tails.\n* [[curved_tail]] - A tail featuring smooth curve(s). Generally used for gradual curves, and treated as separate from curled tails.\n* [[wavy_tail]] - A tail with multiple smooth curves (like a wave).\n* [[erect_tail]] - A complete straight tail, not to be confused with [[raised_tail]].\n\n* [[forked_tail]] - A tail forking in multiple ends.\n* [[scut_tail]] - A type of naturally really short tail with fur.\n* [[docked_tail]] - A tail kind of partially amputated, or with an amputated look. Usually look natural (or healed). Not to be confuse with [[scut_tail]] or [[amputated_tail]].\n* [[amputated_tail]] - The tail has clearly been amputated. Not something natural at all.\n* [[braided_tail]] - A braided tail.\n\nh5. End of tail\n\n* [[tail_tuft]] - A tuft of fur or feathers at the tip of a tail.\n* [[mace_tail]] - A tail ending with a mace.\n* [[spade_tail]] - A tail ending like a ♠.\n* [[tail_blade]] - A tail with or made of blade, usually ending with a blade.\n* [[rattle_(anatomy)]] - Successive rings at the tip of a tail, usually the [[rattlesnake]], that make a known snake sound\n\nh5. Types\n\n* [[furry_tail]] - A tail covered with fur.\n* [[fluffy_tail]] - A tail with a lot of soft fur.\n* [[scaly_tail]] - A tail covered with scales.\n* [[feathered_tail]] - A tail covered with feathers. Not to confuse with [[tail_feathers]].\n* [[tail_feathers]] - Prominent Flight Feathers that arise from a posterior, typically birds.\n* [[fish_tail]] - Finned tail common in marine life.\n* [[flaming_tail]] - A tail that is either made of fire or partially/completely covered in fire.\n* [[leaf_tail]] - A tail that is a [[leaf]], or very similar to a leaf.\n* [[snake_tail]] - A tail which is a snake (with snake head).\n* [[tentacle_tail]] - A tail made of tentacle(s).\n* [[fake_tail]] - A fake tail, not part of the character's body.\n\nh5. Parts\n\n* [[spiked_tail]] - A tail with [[spikes_(anatomy)|spikes]].\n* [[tail_ridge]] - A tail with row of blunt protrusions along the tail.\n* [[tail_blade]] - A tail with one or multiple blade(s), or made of blade(s).\n* [[tail_feathers]] - Prominent Flight Feathers that arise from a posterior.\n* [[tail_fin]]\n* [[tail_frill]]\n* [[tailfro]]\n\n* [[tail_dimple]]\n* [[tail_hand]]\n* [[tail_mouth]]\n* [[tail_penis]]\n* [[tail_pussy]]\n* [[tail_wings]]\n\nh5. Other\n\n* [[messy_tail]] - A messy looking tail, usually a [[furry_tail]].\n* [[glowing_tail]] - A glowing tail.\n\n[/section]\n\n[section=Tail Activity]\n\nh5. Position\n\n* [[raised_tail]]\n* [[tail_around_leg]]\n* [[tail_around_waist]]\n* [[entwined_tails]]\n* [[tail_aside]]\n* [[tail_between_legs]]\n* [[tail_in_pants]]\n* [[tail_in_mouth]]\n* [[tail_in_pussy]]\n* [[tail_in_ass]]\n* [[tail_pillow]]\n* [[tail_scarf]]\n\nh5. Active\n\n* [[balancing_on_tail]]\n* [[coiled_tail]]\n* [[entwined_tails]]\n* [[hanging_by_tail]] - Not to be confused with [[lifted_by_tail]].\n* [[tail_coil]] - Not to be confused with [[coiling]].\n* [[tail_gesture]]\n** [[tail_boner]]\n** [[tail_heart]]\n** [[tailwag]] - Currently being used for more than gestures. \n* [[tail_growth]]\n* [[tail_motion]]\n** [[tail_sway]]\n** [[tailwag]]\n\nh5. Passive\n\n* [[hand_on_tail]]\n* [[holding_tail]]\n* [[lifted_by_tail]] - Not to be confused with [[hanging_by_tail]].\n* [[tail_bite]]\n* [[tail_bondage]]\n* [[tail_fondling]]\n* [[tail_grab]]\n* [[tail_hug]]\n* [[tail_lick]]\n* [[tail_pull]]\n* [[tail_removed]] - The tail has just been amputated. Similar to [[amputated_tail]].\n\nh5. Sexual\n\n* [[tail_play]]\n** [[tail_masturbation]] - Any sexual stimulation to self that involves tail.\n*** [[autotailjob]]\n** [[tail_sex]] - Any sexual stimulation to a partner that involves tail.\n*** [[tailjob]]\n** [[tail_suck]]\n* [[tail_in_pussy]]\n* [[tail_in_ass]]\n\nh5. Vore\n* [[tail_vore]]\n* [[tail_first]]\n\n[/section]\n\n[section=Animal Humanoid Tails]\nSpecify when a tail of one species is used for another species, usually an [[animal_humanoid]] or [[kemonomimi]].\n\nThese tags can also be used for a [[hybrid]] species.\n\n* [[animal_tail]]\n** [[cat_tail]]\n** [[cow_tail]]\n** [[dog_tail]]\n** [[dragon_tail]]\n** [[fox_tail]]\n** [[horse_tail]]\n** [[lion_tail]]\n** [[lizard_tail]]\n** [[monkey_tail]]\n** [[mouse_tail]]\n** [[raccoon_tail]]\n** [[rodent_tail]]\n*** [[rat_tail]]\n** [[scorpion_tail]]\n** [[scut_tail]] ([[cervid]] and [[lagomorph]])\n** [[shark_tail]]\n** [[squirrel_tail]]\n** [[tiger_tail]]\n** [[wolf_tail]]\n\n[/section]\n\n[section=Tail Fashion]\n\n* [[clothing]]\n** [[tail_clothing]]\n*** [[tail_button_bottoms]]\n*** [[tail_warmer]]\n* [[accessory]]\n** [[tail_accessory]]\n*** [[tailband]]\n*** [[tail_bell]]\n*** [[tail_belt]]\n*** [[tail_garter]]\n*** [[tail_orb]]\n*** [[tail_ornament]]\n*** [[tail_ribbon]]\n**** [[tail_bow]]\n* [[jewelry]]\n** [[tail_jewelry]]\n*** [[tail_ring]]\n* [[piercing]]\n** [[tail_piercing]]\n* [[wraps]]\n** [[tail_wraps]] - Not to be confused with [[coiled_tail]].\n* [[markings]]\n** [[tail_markings]]\n* Other\n** [[tail_bag]]\n** [[tail_cuff]]\n\n[/section]\n\n[section=Other tags]\n\nh5. Other\n\n* [[prehensile_tail]] - A tail capable of prehensility : can hold objects.\n* [[head_tail]] - A tail placed behind the head.\n\nh5. Numbers\n\n* [[tailless]] - no tail (for a specie that usually have a tail). Not an amputation.\n* [[multi_tail]] - more than 1 tail\n* [[2_tails]]\n* [[3_tails]]\n\n[/section]\n\n[section=Underused tags]\n\n* [[barbed_tail]]\n* [[misplaced_tail]]\n* [[panties_on_tail]] / [[panties_around_tail]] / [[underwear_around_tail]]\n* [[tail_claws]]\n* [[tail_club]] / [[mace_tail]]\n* [[tail_slap]] / [[tail_swipe]] / [[tail_whip]]\n* [[tail_spin]]\n* [[tail_twist]]\n* [[tail_bag]]\n* etc.\n\n[/section]\n\nh4. Related tags\n\n* [[tail_condom]]\n* [[tail_censorship]]\n* [[cum_on_tail]]\n* [[fake_tail]]\n* [[buttplug_tail]]\n* [[tailmouth_(species)]]\n** See also: forum #192713 - miscategorized tag: Tail_mouth (May. 2016)\n\nh4. Other\n\n[section=Possible tag alias]\n[u]Editor's Note[/u]: I just list some here if someone decides to alias or clean them.\n\n* [[bobtails]] / [[fluffbob_tail]] -> [[bobtail]]\n* [[cotton_tail]] -> ?\n* [[giant_tail]] -> [[huge_tail]]\n[/section]"
