              "wiki_body": "A [b]wavy tail[/b] is a [[tail]] with smooth curves or changes in direction that give it a [i]wavy[/i] appearance. There must be at least two distinct curves to count as a wavy tail. If there is only a single smooth curve, either [[curved tail]] or [[curled tail]] should be used instead. If the bends aren't smooth, [[crooked tail]] should be used instead.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[crooked_tail]] - A tail featuring sharp bends or changes in direction.\r\n* [[curled_tail]] - A tail featuring a smooth curve that curls inwards. It is treated separate from curved tails.\r\n* [[curved_tail]] - A tail featuring a single smooth curve. Generally used for gradual curves, and treated as separate from curled tails."
