              "count": 181332,
              "wiki_body": "[b]Scales[/b] are rigid plate-like growths that arise from the dermal structures of the body and are made for defense. Scales come in many forms and sizes with fish scales generally being circle or half-moon shaped while reptile scales tend to take on angular geometric shapes but may also be pebbled shaped. Scale tend to be large in areas of that may often be exposed to stress and pressure while scales around joints tend to be smaller to allow for mobility. Scales are among the most diverse of all body surface in both form and color. Most common among Reptiles, Fish and Dragons, some mammals may also feature scales.\r\n\r\n* Please note [[bird feet|scaled avian feet]] and/or [[scuted arms|scaled avian arms]] do not count towards this tag group.\r\n\r\n* Please note [[arthropod]] chitin, carapace, and [[exoskeleton|exoskeletal structures]] do not count towards this tag group.\r\n\r\nthumb #1016836 thumb #514309 thumb #834118 thumb #631249 thumb #942578\r\n\r\nh4. Tags About Scales\r\n* [b]scales[/b]\r\n\r\n[section=Colors]\r\nh4. Scale [[tag_group:colors|Colors]]\r\n\r\n* [[black_scales]]\r\n* [[blue_scales]]\r\n* [[brown_scales]]\r\n* [[gold_scales]]\r\n* [[green_scales]]\r\n* [[grey_scales]]\r\n* [[orange_scales]]\r\n* [[pink_scales]]\r\n* [[purple_scales]]\r\n* [[red_scales]]\r\n* [[tan_scales]]\r\n* [[teal_scales]]\r\n* [[white_scales]]\r\n* [[yellow_scales]]\r\n\r\n* [[monotone_scales]] - only one distinct color\r\n* [[multicolored_scales]] - at least two distinct colors\r\n** [[multi_tone_scales]] - more than two distinct colors\r\n*** [[rainbow_scales]] - the entire spectrum of distinct colors\r\n** [[two_tone_scales]] - only two distinct colors\r\n\r\n* [[dark_scales]]\r\n* [[light_scales]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=General]\r\n* [[belly_scales]]\r\n* [[detailed_scales]]\r\n* [[drying_scales]]\r\n* [[facial_scales]]\r\n** [[scale_eyebrows]]\r\n* [[glistening_scales]]\r\n* [[glowing_scales]]\r\n* [[gradient_scales]]\r\n* [[m