            "wiki_body": "thumb #804290 thumb #756215 thumb #3638519 thumb #2294611 thumb #4818469\n\n\"General Muscle Guide\":https://i.imgur.com/5Hmm6w8.png\n\nThe [b]back muscles[/b] is an informal grouping of multiple muscles and tendons along the back, including the [[Trapezius]], Latissimus Dorsi, Extensor Spinae, Teres Major & Minor, Rhomboids and posterior head of the Deltoids.\n\nThese muscles generally contribute to shoulder blade movement as well as support and mobility of the spinal column. They also help maintain the upright posture and anchor other bones such as the shoulder blades to the spine.\n\nBack muscles are most easily visible thru the roughly diamond/kite shaped regions created by the [[Trapezius]] and/or Extensor Spinae when they are well developed, and less commonly furrows created by the boundaries of the Deltoids, Latissimus and uncovered portions of the Teres.\n\nIf the back muscles are well developed and visible in the picture then it should be tagged.\n\nh4. Tags On Muscles\n[section,expanded]\n[section=Muscles by location]\n[section=Head]\n* [[jaw_masseter]]\n[/section]\n[section=Torso]\n* [[abs]]\n* [b]back_muscles[/b]\n** [[trapezius]]\n* [[butt_muscles]]\n* [[latissimus_dorsi]]\n* [[neck_muscles]]\n** [[trapezius]]\n* [[obliques]]\n* [[pecs]]\n* [[serratus]]\n[/section]\n[section=Limbs]\n* arms\n** [[biceps]]\n** [[deltoids]]\n** [[forearm_muscles]]\n** [[triceps]]\n* legs\n** [[calf_muscles]]\n** [[hamstrings]]\n** [[quads]]\n* [[tail_muscles]]\n[/section]\n[section=Internal]\n* [[heart_(organ)]]\n* [[tongue]]\n[/section]\n[/section]\n[section=Muscles by size and presentation]\n* [[big_muscles]]\n* [[huge_muscles]]\n* [[hyper_muscles]]\n\n* [[athletic]] ~ lean muscle, fit\n* [[musclegut]] ~ chunky muscle, fat\n* [[muscular]] ~ chunky muscle, ripped\n* [[striated_muscles]]\n* [[synthetic_muscles]]\n* [[veiny_muscles]]\n[/section]\n[section=Muscles by gender]\n* [[muscular_ambiguous]]\n* [[muscular_male]]\n* [[muscular_female]]\n* [[