          {
            "tag": "stomach",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 5770,
            "wiki_body": "[quote] \r\n\r\nh5. [i]This tag [u]specifically refers to the organ in the body[/u], for [i]external[/i] depictions of [i]the abdomen[/i] where the stomach is located, [u]use [[belly]] or [[midriff]][/u].[/i] \r\n\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\nthumb #2429699\r\n\r\nThe [b]stomach[/b] is the [[organs|organ]] responsible for [[digestion|digesting]] food. The stomach secretes [[stomach acid]] to chemically break down ingested substances into [[chyme]], which is then further processed and absorbed by the [[intestines]].\r\n\r\nIn humans, and many mammals, it is a roughly \"J\"-shaped enlargement of the alimentary canal, located in the abdomen, linking the oesophagus to the small [[intestines]]; the shape, size, and even number varies by species, but anthropomorphic characters are rarely depicted with non-human stomachs.\r\n\r\nh5. Tagging Notes:\r\n\r\nThis tag applies to depictions of the internal organ, such as in anatomical diagrams or cross sections, as a disembodied symbolic image, [[internal]] views of characters, substances or objects within a stomach, or when a character has been traumatically injured and/or [[disembowelment|disembowelled]], exposing the stomach.\r\n\r\n\r\nh3. Stomach Related Tags\r\nMost of those tags does not imply stomach. The stomach itself must be visible for it to be tagged.\r\n\r\nh5. Depiction of stomach\r\n* [[stomach (symbol)]] — for simplified symbolic representations of a stomach, not a direct depiction of a character's stomach\r\n* [[gore]]\r\n** [[exposed_organs]]\r\n* [[xray_view]] - showing inside the body as if nothing was in front\r\n* [[disembodied_organs]] - depicted outside of the body for visibility (not outside of the body in the story)\r\n* [[internal]] - in case we could see inside the stomach\r\n\r\n\r\nh5. Stomach Contents\r\n* [[stomach acid]]\r\n* [[chyme]]\r\n* [[food in stomach]]\r\n* [[object in stomach]]\r\n* [[cum in stomach]]\r\n* [[fully_inside]] - a character is completely inside the body (in our case in the stomach)\r\n** [[inside stomach]] - a character is directly visible inside the stomach (imply an [[internal]] view)\r\n\r\n\r\nh5. Action from the stomach\r\n* [[digestion]]\r\n* [[digestion noises]]  — sounds of air, partially digested food, or liquids moving through the digestive tract\r\n* [[rumbling stomach]] — usually indicates a growling noise signalling hunger or indigestion, similar to digestion noises above\r\n* [[sloshing belly]] — sounds of liquid or semi-solids being moved inside of the stomach by the character moving their belly (e.g. jumping up and down, jiggling their belly with their hands)\r\n\r\n\r\nh5. Action of things going in Stomach\r\n* [[stuffing]]\r\n* [[oral]] - stimulating genitals using the mouth. Almost always involve [[cum in stomach]] if stomach is involved.\r\n* [[vore]] - scenario where a full character gets in a body\r\n** [[oral vore]]\r\n*** [[swallowing]] - if we see the action of swallowing\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[organs]]\r\n* [[esophagus]]\r\n* [[intestines]] \r\n"
