              "count": 97572,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #2934924 thumb #2541137 thumb #2699525 thumb #2684111\r\n\r\nA [b]dress[/b] is a one-piece garment that covers the body and extends down over the legs, typically worn by women. Dresses come in a very wide variety of styles and are worn in a broad variety of contexts and situations.\r\n\r\nh3. Dress Tags\r\n\r\nh5. Types of Dress \r\n\r\nh6. Dresses by Purpose, Theme, or Style\r\n\r\n* [[christmas dress]]\r\n* [[chinese dress]]\r\n* [[cocktail dress]]\r\n* [[evening gown]]\r\n* [[nurse dress]]\r\n* [[sundress]]\r\n* [[wedding dress]]\r\n\r\nh6. Dress Types by Construction\r\n\r\n* [[backless dress]]\r\n* [[frilly dress]]\r\n* [[hobble dress]]\r\n* [[open-butt dress]]\r\n* [[overall dress]]\r\n* [[sideless dress]]\r\n* [[slit dress]]\r\n* [[strapless dress]]\r\n* [[turtleneck dress]]\r\n\r\nh6. Dress Length\r\n* [[short dress]]\r\n* [[long dress]]\r\n\r\nh5. Dress Appearance\r\n\r\nh6. Miscellaneous Appearance\r\nThese tags describe something about the dress' appearance, but not based on specific elements of its construction or its purpose, these tags should be used in combination with tags above.\r\n\r\n* [[glistening dress]]\r\n* [[pattern dress]]\r\n* [[print dress]]\r\n* [[tight dress]]\r\n* [[torn dress]]\r\n* [[translucent dress]]\r\n* [[skimpy dress]]\r\n* [[wet dress]]\r\n\r\nh6. Minor Construction Elements\r\nThese tags describe design features that can alter the appearance of a dress, but aren't important enough to define the name of the dress. These tags should at least be paired with the `dress` tag. These tags are not limited to dresses.\r\n\r\n* [[halter neck]] — the front of the dress is held up by material that wraps around the wearer's neck\r\n* [[pelvic curtain]] — a long piece of material that hangs loosely over, and covers the wearer's crotch\r\n* [[plunging neckline]] — the neckline exposes the wearer's chest and abdomen\r\n* [[cutout]] — \"windows\" in the dress, exposing parts of the wearer's body\r\n** [[belly cutout]] — a large part of the wearer's abdomen is exposed\r\n*** [[navel cutout]] — a small window around the wearer's [[navel]]\r\n** [[cleavage cutout]] — the wearer's cleavage is shown through a window, with material on all sides\r\n\r\nh5. Interacting with Dresses\r\n\r\n* [[dress aside]]\r\n* [[dress pull]]\r\n* [[holding dress]]\r\n* [[raised dress]]\r\n* [[penis under dress]]\r\n** [[erection under dress]]"
