          "school_uniform": {
            "_Self (school_uniform)": [
              {
                "tag": "school_uniform",
                "kor": "",
                "count": 12561,
                "wiki_body": "thumb #1231965 thumb #704224 thumb #2117736 thumb #1900011\r\n\r\nA [b]School Uniform[/b] describes any outfit clearly designed to be worn by students of a school or other educational institution. School uniforms can come in many forms, and differ between countries and schools. \r\n\r\nh4. School Uniform Items:\r\nThe following lists common clothing used for school uniforms, or commonly depicted types of school uniforms seen in art. This is not an exhaustive list:\r\n\r\nh5. Unisex Items:\r\n\r\n* [[Jacket]] (or blazer), worn over a collared shirt.\r\n* [[Dress_shirt|Dress Shirt]] worn with or without a [[necktie]]\r\n* [[Polo_Shirt|Polo Shirt]] almost always with a school emblem or crest\r\n* [[Sweater]] or [[sweater_vest|Sweater Vest]] oftentimes a button up cardigan, and usually worn over a collared shirt\r\n\r\nh5. Girls' Items:\r\nGirls' school uniforms may be limited to unisex items, or combine one or more of the unisex items, with one or more of the following items below:\r\n\r\n* [[Blouse]] (or dress shirt)\r\n* [[Ribbons]] or [[Bow_tie|Bow Tie]]\r\n* [[Pleated_skirt|Pleated Skirt]] Commonly [[plaid]], black, blue or red\r\n* [[Stockings]], [[Thigh_highs|Thigh High Socks]],  or [[Knee_socks|Knee Socks]]\r\n* [[Mary Janes]]\r\n\r\nh4. Common Variants:\r\n\r\nh6.Western School Uniforms\r\nTypically combines the following:\r\n\r\n* Dress shirt/blouse (with or without tie), \r\n* Dress [[pants]] or [[shorts]] for both sexes, but usually only worn by boys \r\n* pleated skirt for girls (often tartan/plaid)\r\n* Sweater or sweater vest\r\n* Jackets (Blazer), usually with school insignia\r\n\r\nh6.Japanese School Uniforms\r\n* Boys may be depicted wearing a dress shirt, trousers and tie, or wearing a uniform called a [i]Gakuran[/i], which consists of a button-up jacket with a standing collar, and dress pants, these uniforms are always black, or dark blue.\r\n* [b][[Serafuku]][/b] or Sailor Fuku, a style of outfit that consists of a blouse (usually white), sailor-style collar, and pleated skirt (usually blue), worn with a ribbon, neckerchief or bow tie. This is the most well known style of Japanese school uniform, and is strongly associated with Japanese culture.\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n* [[Uniform]]\r\n* [[Student]]\r\n* [[Serafuku]]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[tag group:clothes|List of Clothing Related Tags]]"
              }
            ],
            "japanese_school_uniform": [
              {
                "tag": "japanese_school_uniform",
                "kor": "",
                "count": 2288,
                "wiki_body": " thumb #3110689 thumb #2277352 thumb #3094975 thumb #3146607 thumb #3227084\r\n\r\nThis tag collects various styles of [[school uniform]] unique to, or most commonly associated with, [[Japan]]. The two most well known, and easily identified styles of Japanese school uniform are the [[Serafuku]] (example 1 above), and lesser known, but distinctive [[Gakuran]] (example 2 above). While the Serafuku and Gakuran form the majority of this tag, it covers any style of school uniform that is clearly Japanese. \r\n\r\nFor example, \"Japanese school uniform\" can include uniforms [i]similar[/i] to the serafuku, but lacking the characteristic sailor-style collar that defines serafuku (see example 3), or uniforms that combine blazers/cardigans/sweaters, bows/neckties and pleated skirts.\r\n\r\nIf the style of uniform is not clearly Japanese, and/or commonly seen in other countries, use the generic [[school uniform]] tag instead.\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n* [[School Uniform]]\r\n* [[Serafuku]]\r\n* [[Gakuran]]\r\n\r\n"
