          "bunny_costume": [
            {
              "tag": "bunny_costume",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 9704,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #1851263 thumb #2626784 thumb #2699316 thumb #2255906 \r\n\r\nA [b]bunny costume[/b] is an outfit originally popularized by the female staff in Playboy clubs (\"Playboy Bunnies\"), this influence is seen with many depictions of characters in bunny costumes holding trays or acting as waitresses. \r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[rabbit_fursuit]] - A full body costume in the form of a rabbit.\r\n\r\n[quote]\r\n\r\nh6. The bunny costume typically consists of...\r\n\r\n* A pair of [[fake rabbit ears]], but has to be more than just rabbit ears.\r\n* A [[leotard]], [[one-piece swimsuit]], or [[teddy_(clothing)|teddy]], that covers the wearer's torso, while revealing their legs and upper chest/shoulders, sometimes showing [[cleavage]]\r\n* A fake rabbit tail affixed just above the wearer's butt, at the base of their spine \r\n* A [[shirt collar]] with a [[bow tie]]\r\n* A pair of [[shirt cuffs]] \r\n* [[fishnet legwear]] or [[pantyhose]]\r\n* [[high heels]]\r\n\r\nThe costume's design can vary wildly, omitting or altering elements of the costume. Bunny costumes are often changed to be more revealing — a [[navel cutout|navel cutout]] and/or [[cleavage cutout]], more [[cleavage]], a [[plunging neckline]] etc. \r\n\r\n* Bunny ears may be substituted for other animal ears, horns, or omitted entirely (especially when worn by [[anthro]] rabbit or [[rabbit humanoid]] characters)\r\n* The collar may instead have a [[necktie]] worn with it, or be entirely replaced with a [[bow accessory|bow]],  [[choker]], or other [[collar]]\r\n* The leotard/teddy/swimsuit may be switched for a [[corset]]-like top that reveals the wearer's midriff, usually worn with a [[thong]] or [[panties]]\r\n* [[Elbow gloves]] or [[white gloves]] may be worn with, or instead of, the shirt cuffs\r\n* May include [[stockings]], [[garter belt]] and [[garter straps]]\r\n\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n\r\n* [[reverse bunny costume]]\r\n* [[costume]]"
            }
