              "wiki_body": "thumb #2151337 thumb #1903086 thumb #993677 thumb #1525866\r\n\r\n[b]One-Piece Swimsuit[/b] generally describes a type of [[swimwear]] that is a single skin-tight garment. The [i]classic[/i] one-piece swimsuit resembles a [[leotard]], covering most of the upper body and crotch, usually with the exception of the back and upper chest. While usually referring to the swimsuit worn by women, male characters are sometimes depicted wearing them, and there are various one-piece swimsuits designed for men.\r\n\r\nh4. Variations\r\n\r\nMore revealing styles of the classic one-piece swimsuit design may feature plunging necklines that exposes the wearer's [[cleavage]] or entire [[midriff]]; others may have a [[cleavage_cutout|cutout]] for the cleavage or less commonly, the [[navel]].\r\n\r\nOne-piece swimsuits designed for athletics or diving, may extend to cover the wearer's upper legs, similar to [[shorts]], feature a zipper along the front, or cover the upper chest and neck.\r\n\r\nh4. Types of one-piece swimsuits:\r\n* [[school swimsuit]]\r\n* [[sling bikini]]\r\n* [[sharkini]]\r\n\r\nh4. Styles of one-piece swimsuits:\r\n* [[backless swimsuit]] ([[open-back swimsuit]])\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n* [[swimwear]]\r\n** [[bikini]]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n* [[tag_group:clothes|List of clothing related tags]]"
