            "count": 43227,
            "wiki_body": "The process of taking off your own, or another character's clothes. The opposite concept to [[dressing]].\n\nA character must be involved in the undressing process. Other situations in which a character's clothing is removed either fall under [[assisted exposure]], or [[wardrobe malfunction]] instead.\n\n[section,expanded=Examples]\n\nh5. One character\n\nthumb #2909844 thumb #63135 thumb #2868957 thumb #124269 thumb #2574338\n\nh5. Multiple characters\n\nthumb #18887 thumb #2555691 thumb #2566905 thumb #2306675 thumb #2377903\n\n[/section]\n\nh4. Subtags\n\n* [[forced_undressing]]\n** [[forced_to_undress]]\n* [[undressing_another]]\n** [[undressing_partner]]\n* [[undressing_crabs]]\n* [[undressing_self]]\n* [[undressing_spell]]\n\nh4. Not to be confused with\n\nA character that is undressing may involve these concepts, but [[exposed|exposure]] is not the same thing as undressing. The posturing should be consistent with a character taking their or another character's clothes off.\n\n* [[clothing_down]]\n* [[clothing_pull]]\n** [[panty_pull]]\n* [[flashing]]\n* [[partially_clothed]] - The undressing should be actively happening in a scene. Displaced clothing alone is not enough to qualify as undressing.\n* [[raised_shirt]]\n* [[shirt_lift]]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[assisted_exposure]]\n* [[clothing_gain]]\n* [[clothing_loss]]\n* [[dressing]]\n* [[flashing]]\n* [[forced_exposure]]\n* [[wardrobe_malfunction]]"
