            "wiki_body": "A character wearing [[clothing]] typically associated with their opposite gender.\r\n\r\nAs this tag is culture-specific, it generally is applied, as a tag, to male and female characters in specific ways. For [[male]]/masculine characters, it refers to wearing feminine clothing such as a [[dress]], [[skirt]], [[panties]], [[High_heels|high-heels]] and so on. Male characters who are crossdressing may use objects stuffed into their clothes to create [[fake breasts]]. For [[female]]/feminine characters, it means wearing masculine outfits such as a traditional [[tuxedo]], a [[suit]] and [[pants]] combination, as well as traditional pieces of clothing designated for males, like [[boxers_(clothing)|boxers]] or [[boxer briefs]].\r\n\r\nCrossdressing is to be apparent in the posting by [[TWYS]]. In cases where a character is known by lore to be of different gender as their appearance (including clothing) says, the [[trans_woman_(lore)]] and [[trans_man_(lore)]] tags should be used in addition to this tag.\r\n\r\n[b][i]Not to be confused with [[girly]][/i] - which refers to the physical build and demeanour of a male or andromorphic character rather than their outfit. However, girly characters may also crossdress. [/b]\r\n\r\nh4.Crossdressing Males:\r\nthumb #2240610 thumb #1477290 thumb #4099369\r\n\r\nh4.Crossdressing Females:\r\nthumb #404122 thumb #696515 thumb #17636\r\n\r\nh4.Related tags:\r\n* [[drag_(fashion)]]\r\n** [[drag_king]]\r\n** [[drag_queen]]\r\n* [[femboy]]\r\n* [[tomboy]]\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n* [[feminization]]"
