            "wiki_body": "thumb #1187573 thumb #877130 thumb #687331\r\n\r\nAn alternate style of dress is shown that contrasts from what a character normally wears. Alternately, a comparison of different sorts of [[clothing]] is shown on the same character. This doesn't necessarily mean any change in the character's general appearance, such as from a [[humanoid]] to a [[feral]] state or vise versa, but it often entail a change in artistic form, such as from [[traditional_media_(artwork)|traditional artwork]] to a [[digital_media_(artwork)|digital]] style or vise versa.\r\n\r\nFor official non-standard costumes, see [[official alternate costume]].\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n* [[clothed]]\r\n** [[clothing_swap]]\r\n** [[cosplay]]\r\n** [[costume]]\r\n** [[dress_up]]\r\n* [[clothing]]\r\n* [[style_parody]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[alternate_color]]\r\n* [[alternate_form]]\r\n* [[alternate_hairstyle]]\r\n* [[alternate_species]]"
