            "count": 2217,
            "wiki_body": "[[Clothing]] that a [[witch]] would wear, stereotypically a [[witch hat]], a [[black robe]]/[[black dress]], and may have a [[broom]]. Note that this tag should be used for characters that dress as a witch, but aren't actually one. A character that actually is a witch should just be tagged as \"witch\" and not use this tag."
          },
          {
            "tag": "chinese_dress",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 2121,
            "wiki_body": "A Chinese dress, known as cheongsam or qipao is a dress worn by women which takes inspiration from the ethnic clothing of the Manchu people. It is most often seen as a longer, figure-fitting, one piece garment with a standing collar, an asymmetric left-over-right opening and two side slits.\n\nA male version of [I][[cheongsam]][/I] is [I][[changshan]][/I] \n\nh4. See also\n* [[tag group:clothes]]\n* [[pelvic_curtain]]\n\nh4. External Link:\n\"Chinese dress\":https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheongsam"
          },
          {
            "tag": "cosplay_pikachu_(costume)",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 1943,
            "wiki_body": "When a character is wearing one of cosplay pikachu's costumes, such as the [[pikachu libre]] outfit. For cosplay pikachu specificallly wearing one of the outfits, use the [[cosplay pikachu (character)]] tag."
