          {
            "tag": "tracksuit",
            "kor": "tracksuit",
            "count": 677,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #2920484 thumb #2974242 thumb #2457007 thumb #2881822\r\n\r\nA [b]tracksuit[/b] is a matching set of pants and a jacket, commonly worn as [[athletic wear]] usually while running or jogging, but are very frequently worn casually as well. \r\n\r\nTracksuits are made of lightweight water resistant synthetic materials like nylon or polyester, the jackets frequently have zippered fronts, and pants have elastic waistbands or drawstrings. Tracksuits can come in a range of designs, but are most often are depicted as black or navy, with stripes on the sides of the pants and jacket. In some cases, the jacket may be substituted with a matching sleeveless hooded shirt, or [[tank top]], while the pants may be substituted with a matching pair of [[gym shorts]]. If the pants or jacket are individually, consider tagging [[track jacket]] or [[track pants]] instead.\r\n\r\nTracksuits have a stereotypical association with Eastern Europe, specifically the [[Gopnik]] subculture, where tracksuits are usually paired with a [[flat cap]]; tracksuits also have an association with early (1980s) hip-hop/rap subculture.\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n* [[Track Jacket]]\r\n* [[Track Pants]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[Athletic Wear]]\r\n* [[Yoga Pants]]\r\n* [[Sweatpants]]"
          },
          {
            "tag": "hooters_uniform",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 675,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1338557 thumb #2945032 thumb #2288916\r\n\r\n[[Hooters]] is an American restaurant chain, best known for their gimmick of employing scantily clad [[waiter|waitresses]] and explicit use of sex appeal.\r\n\r\nThe \"canon\" [b]Hooters Uniform[/b] mainly consists of a white, [[cleavage]] bearing [[tank top]] with the restaurant's name and logo, and a pair of orange [[hotpants|short shorts]]. \r\n\r\nThis tag can be used for Hooters [i]style[/i] uniforms, which might have changes to the name of the restaurant the character is working for (usually a parody of Hooters), the colors, and extent of [i]how[/i] revealing the outfit is -  changes can include making the tank top a [[crop top]] or [[t-shirt]], or exchanging the shorts for a [[skirt]] or [[panties]]/[[bikini bottom]]. This tag should only be used if it's clear the character is wearing the outfit as part of a waitress uniform, and not simply wearing athletic clothing.\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n* [[Hooters]]\r\n** [[Femboy Hooters]]\r\n** [[Himbo Hooters]]\r\n* [[Waiter]]\r\n* [[Waitress Uniform]]"
