            "kor": "",
            "count": 429,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1862765 thumb #2955362 thumb #1328935 thumb #974523 thumb #2428234\r\n\r\n[b]Waitress Uniform[/b] describes a range of uniforms typically worn by women acting as [[waiter|wait staff]]. \r\n\r\nThe \"classic\" waitress uniform consists of collared shirt, skirt and an apron, or a collared [[dress]] and [[apron]] (this latter style heavily associated with diners and \"retro\" mid-century aesthetics), in more \"contemporary\" styled or upscale restaurants, waitresses often wear a dress shirt and skirt similar to typical office wear.\r\n\r\nCharacters acting as waitresses in retro-style establishments or in period settings (specifically the [[1950s]]) may wear the \"classic\" style uniform, along with a [[bow tie]], paper hat, and roller skates.\r\n\r\nh4. Specific Waitress Uniforms:\r\n[i]These are specific outfits often worn as \"gimmicks\" by waitresses, ideally these should not be tagged as \"waitress uniform\"[/i]\r\n* [[Bunny Costume]]\r\n* [[Maid Uniform]]\r\n* [[Hooters Uniform]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n[i]Items usually worn by, or carried by a waitress[/i]\r\n* [[Apron]]\r\n* [[Name Tag]]\r\n* [[Notebook]]\r\n* [[Tray]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[Waiter]] "
