            "tag": "caption",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 1937,
            "wiki_body": "A [b]caption[/b] is a message that is displayed over an image, or animation, or somewhere nearby that usually describes some aspect of the image. The content of the message is not important; it is how the information is presented that matters.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[image_macro]]\r\n* [[snapchat]]\r\n* [[subtitled]]\r\n\r\nh5. Comic captions\r\n\r\nInformation typically contained within [[text_box|text boxes]] in a [[comic]] are considered a type of caption, but [[narration|narrative elements]], and [[dialogue]] should use their respective tags instead of the caption tag. This tag may be used for comics when the content consists of mostly time, location, or other non-narrative information about the scene. A [[text box]] containing such information should be tagged as a [[caption box]]. The `caption box` tag may be used for any text box that contains a caption.\r\n\r\nh4. Caption messages\r\n\r\n* [[game_over]]\r\n* [[meanwhile]]\r\n* [[the_end]]\r\n* [[time_card]]\r\n* [[to_be_continued]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[header]]\r\n* [[information]]\r\n* [[title]]"
          },
