            "wiki_body": "thumb #1818030 thumb #727597 thumb #3139960 thumb #3513747\r\n\r\nA wholly original image made to resemble a [[screencap|screen capture]] of an animation, film, video recording, video game, website, or computer screen — [b][i]while not actually being a screencap.[/i] [/b] \r\n\r\nh4. Features of a Fake Screencap\r\n[i]Note: not every fake screencap will have all of these features[/i]\r\n\r\nh6. Miscellaneous\r\n* [[style emulation]] — art that is drawn or rendered in a way that emulates the visual style of a particular piece of media or genre/medium, can include using the same materials/medium, and use of filters\r\n** [[on model]] — a character drawn in a way that is nigh-indistinguishable from their source material\r\n* [[dialogue]] in [[subtitled|subtitles]] or [[dialogue box|dialogue boxes]], usually written to imply the fake screencap was taken mid-sentence\r\n\r\nh6. Television/Video Elements\r\n* [[4:3]] or [[16:9]] aspect ratios — to emulate the aspect ratio of old television/film (4:3), or mimic a widescreen television or computer monitor's aspect ratio (16:9).\r\n* [[letterbox]] — black bars at the top and bottom of the image\r\n* [[subtitled|subtitles]] — usually in yellow or white text with black borders, or white text on a black bar (to resemble television closed captioning, sometimes even starting with a \"-\" or \">>>\")\r\n* [[vhs filter]] — grain, static, colour fading, and chromatic aberration added to an image to resemble a frame from a [[video cassette]] recording\r\n\r\nh6. Video Game Elements\r\n* [[user interface]] — buttons or prompts, option menus, scroll bars, minimize/maximize/close buttons\r\n* [[gameplay mechanics]] — UI from video games, such as health or status bars, character portraits etc. \r\n* [[dialogue box]] — contains dialogue in a fake screencap of a video game\r\n** fake video game cutscene screencaps might use subtitles instead of dialogue boxes\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[crossover]]\r\n* [[parody]]\r\n* [[visual novel]] — popular for fake video game screencaps\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[screencap]]\r\n** [[screencap background]]\r\n** [[screencap edit]]\r\n** [[screencap redraw]]"
