          "garter_belt_socks": [
            {
              "tag": "garter_belt_socks",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 332,
              "wiki_body": "Although technically any match of any kind of garter belt with any kind of sock is a \"garter belt sock\", this term is better reserved here for regular, below-the-knee socks being held up by garter belts worn at the legs as opposed to at the waist.\r\n\r\nthumb #3106121\r\n\r\nMore detailed explanation:\r\n\r\nWhereas garter belts are usually worn around the waist and are strapped with [[stockings]] or other female [[thigh_highs|thigh-high socks]] (sometimes even in a one-piece fashion, see [[garter_belt_leggings|garter belt leggings]]), they can also by worn at each individual leg and be strapped to either a thigh-high sock or a common one i.e. which ends below the knee. Whereas the former is often seen as enticing as with the waist-level garter belt and should be tagged as such, the latter is usually considered as purely practical and maybe even comical-looking, being mostly associated with formal menswear."
            }
