                "wiki_body": "thumb #1546701 thumb #711700 thumb #984546 thumb #964715 \r\n\r\nA [b]t-shirt[/b] is a unisex [[shirt]] with short sleeves and no collar. It is a casual dress that can have many different colours, patterns, and imprints written on it, giving it fashionable flexibility.\r\n\r\nA United States invention, the T-shirt was originally seen as juvenile clothing for men, until media attention in the 1950s caused it to be worn by men all over. It wasn't until the 1960s that it gained its reputation as a universal, expressive garment.\r\n\r\nIt is perhaps the most famous shirt in the world, being worn everywhere by everyone. Because of its informal nature, it is seen as predominantly boyish, reinforcing its original use in the United States Navy.\r\n\r\nh4. Tags About Shirts\r\n\r\n* [[shirt]]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Tags About Shirts]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Shirt Types]\r\n* [[crop_top]]\r\n* [[dress_shirt]]\r\n* [[polo_shirt]]\r\n* [[sleeveless_shirt]]\r\n* [b]t-shirt[/b]\r\n* [[tank_top]]\r\n* [[undershirt]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Shirt Status]\r\n* [[discarded_shirt]]\r\n* [[open_shirt]]\r\n* [[raised_shirt]]\r\n** [[shirt_lift]]\r\n* [[torn_shirt]]\r\n* [[wet_shirt]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Shirt Traits]\r\n[section=Colors]\r\n* [[black_shirt]]\r\n* [[blue_shirt]]\r\n* [[brown_shirt]]\r\n* [[green_shirt]]\r\n* [[grey_shirt]]\r\n* [[orange_shirt]]\r\n* [[pink_shirt]]\r\n* [[purple_shirt]]\r\n* [[red_shirt]]\r\n* [[tan_shirt]]\r\n* [[white_shirt]]\r\n* [[yellow_shirt]]\r\n\r\n* [[multicolored_shirt]]\r\n** [[pride_color_shirt]]\r\n** [[rainbow_shirt]]\r\n** [[two_tone_shirt]]\r\n\r\nSee also: [[tag_group:colors]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Patterns / Designs]\r\n* [[pattern_shirt]]\r\n** [[aloha_shirt]]\r\n** [[camo_shirt]]\r\n** [[checkered_shirt]]\r\n** [[plaid_shirt]]\r\n** [[spotted_shirt]]\r\n** [[striped_shirt]]\r\n* [[rental_mommy_shirt]]\r\n* [[translucent_shirt]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[sectio