        {
          "tag": "boob_armor",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 558,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3262060 thumb #3275384 thumb #15820\n[b]Boob Armor[/b], also known as [i]\"Boob Plate\"[/i] or [i]\"Breast Plate\"[/i] (with a space), is a type of [[body armor]] design with a breast cavity (either as a single cavity or individual cavities for each breast), either for practical reasons, aesthetic reasons, or both. This makes the chest armor appear bigger or appear to have [[breasts]] on them.\n\nh4.Why Boob Armor?\n* Practical Reasons:\n** To accommodate/fit a character with [[big breasts]].\n** Single cavity boob armor with sloped shapes deflect blows away from the chest.\n* Aesthetic Reasons:\n** To signal to the audience/viewer(s) that the character is [[female]].\n** To create the illusion of having bigger breasts.\n** Cultural, traditional or ceremonial reasons.\n** As a costume for a [[cosplay]] or television/movie.\n** To make the armor look more sexy.\n\nh4.Why Not Boob Armor?\n* Boob armor often comes in the form of a double cupped design. This particular type of boob armor funnels blows into the sternum.\n* Extra Weight - The added mass to accommodate the breasts means more weight is added to the upper body.\n* Body armor with breast cavities may not be necessary if the wearer's breasts aren't that particularly large (or if they even [[flat chested|have one at all]]).\n\nh4.Related Tags\n* [[body_armor]] - General tag for any type of  torso protection.\n** [[breastplate]] - A plate of armor that protects the chest area.\n** [[cuirass]] -  A combination of breastplate and backplate.\n\nh4.Not to be confused with\n* [[bikini_armor]] - Which only covers the breasts and not the rest of the chest area.\n\nh4.See Also\n* [[furgonomic_armor]] - Armor made to accommodate/fit a non-human character.\n* [[unconvincing_armor]] - Armor designs with little to no protective coverage.\n"
