          "kor": "",
          "count": 119,
          "wiki_body": "This is a misleading term. A [[socks|sock]] [b]cannot[/b] be `footless`. The footless equivalent to a sock is known as a `leg_sleeve` or more specifically [[leg warmers]]. However, you may be looking for a variant of the theme instead.\r\n\r\nh4. Similar tags\r\n\r\n* [[stirrup_socks]] - A style of sock that features a strip of fabric looped under the foot, leaving part of the heel and most of the foot exposed. Other similarly styled [[legwear]] fall under their respective tags, based under [[stirrup_legwear]].\r\n* [[toeless_socks]] - A style of sock that leaves the [[toes]] exposed, but still covers some part of the foot. This includes designs that resemble stirrup socks, but feature a closed heel instead. The design should be considered a `leg warmer` if it covers no more than the ankle. Other similarly styled [[legwear]] fall under their respective tags, based under [[toeless_legwear]].\r\n\r\nAny other type of `footless` legwear should not use this tag and instead use their respective tags based under [[footless_legwear]].\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[stockings]] - Stockings are [b]not[/b] socks, and should not be tagged as socks. Use either [[leg_warmers]] or [[footless_stockings]] instead for any `footless` legwear that does not reach the waist area. \r\n\r\nh4. Tag relations\r\n\r\n* [[footless_legwear]]\r\n** [[footless_leggings]]\r\n** [[footless_stockings]]\r\n** [[footless_pantyhose]]\r\n** [[footless_tights]]\r\n** [[leg_warmers]]\r\n\r\nh4. Tagging project\r\n\r\nThis tag doesn't have a purpose. Posts being tagged as this are better placed in [[footless_legwear]], and given their more accurate clothing tags. \r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[legwear]]"
