          "kor": "",
          "count": 131,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Perspective-incorrect texturing[/b], known on TV Tropes as \"Unmoving Plaid\":https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/UnmovingPlaid, is an artistic technique where a complex texture is applied to an object  (usually [[clothing]]) with no accordance to the perspective and depth of it. \r\n\r\nOften a static and [[tessellation|tessellating]] pattern, the texture is seen through an [[alpha channel]] or chroma keyed in. The texture will appear flat with exception to shading and optical illusions. If the medium is [[animated]], the pattern should remain fixed to the screen while other things move over or around it, creating a \"parallax effect\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parallax\r\n\r\nAn example of perspective-incorrect texturing includes clothing in [i][[Chowder (series)|Chowder]][/i]. Common patterns for clothing are [[fishnets]], [[camo print]], and [[plaid]].\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Perspective-incorrect tags]\r\n\r\nh4.Anatomy\r\n\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect body]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect eyes]]\r\n** [[perspective-incorrect sclera]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect hair]]\r\n** [[perspective-incorrect facial hair]]\r\n*** [[perspective-incorrect beard]]\r\n*** [[perspective-incorrect mustache]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect feathers]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect fur]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect scales]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect skin]]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4.[[perspective-incorrect clothing|Clothing]]\r\n\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect camo]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect denim]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect dress]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect fishnet]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect plaid]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect swimwear]]\r\n** [[perspective-incorrect bikini]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrect headwear]]\r\n** [[perspective-incorrect hat]]\r\n*** [[perspective-incorrect baseball cap]]\r\n*** [[perspective-incorrect beanie]]\r\n*** [[perspective-incorrect top hat]]\r\n** [[perspective-incorrect helmet]]\r\n* [[perspective-incorrec