          "tag": "tattooification",
          "kor": "문신",
          "count": 198,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3793033 thumb #1550597 thumb #4712876 thumb #4380447\r\n\r\n[b]\"Tattooification\"[/b] describes when a character or creature is transformed into a [[tattoo]] on another character's body. \r\n\r\nThis tattoo is usually an image of the character's face, but can also be a small, full body representation of the character; alternatively, the tattoo may be a symbol representative of the character (such as a [[cutie mark]] for a [[My Little Pony]] character). \r\n\r\nThe tattoo may emote or even think/talk in some cases, or possibly allow the bearer of the tattoo to channel the spirit of the character-turned-tattoo. These tattoos may be explicitly explained, or implied to be the result of a curse or magic spell, be a part of [[gameplay mechanics]], or simply be caused by unexplained [[cartoon physics]].\r\n\r\nh5. Tattooification in Vore\r\nTattooificiation is most often seen in [[vore]] content, where the term \"tattooification\" itself may have originated. \r\n\r\nIt is specifically seen in [[after vore]] with the completely digested/absorbed character appearing as a tattoo on the body of the predator character; tattooification can reinforce the themes of domination and humiliation common in vore content, and can also act as an indirect tally of who the predator character has consumed. Post-vore tattooficiation is almost always combined with other effects on the predator, such as weight gain or expansion, and the tattoo of the consumed character will usually appear on expanded or fattened body parts (e.g. butt cheeks, breasts, belly etc.)\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[after vore]]\r\n** [[digestion]]\r\n** [[sentient fat]]\r\n** [[weight gain]]\r\n* [[vore]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[transformation]]\r\n** [[inanimate transformation]]\r\n* Not to be confused with characters that are [[flattened]]\r\n\r\n"
