                "count": 195,
                "wiki_body": "thumb #732270 thumb #232168 thumb #1066674\r\n\r\nA pop out cake, also known as a popout, jump out, or surprise cake, is a large object made to serve as a surprise often for celebration. On the outside, it appears to be a very large [[cake]], and sometimes it is partially or mostly cake (in the realm of fiction, it is often made to be entirely cake). However, mostly it's cardboard or other material to form a space in which to hide a person. This person, often an attractive [[female|woman]] (often an [[stripper|erotic dancer]]), crouches and hides until prompted to stand and \"jump out\" of the cake to [[surprise]] others. This phenomena has become a trope often seen in film and and popular media.\r\n\r\nWhile often sexualized and a form of [[food play]], it can also be done non-sexually as a [[cute]] or [[humor|funny]] gesture to another participant or even to the viewer.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[Birthday]]\r\n* [[Cake]]\r\n** [[Birthday cake]]\r\n** Pop out cake\r\n* [[Foodplay]]\r\n** [[Cake sitting]]"
