                "wiki_body": "thumb #1215105 thumb #966301 thumb #578931 thumb #1262321\r\n\r\nh1.🥪\r\n\r\nA [b]sandwich[/b] is a type of food made by placing items between two slices of [[bread]]. Common ingredients include: [[meat]], [[cheese]], [[onion]], [[tomato]], [[lettuce]], etc. Condiments are sometimes included such as [[mustard]], [[ketchup]] or [[mayonnaise]]. Occasionally a [[toothpick]] may be used to hold all the layers of ingredients pinned into place for easier [[eating]]. \r\n\r\nSometimes other items may be placed between two slices of [[bread]] to make an inedible sandwich. Most often this is used for for [[humor]] or as prank. Even [i]characters[/i] can be part of the sandwich itself, as shown with sandwich connoisseur [[Reuben (Lilo and Stitch)|Reuben]] on the far right image above.\r\n\r\nh4.Types of sandwiches:\r\n* [[dagwood_sandwich]] — A tall sandwich with multiple layers of assorted condiments.\r\n* [[grilled_cheese]] — A hot sandwich made with pre-buttered grilled (or toasted) white bread and melted American [[cheese]].\r\n* [[peanut_butter_and_jelly_sandwich]] — A simple though sometimes messy sandwich made with... [[peanut butter]] and [[jelly]]. Kids love it.\r\n* [[submarine_sandwich]] — A long sandwich made from a bread or roll that is split lengthwise. Known under a variety of names, it's the kind of sandwich that [[Subway (restaurant)|Subway]] serves.\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n* [[sandvich_(team_fortress_2)]]\r\n* [[burger]] — They [i]are[/i] sandwiches, but we're not treating them as such here.\r\n* [[eating]]\r\n* [[food]]\r\n* [[soup]] — Americans often make soup and sandwiches together for a classic combo meal."
