          "food_transformation": [
            {
              "tag": "food_transformation",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 238,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #1895433 thumb #2475611 thumb #1680090\r\n\r\n[b]Food transformation[/b] (or \"Food TF\") describes a character being transformed into some form of [[food]] item or edible substance, how this is depicted and the \"amount of transformation\" can vary.\r\n\r\nh5. Variations on Food Transformation\r\n* The character mostly or entirely retains their form post-transformation, but appears to be made of an edible substance - usually jelly or gelatin, or has become some sort of living candy or cake \r\n* The character is partially transformed, with body parts resembling food items, usually for comedic effect\r\n* The character is transformed into a moulded chocolate, shaped pancake, waffles, or cookie form of themselves\r\n** May look like the character's pre-tf form, or can be a cartoonish flattened version of the character (as if they were pressed or rolled into shape)  \r\n** Usually incapable of movement but still aware, sometimes fully inanimate\r\n* The character becomes a semi-animate food item, usually only with eyes, sometimes an entire face; rarely, the character's entire head, and/or their limbs remain\r\n* The character becomes a completely inanimate food item, nearly indistinguishable from regular food\r\n** Sometimes the food item features body parts (tails, ears), patterns, colours or symbols referencing the character's pre-tf appearance\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n* [[Candy Gore]] - A transformed character might be shown broken, bitten, or cut open, revealing filling, cake layering or other food related substances\r\n* [[Vore]] - Food TF often has a transformed character at risk of being eaten, or is shown being eaten by another character\r\n** Vore should only be tagged if the character is actively being eaten, if there's only the implication (eg. the character having pieces of them broken off with a fork, being served on a plate to another character) it should be tagged as [[imminent vore]] instead\r\n** This should generally not be tagged as hard vore, even if the character is chewed up, unless there is explicit gore or blood\r\n* [[Inanimate Transformation]] - for cases where the character loses any apparent awareness or ability to move\r\n* [[After Transformation]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[Transformation]]\r\n* [[Food Creature]] | [[Goo Creature]] \r\n"
            }
