          "pokemon_berry": {
            "_Self (pokemon_berry)": [
              {
                "tag": "pokemon_berry",
                "kor": "",
                "count": 982,
                "wiki_body": "thumb #4343445 thumb #2282886 thumb #4090105\r\n\r\n[b]Pokémon Berries[/b] (in Japanese: [b]きのみ[/b] [i]Kinomi[/i], \"Tree Fruit\") are small, juicy and fleshy fruits. Like in the real world, a large variety exists in the [i][[Pokemon|Pokémon]][/i] world, with a wide range of flavors and effects. All berries are some extend of [color=#E3765C]spicy[/color], [color=#6DB9D6]dry[/color], [color=#E286B5]sweet[/color], [color=#67C282]bitter[/color], or [color=#DEC240]sour[/color]; and provide the consumer in ways such as regaining \"health\":https://m.bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/HP, healing from a \"status condition\":https://m.bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Status_condition, changing \"stats\":https://m.bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Stat, unique defenses in battle, and more.\r\n\r\nUnlike human-made products such as potions, ethers, or other medicines, [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] are able to utilize berries at their discretion. Humans have incorporated berries into various cooking of [[food]] for them and their Pokémon, such as [[poke block|Poké blocks]], [[poffin|Poffins]], and [[curry]].\r\n\r\nThe first ten berries were introduced in Generation Ⅱ with the introduction of held items, but were revamped for Generation Ⅲ with the addition of thirty-three more berries for recipes (not including e-Reader berries exclusive to [i]Ruby[/i] and [i]Sapphire[/i]). A further twenty-five have been added in the subsequent generations, not including variation of previous berries.\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=List of Pokémon Berries]\r\nBelow is a comprehensive list of berries found in the mainline [i]Pokemon[/i] games, sorted by generation of introduction and (where applicable) their index number as of [i]Brilliant Diamond[/i] and [i]Shining Pearl[/i]. \r\n\r\nh4. Generation Ⅱ\r\n* #01 — [[Cheri berry]] (クラボのみ [i]Kurabo no Mi[/i], \"Kurabo Fruit\") — A red [[cherry]]-like berry of [color=#E3765C]spicy[/color] flavor that cures paralysis. Successor to the PRZCureBerry (まひなおしのみ [i]Mahinaoshi no Mi[/i], \"Paralysis-Curing Fruit\").\r\n* #02 — [[Chesto berry]] (カゴのみ [i]Kago no Mi[/i], \"Kago Fruit\") — A purple-and-tan [[chestnut]]-like berry of [color=#6DB9D6]dry[/color] flavor that awakens the sleeping. Successor to the Mint Berry (はっかのみ [i]Hakka no Mi[/i], \"Mint Fruit\").\r\n* #03 — [[Pecha berry]] (モモンのみ [i]Momon no Mi[/i], \"Momon Fruit\") — A pink [[peach (fruit)|peach]]-like berry of [color=#E286B5]sweet[/color] flavor that cures poisoning. Successor to the PSNCureBerry (どくけしのみ [i]Dokukeshi no Mi[/i], \"Antidote Fruit\").\r\n** [[Mythical Pecha Berry]] (まぼろしモモン [i]Maboroshi Momon[/i], \"Mythical Momon\") — Key Item from The Indigo Disk DLC and MacGuffin for the Mochi Mayhem epilogue.\r\n* #04 — [[Rawst berry]] (チーゴのみ [i]Chīgo no Mi[/i], \"Chiigo Fruit\") — A blue [[strawberry]]-like berry of [color=#67C282]bitter[/color] flavor that cures burns. Successor to the Ice Berry (こおったきのみ [i]Kōtta Kinomi[/i], \"Frozen Fruit\").\r\n* #05 — [[Aspear berry]] (ナナシのみ [i]Nanashi no Mi[/i], \"Nanashi Fruit\") — An Asian pear-like berry of [color=#DEC240]sour[/color] flavor that thaws the frozen. Successor to the Burnt Berry (やけたきのみ [i]Yaketa Kinomi[/i], \"Burnt Fruit\").\r\n* #06 — [[Leppa berry]] (ヒメリのみ [i]Himeri no Mi[/i], \"Himeri Fruit\") — A red-and-yellow plumleaf crab apple-like berry of [color=#E3765C]anything[/color] [color=#E286B5]but[/color] [color=#67C282]dry[/color] [color=#DEC240]flavor[/color] that restores ten power points. Successor to the MysteryBerry (ふしぎなきのみ [i]Fushigina Kinomi[/i], \"Mystery Fruit\").\r\n* #07 — [[Oran berry]] (オレンのみ [i]Oren no Mi[/i], \"Oren Fruit\") — A blue [[orange (fruit)|orange]]-like berry of [color=#E3765C]anything[/color] [color=#6DB9D6]but[/color] [color=#67C282]sweet[/color] [color=#DEC240]flavor[/color] that restores ten health points. Successor to the standard Berry (きのみ [i]Kinomi[/i]) \r\n* #08 — [[Persim berry]] (キーのみ [i]Kī no Mi[/i], \"Kii Fruit\") — A pink [[persimmon]]-like berry of [color=#E3765C]anything[/color] [color=#6DB9D6]but[/color] [color=#E286B5]bitter[/color] [color=#DEC240]flavor[/color] that cures confusion. Successor to the Bitter Berry (にがいきのみ [i]Nigai Kinomi[/i], \"Bitter Fruit\").\r\n* #09 — [[Lum berry]] (ラムのみ [i]Ramu no Mi[/i], \"Lum Fruit\") — A green [[plum (fruit)|plum]]-like berry of [color=#E3765C]anything[/color] [color=#6DB9D6]but[/color] [color=#E286B5]sour[/color] [color=#67C282]flavor[/color] that can awaken the sleeping; thaw the frozen; and cure paralysis, poisoning, burns, and confusion. Successor to the MiracleBerry (きせきのみ [i]Kiseki no Mi[/i], \"Miracle Fruit\").\r\n* #10 — [[Sitrus berry]] (オボンのみ [i]Obon no Mi[/i], \"Obon Fruit\") — A yellow pomelo-like berry of [color=#6DB9D6]anything[/color] [color=#E286B5]but[/color] [color=#67C282]spicy[/color] [color=#DEC240]flavor[/color] that restores a 25% of max health. Successor to the Gold Berry (おうごんのみ [i]Ōgon no Mi[/i], \"Gold Fruit\").\r\n\r\nh4. Generation Ⅲ \r\n* #11 — [[Figy berry]] (フィラのみ [i]Fira no Mi[/i], \"Fira Fruit\") — A yellow [[fig]]-like berry that restores 33% of health points when under 25% health, but causes confusion in those who hate its [color=#E3765C]spicy[/color] flavor.\r\n* #12 — [[Wiki berry]] (ウイのみ [i]Ui no Mi[/i], \"Wi Fruit\") — A purple [[kiwifruit]]-like berry that restores 33% of health points when under 25% health, but causes confusion in those who hate its [color=#6DB9D6]dry[/color] flavor.\r\n* #13 — [[Mago berry]] (マゴのみ [i]Mago no Mi[/i], \"Mago Fruit\") — A pink [[mango (fruit)|mango]]-like berry that restores 33% of health points when under 25% health, but causes confusion in those who hate its [color=#E286B5]sweet[/color] flavor.\r\n* #14 — [[Aguav berry]] (バンジのみ [i]Banji no Mi[/i], \"Banji Fruit\") — A green [[guava]]-like berry that restores 33% of health points when under 25% health, but causes confusion in those who hate its [color=#67C282]bitter[/color] flavor.\r\n* #15 — [[Iapapa berry]] (イアのみ [i]Ia no Mi[/i], \"Ia Fruit\") — An orange [[papaya]]-like berry that restores 33% of health points when under 25% health, but causes confusion in those who hate its [color=#DEC240]sour[/color] flavor.\r\n* #16 — [[Razz berry]] (ズリのみ [i]Zuri no Mi[/i], \"Zuri Fruit\") — A red [[raspberry]]-like berry of [color=#E3765C]spicy[/color] and [color=#6DB9D6]dry[/color] flavor used in cooking, but has been known to make wild Pokémon easier to catch.\r\n** Silver Razz Berry (ぎんのズリのみ [i]Gin no Zuri no Mi[/i], \"Silver Zuri Fruit\") — an uncommon purplish-silver variant of increased pacifying properties.\r\n** Golden Razz Berry (きんのズリのみ [i]Kin no Zuri no Mi[/i], \"Gold Zuri Fruit\") — a rare orangish-gold variant of significant pacifying properties.\r\n* #17 — [[Bluk berry]] (ブリーのみ [i]Burī no Mi[/i], \"Burii Fruit\") — A purple [[blackberry]]-like berry of [color=#6DB9D6]dry[/color] and [color=#E286B5]sweet[/color] flavor used in cooking.\r\n* #18 — [[Nanab berry]] (ナナのみ [i]Nana no Mi[/i], \"Nana Fruit\") — A pink [[banana]]-like berry of [color=#E286B5]sweet[/color] and [color=#67C282]bitter[/color] flavor used in cooking, but has been known to make wild Pokémon calm down.\r\n** Silver Nanab berry (ぎんのナナのみ [i]Gin no Nana no Mi[/i], \"Silver Nana Fruit\") — an uncommon purplish-silver variant of increased calming properties.\r\n** Golden Nanab berry (きんのナナのみ [i]Kin no Nana no Mi[/i], \"Gold Nana Fruit\") — a rare orangish-gold variant of significant calming properties.\r\n* #19 — [[Wepear berry]] (セシナのみ [i]Seshina no Mi[/i], \"Seshina Fruit\") — A green [[pear]]-like berry of [color=#67C282]bitter[/color] and [color=#DEC240]sour[/color] flavor used in cooking.\r\n* #20 — [[Pinap berry]] (パイルのみ [i]Pairu no Mi[/i], \"Pairu Fruit\") — A yellow [[pineapple]]-like berry of [color=#DEC240]sour[/color] and [color=#E3765C]spicy[/color] flavor used in cooking, but has been known to restore 33% of health, make wild Pokémon more likely to drop items, or yield more experience when caught.\r\n** Silver Pinap berry (ぎんのパイルのみ [i]Gin no Pairu no Mi[/i], \"Silver Pairu Fruit\") — an uncommon purplish-silver variant of increased experience yielding properties.\r\n** Golden Pinap berry (きんのパイルのみ [i]Kin no Pairu no Mi[/i], \"Gold Pairu Fruit\") — a rare orangish-gold variant of significant experience yielding properties.\r\n* #21 — [[Pomeg berry]] (ザロクのみ [i]Zaroku no Mi[/i], \"Zaroku Fruit\") — A red [[pomegranate]]-like berry of [color=#E3765C]spicy[/color], [color=#E286B5]sweet[/color], and [color=#67C282]bitter[/color] flavor that improves friendship at the cost of Health effort values.\r\n* #22 — [[Kelpsy berry]] (ネコブのみ [i]Nekobu no Mi[/i], \"Nekobu Fruit\") — A blue [[kelp]]-like berry of [color=#6DB9D6]dry[/color], [color=#67C282]bitter[/color], and [color=#DEC240]sour[/color] flavor that improves friendship at the cost of Attack effort values.\r\n* #23 — [[Qualot berry]] (タポルのみ [i]Taporu no Mi[/i], \"Taporu Fruit\") — A pink [[loquat]]-like berry of [color=#E3765C]spicy[/color], [color=#E286B5]sweet[/color], and [color=#DEC240]sour[/color] flavor that improves friendship at the cost of Defense effort values.\r\n* #24 — [[Hondew berry]] (ロメのみ [i]Rome no Mi[/i], \"Rome Fruit\") — A green [[honeydew melon]]-like berry of [color=#E3765C]spicy[/color], [color=#6DB9D6]dry[/color], and [color=#67C282]bitter[/color] flavor that improves friendship at the cost of Special Attack effort values.\r\n* #25 — [[Grepa berry]] (ウブのみ [i]Ubu no Mi[/i], \"Ubu Fruit\") — A yellow [[grapefruit]]-like berry of [color=#6DB9D6]dry[/color], [color=#E286B5]sweet[/color], and [color=#DEC240]sour[/color] flavor that improves friendship at the cost of Special Defense effort values.\r\n* #26 — [[Tamato berry]] (マトマのみ [i]Matoma no Mi[/i], \"Matoma Fruit\") — A red [[tomato]]-like berry of [color=#E3765C]spicy[/color] yet [color=#6DB9D6]dry[/color] flavor that improves friendship at the cost of Speed effort values.\r\n* #27 — [[Cornn berry]] (モコシのみ [i]Mokoshi no Mi[/i], \"Mokoshi Fruit\") — A 