        "alcohol": {
          "_Self (alcohol)": [
            {
              "tag": "alcohol",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 33205,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #148137 thumb #2297482 thumb #1628881 thumb #3085442 thumb #5054345 thumb #2541330 thumb #3030095 thumb #3964969\r\n\r\nAn [b]alcoholic beverage[/b] (or simply [b]alcohol[/b]) is a [[beverage]] containing \"ethanol\":https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethanol.\r\nThere are a multitude of these beverages and they are typically divided into three classes– [[beer|beers]], [[wine|wines]], and \"spirits\":https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liquor – and typically their alcohol content is between 3% and 50%.\r\n\r\nMany countries have their own alcoholic beverages, such as [[champagne]] in France, [[sake]] in Japan or [[vodka]] in Russia.\r\n\r\n[b]Alcohol[/b] is a [[drugs|drug]], and heavy or chronic consumption can degenerate into an [[addiction]] known as \"alcoholism\":https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcoholism.\r\n\r\n[spoiler]Contrary to popular belief, all alcohol consumption, even at low doses, is a factor in premature mortality, and exposes us to multiple health risks.\r\nUnfortunately, along with tobacco, it is also one of the world's leading causes of death\r\n[i](So remember to drink as little as possible!)[/i][/spoiler]\r\n\r\nThis tag is used to describe [b]all[/b] alcoholic beverages, which are ingested both for their flavor and to become [[drunk]].\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n\r\n* [b]alcohol[/b]\r\n** [[beer]]\r\n** [[champagne]]\r\n** [[rum]]\r\n** [[sake]]\r\n** [[whiskey]]\r\n** [[wine]]\r\n** [[vodka]]\r\n* [[drugs]]\r\n** [[stoned]]\r\n* [[smoking]]\r\n** [[cigar]]\r\n** [[cigarette]]"
            }
