                "count": 14133,
                "wiki_body": "thumb #382402 thumb #99747 thumb #2361800 thumb #1139264\r\n\r\nAn elevated horizontal surface (usually made of wood) used for writing, reading, using a computer, etc. which are often accompanied by a [[chair]].\r\n\r\nThere are many types of desk ranging from a simple flat surface raised on four legs, to more elaborate designs with drawers, multiple tiers, L-shaped layouts, etc. Great majority of desks are similar to tables in that they stand on their own and have a surface to place objects on. It is, however not necessary for a desk to have free open area, and it can be just a surface that can even be moved and placed elsewhere.\r\n\r\nA desk has typically dedicated sides, such as the working side and the client side. This is a distiction to a typical table. This also applies to a [[counter]], which differs from desk by being an unmovable fixure.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[lectern]]\r\n* [[table]]\r\n\r\n"
