          {
            "tag": "tablet",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 1980,
            "wiki_body": "A rectangular slab, meant to store information and/or be written on, this traditionally describes stone or clay tablets, but also describes a tablet computer \r\n\r\nSometimes used as another word for a [[pill]], when composed of solid medicine rather than enclosed in a capsule (do not use this tag for pills).\r\n\r\nh4. Tablets\r\nThese tags are preferable to only using `tablet`\r\n\r\n* [[drawing_tablet]] - Drawing tablets are a peripheral device that is connected to a [[computer]] or a [[laptop]] and cannot function on its own, even if they can have screens and look similar to tablets.\r\n* [[tablet_computer]] - A portable, handheld [[computer]] with a touchscreen interface\r\n* [[stone_tablet]] - a chiselled stone or hardened clay slab used to record information\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[computer]]\r\n* [[laptop]]\r\n* [[smartphone]]\r\n* [[paper]]\r\n* [[book]]"
          },
          {
            "tag": "stable",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 1691,
            "wiki_body": "A stable is a building in which livestock, especially horses, are kept. It most commonly means a building that is divided into separate stalls for individual animals and livestock. There are many different types of stables in use today; the American-style barn, for instance, is a large barn with a door at each end and individual stalls inside or free-standing stables with top and bottom-opening doors. The term \"stable\" is additionally utilised to denote a collection of animals under the care of a single owner, irrespective of their housing or whereabouts.\r\n\r\nThe exterior design of a stable can vary widely, based on climate, building materials, historical period and cultural styles of architecture. A wide range of building materials can be used, including masonry (bricks or stone), wood and steel. Stables also range widely in size, from a small building housing one or two animals to facilities at agricultural shows or race tracks that can house hundreds of animals."
          },
