          {
            "tag": "tablet_computer",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 991,
            "wiki_body": "A [b]tablet computer[/b], often simply called a \"[b]tablet[/b]\", is a mobile computing device with a touch screen display. While \"[[tablet]]\" alone is also used to refer to a [[drawing tablet]], or a [[stone tablet]], in this article \"tablet\" will be used to refer to tablet computers.\r\n\r\nMost tablets have similar capabilities, share operating systems with, and even visually resemble [[smartphone|smartphones]], but are physically larger than any cellphone. Tablets are used to view media, communicate, record information and browse the internet, while not used as a cellphone, a tablet may be used to make and receive voice or video calls. \r\n\r\nh4. Tagging Notes\r\n* Tablet may be seen used with wireless keyboards, or used for writing or drawing with a [[stylus]] pen, but should never be confused with a [[laptop computer]] or [[drawing tablet]]. \r\n** Tablets do not have attached keyboards, and are usually smaller than a laptop\r\n** Tablets are self-contained mobile computers — drawing tablets are merely interface devices that require a connection to a computer in order to function\r\n* Sci-fi or fantasy devices that have similar forms and functions to real world tablet can be tagged as `tablet_computer`\r\n** The exception to this is the [[Sheikah Slate]] from [i]Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild[/i], which is a distinct enough device to have its own tag\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[drawing tablet]]"
