                "wiki_body": "thumb #2671596 thumb #3735319 thumb #1588378 thumb #2544148\n\nImages or animations which contain a tree.\n\nA [b]tree[/b] is a perennial woody [[plant]]. It is most often defined as a woody plant that has many secondary branches supported clear of the ground on a single main stem or trunk with clear apical dominance.\n\nPlease tag the tree species if it can be identified from the image. If there is a tree that isn't listed on this wiki, please include it.\n\nh4. Species\n\n* [[bamboo_tree]]\n* [[conifer]]\n*** [[cedar_tree]]\n*** [[cypress_tree]]\n*** [[fir_tree]]\n*** [[juniper_tree]]\n*** [[larch_tree]]\n*** [[pine_tree]]\n*** [[redwood_tree]]\n*** [[spruce_tree]]\n* [[deciduous_tree]]\n** [[aspen_tree]]\n** [[beech_tree]]\n** [[birch_tree]]\n** [[larch_tree]]\n** [[maple_tree]]\n*** [[maple leaf]]\n** [[oak_tree]]\n** [[willow_tree]]\n* [[evergreen_tree]]\n** [[pine_tree]]\n* [[fruit_tree]]\n** [[apple_tree]]\n** [[banana_tree]]\n** [[cherry_tree]]\n** [[citrus_tree]]\n*** [[lemon_tree]]\n*** [[lime_tree]]\n*** [[orange_tree]]\n** [[peach_tree]]\n** [[pear_tree]]\n** [[plum_tree]]\n* [[palm_tree]]\n** [[coconut_tree]]\n* [[rowan_tree]]\n\nh4. Other types\n\n* [[bonsai]] - A small potable tree that is designed to mimic its full-sized counterpart.\n* [[christmas_tree]]\n* [[dead_tree]]\n\nh4. Anatomy\n\n* [[branch]] - A narrow structure that extends from the body of a tree.\n* [[leaf]] - A thin stemmed structure that extends from the tips of a tree branch.\n* [[log]] - A thick section of wood that has been fully separated from the body of a tree.\n* [[roots]] - Long woody structures that extend into the ground to absorb water and / or nutrients.\n* [[tree_bark]] - The outer surface of many trees. Consider tagging only if it is detailed or textured in some way.\n* [[tree_stump]] - The base of a tree that makes contact with the ground.\n* [[tree_trunk]] - The main stem (body) of a tree. \n* [[wood]] - The material most trees are made of