              "wiki_body": "* Commonly confused with [[mistletoe]], holly has sharp-pointed leaves with red (common) or white (inkberry) berries, while mistletoe has smooth-edged leaves and (commonly) white  or (sometimes) red berries. Leaf shape is the determining factor.\r\n\r\nIn many Western Christian cultures, holly is a traditional [[Christmas]] decoration, used especially in wreaths and illustrations, for instance on Christmas cards.\r\n\r\nh4. Examples\r\n\r\nthumb #276082 thumb #952626 thumb #2685281"
