              "count": 830,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #1179541 thumb #1531052 thumb #1627379\r\n\r\nh1.🍆\r\n\r\n[b]Eggplant[/b] (United States, Australia, New Zealand, anglophone Canada), [b]aubergine[/b] (United Kingdom, Ireland, Quebec, and most of mainland Western Europe) or [b]brinjal[/b] (South Asia, South Africa) is a plant species in the nightshade family that produces a usually purple, spongy, absorbent [[fruit]] with a long body. The edible fruit of [i]Solanum melongena[/i] is normally used as a [[vegetable]] in cooking, but it is botanically a [[berry]]. Although it doesn't have much nutritional content, its capabilities of absorbing oils and flavors into its flesh makes it very popular in cooking.\r\n\r\nInternet culture seems to make the long, plump fruit sensual for some reason.\r\n\r\nEmoji version (🍆) tagged as [[eggplant_emoji]]"
