            "tag": "star_polygon",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 1762,
            "wiki_body": "A [b]star polygon[/b] refers to a pointed star shape, often made by skipping every 2/3 vertices while drawing a regular polygon. The shape is the geometric representation of a celestial [[star]]. Actual stars are difficult to physically depict in their natural form outside of a night sky or [[spacescape]], and polygons are used in their place. This concept shares the [[star]] tag with celestial stars.\r\n\r\nh4. Types\r\n\r\n* [[hexagram]] (six-pointed star)\r\n* [[septagram]] (seven-pointed star)\r\n* [[outline_star]] - The star lacks a fill color.\r\n* [[pentagram]] (five-pointed outline star)\r\n* [[rounded_star_polygon]] - A star polygon that are rounded at the points.\r\n\r\nh4. Categories\r\n\r\nh6. Design themes\r\n\r\n* [[star_cutout]]\r\n* [[star_pattern]]\r\n* [[star_print]]\r\n\r\nh6. Usage\r\n\r\n* [[celestial_star_polygon]] - Star polygons that represent or take the place of celestial stars.\r\n* [[star_accessory]]\r\n* [[star_clothing]]\r\n* [[star_decoration]]\r\n** [[christmas_star]]\r\n** [[star_string_lights]]\r\n* [[star-shaped_background]]"
