            "tag": "maple_leaf",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 495,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1779506 thumb #2027134 thumb #4458309 thumb #239344\r\n \r\nThe leaf of a maple [[tree]], frequently depicted in art set during the [[autumn]] as [[falling leaves]], maple leaves are also depicted on packaging for maple products, such as [[maple syrup]].\r\n\r\nThe maple leaf is the national icon of [[Canada]], and is seen on the [[Canadian flag]] as a red, stylized, 11-pointed symbol (however, artwork may further simplify this leaf). Maple leaves are frequently seen in art with Canadian themes, and on characters wearing clothing associated with Canada (e.g. sports jerseys, uniforms, hats, patches for Canadian organizations)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n* [[Leaf]]\r\n** [[Falling Leaves]]\r\n** [[Leaf Pile]]\r\n* [[Autumn]]\r\n* [[Maple Syrup]]\r\n\r\n\r\n"
