            "tag": "rockabilly",
            "kor": "로커빌리",
            "count": 176,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #470835 thumb #93400 thumb #63978 thumb #4222966\r\n\r\n[b]Rockabilly[/b] is an early style of rock and roll music. It dates back to the early 1950s in the United States, especially the South. As a genre, it blends the sound of Western musical styles such as country with that of rhythm and blues, leading to what is considered \"classic\" rock and roll.\r\n\r\nThe fashion of rockabilly is reminiscent of vintage 1950s fashion and [[greaser|greasers]]. The clothing typically ranges in [[leather jacket|leather jackets]], faux western shirts, [[dress|dresses]], [[jeans]], and accessories such as [[rose_(flower)|roses]] or [[ribbons]]. The common patterns for clothing are [[polka dots]] and [[stripes]]. Common colors of the clothing - though not limited to - comprise of blacks, whites, and reds.\r\n\r\n\"Wikipedia article on Rockabilly\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockabilly\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[tag group:fashion]]"
