          "currency_symbol": [
            {
              "tag": "currency_symbol",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 1162,
              "wiki_body": "A [b]currency symbol[/b] , also known as a [b]currency sign[/b], is a [[symbol|symbolic]] representation of [[money]]. Currency symbols are used next to value amounts to indicate those amounts are a currency, and the specific symbol used determines the type of currency.\r\n\r\n[table][thead]\r\n[tr][th] Currency [/th]\r\n[th] Symbol [/th]\r\n[th] Extra Information [/th]\r\n[/tr][/thead]\r\n\r\n[tbody]\r\n[tr][td] [[cent_sign]] [/td][td] ¢ [/td][td] Used by multiple currencies to denote 1/100th the value of the basic monetary unit. [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] [[dollar_sign]] [/td][td] $ [/td][td] Represents various currencies around the world called \"dollar\" and \"peso\". Is often used as shorthand for currency in general due to the widespread use of the term.[/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] [[euro_sign]] [/td][td] € [/td][td] Represents the euro - the currency of the European Union [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] [[pokedollar_sign]] [/td][td] ₽ [/td][td] Based on the Japanese yen, the Pokédollar is the fictional currency depicted in [[Pokémon]] franchise video games. [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] [[pound_sign]] [/td][td] £ [/td][td] Represents various currencies called \"pound\" and \"lira\", such as the currency of the United Kingdom. [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] [[yen_sign]] [/td][td] ¥ [/td][td] May refer to the Japanese yen, or the Chinese yuan (same symbol). [/td][/tr]\r\n\r\n[/tbody][/table]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[money]]\r\n** [[banknote]]\r\n** [[coin]]\r\n* [[number]]\r\n* [[price]]"
            }
