              "wiki_body": "thumb #4569988 thumb #4456612 thumb #1674637\r\n\r\nThe skull is the bone structure of the head, including the bones of the face, and forms a cavity for the brain. \r\n\r\nWhen used alone, this tag often describes \"actual skulls\", a full or partial skull of a previously living being that is present in a scene, it may also describe depictions of the skull in an anatomical [[cross section]], or a [[radiograph]], it can also describe skulls created artificially, for decoration or anatomical/medical reference (e.g. a throne with carved skulls, or a decorative, fake skull on a bookshelf). \r\n\r\nh4. Skull tags\r\nNote that not all of the tags bellow involve an actual skull\r\n\r\n* [[holding_skull]] - a character using their hands, feet, tail, or other appendages to hold a skull\r\n* [[skull_(marking)]] - naturally occurring markings resembling skulls on/in the skin, fur, scales, etc. of a character's body\r\n* [[skull_accessory]] - fashion accessories that resemble skulls, or actual skulls used as accessories\r\n* [[skull_and_crossbones]] - a symbol of a skull above or over top of a pair of crossed bones\r\n* [[skull_face paint]] - a character's face painted to resemble a skull\r\n* [[skull_hat]] - Any hat with a skull inspired design.\r\n* [[skull_head]] - a character with a bare skull for a head\r\n** [[exposed_skull]] - A character with a (partially or entirely) peeled off face.\r\n* [[skull_helmet]] - a  skull-shaped helmet or an actual skull being used as a helmet.\r\n* [[skull_mask]] - a character wearing a skull or parts of a skull as a facial covering\r\n* [[skull_pauldron]] - A skull-shaped shoulder armor or an actual skull being used as one.\r\n* [[skull_print]]\r\n* [[skull_symbol]] - stylized representations of a skull as clothing prints, tattoos and iconography\r\n* [[skull_tattoo]] - A skull-inspired design tattooed somewhere on a character's body.\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[bone]]\r\n* [[skeleton]] "
