              "tag": "shredder_(machine)",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 106,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #4536911 thumb #335329 thumb #1870908\r\n\r\n[b]Shredders[/b] are types of machinery that shred/grind whatever is placed in it into pieces.\r\n\r\nh6.Examples:\r\n* [[meat_grinder]] — An appliance generally loaded through a funnel at the top, mincing the input which is then pushed out of a tube to the side.\r\n* [[woodchipper]] — An appliance generally loaded through a hopper on the side, shredding the input which is then ejected through a raised funnel on the side.\r\n* [[industrial_shredder]] — Large shredding appliances that come in a variety of forms, featuring horizontal cylinders covered in hooks or blades, the input being dropped in and dragged through, exiting below in pieces.\r\n* [[paper_shredder]] — A tall container with a shredder built into the top, where thin input materials can be inserted to be vertically cut into strips, with or without horizontal cutting.\r\n* [[food_processor]] — An appliance with interchangeable shredding disks, which can be loaded through a chamber on the lid, where the input is manually pressed down through the spinning disk and into the container below.\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n* [[blender_(object)]]"
