              "wiki_body": "thumb #524112 thumb #366208 thumb #117805 thumb #316533\r\n\r\n[b]Vehicles[/b] are self-propelled [[machine]]s designed to transport things (such as people and cargo) through a variety of terrain depending on the type (land, water, air, space, etc.) and make use of a wide range of means of self-propulsion. In early time periods vehicles are propelled and powered by natural phenomena (eg.: wind power (sails), water flow, gravity, etc.) to muscle power (from animals and even other people). In modern times most vehicles are now powered by complex mechanisms such as [[engine]]s and motors.\r\n\r\nh4. Types (incomplete)\r\n* [b]Land vehicles[/b] - Vehicles that traverse on land.\r\n** [b]Man/animal-powered vehicles[/b]\r\n*** [[Bicycle]]\r\n**** [[Unicycle]]\r\n*** [[chariot_(vehicle)|Chariot]]\r\n*** [[Carriage]]\r\n*** [[Sled]]\r\n*** [[Sleigh]]\r\n*** [[wagon]]\r\n** [b]Motor vehicles[/b] - Vehicles powered by an engine or motor.\r\n*** [[ATV]]\r\n*** [[Car]]\r\n**** [[Limousine]]\r\n**** [[Van]]\r\n*** [[Combat vehicle]]\r\n**** [[AFV]]\r\n***** [[APC]]\r\n***** [[IFV]]\r\n***** [[Tank]]\r\n*** [[Kart]]\r\n*** [[Motorcycle]]\r\n**** [[Dirt bike]]\r\n**** [[Motor scooter]]\r\n**** [[Moped]]\r\n*** [[Train]]\r\n**** [[Locomotive]]\r\n*** [[Truck_(Vehicle)|truck]]\r\n\r\n* [b][[Watercraft]][/b] - Vehicles that can travel on or through water.\r\n** [b]Man/animal-powered watercraft[/b]\r\n*** [[Boat]]\r\n*** [[canoe]]\r\n*** [[Raft]]\r\n** [b]Nature-powered watercraft[/b]\r\n*** [[Sailing boat]]\r\n** [b]Motorized watercraft[/b]\r\n*** [[Hovercraft]]\r\n*** [[Jetski]]\r\n*** [[Ship]]\r\n*** [[Submarine]]\r\n\r\n* [b][[Aircraft]][/b] - Vehicles capable of atmospheric flight.\r\n** [b]Lighter-than-air aircraft[/b]\r\n*** [[Airship]]\r\n*** [[Hot air balloon]]\r\n** [b]Fixed-winged aircraft[/b]\r\n**** [[Glider]]\r\n**** [b]Powered aircraft[/b]\r\n***** [[Airplane]]\r\n****** [[Biplane]]\r\n****** [[Bomber]]\r\n****** [[Jet]]\r\n***** [b]Rotorcraft[/b] - Vehicles that make use of rotors blades to achieve flight.\r\n****** [[Helicopter]]\r\n\r\n* [b][[Spacecraft]][/b] - Vehicles designed for space travel.\r\n** [[Space shuttle]]\r\n** [[Rocket ship]]\r\n\r\nh4. Fictional Vehicles (Incomplete)\r\n* [b][[Superhero]] vehicles[/b]\r\n** [[Batmobile]]\r\n** [[Blackbird (x-men)]]\r\n** [[Fantasticar]]\r\n** [[Quinjet]]\r\n** [[Spidermobile]]\r\n* [b]spacecrafts[/b]\r\n** [[Flying saucer]]\r\n** [[Millenium Falcon]]\r\n** [[Dropship]]\r\n* [[Mecha]] - Vehicles that make use of legs to move.\r\n\r\nh4. Descriptions\r\n* [[vehicle interior]] - when we can see the interior of a vehicle\r\n* [[inside vehicle]] - when a scene is taking place inside a vehicle\r\n* [[Driver]] - when we can see the driver of land vehicle\r\n* [[Pilot]] - when we can see non-land vehicle operators\r\n\r\nh4. Actions\r\n* [[driving]]\r\n* [[vehicle collision]] or [[vehicle crash]] (maybe one should be redirected to the other)\r\n* [[vehicle transformation]]\r\n* [[vehicle destruction]] - the vehicle is destroyed\r\n* [[vehicle ingestion]] - the vehicle is being swallowed\r\n* [[vehicle insertion]] - the vehicle (as a whole) is inserted in an orifice\r\n* [[vehicle penetrated]] - the vehicle is sexually penetrated\r\n* [[sex on vehicle]] - a sex scene is happening on the vehicle\r\n\r\nh4.See Also\r\n* [[Drone (vehicle)]] - Unmanned vehicles."
            }
