          "airship": [
            {
              "tag": "airship",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 683,
              "wiki_body": "In real life an [b]airship[/b] (or [i]dirigible balloon[/i]) is a lighter-than-air [[aircraft]] that's filled with lighter-than-air gas, such as Hydrogen or Helium, to make itself float into the sky as well as being equipped with self-propulsion systems such as [[propeller|propellers]] and [[thrusters]].\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Examples]\r\nthumb #223862 thumb #43030 thumb #4091967 thumb #545267\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nIn [[fiction]] an airship also refers to any large floating aircraft that makes use of exotic technologies, concepts, and fictional materials and substances to stay afloat. These include things such as [[anti-gravity]], [[magic]], [[telekinesis]], and [[floating rocks]].\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Examples]\r\nthumb #52250 thumb #3998575 thumb #3675686 thumb #4114255\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4.Classifications\r\n* [b]Non-rigid[/b] - Airships that rely on internal gas pressure to retain its shape.\r\n** [[blimp]]\r\n* [b]Semi-rigid[/b] - Airships with some internal support structures but mainly relies on internal gas pressure.\r\n* [b]Rigid[/b] - Airships that rely on a framework or skeleton to retain its shape.\r\n** [[zeppelin]]\r\n\r\nh4.See also\r\n* [[hot_air_balloon]]"
            }
          ]
