              "tag": "phone",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 54062,
              "wiki_body": "A [b]Phone[/b], short for [i]telephone[/i] is a telecommunications device that transmits sound through electronic signals over a distance. This is most often used to conduct conversations between individuals. For a character actively talking on a phone, use [[phone call]].\r\n\r\nh5. Types of Phones\r\n\r\n* [[cellphone]]: any handheld mobile telephone\r\n** [[brick phone]]: the earliest cellphones, large, blocky mobile phones with antenna used from the 1980s to early 1990s\r\n** [[bar phone]]: a wide range of bar-shaped cellular devices\r\n** [[flip phone]]: a clamshell style folding cellphone, popular from the 1990s to late 2000s\r\n** [[smartphone]]: a mobile computing device with telephone capabilities\r\n* [[landline phone]]: a phone connected via wires to a telephone line, usually sits on a desk or is mounted to a wall\r\n* [[payphone]]: A public pay-per-use telephone, usually wall mounted or housed inside a [[telephone booth]]\r\n* [[rotary phone]]: a telephone with a rotary dial instead of buttons or a touch screen interface\r\n\r\nh5. Phone Related Tags\r\n* [[holding phone]]\r\n* [[looking at phone]]\r\n* [[texting]]\r\n** [[text message]]\r\n* [[phone call]]\r\n* [[ringing phone]]\r\n* [[vibrating phone]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[electronics]]"
