              "wiki_body": "A [b]playing card[/b] refers to a special card used in playing card games and gambling.\n\nThe most common type of playing card and the most likely to be encountered on e621 is the international (French) 52-card deck or one of its variants (which are often only distinguishable by the number of cards used in the deck; an example is the \"pinochle\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinochle deck which uses two copies each of 24 cards to make a total of 48 cards).\n\nthumb #4291103\n\nOther varieties include various non-[[fortune telling]] variants of [[tarot_card|tarot cards]], Spanish/Italian-suited decks, German-suited decks, Swiss-suited decks and so on.\nthumb #4792907 – [[tarot_nouveau|Tarot Nouveau]]\n\nthumb #5277632 – German suits\n\nthumb #5274841 – Spanish suits\n\nh2. International (French) Cards\n\n* 2-10, Jack, Queen, King, Ace in the following four suits:\n** ♣ – [[clubs_(suit)]]\n** ♦ – [[diamonds_(suit)]]\n** ♥ – [[hearts_(suit)]]\n** ♠ – [[spades_(suit)]]\n* 0, 1, 2 or more [[joker_(playing_card)|jokers]], usually distinguishable by color\n* A [[tarot_card|tarot]] deck adds the knight rank between jack and queen, 21 permanent [[trump_(tarot)|trumps]] and [[the_fool_(tarot)|one Fool]], but may remove other ranks\n* Traditionally, clubs and spades are colored black while diamonds and hearts are colored red, but other combinations are possible, such as green clubs and blue diamonds or green spades and yellow diamonds.\n\n[table][tr][th]thumb #4859421[/th][/tr][/table]\n[table]\n[tr][th][[ace of clubs|Ace of Clubs]][/th]\n[th][[ace of diamonds|Ace of Diamonds]][/th]\n[th][[ace of hearts|Ace of Hearts]][/th]\n[th][[ace of spades|Ace of Spades]][/th][/tr]\n[tr][th][[two of clubs|Two of Clubs]][/th]\n[th][[two of diamonds|Two of Diamonds]][/th]\n[th][[two of hearts|Two of Hearts]][/th]\n[th][[two of spades|Two of Spades]][/th][/tr]\n[tr][th][[three of clubs|Three of Clubs]][/th]\n[th][[three of diamonds|Three of Diamonds]][/th]\n[th]