            {
              "tag": "police_vehicle",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 820,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #4558659 thumb #3922373 thumb #3447008\r\n\r\nA [[vehicle]] used in service of a [[police]] agency. Including [[aircraft]] (particularly [[helicopter|helicopters]]) and [[motor vehicle|motor vehicles]].\r\n\r\nThis tag is particularly useful for common police motor vehicles that are not police cars or motorcycles — such as pickup trucks, SUVs, armoured vehicles, and three wheel service vehicles.\r\n\r\nh5. Visual Aspects of a Police Vehicle\r\n\r\n* Easily identifiable paint job:\r\n** black and white\r\n** navy blue and white\r\n** white, with blue and/or red markings\r\n** neon yellow and blue \"Battenburg\" checkerboard pattern \r\n* Red and blue, all-red or all-blue light bar or beacon lights affixed to the roof of the vehicle\r\n* Markings including the police agency's insignia, \"POLICE\" in large text, name of the city or area served\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[police car]]\r\n* [[police motorcycle]]"
            }
          ],
          "police_car": [
            {
              "tag": "police_car",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 720,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #953103\r\n\r\nA [[car]] used by a [[police]] agency (or other law enforcement). Police cars will almost always feature mounted flashing lights on the roof of the vehicle that are either red, blue, or a mix of red and blue. \r\n\r\nPolice cars, as with other police vehicles, are often depicted in two-tone black and white, blue or navy, or white; the colours and design of a police car can vary significantly depending on country and even from city to city within the same country.\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[police vehicle]]\r\n\r\n "
            }
          ]
