            "wiki_body": "A [b]computer[/b] is a programmable machine designed to sequentially and automatically carry out a sequence of arithmetic or logical operations. The particular sequence of operations can be changed readily, allowing the computer to solve more than one kind of problem.\r\n\r\nYou should seriously know what this is, as you MUST be on a form of computer in order to view this page!\r\n\r\nh4. Hardware\r\n\r\n* [[computer_keyboard]]\r\n* [[computer_monitor]]\r\n* [[computer_mouse]]\r\n* [[computer_tower]]\r\n\r\nh6. Internal hardware\r\n\r\n* [[graphics_card]]\r\n* [[processor]]\r\n* [[power_supply]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[electronics]]\r\n* [[video_games]]\r\n** [[game_console]] - For gaming hardware\r\n** [[game_controller]]\r\n* [[television]]\r\n* [[monitor]] - For monitors in general\r\n* [[laptop]]\r\n* [[phone]]\r\n** [[cellphone]] - Portable (mobile) phone, not necessarily with a big amount of features\r\n** [[smartphone]]\r\n* [[wrist_computer]] - Portable wrist-mounted devices often found in [[science fiction]]."
