            "tag": "robotization",
            "kor": "로봇화",
            "count": 445,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #3839323 thumb #3522587\n\nWhen a character is [[transformation|transformed]] into a [[robot]], an [[android]], or a full-body [[cyborg]]. Typically, this is done by a [[machine]] that replaces all of the subject's [[organs]] and bone structure with mechanical equivalents, and converts the victim's skin into a metallic chassis that houses the robot's components within. The transformation is often depicted as extremely painful.\n\nThis originated from the 1993 cartoon, \"Sonic the Hedgehog\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonic_the_Hedgehog_(TV_series), in which Dr. Robotnik combines robotic transformation with mind control to force people to act as a [[drone]] army under his command. This depiction of robotization continues in the spinoff comic series of the same name.\n\nh4.Not to be Confused with:\n* [[alternate species]] -  When the character is depicted by the artist as a robot but there is no [[transformation sequence]] nor [[mid transformation]] present in the post. Being depicted as a robot doesn't automatically imply robotization as this could be a case of [[alternate universe]] (as in this version of the character has always been a robot).\n\nh4. Related Tags:\n* [[android]] - an artificial lifeform made in the shape of a human or anthropomorphic character.\n* [[drone]] - when a character is brainwashed to have little or no thoughts, emotions, or personality aside from following commands.\n* [[robot]] - a mechanical device or entity which can either perform tasks on its own, or with guidance.\n* [[transformation]] - when a character transforms from one form to another.\n\nh4. See also:\n* [[reverse_robotization]] - when a robot becomes a living species."
