            "tag": "placard",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 289,
            "wiki_body": "[b]Placard[/b] is a small and usually impermanent notice, or [[sign]]. A placard is usually flat, small enough to be carried around, and commonly used in public spaces as a form of advertising. Most placards do not have a [[signpost]], or a method of self-support. The root of the term comes from the old French word [i]plaquier[/i], which means to plaster, or to lay flat.\r\n\r\nThe term can refer to any paperboard, or similar material sign, yard sale / garage sale / for sale signs, place card / table tent cards, most kinds of [[hanging_sign|hanging signs]], and hazard identification placards.\r\n\r\nh4. Types\r\n\r\n* [[hazard_placard]]\r\n* [[jail_placard]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[dogshaming]]\r\n* [[mugshot]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[plaque]]"
