            "tag": "through_screen",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 261,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #2777872 thumb #3970775 thumb #4672970 thumb #4536608\n\nWhen a character is shown emerging from, or entering into, an electronic screen, such as through a computer monitor, television or smartphone. This also applies to a character sticking parts of their body into or out of a screen, or reaching into one screen, and their hand emerging through another. \n\nThis visual trope is strongly associated with characters who are digital or virtual in nature, and with supernatural horror entities, most famously seen with [[Sadako Yamamura]] from [[The Ring]]. Other characters such as [[Rambley Raccoon]] from [[Indigo Park]] and [[scp-1471-a]] (\"Mal0\") of [[SCP Foundation]] lore are also commonly seen with this trope. \n\nh4. Commonly Seen With... \n\n* [[breaking the fourth wall]] - when images feature a cracked/broken glass overlay, and/or static, digital glitching, or a broken LCD effect, implying the character is coming out of the viewer's screen.\n* [[thinking with portals]] - when a character is using multiple screens to reach otherwise unreachable places, or access/present body parts in a way that would be impossible (e.g. a character's upper body emerging from one screen, and their butt emerging from another)\n* [[reaching towards viewer]]\n* [[talking to viewer]]\n"
