            "club_(weapon)": [
              {
                "tag": "club_(weapon)",
                "kor": "",
                "count": 1639,
                "wiki_body": "A club (also known as cudgel, baton, truncheon, cosh, nightstick, or bludgeon) is among the simplest of all weapons. A club is essentially a short staff, or stick, usually made of wood, and has been wielded as a weapon since prehistoric times.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[Club (disambiguation)]]\r\n* [[♣]]\r\n* [[Nightclub]]\r\n* [[Mace]]\r\n"
              }
            ],
            "cleaver_(weapon)": [
              {
                "tag": "cleaver_(weapon)",
                "kor": "",
                "count": 184,
                "wiki_body": "thumb #4542200 thumb #1551696 thumb #3597886 thumb #1831850\r\n\r\nThe [b]cleaver[/b] is a weaponized variant of the kitchen utensil of the [[cleaver_(knife)|same name]]. It's also larger in size; Large enough to be considered a type of [[sword]].\r\n\r\nThe [[blade]] is single edged, [[broadsword|broad-bladed]], of variable length (from a [[short_sword]] to a [[greatsword]]), a blunt flat top, and may be sloped or straight edged.\r\n\r\nThe [[hilt]] is guardless and is connected at the back end of the bottom of the blade as opposed to the center like most swords do.\r\n\r\nIn most depictions, cleavers are wielded by savage or bloodthirsty characters, reflecting the blade's original purpose as a meat chopping implement."
              }
            ],
