              "wiki_body": "A [b]battle axe[/b], as the name implies, is an [[axe]] made for combat. It consists of an arm-length handle and an axe head of varying shapes and sizes.\r\n\r\nh4. Types:\r\n* Simple:\r\n** [[adze]] - Horizontal bit.\r\n** [[broad_axe]] - Wider bit.\r\n** [[felling_axe]] - The \"normal\" axe used for chopping wood.\r\n** [[double_bitted_axe]] - Axe bit × 2\r\n*** [[labrys]] - Short handle + symmetrical bits\r\n** [[double_axe]] - Axe head × 2\r\n\r\n* [[Tools]]\r\n** [[fire_axe]] - Axe + Pick\r\n** [[hatchet]] - A small one-handed axe.\r\n** [[ice_axe]]\r\n** [[mattock]] - Axe + Adze\r\n** [[pickaxe]] - Axe / Adze + Point\r\n** [[pulaski]] - Axe + Adze\r\n\r\n* [[weapon|Weapons]]\r\n** [[greataxe]] - Polearm + Big axe head\r\n** [[halberd]] - Polearm + Axe + Spear + Pick\r\n** [[poleaxe]] - Polearm + Axe + Spear + Hammer\r\n** [[shepherd's_axe]] - Axe + Walking stick\r\n** [[tomahawk]] - A hatchet-like axe from North America.\r\n\r\nh4. External:\r\n* \"Wikipedia - Axe\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axe"
