            "kor": "",
            "count": 308,
            "wiki_body": "An [b]energy weapon[/b] is a [[weapon]], [[artifact]], or [[device]] that makes use of some type of [[energy]] (such as light, plasma or even [[magic]]) as its primary means of inflicting damage.\r\n\r\nh4.Ranged Energy Weapons\r\n\r\nthumb #3067795 thumb #4083213 thumb #4329537 thumb #2810780\r\n\r\nAlso known as [i]directed-energy weapons[/i] in real life, these types of energy weapons produce energy projectiles or emit beams of energy instead of solid projectiles.\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Types]\r\n* [[energy_gun]] - Energy weapons designed like a handheld [[gun|firearm]] for ergonomic convenience.\r\n** [[laser_gun]] - Guns that fire focused beams of light.\r\n** [[plasma_gun]] - Guns use plasma as its projectile.\r\n*** [[plasma_pistol]] - A [[handgun]] that fires plasma bolts.\r\n*** [[plasma_rifle]] - A larger plasma gun designed after a [[rifle]].\r\n** [[raygun]] - Consisting of coiled energy projector and a bulbous body, this is an old school energy gun that can fire all sorts of exotic energies at the target that causes a myriad of effects from [[transformation]] to [[disintegration]]. \r\n** [[blaster]] - Another old school energy weapon. This one is more gun-like in appearance with an energy projector shaped like a barrel of a gun.\r\n** [[arc_thrower]] - An energy gun that shoots directed steams or bolts of [[electricity]] at a target from long range.\r\n** [[energy_bow]] - A [[bow_(weapon)|bow]], and its [[arrow_(weapon)|arrows]], that are made out of pure [[energy]] or [[magic]].\r\n* [[tesla_coil]] - A metal rod enclosed by a series of rings and topped with a sphere that electricity. Although not a weapon in real life, in fiction these devices have been used as directed energy weapons.\r\n* [[sonic_weapon]] - Weapons that makes use of strong sound waves to subdue or even harm a target from a distance.\r\n** [[dubstep_gun]] - A sonic gun with a speaker-like energy emitter that fires weaponized [[dubstep]] at a target.\r\n* [[plasma_grenade]] - A thrown ranged explosive ([[grenade]]) that releases plasma explosions instead of conventional ones.\r\n* [[particle_weapon]] - Energy weapons that fire hyper-accelerated molecular projectiles.\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Projectile Types]\r\n* [[energy_beam]] - A continuous stream of projected energy.\r\n** [[energy_blast]] - An energy beam with a cone-shaped area of effect.\r\n** [[laser_beam]] - an energy beam made out of focused light.\r\n* [[energy_ball]] - An orb or sphere of pure energy or magic fired as a projectile.\r\n* [[plasma_ball]] - A glob of hot plasma fired as a projectile.\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4.Melee Energy Weapons\r\n\r\nthumb #3135584 thumb #2972516 thumb #4059423 thumb #2237912\r\n\r\nA weapon that emits energy to be used as a close-quarters combat weapon. They're usually devices designed after a conventional melee weapon and emit energy constructs from an emitter in place of a solid blade or weapon head. Alternatively these are spectral weapons made entirely out of pure energy which are usually created by a [[magic spell]] by a [[magic user]].\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Types]\r\n* [[energy_blade]] - A device that emits a steady stream of thin length of energy in place of and acts as a cutting blade.\r\n** [[energy_sword]] - A [[hilt]]-like handheld device that emits a long energy blade. Alternatively a long paddle-like device that emits energy from its edges.\r\n** [[energy_axe]] - A haft or polearm that projects a wide but short steam of energy.\r\n** [[energy_dagger]] - A small handheld device that emits a short energy blade. Alternatively a short stick-shaped device that emits energy from its edges.\r\n** [[energy_claws]] - A device that projects a row of energy blades, creating a [[claw]]-like effect.\r\n* [[energy_polearm]] - A [[quarterstaff]]-like device that emits energy from its business end.\r\n** [[energy_scythe]] - A [[polearm]] that projects a long forward-facing curved energy blade.\r\n** [[energy_spear]] - A polearm that projects a concentrated spike of energy from the top of the device.\r\n* [[energy_hammer]] - An energy weapon that causes crushing or concussive damage despite being made of energy.\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4.Named Energy Weapons\r\n* [[lightsaber]] - A type of energy sword from the [i][[Star Wars]][/i] franchise.\r\n* The [b]Type-1 Energy Weapon[/b], or just [i]\"energy sword\"[/i], from the [i][[halo_(series)|Halo]][/i] franchise. A [[katar]]-like energy blade.\r\n* The [b]Psionic Blade[/b], or just [i]\"psi-blade\"[/i], from the [i][[starcraft_(series)|StarCraft]] [/i]. A [[vambrace]] with a blade emitter powered by psionic energy.\r\n* [[mega_buster]] - An [[arm_cannon]] used by [[mega_man_(character)|Mega Man]] from the franchise of the [[mega_man_(series)|same name]].\r\n\r\nh4.Not to be confused with\r\n* [[futuristic_gun]] - Not all guns with futuristic designs fire energy projectiles.\r\n\r\nh4.See also\r\n* [[electromagnetic_launcher]] - Ranged weapons that uses magnetism to accelerate solid ammunition.\r\n** [[gauss_rifle]] - A single-railed launcher.\r\n** [[railgun]] - A launcher that makes use of parallel rails.\r\n** [[coilgun]] - A barreled launcher with electrical coils wrapped around it."
