          "tag": "american_football",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 698,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1315091 thumb #473086 thumb #473081\r\n\r\n[b]American football[/b], also known as [b]Gridiron football[/b], is a sport played with an oval shaped ball ([[gridiron_ball]]) by two teams of eleven players on a rectangular field with goalposts at each end.\r\n\r\nAs the name suggests, American football is most popular in America where it is more commonly known as [b]football[/b].\r\n\r\nThe term \"football\" used to refer to American football can be confusing, as outside North America, \"football\" is more commonly used to refer to [[soccer]] (association football) or [[Australian rules football]] in the case of Australia.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[cheerleader]]\r\n* [[gridiron_ball]]\r\n* [[mascot]]\r\n* [[nfl]] (National Football League)\r\n* [[shoulder_pads]]\r\n* [[sports]]\r\n* [[uniform]]"
