        {
          "tag": "planted_leg",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 669,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1774638 thumb #375218 thumb #1548417 thumb #123877\r\n\r\nA character with a single leg that is planted. If both legs are planted, use [[planted_legs]] instead.\r\n\r\nThe term [i]planted[/i] in this context refers to a leg (or foot rather) that is firmly contacting a surface through the sole. For tagging purposes, this applies to a leg that is either in a resting posture (not supporting body weight), or the unsupportive leg of a [[standing]] posture on one leg.\r\n\r\nA leg that is supporting a character does not count as planted, which will exclude this tag from applying to most standing, crouching, or kneeling postures. A leg that is planted is almost always going to be bent at the knee.\r\n\r\nNote: Due to the extra joint in [[digitigrade]] characters, this tag may apply to situations where the leg is resting on the joint, as well as the paw.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[bent_leg]] (when the other leg is [[extended_leg|extended]] or [[straight_leg|straight]])\r\n* [[bent_legs]] (when the other leg is [[raised_leg|raised]], [[leg_over_edge|over an edge]], [[crossed_legs|crossed]], bent and on its side, or bent and supporting the character on [[on_one_knee|one knee]], [[on_one_leg|one leg]] etc)\r\n* [[knee_pulled_up]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related postures\r\n\r\n* [[lying]]\r\n* [[reclining]]\r\n* [[sitting]]\r\n* [[step_pose]] / [[step_position]]"
