          "tag": "bow_(feature)",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 42699,
          "wiki_body": "A [b]bow[/b] is a feature of a [[ribbons|ribbon]], or twine ([[string]], [[rope]]) characterized by two loops, or flared ends fastened together by a knot, or in some instances clamped together with glue.\r\n\r\nh4. Tagging notes\r\n\r\n* These bows are attached to, or designed to attach to characters, clothing, or other objects.\r\n* Not all bows are [i]real[/i], or constructed from actual ribbon.\r\n* Not all bows are in the main scene. Some will be part of a [[bow_print|print]] instead.\r\n* The term [i]bow[/i] tends to loosely apply whether the ends are loops, or flared. Some concepts that just appear tied, especially for concepts like wearing a [[kerchief]], shouldn't be considered a bow.\r\n* Anatomy bows should be introduced into this tag in the future. The concept is comparably relevant to wearable bows, and makes tagging easier.\r\n** Anatomy bows should be kept out of accessory dedicated tags ([[bow_tie]], [[ear_bow]], [[hair_bow]], [[neck_bow]]), and use the anatomy dedicated tags instead.\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Bow terms]\r\n\r\nThese definitions can be used to make design based categories in the future.\r\n\r\n* Butterfly Bow: A bow with flared ends, and no tails.\r\n* Loop Bow: A bow with at least two loops. Some bows don't have any loops, and a [[gift bow]] can have more than two. \r\n* Sailor Bow: A bow with its tails underneath the loops, or the flared ends / loops are longer on the bottom than at the top.\r\n* [[Twin Bows]]: Bows located in the same relative location on hair, body parts, or clothing.\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Bow categories]\r\n\r\nh4. Accessories\r\n\r\nA bow that is adorned to a character's skin, fur, hair for the purpose of improving a character's appearance.\r\n\r\nthumb #1156647 thumb #52215 thumb #1503857\r\n\r\n* [[bow_accessory]]\r\n\r\nh4. Clothing\r\n\r\nA bow that is attached to an article of clothing, or is perceived as part of an outfit.\r\n\r\nthumb #2220096 thumb #2429819 thumb #2078461\r\n\r\n* [[bow_tie]]\r\n* [[clothing_bow]]\r\n** [[bow_apron]]\r\n** [[bow_dress]]\r\n** [[bow_panties]]\r\n\r\nh4. Decorations\r\n\r\nA bow that is attached to a prop such as a [[gift]], or integrated with the background in some kind of creative way.\r\n\r\nthumb #2431901 thumb #868227\r\n\r\n* [[bow_(decoration)]]\r\n* [[gift_bow]] - It may not be useful to include these with the other decorative bows.\r\n\r\nh4. Bondage\r\n\r\nA bow that is associated with [[ribbon bondage]]. These probably shouldn't be treated as accessories.\r\n\r\nthumb #792858 thumb #573486 thumb #405829\r\n\r\n* [[bow_ribbon]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Types\r\n\r\n* [[bow_(anatomy)]] - Such as the ones seen on [[Sylveon]]. Concept is not officially part of the `bow_(feature)` tag yet, and has its own anatomy based tags.\r\n* [[bow_ribbon]]\r\n* [[decorated_bow]]\r\n* [[string_bow]]\r\n\r\nh6. By usage\r\n\r\n* [[bow_accessory]]\r\n** [[hair_bow]]\r\n** [[tail_bow]]\r\n* [[bow_collar]]\r\n* [[bow_(decoration)]]\r\n** [[wreath_bow]]\r\n* [[bow_tie]]\r\n* [[clothing_bow]]\r\n* [[gift_bow]]\r\n\r\nh6. By location\r\n\r\n* [[arm_bow]]\r\n** [[shoulder_bow]]\r\n** [[wrist_bow]]\r\n* [[back_bow]]\r\n* [[balls_bow]]\r\n* [[belly_bow]]\r\n* [[bow_in_back]]\r\n* [[bow_in_front]]\r\n* [[breast_bow]]\r\n* [[chest_bow]]\r\n* [[crotch_bow]]\r\n* [[ear_bow]]\r\n* [[facial_bow]]\r\n* [[hair_bow]]\r\n* [[horn_bow]]\r\n* [[leg_bow]]\r\n** [[ankle_bow]]\r\n** [[thigh_bow]]\r\n* [[neck_bow]]\r\n* [[nipple_bow]]\r\n* [[penis_bow]]\r\n* [[sheath_bow]]\r\n* [[tail_bow]]\r\n* [[waist_bow]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[gift]]\r\n* [[gift_wrapped]]\r\n* [[ribbon_bondage]]"
