          "tag": "bicycle",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1182,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #2308262\r\n\r\nA [b]bicycle[/b], also called a [b]bike[/b], is a muscle powered, two-wheel typically pedal-driven [[vehicle]]. Bicycles are a ubiquitous means of personal transportation, exercise, sport, and recreation around the world. Bicycles may be used for policing and military purposes (in the latter case, for reconnaissance); as well as commercial purposes, when hitched to a trailer to haul cargo, or used to make deliveries.\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n* [[Cycling]] - for a character in the process of riding a bicycle\r\n* [[Bicycle Helmet]] - protective headgear worn while operating a bicycle \r\n\r\nh4.See Also:\r\n* [[BMX]] - an off-road sport bicycle used for racing and stunt riding\r\n* [[Exercise Bike]] - a stationary piece of exercise equipment that allows one to cycle in place\r\n* [[Motorcycle]] - A motorized two-wheel vehicle similar in form as a bicycle\r\n* [[Tricycle]] - a three-wheeled vehicle similar to a bicycle\r\n* [[Unicycle]] - a one-wheeled pedal-powered vehicle\r\n"
