        {
          "tag": "device",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 341,
          "wiki_body": "A [b]device[/b] refers to physical hardware or equipment that is made for a particular purpose. This is a broad term that includes electrical, [[electronics|electronic]], and [[machine|mechanical]] devices. Fantasy oriented settings may contain other types of devices (e.g. [[magic]]).\r\n\r\nThis tag can be used for visible mechanical or electrical contraptions, or machines. Consider using more specific tags in addition to this tag such as the [i]name of the device[/i], and [i]what type it is (electrical, electronic, mechanical)[/i].\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[component]] - A smaller part of a device or machine. If the object is attached to a larger device, this tag is probably more appropriate. \r\n* [[plot_device]] - Abstract examples of devices should not use the device tag.\r\n\r\nh4. List of devices\r\n\r\n* [b]device[/b]\r\n** [[computer]]\r\n** [[console]]\r\n** [[controller]]\r\n** [[handheld_device]]\r\n*** [[cellphone]]\r\n*** [[handheld_console]]\r\n*** [[remote_control]]\r\n** [[phone]]"
