        {
          "tag": "papercraft",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 280,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #451639 thumb #2796695\r\n\r\n[b]Papercraft[/b] is an umbrella tag for a number of related arts and crafts, all of which primarily use paper as material. This can range from simple crafts like a \"paper people chain\", to more complex arts like origami or using pieces of carefully cut card stock/paperboard to create 3d models. This tag can refer to the medium a submission is created in, or depictions of characters creating papercrafts (or are living papercraft themselves).\r\n\r\nh4. Papercraft Related Tags:\r\n* [[Origami]] - A Japanese art form of using folded paper to create figures\r\n* [[Paper Doll]] - A figure cut out of paper, often includes clothing that can also be cut out and stuck on the figure using attached tabs\r\n* [[Paper Child]] - A drawing of a character cut out of paper, drawn in a pose that gives the illusion of the character interacting with real world objects\r\n* [[Paper Chain]] - A series of paper loops chained together, often for decoration (not to be confused with a paper people chain)\r\n* [[Paper Airplane]] - A folded piece of paper resembling an [[airplane]] that can glide through the air when tossed"
