        {
          "tag": "object_ingestion",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 269,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #5080835 thumb #2238391 thumb #2432057 thumb #2132562\n\n[b]Object ingestion[/b] describes a character orally consuming an inanimate, non-food object. \n\n\n\nUsually, this involves the character [[swallowing]] the object whole, less commonly, the character may bite off piece of the object, chew up the object, and swallow the chewed pieces or remains of the object. \n\nThis tag [i]should not[/i] be confused with or applied to depictions of a character merely [[deep throat|deep throating]] an object, where the object being held and inserted into the mouth/throat, simulating fellatio. This tag requires the object being actively eaten or swallowed, if not already inside of the character's body, as well as characters implicitly having ingested, and regurgitating the previously ingested object. This tag can also apply to [i]technically[/i] edible items being consumed whole - such as a character swallowing a whole egg. \n______________________________________________________________________________________________________________\n\nObject ingestion may be shown in a humorous context, with a character gleefully eating absurdly inedible objects, or alternatively, accidentally swallowing an object. A character might intentionally eat objects to [[stuffing|stuff themselves]] or to satisfy their hunger - either swallowing a large number of inanimate objects, or a single, very large object, causing their belly to [[bloated|bloat]]. Characters may also ingest objects to [[stomach storage|store them in their stomach]], this is usually shown alongside the use of other orifices to store items. \n\nAn ingested object may end up being regurgitated, pass through the digestive tract and excreted intact, or end up [[digestion|digested]] in the stomach; however, few images [i]explicitly[/i] show the fate of ingested items, and any result is usually only conveyed by dialogue, or implied by digestive noises. \n\n[section=Object Ingestion Vs. Object Vore]\n\nThe line between these two tags can be fuzzy, object ingestion is often associated with [[vore]], and object ingestion can appeal to vorarephiles. \n\nPosts tagged as object ingestion may also feature [[vore]] elements - such as a character shown consuming an object, and telling another character to \"go in after it\", or threatening that another character is next to be eaten - posts like this are better tagged as [[imminent vore]] and object ingestion, rather than [[object vore]]. Object ingestion, [i]unlike object vore[/i], specifically applies to [i]oral consumption[/i] of inanimate objects, while object vore can apply to more exotic means of consumption.\n\n[[Object vore]] should ideally be applied when characters are ingested with objects, characters transformed into objects, or when a character who is [[animate inanimate]] (and leaning towards the inanimate in appearance) is consumed by another; object vore is most often applied to when a character consumes an object that explicitly or implicitly, holds living beings - such as a planet, building, or vehicle - as well as objects like a [[pokéball]] or a [[magic lamp]] that holds living creatures or characters as energy or magic. \n[/section]\n\nh4. Related Tags\n\n* [b][i]Location of Object:[/i][/b]\n** [[object in mouth]]\n** [[object in throat]]\n** [[object in stomach]]\n\n\n* [[condom swallowing]]\n* [[swallowing eggs]]\n\nh5. See Also\n* [[pica]]\n* [[vore]]\n** [[object vore]]\n* [[object insertion]]\n* [[deep throat]]\n* [[cavity storage]]\n** [[stomach storage]]\n** [[anal storage]]\n** [[breast storage]]\n** [[vaginal storage]]\n** [[bladder storage]]\n** [[testicle storage]]\n"
        },
