          "tag": "xbox_console",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 146,
          "wiki_body": "The umbrella tag for any model of [[Xbox]] gaming console. An Xbox console is a rectangular piece of equipment designed to read, and play Xbox video games. An Xbox console is operated by a detached controller interface, and in later model releases included voice activation and motion tracking support via the [[Kinect]] controller. The Kinect is considered an [[Xbox controller]], and not part of the console itself.\r\n\r\nMost of the time the specific model can be identified, and the most specific model tag applicable to the image should be used. Sub model tagging is optional.\r\n\r\nh4. Xbox consoles\r\n\r\n* [[xbox_360_console]]\r\n** [[xbox_360_e]]\r\n** [[xbox_360_s]]\r\n* [[xbox_one_console]]\r\n** [[xbox_one_s_console]]\r\n** [[xbox_one_x_console]]\r\n* [[xbox_original_console]]\r\n* [[xbox_series_x/s]] - These are not console tags. The Xbox console tag needs to be added separately.\r\n** [[xbox_series_s]]\r\n** [[xbox_series_x]]\r\n\r\nh4. External links\r\n\r\n* Console reference information: https://bestreamer.com/gaming-hardware/all-xbox-generations-in-order/\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[xbox]]\r\n** [b]xbox_console[/b]\r\n** [[xbox_controller]]\r\n** [[xbox_software]]"
