          "wiki_body": "thumb #2893373 thumb #3880799 thumb #3844730 thumb #3399155 thumb #1531707\n\nA [[seductive]] facial expression with [[narrowed eyes]], [b]bedroom eyes[/b] is a sultry look that expresses interest in romantic or sexual activity. This subtle form of seduction is often combined with a coy or naughty [[smile]] and more direct seductive expressions, like a [[beckoning]] gesture, [[inviting]] [[dialogue]], or outright sexual [[presenting]]. Bedroom eyes look at, and are meant to be seen by, a target, usually [[looking_at_viewer|the viewer]].\n\nh5. Do not confuse with\n\n* [[looking_pleasured]] - pleasure is an overpowering feeling that disrupts a person's composure. Thus, [i]looking_pleasured[/i] is incompatible with most other expressions, including [i]bedroom_eyes[/i]. Also, as a concept, seduction seeks intimacy and pleasure, so a seductive character should not already have pleasure.\n\n* [[masturbation]] - a character may [[teasing|teasingly]] masturbate to entice their target, but active forms of masturbation will generally only show [i]looking_pleasured[/i]. Bedroom eyes are possible with passive masturbation, like a [[buttplug in ass]] without manual stimulation, because this masturbation may not cause much if any pleasure.\n\n* [[sex]] - as a form of seduction, a character does not show bedroom eyes during sex. Sex is often the goal of seduction, but the two do not overlap.\n** A character having sex may show facial expressions that look a lot like bedroom eyes and not necessarily like pleasure. This expression may not have a tag yet, but it is not [i]bedroom_eyes[/i] because the time for seduction has passed.\n\n* [[looking_down]] - looking down doesn't imply to look at someone with a positive attitude, and even don't imply to look at someone.\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[beckoning]]\n* [[coy]]\n* [[dirty_talk]]\n* [[foreplay]]\n* [[inviting]]\n* [[looking_at_viewer]]\n* [[lust]]\n* [[naughty_face]]\n* [[presenting]]\n* [[smile]]\n* [[stripper