        {
          "tag": "street",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 3781,
          "wiki_body": "A [b]street[/b] is a pathway designed for vehicular traffic within a populated area, such as a [[city]], [[town]], or [[village]], they are found in [[urban]] and [[suburbs|suburban]] areas. Streets are usually bordered on either side by a [[sidewalk]] for pedestrian travel, and may have [[street lamp|street lamps]], and/or [[utility pole|utility poles]], and have buildings along them. While usually paved with asphalt in modern times, a street (especially in a fantasy or period setting) may be paved in stone or even tiling.   \r\n\r\nh5. [[Road]] vs. Street\r\nFor the purposes of tagging, street should only be used for pathways with the characteristics described above — found in urban/suburban areas, with buildings along them, and having lighting, sidewalks and possibly utility poles. [[Road]] is specifically intended for paved, gravel, or dirt pathways for vehicles, or more generally for roads in [[rural]] or remote settings. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[road_sign]]\r\n* [[sidewalk]]\r\n* [[street_lamp]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[path]]\r\n* [[road]]\r\n** [[highway]]\r\n** [b]street[/b]"
