          "count": 21588,
          "wiki_body": "When a censor isn't censoring the thing that was intended to be censored. This is usually because of an extremely thin and poorly placed [[censor bar]] (whether on purpose or not), but it can also be because the artist simply wanted to be funny.\r\n\r\nThis is often done by Japanese artists as a token to comply with the vaguely-worded \"Article 175\":https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Penal_Code_%28Japan%29#Chapter_XXII_Crimes_of_Obscenity,_Forcible_Sexual_Intercourse,_and_Bigamy of the Japanese Penal Code which prohibits distributing obscene imagery.\r\n\r\nA more effective version of this would be [[fill-in_censorship]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[censored]]\r\n** [[<3_censor]]\r\n** [[censor_bar]]\r\n** [[convenient_censorship]]\r\n*** [[hair_covering_breasts]]\r\n*** [[light_censorship]]\r\n*** [[tail_censorship]]\r\n** [[creative_censorship]]\r\n** [[fill-in_censorship]]\r\n** [b]ineffective_censorship[/b]\r\n** [[mosaic_censorship]]\r\n** [[naturally_censored]]\r\n*** [[nipple_tuft]]\r\n** [[pokéball_censor]]\r\n* [[uncensored]]\r\n* [[uncensor_request]]"
