          "wiki_body": "Though the actual definition is somewhat rocky, a planet can be simply defined as a large celestial body with a spherical shape other than a star or satellite (i.e. moons).\r\nObviously, this tag only applies when the planet in question is observed from outside (or, in borderline cases, very near the edge of) the atmosphere.\r\n\r\nh4. Planets\r\n\r\n* [[earth]]\r\n* [[jupiter_(planet)]]\r\n* [[mars_(planet)]]\r\n* [[mercury_(planet)]]\r\n* [[neptune_(planet)]]\r\n* [[pluto_(dwarf_planet)]]\r\n* [[saturn_(planet)]]\r\n* [[uranus_(planet)]]\r\n* [[venus_(planet)]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[asteroid]]\r\n* [[comet]]\r\n* [[moon]]\r\n* [[moon_(celestial_body)]]\r\n* [[planet destruction]]\r\n* [[planetoid]]\r\n* [[space]]"
