          "tag": "cart",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 566,
          "wiki_body": "[i]This wiki is under construction.[/i]\r\n\r\nA [b]cart[/b] may refer to any small typically rectangular two or four wheeled structure used to carry heavy materials, animals, and other objects more easily. Traditional carts often appear in [[Old West]], [[farm|agricultural]], and [[medieval]] settings, but more modern cart variations can be found in various settings, particularly [[grocery_store|grocery stores]], and the hospitality, or [[airport|airlines]] industries.\r\n\r\nTraditional carts typically have two large wheels and a flat surface to hold freight; they are sometimes pulled by horses, goats, dogs and (in Ancient Rome) geese.\r\n\r\nIf you're being really pedantic, a cart is different from a [[wagon]], which has four wheels, and a [[carriage]], which is designed for transporting humans specifically. The difference between modern wagons, and carts is minor, and hybridized variants have been produced and marketed as [i]wagon carts[/i] or [i]cart wagons[/i].\r\n\r\nh4. Types (Incomplete)\r\n\r\n* [[hand_cart]]\r\n* [[hand_truck]]\r\n* [[trolley]]\r\n** [[baggage_cart]]\r\n** [[service_cart]]\r\n*** [[food_service_cart]]\r\n** [[shopping_cart]]\r\n*** [[motorized_shopping_cart]]\r\n* [[vending_cart]]\r\n** [[food_cart]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[load_carrier]]\r\n** [b]cart[/b]"
