          "wiki_body": "thumb #1026719 thumb #1339025 thumb #372136\r\nA bustier is a form-fitting garment for women traditionally worn as [[lingerie]]. Its primary purpose is to emphasize [[cleavage]] by compressing the [[breasts]] up and inwards, while gently shaping the waist.\r\n\r\nOften confused with a [[corset]]; the primary difference is that a bustier always supports the breasts directly and often has distinctly molded cups similar to a [[bra]] for this purpose, while a corset is primarily designed to slim the waist and overall figure and may not cover the breasts at all.\r\n\r\nA bustier never has shoulder straps, but can have [[Garter Straps]]. It must also extend somewhat below the bust line - a garment which supports the breasts but not the waist is likely a [[strapless bra]].\r\n\r\nGeneral tag: [b][[Lingerie]][/b]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[Babydoll]]\r\n* [[Basque]]\r\n* [[Camisole]]\r\n* [[Chemise]]\r\n* [[Corset]]\r\n* [[Negligee]]\r\n* [[Teddiette]]\r\n* [[Teddy_(clothing)]]"
