          "count": 429,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3541513 thumb #3218049 thumb #1387140 thumb #3355144\r\n\r\nAn individual who delivers [[letter|letters]] and [[packages|packages]] to specified destinations, while working for a postal service. \"Postal carriers\" are more popularly known as postal workers, or referred to with gendered terms such as mailman/mailwoman or postman/postwoman. \r\n\r\nCharacters working as postal carriers are almost always depicted with a large, over the shoulder satchels, they will usually have a prominent logo featuring elements such as an envelope, post horn, and/or wings, on their cap, shirt, or satchel. They may be shown with, or driving in, a [[postal van]].\r\n\r\nPostal uniforms vary by country,  but typically consist of a collared or button-up shirt, a coat or jacket (depending on weather conditions), the jacket may possibly be in high visibility colours (or they may wear a safety vest, bottomwear is limited to [[pants|slacks]] or [[shorts]].  Postal workers may be shown wearing baseball caps, peaked caps, wide brimmed [[pith_helmet|safari helmets]], or bucket hats.\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[mail]]\r\n* [[letter]]\r\n* [[envelope]]\r\n* [[mailbox]]\r\n* [[postal van]]\r\n* [[mailbag]]\r\n* [[satchel]]\r\n* [[uniform]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n\r\n* [[tag group:professions]]"
