          "tag": "lake",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 4609,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #877122 thumb #560001 thumb #720117\r\n\r\nA [b]lake[/b] is an area of variable size filled with [[water]], [[lava]], or other fluids. Lakes are usually fed by [[river|rivers]] and streams, and are generally deep enough to support aquatic life.\r\n\r\nLakes may be large enough to support activities such as [[boat|boating]], underwater [[diving]], or [[airplane|seaplane]] operations. During [[winter]], lakes can freeze over in sufficient thickness to allow [[ice skating]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n* [[tag_group:locations]]\r\n* [[pond]] – a body of standing water smaller than a lake\r\n* [[sea]] – a body of water larger than a lake"
