          "count": 1866,
          "wiki_body": "A [b]bridge[/b] is a structure that spans an obstacle (such as a body of water, valley, road, or rail), and allows passage across it, without blocking the way underneath. Bridges can be made to specifically carry pedestrians, automobiles, trains or even boats, and can vary from a small wooden or stone bridge across a stream, to a rail bridge over a road, to a massive suspension bridge across a bay. \r\n\r\nThis tag is best used when a bridge is not merely a small background element, but when it is detailed or visually prominent in the scenery, or has characters standing on it, sitting on the edge of, jumping from, walking across, or otherwise interacting with the bridge.\r\n\r\nh5. Famous Bridges\r\n* [[tower bridge]]\r\n* [[golden gate bridge]]\r\n* [[sydney harbour bridge]] \r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[suspension bridge]]\r\n* [[rope bridge]]"
