          "count": 3820,
          "wiki_body": "Thumb #2018255 thumb #1148509 thumb #1999484\r\n\r\nA fortified structure, commonly made of stone.  Primarily found in the middle ages, these buildings are usually the residence of a lord or noble.  \r\n\r\nAt least in the real world, a castle *must* be fortified.  If it is not, it is a palace instead.\r\nIf a noble does not live there, it is a fortress instead.\r\nIf it is a village with a set of defensive walls, it is a fortified settlement.\r\n\r\nHowever, in the realm of art, it can be very challenging to determine if a structure is home, or not, to a noble. Indeed, it can be hard to tell if a structure is a building or just a stone wall.\r\n\r\nAs such, here are some guidelines for tagging castle-ish structures.\r\n\r\n* If it seems to be a 'set piece' designed to add a fantasy-flare to an image, tag it as castle.\r\n* If the structure appears to be large and grand, with many parts and structures (even if off screen) tag it castle\r\n* if the structure appears to consist only of a single tower, tag it as [[tower]], not castle.  A castle may have towers, a tower does not need a castle.\r\nthumb #1811954 thumb #2235429\r\n* In the event that there appears to be a village or city included within a set of walls, or an otherwise highly defensible position, tag [[Fortified_settlement]] as well as castle\r\nthumb #2242077 thumb #315433\r\n* A small structure with heavy defenses, which may be made of stone or would and may or may not have a castle-like design may be a [[fort]]\r\n* A castle cannot be tagged from within(?)\r\n** If you feel that an image takes place inside of a castle, tag [[throne_room]] if the room is particularly pretty or imposing, or features a throne.\r\n* If the castle is destroyed, tag [[ruins]] as well\r\n\r\nh4. Features\r\n\r\n* [[Stone Wall]] - though please only tag should the wall be prominent in the image, making up a major part of the background.\r\n* [[Stone floor]] - The same rules apply here, of course.  \r\n* [[Tower]]\r\n* [[Battlement]] - A wall you can stand on, usually with parapets.\r\n** If there is a guard, they may be [[on battlements]]\r\n* [[Parapet]] - A low defensive wall on top of a larger wall, used to shield defenders from enemy missiles.  May or may not be crenelated.\r\n* [[Crenelations]] are the distinctive part of the castle wall that goes up and down.\r\n* [[Arrowslit]] - a tall narrow window used to shoot out of.\r\n* [[Portcullis]] - a wooden or metal grill intended to block a major entry way.\r\n* [[Moat]] - a body of water around a castle. May contain monsters.\r\n\r\nh4. Named Castles\r\n\r\n* [[Bowser's Castle]]\r\n* [[Castle Grayskull]]\r\n* [[Cinderella Castle]]\r\n* [[Peach's Castle]]"
