        "magic_user": {
          "_Self (magic_user)": [
            {
              "tag": "magic_user",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 21569,
              "wiki_body": "A [b]magic user[/b] is any character who is capable of using [[magic]] in some form, usually a [[magician]] or some sort of spellcaster. For the latter, they tend to take the form of wizards, sorcerers, and mages.\r\n\r\nFor tagging purposes, magic users are generally defined as casting magic on screen, or matching up with the \"visual stereotype\" of a spellcaster.\r\n\r\n* [[dark_magic]] - Typically relates to darkness, death, diseases, and/or the [[demonic]].\r\n** [[necromancer]]\r\n** [[plague_doctor]]\r\n** [[witch]]\r\n* [[holy_spellcaster]] - Affiliated with \"divine\"/\"holy\"-type magic. Also known as a \"divine spellcaster.\"\r\n** [[cleric]]\r\n** [[paladin]]\r\n** [[priest]] \r\n* [[tribal_spellcaster]] - Affiliated with \"nature\"/\"plant\"-type magic. Also known as a \"druidic spellcaster.\"\r\n** [[druid]]  \r\n** [[shaman]]\r\n** [[witch_doctor]]\r\n\r\n* [[mage_(final_fantasy)]] - A mage who is associated with the [i][[Final Fantasy]][/i] franchise.\r\n** [[black_mage_(job)]]\r\n** [[blue_mage]]\r\n** [[illusionist_(final_fantasy)]]\r\n** [[red_mage]]\r\n** [[scholar_(final_fantasy)]]\r\n** [[summoner_(final_fantasy)]]\r\n** [[time_mage]]\r\n** [[white_mage]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[tag group:magic]]"
            }
          ],
          "tribal_spellcaster": [
            {
              "tag": "tribal_spellcaster",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 1835,
              "wiki_body": "A tribal spellcaster is a special breed of spellcaster who's spells are traditionally natural, or nature themed, as opposed to the arcane flavor of a [[spellcaster|wizard's]] spells.  Typically, a tribal spellcaster is more in tune with the earth and it's spirit, and the life of the creatures in it. \r\n\r\nThey are typically, but not always [[tribal]], despite the name.  Many times they wear [[loincloth]]s, [[beads]], and [[feathers]].  They may have small [[bone]]s or [[skull]]s , a [[staff]] or [[spear]], [[body paint]] or an animal companion of some sort.\r\n\r\nThey come in several different 'flavors':\r\n\r\n* [[druid|Druids]] typically are shapechangers, and the recent success of the [[warcraft]] franchise means that many of the images of druids are of warcraft druids--cats, bears, and others. \r\n* [[Shaman]] typically commune more with [[spirits]], and nature.  They often will wear tribal clothing, and may have small bones and bits of nature on their person.  \r\n* [[witch_doctor|Witch doctors]] have a darker feel to them, as they are most likely to have [[bone]]s and [[bodypaint]], to use [[blood]] as a material component to their spells.  They often use voodoo magic, and [[voodoo_dolls]].\r\n\r\nh4.  See Also:\r\n\r\n* [[druid]]\r\n* [[shaman]]\r\n* [[witch doctor]]\r\n\r\n-----This page is part of [[Tag Group:Magic]]-----"
            }
          ]
        },
        "bubble": {
          "_Self (bubble)": [
            {
              "tag": "bubble",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 18519,
              "wiki_body": "A [b]bubble[/b] is a globule of one substance in another, usually gas in a liquid. Due to the Marangoni effect, bubbles may remain intact when they reach the surface of the immersive substance.\r\n\r\nh5. Examples\r\n\r\n[section,expanded]\r\n[sup]Non-exhaustive list[/sup]\r\n\r\n* [[blowing_bubble_gum]] - filling [[bubble_gum]] with air from a character's mouth for personal amusement\r\n\r\nthumb #2412556\r\n\r\n* [[blowing_soap_bubbles]] - [[playful]] activity of blowing [[soap_bubbles]] from a [[bubble_wand]] or soap foam\r\n\r\nthumb #1669956\r\n\r\n* [[bubble_bath]] - a recreational or beauty product that covers the surface of bathwater with foamy bubbles, which can also [[convenient_censorship|preserve modesty]]\r\n\r\nthumb #2231783\r\n\r\n* carbonation of [[beverage|beverages]] like various [[soda|sodas]] and [[alcohol|alcoholic drinks]]\r\n\r\nthumb #2750090\r\n\r\n* [[cum_bubble]] - air trapped in cum, suggesting continued sexual contact after ejaculation or a forced exit from [[cum_inside|an orifice]]\r\n\r\nthumb #1838346\r\n\r\n* [[drunk_bubble]] - cartoony [[emanata]] indicating drunkeness\r\n\r\nthumb #3476862\r\n\r\n* [[foam]] - a usually whitish mass of many small bubbles, often soap bubbles, sometimes \"[[beer]] head\" or sea foam\r\n\r\nthumb #2904891\r\n\r\n* [[snot_bubble]] - bubble blown from the [[snot]] of a character's nose, perhaps as a comical [[sleeping]] effect or from a stuffy or [[runny_nose]]\r\n\r\nthumb #3435560\r\n\r\n* [[suds]] - a foamy mix of soap and water\r\n\r\nthumb #1364876\r\n\r\n* [[underwater]] gases expelled from creatures [[breathing]], man-made structures, and natural geological processes\r\n\r\nthumb #2875887\r\n[/section]"
