          {
            "tag": "magic_wand",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 1328,
            "wiki_body": "[i]Not to be confused with the [[hitachi_magic_wand]].[/i]\r\n\r\nA [b]magic wand[/b] is an implement associated with supernatural [[magic]] and [[magic_user|magic users]], such as wizards, witches, or sorcerers. Magic wands can also be seen in stereotypical depictions of stage [[magician|magicians]], invoking the same imagery of supernatural magic.\r\n\r\nIn modern media, magic wands are commonly (though not exclusively) depicted as long, narrow, rigid objects roughly the length of a human forearm.\r\n\r\nIf the implement is significantly longer (e.g. approaching human height), then the [[magic staff]] tag should be used instead.\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n* [[tag_group:magic]]"
