        {
          "tag": "dialogue_with_sound_effects",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1143,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3681279 thumb #2998837  thumb #3547061 thumb #2787961\r\n\r\nUse this tag when [[sound effects]] are incorporated as part of a [[dialogue]] segment. \r\n\r\nh4. General guidelines\r\n\r\n- Do not use for any image with just dialogue and sound effects. The themes need to be paired together. Check examples, and common usages.\r\n- Do not assume that all effects paired with dialogue are sound effects. Some are better described as a [[vocalization]].\r\n\r\nA good rule is to ask yourself if it is best described as a [[grunting|grunt]], or [[moan]], it probably isn't a sound effect.\r\n\r\nIf the concept doesn't fit under this tag, it might apply as [[interrupted by reaction]], which applies to both sound effects and vocalizations.\r\n\r\nh4. Sound effects that commonly apply\r\n\r\n* All forms of [[breathing noises]] (\"Gasp\", \"Huff\", \"Pant\", \"Sigh\", etc.)\r\n* [[Burping]]\r\n* [[Hiccuping]]\r\n\r\nh4. Methods\r\n\r\n- [[Interrupted speech]]\r\n- Preceding, or trailing dialogue (being in a speech bubble that is part of a dialogue chain qualifies)\r\n- Being near dialogue in a way that suggests it occurs during the dialogue, usually the sound effect is placed in an unnatural location."
