        {
          "tag": "slightly_chubby",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 165503,
          "wiki_body": "A little thick here and there. Maybe a small \"gut\" but the majority of the body structure is fairly similar to a non-chubby person.\n\n* Note that this is not to be used for [[overweight]] characters.\n** Please keep in mind that tag aliasing causes [[chubby]] to automatically be changed into slightly_chubby, not [[overweight]].\n\nThe full range of fatness can be approximated using the following tiered system. There will always be a few cases that are difficult to place in one category or the other but most should be close enough; just do your best to fit them into one or the other.\n\n[section=Scale of fatness]__________________________________________________\n\nh3. Fat distribution by gender\n\nA small consideration, but important nonetheless. \n\nThe fat distribution can vary in subtle ways between genders and body types. While occasionally this can aid in identifying the gender of an otherwise ambiguous character, for our purposes it mostly just affects minor differences that might push a character into a different category. \n\nWithout going into details, this picture should give a pretty rough idea: http://i.imgur.com/92NarxH.jpg\n__________________________________________________\n\nh3.Slightly chubby\n\nA little thick here and there. Maybe a small \"gut\" but the majority of the body structure is fairly similar to a non-chubby person. \n\nIn human terms I'd say most would fall under 100 kg (220 lbs) depending on height.\n\nthumb #273286 thumb #4923173 thumb #167506 thumb #3277457\n\n__________________________________________________\n\nh3.[[Overweight]]\n\nThis tag is really hard to define, but it shouldn't go past \"Santa fat\".  \n\n* Note that this doesn't count the butt, which can be huge (even in some skinny people) regardless of weight.\n\nThis tier is the hardest to judge in terms of weight because it is hugely dependent on height. 90-135 kg (200-300 lbs) would be a pretty broad estimate.\n\nthumb #4659996 thumb #3051762 thumb #117362 thumb #466511\n\n__________________________________________________\n\nh3.[[Obese]]\n\nSmall rolls in the places you would expect. Fat in torso still shouldn't go past the shoulders in most cases.\n\nIn human terms, most will fall within  125-175 kg (275-385 lbs). \n\nthumb #556914 thumb #564864 thumb #4754608 thumb #4519111\n__________________________________________________\n\nh3.[[Morbidly obese]]\n\n\"Jabba the Hut fat\", \"Hyper fat\". Has trouble walking, or can't walk.  Rolls in places you didn't even know existed.\n\nthumb #4264691 thumb #3914907 thumb #3174103\n\n__________________________________________________\n\nh3.[[Blobby]]\n\nAn obesity so unrealistically enormous that their ordinary part of body is very tiny in comparison, potentially submerged.\n\nthumb #4739588 thumb #498794 thumb #4939561 thumb #4928064\n\n__________________________________________________\n[/section]\n\n\nh4. Related Tags:\n* [[belly]]\n* [[potbelly]]\n* [[musclegut]]\n* [[thick_thighs]]\n* [[voluptuous]]\n* [[love_handles]]\nh6. Sex\n* [[slightly_chubby_male]]\n* [[slightly_chubby_female]]\n* [[slightly_chubby_intersex]]\n** [[slightly_chubby_gynomorph]]\n* [[slightly_chubby_ambiguous]]\nh6. Form\n* [[slightly_chubby_anthro]]\n* [[slightly_chubby_humanoid]]\n* [[slightly_chubby_feral]]\n* [[slightly_chubby_human]]\n* [[slightly_chubby_taur]]\n\nh4. See also:\n* [[tag_group:figures]]\n** [[overweight]]\n\nh4. Tagging Projects\n* Correctly label slightly chubby posts mistagged as [[overweight]] or other figures.\n* {{slightly_chubby -slightly_chubby_*}}: Tag forms and genders where possible.\n* {{slightly_chubby overweight solo}}: Characters can't be tagged with both [[slightly_chubby]] and [[overweight]] at once."
        },
