        {
          "tag": "pokemorph",
          "kor": "포케모프",
          "count": 75552,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #2049621 thumb #4209704 thumb #1583028 thumb #2499623 thumb #4462045 thumb #2105135\n\nA [b]Pokémorph[/b] is a [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]] with a body type that is depicted as more human-like than their canon form. In simple terms, it's an anthropomorphized/\"furry\" or humanoidized version of a Pokémon.\n\nh4. The difference between Pokémorph and anthro.\n[[Anthro]] is when a character has both animal features and a general shape resembling that of a human. Pokémorph is when a Pokémon is made more human-like than their canon form.\n\nthumb #5426600 thumb #4766822\n\nSome Pokémon are already [[anthro]] by canon standards; {{pokemon anthro -pokemorph|merely anthropomorphic and not a Pokémorph}}.\n\nthumb #2284674 thumb #5121313\n\nWhen they are made more human-like than before, they become a {{Pokémorph}}.\n\nh4. Related tags:\n* [[alternate_species]]\n** [[humanoidized]]\n*** [[pokémon_humanoid]]\n** [[taurification]]\n* [[anthrofied]]\n\nh4. See also\n* [[digimorph]]\n* [[humanoid]]\n** [[animal_humanoid]]\n* [[neomorph_(neopets)]]\n\n* topic #55877 - Discusses the differences between Pokémorph and anthro."
