          "tag": "status_effect",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 540,
          "wiki_body": "A [b]status effect[/b] is a symbolic representation of a physical, or mental condition affecting a character's status in a roleplaying or videogame setting. Status effects can be positive or negative, and are generally temporary. An item known to create a positive status effect when used is known as a [[power-up]], while an item known to cause a negative status effect may be known as a [[cursed object]].\r\n\r\nh4. Categories\r\n\r\n* [[negative_status_effect]]\r\n* [[positive_status_effect]]\r\n\r\nh4. Examples\r\n\r\n- Small status icons underneath a player [[health bar]].\r\n- Text that indicates an effect on another character used in place of a status icon. In Pokémon for example, the Frozen status effect will show as \"FRZ\".\r\n- Other visual or textual indications may apply.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[gameplay_mechanics]]"
        },
