        {
          "tag": "superpowers",
          "kor": "초능력",
          "count": 317,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1236954\r\n\r\nWhen a character demonstrates fantastical powers that are beyond natural capabilities, \"superhuman\" or \"supernatural\" abilities. \r\n\r\nThis tag should be used for otherwise normal [[anthro]], [[humanoid]] or [[human]] characters that display powers that aren't natural to them — a [[Charizard]], [[Godzilla]] or fire elemental creature breathing fire is not a superpower, while an otherwise normal anthro wolf breathing fire is displaying a superpower. This is even more appropriate when the character is in a modern or futuristic setting (powers are less likely to be \"magic\" than a [[fantasy]] setting), and intended to be a [[superhero]] or [[supervillain]]\r\n\r\nh5. Examples of Superpowers\r\n\r\n* [[flying]] (if the character has no wings) and/or [[levitation]]\r\n* [[telekinesis]]\r\n* [[super strength]] \r\n* super [[speed]]\r\n* [[bulletproof]] (a feature of general \"invulnerability\")\r\n* [[laser eyes]] (or \"eye beams\")\r\n* [[elastic body]]\r\n* [[elemental manipulation]]\r\n** [[earth manipulation]]\r\n** [[electricity manipulation]]\r\n** [[fire manipulation]]\r\n** [[plant manipulation]]\r\n** [[water manipulation]]\r\n\r\nh5. Tagging Notes\r\n* This tag should not be used for most [[magic user|magic users]]...\r\n** ...however a character that is visibly a superhero or supervillain who uses [[magic]], can fall under this tag when using their powers (e.g. [[Raven (DC)|Raven from Teen Titans]])\r\n* This tag should not be applied to characters who have abilities inherent to their fictional species\r\n\r\n"
