        {
          "tag": "vaporwave",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 278,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1273005 thumb #1116123 thumb #1833459 thumb #1885187\r\n\r\n[b]Vaporwave[/b] is a visual aesthetic tied to a music genre of the same name. Vaporwave is strongly associated with 1990s pop culture, cyberpunk, and retro-futurism. Vaporwave will often feature imagery of 1990s web design and technology, as well as products and fashions of the 90s. Pastel colours, and to a lesser extent, neon colours, are characteristic of Vaporwave aesthetics.  While Vaporwave revolves around 90s nostalgia, it often uses humour, irony, and surrealism in its appreciation of the decade.\r\n\r\n[b]Not to be confused with: [[Synthwave]][/b]\r\n\r\nh4. Vaporwave Elements\r\n* Vaporwave will almost always feature bright pastel colour palettes, particularly pink, blue and yellow. Checkerboard patterns, \"[[glitch|Glitch]]\" distortions, grainy overlays, and [[Chromatic aberration]] are commonly used in Vaporwave aesthetics.\r\n\r\n* Common visuals in Vaporwave include:\r\n** Windows 95 logo, Windows 95 interface\r\n** 90s era Web Design\r\n** 1990s technology, ie computers, Game Boys, Playstations etc\r\n** (Gratuitous) [[Japanese text]]\r\n** VHS overlays, scanlines, static distortion\r\n** [[3d_(artwork)|3d art]], [[pixel_(artwork)|Pixel art]], and [[animated]] art\r\n** 1980s and 1990s [[anime]] characters\r\n** Classical Roman statues and pillars \r\n** Palm trees and fake plants\r\n** Beaches, tropical locations\r\n** Products such as Fiji water and Arizona Iced Tea\r\n\r\n* Vaporwave images are often collages consisting of the above items\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n\r\n* [[1990s]]\r\n* [[Synthwave]]\r\n* [[Cyberpunk]]"
        },
