          "count": 236,
          "wiki_body": "Use for [[sound effects]] associated with gripping, grabbing, or holding. These will commonly be in [[contact_onomatopoeia|onomatopoeia]] form, but sometimes they may not be.\r\n\r\nh4. Sound effects\r\n\r\nGripping terms that qualify as onomatopoeia should be tagged as [[contact_onomatopoeia]] specifically.\r\n\r\n* \"Clutch\"\r\n* \"Grab\", \"Grb\"\r\n* \"Grasp\"\r\n* \"Grip\", \"Grp\"\r\n* \"Grope\"\r\n* \"Hold\"\r\n\r\nh5. Grey area\r\n\r\nTerms that are associated with compression (such as [[squeeze_(sound_effect)|\"Squeeze\"]]) are currently not included in this tag. \"Squeeze\" is sometimes used in the same context as other gripping terms. It still needs to be determined if all usages of the term, or just the gripping ones could fall under this tag's definition.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:sound_effects]]\r\n\r\n* [[sound_effects]]\r\n** [[compression_sound_effect]] - \"Coil\", \"Crush\", \"Squeeze\", etc.\r\n** [b]gripping_sound_effect[/b]\r\n** [[rubbing_sound_effect]]"
