              "wiki_body": "thumb #693415 thumb #679884 thumb #664907\n\nThis tag is used when a character is shown to be laughing, either by vocalized [[text]] ([i]Hahaha[/i], etc) or through use of expressions and gestures.\n\nh4. Categories\n\n* [[audible_laugh]]\n* [[laugh_vocalization]]\n\nh5. Forms of laughter\n\n* [[giggling]] - Higher pitched noises, tends to represented by \"He\", rather than \"Ha\", but could also be tagged based on stereotypes.\n* [[snickering]] - Laughter that tends to last a few seconds, and commonly as a form of ridicule. A character may try to hide the fact that they are snickering.\n\n[section=Laughter examples]\n\nCommonly take the form of a two letter vocalization: \"Ha ha\", \"He he\", \"Hi hi\" , \"Oh ho ho\", \"Tee hee hee\", but can take many other forms. Some languages have their own ways of depicting laughter.\n\nh4. Sound effects\n\n* \"Cackle\"\n* \"Giggle\"\n* \"Laugh\"\n* \"Snerk\"\n* \"Snicker\"\n* \"Wheeze\" - Conditionally\n\nh4. Japanese\n\nIf `ハハ` is present in an image, it is most likely a laughing form of some sort. It is also common to use the letter `w` to indicate laughter. It is the Japanese representation of \"LOL\" (Laughing Out Loud).\n\n* \"[[Fufufu]]\" or \"Fu fu\"\n* \"アハハ\"\n* \"あはは\"\n\nh4. Korean\n\nh4. Russian\n\n* \"Xa xa\"\n\nh4. Spanish\n\n* \"Je je\"\n\n[/section] \n\nh4. Related themes\n\n* [[embarrassed]]\n* [[humiliation]]\n* [[tickling]]\n\nh4. Related tags\n\n* [[emanata]]\n** [[bar_emanata]]\n** [[crossbar_emanata]] - The most common [[emanata]] associated with laughter.\n* [[open_mouth]]\n** [[open_smile]]\n\nSpeech interruption themes\n\n* [[interrupted_speech]]\n** [[interrupted_by_reaction]]\n* [[stuttering]]\n** [[intense_stutter]]\n\nTickling subset\n\n* [[asking_to_stop]]\n* [[begging]]\n* [[command]]"
            }
