            "count": 41152,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #2084442 thumb #2023017 thumb #2666876 thumb #1535551 thumb #2546566 thumb #2535044 thumb #3241866\n\nh1.😢\n[b]Crying[/b] [i](also called sobbing, wailing, weeping, whimpering, bawling, blubbering and QQ-ing)[/i] is shedding [[tears]] as a response to an emotional state in [[human|humans]].\nThe act of [b]crying[/b] has been defined as:\n\n\"A complex secretomotor phenomenon characterized by the shedding of tears from the lacrimal apparatus, without any irritation of the ocular structures\".\nThe medical term for this is \"to [b]lacrimate[/b]\" which also refers to non-emotional shedding of tears.\n\nh4.Emotions\n[[Sad|Sadness]] and [[depression]] are the most common [[tag_group:facial_expressions#emotions|emotions]] leading to this action, but [b]crying[/b] can occur in some other emotions. Such as: [[happy|overwhelming joy]], [[</3|heartbreak]], [[angry|anger]], being [[scared]]/frightened, [[fear]]/[[anxiety]], [[guilty|guilt]]/remorse, despair\nOr other equivalent emotions.\n\nh4. Non-emotion\n[b]Crying[/b] may also sometimes happen when anyone is cutting up [[onion|onions]].\n\nh3. Related tags\n* [[emotional]]\n* [[sad]]\n* [[shaking]]\n* [[tears]]\n* [[wavy mouth]]\n* [[worried]]\n\nh3. See also\n* [[comforting]]\n* [[frown]]\n* [[tears of joy]]"
