            "kor": "",
            "count": 6789,
            "wiki_body": "[b]X-ray view[/b] is a type of visual effect where a portion of an image that should be opaque is made transparent to show elements of the scene that would be otherwise hidden.\n\n[section,expanded=Categories]\n\nMost examples will feature an [[internal]], [[cutaway]], or both.\n\nh4. [[Internal]]\n\nh5. [[Penetration]]\n\nthumb #3222361 thumb #3854528 thumb #3295262 thumb #3695014\n\nh5. [[Vore]] \n\nthumb #3865536 thumb #2309657\n\nh4. Other surfaces\n\nthumb #1936394 thumb #3550859 thumb #2865678\n\n[/section]\n\nh4. Similar themes\n\nThe inclusion of a [[cutaway]] frame allows for these similar concepts to be possible. It is possible that these could be considered a specific type of x-ray view. Ideally there should be a way to distinguish the two concepts if they were to be included under the same tag. The [[translucent body]] tag can be used for this purpose, but it would be beneficial to phase out usage of the `translucent body` tag for the purpose of x-ray views in favor of natural translucency.\n\nthumb #3860781 thumb #3819067 thumb #3240316 thumb #2561686\n\nh4. Related themes\n\n* [[hidden_sex_toy]]\n** [[hidden_vibrator]]\n* [[internal]]\n* [[penetration]]\n* [[stealth_masturbation]]\n* [[stealth_sex]]\n* [[under_table]]\n* [[x-ray_vision]] - The effect is made to appear like it is a power bestowed to the viewer by a special device, or power.\n* [[vore]]\n\nh4. Not to be confused with\n* [[radiograph]] - An image of the internal structure of an object or living creature produced using X-ray radiation. Commonly referred to as \"an x-ray\".\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[translucent]]\n** [[translucent_body]]\n* [[x-ray_flash]]"
