            "tag": "step_pose",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 2447,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #819101 thumb #792647 thumb #705345\r\n\r\nA generally upright [[standing]] pose where one [[feet|foot]] is slightly elevated above the other, typically with the foot resting on something or while [[climbing]] or stepping up onto something.\r\n\r\nA well-known specific variant of this pose is known as the \"Captain Morgan pose\":https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CaptainMorganPose, after the brand of rum whose mascot is known to do this.\r\n\r\nThis pose may apply to characters being [[stepped on]], but not if the post qualifies as a [[stomping]] theme, and probably not for sex based postures. This tag should be used only if the posture stays within the guidelines for the pose itself. Use the thumbnails as a reference.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[step_position]] - A sex position involving a partner being [[stepped on]].\r\n* [[stomping]] - An activity involving firmly stamping one's foot into the ground. Do not tag this as step pose, but [[raised_foot]], or [[stepped_on]] instead.\r\n* [[strutting]] - A showy kind of walking posture commonly featuring [[aligned feet]].\r\n\r\nh5. Stepping postures\r\n\r\n* [[walking]] / [[jogging]] / [[running]] - Step pose shouldn't suggest movement\r\n\r\nThese are postures related to stepping that sometimes get confused for the pose. Please add them if they apply.\r\n\r\n* [[on_heel]] / [[on_heels]] - Resting on the back on the foot / feet (singular / plural)\r\n* [[raised_foot]]\r\n* [[raised_heel]] - The opposite of `on_heel` and `on_heels`\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[bent_leg]] - Commonly paired with `straight_leg` \r\n* [[on_one_leg]] - As long as the character isn't on both of their feet, this tag will apply.\r\n* [[raised_foot]] - This tag applies when a stepping, step pose, or related posture has the raised foot not making contact with the ground. This tag should be used instead of [[raised leg]] in many cases.\r\n* [[straight_leg]] - Commonly paired with `bent_leg`\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:pose]]\r\n\r\n* [[climbing_on]]\r\n* [[lunging]]\r\n* [[on_one_knee]]\r\n* [[planted_leg]]"
