            "tag": "looking_well-fed",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 143,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #4841533\r\nCartoonish (behavior and exaggeration usually seen in fiction rather than real life) expressions and body language that convey enjoyment of being satiated after eating. Such behavior for example can be a character with a [[open_mouth]] and [[tongue_out]], with a delighted look on their face. Or, maybe they are [[happy]] with [[half-closed_eyes]] and [[hand_on_belly]], maybe rubbing or even slapping it.\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Tag Guidance]\r\n\r\nh4. Nuances and Distinctions\r\n[s][/s]\r\n* A post with a character looking happy with [[big_belly]], [[hand_on_belly]], etc. isn't enough for the tag to apply. There should be evidence that the expression was from the consumption of something.\r\n** For example, the tells can be:\r\n*** Visuals that the food items have been eaten like leftovers on a plate or bitten into food.\r\n*** [[motion_lines]] on the abdomen from digestive activity.\r\n*** digestive [[onomatopoeia]].\r\n*** And graphics such as [[iconography]] of a digested character in [[vore]].\r\n\r\n* There are things a character may do after eating where this tag can apply, but not always. If a character does not show positive emotion then the tag doesn't apply.\r\n** These things could be:\r\n*** [[picking_teeth]]\r\n*** [[burping]]\r\n\r\n* A character looking [[happy]] after eating something is not enough for the tag to apply. They have to have some exaggeration of character. Whether it be something like [[licking_lips]], [[hand_on_belly]], or [[burping]].\r\n\r\n* [[looking_pleasured]] should be used instead when the expression stems from sexual stimulation, like when a character fully inserts another character into themselves in [[cock_vore]] or [[unbirthing]].\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nThis tag has nothing to do with a person appearing well nourished, unlike the actual definition for well-fed. I just couldn't find a better name for this tag."
