            "count": 2814122,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #768299 thumb #258126 thumb #1774850 thumb #647901 thumb #1872787\n\nIf a character only has apparent [b]female[/b] genitalia or otherwise exclusively female physical traits that are in some way visible, or traits befitting of its species (ex. breasts/teats, pseudo-penis, eyelashes...), then it is to be tagged female.\n\nFollowing the '[[tag what you see]]' rule, this includes images of characters known to be [[intersex]] of the [[herm]] or [[gynomorph]] variety, but whose [[penis]] and [[balls]] (if applicable) are not evident in the specific picture.\n\n* Please note that the gender of a fictional character/ species cannot be tagged based on its own proprietary gender-specific features. (further reading: forum #239784)\n\n* Additionally, while most non-feral characters may have breasts in some form, the absence of such alone does not disqualify them from being tagged as female.\n\n\nh4. Related tags:\n\n* [b]Gender[/b]\n** [[ambiguous_gender]]\n** [[male]]\n** female\n** [[intersex]]\n*** [[andromorph]] - Male based body with a vulva, but no penis.\n*** [[gynomorph]] - Female based body with a penis, but no vulva.\n*** [[herm]] - Female based body, with a vulva and a penis.\n*** [[maleherm]] - Male based body, with a vulva and a penis.\n\n* [b]Appearance[/b]\n** [[tomboy]]\n\n* [b][[Symbol]][/b]\n** [[♀]]\n\n\nh4. See also:\n\n* [[howto:tag genders]] - Recommended\n\n* [[gender_transformation]]\n* [[crossgender]] - For characters normally male or female being depicted as their opposite gender or intersex.\n\n* [b][[tag group:index|Tag Group]][/b]\n** [[tag group:genders]]\n\nh4. Tagging Projects\n* {{female -female_*}}: Tag the form of the female character."
