          "count": 5267,
          "wiki_body": "Refers to anything that originates in [[Japan]], or general \"Japanese\" aesthetics or visuals. Note that this does not automatically include all art drawn in Japan. The post content must include something like Japanese food, clothing, locations, culture, etc. \r\n\r\n[b]For a post that depicts a scene set [i]in Japan[/i], depicts the country on a map or from an aerial view, or shows the Japanese flag — use [[Japan]][/b]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Japanese Meta Tags]\r\n[b]Tags describing \"something Japanese\" about posts on this site[/b]\r\n\r\n** [[japanese audio]] - spoken Japanese audio\r\n** [[japanese text]] - written Japanese text \r\n*** [[japanese tally marks]] \r\n** [[japanese description]] - a post description written in Japanese\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh3. Japanese Tags\r\n[sup]note: tags marked with (*) do not yet have wiki pages[/sup]\r\n\r\n[section=General Tags]\r\n\r\n* [[japanese architecture]] (*)\r\n* [[japanese armor]] (*)\r\n* [[japanese clothing]] (see tag for clothing items)\r\n** [[japanese school uniform]]\r\n* [[japanese mythology]]\r\n* [[japanese flag]] (*)\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Japanese Food]\r\n\r\n* [[bento box]]\r\n* [[dango (food)|dango]] \r\n* [[kakigori]]\r\n* [[mochi (food)|mochi]] (*)\r\n* [[onigiri]] \r\n* [[pocky]]\r\n* [[ramune]]\r\n* [[takoyaki]]\r\n* [[yakitori]]\r\n\r\nh6. [i]Japanese [[noodles|Noodle]] Dishes[/i]\r\n\r\n** [[ramen]]\r\n** [[soba (food)|soba]]\r\n** [[yakisoba]]\r\n\r\n\r\nh6. [i][[Sushi]][/i]\r\n\r\n** [[ehomaki]]\r\n** [[inarizushi]]\r\n** [[makizushi]]\r\n** [[nigirizushi]]\r\n** [[uramaki]]\r\n\r\n[/section] \r\n[section=Japanese Animals]\r\n\r\n* [[japanese_badger]]\r\n* [[japanese_kobold]]\r\n* [[japanese_marten]]\r\n* [[japanese_macaque]]\r\n* [[japanese_river_otter]]\r\n* [[japanese_weasel]]\r\n\r\nh6. [i]Japanese Dog Breeds[/i]\r\n\r\n* [[akita]]\r\n* [[hokkaido]]\r\n* [[japanese_chin]]\r\n* [[japanese_spitz]]\r\n* [[japanese_terrier]]\r\n* [[kai_ken]]\r\n* [[kishu]]\r\n* [[sakhalin_husky]]\r\n* [[shiba_inu]]\r\n* [[shikoku]]\r\n* [[tosa]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh5. Miscellaneous Japanese \r\nThese are tags with names or concepts that come from Japan, and may be associated with Japanese culture, pop culture and/or history. The `japanese` tag does NOT need to be added to posts with these tags.\r\n\r\nh6. Art \r\n* [[chibi]]\r\n* [[kemono]]\r\n* [[oekaki]]\r\n* [[ukiyo-e]]\r\n* [[manga]]\r\n* [[doujinshi]]\r\n\r\nh6. Culture and Concepts\r\n\r\n* [[barazoku]] \r\n* [[kaiju]] — monsters, usually [i][b]dai[/b]kaiju[/i], giant monsters\r\n* [[maneki-neko]] (*)\r\n** [[koban (coin)]] (*)\r\n\r\nh6. Fashion Styles/Subcultures\r\n* [[ganguro_(fashion)|ganguro]] \r\n* [[gyaru]]\r\n* [[sukeban]]\r\n* [[otaku]]\r\n\r\nh6. Religion\r\n* [[shinto]] \r\n** [[gohei]]\r\n** [[shide]]\r\n** [[shrine maiden]] (*)\r\n** [[torii]]\r\n\r\n* [[bullet train]]  (*) — AKA [i]Shinkansen[/i] \r\n* [[dojo]] \r\n* [[katana]]\r\n* [[karate]] (*)\r\n* [[kigurumi]] \r\n* [[ninja]] \r\n* [[samurai]] \r\n\r\nh6. Not Inherently Japanese, but frequently seen in Japanese Scenes\r\n* [[cherry blossom tree]]\r\n* [[chopsticks]]\r\n* [[hot spring]] \r\n* [[paper lantern]] — sometimes called \"Japanese lanterns\"\r\n"
