          "tag": "repeated_text",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1879,
          "wiki_body": "The deliberate repetition of a word, or phrase, usually in a way that highlights an aspect of context, such as an expression of thoughts and emotions.\r\n\r\nh4. General guidelines\r\n\r\n* Content appears three or more times. Phrases only need to appear twice. Slight variations are okay. This tag should be used sparingly if the content only repeats once.\r\n* Use for terms that are clearly paired together, and belong to the same context.\r\n* Avoid use for [[stuttering]] unless the entire word is duplicated the required number of times. Do not use for single letter words (\"I\").\r\n\r\nh6. Handling short forms\r\n\r\n\"Ha ha\" is not a valid usage of `repeated_text` as the content repeats only once. \"Ha ha ha!\" on the other hand satisfies the three form guideline, and can be tagged accordingly.\r\n\r\nh4. Common usages\r\n\r\n* Phrases are repeated for emphasis. This theme can appear in both dialogue and inner monologue.\r\n* Phrases may repeat on a [[chalkboard]] as a form of [[punishment]].\r\n* Text may repeat in a [[text background]].\r\n* Text may repeat on the stretchy liner of some [[bottomwear]], and [[underwater]].\r\n\r\nh6. Sound effects\r\n\r\nThis tag can be used for [[sound effects]]. Sound effects are used multiple times to indicate that an action is happening multiple times often consecutively. Sound effects should be limited to three or more repetitions.\r\n\r\nh4. Categories\r\n\r\n* [[repeated_dialogue]]\r\n* [[repeated_internal_monologue]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[i_mean_breast_milk]] - Although the theme appears less than one might think. Try using this tag to see how many actually contain repeating text."
