          "kor": "",
          "count": 261,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Stylized text[/b] should be used whenever there is [[text]] that is visibly different from standard fonts, and character symbol orientations. Stylized text may be skewed, or modified in such a way that it no longer conforms with standard text alignment, may feature alternating text positions or fonts, or have inconsistent or changing font, or the text itself may have some texturing along the surface that makes it different than typical flat-colored text.\r\n\r\nStylized text is most commonly used for [[sound effects]], but [[title|titles]], and artist watermarks may also feature stylized text. Most examples of traditional [[signature|signatures]], and [[cursive]] writing in general should not use this tag.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[text]]\r\n** [[curved_text]]\r\n** [[extruded_text]]\r\n** [[perspective_text]]\r\n** [[textured_font]]\r\n** [[unusual_font]]"
