          "count": 8226,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #4787033 thumb #194731 thumb #2401534 thumb #2730967\n\nAn instance wherein two or more versions of the same character meet each other, or are at least in the same vicinity of one another.\n\n[sup][b]Note:[/b] Don't ask about the name, nobody remembers the origin for certain. Some believe it to have come from [[Square Enix]] and some [[Disney]] characters meeting older versions of themselves in [i][[Kingdom Hearts]][/i], but this does not happen in the series more than a handful of times. It may also come from squaring in mathematics, where a number is multiplied by itself. But any given origin theory is largely speculation, and this is merely the term that stuck.[/sup]\n\nh4. Related tags:\n* [[altered_reflection]]\n* [[alternate_color]]\n* [[alternate_costume]]\n* [[alternate_form]]\n* [[alternate_hairstyle]]\n* [[alternate_species]]\n* [[body_swap]]\n* [[clone]]\n* [[crossgender]]\n* [[dual_persona]]\n* [[past_meets_present]]\n\nh4. See also\n* [[celebrity_paradox]]\n* [[selfcest]]"
