          "kor": "골반",
          "count": 3061,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1016515 thumb #585983 thumb #838391\r\n\r\n[i]Ossicones[/i] are horn-, or antler-, -like protuberances on the heads of [[giraffid|giraffids]], and the climacoceratids. Ossicones are similar in appearance and use to the [[horn|horns]] of [[antelope]] and [[cattle]]. However, unlike their horns, ossicone derived from ossified (\"turned into bone/bony tissue or calcified\") cartilage rather than [[bone]]. They also often remain covered in skin and [[fur]], rather than horny keratin.\r\n\r\nh4. Related\r\n\r\n* [[giraffid]]\r\n* [[horn]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag group:feral anatomy]]\r\n* [[antlers]]"
