        {
          "tag": "iconography",
          "kor": "도상학",
          "count": 1775,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Iconography[/b] in this context, refers to [[symbol|symbols]] drawn to express things that cannot be easily shown in a static visual medium, or, more often, to reinforce something that is also being conveyed by a character's pose or expression.\n\nIconography may be used to represent movement, a character's physical status, or as abstract representations of emotions. As a tag, this primary focuses on abstract emotions, and concepts that do not easily fall into other categories like [[pictographics]], [[motion lines]], or [[emanata]].\n\nSome iconography is used interchangeably with [[onomatopoeia]], or is often depicted alongside related onomatopoeia, such as the iconographic [[snot bubble]] and onomatopoetic [[zzz]], both for sleeping.\n\nh4. Iconographic Tags\n\n[i]These are often depicted on or around a character's head or face[/i]\n\n* [[cross-popping_vein]] – anger\n* [[frustration_cloud]] – frustration\n* [[giving_up_the_ghost]] – trauma, exhaustion\n* [[gloom_lines]] – anxiety, depression\n* [[idea]] – getting an idea (lightbulb lighting up) \n* [[seeing_stars]] – disorientation\n* [[snot_bubble]] – sleeping\n* [[skull_symbol]] - death, anger, malicious intent \n* [[skull_and_crossbones]] - similar to the above\n* [[squean]] – swirls, popping bubbles, squiggles - indicates dizziness, intoxication, sickness, among other ideas\n* [[steaming_mad]] – anger\n* [[sweatdrop_(iconography)]] – nervousness, embarrassment, confusion\n** [[flying_sweatdrops]] – nervousness or physical effort, sometimes known as \"plewds\"\n* [[x_eyes]] – indicates a character being dead, unconscious, dizzy or intoxicated\n* [[spiral_eyes]] – indicates a character hypnotized, unconscious, dizzy or intoxicated\n** [[spiral_pupils]]\n\nh4. Iconographs that should not use this tag\n\n* [[breath_cloud]] - sighing, relief, snorting through nose\n* [[dripping_lines]] - vertical lines used to convey negative emotion\n* [[emanata]] – radiation of emotion such as surprise or anger\n* [[grawlixes]] - a string of symbols representing swearing or anger ([i]$#@*!![/i])\n* [[motion_lines]] – motion\n* [[musical_note]] - whistling, singing, music, happiness\n* [[speed_lines]] – motion\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[tag_group:narrative_elements]]\n\n* [[pictographics]]\n* [[symbol]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "emoticon",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1623,
          "wiki_body": "An [b]emoticon[/b] is a depiction of an object, shape, or expression formed by using various text symbols and characters.\r\n\r\nJapanese emoticons, known as [[kaomoji]], incorporate unicode in order to capture more complex expressions or even full actions. This tag should be used when there is more than just the eyes or mouth present, or there appears to be unicode as part of the emoticon.\r\n\r\nh4. Types\r\n\r\n* [[blush_emoticon]] - Any emoticon featuring [[blush lines]] (slash marks).\r\n* [[heart_emoticon]] - A heart portrayed as `<3`\r\n* [[wink_emoticon]] - Any emoticon that implies winking. These will typically feature a semi-colon (;).\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[chat]]\r\n* [[chat_box]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:facial_expressions]]\r\n\r\n* [[emoji]] - A symbolic representation of an object, shape, or expression rendered in the form of an icon."
        },
