        {
          "tag": "skull_symbol",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 920,
          "wiki_body": "A symbolic representation of a [[skull]], usually heavily stylized or simplified. \r\n\r\nA skull symbol may be a design on clothing items, painted or printed onto a surface, painted or tattooed onto a character's body, or used in an abstract background. A skull symbol also can appear as [[iconography]]. When seen on clothing, the [[skull_print]], or [[skull_accessory]] tag may apply. \r\n\r\n[quote]\r\n\r\nh5. Important Note:\r\n\r\nThis tag should [b]not be confused with[/b] a physical [[skull]], a naturally occurring [[skull (marking)|skull shaped marking]] on a character's skin, fur or scales, or with a [[skull and crossbones]] symbol.\r\n\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\nh6. Skull Symbol As Iconography\r\n\r\n[i]A skull symbol may represent:[/i]\r\n* a character dying (or merely feeling like they're dead), similar to [[x eyes]] \r\n* a character being [i]very angry[/i] \r\n* a character having mischievous, violent or evil intent\r\n* poison or a deadly hazard, especially on labels and signage \r\n** if joined by crossed bones, it should instead be tagged as [[skull and crossbones]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[skull_and_crossbones]]\r\n* [[skull_print]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[skull]]\r\n* [[skull_accessory]]\r\n* [[skull_head]]\r\n* [[skull_mask]]\r\n"
        },
