          "tag": "queen_of_spades_symbol",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 314,
          "wiki_body": "Typically a symbol featuring a black [[spade (suit)|spade]] suit symbol with a Q, but can also be the chain of letters QoS. This symbol indicates a (racial) sexual preference for Black [[male|men]] or [[dark_skin|dark-skinned]] [[human|humans]]. Usually, it signifies the \"[[blacked_(kink)|blacked]]\" kink in human or [[human_on_anthro|human on anthro]] relationships. The Queen of Spades symbol is a known [[raceplay]] marking.\n\nAlternatively, \"QoS\" spade symbol using a \"Z\" instead of \"Q\" which can stand for sexual preference for [[zebra|zebras]] substituting dark skin humans. This was evident in [[My_Little_Pony|My Little Pony]] art which is \"[[striped_(kink)|striped]]\" instead but has expanded beyond that. For now, if a post contains raceplay tattoo(s) or symbol(s) with a spade shape marked for zebras, dark-skinned humans, or other species, tag it as queen_of_spades_symbol.\n\nA plain spade symbol without a \"Q\" or \"Z\" can be consider as a \"queen of spades\" if the person's partner is either dark skin, zebra, other species or themselves have an implied racial preference. There exists different symbols or brandings that are considered \"Queen of Spades\" raceplay theme so tagging may be varied.\n\nNot to be confused with the [[playing card]] [[Queen of Spades]].\n\nOpposite of [[Queen of Hearts Symbol]]."
