        {
          "tag": "warning_sign",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 543,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3019852 thumb #3084851 thumb #3097141 thumb #3312559\r\n\r\nA [b]warning sign[/b] is a [[sign]] containing precautionary information or symbolism on it. Any sign containing a signal word such as [i]warning[/i], [i]caution[/i], [i]danger[/i], or contains the general [[warning symbol]], or any of the various [[hazard symbol|hazard symbols]] will always qualify as a warning sign. Many warning signs are yellow, including American-based [[traffic sign|traffic signs]]. If a traffic sign happens to be yellow, it can be tagged as a warning sign.\r\n\r\nh4. Usage tips\r\n\r\n- Try not to confuse [[warning_label|labels]] with signs. Labels are placed on other objects, while signs are their own complete object.\r\n- A warning sign does not need to contain any symbols, and can be entirely text.\r\n- Warning signs may contain the general [[warning symbol]], or a [[hazard symbol]]. The general warning symbol does not count as a [[sign graphic]], but many hazard symbols will. Most traffic warning signs will contain a graphic.\r\n\r\nh4. Related signs\r\n\r\n* [[beware_of_dog]]\r\n* [[do_not_enter_sign]]\r\n* [[prohibition_sign]]\r\n* [[traffic_sign]]\r\n* [[wet_floor_sign]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[no_symbol]]\r\n* [[sign_graphic]]\r\n* [[text]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[sign]]\r\n* [[warning]]\r\n** [[warning_label]]\r\n** [[warning_message]]\r\n** [b]warning_sign[/b]\r\n** [[warning_symbol]]"
        },
