          "tag": "teapot_(body_type)",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 4369,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3128874 thumb #1599491 thumb #2762375 thumb #2648880 thumb #3052929 \n\n[b]Teapot[/b] describes [b]short, squat, male-bodied characters with generally bottom-heavy and/or curvy figures[/b]. \"Teapots\" are essentially the male equivalent of the more common female [i][b][[short stack]][/b][/i]. The term comes from the comparison of the character's figure (squat and curvy) to the shape of a traditional [[teapot]], with the character's penis representing the \"spout\". \n\n\n[quote]\nh3. Tagging Notes\n\nh5. Teapot Attributes \n\n* [b]Must be/have:[/b]\n** Short in height, or appears short proportionally - larger head, short limbs etc.\n** Some degree of a curvy figure - including [[wide hips]], [[thick thighs]], [[big butt]] (or larger)\n\n* [b]Optional:[/b]\n** [[slightly chubby]] or [[overweight]]\n** [[small but hung]] - may have a proportionally large genitals, or disproportionate huge/hyper penis and balls \n*** teapot characters, even when fully clothed, usually have a bulge, hinting at the size of their \"spout\"\n\nh5. What is [i][color=red]NOT[/color][/i] a Teapot\n\n* [[short]] [[femboy]] male characters that do not have squat proportions [b]are not teapots[/b]\n* short male characters with an overtly masculine (muscular, broad shoulders) figure, these should be tagged as [[short]] or [[dwarfism]], and/or [[stocky]].\n* male characters that have curvy figures (big butt, thick thighs, wide hips etc.) but are of normal height/proportions\n\nh5. Other Notes\n\n* Avoid tagging [[femboy]] male characters bending over, with their butt in perspective as teapot, unless their proportions visibly justify it\n* Female-bodied [[intersex]] characters should be tagged as [[short stack]]\n* Not all [[small but hung]] characters are teapots\n\n[/quote]\n\n\nh4. Related tags\n\n* [[short male]]\n* [[girly]] \n* [[small but hung]] \n* [[short]]\n* [[curvy figure]]\n* [[dwarfism]]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[tag group:figures]]\n* [[pear-shaped figure