                "wiki_body": "thumb #2290517 thumb #4587023 thumb #3491858 thumb #4545056\n\nWhen a character's [[balls]] are drawn with a [i]dramatic or notable[/i] amount of difference in sag (when hanging neutrally), or notable difference in size between the two balls. \n\nWhile exaggerated in artwork, the scrotum is asymmetric in reality, causing one testicle to hang lower than the other. It is not fully confirmed why, but most believe that this helps with temperature regulation and/or help prevent injuries in an impact. \n\nSize asymmetry without health complications also exists, as genetics can cause one testicle to potentially develop faster and/or sooner than the other during puberty (the shape of the testicles would still be the same, and the size difference should only be noticeable when the scrotum is in its relaxed/sagging state. Ask your doctor for an examination if you're concerned or unsure).   \n\nh4. Ball appearance:\n\n* [[ball_tuft]], [[hairy_balls]]\n* [[glowing_balls]], [[translucent_balls]]\n* [[lemon_testicles]], [[balls_above_penis]]\n* [[sweaty_balls]]\n* [[saggy_balls]], [[tight_balls]]\n* uneven_balls\n* [[uniball]], [[multi_balls]]\n* [[veiny_balls]]\n\nh4. See also:\n\n* [[balls]]\n* [[tag group:anatomy]]"
