                "count": 420,
                "wiki_body": "thumb #138533\r\n\r\n[color=tomato][b]Explicit Tag[/b][/color]\r\n[sup]See \"Help: Ratings\":https://e621.net/help/ratings for more info.[/sup]\r\n\r\nCharacters whose balls are distinctly ovular in shape with the bottom portion each coming to a clear point. Points of both halves often may be touching.\r\nCommon species among this tag include [[cervine|cervines]] and [[caprine|caprines]] among other species.\r\n\r\nThis is noted by a distinct lemonlike shape with a clear Nub on the bottom easily visible. This is not to be confused with [[scrotum_flap]]  wherein the scrotal skin is simply longer than usual and collects as a flap at the bottom of the sac.\r\n\r\nNotably, as the tag name suggests this feature is confined to the testicles and is [i]Not[/i] a feature of the scrotum itself. In certain species (such as sheep or goats) repeat selective breeding and human intervention has pulled the scrotum hemispheres closer and forced both testicles to be closer to the middle, creating a heart shaped scrotum considered a desirable trait for farming competitions, however goats and sheep can still retain the more common, split scrotum appearance equally as often. Be aware that this can result in the need for both the [[scrotum_flap]] [b]and[/b] [[lemon_testicles]] tags. But when tagging be sure to check whether the area is being pushed out by the balls being there for [[lemon_testicles]], or whether the area is empty skin for [[scrotum_flap]].\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Ball appearance:\r\n\r\n* [[ball_tuft]], [[hairy_balls]]\r\n* [[glowing_balls]], [[translucent_balls]]\r\n* lemon_testicles, [[balls_above_penis]]\r\n* [[sweaty_balls]]\r\n* [[saggy_balls]], [[tight_balls]]\r\n* [[uneven_balls]]\r\n* [[uniball]], [[multi_balls]]\r\n* [[veiny_balls]]\r\n* [[scrotum_flap]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[balls]]\r\n* [[tag group:anatomy]]\r\n** [[tag_group:feral_anatomy]]\r\n* [[anatomically_correct_genitalia]]\r\n\r\nH4. More info:\r\n\r\n* \"scrotum @ Wikipe