              "wiki_body": "thumb #5615573 thumb #1660088 thumb #2080111\n\nThe [b]Butt[/b] is a pair of rounded masses on the posterior of the pelvis - buttocks - which are made up of skin, fat, and the gluteal muscles (hence the term \"glutes\"). The buttocks [b]ass[/b]ist with balance, with walking/running, as well as acting as a cushion and allowing for upright posture when sitting. The butt is particularly prominent on humans - and thus are always drawn on [[anthro]] and [[humanoid]] characters. \n\nButts have a prominent role in sexual attraction and body aesthetics, conversely, they are a subject of comedy and amusement in other contexts.\n\n\n\"Butt\" should be tagged if a character's butt is present and visible, regardless of whether it is covered by clothing, partially exposed, or fully naked.\n\n[b]Rating:[/b]\n* An image featuring a butt can be rated [color=green][b]Safe[/b][/color].\n* If the butt is the [[butt_focus|focus of the image]], or the character is [[presenting_hindquarters|presenting it provocatively]], the image should be rated [color=yellow][b]Questionable[/b][/color].\n* Exposed [[genitals]] or [[anus]] require an [color=tomato][b]Explicit[/b][/color] rating.\n\n\nh4. Butt Size Tags\n[i]See the section bellow for examples and notes on sizes[/i]\n\n* [[small butt]]\n* [b]butt[/b]\n* [[big butt]]\n* [[huge butt]]\n* [[hyper butt]]\n\n\n[section=Butt Sizes Examples and Notes]\n[sup][i]For more details on each size, visit the linked wiki pages[/i][/sup]\n\nh5. [[Small Butt]]\n\nthumb #2821873 thumb #1968087 thumb #3201816 thumb #2952369\n* Butts that are smaller than \"average\" - small butts may be flat, muscular or bony, or may simply be petite and perky\n** Muscular, slim, skinny and young characters will most often have a small butt\n** Usually drawn with minimal lines or shape to distinguish the buttocks from the thighs and pelvis\n** Extremely under-tagged\n\nh5. Butt (As a Size Tag)\nthumb #1713773 thumb #2966939 thumb #2425753 thumb #4472466 thumb #3241468\n* While \"Butt\" serves as the umbrella tag for all sizes, and not specifically intended to describe any size of butt, this tag alone is used for nondescript \"average\" butts\n** An \"average\" butt has with defined buttocks, with shading and/or lines clearly dividing the cheeks from upper thigh; when a character is bent over, the shape of the buttocks is clearly distinct from the thighs (see example 5), unlike a character with a small butt\n** \"Butt\" is also used alone when the size of the character's buttocks are hard to determine or describe within an image, such as with feral characters, or with humanoid/anthro characters in poses where the buttocks are stretched and flattened\n\nh5. [[Big Butt]]\nthumb #804954 thumb #3146506 thumb #3137638 thumb #2865744\n* Noticeably larger than \"average\", prominent buttocks. \n** Rarely if ever drawn as \"fat\" - ie sagging, dimpled, with cellulite, most often drawn plump and round.\n\nh5. [[Huge Butt]]\nthumb #2077911 thumb #3179956 thumb #2371816 thumb #2734426\n* [i]Very[/i] large buttocks, far larger than average - they may be round, muscular, fatty, perky or flabby, but are proportionate to the bearer of the buttocks \n\nh5. [[Hyper Butt]]\nthumb #3838280 thumb #3018754 thumb #2951787 thumb #2092175\n* Butts that are cartoonishly massive and disproportionately large in comparison to their owner\n** May defy gravity, be unrealistically perky and round\n** Often over-tagged on butts that would be better described by \"huge butt\"\n[/section]\n\nh4. Butt Tags\n\n[section= Appearance]\n\nh5. Variations and features\n\n* [[bubble butt]] - Perky, round buttocks, sometimes highly stylized and spherical\n* [[monobutt]] - A character whose butt is not divided into buttocks, usually seen on [[toony]] characters\n* [[butt markings]]\n** [[butt heart]] - markings on the inner sides of the cheeks that form a 🤍 shape\n** [[spotted_butt]] - markings shaped like [[spots]], not to be confused with [[freckles_o