              "wiki_body": "thumb #4338639 thumb #4549573 thumb #4089352 thumb #4416971 thumb #1051006 thumb #498794\n\nA character that has [b]EXTREME[/b] amounts of excess body fat. [color=yellow][b][u]This tag is NOT using the medical definition of morbid obesity[/u][/b][/color] — it is intended to describe characters that are overwhelmingly obese, frequently beyond what is physically possible for a human being or real life animal. See the examples above for a range of what is considered morbid obesity. \n\nTypically a morbidly obese character will have a large, fat belly that hangs down over the legs, large rolls of [[fat_arms|arm fat]] and [[fat_legs|leg fat]], and at the very least a [[double chin]] if not multiple chins. A morbidly obese character's figure will be significantly impacted by their excess fat, making many of them very round in overall shape.\n\nA morbidly obese character's ability to move is usually impacted by their large amount of body fat; they may even be rendered entirely [[immobile]]. In the most extreme cases, a morbidly obese character will be impossibly fat, and essentially a living blob of fat rolls. \n\nh4. Features of Morbid Obesity\n\n* A [[huge belly|huge]] or even [[hyper belly|hyper sized]] belly\n* Large amounts of [[belly rolls]] and/or [[back rolls]]\n* A very [[belly overhang|low hanging belly]], usually covering the entire upper legs, if not reaching the ground\n* [[chubby cheeks]]\n* [[double_chin|multiple chins]]\n* very prominent [[moobs]]\n* [[fat arms]]\n* [[fat legs]]\n* [[huge breasts]], often [[sagging breasts]]\n* [[stretch marks]]\n* [[cellulite]]\n\nh4. Common/Related Tags\n* [[immobile]] — when a morbidly obese character is so fat that they are incapable of moving \n* [[slob]] — morbidly obese characters covered in sweat, dirt, and frequently old food, suggesting a gluttonous and sedentary lifestyle\n* [[stuffing]] — morbidly obese characters are often shown eating large amounts of food\n* [[feederism]] — a fetish revolving around feeding someone excess amounts of food\n* [[weight gain]] — when a character gains weight\n\nh4. Morbidly Obese Tags\n\nh6. Form\n* [[morbidly obese anthro]]\n* [[morbidly obese feral]]\n* [[morbidly obese human]]\n* [[morbidly obese humanoid]]\n* [[morbidly obese taur]]\n\nh6. Sex\n* [[morbidly obese ambiguous]]\n* [[morbidly obese female]]\n* [[morbidly obese intersex]]\n* [[morbidly obese male]]\n\nh4. See Also\n* [[overweight]]\n* [[obese]]"
