              "wiki_body": "thumb #3903502 thumb #5094050 thumb #5606219 thumb #5621736 thumb #3467364 thumb #4119558 thumb #1913966 thumb #5060628 thumb #3667946\n\n[b]Nipple fetish[/b] indicates that not only are [[nipples]] present in the image, but that the image sexualises or fetishises them in some way. Note that this applies specifically to the [[nipples]], not the [[areola]] or [[breasts]]. The main situations where this tag applies are:\n* The work depicts [[nipple play]] (handled automatically via tag implication).\n* No [[nipple play]] is [i]currently[/i] taking place, but the composition of the image makes it clear that some is [i]about to[/i], or recently has.\n* The work depicts [[lactation]] (or secretion of some other fluid through the nipples) in an erotic manner.\n* The nipples appear unusually large or otherwise prominent relative to the character's other proportions (especially of the [[pecs]]/[[breasts]]), or they have some other noticeable unique or unusual feature such that they form a significant erotic focal point of the work. \n* The composition and framing of the work makes it clear that nipples are a major erotic focus of the work. \n\nMost instances of works being tagged with nipple_fetish are a result of the implication nipple_play -> nipple_fetish. However, nipple_fetish is broader than this - many works that don't depict [[nipple play]] do still meet the sexualisation/fetishisation criteria.\n\nSimply being [[rating:e]] with visible nipples is not enough to warrant a nipple_fetish tag, but the right style and composition are often all it takes. There's a fair bit of grey area and interpretation here, but it essentially boils down to:\n\n[b]Are [[nipples]] a key erotic focus of this work? If the answer is yes, then it deserves a nipple_fetish tag.[/b]\n\nh4. Is [[lactation]] nipple_fetish?\n\n[[Lactation]] does not automatically imply nipple_fetish [i]per se[/i], as lactation can be depicted without a fetishistic or sexualised focus on