            {
              "tag": "tights",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 3976,
              "wiki_body": "[b]Tights[/b] is an article of skintight [[legwear]] that is worn like [[pants]], but cover the feet. Tights may extend above the waist covering the abdomen. Body tights are a form of tights that cover most of the torso area.\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Similar clothing]\r\n\r\nTry your best to distinguish tights from these very similar clothing forms.\r\n\r\nh4. [[Pantyhose]]\r\n\r\nthumb #3390605 thumb #3306062\r\n\r\n[b]Pantyhose[/b] is an American term for garments that take the form of tights, but are thinner, and more sheer than tights. Pantyhose and tights are functionally a form of underwear intended to be worn under [[bottomwear]].\r\n\r\nThe main difference between tights and pantyhose is the thickness of the material. In some countries, the term `tights` refers to both thin, and thick constructions.\r\n\r\nPerformers will prefer to wear tights over pantyhose. Pantyhose is more commonly associated with [[lingerie]], and [[bunny_costume|bunny costumes]].\r\n\r\nhttp://www.differencebetween.net/miscellaneous/fashion-beauty/difference-between-pantyhose-and-tights/\r\n\r\nh4. [[Leggings]]\r\n\r\n[b]Leggings[/b] are essentially [[legwear]] that essentially function as tight [[pants]] similar to [[yoga pants]]. Unlike tights, leggings do not cover the feet, and are thick enough to be worn casually without bottomwear. Most real leggings are not translucent.\r\n\r\nhttp://www.differencebetween.net/miscellaneous/fashion-beauty/difference-between-yoga-pants-and-leggings/\r\n\r\nh4. [[Yoga Pants]]\r\n\r\n[b]Yoga pants[/b] are tight [[pants]] similar to leggings, but usually have a flared pantleg. Yoga pants have a waistband, and are more flexible than leggings.\r\n\r\n[/section]"
            }
