            "wiki_body": "thumb #1961846 thumb #1942401 thumb #1738233 thumb #1841986\r\n\r\nUsed to describe when a character has part of their body exposed, or is being undressed by anyone or anything other than themselves. The clothes do not need to be physically removed for a character to be exposed.\r\n\r\nh4. Examples\r\n\r\n-[b]Character A[/b] is helping [b]Character B[/b] undress.\r\n-[b]Character A[/b] is forcefully undressing [b]Character B[/b] by physically ripping their clothes off.\r\n-[b]Character A[/b] is using magic/telekinesis to undress [b]Character B[/b].\r\n-A [b]character[/b] is undressed by an [b]inanimate object[/b] (for example, clothing caught on a branch or ripped off by a trap).\r\n\r\nWhat does [b]not[/b] count as assisted exposure:\r\n\r\n-If clothing fails to function properly and just falls off, such as a button failing and pants dropping.  For situations like this, see [[wardrobe malfunction]].\r\n-If a character removes their own clothing, whether on purpose or on accident.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[clothing_pull]]\r\n* [[clothing_theft]]\r\n* [[exposed]] - Used for a character unintentionally exposing themselves or being exposed by force. [[Pantsing]] tends to fall under this category.\r\n* [[partially_clothed]] - Acts of [[clothing_pull|clothing pulling]], or revealing body parts without removing clothing. [[Pantsing]] tends to fall under this category.\r\n* [[undressing]]\r\n** [[forced_undressing]] - Undressing against one's will - either by force, or by [[magic_undressing|magic]].  Hypnosis, and body control are related, but tend to fall under [[forced_to_undress]] instead.\r\n** [[undressing_another]] - Situations involving actual removal of clothing involving a second character.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[accidental_exposure]]\r\n* [[pantsing]]"
