            "count": 7118,
            "wiki_body": "For when the species does not match the [[genitals]], such as a [[feline]] possessing a [[canine penis]].\r\n\r\nThis is a complicated subject that is still being refined. It is related to and can overlap with the [[anatomically inaccurate]] tag. One of the key differences is that this tag isn't restricted to feral body types.\r\n\r\nh4. Subtags\r\n\r\nThis concept is organized by type of genitalia ([[penis]], [[pussy]], etc), and separated by humanoid, and animal genital variants.\r\n\r\n* [b]mismatched_genitalia[/b]\r\n** [[mismatched_penis]]\r\n*** [[mismatched_animal_penis]]\r\n*** [[mismatched_humanoid_penis]]\r\n*** [[varied_multi_penis]]\r\n** [[mismatched_pussy]] (This concept is not yet well defined and as such is undertagged. Most mismatched examples fall under the 'penis' category.)\r\n*** [[mismatched_animal_pussy]]\r\n*** [[mismatched_humanoid_pussy]]\r\n\r\nh4. General guidelines\r\n\r\nh5. Restrictions and limitations\r\n\r\n* Does not apply to [[humanoid|humanoids]], including [[animal_humanoid|animal humanoids]].\r\n* Probably does not apply to mythological and other fictional species (such as [[dragon|dragons]]). It will depend on how closely they resemble a real life species or a character's established genitals (if any).\r\n* The depicted genitalia should resemble a well established genitalia category ([[humanoid_penis]], [[canine_penis]], [[tapering_penis]], etc)\r\n** Obscured or ambiguous examples are probably not a great fit for this tag.\r\n** Generic [[animal_penis|animal penises]], and other [[genitals|genitalia]] is a grey area, and probably shouldn't be applicable. Use good judgment in this regard.\r\n* [[Hybrid genitalia]] that matches the species of a character doesn't apply towards this tag.\r\n\r\nCharacters that possess genitalia from multiple species serve as an exception to the above restrictions.\r\n\r\nh5. Applications\r\n\r\n* Characters with a well defined body resembling a real life species featuring [[genitals|genitalia]] that does not match the genitalia that species should have.\r\n** This includes [[feral]], [[anthro]], and [[taur]] body types. Other forms such as [[split form]] should be handled on a case by case basis. \r\n* Characters that have the wrong genitalia for their species entirely are applicable for this tag, and also [[anatomically_inaccurate]]. Example - Most birds (males included) have a [[cloaca]], not a [[penis]]. \r\n* Characters featuring multiple types of genitalia are applicable towards this tag. See [[varied_multi_penis]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[tag_group:feral_anatomy]]\r\n\r\n* [[anatomically_correct]]"
