              "wiki_body": "thumb #1518232 thumb #2477744 thumb #2465261 thumb #4744959\r\n\r\n[b]Recursive penetration[/b] is when someone is being penetrated through an orifice that is currently inside someone else, such that in order to access it from \"the outside\", the \"outer\" must be penetrated to reach the \"inner\" one. In other words, the destination orifice is (at least) \"one level down\".\r\n\r\nThis usually only makes sense in [[vore]], in cases where a prey is penetrated by someone outside (who is then also penetrating the pred to get there), but also works in cases like [[matryoshka_sex]] (where an unborn baby is penetrated through the mother's womb, via [[in_utero_penetration]]) or possibly some [[goo creature]] enveloping someone else.\r\n\r\nLike with [[penetration_tunneling]], internal orifices in situations like the [[cervix]] during [[cervical_penetration]], the [[urethra]] during [[slit_sounding]], or the \"inner mouth\" of [[xenomorph|xenomorphs]] aren't \"re-counted\", so these scenarios don't qualify as [[recursive penetration]] on their own.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[recursive_vore]]: Vore multiple levels down instead of penetration\r\n* [[thread_transfer]]/[[serial_threading]]: Penetrating multiple people at once in a chain instead of in levels\r\n* [[penetration_tunneling]]: Penetration of someone whose other end is partly inside someone else, somewhat like a [[living condom]]. May turn into [[recursive penetration]] if the penetration continues once the prey goes completely inside.\r\n* [[penetration_interlock]]: Similar to (but distinct from) [[recursive penetration]] in the case where the prey ends up penetrating/being vored by whatever is penetrating the \"outer\" orifice.\r\n* [[through_body]]/[[bulge_insertion]]: Use of bulges in ways that may involve penetrating someone else in a kind of [[train position]], though this wouldn't be [[recursive_penetration]].\r\n\r\nh4. Visual Guide\r\n[table]\r\n  [thead]\r\n    [tr]\r\n