          "wiki_body": "thumb #3289091 thumb #3745986 thumb #3923904 thumb #3734718\r\n\r\nA character asking, encouraging, or demanding another — directly, or indirectly — to perform [[rimming|analingus]] on them. Alternatively, this can describe the far rarer case of a character asking or demanding [i]to perform[/i] rimming on another.\r\n\r\nA character asking to be rimmed frequently involves the character [[presenting hindquarters|presenting their hindquarters]], and their [[presenting anus|anus in specific]]. A character specifically commanding or requesting [[talking to viewer|the viewer]] to rim them is extremely common. \r\n\r\nh6. A rimming request may be...\r\n* direct and descriptive (\"stick your tongue in my asshole\")\r\n* playful, direct, but context dependent (\"kiss my butt!\", with the added context of the character presenting their anus)\r\n* indirect, implied, and relying on visual context (e.g. \"go ahead, you know you want to\"/\"I brought you something to eat!\"/\"make yourself useful\"/\"show me how you use that tongue\")\r\n* presented through \"spoken\" images or icons, e.g. \"👅🍩?\".\r\n\r\n[quote]\r\nh5. Tagging Notes\r\n\r\n* If the character specifically mentions [i]kissing[/i] their anus or ass, \"[[kiss my ass]]\" can also be tagged — however, not all posts under `kiss_my_ass` are rimming requests, the character should be specifically presenting their anus or specifying the anus to be tagged under this tag, and `kiss_my_ass`\r\n\r\n* A character saying \"eat my ass\" in the context of an insult, without the character presenting their butt or anus, should not be tagged as `rimming_request`\r\n\r\n* A character may be already [[facesitting]] or performing [[stinkface]] on another character, while requesting the other character rim them, or encourage them to do further rimming\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\nh4. Useful Tags\r\n\r\n* [b]Common Dialogue Themes[/b]\r\n** [[talking to another]]\r\n*** [[talking to partner]]\r\n** [[talking to viewer]]\r\n