              "wiki_body": "Any kind of damage to living tissue, be it a bruise, a laceration, a burn, etc.\n\n[section,expanded=Tags About Wounds]\n\nh4. Severity\n\n[i]Not all types of wounds may fall neatly into one of these categories. Leaving the severity untagged is always an option.[/i]\n\n* [[minor_wound]] - Scratches, scrapes, bruises etc. apply towards this tag.\n* [[severe_wound]] - The [[gore|gory]], and potentially life threating kind of stuff.\n** [[fatal_wound]] - Wounds so severe that that [[death]] is unavoidable.\n** [[just_a_flesh_wound]] - A character blissfully disregards severe or fatal wounds.\n\nh4. Injuries\n\n* [[black_eye_(injury)]]\n* [[bruised|bruise]]\n* [[burn]]\n* [[crush]]\n* Cuts and lacerations\n** [[slit_(wound)]]\n*** [[slit_throat]]\n*** [[slit_wrists]]\n** [[laceration]] - Similar to a cut, but the wound is the result of body tissue being torn open in a jagged and uneven sort of way. A cut is more uniform in appearance.\n** [[gash]] - A deep cut or laceration. Does not include [[amputation]] or [[decapitation]].\n* Severe Injuries\n** [[amputation]]\n** [[bisected]]\n** [[decapitation]]\n** [[disembowelment]]\n** [[dismemberment]]\n** [[heartshot]]\n** [[impalement]]\n** [[shot_in_head]]\n* Misc.\n** [[broken_bone]]\n** [[broken_horn]] - May not make sense to tag this as wounded. \n** [[broken_nose]]\n** [[broken_wing]]\n\nh5. Injuries By Objects\n\n* [[puncture_wound]]\n** [[arrow_wound]] (See [[arrowed]])\n** [[bullet_wound]]\n** [[perforating_wound]] (this occurs when the object passes through - it enters on one side and exits on the other.\n** [[stab_wound]] (See [[stab]])\n\nh4. Body Position\n\n* [[arm_wound]]\n* [[butt_wound]]\n* [[foot_wound]]\n* [[genital_wound]]\n** [[penis_wound]]\n** [[pussy_wound]]\n** [[ball_wound]]\n*** [[ballbusting]]\n* [[hand_wound]]\n* [[head_wound]]\n** [[facial_wound]]\n*** [[eye_wound]]\n**** [[black_eye_(injury)]]\n** [[nosebleed]]\n* [[leg_wound]]\n* [[torso_wound]]\n** [[back_wound]]\n** [[chest_wound]]\n** [[stomach_wound]]\n\nh4. Other\n\n* [[first_aid]]\n** [[bandages]]\n** [[tourniquet]]\n* [[healing]]\n** [[healing_wound]] - A wound in the process of being healed.\n* [[healed_wound]]\n** [[scar]]\n*** [[slit_(scar)]]\n** [[scab]]\n\n[/section]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[blood]]\n* [[gore]]\n* [[violence]]"
