              "kor": "j-패션",
              "count": 9695,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #3059052 thumb #4335781 thumb #3484100 thumb #4518649 thumb #4589651 thumb #2321775\r\n\r\n[b]J-Fashion[/b] is an umbrella term used for Japanese street fashion styles. It is typically considered a subcategory of [[alternative fashion]]. \r\n\r\nSome popular J-Fashion styles include [[lolita_(fashion)|Lolita]], [[Gyaru]], [[Fairy Kei]], [[decora_(fashion)|Decora]] and [[Jirai Kei]].\r\n\r\nJ-Fashion should generally not be tagged as [[Japanese clothing]] unless traditional Japanese clothing or school uniforms are an influence on the style, such as in [[Wa Lolita]] or [[Kogal]]. While J-Fashion originates in Japan, these styles are worn around the world.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n* [[cosplay]]\r\n* [[japanese_clothing]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[tag group:fashion]]"
