              "wiki_body": "thumb #2370783 thumb #2496094 thumb #1721882 thumb #3201155 \r\n\r\n[b]Fairy Kei[/b] is a Japanese street fashion style inspired by children's clothing and pop culture of the 80s and 90s, particularly brands such as [[My Little Pony]] and [[Care Bears]]. It typically features [[pastel]] colors, graphics on clothing, and oversized clothing. Common motifs in Fairy Kei include [[rainbow]]s, [[unicorn]]s, [[candy]], [[confetti]], [[balloon]]s, [[domestic_cat|cats]], and [[star]]s.\r\n\r\nFairy Kei is associated with a larger aesthetic style known as \"yume kawaii\" (literally \"dreamy cute\"). As a result, you may sometimes hear this style be referred to as such instead.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[sweet_lolita]]\r\n* [[tag group:fashion]]"
