            "wiki_body": "thumb #1307323 thumb #2399924 thumb #812642\r\n\r\n[b]Blush[/b] describes the responsive reddening of the skin caused by blood vessels dilating. This can happen on many parts of the body, but is typically connected with the face as this is where it is often most obviously seen - this tag is used to cover all blushing, but when used alone refers to facial blushing.\r\n\r\nBlushing has various causes, however, blushing of the face in particular is frequently due to [[embarrassed|embarrassment]] or [[shy|shyness]]. Blushing can also be caused as a result of [[aroused|sexual arousal]], excitement, [[angry|anger]], physical exertion, or [[substance intoxication|drunkenness]]. Exaggerated blushing of the face is very common in [[cartoon|cartoons]] and [[anime]]. \r\n\r\nWhile blush shouldn't realistically be visible through fur, feather, or scales, it's frequently used and accepted by suspension of disbelief for added expressiveness.\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Related tags]\r\nh4. Body location\r\n\r\nh5. Face and Head Blush\r\n\r\n* [[nose_blush]]\r\n* [[ear_blush]]\r\n* [[full-face_blush]]\r\n\r\nh5. [[Body Blush]]\r\n\r\n* [[arm_blush]]\r\n* [[balls_blush]]\r\n* [[belly_blush]]\r\n* [[breast_blush]]\r\n* [[butt_blush]]\r\n* [[foot_blush]]\r\n* [[leg_blush]]\r\n* [[penis_blush]]\r\n* [[pussy_blush]]\r\n\r\nh4. Symbolic\r\n\r\nBlush effects are used as an [[iconography|iconograph]] similar to [[cross-popping vein]], and the [[sweatdrop_(iconography)|sweatdrop iconograph]]. These tags should be kept separate from actual blushing.\r\n\r\n* [[blush_emoji]]\r\n* [[blush_emoticon]]\r\n* [[blush_symbol]]\r\n\r\nh4. Intensity\r\n\r\n* [[heavy_blush]]\r\n* [[light_blush]]\r\n\r\nh4. Other\r\n\r\n* [[blush_lines]]\r\n* [[blush_stickers]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag group:facial expressions]]"
