            "wiki_body": "thumb #539888 thumb #1367432 thumb #672692  \r\n\r\n[b]Dialogue[/b] is a form of verbal communication presented through [[text]] consisting of words perceived to be spoken aloud. Such words are generally, but not always, found in [[speech_bubble|speech bubbles]].\r\n\r\nh4. What counts as dialogue?\r\n\r\n* Content perceived to be spoken out loud. It does not have to be a conversation, nor does it need to be targeted at anyone.\r\n* Content that is recorded, or transmitted (broadcasts, phone calls, etc). Try to make sure that the text is perceived to be audible, instead of a [[text message]].\r\n* Content that is from [[offscreen_character|offscreen]], or [[unseen_character|unseen]] sources.\r\n\r\nh5. What content is applicable?\r\n\r\n* Most words\r\n** [[fictional_language|Fictional]], [[constructed_language|constructed]], and [[unknown_language|unknown]] languages may be assumed to be dialogue.\r\n* [[Profanity]] (any context)\r\n* Proper nouns (names of characters, locations, species etc.)\r\n* Abbreviations (\"BTW\", \"WTH\", \"BRB\"), and simplified speech (shortened words)\r\n* [[Muffled]], or garbled speech that appears inspired by actual words.\r\n\r\nh5. Communication vs Conversation vs Dialogue\r\n\r\nThe intent of communication is to share ideas through a language medium. A conversation is the sharing of ideas between two, or more subjects. Dialogue that is perceived as communicating an idea can be thought of as conversational dialogue.\r\n\r\nNot all forms of communication are considered `dialogue` by our tagging definition.\r\n\r\nh4. What should not be treated as dialogue?\r\n\r\nCommunication through one's thoughts is not considered dialogue, and should be tagged as [[inner monologue]] instead.\r\n\r\n* Most forms of [[vocalization]] should not be treated as dialogue. Consider whether the character is producing words, or sounds, and tag accordingly.\r\n** The most common forms of vocalization include [[moan|moans]], [[grunting|grunts]], and [[laugh|laughter]].\r\n** [[Animal noises]] are considered vocalizations too.\r\n** Generic [[screaming]] (\"Aaaaaaaaahhh\")\r\n* Certain [[interjection|interjections]] (\"Ack\", \"Eek\", \"Eep\", \"Eww\", \"Gah\", \"Ugh\")\r\n* [[Sound effects]] inside of a [[speech bubble]].\r\n* Standalone punctuation ([[exclamation_point|!]], [[question_mark|?]], [[ellipsis|...]])\r\n* [[Muffled]], or garbled speech that does not appear inspired by actual words. (\"Hmph\", \"Mmph\")\r\n* [[Whistling]], or [[humming]]\r\n\r\nh5. Grey areas\r\n\r\nMost grey areas involves content that is more expressive in nature. Some can be thought of as a valid form of communication\r\n\r\n* [[emoji|Emojis]] and [[emoticon|emoticons]]\r\n* [[Pictographics]] - The use of symbols, or images to convey ideas instead of words.\r\n* [[Sound effects]], or vocalizations that represent socializing, or speaking such as \"Chatter\", [[blah_blah_blah|\"Blah blah blah\"]], \"Loud talking\", \"Whisper\".\r\n* [[voice_acted|Voice acting]], where words are spoken through [[sound]] instead of text. Many images convey dialogue in this way, and [[subtitled|subtitles]] are optional.\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Speech and communication themes]\r\n\r\nMany of these themes apply to more than one interactive method including [[text_message|text messages]], which are not considered dialogue. \r\n\r\nh4. Text containers\r\n\r\n* [[flash_bubble]] - Usually a special type of [[thought_bubble]]\r\n* [[speech_bubble]] - A container used for dialogue, and sound effects.\r\n* [[text_box]]\r\n** [[dialogue_box]] - A narrative interface [[text box]] that contains speech related content.\r\n** [[message_box]] - A container used for [[text_message|text messages]], and similar non-dialogue content.\r\n* [[thought_bubble]] - A container used for [[inner monologue]].\r\n\r\nh4. Concepts\r\n\r\n* [[apology]]\r\n* [[begging]]\r\n* [[command]]\r\n* [[complaining]]\r\n* [[compliment]]\r\n* [[encouragement]]\r\n* [[excusing]]\r\n* [[good_wishes]]\r\n* [[greeting]]\r\n* [[insult]]\r\n* [[introduction]]\r\n* [[lies]]\r\n* offer\r\n* [[praise]]\r\n* [[propositioning|proposition]]\r\n* [[question]]\r\n* [[refusing]]\r\n* request\r\n* [[suggestion]]\r\n* [[thanking]]\r\n* [[welcoming]]\r\n\r\n[b]Calling[/b]\r\n\r\n* [[calling_for_help]]\r\n* [[calling_for_release]]\r\n\r\n[b]Declaration[/b]\r\n\r\n* [[stating_intentions]]\r\n* [[announcing_orgasm]]\r\n\r\n[b]Inviting[/b] - An offer to go somewhere, or participate in an event.\r\n\r\n* [[inviting]] - Usually limited to intimate / romantic / sexual invitations\r\n* [[inviting_home]]\r\n\r\n[b]Offering[/b] - An object, or service presented to another character or the viewer.\r\n\r\n* [[offering_to_another]]\r\n* [[offering_to_viewer]]\r\n\r\n* [[offering_food]]\r\n* [[offering_gift]]\r\n* [[offering_sex]]\r\n\r\n[b]Request[/b]\r\n\r\n* [[asking]] - Questions / Requests\r\n* [[asking_for_hug]]\r\n* [[cuddle_request]]\r\n* [[cum_request]]\r\n** [[insemination_request]]\r\n* [[impregnation_request]]\r\n* [[pull_out_request]]\r\n* [[requesting_position_change]]\r\n\r\n[b]Talking[/b] - The making of a statement to another character or the viewer.\r\n\r\n* [[talking_to_another]]\r\n** [[talking_to_partner]]\r\n** [[talking_to_pred]]\r\n** [[talking_to_prey]]\r\n* [[talking_to_viewer]]\r\n\r\nh4. Categories of speech\r\n\r\n* [[dirty_talk]]\r\n* [[explicitly_stated_consent]]\r\n* [[explicitly_stated_nonconsent]]\r\n* [[figure_of_speech]]\r\n** [[metaphor]]\r\n** [[simile]]\r\n* [[freudian_slip]]\r\n* [[idiom]]\r\n* [[porn_dialogue]]\r\n* [[profanity]]\r\n\r\nh4. Phonetic Dialogue\r\nWhen dialogue is written (intentionally misspelt) to convey a particular pronunciation of words \r\n\r\n* [[accent]]\r\n* [[lisp]]\r\n* [[stuttering]]\r\n\r\nh4. Common phrases / speech tropes\r\n\r\n* [[be_gentle]], [[not_so_rough]]\r\n* [[does_this_make_me_look_fat]]\r\n* [[don't_tell]]\r\n* [[don't_stop]]\r\n* [[don't_struggle]]\r\n* [[good_boy]], [[good_girl]]\r\n* [[i_love_you]], [[i_hate_you]]\r\n* [[kiss_my_ass]]\r\n* [[mommy_kink]], [[daddy_kink]]\r\n* [[not_what_it_looks_like]]\r\n* [[too_big]]\r\n* [[too_fast]]\r\n\r\nh5. Dialogue specific\r\n\r\n* [[location_in_dialogue]]\r\n* [[name_in_dialogue]]\r\n* [[species_in_dialogue]]\r\n\r\nh4. Tone and intensity\r\n\r\n* [[whisper]]\r\n* [[yelling]]\r\n\r\nh4. Narrative presentation\r\n\r\nThese tags cover how the dialogue is structured within the scene - concepts like if there are pauses, or repeated letters, or words.\r\n\r\n* [[interrupted_speech]]\r\n* [[repeated_dialogue]]\r\n* [[shared_dialogue]]\r\n* [[split_dialogue]]\r\n* [[stuttering]] - Not always dialogue\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:narrative_elements]]\r\n\r\n* [[moan]]\r\n* [[text]]\r\n** [b]dialogue[/b]\r\n** [[inner_monologue]]\r\n** [[narration]]\r\n* [[pictographics]]\r\n* [[thought_bubble]]"
