            "wiki_body": "[b]Anthrofied[/b] is when a beastly character ([[feral]], [[anthro]], [[animal humanoid]], [[taur]], etc.) is depicted with either their animal or humanoid traits amplified or lessened to make them more anthropomorphic in appearance compared to their original form.\n\n[sub]Note: this tag is a sub-genre of [[alternate_form]], so this isn't [[transformation]].[/sub]\n\nh4. Scenarios\n* A feral is depicted with more humanoid traits and less animal traits.\n* An animal humanoid is depicted with more beastly traits, their existing ones are amplified, and their humanoid traits are lessened.\n* An anthro is drawn more humanoid or beastly depending on which side of the anthropomorphic scale they lean on.\n* A taur's secondary lower torso is replaced with bipedal legs and their upper-half is anthrofied (if they weren't already).\n\nh4. Anthrofying a character\nIn order to identify or make an anthrofied character, the following traits should be considered:\n\n[section,expanded=Essential Traits:]\n* An animal's head (having this trait alone would make the character into an [[animal head]], which is not a true anthro).\n* A body that is covered in [[fur]], [[feathers]], or [[scales]] (depending on the species).\n* A humanoid torso.\n* Humanoid arms and legs.\n* [[biped|Bipedalism]].\n* An upright posture.\n[/section]\n\n[section,expanded=Optional Traits:]\n* A [[snout]] (the \"Furry-O-Meter\":https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/SlidingScale/FurryFandom applies here).\n* Beastly hands and feet ([[claws]], [[talons]], [[handpaw]], [[hooves]], etc.).\n* Additional body parts ([[tails]], [[wings]], extra limbs, [[dorsal fin|dorsal fins]], etc.).\n* [[Digitigrade]] legs (depending on the species).\n* [[Animal genitalia]] (depending on the species).\n[/section]\n\nh4. Examples\n\n[section,expanded=Anthrofied ferals]\nthumb #871429 thumb #1555323 thumb #1896000 thumb #428499 thumb #1201074 thumb #1429188 thumb #4117704\n[/section]\n\n[section,expanded=Anth