            "count": 116886,
            "wiki_body": "The [b]beak[/b], [b]bill[/b], or [b]rostrum[/b] is an external anatomical structure of [[bird|birds]] that is used for [[eating]], [[preening]], manipulating objects, killing prey, fighting, probing for food, courtship and feeding young. The terms beak and rostrum are also used to refer to a similar mouth part in [[dinosaur|dinosaurs]], [[cephalopod|cephalopods]], [[cetacean|cetaceans]], [[billfish|billfishes]], [[pufferfish|pufferfishes]], [[turtle|turtles]], [[tadpole|tadpoles]] and siren [[salamander|salamanders]].\r\n\r\nAlthough beaks vary significantly in size, shape, color and texture, they share a similar underlying structure. Two bony projections—the upper and lower mandibles—are covered with a thin keratinized layer of epidermis known as the rhamphotheca. In most species, two nostril cavities known as nares lead to the respiratory system.\r\n\r\nh4. Types\r\n\r\n* [[axe_beak]]\r\n* [[beak_pussy]]\r\n* [[nose_beak]]\r\n* [[toothed_beak]]\r\n\r\nh4. Accessories\r\n\r\n* [[beak_guard]]\r\n* [[beak_piercing]]\r\n* [[beakstick]]\r\n* [[condom_on_beak]]\r\n\r\nh4. Acts/Actions\r\n\r\n* [[beak_fuck]]\r\n* [[beak_grab]]\r\n* [[beakjob]]\r\n** [[autobeakjob]]\r\n* [[cum_in_beak]]\r\n** [[cum_from_beak]]\r\n* [[cum_on_beak]]\r\n* [[beak_lick]]\r\n** [[licking_own_beak]]\r\n* [[open_beak]]\r\n* [[taped_beak]]\r\n\r\nh4. Anatomy\r\n\r\n* [[casque_(anatomy)]]\r\n* [[cere (anatomy)|cere]]\r\n* [[gonydeal_spot]]\r\n* [[lores (anatomy)|lores]]\r\n* [[opercula]]\r\n\r\nh4. Appearance\r\n\r\nh6. Size\r\n\r\n* [[small_beak]]\r\n* [[big_beak]]\r\n* [[huge_beak]]\r\n* [[hyper_beak]]\r\n\r\nh6. Shape\r\n- A beak may feature more than one of these tags.\r\n\r\n* [[bent_beak]]\r\n* [[conical_beak]] - Beak forms a cone shape.\r\n* [[curved_beak]]\r\n* [[flat_beak]]\r\n* [[hooked_beak]]\r\n* [[jagged_beak]]\r\n* [[long_beak]]\r\n* [[narrow_beak]]\r\n* [[pointy_beak]]\r\n* [[short_beak]]\r\n* [[thin_beak]]\r\n* [[unusual_beak]]\r\n\r\nh6. Colors\r\n\r\n* [[