            "count": 34634,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #4251906 thumb #2282817  thumb #3728702 thumb #4039975 thumb #1750580\n\n[b]Semi-anthro[/b] describes characters with a form that lies somewhere between being [[feral]], and being \"fully\" [[anthro|anthropomorphic]] — that is, having entirely humanoid proportions and features. This can apply to a wide range of character designs.\n\nSemi-anthro characters almost always [[biped|stand upright]] (although some may be able to run on all-fours), they usually have human-like hands (or use their paws as hands: [[handpaw]]), and are capable of human-like expressions. However, they typically have more animalistic proportions and more animal features than a standard anthro character. Semi-anthro characters are often more squat than a fully anthro character, and frequently do not wear clothes,\n\nMost \"funny animal\":https://en.wikifur.com/wiki/Funny_animal cartoon characters will fall under this designation, as well as many [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]], [[digimon_(species)|Digimon]], and upright [i][[My Little Pony]][/i] characters.\n\n\nh5. Tagging note:\nThis is a [i]supplementary[/i] tag used to indicate the grey area between [[anthro]] and [[feral]], and is not intended to be a separate category. This means that depending on the image, tagging [[anthro]] [u]or[/u] [[feral]] should be tagged [i]in addition[/i] to semi-anthro, indicating which form the character is closer to.\n\nh5. Common semi-anthro features:\n* Upright and [[biped|bipedal]]\n* Semi-anthro bodies can vary, but even the most \"anthro-leaning\" semi-anthro character will have proportions closer to that of their animal species than a human\n** Semi-anthro characters' bodies will often be squat and [[bottom heavy]], with [[digitgrade]] feet/legs\n** Female characters may have [[wide hips]] and a [[small waist|narrow waist]], they may also have a \"puffed out\" chest to resemble breasts (though some have actual breasts)\n* Expressive faces that can emote in human ways despite otherwise animal anatomy\n** More feral examples of semi-anthro characters may have mostly animalistic faces with human-like eyes\n* Semi-anthro characters (in media and [[rating:safe|safe for work art]]) may go partially or entirely nude (with featureless nudity), with clothing usually limited to [[headwear]], [[topwear]], only accessories, or some combination of the three\n* \"Feral leaning\" semi-anthro characters will display human level intelligence and capacity for speech while showing generally animal behaviour, while \"anthro leaning\" semi-anthro characters will possibly display some superficial animal behaviours\n\n[b]Note:[/b] Not to be confused with [[chibi]] or [[toony]] characters, though there may be crossover\n\nh4. See also:\n* [[anthro]]\n* [[feral]]\n** [[busty_feral]]\n\nh4.Tagging Projects:\n\n* {{semi-anthro -feral -anthro}} — semi-anthro should not be tagged without [[feral]] or [[anthro]], so anything under this search needs to be fixed.\n\n\n[Section=Forum Discussions]\n* Forum Discussions about this tag, for more details:\n** forum #138155\n** forum #141795\n** forum #168743\n** forum #189979\n[/section]"
