            "count": 8027,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #3017423 thumb #2207129 thumb #2550048 thumb #4881016\n\n[b]Burping[/b] is the release  through the [[mouth]] of excess gases and swallowed air that have built up in the [[stomach]]. Burping is especially common in images featuring [[stuffing]], [[weight gain]], and [[vore]]; it may also indicate the character is [[substance intoxication|drunk]]. \n\n[section,expanded= ]\nh5. How Burping Is Depicted\n\nh6. Onomatopoeia\nWhen represented visually, burps are often are communicated by [[onomatopoeia]] or (non-onomatopoeic) [[sound effects]], ranging from straightforward \"burp\" or \"urp\" to a wide variety of more creative and evocative onomatopoeia like [i]\"bworp\" \"bwarp\" \"hooorp\"[/i] etc. Burps may be simply written out in a speech bubble indistinguishable from [[dialogue]], or they may be written larger or outside of the speech bubble - text conveying burping is sometimes creatively drawn to evoke the sound of the burp, ie increasing or decreasing in size mid-word to imply the volume of the burp, or the letters drawn to be wavy. \n\nh6. Visual Effects and Body Language\nBurping sound effects are often paired with bubbles, [[squean|squeans]] and [[emanata|emanating lines]] around the text, and/or character burping, potentially with a visible [[burp cloud]] escaping the character's mouth, as with other bodily noises, especially [[fart|farting]], burps are frequently associated with the colour green, and may be written in green or within a green cloud of gas. \n\nSymbols such as the bubbles, squeans and emanating lines can be used with or without written words to convey burping. A character's pose or expression can also visually imply or reinforce the act of burping - such as having a character pounding their chest with a fist, [[covering mouth|covering their mouth]] as they burp, or having [[puffed cheeks]] from the gas filling their mouth.\n\nA combination, or all of the above, can be seen in a single image. [/section]\n\nh4. Burping Tags\n\n* [[burp cloud]]\n* [[burping in face]] \n** [[burping in mouth]]\n* [[burping up objects]]\n** [[burping up clothes]]\n** [[burping up bones]]\n\nh4. Related Tags\n* [[open mouth]]\n** [[gaping mouth]]\n\nh4. See also\n* [[hiccuping]]\n* [[fart]]"
