            "wiki_body": "thumb #647772 thumb #1235888 thumb #4589221 thumb #3833974 thumb #4576728\r\n\r\nAn object, or body part, generally a [[penis]] or [[tentacles|tentacle]], shown entering one end of the body and exiting the other end.\r\n\r\nTypically, this is non-lethal and does not involve large amounts of [[blood]], though small amounts may be seen. For more lethal or painful situations, use [[fully_impaled]] instead.\r\n\r\nUsually this is meant to be interpreted as \"all the way through the digestive system\" (anus <-> mouth), since the digestive tract is the only tube in the human body that connects orifices in such a way. Most other orifice combinations (pussy <-> mouth, anus <-> urethra, etc.) would count as [[mismatched_threading]].\r\n\r\nh4. Similar concepts\r\n\r\n[u][b]If [[cum]] goes all the way through, use [[cum_through]] instead.[/b][/u]\r\n\r\nIf the \"penetrating object\" is a living creature, see [[snake_impalement]].\r\n\r\nIf it's two objects entering through separate ends and reaching each other from the inside, use [[meeting_in_the_middle]] instead. If it's a parasite coming out of two orifices at once, use [[emerging_from_both_ends]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[thread_transfer]] (one penis/tentacle going into a person while already threading another)\r\n** [[serial_threading]] (one penis/tentacle threading multiple people)\r\n* [[parallel_threading]] (multiple individuals being threaded separately on the same image)\r\n* [[u-turn_penetration]] (something emerging from an orifice and then re-entering the same person via a different orifice)\r\n* [[self_threading]] (someone threading themselves with their own penis/tail/tentacle)\r\n* [[mismatched_threading]] (when the orifices are generally not thought of as connected, see wiki page for details)\r\n* [[detached_threading]] (when either orifice doesn't exist on a \"whole\" body and is there from a missing/detached body part)\r\n\r\n* [[sparrow_(artist)]] (commonly associated with t