            "wiki_body": "thumb #2778900 thumb #2643849 thumb #681597 thumb #455798 thumb #749521 thumb #2344455\n\nA \"move\" is a [[Pokemon]] term for named skills that Pokémon use in battle.\n\nIdeally, this tag is used when a Pokémon's move is named in a post (a \"called attack\":https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CallingYourAttacks ), a Pokémon is depicted, and the art matches canonical depictions of that move. Alternatively, this tag can be used when highly recognizable signature moves, like [[aura sphere]] or [[draco meteor]], are used by a Pokémon. Preferably, the Pokémon using the move makes canonical sense, but E621 tagging usually ignores such lore constraints. \n\n[i]\"[Pokémon] used [move]! It's super effective!\"[/i] was a popular [[meme]] format (\"KYM\":https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/its-super-effective) that is not currently tagged on E621 (but easily could be) and will have many examples of the [i]pokemon_move[/i] tag, especially the move [[Attract]] in erotic Pokémon posts.\n\nthumb #1920502\n\n[section,expanded=List of Moves]Please also tag move names[sup]1[/sup] and add to this list:\n\n* [[acid_armor]]\n* [[attract]]\n* [[aura_sphere]]\n* [[blaze_kick]]\n* [[bone_rush]]\n* [[brave_bird]]\n* [[crush_claw]]\n* [[dark_pulse]]\n* [[dark_void_(move)]]\n* [[draco_meteor]]\n* [[ember_(move)]]\n* [[energy_ball_(move)]]\n* [[fire_fang_(move)]]\n* [[flamethrower_(move)]]\n* [[flash_(move)]]\n* [[focus_blast]]\n* [[frenzy_plant]]\n* [[fusion_bolt]]\n* [[harden_(move)]]\n* [[heart_swap]]\n* [[hyper_beam]]\n* [[hypnosis_(move)]]\n* [[ice_beam]]\n* [[iron_tail]]\n* [[kinesis_(move)]]\n* [[leaf_blade_(move)]]\n* [[leaf_storm]]\n* [[light_screen]]\n* [[mean_look_(move)]]\n* [[metal_claw_(move)]]\n* [[mystical_fire]]\n* [[night_daze]]\n* [[oblivion_wing]]\n* [[origin_pulse]]\n* [[precipice_blades]]\n* [[protect_(move)]]\n* [[psycho_boost]]\n* [[psyshock]]\n* [[razor_leaf]]\n* [[razor_shell_(move)]]\n* [[roar_(move)]]\n* [[self-destruct]]\n* [[shadow_ball]]\n* [[solar_beam]]\n* [[spiky_shield_(move)]]\n* [[sky_uppercut]]\n* [[techno_blast]]\n* [[teleport_(move)]]\n* [[tri_attack]]\n* [[vine_whip]]\n* [[water_gun_(move)]]\n* [[water_shuriken]]\n\n[sup]1. To disambiguate generically named moves from other tags, add a tag suffix like [i][name]_(move)[/i].[/sup]\n[/section]\n\nh4. Do not confuse with\n\nAvoid tagging this when a specific move cannot be identified. For example:\n\n* a [[Snorlax]] [[sleeping]] might not be using Rest\n* a [[Dugtrio]] tunneling [[underground]] may just be \"[[digging]]\" and not explicitly using Dig\n* a [[hypno_(pokemon)|Hypno]] performing [[mind control]] might not be using its Hypnosis move although may still qualify for the general [[hypnosis]] tag\n** however, a Hypno performing mind control via a swinging [[pendulum]] could reasonably be tagged [i]pokemon_move[/i]\n* [[salazzle|Salazzle's]] highly fetishized [[pheromones]] does not seem to specifically match any of its many Poison and other mind-altering moves and is probably not even a move\n\nPokémon manifesting generic powers, like a Fire-type Pokémon performing simple [[fire manipulation]], can be impossible to match to a specific move. At best, these unknown powers can be grouped into generic tags like [[psychic]], but they should probably not be tagged as moves.\n\nPokémon \"abilities\":https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Ability are not moves.\n\nPokémon moves are not regarded as [[magic]]. Whether or not this is semantically correct for tagging probably does not have a clear answer.\n\nh4. See also\n* [[gameplay mechanics]]\n* [[pokemon battle]]"
