          {
            "tag": "unwilling_pred",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 563,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #2119485 thumb #1262000\r\n\r\n[b]Unwilling pred[/b] describes a character (the \"pred\") in a vore or imminent vore scenario who unwillingly, through [[forced|force]] or by [[accidental_vore|accident]], consumes, inserts or ingests another. \r\n\r\nAn unwilling pred may be shown physically resisting, show unwillingness in their expression, or unwillingness may be conveyed through dialogue before, during, or after consuming the other character. The degree of willingness can vary - an initially unwilling pred may become \"willing\" by allowing the prey to be digested, absorbed or otherwise remain within their body. [[Accidental vore]] can involve an unwilling pred, but only if there is an expression of unwillingness, not simply of [[surprised|surprise]].\r\n\r\nh6. Examples of Unwilling Pred:\r\n* Another character [[willing_prey|willingly]] forcing themselves into the predator's mouth or other orifice, sometimes causing the other to involuntarily swallow them\r\n* The pred is restrained, and is either [[forced|force fed]] an equally unwilling prey by a third character, or through some device (e.g. a feeding tube or a slide directing a character into their mouth)\r\n* A character is hypnotized, drugged or drunk and consumes someone they wouldn't have while sober\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[Willing Prey]] - the exact opposite of this tag\r\n* [[Unwilling Prey]] - the default for prey, may be tagged in specific circumstances\r\n* [[Accidental Vore]]\r\n* [[Hypnotized Pred]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[Vore]] - when a character has eaten another\r\n* [[Imminent Vore]] - when the character is only about eat or can be implied to eat someone in the near future\r\n \r\n\r\n"
