            "wiki_body": "\"[b]Full Tour[/b]\" is a term for a vore scenario where the prey character is ingested through one orifice and eventually exits through another, alive and unharmed - having been given the \"full tour\" of the other character's insides. Most full tour scenarios involve a character being swallowed whole ([[oral vore|orally ingested]]), travelling through the digestive tract, and exiting from the [[anus]]; however, \"reverse\" full tours are not unheard of, with the prey character being [[anal vore|anally ingested]], travelling through the body and exiting the mouth.\r\n\r\nA full tour image may not necessarily show the full process, in some cases, the full tour is implied by showing a character travelling through the intestines of another.\r\n\r\nh6. These are NOT Full Tour:\r\n* The prey does not come out safely (or at all), having been digested partially or entirely \r\n* The predator consumes prey, who later comes back out from the same orifice they came in\r\n* A predator consumes a prey who is then is removed from the predator's body by force, magic, or through surgery\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[Vore]]\r\n* [[Endosoma]]\r\n* [[Willing Prey]]\r\n* [[Living Insertion]]\r\n* [[Snake Impalement]] (where the prey can be seen coming out of both orifices at the same time)\r\n"
