            "count": 229,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1893530\r\n\r\nThe ability to communicate through psychic means — projecting speech, images or ideas into the mind of another person without speaking physically. Telepathy also describes the ability to [[mind reading|read minds]] — which may or may not be shown alongside communicating telepathically.\r\n\r\nThis tag can describe a character demonstrating telepathy (even in the context of a character saying they are telepathic, and reacting to what they see or hear), a character seeing imagery from the mind of another character (usually drawn inside of a thought bubble style frame) and reacting or commenting on it.\r\n\r\n\r\nh6. Ways Telepathic Dialogue Can Be Depicted\r\n\r\n* No matter the \"container\" for the dialogue, distinct colouring, translucence, or a glowing aura around the bubble/box are common shorthand for telepathic dialogue \r\n* tailless [[speech bubbles]], usually near the \"speaking\" character's head, or indicated to be the character projecting speech at another or the viewer\r\n* Distinctly drawn bubbles/boxes containing the dialogue, sometimes with tails emerging from the \"speaking\" character's head\r\n* traditional [[thought bubbles]]\r\n** the telepathic character reacting to another character's thoughts\r\n** a telepathic character \"speaking\" in thought bubbles, sometimes with a response by the other character in a speech bubble\r\n** conversations between two characters entirely within thought bubbles\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[mind control]]\r\n* [[telekinesis]]\r\n\r\n"
