            "count": 211,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #2884431 thumb #2146226 thumb #1616455 thumb #2265332\r\n\r\n[b]Imminent danger[/b] describes a situation where it's visually implied that a character (or in some cases, the viewer) is in, or will soon be in a perilous situation that will likely cause injury or harm. Some examples include: a character about to fall, asphyxiate, be infected, poisoned, attacked, burned, captured, kidnapped, tortured, crushed, eaten, or shot. Alternatively, this tag can suggest that a character is about to put unseen others (possibly including the viewer), in danger.\r\n\r\nh5. Tag Notes:\r\nThis tag is intended to fill the gaps between other `imminent_*` tags that suggest more specific forms of harm - where the exact nature of what's coming is either vague, could be threatening in multiple ways, have an outcome that is unknown, or is too specific to justify its own tag. Imminent danger can potentially be used with any of the [i]Related Tags[/i] below, if there's an overall implication that leans towards a specific danger, or if the outcome is depicted in a followup scene. If what's about to happen is overwhelmingly clear, using the relevant `imminent_*` tag is more appropriate.\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n* [[imminent death]]\r\n* [[imminent pain]]\r\n* [[imminent rape]]\r\n** [[imminent tentacle rape]]\r\n* [[imminent vore]]"
