              "count": 281271,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #676207 thumb #674612 thumb #671766\n\nA [b]speech bubble[/b] is a text container used to show the [[dialogue]] of one or more characters. The name is derived from the oval shape that most speech bubbles resemble, but speech bubbles can come in many shapes. A speech bubble usually will contain a narrow section extending from the container known as the [i]tail[/i] of the speech bubble that indicates where the dialogue is coming from. A speech bubble can also contain [[pictographics]], [[grawlixes]] or be empty (to denote speechlessness, for example).\n\nNote: This should not be tagged for [[text message]] containers even if they resemble a speech bubble. Use [[message box]] instead.\n\nh4. Not to be confused with\n\n* [[text_box]]\n\nh4. Identifying forms\n\nDue to the wide number of shapes that a speech bubble can take, not all forms may fit nicely within a subgroup. It is fine to leave untagged if it doesn't seem to fall into one of the subgroups.\n\nHybrid forms may exist that modify how we approach tagging. Any form can be linked together, or contain dotted borders; a polygonal form may sometimes appear pointy. A speech bubble can fall into multiple subgroups, and the subgroup tags may be added as needed.\n\nA speech bubble that lacks a consistent form such as those that keep alternating between flat, and curved edges, or the length of the edges keeps changing is considered an [[irregular speech bubble]].\n\nFor tagging purposes, a [[pointy speech bubble]] should not be considered part of the polygonal group, because of the points. \n\nh5. Handling other text containers\n\nForm tags exist for each type of text container ([[text_box]], [[thought_bubble]]). Replace `_speech_bubble` with the text container tag name (e.g. [[polygonal_thought_bubble]]) to find the proper tag for that container. Please do not use speech bubble tags for other text containers. \n\nh4. Form examples\n\n[table]\n[tbody][tr][td]\nthumb #4019646\n[/td][td]\nthumb #3415860\n[/td][td]\nthumb #2094672\n[/td][td]\nthumb #2618936\n[/td][td]\nthumb #3089004\n[/td][/tr][/tbody]\n[tbody]\n[tr][td]Standard[/td][td][[Linked Speech Bubble]][/td][td][[Conjoined Speech Bubble]][/td][td][[Pointy Speech Bubble]][/td][td][[Polygonal Speech Bubble]][/td][/tr]\n[/tbody]\n[tbody][tr][td]\nthumb #2986338\n[/td][td]\nthumb #2528760\n[/td][td]\nthumb #2541371\n[/td][td]\nthumb #3448131\n[/td][td]\nthumb #2480778\n[/td][/tr][/tbody]\n[tbody]\n[tr][td][[Wavy Speech Bubble]][/td][td][[Puffy Speech Bubble]][/td][td][[Irregular Speech Bubble]][/td][td][[Inward Tail Speech Bubble]][/td][td][[Partial Line Speech Bubble]][/td][/tr]\n[/tbody]\n[tbody][tr][td]\nthumb #1374983\n[/td][td]\nthumb #3641006\n[/td][td]\nthumb #3057222\n[/td][td]\nthumb #1552572\n[/td][td]\nthumb #1564614\n[/td][/tr][/tbody]\n[tbody]\n[tr][td][[Dotted Line Speech Bubble]][/td][td][[Outline Speech Bubble]][/td][td][[Heart Speech Bubble]][/td][td][[Color Coded Speech Bubble]][/td][td][[Dripping Speech Bubble]][/td][/tr]\n[/tbody]\n[/table]\n\nh4. Speech bubble forms\n\n* [[conjoined_speech_bubble]] - Two bubbles fused together\n* [[linked_speech_bubble]] - Two bubbles linked by a chain\n* [[pointy_speech_bubble]] - A bubble that is exploded outward into pointed spikes, commonly used for raised voices / [[yelling]].\n* [[polygonal_speech_bubble]] - A bubble with only flat sides\n\nh5. Uncommon\n\n* [[dotted_line_speech_bubble]]\n* [[inward_tail_speech_bubble]]\n* [[irregular_speech_bubble]]\n* [[outline_speech_bubble]]\n* [[partial_line_speech_bubble]] - This is like a partial speech bubble, but has a body.\n* [[puffy_speech_bubble]]\n* shape speech bubble\n** [[heart_speech_bubble]]\n* [[wavy_speech_bubble]]\n\nh5. Partial speech containers\n\n* [[partial_speech_bubble]] - Depending on how complete it is, this may not count as an actual speech bubble.\n\nh4. Speech bubble properties\n\n* [[empty_speech_bubble]]\n\nh5. Appearance\n\n* [[color_coded_speech_bubble]]\n* [[dripping_speech_bubble]]\n* [[speech_bubble_drop_shadow]]\n\nh5. Colors\n\n- TODO: add\n\nh4. Other speech indicators\n\n* [[speech_marker]] - Used when there is a line of some kind that indicates that dialogue is by a certain speaker, but the dialogue text is not enclosed by any sort of speech bubble (either fully or partially).\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[tag_group:narrative_elements]]\n\n* [[dialogue]]\n* [[inner_monologue]]\n* [[thought_bubble]]"
