an't go further into the pred's throat due to an object making the neck too narrow.\n\n\n* [[Cooking with furs]] - A character is cooked, butchered, or prepared as food, while this tag names \"furs\", this tag applies to any form or species \n** Note: This tag does not inherently involve vore, [u]a post should [b]only [/b]be tagged as vore if the cooked character is actively shown being consumed[/u] (usually as hard vore).\n\nh5. Progression Tags\n\n* [[Imminent Vore]] (do not imply vore) - An image or animation that implies a character (or the viewer) is about to be consumed by another character.\n* [[Partially Inside]] - When a character is partially in another character's body as part of a vore action. [i](Subject to rename to [[Prey Partially Inside]] for clarity reason : https://e621.net/forum_topics/37564 )[/i]\n** [[Almost Fully Inside]] - When a character is almost completely in another character.\n* [[Fully Inside]] - When a character is completely inside another character.\n* [[After Vore]] - An image that depicts the aftermath of a character being completely digested/absorbed or safely released.\n\nSee [b]Prey Location[/b] bellow for more descriptive tags.\n\nh5. Safe Vore Tags\n\nThese tags describe vore scenarios where the prey is consumed (often willingly) and is not digested or otherwise harmed\n* [[Endosoma]] - The prey lives safely and indefinitely within the pred's body, the character isn't implied or shown to be leaving the pred's body\n* [[Full Tour]] - The prey is ingested or inserted at one end of the digestive tract, and travels through to the other end unharmed\n* [[Regurgitation]] - The prey is swallowed, and then \"spat back up\" unharmed, from the same orifice. Not [i]inherently[/i] a vore tag, but often is used for vore.\n\nh5. Tags describing who or what is being consumed:\n\n* [[Multiple Prey]] - When more than one character is consumed, or implied to be consumed\n** [[Mass Vore]] - The pred consumes a very large number of prey at once 