              "wiki_body": "[b]After Vore[/b] broadly describes the \"final\" results of a [[vore]] scenario - this includes content where the prey character is clearly no longer alive within the predator's body, where the predator has completely [[digestion|digested]] or [[absorption_vore|absorbed]] the prey character, or, alternatively, scenarios where the prey has been safely released from the predator's body. This tag also covers the consequences that the prey's ingestion and digestion has had on the predator character's body. \r\n\r\nAs \"After Vore\" covers a wide variety of scenarios, this tag may be implied by visual evidence, shown as part of a sequence, comic or animation, or explicitly stated in dialogue (usually featured alongside visual clues).\r\n\r\n[quote]\r\n\r\nh4. [color=yellow]Important Note:[/color]\r\nThis tag should [b][u]NEVER[/u][/b] be used for scenarios where the prey character is indirectly shown to be still alive (speaking while inside the predator's body, struggling bulges), or in cases where their status is unknown; `after_vore` should [i][b]especially [/b][/i]not be tagged when an [[internal]] depicts the prey character alive and intact while inside the predator. \r\n\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Examples of After Vore\r\n\r\n[b]Below are various ways \"after vore\" is depicted, with subsections for different themes. [u]Several of these elements can be (and often are) combined into a single post:[/u][/b]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=General Elements]\r\nthumb #1869316 thumb #2551374 thumb #1996684 thumb #3116007 thumb #2574421\r\n\r\nThese are various indirect and direct signs indicating that the vore scenario has entered the \"after vore stage\"\r\n\r\n\r\n* [b]External Views[/b]\r\n** A character with a rounded and/or smooth [[bloated]] belly, with dialogue and/or visual evidence (see below) indirectly showing or implying that the bloating is the result of the character having ingested a living creature or character of the same or similar size and is in the later stages of digesting them. A character with a bloated belly, and no evidence to indicate vore, even with [[rumbling stomach|digestion noises]], shouldn't be tagged as `after_vore`.\r\n** A comic, sequence or animation may show the predator's belly shrinking in size over time after consuming another character; the belly will also show no evidence of bulges or struggling\r\n*** the digestive process may be implied to take place over a period of time, or may occur unnaturally fast or even instantaneously, as seen with [[rapid digestion]]\r\n** Skeletal [[imprint|imprints]] appearing through the surface of the predator's belly, showing that the prey has been reduced to bones\r\n\r\n__________________________________________________\r\n\r\n* [b]Internal Views[/b]\r\n** An [[internal]] depicting the prey's digested remains, clothing or belongings within the predator's [[stomach]], [[intestines]] or other organs\r\n** An internal showing a stomach and/or intestines filled with [[chyme]] (unidentifiable digested mush), or is completely empty at the end of a sequence \r\n*** In [[cock vore]] and [[unbirthing]] this will similarly be seen in an internal of the testes or womb with the prey reduced to [[cum]] \r\n\r\n__________________________________________________\r\n\r\n* [b]Symbols[/b]\r\n** A [[skull]] symbol or [[skull and crossbones]] near the predator's body, or in a speech bubble pointing towards the predator's body\r\n** An image of the prey's face with [[x eyes]] near to the predator's body, or in a speech bubble pointing towards the predator's body\r\n*** These symbols may be \"belched up\" in a [[burp cloud]] or depicted alongside the written sound effects for the burp\r\n** An empty [[health bar]] or other status indicator decreasing to 0; alternatively a \"digestion status\" indicator reaching 100%, either of which indicating the death and/or digestion of the prey\r\n** The prey character depicted as a [[ghost]], either literally (becoming a [[spirit]] upon death) or symbolically (a ghost pictogram resembling the prey)\r\n\r\n__________________________________________________\r\n\r\n* [b][[Burping Up Objects]]/[[Burping Up Clothes]][/b]\r\nA character is shown belching up clothing, personal items, hair, bones, or feathers; this is frequently used in combination with other aspects of \"after vore\", images that involve a character burping up clothing or items should only be tagged as after vore if there is no explicit evidence that the prey character is still alive.\r\n\r\n__________________________________________________\r\n\r\n* [b]Indirect visual evidence implying an \"after vore scenario\" can include...[/b]\r\n\r\n** [[discarded clothing]]\r\n** [[discarded_object|discarded objects]]\r\n** [[discarded bones]]\r\n\r\n** [[burping]] or [[fart|farting]]\r\n** digestive [[onomatopoeia]] - [[rumbling stomach]] and [[digestion noises]]\r\n*** [i]these elements alone don't warrant the `after_vore` tag unless paired with more obvious indications that an image is taking place \"post-vore\"[/i]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Changes to Predator]\r\nthumb #2976563 thumb #2451223 thumb #2791990 thumb #2168640\r\n\r\nh6. Common Changes:\r\n\r\n* [b][[Weight Gain]][/b] \r\n[i]A character gains a noticeable amount of weight to their entire body after digesting or absorbing another.[/i]\r\n** [[Sentient Fat]] - The prey character retains consciousness as fat on the predator's body.\r\n\r\n* [b][[Expansion]][/b]\r\n[i]After digesting their prey, the predator character gains a especially large amount of mass to one or more [b]specific[/b] body parts, this can sometimes be seen alongside more general weight gain.[/i]\r\n** [[Butt Expansion]] - The prey's digested mass is added mostly, or entirely to the pred's buttocks, the most commonly seen post-vore expansion.\r\n** [[Breast Expansion]] - Can describe a character's breasts exclusively growing (sometimes to [[hyper breasts|hyper]] size), or a character gaining weight with a large amount to their breasts.\r\n** [[Balls Expansion]] - The prey is digested/absorbed, and their mass is added to the pred's testicles. Rarely seen outside of [[cock vore]].\r\n\r\n__________________________________________________\r\n\r\nh6. Less Common:\r\n\r\n* [b][[Growth]][/b]\r\n[i]The character grows in height, instead of in weight, after digesting or absorbing another character; this is most commonly seen in sequences with [[macro]] characters[/i]\r\n\r\n* [b][[Transformation]][/b] \r\n[i]A character takes on physical traits or abilities of their prey after digesting/absorbing/releasing them, sometimes referred to as \"Trait Absorption\".[/i]\r\n** [[Gender Transformation]] - A character takes on traits of the opposite sex, often the sex of the digested prey character.\r\n** [[Species Transformation]] - A character takes on the species of the prey character after digesting them.\r\n\r\n* [b][[Tattooification]] [/b]\r\n[i]Sometimes known as Tattoo Transformation; a character is digested or absorbed, and their face, body, or a symbol representing them, appears somewhere on the predator's body.[/i]\r\n* Usually paired with weight gain or expansion, can also be a part of the prey becoming sentient fat.\r\n\r\n* [b][[Possession]][/b]\r\n[i]The prey character's mind or spirit possesses the body of the character who consumed them[/i]\r\n** This can involve physical transformation of the pred to more resemble the prey\r\n** This can be the goal of [[willing vore]], with the prey forcing themselves into an unwilling pred, and taking over their body\r\n** This can relate to [[sentient fat]], with the prey's mind/spirit as a \"passenger\" in the predator's body, with the pred retaining partial or full control of their body\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Safe Vore]\r\nthumb #1621068 thumb #2351798 thumb #2338455\r\n* [[Full Tour]] - A character travels through the predator's body and is shown to be released unharmed.\r\n* [[Regurgitation]] - The prey character is \"spat up\" alive and intact after being ingested\r\n* The prey character is defecated whole and alive after being anally inserted\r\n* The prey character is ejaculated whole and alive after being unbirthed or inserted into the penis/balls\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section=Excretion]\r\nthumb #3074728 thumb #2627788 thumb #3115646 \r\n\r\n* [b][[Disposal]][/b]\r\n[i]The predator defecates the prey's remains from their [[anus]]. This may be merely implied by dialogue or non-graphically shown with a character using a toilet, or can explicitly depict [[pooping|defecation]] with [[feces]].[/i]\r\n** [[Bones in Feces]] - Fecal matter with bones embedded in it; even with without a scene of the character actually consuming another, if they are excreting feces with bones in them, the post should be tagged as [i]after vore[/i]\r\n** [[Diaper Disposal]] - The predator excretes the prey or the prey's remains into a [[diaper]]\r\n** The disposal tag can also be applied to the pred excreting clean bones, with no fecal matter\r\n\r\n__________________________________________________\r\n\r\n* [b][[Cum Vore]]/[[Cum Transformation]]/[[Pussy Juice Vore]][/b] \r\n[i]A character is transformed/digested by [[cum]] or vaginal secretions as the result of [[cock vore]] or [[unbirthing]][/i]\r\n** [[Condom Disposal]] - The cum resulting from a digested character is ejaculated into a condom\r\n\r\n__________________________________________________\r\n\r\nh6. Other Methods of Excretion:\r\n\r\n* [[Fart|Farting]] - The prey has been digested, has completely converted into gas, and expelled anally\r\n** Alternatively, the predator farting may indicate imminent or future disposal.\r\n* [[Vomit]] - The prey's partially or mostly digested remains, along with other contents of the stomach, are forcefully expelled from the mouth, usually as a result of sickness\r\n* Regurgitation (Fatal) - A character spits up a hairball, [[pellet]], objects and/or bones, belonging to the digested prey, not to be confused with vomiting or burping up objects\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[before and after]] - many after vore images are two part sequences, featuring a \"before\" and \"after\" \r\n* [[imminent vore]] - the opposite of after vore\r\n* [[digestion]] - the process leading to, and the latter parts of which are included as, after vore\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[vore]]\r\n* [[after sex]]\r\n* [[after transformation]]"
