              "count": 1379,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #2241408 thumb #2169656 thumb #3256086 thumb #1358252 thumb #3217321\r\n\r\n[b]Mass Vore[/b] describes when a single character consumes [i]a [b]large [/b]number[/i] of people or creatures - beyond what would only be tagged as [[multiple prey]].\r\n\r\nIf the prey are visible in an [[internal]] or are shown prior to/while being consumed, mass vore posts should be tagged as [[group]], possibly [[large group]] and/or [[crowd]]. \r\n\r\n[quote]h6. What counts as [i]mass[/i] vore?\r\n\r\n* This tag is best applied when the number of prey is not easily countable at a glance, if they're fully visible at all\r\n** 6-7 [i]distinct[/i] characters can be a loose, arbitrary lower limit (distinct meaning clearly visible in an [[internal]] or as [[body outline|body outlines]])\r\n\r\n* In [i]most [/i]posts involving mass vore, the total number of prey is ambiguous, even if individual [[body outlines]] or prey characters are depicted. \r\n** The large number of prey can be implied by the pred's massively bloated [[hyper belly]], along with a large number of vague bulges\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\n[section=How Mass Vore Can Be Depicted:]\r\n\r\n* [b]General[/b]\r\n** An [[internal]] view of the character's [[stomach]] depicting a large group of characters; in vore with macro or micro characters, this often involves a crowd of [[anonymous character|anonymous characters]].\r\n*** This can also apply to an internal showing masses of [[bones in stomach|bones and/or skeletons in their stomach]].\r\n** Dialogue implying or explicitly stating the character has consumed a mass number of people, with visual evidence to back it up (e.g. extreme weight gain, hyper belly, macro with a bloated belly).\r\n** A tally or counter of how many people one character has consumed.\r\n** A scene of a comic, animation, or sequence may first show an indistinct crowd of characters, with individuals being actively consumed by the pred, followed by a second scene, with the crowd gone, and the pred having a hyper belly\r\n\r\n* [b]Same Size Vore/Minor Size Differences[/b]\r\n** A character having a [[hyper belly]] that is clearly far larger than a single person, this usually includes multiple indistinct bulges implying prey.\r\n** A character with big belly that features a large number of imprints or distinct [[body outline|body outlines]] pushing through its surface.\r\n** Implied in an [[after vore]] image by dialogue or other visual clues (such as weight gain, discarded clothing, bones of prey etc.) - a character sitting in an empty room, massively overweight, surrounded by saliva covered clothes would imply mass vore.\r\n\r\n* [b][[Macro]] preds or [[micro]] prey:[/b]\r\n** A character licking up or dropping masses of tiny characters into their mouth, shown having several people in their mouth, or masses of prey being swallowed down their throat.\r\n** A character with a bloated belly - shown via internal, stomach noises, imprints/body outlines, speech bubbles coming from their belly, etc. - to have eaten many smaller prey.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[b]Note: The above applies to all non-oral varieties of vore, but involving the orifices or organs that are a part of that type of vore (eg. mass [[unbirthing]] with an internal of the pred's [[uterus]]). [/b]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[group]] - scenes with more than three characters\r\n** [[large group]] - scenes with at least 10 fully detailed characters interacting\r\n** [[crowd]] - an uncountable number of characters gathered in one scene\r\n* [[hyper belly]]\r\n* [[macro]] - larger than \"normal sized\" characters\r\n** [[macro pred]]\r\n* [[micro]] - smaller than \"normal sized\" characters\r\n** [[micro prey]]\r\n* [[multiple prey]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[vore]]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n"
