              "wiki_body": "thumb #2332589\r\n\r\n[b]Hard Vore[/b] refers to any image depicting a character being eaten alive \"in pieces\" by another character - which can mean being torn apart or having pieces bitten off - or chewed up if the predator is larger than the prey. Some images featuring hard vore involve the prey character being butchered and/or cooked before consumption, these images should be also be tagged as [[cooking with furs]]. \r\n\r\n[b]Hard Vore should always be tagged as [[e621:ratings|Explicit]].[/b]\r\n\r\n\r\n[b]Important Note:[/b] [i]While most, if not all depictions of Hard Vore are also inherently [[oral_vore|Oral Vore]], it's uncommon to have both tags on a single image.[/i] Some examples of exceptions to this general rule would be if a prey character is swallowed after being chewed \"in one piece\" by a much larger predator character, or if the prey character is swallowed whole after sustaining an injury from being bitten or having pieces torn off of them and eaten.\r\n\r\nCompare with [[soft_vore|Soft Vore]] which involves the character being swallowed whole and alive, without [i]any[/i] injuries from biting or chewing.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[gore]]\r\n** [[mutilation]]\r\n** [[dismemberment]]\r\n** [[disembowelment]]\r\n* [[blood]]\r\n* [[death]]\r\n** [[snuff]]\r\n** [[imminent_death|imminent death]]\r\n* [[cannibalism]]\r\n* [[cooking with furs]] \r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[Vore]]\r\n** [[anal_vore|Anal Vore]]\r\n** [[cock_vore|Cock Vore]]\r\n** [[oral_vore|Oral Vore]]\r\n** [[Unbirthing]] - Vaginal vore\r\n** [[Soft Vore]] / [b]Hard Vore[/b]\r\n* Safe Vore\r\n** [[Endosoma]]\r\n** [[Full_tour|Full Tour]]"
