              "wiki_body": "thumb #4683791 thumb #4109341 thumb #3789856 thumb #3554264 thumb #2385281\r\n\r\n[b]Classic Lolita[/b] is one of the three main substyles of Lolita fashion. It is highly inspired by historical fashion, particularly of the [[Victorian]] era. It focuses on elegance and maturity, aiming for the appearance of a dignified noble lady.\r\n\r\n[quote]h5. Common elements\r\n* Longer, \"a-line\" shaped skirts and dresses\r\n* Underskirts used to lengthen the appearance of a skirt\r\n* Solid colors, [[floral]] patterns and [[stripes]]\r\n* Pintucks, ruffles, and other sewn details\r\n* Motifs of [[crown]]s, [[fleur-de-lis]], crests, antiques, architecture, and [[formal art]]\r\n** Animal and [[fruit]] themes are also used, but have a more realistic and \"antique\" look than the prints used in Sweet Lolita\r\n* [[High heels]], Victorian-style [[boots]]\r\n* [[Curled hair]]\r\n* [[Parasol]]s and [[umbrella]]s\r\n* [[Jewelry]]\r\n* Natural makeup\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\nh4. External links\r\n* https://lolitafashion.fandom.com/wiki/Classic_Lolita\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n* [[victorian]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n[section=Lolita]\r\n* [[lolita_(fashion)]]\r\n** [[casual_lolita]]\r\n** [b]classic_lolita[/b]\r\n** [[cosplay_lolita]]\r\n** [[country_lolita]]\r\n** [[cyber_lolita]]\r\n** [[deco_lolita]]\r\n** [[ero_lolita]]\r\n** [[gothic_lolita]]\r\n** [[guro_lolita]]\r\n** [[hime_lolita]]\r\n** [[kuro_lolita]]\r\n** [[military_lolita]]\r\n** [[nurse_lolita]]\r\n** [[pirate_lolita]]\r\n** [[punk_lolita]]\r\n** [[qi_lolita]]\r\n** [[sailor_lolita]]\r\n** [[shiro_lolita]]\r\n** [[steampunk_lolita]]\r\n** [[sweet_lolita]]\r\n** [[wa_lolita]]\r\n[/section]"
