            "wiki_body": "[b]Extreme size difference[/b] describes when there is a [b][i]very[/i] large difference in scale[/b] between two or more characters or creatures. \r\n\r\nThis typically applies to scenes featuring a [[macro]] OR [[micro]] sized character interacting with, or being depicted alongside characters who are [i]normal sized[/i]. Less commonly, this tag describes two creatures of naturally extreme difference in size interacting or being compared – such as a feral rat and feral elephant, or arguably, a feral dragon and human or anthro character (as they are generally depicted as being very large animals). \r\n\r\nh5. Tagging Notes\r\n[quote]\r\n[b]IMPORTANT NOTE:[/b]\r\n* Do NOT tag an extreme size difference post with both `macro` AND `micro` tags [sup]with rare exceptions[/sup]\r\n** If there is no background, scenery, or objects to suggest that the larger character is [[macro]]-sized, it should be assumed that the smaller character is [[micro]] sized.\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\n* Extreme size difference posts should ideally always be tagged with:\r\n**  `larger_[sex]` `smaller_[sex]` (e.g. [[larger male]], [[smaller female]] etc.)\r\n**  `larger_[form]`, `smaller_[form]` (e.g. [[larger anthro]], [[smaller humanoid]] etc.)\r\n** optionally, tags for `macro_[sex/form]` or `micro_[sex/form]` can be applied\r\n\r\n* If there is only a macro or micro character within the scene, and no smaller or larger characters visible, the post should not be tagged with `extreme_size_difference`\r\n\r\nh4. Extreme Size Difference Interactions\r\n\r\n* [[holding character]]\r\n* [[between breasts]]\r\n* [[between cheeks]]\r\n* [[between feet]]\r\n* [[in mouth]]\r\n** [[holding mouth open]]\r\n** [[on tongue]]\r\n* [[underfoot]]\r\n* [[trapped in clothing]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[size difference]] \r\n* [[size play]]"
          }
