            "wiki_body": "h5. Pupils\r\n\r\n* [i](anatomy)[/i] A black hole located in the center of the eye that allows light to strike the retina.\r\n\r\n[i](Informal)[/i] In created work, the pupil of an eye may inherit accents of color. This visual effect can be based on stylistic means, fictional  phenomena; or natural occurrences such as [[glistening_eyes|eyeshine]].\r\n\r\n* [i][[pupil_(education)|Referring to education]][/i]\r\n\r\nh4. Colors\r\n\r\n* [[amber_pupils]]\r\n* [[black_pupils]]\r\n* [[blue_pupils]]\r\n* [[cyan_pupils]]\r\n* [[brown_pupils]]\r\n* [[green_pupils]]\r\n* [[grey_pupils]]\r\n* [[orange_pupils]]\r\n* [[pink_pupils]]\r\n* [[purple_pupils]]\r\n* [[red_pupils]]\r\n* [[tan_pupils]]\r\n* [[teal_pupils]]\r\n* [[white_pupils]]\r\n* [[yellow_pupils]]\r\n\r\nh4. Other\r\n\r\n* [[big_pupils]]\r\n* [[horizontal_pupils]]\r\n* [[no_pupils]]\r\n* [[slit_pupils]]\r\n* [[small_pupils]]\r\n* [[unusual_pupils]]\r\n** [[symbol-shaped_pupils]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related anatomy\r\n\r\n* [[eyes]]\r\n* [[iris]]\r\n* [[sclera]]\r\n\r\nh4. External links\r\n\r\n* \"Pupil [i](anatomy)[/i] on Wikipedia\":https://wikipedia.org/wiki/Pupil"
