            "wiki_body": "thumb #2837422 thumb #2482361 thumb #3170848 thumb #1762544\r\n\r\n[b]Spandex shorts[/b] (also known as [i]compression shorts, cycling shorts, bike shorts[/i], or [i]spats[/i]) are  tight, stretchy, pocketless [[shorts]] that, as the name suggests, are made of spandex (or a mix of spandex and polyester). \r\n\r\nSpandex shorts are typically worn while [[cycling]], weightlifting, doing [[yoga]] or other [[exercise]], and commonly seen around gyms, but they may be worn casually as well. While spandex shorts are most often worn by women, they are unisex [[bottomwear]], men can be seen wearing them as well. \r\n\r\nSpandex shorts are usually matte black in reality - or another flat dark/neutral colour - but are frequently depicted as shiny in artwork. Most spandex shorts are \"boy cut\", with coverage similar to [[boxer briefs]], however, they can come in a variety of leg lengths, ranging from a length comparable with [[hotpants]], to coming down to just above the wearer's knees.\r\n\r\n\r\nh5. Related Tags\r\n* [[athletic_wear]]\r\n* [[shorts]]\r\n** [[hotpants]]\r\n* [[spandex]]\r\n* [[tight_clothing]]\r\n\r\nh5. See Also\r\n* [[gym_shorts]]\r\n* [[leggings]]"
