            "count": 109487,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #118882 thumb #2118534\r\n\r\n[b]Electronics[/b] refers to any kind of electronic equipment, especially those that are sold commercially, and typically used in the household. This is a broad subject, and is primarily useful to describe home entertainment equipment such as [[television|televisions]], VCR / DVD / Blu-ray players and recording equipment, radios, and digital clocks. Although not as useful for this tag devices such as [[computer|computers]], and [[phone|phones]] are categorized as electronics.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n* [[computer]]\r\n** [[laptop]] - A portable computer with own battery, built in screen and (unlike a [[tablet]]), built in keyboard. \r\n** [[server]] - A computer which allows client computer(s) to access resources and/or services. Example, a web server providing clients with access to resources such as images. Commonly confused with [[waiter]]\r\n*** [[server_room]]\r\n** Major companies currently or previously producing computing and server hardware, mainframes\r\n*** [[atari]]\r\n*** [[sun_microsystems]]\r\n*** [[ibm]]\r\n** Internal computer components\r\n*** [[graphics_card]]\r\n*** [[processor]]\r\n*** [[power_supply]]\r\n** [[drawing_tablet]] - Computer (or laptop or other similar device) connected peripheral device for high precision pen input, with or without a screen. Also called \"digitizer\" and \"graphics tablet\". Not to be confused with a [[tablet]]\r\n* [[television]]\r\n* [[game_console]] - Gaming hardware in general, with more specific tags listed there\r\n** [[tag_group:video_games]]\r\n** [[game_controller]]\r\n** [[game_cartridge]]\r\n* [[tablet]] - A portable computing device, usually either with a touchscreen or pen input, without own built-in keyboard (unlike a [[laptop]])\r\n* [[phone]]\r\n** [[rotary_phone]]\r\n** [[wired_phone]] - A stationary phone with a base and a wired received or handset\r\n** [[flip_phone]]\r\n** [[cellphone]] - Portable (mobile) phone, not necessarily with a big amount of features\r\n** [[smartphone]] - Modern variation with more features and a big touchscreen\r\n** [[payphone]] - Public and usually paid landline phone\r\n*** [[phone_booth]] - Some payphones are located in a door-less or fully enclosed booth\r\n* [[digital_clock]]\r\n* [[radio]]\r\n** [[boombox]]\r\n* [[jukebox]]\r\n* [[portable_music_player]] - A standalone device for playing music, usually from internal or removable storage (like a [[cassette_tape]] or [[cd]]). Most variations are called \"MP3 player\"\r\n** [[music_player]] - Another tag in use?\r\n** [[listening_to_music]] - Most likely thing to be going on\r\n* [[dvd_player]]\r\n** [[dvd]]\r\n* [[cd_player]]\r\n** [[cd]]\r\n* [[record_player]] - A device for playing vinyl records in general\r\n** [[gramophone]] - Most are electronic, even though some old variants are not\r\n** [[turntable_(record_player)]]\r\n** [[vinyl_record]]\r\n* [[usb]] - A connector and cable standard for electronic devices\r\n** [[usb_drive]] - Removable storage device\r\n* [[wire]]"
