              "count": 392,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #2321124 thumb #4576875 thumb #3863655\r\n\r\nA style of [[Gyaru]] that incorporates [[Japanese school uniform]]s. For obvious reasons, the style is primarily worn by high school students, though not exclusively. \r\n\r\nTypical Gyaru accessories are worn alongside the school uniform, and [[loose socks]] are also a common element. Kogals often wear [[miniskirt]]s and [[microskirt]]s, and [[platform boots]].\r\n\r\nThe kogal subculture is based in a rejection of the traditionalist and nationalist views common in Japan, with kogals engaging in \"mindless consumerism\" through things like buying expensive (or knock-off) designer clothing, partying, going to photo booths, and more.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[tag group:fashion]]"
            }
          ],
