          "onee_gyaru": [
            {
              "tag": "onee_gyaru",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 183,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #2338074 thumb #4028876 thumb #2972209 thumb #3354088 thumb #4039834\r\n\r\n[b]Onee Gyaru[/b], literally \"big sister gyaru\", is a substyle of [[Gyaru]] more commonly worn by women in their 20s and 30s, putting a classier spin on typical Gyaru fashion. Onee Gyaru is focused on maturity and sexiness, and emphasizes brand clothing. [[Leopard print]] is still common, but in general the style is much more toned down.\r\n\r\nCommon elements of the style include [[sunglasses]], use of pinks/purples/blacks/gold, [[curled hair]] (or wavy) in blonde and light brown, [[thigh boots]], fluffy/fuzzy clothing, and [[leather]] and [[latex]]. Typical gyaru staples such as [[animal print]], [[loose socks]] and [[miniskirt]]s are still common, though the style is typically much more subtle.\r\n\r\nDue to its subtlety, it is one of the blurrier substyles, being harder to pinpoint. It may sometimes overlap with [[amekaji]] and/or [[tsuyome]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[tag group:fashion]]"
            }
          ],
