            "wiki_body": "[b]Antennae[/b] (singular: [b]antenna[/b]), sometimes referred to as \"feelers\", are a pair of sensing appendages seen in [[arthropod|arthropods]]. In popular media, they're also seen on various fictional creatures, most often [[alien|aliens]].\r\n\r\nConnected to their heads, antennae can vary drastically between species, though they all are made of one or more jointed segments. While generally used for sensing, this \"sensing\" and what it's used for can vary, and some often have other purposes as well. Social arthropods such as [[hymenopteran|Hymenopterans]] often use them for detecting other members of their group.\r\n\r\nFor wire used for sending and receiving signals, use [[antenna_wire]] instead.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:feral_anatomy]]\r\n* [[alien]]\r\n* [[arthropod]]\r\n* [[fake_antennae]]"
