      "tools": {
        "_Self (tools)": [
          {
            "tag": "tools",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 24908,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1335907 thumb #729109 thumb #225637\r\n\r\nThis tag is used when a post contains objects such as [[hammer|hammers]], [[wrench|wrenches]], [[screwdriver|screwdrivers]], etc.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with:\r\n* [[e621:tools]]\r\n\r\nh4. Types:\r\n\r\n* [[axe]]\r\n* [[chisel]]\r\n* [[hammer]]\r\n* [[hoe]]\r\n* [[pitchfork]]\r\n* [[pliers]]\r\n* [[power_tool]]\r\n** [[chainsaw]]\r\n** [[jackhammer]]\r\n* [[rake]]\r\n* [[saw]]\r\n* [[screwdriver]]\r\n* [[shovel]]\r\n* [[wrench]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related:\r\n\r\n* [[holding_tool]]\r\n* [[planted_tool]]\r\n* [[tool_belt]]\r\n* [[toolbox]]"
          }
        ],
        "cutlery": {
          "_Self (cutlery)": [
            {
              "tag": "cutlery",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 6628,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #3115184 thumb #3138986 thumb #2419196\r\n\r\n[b]Cutlery[/b] is the utensil used for eating during a meal. There are several types of cutlery, the most well-known are the [[knife]], the [[fork]], and the [[spoon]].\r\n\r\n* Tag a post when you see at least one cutlery like in the examples.\r\n\r\nh4.Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[knife]]\r\n** [[holding_knife]]\r\n* [[fork]]\r\n** [[holding_fork]]\r\n* [[spoon]]\r\n** [[holding_spoon]]\r\n* [[food]]\r\n** [[eating]]"
            }
          ],
          "spoon": [
            {
              "tag": "spoon",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 3286,
              "wiki_body": "A utensil that is used for eating soft foods such as soups, ice cream, jello, etc. It was also used for cooking food."
            }
          ],
          "fork": [
            {
              "tag": "fork",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 2968,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #1014029 thumb #162759 thumb #903167\r\n\r\nUtensil commonly composed of plastic, metal and/or wood, constituted of a rod with two to four parallel tips (prongs) in one of its extremities. It is a flatware used for piercing food and take it to the mouth, as well as holding it to make easier to cut.\r\n\r\nSome melee weapons and other tools have the same basic format and similar usage (pierce, lift and hold). \r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n\r\n* [[pitchfork]]\r\n* [[trident]]\r\n* [[spoon]]"
            }
          ]
        },
        "hammer": {
          "_Self (hammer)": [
            {
              "tag": "hammer",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 6030,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #4269450 thumb #933081 thumb #892228\r\n\r\nA [b]hammer[/b] is a striking [[tools|tool]], meant to deliver an impact to an object. The most common uses are for driving nails, fitting parts, forging metal and breaking up objects. Hammers are often designed for a specific purpose, and vary widely in their shape and structure. The usual features are a handle and a head, with most of the weight in the head. This tool can also be used as a [[weapon]].\r\n\r\nh4.Types\r\n\r\n* [[claw_hammer]]\r\n* [[sledgehammer]]\r\n* [[warhammer]]\r\n* [[maul]]\r\n* [[poleaxe]]\r\n* [[gavel_(object)]]"
            }
          ],
          "warhammer": [
            {
              "tag": "warhammer",
              "kor": "워해머",
              "count": 206,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #3664899 thumb #3107433 thumb #1808842\r\n\r\nA mid-sized combat [[hammer]], usable with either one or two hands. It comprised of a shaft that is topped with a hammer head with a rear spike.\r\n\r\nThe [b]warhammer[/b] was generally used against [[armor|armored]] targets, with the blunt end dealing concussive damage while the spiked end was used for armor-piercing strikes or exploiting armor gaps.\r\n\r\nh5. Not to be confused with\r\n* [[warhammer_(franchise)]]\r\n** [[warhammer_fantasy]]\r\n** [[warhammer_40000]]\r\n** [[warhammer_age_of_sigmar]]\r\n* [[maul]] - Often mislabeled as a warhammer, mauls rely on its heavy weight to deal damage and is blunt on both ends.\r\n* [[pick_(weapon)]] - Similar in appearance though the key difference here is it only has the spike and no hammer head.\r\n\r\nh5. See also\r\n* [[hammer]]\r\n* [[poleaxe]] - An axe and hammer combination polearm."
            }
          ],
          "sledgehammer": [
            {
              "tag": "sledgehammer",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 166,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #5074\r\n\r\nA [b]sledgehammer[/b] is a [[tools|tool]] with a large, flat, often metal head, attached to a lever (or handle). The size of its head allows a sledgehammer to apply more force than other hammers of similar size. Along with the [[mallet]], it shares the ability to distribute force over a wide area. This is in contrast to other types of hammers, which concentrate force in a relatively small area.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[hammer]]\r\n* [[warhammer]]\r\n* [[maul]]\r\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        "wrench": [
          {
            "tag": "wrench",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 2991,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #558866 thumb #143527\r\n\r\nA [b]wrench[/b] or [b]spanner[/b] is a [[tool]] used to provide grip and mechanical advantage in applying torque to turn objects-usually rotary fasteners, such as nuts and bolts.\r\n\r\nh4. Types:\r\n\r\n* [[Adjustable wrench]]\r\n* [[Monkey wrench]]\r\n* [[Pipe wrench]]\r\n* [[Socket wrench]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[holding_wrench|Holding wrench]]\r\n* [[Tools]]"
          }
        ],
        "shovel": [
          {
            "tag": "shovel",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 1337,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #465596\r\n\r\nA [[tool]] for [[digging]], lifting, and moving bulk materials, such as soil, [[coal]], gravel, [[snow]], [[sand]], or ore. Shovels are used extensively in agriculture, construction, and gardening."
          }
        ],
        "cookware": [
          {
            "tag": "cookware",
            "kor": "조리도구",
            "count": 1320,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #4598766 thumb #4113675\r\n\r\n[b]Cookware[/b] refers to larger cooking [[tools]] used in the kitchen such as pots, pans, and [[bakeware]]. Cookware is primarily used on a [[stove]] or in an [[oven]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[cooking]]\r\n* [[container]]\r\n* [[kitchen_utensils]]"
          }
        ],
        "power_tool": {
          "_Self (power_tool)": [
            {
              "tag": "power_tool",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 954,
              "wiki_body": "A [b]power tool[/b] is a [[tools|tool]] that is actuated by an additional power source and mechanism other than the solely manual labour used with hand tools."
            }
          ],
          "chainsaw": [
            {
              "tag": "chainsaw",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 807,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #381458\r\n\r\nA [b]chainsaw[/b] is a portable, mechanical [[saw]] which cuts with a set of teeth attached to a rotating [[chain]] that runs along a guide bar. It is used in activities such as tree felling, limbing, bucking, pruning, cutting firebreaks in wildland fire suppression, and harvesting of firewood. Chainsaws with specially designed bar and chain combinations have been developed as tools for use in chainsaw art and chainsaw mills. Specialized chainsaws are used for cutting concrete. Chainsaws are sometimes used for cutting ice, for example for ice sculpture and in Finland for winter swimming. Someone who uses a saw is a sawyer.\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[tools]]"
            }
          ]
        },
        "screwdriver": [
          {
            "tag": "screwdriver",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 928,
            "wiki_body": "A [b]screwdriver[/b] is a [[tools|tool]], manual or powered, for turning (driving or removing) screws. A typical simple screwdriver has a handle and a shaft, and a tip that the user inserts into the screw head to turn it."
          }
        ],
