          {
            "tag": "frill_(anatomy)",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 18466,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1395570 thumb #267735 thumb #649291 thumb #221058\r\n\r\nAn anatomical structure most often found on lizards, dragons and other similar creatures. Often positioned at the neck and on top of the head and forms a membranous surface.\r\n\r\nHowever, while almost all are membranous, not all frills are. Specifically, bone frills generally aren't membranous and instead are hardened structures made of [[bone]].\r\n\r\nOften similar in appearance to the [[fin]] of some fishes.\r\n\r\nCommonly seen on reptilian/[[scalie]] characters and some [[pokemon|Pokémon]].\r\n\r\nh3. Frill tags\r\n\r\nh4. Body part\r\n\r\n* [[dorsal_frill]]\r\n* [[ear_frill]]\r\n* [[fin_frill]]\r\n* [[head_frill]]\r\n* [[neck_frill]] - A frill that [b]encircles[/b] the neck\r\n* [[tail_frill]]\r\n\r\nh4. Types\r\n* [[membranous_frill]]\r\n* [[bone_frill]]\r\n\r\nh4. Colors\r\n\r\n* [[blue_frill]]\r\n* [[green_frill]]\r\n* [[pink_frill]]\r\n* [[red_frill]]\r\n\r\nh4. Features\r\n\r\n* [[frill_piercing]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[fin]]\r\n* [b]frill_(anatomy)[/b]\r\n* [[membrane_(anatomy)]]\r\n** [[membranous_frill]]\r\n** [[membranous_wings]]\r\n** [[patagium]]"
          }
