      "royalty": {
        "_Self (royalty)": [
          {
            "tag": "royalty",
            "kor": "왕족",
            "count": 17923,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #14617 thumb #46407 thumb #109909 thumb #885205 thumb #3770008\r\n\r\nA royal family is the extended family of a king or queen regnant. The term imperial family appropriately describes the extended family of an emperor or empress, while the terms \"ducal family\", \"grand ducal family\" or \"princely family\" are more appropriate to describe the relatives of a reigning duke, grand duke, or prince. However, in common parlance members of any family which reigns by hereditary right are often referred to as royalty or \"royals\". It is also customary in some circles to refer to the extended relations of a deposed monarch and his or her descendants as a royal family.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n* [b]royalty[/b]\r\n** [[emperor]]\r\n** [[king]]\r\n** [[pharaoh]]\r\n** [[prince]]\r\n** [[princess]]\r\n** [[queen]]\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n* [[noble]] - Despite both nobles and royalties being of high social or political status, the latter ranks higher than the former."
          }
        ],
        "princess": [
          {
            "tag": "princess",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 7732,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #513508 thumb #2456957 thumb #231244 thumb #53788\r\n\r\nA royal title for women, commonly reserved for the daughter of a king and/or queen, or the wife of a prince. \r\n\r\nPrincess characters are very popular in storytelling, with princesses often being the protagonist (or major secondary character) of a given piece of media, this is especially common in fairy tale/fantasy settings. Princesses are typically depicted wearing long, flowing, ornate [[dress|dresses]] or gowns, and most importantly [[tiara|tiaras]] or [[crowns]] (even when drawn wearing street clothes or nude).\r\n\r\nWhile princesses [i]usually[/i] don't have the \"supreme authority\" of an emperor/empress, king or queen, a princess may be the ruling monarch of a nation — this is more common in fiction than in real life, characters such as [[Princess Peach]] or the various princesses of [[Friendship is Magic|My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic]] act as the ruling sovereigns over their respective countries, with no kings or queens above them [sub](a nation ruled by a prince or princess is actually called a [b]principality[/b], although the Mushroom Kingdom and Equestria are never referred to as such)[/sub]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nh5. Princess Characters \r\n[sup]Some popular characters in media holding the title of princess[/sup]\r\n\r\n* [[princess celestia (mlp)|Princess Celestia]] - [i]My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic[/i]\r\n* [[princess luna (mlp)|Princess Luna]] - [i]My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic[/i]\r\n* [[princess cadance (mlp)|Princess Cadance]] - [i]My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic[/i]\r\n* [[princess_twilight_sparkle_(mlp)|Twilight Sparkle]] - [i]My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic[/i] [sub](is named as \"Princess of Friendship\", and later becomes ruler of Equestria)[/sub]\r\n* [[leia_organa|Princess Leia]] - [i]Star Wars[/i]\r\n* [[Princess Zelda]] - [i]The Legend of Zelda[/i]\r\n* [[Princess Peach]] - [i]Super Mario[/i]\r\n* [[Princess Daisy]] - [i]Super Mario[/i]\r\n* [[Rosalina (mario)]] - [i]Super Mario Galaxy[/i] [sub](referred to as a princess in development/marketing material, considered one by fans, and \"dresses like one\", but isn't given the title in-game)[/sub]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nh4.See Also:\r\n* [[royalty]]\r\n** [[emperor]]\r\n** [[king]]\r\n** [[pharaoh]]\r\n** [[prince]]\r\n** princess\r\n** [[queen]]"
          }
        ],
