              "tag": "drum_set",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 430,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #996269\r\n\r\nA [b]drum kit[/b]—also called a [b]drum set[/b], [b]trap set[/b], or simply [b]drums[/b]—is a collection of [[drum|drums]] and other percussion instruments, typically [[cymbals]], which are set up on stands to be played by a single player with [[drumstick|drumsticks]] held in both hands and the feet operating pedals that control the hi-hat cymbal and the beater for the bass drum.\r\n\r\nA drum kit consists of a mix of membranophones (ie. drums) and idiophones (mostly cymbals but may include the [[woodblock]] and [[cowbell]]).\r\n\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drum_kit"
