            "count": 197,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1039112\r\n\r\n[b]Accordions[/b] are a family of box-shaped [[musical_instrument|musical instruments]] of the bellows-driven free-reed aerophone type, colloquially referred to as a squeezebox. The instrument is played by compressing or expanding the bellows while pressing buttons or keys, causing pallets to open, which allow air to flow across strips of brass or steel, called reeds. These vibrate to produce sound inside the body."
