          "playstation_controller": [
            {
              "tag": "playstation_controller",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 996,
              "wiki_body": "Broad tag for any [[video games|video]] [[game controller]] manufactured by [[Sony]] for their [[PlayStation]] brand of consoles, including the brand's famous [[DualShock]] line and the [[PlayStation Move]] for PlayStation 3 and 4.\r\n\r\nThese controllers are best identified by having four separate directional buttons in place of a D-pad, symmetrically-placed convex analog sticks on the lower part of the controller (except on the stickless [[original PlayStation Controller]]), and the brand's iconic symbols presented on their face buttons; a red circle, a pink square, a green triangle, and a blue cross that appears as an X."
            }
          ],
          "xbox_controller": {
            "_Self (xbox_controller)": [
              {
                "tag": "xbox_controller",
                "kor": "",
                "count": 565,
                "wiki_body": "A broad tag for any [[game_controller|video game controller]] manufactured by [[Microsoft]] for their [[Xbox]] brand of consoles as well as [[Microsoft Windows|Windows]] PCs, including the [[xbox_original_controller|original Xbox controllers]] (especially the first model, also known as \"The Duke\"), the [[Xbox 360 controller]], the [[Xbox Wireless Controller]] (this tag includes the [[Xbox Elite Wireless Controller]] and the later revisions of the standard controller released for the Xbox One S and X models and the [[Xbox Series X/S]]), and the [[Kinect]] motion sensor peripherals for Xbox 360 and Xbox One.\r\n\r\nXbox controllers can be identified by their multicolored [color=lightgreen]A[/color], [color=red]B[/color], [color=skyblue]X[/color], and [color=yellow]Y[/color] face buttons, asymmetrically placed analog sticks (an upper-left stick and a lower-right one), a D-pad underneath the left stick, and an Xbox logo at or near the middle, which is the \"Guide\" button on Xbox 360 and later controllers (this also includes Hyperkin's officially licensed recreation of \"The Duke\" for Xbox One, Xbox Series X|S, and Windows PCs, with the faceplate now being a Guide button with an OLED screen that features the original Xbox's boot sequence).\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n* [[xbox]]\r\n** [[xbox_console]]\r\n** [b]xbox_controller[/b]\r\n*** [[kinect]] (motion sensor for Xbox 360 and Xbox One)\r\n*** [[xbox_original_controller]] (for the first Xbox console)\r\n*** [[xbox_360_controller]]\r\n*** [[xbox_wireless_controller]] (for the Xbox One and Xbox Series X/S)\r\n**** [[xbox_elite_wireless_controller]] (premium version of the standard Wireless Controller)"
              }
            ],
            "xbox_wireless_controller": [
              {
                "tag": "xbox_wireless_controller",
                "kor": "",
                "count": 126,
                "wiki_body": "The [b]Xbox Wireless Controller[/b] the official game controller of the [[Xbox One]] and [[Xbox Series X/S]] consoles, and also commercialized for [[Microsoft Windows]] PCs. It maintains the overall layout of its predecessor, the [[Xbox 360 controller]], but with refinements to its shape, analog sticks, shoulder buttons, and triggers. It's received multiple revisions over the years. The first version of the controller was introduced in 2013 with the launch of the Xbox One.\r\n\r\n* Note that \"Wireless Controller\" is purely part of its official brand name; it can be used as a wired controller with a USB cable attached to it. The controller still gets this tag even if there is a USB cable attached to it in the post.\r\n* A wireless [[Xbox 360 controller]] does [b][i]not[/i][/b] count towards this tag, as that controller has a number of differences between that and this controller (e.g. the prominent battery casing on the back of the wireless 360 controller, which the Xbox Wireless Controller has flush with the rest of the body).\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n* [[game_controller]]\r\n** [[wireless_controller]]\r\n** [[xbox_controller]]\r\n*** [[kinect]]\r\n*** [[xbox_360_controller]]\r\n*** [[xbox_original_controller]]\r\n*** [b]xbox_wireless_controller[/b]\r\n**** [[xbox_elite_wireless_controller]]"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
