      "pastry": {
        "_Self (pastry)": [
          {
            "tag": "pastry",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 6717,
            "wiki_body": "[b]Pastry[/b] is baked [[food]] made with a dough of flour, water and shortening (solid fats, including butter or lard) that may be savoury or sweetened. Sweetened pastries are often described as [i]bakers' confectionery[/i].\r\n\r\nThe word \"pastries\" suggests many kinds of baked products made from ingredients such as flour, sugar, milk, butter, shortening, baking powder, and eggs. Small tarts and other sweet baked products are called pastries. Common pastry dishes include [[pie]]s, [[tart]]s, [[quiche]]s, [[croissant]]s and pasties.\r\n\r\n\"Pastry - From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastry"
          }
        ],
        "doughnut": [
          {
            "tag": "doughnut",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 3780,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #842474\r\n[quote]Mmmm, doughnuts. Glaaaaargh...\r\n[B]—Homer J. Simpson[/B][/quote]\r\nA [b]doughnut[/b] or [b]donut[/b] is a type of fried dough confectionery or dessert [[food]]. May or may not have a hole in it. Often confused with [[bagel]].\r\n\r\nAlthough [b]donut[/b] is also used as a playful term for a big round puffy anus, please use [[puffy_anus]] and [[big_anus]] instead.\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n* [[Dunkin' Donuts]] (today officially named just Dunkin') – American doughnut shop franchise.\r\n* [[Tim Hortons]] – Canadian doughnut shop franchise."
          }
        ],
        "pie": [
          {
            "tag": "pie",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 2139,
            "wiki_body": "[B]Pie[/B] is a foodstuff consisting of a pastry crust holding a filling. The filling may be either sweet, in the case of a [[dessert]], or a savoury, in the case of a main course."
          }
        ],
        "croissant": [
          {
            "tag": "croissant",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 233,
            "wiki_body": "A croissant is a buttery and flaky [i]viennoiserie[/i] [[pastry]] inspired by the shape of the Austrian kipferl but using the French yeast-leavened laminated [[dough]].\r\n\r\nCroissants are named for their crescent shape. The dough is layered with [[butter]], rolled and folded several times in succession, then rolled into a thin sheet, in a technique called laminating. The process results in a layered, flaky texture, similar to a puff pastry.\r\n\r\n\"Croissant - From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Croissant"
          }
        ],
        "cinnamon_bun": [
          {
            "tag": "cinnamon_bun",
            "kor": "",
            "count": 176,
            "wiki_body": "The baked pastry that's too pure for this sinful site, a [b]cinnamon bun[/b] (also called [b]cinnamon roll[/b], [b]cinnamon swirl[/b], [b]cinnamon Danish[/b], and [b]cinnamon snail[/b]) is a sweet roll made with flour, [[cinnamon]], sugar, and [[butter]] commonly served in Northern Europe and North America, the latter of which most commonly eats this as a breakfast food or a dessert. It is often served with cream cheese or icing.\r\n\r\nh4.External link:\r\n* \"Cinnamon roll on Wikipedia\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinnamon_roll"
          }
        ],
        "eclair": [
          {
            "tag": "eclair",
            "kor": "에클레어",
            "count": 102,
            "wiki_body": "thumb #1007486 thumb #154057 thumb #2780536\r\n\r\nAn [b]éclair[/b] is a type of cream-filled pastry. The traditional shape is visually similar to a narrow boston cream donut, though more sandwich-like variants exist.\r\n\r\nDue to its oblong shape and how the cream inside tends to seep from the tip, it makes for a popular type of [[suggestive food]]. The \"cream stuffing\" part is also a fairly common analogy for the the likes of [[cum inflation]]."
          }
        ]
