          "fried_chicken": [
            {
              "tag": "fried_chicken",
              "kor": "",
              "count": 164,
              "wiki_body": "thumb #197776\r\n\r\n[b]Fried chicken[/b] is [[chicken meat]] that is coated with a batter or seasoned flour and then fried.\r\n\r\nProcesses used to fry chicken include pan frying (cooked in a [[frying pan]] with some oil or fat as lubricant), deep frying (submerging the meat in a vat of hot oil), pressure frying (the meat and cooking oil are held to both high temperatures and pressure using a dedicated pressure cooker; this is the method used by [[KFC]]), and air frying (the meat is placed in convection oven that uses hot air instead of oil to fry the meat).\r\n\r\nFried chicken can be in the form of breasts, [[chicken wing|wings]], thighs, or legs.\r\n\r\nh4.See also\r\n* [[roast_chicken_leg]]"
