          "tag": "biped",
          "kor": "두 발",
          "count": 541277,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #862858 thumb #1475722 thumb #517548 thumb #1615965\r\n\r\nA character with an anatomical structure that engenders walking primarily on two legs. [[avian|Birds]], [[human|humans]], and most [[anthro|anthros]] are all common examples of this.\r\n\r\nThis tag refers to a character's anatomical structure, and [u]not[/u] their current posture; they can be lying down, sitting, standing, etc. If someone bipedal is positioned on their hands and knees, use [[all_fours]] to tag their position.\r\n\r\nNote that [[amputee|amputees]] are still counted as bipeds, even if their lower limbs have been removed.\r\n\r\nh4.See also\r\n\r\n* [[legless]]\r\n* [[uniped]]\r\n* [b]biped[/b]\r\n* [[triped]]\r\n* [[quadruped]]\r\n* [[pentaped]]\r\n* [[hexapod]]\r\n* [[septaped]]\r\n* [[octoped]]\r\n"
