          "tag": "motion_lines",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 75611,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #560749 thumb #1295564 thumb #806227\n\nLines in artwork drawn near or surrounding an object used to denote movement.\n\n[section,expanded=Examples]\n\nh4. [[Motion outline]]\n\nThe most common form of motion line. These lines appear along the contours of a character, or object.\n\nthumb #2932735 thumb #586284  thumb #2759235 thumb #2596272\n\n\nh4. [[Directed motion outline]]\n\nThe combination of a motion outline with path / direction lines. This will usually have at least one intersecting line.\n\n thumb #2048021 thumb #2820039 thumb #1722202\n\nh4. [[Path lines]]\n\nA component frequently seen in [[motion blur]], these lines show the travel path of a moving character, or object.\n\nthumb #2879438 thumb #3089944 thumb #2385364 thumb #3022055\n\nh4. [[Direction lines]]\n\nDirection lines are similar to path lines, but are actually a variant of [[speed lines]]. These lines consist of spaced or clustered groups of parallel lines set in the direction of a forceful action. These often appear along contours, and may even intersect with the contour. See also [[distorted contour]]\n\nthumb #2491159 thumb #2903562 thumb #2327575 thumb #2907498\n\n[/section]\n\nh4. Related tags\n\nMost motion lines will have an applicable action tag associated with it. Here are some common ones.\n\n* [[shaking]]\n* [[throbbing]]\n* [[thrusting]]\n* [[twitching]]\n* [[vibrating]]\n* [[wiggle]]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[tag_group:narrative_elements]]\n\n* [[iconography]]\n* [[emanata]]\n* [[motion_blur]]\n* [[speed_lines]] / [[zoom_lines]]\n* [[tremble_spikes]]"
