          "count": 33405,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #496734 thumb #707909 thumb #32779 thumb #832278\r\n\r\nImages or animations depicting a character with the medical condition known as [i]complete heterochromia iridis[/i], a genetic quirk which causes their eyes to be separate colors.\r\n\r\nThis includes characters with asymmetrically colored eyes, e.g. a [[green eyes|green eye]] and a [[blue eyes|blue eye]], or a notably lighter or deeper shade of a single color.\r\n\r\nNote that for simplicity's sake, if a pre-existing character is known to have heterochromia, but it is not apparent in an image (if they're turned to the side or have one eye closed, for example, or if the image is in black-and-white), that particular image should [b]not[/b] be tagged with \"heterochromia\".\r\n\r\nFor the condition where a character has [b]multiple colors in the same eye[/b] (or [i]sectoral heterochromia idris[/i]), see [[multicolored_eyes]].\r\n\r\nh3. [[tag group:colors|Eye colors]]\r\n\r\n* [[amber_eyes]]\r\n* [[black_eyes]]\r\n* [[blue_eyes]]\r\n* [[brown_eyes]]\r\n* [[cyan_eyes]]\r\n* [[green_eyes]]\r\n* [[grey_eyes]]\r\n* [[orange_eyes]]\r\n* [[pink_eyes]]\r\n* [[purple_eyes]]\r\n* [[red_eyes]]\r\n* [[white_eyes]]\r\n* [[yellow_eyes]]\r\n\r\n* heterochromia\r\n* [[multicolored_eyes]]\r\n** [[rainbow_eyes]]\r\n** [[two_tone_eyes]]\r\n\r\nh3. See also: \r\n\r\n* http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heterochromia\r\n\r\n"
