          "tag": "reclining",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 19456,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #574358 thumb #286079 thumb #82270\r\n\r\n[b]Reclining[/b] is a positional state that is between [[lying]] and [[sitting]]. It can be used as a singular tag or be used in combination with lying or sitting if the pose is very close to one particular state. Reclining can be recognized by a character leaning back against an angled surface or on their arms. If the character's upper body isn't being supported by anything, using [[leaning back]] may be more appropriate.\r\n\r\nIf the character is in a relaxed state, usually indicated by a character sitting or lying with their back physically pressed against a surface the [[lounging]] tag should also be used.\r\n\r\n[section=Examples]\r\n\r\nh4. Sitting\r\n\r\nCharacters reclining at these angles will still be mostly upright, and usually will have their arms fully extended if not propped up against a surface.\r\n\r\nthumb #2340441 thumb #2322714 thumb #2293339 thumb #1395389 thumb #1034466\r\n\r\nh4. Lying\r\n\r\nCharacters reclining at these angles are close to the lying position, and often will have their arms bent.\r\n\r\nthumb #1016073 thumb #1600784 thumb #1312595\r\n\r\nh4. Lounging \r\n\r\nCharacters that are [[lounging]] tend to to be laying against an object that provides back support. This position is designed to be comfortable.\r\n\r\nthumb #479977 thumb #2265731 thumb #761181\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[crossed_legs]]\r\n* [[hands_behind_head]]\r\n* [[leaning_backward]] - Often used along with [[arm_support]], or [[against_wall]].\r\n* [[lying]], [[sitting]]\r\n* [[pinup]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also \r\n\r\n* [[standing]] \r\n* [[lying]] \r\n* [[crouching]]\r\n* [[kneeling]]\r\n* [[tag_group:pose]]"
