          "tag": "shackles",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 19163,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Shackles[/b] are a specific, heavy type of [[cuff_(restraint)]]. \r\n\r\nHistorically, shackles were used to define thick, round [[metal_cuffs]] linked by a chain; the term most often refers to ankle cuffs, but this is not mandatory. Shackles are much wider than [[handcuffs]].\r\n\r\nNot to be confused with police [[handcuffs]].\r\n\r\nFor tagging purposes, use [[shackles]] if:\r\n* Wide [[metal_cuffs]] are linked by a chain of significant length (more than a few links), or\r\n* The [[metal_cuffs]] are very bulky\r\n\r\nAdd [[magical_binding]] if the shackles are magic, and [[metal_cuffs]] otherwise.\r\n\r\nDo [b]not [/b]use [[shackles]] for:\r\n* Traditional thin police handcuffs (use [[handcuffs]] instead)\r\n* [[leather_cuffs]]\r\n* [[fuzzy_handcuffs]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[bdsm]]\r\n** [[bondage]]\r\n** [[bondage_gear]] \r\n*** [[blindfold]]\r\n*** [[restraints]]\r\n**** [[chain]]\r\n**** [[rope]] \r\n**** [b][[cuff_(restraint)]][/b]\r\n***** [[ankle_cuffs]]\r\n***** [[wrist_cuffs]]\r\n***** [[tail_cuff]]\r\n***** [[handcuffs]]\r\n***** [[metal_cuffs]]\r\n***** [[leather_cuffs]]\r\n*** [[gag]]\r\n*** [[harness]]"
