          "tag": "digestion",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 18085,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #2938547 thumb #2433798 thumb #3011184 thumb #2484743\n\n[b]Digestion[/b] is the process of [[food]] being broken down via chemical and mechanical means, and absorbed by a living being for sustenance. \n\nThe digestive process in art is usually only implied by [[rumbling stomach|stomach noises]] and context (e.g. a character's stomach rumbling after eating), however, it can be depicted explicitly via an [[internal]] of substances, objects or ingested creatures being digested within the stomach, the stomach contracting, or filling with [[stomach acid]]; rarely, this can include other parts of the gastrointestinal tract. Digestion may be implied in sequence by a character ingesting, and then digesting something, causing them to gain weight, grow, or expand.\n\nDigestion can be a part of [[stuffing]], [[cum inflation]], [[weight gain]] or even posts depicting a character simply [[eating]] food, and is a major part of [[vore]] content (see section below).\n\nh4. Tags Related To Digestion\n\n[section= General Tags]\n\n* [[digestion_noises]] - sound effects related to the digestive process\n** [[rumbling_stomach]] - sounds created by substances moving within the gastrointestinal tract\n* [[eating]] - ingesting edible items or substances\n** [[chewing]] - food being crushed by teeth\n** [[swallowing]] - the act of pushing something from the mouth down the throat, which is then involuntarily pushed down the esophagus to the stomach\n* [[rapid_digestion]] - a character digesting something at an unrealistic speed\n\n[/section]\n\n[section=Digestive Organs]\n\n* [[organs]] - for all internal organs\n** [[guts]]\n** [[esophagus]] \n** [[stomach]]\n** [[intestines]]\n\n[/section]\n\n[section=Stomach Contents]\n\n** [[food_in_stomach]] - self descriptive\n** [[cum_in_stomach]] - [[cum]] inside of the stomach\n** [[object_in_stomach]] - an inanimate, non-food item inside of a stomach\n** [[inside_stomach]] - a character inside of a stomach, or first person perspectives/landscape depictions of the inside of a stomach\n** [[stomach_acid]] - an acid secreted by the stomach to chemically break down food\n** [[chyme]] - mushy, partially digested matter mixed with gastric juices\n** [[vomit]] -  chyme, potentially along with intact food/objects/characters that is being, or has been ejected through the mouth \n\n[/section]\n\nh4. Digestion and Vore\n\nDigestion plays a major role in [[vore]] content, particularly [[oral vore]]. It may be implied or explicitly shown by [[sequence]], [[comic]] or in animation, internally or externally. Note that a character simply being in another's stomach isn't enough to be tagged digestion, unless it has occurred to other contents of the stomach, or strongly implied to be occurring by pooling stomach acid, contractions of the stomach, rumbling stomach, or even dialogue. \n\nIn vore scenarios, digestion may be shown to occur in organs other than those of the digestive tract, such as within the testicles in [[cock vore]], uterus in [[unbirthing]], and sometimes the colon or rectum in [[anal vore]] (although typically, digestion in anal vore still occurs via the stomach, with the prey sucked in reverse, through the intestines).\n\n[section=Vore Specific Digestion Tags]\n\n* [[after_vore]] - if the prey is shown to be, or implied to have been completely digested (see page for more)\n* [[imminent_digestion]] - the prey has [i]just[/i] been swallowed and is clearly facing digestion, but is not being digested at the moment\n* [[cum_vore]] - a character being digested by, or absorbed into cum (usually within the testes)\n* [[pussy_juice vore]] - a character being digested by, or absorbed into vaginal secretions\n* [[melty digestion]] - Internal shot where the prey appears to be [[melting]] into some form of goo\n* [[graphic digestion]] - Internal shot where, somewhat realistically, the prey's skin appears to be dissolved by (usually gastric) acid, exposing muscles and bones\n* [[rising tide digestion]] - Internal shot where the prey is submerged by some \"digestive fluid\", though possibly threatening to drown them before they get digested\n* [[smoothening bulge digestion]] - Sequence if external shots where an initially lumpy bulge, possibly with [[imprint|imprints]] or a [[body outline]], becomes smoother as the digestion process liquifies what's inside\n* [[shrinking space digestion]] - Internal shot where the space the prey is in starts to shrink around them or even compress them, usually until they aren't visible anymore.\n\n[/section]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[belly]]\n* [[inflation]]\n** [[cum_inflation]]\n* [[stuffing]]\n* [[weight_gain]]\n* [[vore]]"
        },
