          "wiki_body": "thumb #5009239 thumb #4314028 thumb #3244805 thumb #1758012 thumb #4775570 thumb #4295941 thumb #4383570 thumb #4547510 thumb #4964478\n\n[b]Manly[/b] defines a [[male]], [[andromorph]], or [[maleherm]] character who shows some physical and/or behavioral characteristics that denotes his masculinity, and are traditionally associated with men. Notable examples includes:\n \n* Their [b]physical[/b] appearance of developed musculature (like an [[athletic male]], [[muscular male]], and/or a male with [[big muscles]]), presence of [[body hair]] and/or [[facial hair]], broad shoulders, a [[big penis]] and/or [[big balls]], and harsh features.\n\n* Their [b]behavioral[/b] appearance of confident posture and/or expression, competitiveness, aggressiveness, dominant behavior, and abruptness. Often associated with [[jock|jocks]] and [[frat_boy|frat boys]].\n\nh4. Related tags:\n* [[barazoku]]\n* [[daddy_kink]]\n* [[daddyfication]]\n\nh4. See also\n* [[girly]] - The complete opposite of this tag.\n* [[tomboy]] - When the opposite gender displays qualities of masculinity."
