          "tag": "number",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 12740,
          "wiki_body": "Images or animations that features a number (besides a [[year]] or an artist that happens to feature a number in their name or alias) somewhere.\n\n[table][thead]\n[tr][th] Theme [/th]\n[th] Example [/th]\n[/tr][/thead]\n\n[tbody]\n[tr][td] [[count]] [/td][td] A running total of something. Benjamin has 5 carrots.[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td] [[counting]] [/td][td] Numbers displayed in a sequential order. 1, 2, 3...18, 19, 20[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td] [[math]] [/td][td] The study of numbers, and their associated properties. [/td][/tr]\n[tr][td] [[percentage]] [/td][td] A proportion of a whole. 58% [/td][/tr]\n[tr][td] [[price]] [/td][td] The value of a good or service. $5.00 [/td][/tr]\n[tr][td] [[probability]] [/td][td] The odds of an event happening. Chances are 1 out of 10,000. [/td][/tr]\n[tr][td] [[rating_scale]] [/td][td] A scale of satisfaction often in the form of x out of y. [/td][/tr]\n[tr][td] [[time]] [/td][td] A point in time, or representation of time. 9:00 PM, 3:00 AM [/td][/tr]\n[tr][td] [[time_period]] [/td][td] A duration of time. 8 months from now, 3 hours ago, 15 seconds[/td][/tr]\n\n[/tbody][/table]\n\nh4. Numbered tags\n\nNumbered themes mainly involve objects with numbers on them, or concepts such as numbered lists, sequences etc.\n\n* [[numbered_heart]]\n* [[numbered_sequence]]\n* [[numbered_sex_toy]]\n** [[numbered_anal_beads]]\n* [[numbered_tag]]\n* [[number_print]]\n\nh6. Counts (these apply towards the [[count]] tag)\n\nA running total of something, as explained above. Several subtags exist for this general concept, mainly regarding video games.\n\n* [[damage_numbers]]\n* [[stats]]\n\nh6. Enumerations (these do not apply towards the [[count]] tag)\n\nEnumerations differ from counts in that they are indexed values. These numbers are assigned to an object, character, or location and do not necessarily represent a running total.\n\n* [[id_number]]\n* [[page_number]]\n* [[chapter_number]]\n* [[stage_number]]\n* [[title_number]]\n* [[phone_number]]\n* [[address_number]]\n* [[room_number]]\n\nh6. Ranked numbers  (these do not apply towards the [[count]] tag)\n\n* [[level_number]]\n* [[rank]] - 1st, 2nd, 3rd, etc\n\nh4. Numeric forms and systems\n\nThese tags are alternate ways of showing numeric information.\n\n* [[binary_code]] - Most numbers are portrayed in base 10. This is the name for the base 2 numerical system (series of ones and zeroes) \n* number words - [i]One[/i], [i]two[/i], [i]three[/i], [i]uno[/i], [i]dos[/i], [i]tres[/i]\n* [[roman_numeral]] - Ancient number system using an arrangement of the following characters: I (1), V (5), X (10), L (50), C (100), D (500), and M (1000).\n* [[tally_marks]] - Lines in a row. Every fifth line crosses through the previous four lines.\n\nh4. Special numbers\n\n* [[69_(number)]]\n* [[420_(number)]]\n* [[621_(number)]]\n\nh4. Related tags\n\n* [[currency_symbol]]\n** [[dollar_sign]]\n* [[milestone]]\n* [[money]]\n* [[stats]]\n* [[algebralian]]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[tag_group:narrative_elements]]\n\n* [[text]]\n* [[grade]]"
