ll often have this type of \"bottom heaviness\". \r\n\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\nh6. Bottom Heavy Vs Pear-Shaped Figure\r\n\r\n[section=These tags can easily be confused with one another...]\r\n\r\nthumb #2568391 thumb #756438 thumb #3177528\r\n\r\nWhile [[pear-shaped figure]] inherently describes a body type with a larger lower half, and bottom heavy characters may sometimes have a [i]pear-like[/i] shape - \"pear-shaped figure\" describes a character with a generally more proportionate body, the difference between the character's upper body (with narrow shoulders and often small bust/chest), and lower body (broad midsection, wide hips/thick thighs) is more subtle than a bottom heavy character.\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[Top Heavy]] The opposite of this tag\r\n* [[Tag Group:Figures]]"
