          "tag": "squeezing",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 10302,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Squeezing[/b] involves a character or body part being compressed or having pressure applied to by an outside force. This usually involves being grabbed in some way (hands, [[tentacles]], [[coiling]]), but certain [[restraints]] may qualify towards this tag.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[squish]]\r\n\r\nh4. Types\r\n\r\nThese are only the most used examples. Use the tag format `x_squeeze` to find other tags or to create new ones.\r\n\r\n* [[ball_squeeze]]\r\n* [[belly_squeeze]]\r\n* [[breast_squeeze]]\r\n* [[pec_squeeze]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[coiling]]\r\n* [[deep_skin]]\r\n* Grabbing: (involves multiple characters) / Holding: (involves a single character)\r\n** [[ball_grab]], [[holding_balls]]\r\n** [[breast_grab]], [[holding_breast]]\r\n** [[butt_grab]], [[holding_butt]]\r\n** [[self_grab]] - The modifier tag for acts of holding that count as grabbing / squeezing.\r\n* [[grope]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[crush]]\r\n* [[smothering]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "on_model",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 10139,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1979707 thumb #2184996 thumb #4326018 thumb #4348634 \n\n[b]\"On model\"[/b] describes fan-made artwork or animations of copyrighted characters, which are made to be extremely similar in style to the canonical art style of the media the characters are from, sometimes to the point of being indistinguishable from actual [[official art]]. \n\nIn some cases, the only way to distinguish it from official art may either be the subject matter of the work, or alterations made to a character's design that doesn't break away from the overall art style.\n\nAdditionally, the on model tag can be used to describe when characters are depicted in a way that is [b]heavily[/b] based on the official style and proportions of the original character designs, or where the character's face alone is more or less on model, while the rest of their body is altered.\n\nh6. Notes\nAs hinted above, there is [i]some[/i] \"wiggle room\"...\n\n* `on_model` can still apply to fan art that uses a different medium than the source material, or is slightly different in terms of colour, line thickness or line art style, etc — so long as the character design remains extremely close to the official artwork , it should look like the artist based the drawing off of screenshots or the official [[model sheet]] of the character\n** e.g. an [[Animal Crossing]] character digitally painted rather than 3d rendered, but retains the anatomy and proportions of the game\n\n* this tag applies regardless of subject matter, and can apply even if there are changes to the anatomy of the character without changing the art style they are depicted in\n** Explicit fan art that gives the on model character genitalia, or fan art that gives a character larger breasts or buttocks is still `on_model` so long as the [i]overall style [/i]of the character design remains similar to the original source material.\n\n\nh4. Related Tags\n* [[fake screencap]], on model artwork may be seen in a fake screencap of a real piece of media\n* [[official art]], art from a production which is officially sanctioned, e.g. model sheets, advertisements, comics\n\nh4. See Also\n* [[on style]], art that replicates the source material's style, but may deviate from the character's typical design\n* [[style crossover]], when two or more characters drawn in visually distinct styles are interacting in a single scene\n** this is frequently seen in [[crossover]] art with both characters drawn `on_model`\n* [[style emulation]], when art is drawn to emulate a particular style, regardless of whether it is fan art, or on model for the character depicted"
        },
