          "tag": "cutout",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 9971,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #2361889 thumb #2580136 thumb #3031416 thumb #1839743\n\n[b]Cutout[/b] describes an intentional hole or \"window\" in a garment, which exposes and frames part of the body.\n\nThe most popular type of cutout [[cleavage cutout|shows off the cleavage]], but cutouts can also expose the navel, abdomen, \"[[butt cleavage]]\", crotch, breasts and so on. Cutout should only be applied to garments where the hole is intentional and is completely surrounded by material.\n\nWhen used alone, this tag can be used to describe images with cutouts that combine more specific cutout tags (commonly clothing exposing the inner cleavage and midriff), or that lack specific cutout tags.\n\n[b]Not to be confused with [[cutaway]][/b]\n\nh4. Cutout Tags\n\nh6. Types of Cutout\n* [[belly cutout]]\n** [[navel cutout]]\n* [[butt cutout]]\n* [[cleavage cutout]]\n* [[crotch cutout]]\n* [[hip vent]]\n* [[nipple cutouts]]\n\nh6. Popular Cutout Shapes \n* [[cat cutout]]\n* [[heart cutout]] \n* [[star cutout]]\n\nh4. Clothing Defined By Cutouts\n* [[keyhole clothing]]\n** [[keyhole bra]]\n** [[keyhole turtleneck]]\n* [[sharkini]]\n\nh4. Related Tags\n* [[easy access]] \n* [[ineffective clothing]]\n\nh4. See Also\n* [[backless clothing]]\n** [[backless dress]]\n* [[breastless clothing]]\n* [[crotchless clothing]]\n"
