          "count": 9789,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Plap[/b] is an [[onomatopoeia]] commonly introduced into [[sex]] scenes to portray a thrusting impact into something or someone. Other thrusting impact sound effects include \"[[clapping|Clap]]\", and \"[[slap_(sound_effect)|Slap]]\". Thrusting motion sounds include \"Hump\", and \"Thrust\".\r\n\r\nh4. Tagging notes\r\n\r\n- This tag should only be used for \"Plap\", and its related sound forms (such as \"Pap\"), and not for alternative onomatopoeia.\r\n\r\n[b]Sound effect forms:[/b] \"Plap\", \"Palap\", \"Plop\" (Sometimes, and usually only as a complement to another \"Plap\"), \"Pap\", \"Plp\"\r\n\r\n- For tagging purposes, \"Plap\" and \"Plop\" should not count as distinctly different enough to qualify towards the requirements for [[different_sound_effects]], but \"Plop\" can be considered a [[derived_sound_effect|derived form]] of \"Plap\".\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\nThese all commonly apply. Try not to forget to add these tags.\r\n\r\n* [[impact_onomatopoeia]]\r\n* [[sex]]\r\n* [[thrusting]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:sound_effects]]\r\n\r\n* [[sound_effects]]\r\n** [[onomatopoeia]]\r\n*** [[impact_onomatopoeia]]\r\n**** [[clapping]]\r\n**** [b]plap[/b]\r\n**** [[slam]]\r\n**** [[slap_(sound_effect)]]\r\n**** [[smack_(sound_effect)]]\r\n**** [[spank_(sound_effect)]]\r\n**** [[thwap]]\r\n**** [[whack]]\r\n**** [[whap]]\r\n** [[thrusting_sound_effect]] - \"Hump\", \"Thrust\""
