          "count": 9410,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #2271411 thumb #4744727 thumb #1055873 thumb #1913911 thumb #4030773\n\nA ring around a character's head, normally seen decorating holy beings. More modern representations often take the form of a frisbee-sized ring hovering above the head, older religious iconography often depicts it face-on to the viewer.\n\nThe name is also used for an optical phenomenon which circles the sun with a ring of light, and there's another optical phenomenon called a \"glory\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glory_%28optical_phenomenon%29 where a rainbow ring surrounds the head of the viewer's cast shadow. For tagging art, anything bright or rainbow-ish haloing the head makes this tag applicable. Artistically it's a good way of picking out the main character or flagging a character's head for attention, as you'd expect.\n\nh4. Not to be confused with\n* [i][[halo (series)|Halo]][/i], an Xbox and PC gaming franchise featuring a battle between the alien group, the Covenant, and the human colonies.\n\nh4. See also\n* [[angel]]\n* [[aureola]]\n\n* \"wikipedia:Halo (optical phenomenon)\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halo_%28optical_phenomenon%29\n* \"wikipedia:Halo (religious iconography)\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halo_%28religious_iconography%29\n* \"wikipedia:Glory (optical phenomenon)\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glory_%28optical_phenomenon%29"
