          "tag": "poster",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 8893,
          "wiki_body": "Is a large piece of paper created to be attached in flat surfaces (mainly walls), with a printed content that can varies between an image, text or both, the main two uses of posters are for decoration and advertisement.\r\n\r\nIn [i]e621[/i] posters are most likely to show something pornographic, parodic or humoristic. In that order from high to low.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[cover_art]] - Artwork created for a comic, or image set is cover art, not a poster.\r\n* [[pinup]] - A seductive pose by itself is not a poster.\r\n* [[portrait]]\r\n\r\nh4. Poster formats\r\n\r\n* [[poster_template]] - The entire image is the poster.\r\n\r\nh4. Poster types\r\n\r\n* [[game_poster]]\r\n* [[medical_poster]]\r\n* [[missing_poster]]\r\n* [[motivational_poster]]\r\n* [[movie_poster]]\r\n** [[pulp_fiction]]\r\n* [[music_poster]]\r\n* [[pokemon_poster]]\r\n* [[propaganda_poster]]\r\n* [[wanted_poster]]\r\n\r\nh4. Particular posters\r\n\r\n* [[barack_obama_\"hope\"_poster]]\r\n* [[coffee!_poster]]\r\n* [[hang_in_there]]\r\n* [[keep_calm_and_carry_on]]\r\n* [[we_can_do_it!]]\r\n"
