          "wiki_body": "thumb #671633 thumb #1500981 thumb #1384019\n\nSometimes called a double nelson or a double shoulder lock, [b]full nelson[/b] is a grappling hold which is executed from behind the opponent, facing the same direction as them.\n\nBoth arms are used to encircle the opponent's arms under the armpits, and secured behind the opponent's neck and head.\n\nBecause it can be used as a limited neck crank, it is considered dangerous in some grappling arts, and is banned, for instance, in amateur wrestling.\n\nh4. See also\n* [[anal_full_nelson]], the anal version.\n* [[full_nelson_(arms_held)]], when only the arms are encircled.\n* [[full_nelson_(legs_held)]], when also the legs are encircled.\n* [[full_nelson_position]], a sex position utilizing full nelson.\n* [[half_nelson]]"
