        {
          "tag": "spines",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 8616,
          "wiki_body": "Posts depicting needle-like protrusions in parts of a body.\r\nSpines are found in both vertebrate and invertebrate animals alike, in mammals they are more commonly seen in [[hedgehog|hedgehogs]] and [[porcupine|porcupines]]. Also found on some plants, such as [[cactus|cactuses]].\r\n\r\nNote that although animals such as hedgehogs are expected to have these, most of the [[anthro]] hedgehogs (such as the ones in [[Sonic the Hedgehog (series)]]) actually lack anything that could be tagged as spines.\r\n\r\nh5. Not to be confused with:\r\n\r\n* [[penile_spines|barbs]]\r\n* [[spikes_(anatomy)]], which should be used instead if the protrusions are not shaped like a needle\r\n** [[spiked_penis]]\r\n* [[dorsal_ridge]]\r\n* [[tail_ridge]], blunt protrusions commonly found in [[crocodilian|crocodilians]], lizards, and dragons\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[frill_spines]], spines combined with membranous frill\r\n* [[head_spines]]\r\n* [[back_spines]]\r\n* [[tail_spines]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[head_crest]]"
