          "tag": "fantasy",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 8476,
          "wiki_body": "Fantasy is a genre of fiction that typically uses [[magic]] and other supernatural phenomena as a primary element of plot, theme, or setting. Many works within the genre take place in imaginary worlds where magic is common, with [[medieval]] often serving as the basis. Fantasy is generally distinguished from science fiction and horror by the expectation that it steers clear from themes of (pseudo-)scientific and macabre, respectively, though there is a great deal of overlap between the three (which are subgenres of speculative fiction).\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n* [[fantasizing]]"
