          "wiki_body": "The [b]abdomen[/b], the by far most recognizable part of insect anatomy is the bulbous posterior portion of the body on most arthropod species that typically holds the digestive and reproductive systems of the arthropod. May be synonymous within context to a tail in anthropomorphic and humanoid arthropods.\r\n\r\n*  Do not tag with tail.\r\n\r\nthumb #349353\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[arthropod]]\r\n* [[exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[stinger]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* \"Wikipedia entry\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abdomen#Other_animals\r\n\r\n* [[tag group:anatomy]]\r\n* [[tag group:feral anatomy]]"
