          "tag": "obliques",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 8097,
          "wiki_body": "The obliques are the muscles at either side of the [[abs|abdominal muscles]], technically called the [i]abdominal external oblique muscles[/i], but could possibly also refer to the underlying [i]abdominal internal oblique muscles[/i].\r\n\r\nThe anterior [[serratus|serratus muscles]] can be found slightly above these.\r\n\r\nThe obliques as well as serratus muscles are sometimes overlooked by artists despite showing bulging abs and [[pecs|pectorals]], either intentionally, to simplify, or by not having studied muscle anatomy.\r\n\r\nh4. Muscular Scale\r\n\r\n[ltable]\r\nNot Muscular | &pipe; | [[Muscular]] ->   |                  |                   |\r\n[[athletic]] | &pipe; | [[big_muscles]]   | [[huge_muscles]] | [[hyper_muscles]] |\r\n             | &pipe; | [[musclegut]]     |                  |                   |\r\n[/ltable]\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n\r\n* [b][[muscular]][/b]\r\n\r\n* [b]Muscles[/b]\r\n** Torso: [[abs]] / [[back_muscles]] / [[pecs]] / [[serratus]] / obliques\r\n** Arm: [[biceps]] / [[triceps]] / [[deltoids]] / [[forearm_muscles]]\r\n** Leg: [[quads]]\r\n** Butt: [[butt_muscles]]\r\n\r\n* [b]Gender specific[/b]\r\n** [[muscular_ambiguous]]\r\n** [[muscular_male]]\r\n** [[muscular_female]]\r\n** [[muscular_intersex]]\r\n*** [[muscular_andromorph]]\r\n*** [[muscular_gynomorph]]\r\n*** [[muscular_herm]]\r\n*** [[muscular_maleherm]]"
