          "tag": "canon_x_oc",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 6682,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Canon x OC[/b] describes scenes with sexual, suggestive, and/or romantic interaction, between a character from a copyrighted series or media property (such as a video game, cartoon, anime or book) and a character owned by an individual artist, commissioner, or otherwise.\n\n[quote]\nh5. Tagging Notes\n\n* [b][i]For the purposes of this tag \"OC\" can apply to...[/i][/b]\n** A wholly original character — a character owned by an individual with no connection to any outside media\n** A [[fan character]] — characters made to fit into the \"universe\" of a specific media property\n** A fursona — an artist or commissioner's furry self representation\n** A self insert — a more overt and direct artist/commissioner self representation, will be human or humanoid  \n\n* [b][i][color=yellow]What is [u]NOT[/u] Canon x OC:[/color][/i][/b]\n** images where the non-canon character is an [[anon]], the character is [[faceless character|faceless]], or is [[mostly off screen character|mostly off screen]], unless the partially visible character is specifically intended to be an identifiable character. \n** An OC engaging in romantic or sexual activity with \"generic\" unnamed individuals of a species specific to a franchise — e.g. a generic [[changeling]] from [i]My Little Pony[/i] or a [[Lopunny]] from [i]Pokémon[/i]  \n\n* The original character does not need to have a tag entry to count for this tag, but having the OC's name tagged is encouraged.\n[/quote]\n\nh4. Related Tags\n* [[fan character]]\n\nh4. See Also\n* [[canon couple]]\n* [[crossover]]"
