          "wiki_body": "thumb #1281894 thumb #1264521 thumb #147110\r\n\r\n[b]Exoskeletons[/b], often found on [[insect|insects]] and [[crustacean|crustaceans]], are external [[skeleton|skeletons]] that supports and protect the creature that has it. They're often composed of [b]chitin[/b], a material seen in things such as fish scales. Aliens in popular media are commonly portrayed with external skeletons, such as the infamous [[xenomorph|xenomorphs]].\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[body_armor]] - While often called \"exoskeletons\" casually, they are not the same as actual exoskeletons. They're artificially made hi-tech, often tighter fitting [[armor|armors]], whereas actual exoskeletons are a natural, external [[skeleton]].\r\n* [[power_armor]]\r\n\r\nh4. Tags About Exoskeletons\r\n\r\n* [b]exoskeleton[/b]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Colors]\r\nh4. Exoskeleton [[tag_group_colors|Colors]]\r\n\r\n* [[black_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[blue_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[brown_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[green_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[grey_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[orange_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[pink_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[purple_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[red_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[tan_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[white_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[yellow_exoskeleton]]\r\n\r\n* [[monotone_exoskeleton]] - only one distinct color\r\n* [[multicolored_exoskeleton]] - at least two distinct colors\r\n** [[multi_tone_exoskeleton]] - more than two distinct colors\r\n*** [[rainbow_exoskeleton]] - the entire spectrum of distinct colors\r\n** [[two_tone_exoskeleton]] - only two distinct colors\r\n\r\n* [[dark_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[light_exoskeleton]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=General]\r\n* [[glistening_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[glowing_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[gradient_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[mottled_exoskeleton]]\r\n** [[piebald_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[spotted_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[striped_exoskeleton]]\r\n* [[translucent_exoskeleton]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n[section=General Anatomy]\r\n* [[tag_group:anatomy]]\r\n** [[tag_group:feral anatomy]]\r\n\r\n* [[body]] - A fallback for when the body texture is difficult to decipher.\r\n** [b]exoskeleton[/b] - An external skeleton often made of chitin, seen in [[insect|insects]] and [[crustacean|crustaceans]].\r\n** [[feathers]] - A complex texture, seen in [[bird|birds]], and most [[gryphon|gryphons]]. Often applied to [[feathered_wings|wings]] of such species.\r\n** [[fur]] - A furry texture, seen in most [[mammal|mammals]]. Even a single [[tuft]] will influence this.\r\n** [[scales]] - A squamous texture, seen in  [[reptile|reptiles]], [[scalie|scalies]], and most [[dragon|dragons]].\r\n** [[skin]] - A smooth texture, seen in [[human|humans]], [[dolphin|dolphins]], and [[amphibian|amphibians]].\r\n[/section]"
        },
