          "tag": "yes-no_question",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 4352,
          "wiki_body": "The [b]yes-no question[/b] group, also known as [b]simple[/b] or [b]general[/b] questions, are [[question]] forms that ask for a [i]yes[/i], [i]no[/i], and sometimes [i]maybe[/i] answer.\r\n\r\n[b]Question forms[/b]\r\n\r\nPositive: \"Am\", \"Are\", \"Can\", \"Could\", \"Do\", \"Does\", \"Have\", \"Is\", \"May\", \"Will\", \"Would\"\r\nNegative: \"Ain't\", \"Aren't\", \"Can't\", \"Couldn't\", \"Don't\", \"Doesn't\", \"Haven't\", \"Isn't\", \"Won't\", \"Wouldn't\"\r\n\r\nQuestions that express wants tend to be simple questions. Look for questions that start with \"Want\", or \"Wanna\".\r\n\r\nh4. Partial / Tag questions\r\n\r\nPartial questions are sometimes difficult to determine if they qualify as a simple question. Try your best to determine if the form can be phrased as a yes-no question form; in any case partial questions should be tagged as [[questioning tone]].\r\n\r\n[[tag_question|Tag questions]] are commonly simple in form, often being a variation of \"Do you?\", \"Does this make sense?\", or \"Is that so?\"\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[asking]]\r\n* [[command]]\r\n* [[question]]"
