          "count": 4332,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #2691077 thumb #3378213 thumb #3707289 thumb #2158936 thumb #3885948\r\n\r\n[b]Stairs[/b] (also known as [b]staircase[/b],  [b]stairway[/b] and other terms) are an architectural [[construction]] consisting of a series of [[steps]] providing access to a [[floor]] of a public or private area or [[building]] [i]([[hotel]], [[house]], [[school]], [[skyscraper]], etc...)[/i]\r\n[b]Stairs[/b] allow you to go up [i](to a higher level)[/i] and down [i](to a lower level)[/i].\r\n\r\nStaircases can be made of [[stone]], [[wood]], [[metal]], [[concrete]], [[glass]] or even [[plaster]]...\r\nThese constructions are often placed next to emergency exit [[door|doors]] of [[apartment|apartments]] to enable users to evacuate more quickly.\r\n\r\nA [[handrail]] is a safety element located at the side of a stairway. [i](For your safety, please hold the handrail when climbing up and down, and do not sit or slide on the handrail).[/i]\r\n\r\nStairways with steps that move automatically are called [b]\"[[escalator]]\"[/b].\r\n\r\nh4.Related Tags\r\n* [[handrail]]\r\n* [[steps]]\r\n** [[floor]]\r\n\r\nh4.See Also\r\n* [[elevator]] \r\n* [[escalator]] – [i]For stairs with automatically moving steps[/i]"
