          "count": 3425,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #413429 thumb #12726 thumb #67934\r\n\r\nThe [b]ankh[/b], also known as the [b]key of life[/b], [b]key of the Nile[/b], [b]crux ansata[/b], or [b]ansatic cross[/b], was the Egyptian hieroglyph for the consonants '-n-h and meant \"eternal life\".  It resembles a cross with a loop over the crossbar.\r\n\r\nOften graphically synonymous with Egypt, the ankh is also associated with pagan, New Age, and neo-pagan religions, as well as the occult.\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Ankh Items and Designs\r\n\r\n* [[ankh necklace]]\r\n* [[ankh panties]]\r\n* [[ankh pendant]]\r\n* [[ankh piercing]]\r\n* [[ankh marking]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* \"Ankh (Wikipedia)\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ankh"
