          "wiki_body": "An intricate and distinctive pattern from the almost net-like, suspended traps that spiders will weave in order to catch their prey. \r\n\r\nh6. Important Note: \r\n\r\nThis tag includes both actual spider_webs and spider_web patterns (sometimes seen in clothing, tattoos and backgrounds).\r\n\r\nBut you can use searches like {{spider_web arthropod_webbing}} to search only for spider_webs that are made of actual [[arthropod_webbing|web]] material. Or use {{spider_web -arthropod_webbing}} to search for just the spider_web pattern.  \r\n\r\nNote this tag only applies if the distinct visual design of a spider web is visible either in frame or as a background object. If all that's seen is the silk used to make said webs, use [[arthropod_webbing]] instead.\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n\r\n* [[arthropod_webbing]] - for all instances of web-like material, including those from an actual [[spider_web]] and [[cocoon]]s. Note: actual spider webs will be tagged with both [[spider_web]] and [[arthropod_webbing]], since arthropod webbing is the material used to make them.\r\n* [[spider]] - the species that is most likely to make a spider_web"
