          "wiki_body": "[b]Emojis[/b] are ideograms and smileys used in electronic messages and Web pages. Emojis are used much like [[emoticon|emoticons]] and exist in various genres, including facial expressions, common objects, places and types of weather, and animals.\r\n\r\nOriginally meaning pictograph, the word emoji comes from Japanese [i]e[/i] (絵, \"picture\") + [i]moji[/i] (文字, \"character\"). The resemblance to the English words [i]emotion[/i] and [i]emoticon[/i] is purely coincidental.\"\r\n\r\n[b]Source:[/b] \"Wikipedia\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emoji\r\n\r\nh3.Emojis (selection)\r\nThis is not an exhaustive list, just a random selection of emojis. They are linked to wiki pages here, however, so feel free to click on them.\r\n\r\nh1. [[grin|😀]] [[open smile|😃]] [[surfing|🏄]] [[thumbs up|👍]] [[fist|👊]] [[waving|👋]] [[balloon|🎈]] [[sunglasses|🕶]] [[<3|♥]] [[pizza|🍕]] [[fries|🍟]] [[palm tree|🌴]] [[beach|🏖]] [[domestic_dog|🐶]] [[domestic_cat|🐱]] [[penguin|🐧]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:facial_expressions]]\r\n\r\n* [[emoticon]]\r\n* [[pictographics]]\r\n* [[symbol]]"
