          "wiki_body": "thumb #4317585 thumb #3945754 \n\nWhen a character expresses an intention, implied or explicit, to do something undesirable to someone else.\n\nThis may be only a vague threat, like \"you'll pay for this\", \"I'm going to teach you a lesson\", or \"you're going to be sorry\". Alternatively, the threat may specifically reference what kind of undesirable action will be enacted on or undesirable result will occur to the target of the threat. \n\nMost often, `threatening` involves a threat of some sort of physical harm, whether it's a threat of being punched, bitten, or beaten, a threat of being shot or stabbed, or a threat of being killed.\n\nWhile usually conveyed through dialogue, this may also apply to a character speaking in [[pictographics]], using threatening gestures, or by holding a weapon to/pointing a weapon at, another character.\n\nThreatening is often done in the context of a character giving a [[command]] to another, and threatening something undesirable if their command isn't followed. Threatening is also commonly seen when a character is [[forced|forcing]] another to do something. \n\nh4. Threatening Tags\n\n* [[threatening viewer]]\n\nh5. Specific Threats\n\n* [[death threat]]\n* [[threatening abstinence]]\n* [[threatening castration]] \n* [[threatening rape]] \n* [[threatening violence]] \n* [[threatening vore]]\n* [[threatening with weapon]] \n\n\n\n\n\n"
