          "wiki_body": "thumb #2866581 thumb #3813962 thumb #4064772 thumb #4136557\n\n\n[b]Before and after[/b] describes posts that juxtapose a pair of images to show a transition between two distinct states of a character's pose, costume, size, age, physical form. This often shows the \"cause and effect\" how the something changes a character or a scene. It can also show a character/scene at two points in time.\n\n[quote]h5. Tagging Notes\n\n* [b]This tag should only apply when both the \"before\" and \"after\" are depicted in the same image.[/b] \n** If the transition is shown across multiple posts, this tag should not be used, and the posts should simply be linked by a parent/child relationship. \n** If more than one image is [i]used to show the transition[/i], then the post should not be tagged as `before_and_after` but as a [[sequence]]\n*** Rarely, posts may show multiple images/panels to show something different within the same \"before\" or \"after\" state, see example two above\n\n* While `before_and_after` posts are often two panel comics, or two images of the character given equal visual space, this tag can be used for posts that show the \"before\" and \"after\" states in less straightforward ways, such as...\n** A character shown in an old photograph (before) within the image, compared to their present self (after) in the main part of the image\n** The before or after state shown as a smaller [[cutaway|inset panel]] or close-up illustration next to, or within a larger image\n** A \"split screen\" image where the same character or scene is split down the middle, with the before and after states being on either side of the split.\n\n* [[Instant loss 2koma]] is often, (but not inherently) formatted as `before_and_after`\n[/quote]\n\nh4. Common Subjects\n\nThese fetishes/actions are commonly shown through `before_and_after` images:\n\n* [[age progression]]\n* [[age regression]]\n* [[bimbofication]]\n* [[expansion]]\n* [[growth]]\n* [[hypnotized]]\n* [[imp