        {
          "tag": "motion_onomatopoeia",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 2352,
          "wiki_body": "An umbrella tag for [[onomatopoeia]] closely associated with motion. With the exception of [[velocity_sound_effect|velocity sound effects]], these will almost certainly by action verbs.\r\n\r\nh4. Tagging guidelines\r\n\r\n* Do not use for a sound effect that is the result of motion. Motion onomatopoeia describe the motion itself as a sound effect.\r\n* Some verbs are better to use for this tag than others. Consider whether the verb involves physical contact, or not. There should be minimal overlap between contact sound effects, and motion sound effects. A term should better fit into one group or the other, and if it is unclear consider leaving the verb uncategorized.\r\n\r\nExample: [i]Rub[/i] should be tagged as [[contact_onomatopoeia]] instead even though it requires movement.\r\n\r\nThe reason for tagging this way is to avoid complex relationships that exist with verbs that occupy multiple categories. \r\n\r\nh4. Common applications\r\n\r\n* [[Bouncing]], or [[jumping]]\r\n* Indicators of fast, or sudden movement\r\n* [[Nodding]]\r\n* [[Shaking]] themes\r\n* [[Throbbing]], or pulsing\r\n* [[Thrusting]] (excluding impact sounds)\r\n* Waving, or wagging ([[tailwag]])\r\n\r\nh4. List of motion onomatopoeia (Incomplete)\r\n\r\n[table][thead][tr][th] Sound effect[/th][th] Included sound effects [/th][th] Related tags [/th][th] Extra information [/th][/tr][/thead]\r\n[tbody]\r\n\r\n[tr][td] [[bouncing_sound_effect]] [/td][td]  boing, bounce [/td][td] [[bouncing]] [/td][td] Apply specific body part tags when applicable (e.g. [[bouncing_breasts]]) [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] flail [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] [[flailing]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] flinch [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] [[flinch]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] jiggle [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] [[jiggling]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] [[jumping_sound_effect]] [/td][td] jump, hop, leap [/td][td] [[jumping]], [[hopping]], [[leaping]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] pounce, lunge [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] [[pounce|pouncing]], [[lunging]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] [[rotational_sound_effect]] [/td][td] flip, fwip (usually), spin, turn, twirl, twist [/td][td] [[spinning]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] shake, shiver, tremble [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] [[shaking]], [[shivering]], [[trembling]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] swing [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] [[swinging]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] [[swish_(sound_effect)]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] throb, pulse [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] [[throbbing]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] throw [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] [[throwing]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] [[thrusting_sound_effect]] [/td][td] hump, thrust [/td][td] [[thrusting]] [/td][td] This includes the verb, not the [[impact_onomatopoeia|impact sound effect]]. [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] twerk [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] [[twerking]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] twitch [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] [[twitching]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] [[velocity_sound_effect]] [/td][td] rush, woosh, zoom [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] wag [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] [[finger_wag]], [[tailwag]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] wiggle [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] [[wiggle]] [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n[tr][td] wobble [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] N/A [/td][td] N/A [/td][/tr]\r\n\r\n[/tbody][/table]\r\n\r\nh5. Grey areas\r\n\r\n- Terms related to pushing, or pulling. Probably should avoid categorizing, or treat them as contact terms. See [[pulling_sound_effect]]\r\n\r\nh5. Exclusions\r\n\r\nFor tagging purposes, the following concepts should not be considered a part of this tag:\r\n\r\n- Swallowing sounds\r\n- Kissing, licking, or biting\r\n- Motion terms exclusively related to water, or other liquids ([[gushing|gush]], [[squirt_(sound_effect)|squirt]]). These are better placed in their own sound effect category.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:sound_effects]]\r\n\r\n* [[sound_effects]]\r\n** [[onomatopoeia]]\r\n*** [[contact_onomatopoeia]]\r\n**** [[impact_onomatopoeia]]\r\n*** [b]motion_onomatopoeia[/b]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "poncho",
