          "tag": "grid_layout",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 2334,
          "wiki_body": "Any image that can be broken up into evenly spaced rows and columns. The images do not have to be related for this tag to apply.\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Categories]\r\n\r\nh5. [[Regular grid layout]]\r\n\r\nAll regions in a regular grid should be the same size.\r\n\r\nthumb #3399768 thumb #2455245 thumb #2159685\r\n\r\nh5. [[Irregular grid layout]]\r\n\r\nRegions in an irregular grid may vary in size and shape, and all of the gutters must align.\r\n\r\nthumb #3435651 thumb #3325490 thumb #3297799\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Other grid forms]\r\n\r\nh5. Staggered grids\r\n\r\nA [[staggered grid]] refers to when number of regions in each row are the same, and the number of regions in each column are the same, but the gutter space does not align.  This type of grid should not be tagged as a grid layout.\r\n\r\nh5. Partial grids\r\n\r\nA partial grid layout occurs when only part of the image is divided up into a grid region. Do not tag these as a grid layout. Use the grid count tag for the type of grid it resembles instead (standard / staggered).\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Grid count tags\r\n\r\nFor staggered variants, use the `<count>_frame_staggered_grid` format instead.\r\n\r\n* [[four_frame_grid]]\r\n* [[six_frame_grid]]\r\n* [[eight_frame_grid]]\r\n* [[nine_frame_grid]]\r\n* [[ten_frame_grid]]\r\n* [[twelve_frame_grid]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related themes\r\n\r\n* [[comic]]\r\n* [[multiple_versions]]\r\n* [[sequence]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[4_koma]]\r\n* [[four_frame_image]]\r\n** [[four_frame_sequence]]\r\n* [[six_frame_image]]\r\n** [[six_frame_sequence]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[comic]]\r\n* [[sequence]]\r\n\r\n[b]Layout tags[/b]\r\n\r\n* [[blockage_(layout)]]\r\n** [[horizontal_blockage]]\r\n** [[vertical_blockage]]\r\n* [b]grid_layout[/b]\r\n* [[staggered_grid_layout]]\r\n* [[staggering_(layout)]]\r\n** [[horizontal_staggering]]\r\n** [[vertical_staggering]]"
