        {
          "tag": "role_reversal",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 2301,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #5197306 thumb #2995883 thumb #2812525 thumb #2371296\n\n[b]Role Reversal[/b] describes situations where two or more characters of a pre-established setting displaying behaviour or other traits opposite their normally established, or expected characterization. \nThis can also apply to [[predator/prey]] situations, where the character of a prey species is behaving in a dominant manner, while the character of a predator species is submissive.  \n\n\nh5. Examples\nIn most cases, this implies a normally submissive, or normally dominant character (in a broad sense, not necessarily sexually dominant or submissive), behaving dominant or submissive respectively. Below are some examples of role reversal that are not necessarily sexual or along dominant/submissive lines:\n\n* A character in a position of authority being put in the role of, or treated or acting subserviently to their \"lesser\", someone who would typically be under their authority\n** A teacher being subservient or submissive to their student\n** A character in a managerial role or high ranking business position being treated as a servant by a \"lower\" office worker\n* A [[pokemon]] catching, or training a human character\n* A human or anthro character being treated as, and/or acting like the pet of a feral animal, or acting as a feral character while feral characters act like humans/anthro characters\n* A male character acting as the bride, and a female character acting as the groom at a wedding - wearing opposite outfits and performing the typically opposite gendered role\n* [[size swap]] - a typically small character and typically large character have their physical size swapped and their roles are therefore reversed\n\n\n\nh4. See Also\n* [[top turned bottom]]\n* [[versatile]] "
        },
