          "wiki_body": "Use this tag when there is a statement, phrase, or message that ends with a ?, but not phrased like a proper question. It may still be asking something in many cases, but sometimes this is unclear.\r\n\r\nh6. Normal question form\r\n\r\n- \"Do you like this?\"\r\n\r\nh6. Partial question form\r\n\r\n- \"You like?\"\r\n\r\nQuestioning names, pictographics, muffled statements, vocalizations should all fall under this umbrella tag. Many exclamations will end up having a questioning tone as well.\r\n\r\nh4. Examples\r\n\r\n* \"Jeremy?\"\r\n* \"Pika?!\"\r\n* \"Purrr?\"\r\n* Terms such as \"Oh?\", \"Hmm?\", \"Huh?\" probably apply.\r\n\r\nh4. Exclusions\r\n\r\n* [[tag_question]] - Questions attached to the end of phrases are excluded from this tag.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[asking]] - It usually counts as asking.\r\n* [[question]] - It usually counts as a question if the statement can be rewritten as a question."
