        {
          "tag": "visibly_trans",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 2079,
          "wiki_body": "When a character is clearly, visibly transgender – that is, when there is evidence that they are undergoing, or have undergone, surgery and/or hormone replacement therapy to present as a different sex.\r\n\r\nThis is not a gender tag.  It exists separately from, and neither affects, nor is affected by, the \"gender tags\":https://e621.net/wiki/show/tag_group:genders.\r\n\r\nh4.Things that might make a character `visibly_trans`, especially when seen together:\r\n\r\n* [[mastectomy scar|Mastectomy scars]] on what we tag as an [[andromorph]]\r\n* [[orchiectomy scar|Orchiectomy scars]] (see [[eunuch]]) on what we tag as a [[gynomorph]]\r\n* [[mammoplasty scar|Mammoplasty scars]]\r\n* An [[enlarged clitoris]]\r\n* [[chest binder|Breast binding]], often with tight clothing such as [[sports bra|sports bras]], [[breast binder|breast binders]], or [[bandage|bandages]]\r\n* [[penis tuck|Penis tucking]], however use caution with this and only tag tucking as visibly trans when it's very obvious (i.e. a character wearing a gaff.)\r\n\r\nAs always, use your best judgment.  For example, mastectomy scars don't make a character trans if there's evidence in the post of breast cancer.\r\n\r\nh4.Things that do [i]not[/i] make a character `visibly_trans`:\r\n\r\n* Statements from the character owner or artist (see [[trans_(lore)]])\r\n* How the character is tagged in other posts\r\n\r\nh4.Not to be confused with:\r\n\r\n* [[Gender transformation]], which is a short-lived process, often supernatural\r\n* [[Tag group:genders]]"
