          "count": 2067,
          "wiki_body": "A [b]slurp[/b] is a loud sloppy sucking noise usually associated with [[eating]], or [[drinking]]. This tag is usually applied when the sound effect, or audible noise is present.\r\n\r\n[b]Sound effect forms:[/b] \"Slurp\", \"Slurrp\", \"Shlurp\", \"Slrp\"\r\n\r\nNote that \"Shlrp\", and \"Slorp\" are usually tagged as \"[[Shlorp]]\" instead of \"Slurp\". The proper tag to use may depend on context. \r\n\r\nh4. Related themes\r\n\r\n* [[drinking]]\r\n* [[eating]]\r\n* [[licking]] - Slurp is sometimes used as a licking sound.\r\n* [[sucking]]\r\n* [[vore]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[sound_effects]]\r\n** [[onomatopoeia]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:sound_effects]]\r\n\r\n* [[shlorp]]\r\n* [[slurk]]"
