          "tag": "mecha",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1942,
          "wiki_body": "A [b]mecha[/b] or [b]mech[/b] is a [[robot]] that is operated by a [[pilot]] from the inside via a [[cockpit]]. Usually these [[machine]]s act more like [[vehicle]]s with [[robotic arm|arms]] and [[robotic leg|legs]] rather than its own autonomous entity though some mechas can switch to autopilot via their on-board [[computer]]s, or even a full-on [[artificial intelligence]] personality, when need be.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n* A [[drone (vehicle)|drone]] which is piloted remotely,\r\n* [[Power armor]] which is worn by the operator rather than piloted,\r\n* And a [[robot]] which is fully autonomous and doesn't require a pilot.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[science_fiction]]\r\n* [[machine]]\r\n** [b]mecha[/b]\r\n** [[power_armor]]\r\n** [[drone (vehicle)]]\r\n\r\nForum discussion:\r\n* forum #141131 - Cyborgs, Androids, and Robots. Oh my! (Oct. 2014)\r\n* forum #145008 - Calling all robot, android, mecha, etc. experts! (wiki project) (Dec. 2014)"
