        {
          "tag": "serafuku",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1842,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #111588 thumb #1721111 thumb #3187382 thumb #3119177\r\n\r\n[b]Serafuku[/b] (literally translating to \"[i]sailor outfit[/i]\")  is a type of [[school uniform]] commonly worn by Japanese girls in middle and high school.  Outside of Japan, the uniform is often popularly associated with the anime character [[sailor_moon_(character)|Sailor Moon]], and more broadly, with anime in general. \r\n\r\nThe \"classic\" serafuku consists of a white [[blouse]], a [[sailor_collar|sailor-style collar]], a red [[neckerchief]], and a [[pleated skirt]] - which is often blue or black. However, there are many variations on the uniform, some officially used in real life, and others purely worn as cosplay or drawn with artistic license. Serafuku may vary in colour, length of the shirt and skirt, swap the neckerchief for a [[ribbon]], [[bow]], [[bolo tie]] or [[necktie]], and may feature a cardigan or pull-over sweater worn over the blouse.\r\n\r\n[quote]\r\n[b]Important Note:[/b] Serafuku [u]should not be confused[/u] with [[Sailor Uniform]] - which describes the style of naval uniform the serafuku is patterned after.\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSerafuku are variously also referred to as [i]\"Sailor-Fuku\", \"seifuku\", \"sailor uniform\", or \"Japanese schoolgirl outfit\"[/i] - while \"seifuku\" is sometimes used to refer to the [i]serafuku[/i], seifuku simply means [[school uniform]], and can apply to any [[Japanese school uniform]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n* [[School_uniform|School Uniform]]\r\n* [[Japan]]\r\n* [[tag_group:clothes|List of Clothing Related Tags]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "montgomery_glands",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1840,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #2270761 thumb #3091060 thumb #2949902\r\n\r\nThis tag describes the appearance of small bumps on the [[areola]]. They can be drawn as small circles, or merely implied by subtle painting.\r\n\r\nThe [b]Montgomery glands[/b] are sebaceous (oil) glands, their primary function is lubricating the areola and keeping germs away from the [[breasts]] in preparation for suckling. The oil also has antibacterial properties, and research has suggested that infants may even detect the smell of the secretions, helping direct them to the breast to latch onto for feeding. The number of bumps varies from person to person from just a few, while others may have dozens.\r\n\r\nMontgomery glands can become more prominent during [[pregnant|pregnancy]].\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also: \r\n* [[Breasts]]\r\n* [[Nipples]]\r\n* [[Areola]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "fishing_rod",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1840,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #476071\r\n\r\nA [b]fishing rod[/b] is a long, flexible rod used to catch [[fish]]. At its simplest, a fishing rod is a simple stick or pole attached to a line ending in a [[hook]] (formerly known as an angle, hence the term angling). The length of the rod can vary between 2 and 20 feet (0.61 and 6.10 m). To entice fish, bait or lures are impaled on one or more hooks attached to the line. The line is generally stored on a reel which reduces tangles and assists in landing a fish."
        },
        {
          "tag": "groping_from_behind",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1840,
          "wiki_body": "When a character [[grope]]s another character from behind them. This can be a character groping the other character's chest ([[pecs]], [[breasts]]), or [[genitals]] ([[penis]], [[pussy]], [[cloaca]]) for example. Not to be confused with [[fondling]]."
        },
        {
          "tag": "clown",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1838,
          "wiki_body": "A [b]clown[/b] is a type of comic performer who aims to entertain an audience, often employing slapstick humor. They are somewhat similar to [[mime|mimes]].\r\n\r\nThe most common depiction of a clown is recognised by an outlandish costume featuring distinctive [[makeup]], exaggerated footwear, a colorful [[wig]], and prominent brightly-colored nose. This is most commonly [[red_nose|red]], but can be any color.\r\n\r\nModern clowns are strongly associated with the tradition of the circus clown, which developed out of earlier comedic roles in theatre or [i]Varieté[/i] shows during the 19th to mid 20th centuries.\r\n\r\nThe psychological fear of clowns is known as coulrophobia.\r\n\r\nClowns are also popular villains in the horror genre, where their negative aspects are more prominent and played up for the sake of drama.\r\n"
        },
        {
          "tag": "popcorn",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1831,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #699707\r\n\r\n[b]Popcorn[/b] is a type of corn that expands from the kernel and puffs up when heated. A very common snack for movie-goers."
        },
        {
          "tag": "trash",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1823,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Trash[/b], also known as [i]garbage [/i]or [i]rubbish[/i], is discarded, unwanted, and/or unusable waste materials. \r\n\r\nThis tag is most often used for scenes where various items such as half-eaten food, containers (bottles, boxes, etc.), wrappers, sheets of paper, or crumpled up papers are shown littered on the ground or shown within a trash can, trash bag, or dumpster. \r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n\r\n* [[dumpster]]\r\n* [[recycling bin]]\r\n* [[trash bag]]\r\n* [[trash can]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[discarded object]] - (for items that aren't trash, but have been thrown aside)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "leucistic",
          "kor": "백색증",
          "count": 1822,
          "wiki_body": "Leucism appears similar to, and often confused for, [[albino|albinism]]. \r\n\r\nThe main difference is in the eye color, which is not affected by Leucism. It's safe to assume that if a character doesn't have red eyes, they are leucistic and not albino.\r\n\r\n[[piebald|Piebaldism]] is technically partial leucism, but is unique enough to have its own classifications and designations. \r\n\r\nAlso, characters based on species that can't be albino (like [[white_tiger|white tigers]]) CAN be leucistic. \r\n\r\nWikipedia page: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leucism"
        },
