        {
          "tag": "moss",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1766,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Mosses[/b] are small flowerless [[plant|plants]] that typically grow in dense green clumps or mats, often in damp or shady locations. The individual plants are usually composed of simple [[leaf|leaves]] that are generally only one cell thick, attached to a stem that may be branched or unbranched and has only a limited role in conducting water and nutrients.\r\n\r\nMosses do not produce seeds. They are also commonly confused with [[lichen|lichens]], hornworts, and liverworts."
