        {
          "tag": "bouncing",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1755,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3253809 thumb #3259704 thumb #2026031 thumb #2036016 thumb #1480912 thumb #3187562 thumb #2697050\r\n\r\n[b]Bouncing[/b] can describe several similar concepts related to a character's whole body moving up and down. As most posts tagged \"bouncing\" are animations, all examples above are animated.\r\n\r\n[quote]\r\n\r\nh6. Bouncing can be applied to:\r\n\r\n* A character bouncing on their feet, shifting their weight from foot to foot \r\n** often seen as an \"idle movement\" or \"idle animation\" for a character in animations styled after video games (and frequently seen in pixel art)\r\n* A character bouncing up and down on a soft surface or object, such as a bed, trampoline, or large ball\r\n* A character bouncing up and down during sex, or riding a sex toy,  this should only be applied if the character is [i]actually bouncing[/i], not simply because they're thrusting or lowering themselves onto the sex toy or their partner's penis\r\n\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\nA bouncing character may wobble, or squish as they bounce. A character bouncing may cause specific parts of their body to also bounce or jiggle (e.g. [[bouncing breasts]], [[butt jiggle]]) - ideally, this tag should be reserved to describe \"whole body bouncing\", rather than being automatically added alongside specific `bouncing_*` tags. \r\n\r\nh4. Bouncing Tags:\r\n* [[Bouncing Balls]]\r\n* [[Bouncing Belly]]\r\n* [[Bouncing Breasts]]\r\n* [[Bouncing Butt]]\r\n* [[Bouncing Ears]]\r\n* [[Bouncing Pecs]]\r\n* [[Bouncing Penis]]\r\n* [[Bouncing Tail]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[Jiggling]]\r\n** [[Breast Jiggle]]\r\n** [[Belly Jiggle]]\r\n** [[Butt Jiggle]]\r\n** [[Thigh Jiggle]]\r\n\r\n"
