        {
          "tag": "thick_calves",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1724,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #2235424 thumb #1535074 thumb #3866275 thumb #3129548 thumb #54576\r\n\r\n[b]Thick calves[/b] describes a character whose lower legs are large in circumference and/or overall size. While the [i]calf muscles[/i] are specifically located on the back of the legs, this tag uses \"calves\" as shorthand for the entire lower leg. \r\n\r\nA character may have thick calves due to muscle definition, fat, or the art style - when done as a stylistic choice, the character's lower legs will often \"merge\" with their ankles and feet (see example 4 and 5).\r\n\r\nCharacters with thick calves will almost always also have [[thick thighs]].\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[muscular legs]]\r\n** [[muscular thighs]]\r\n** [[muscular calves]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "fully_submerged",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1720,
          "wiki_body": "A character that has no part of them that isn't submerged in a liquid. This tag also applies to aquatic life.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[underwater]] - Use when the scene is viewed from entirely below the surface of a liquid.\r\n* [[waterline_view]] - Use when the scene is viewed partway inside of a liquid.\r\n* [[waterscape]] - Use when the scene is viewed from above the water, but there is mostly water visible.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[partially_submerged]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "cabinet",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1706,
          "wiki_body": "A box shaped piece of furniture featuring a door and / or drawers. Cabinets are primarily used for storage.\r\n\r\nh4. Types of Cabinets\r\n\r\nh5. Structures\r\n\r\n* [[base_cabinet]] - A cabinet featuring a [[countertop]] or base on top.\r\n* [[wall_cabinet]] - A cabinet fixed onto a wall surface. Kitchen cabinets are commonly wall cabinets.\r\n\r\nh5. Function\r\n\r\n* [[file_cabinet]] / [[filing_cabinet]] - A cabinet used to store documents and files. It is commonly seen in [[office|offices]]. \r\n* [[kitchen_cabinet]] - A cabinet used to store kitchenware, or food.\r\n* [[locker]] - A metal cabinet commonly found in [[locker_room|locker rooms]], schools, and other public areas. The primary function of a locker is to securely store items with a padlock or built-in locking mechanism.\r\n* [[medicine_cabinet]] - A metal container that is commonly seen in [[bathroom|bathrooms]] to store ointments, and medications.\r\n* [[wardrobe]] - A standing closet usually placed in a bedroom for storing clothes.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[closet]]\r\n* [[dresser]]\r\n* [[pantry]]"
