        {
          "tag": "toothed_beak",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1698,
          "wiki_body": "A toothed beak is a [[beak]] of a character that contains visible [[teeth]]. They're almost always [[sharp teeth]], and sometimes these teeth are built into the beak and are [[jagged mouth|jagged edges acting as teeth]]. These types of beaks are often seen in marine [[avian|avians]] such as [[goose|geese]]. They often are seen on [[dinosaur|dinosaurs]] as well, especially [[feathered dinosaur|feathered dinosaurs]] and/or [[theropod|theropods]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[Avian]]\r\n* [[Beak]]\r\n* [[Dinosaur]]\r\n** [[Feathered Dinosaur]]\r\n** [[Theropod]]\r\n* [[Jagged Mouth]]"
