        {
          "tag": "map",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1696,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1323581 thumb #1125594 thumb #226843\r\n\r\nA map (specifically a geographic map) is a section of the [[earth]], or the entirety of it, depicted on a flat surface (typically a foldable sheet of [[paper]]). The appearance of this depiction differs from map to map, depending on the given map's purpose. For example, maps intended for [[hiking]] will often paint different types of terrain with different colors and add icons denoting points of interest. A notable type of map is the [[treasure_map]], which features a large X-shape to mark the location of buried [[treasure]].\r\n\r\nDue to the fact that the surface of a sphere cannot be projected onto a flat surface without distortion, no map can be completely accurate to how the earth really looks. For that purpose, you'll need a [[globe]]."
