          "tag": "the_truth",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1548,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3527671 thumb #2290317 thumb #1522870 thumb #1633895 thumb #1698881\r\n\r\nA tag used for posts that may depict something \"truthful\" but in a funny way, something negative that isn't (necessarily or entirely) true, and/or depict something relatable (usually with a lot of self-depreciation).\r\nThey may also take something overly literally or apply realism to a fictional scenario for comedic effect, or simply state something extremely obvious. \r\n\r\nPosts under this tag are often meta-commentary on the Furry Fandom or e621 itself, reference the artist's life, or are generally relatable. As a fairly subjective tag, older posts tend to be dated memes, negative stereotypes, or confusing [[grandfathered content]]. \r\n\r\n[b]Note: While [[lies]] is [i]technically[/i] the opposite of this tag, it is used in a more straightforward manner — for characters actually telling lies.[/b]\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[meme]]\r\n* [[humor]]\r\n* [[relatable]] \r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[grandfathered content]]\r\n* [[what]]\r\n** [[why]]\r\n** [[where is your god now]]\r\n** [[what has science done]]\r\n"
