          "tag": "v-cut",
          "kor": "V컷",
          "count": 1525,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1975060 thumb #1172208 thumb #1831239 thumb #1292092\r\n\r\nThe [b]v-cut[/b] (also known as [b]apollo's belt[/b], [b]adonis belt[/b], [b]iliac furrow[/b], [b]inguinal crease[/b] and [b]v-muscle[/b]) is a distinctive v-shape besides and below the [[abs]] formed by the inguinal ligaments. Their particular shape and angle serve to draw attention to the crotch. They're determined by genetics but their prominence is affected by fat deposits, muscle tone and others, as are [[hip dips]], and [[butt dimples]] and [[back dimples]].\r\n\r\nThese are distinct from simple [[crotch lines]], the folds on the front of the body at the point the legs meet the hip, which obviously is universal in humans.\r\n\r\nh4. External:\r\n* \"Wikipedia - Apollo's_belt\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo%27s_belt\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[abs]]\r\n* [[athletic]]\r\n* [[back dimples]]\r\n* [[butt dimples]]\r\n* [[crotch lines]]\r\n* [[fupa]]\r\n* [[hip dips]]\r\n* [[iliac crest]]\r\n* [[muscular]]\r\n* [[pubic mound]]\r\n\r\nNot to be confused with [[v-neck]]."
