          "kor": "",
          "count": 1414,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1772114 thumb #1427095 thumb #2871750\r\n\r\nA [b]wrestling singlet[/b] (or simply a [b]singlet[/b]) is a one-piece, tight-fitting, article of [[sportswear]] clothing, used in wrestling that's made of elastic materials like [[spandex]]. It consists of straps that go over the shoulders similar to a [[tank top]] fused at the waistline to a [[shorts]]-like bottom.\r\n\r\nh3. Variations:\r\n* thumb #4155131 The [i]high cut[/i], which covers most of the chest and reaches up to the under-arms on the side. \r\n* thumb #2173047 The [i]low cut[/i], which reaches down to the lower/middle abdomen in the front, reaches down to the hips on the sides, and features a single strap that runs up the back that is very thin.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with:\r\n* [[Tank Top]] - Usually made of polyester and cotton without a bottom part.\r\n** Also, a tank top and shorts are two separate articles of clothing that are not joined at the waistline, unlike a wrestling singlet.\r\n* [[One-piece Swimsuit]] - One-piece swimsuits make a \"V\" shape pattern around the thigh similar to that of a [[bikini]], and typically do not have the parts that cover the uppermost part of the legs.\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[Tag Group:Clothes]]\r\n* [[Leotard]]\r\n* [[Sportswear]]\r\n* [[Tight Clothing]]\r\n* [[Wrestling Briefs]] - In \"rare cases\":/posts/2017165, a character might wear both a singlet and briefs."
