          "tag": "interjection",
          "kor": "감탄사",
          "count": 1387,
          "wiki_body": "An [b]interjection[/b] is a word, phrase, or expression that occurs as an utterance on its own. \nUsed to express a spontaneous feeling, situation, or reaction, interluding their [[dialogue]] and/or absence of it. Use of interjections is diverse, taking the form of [[exclamation point|exclamations]], [[insult|insults]], [[profanity]], [[greeting|greetings]], responses, or hesitation markers, among miscellaneous uses and combinations thereof.\n\n[section=Examples of interjections]\nh4. \"English\":https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:English_interjections\n* bingo\n* bitch\n** son of a bitch\n* cheers\n* [[come_on_(interjection)|come on]]\n* damn\n** god damn\n* damnit\n** god damnit\n* [[dunno]]\n** i dunno\n* err\n* fuck\n** fuck off\n** fuck you\n** holy fuck\n* good day\n** good morning\n** good afternoon\n** good evening\n* good night\n* golly\n** by golly\n** golly gosh\n* gosh\n** golly gosh\n* haha\n* hallelujah\n* [[happy birthday]]\n* [[hawk_tuah_(meme)|hawk tuah]]\n* hello\n** hewwo\n* hey\n** heya\n* [[hmm]]\n* how\n* howdy\n* huh\n* [[huzzah]]\n* let's go\n* [[oh my]]\n** [[oh my god]]\n* okay\n* [[ouch]]\n* [[ow]]\n* shit\n** holy shit\n* uh\n* um\n* welcome\n* what\n* who\n* wow\n** wowie\n** wowzers\n* yes\n* yeah\n\nh4. \"French\":https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:French_interjections\n* au revoir \"goodbye\", \"until the reseeing\"\n* bon appétit \"enjoy your meal\"\n* bonjour \"good day\"\n* [[sacre bleu]] \"holy blue\"\n* voilà \"look there\"\n\nh4. \"German\":https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:German_interjections\n* achtung \"warning\", \"careful\"\n* [[heil]] \"health\", \"hail\", \"salvation\"\n* ja \"yes\"\n* nein \"no\"\n* prost \"cheers\"\n* scheißen \"shit\"\n* willkommen \"welcome\"\n\nh4. \"Greek\":https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Greek_interjections\n* εύρηκα [i]éurika[/i] \"I have found it\"\n\nh4. \"Italian\":https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Italian_interjections\n* arrivederci \"goodbye\", \"to see ourselves again\"\n* ciao \"hello\", \"goodbye\"\n\nh4. \"Japanese\":https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Japanese_interjections\n* はい [i]hai[/i] \"yes\", \"uh-huh\", \"sorry\", \"go\"\n* いいえ [i]īe[/i] \"no\"\n** いえいえ [i]ieie[/i] \"not at all\"\n* 何 [i]nani[/i] \"what\"\n* 笑 [i]warai[/i] \"haha\", \"w(arai)\"\n\nh4. \"Portuguese\":https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Portuguese_interjections\n* oi \"hey\"\n\nh4. \"Russian\":https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Russian_interjections\n* блядь [i]blyadʹ[/i] \"whore\"\n** сука блядь [i]súka bljadʹ[/i] \"son of a bitch\", \"what the fuck\"\n* да [i]da[/i] \"yes\"\n* нет [i]nyet[/i] \"no\"\n\nh4. \"Spanish\":https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Spanish_interjections\n* ay caramba \"by golly\"\n* bueno \"good\"\n** buenos días \"good morning\"\n** buenos tardes \"good afternoon\"\n** buenos noches \"good night\"\n** muy bueno \"very good\"\n* dale \"go ahead\", \"do it\"\n* dios mío \"oh my god\"\n* jaja \"haha\"\n* mierde \"shit\"\n* vamos \"come on\"\n* vualá \"look there\"\n[/section]\n"
