          "wiki_body": "[b]Top Heavy[/b] describes a physique where the upper body has noticeably more mass than their lower body, often to an exaggerated or disproportionate degree. [i]This tag can be used in two ways:[/i]\r\n\r\n\r\nthumb #3337634 thumb #2888047 thumb #3086509 thumb #1917410 \r\n\r\nTop heavy can be applied to female or gynomorph characters with very large breasts, which together, are equal to, or wider than any lower point of the character's body (waist, hips, etc.). \r\n\r\nThis figure almost always has a [[small waist]], sometimes with narrow hips, comparatively wide shoulders, and a [[skinny]] body (see examples above). A top heavy character of this type will never be overweight or obese, this tag should ideally not be used for characters with average bodies and [[hyper breasts]]. \r\n\r\nthumb #888491 thumb #2485094 thumb #1691775\r\n\r\nTop heavy can also apply to any character with a much larger upper body/chest than lower body, often seen with [[toony]] and exaggerated masculine figures, who will have a very large \"[[big chest|barrel chest]]\" (often muscular), [[broad shoulders]], muscular and/or [[big arms]], and conversely, a small waist, and much smaller/[[short legs|shorter legs]].\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n* [[Small Waist]]\r\n* [[Big Breasts]] | [[Huge Breasts]]\r\n* [[Slim]]\r\n* [[Big Chest]]\r\n* [[Big Hands]]\r\n* [[Big Arms]]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Other Body Types:\r\n* [[Hourglass Figure]]: A character with equally wide shoulders and hips, with a small waist, usually large breasted\r\n* [[Pear-Shaped Figure]]: A character with wide hips, often chubby midsection \r\n* [[Voluptuous]]\r\n* [[Overweight]]\r\n** [[Obese]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[Bottom Heavy]]: The opposite of this tag\r\n* [[Tag Group:Figures]]"
