          "wiki_body": "A [b]jersey[/b] in a sports context refers to a [[shirt]] commonly worn as part of a uniform in competitive sports such as [[American football]], [[basketball]], [[hockey]], [[rugby]], and [[soccer]]. Jerseys commonly feature a team's colors as well as a print of the name, and associated number of a player. Some jerseys will have the name of the team, or that team's [[logo]] printed instead of a player's name.\r\n\r\nA jersey in a non-sports context is a knitted garment that resembles a [[t-shirt]]. It is uncommon to be able to tell the difference, and modern sports jerseys do not adhere to the tradition of knitting the garments. \r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[logo]]\r\n** [[logo_print]]\r\n* [[number_print]]\r\n** [[number_on_jersey]]\r\n* [[text_print]]\r\n** [[text_on_jersey]] \r\n* [[uniform]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:clothes]]"
        },
