          "tag": "torogao",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1262,
          "wiki_body": "トロ顔　(from Japanese – \"[i]Melting Face[/i]\")\r\n\r\nTorogao is a facial expression that indicates a trance-like state of pleasure. The eyebrows are slanted downward toward the sides, framing [[half-closed eyes]] that may be moist with [[tears]]. A half-open mouth, perhaps carelessly adorned with [[saliva]] as pleasure relaxes the facial muscles, is also commonly featured. May furthermore involve [[heavy breathing]] and/or a contented [[smile]].\r\n\r\nWhile often triggered from sexual pleasure, this facial expression might come from other sources of rapture such as eating one's favorite food or receiving a massage.\r\n\r\n[b]Note:[/b] Not to be confused with [[ahegao]], an exceptionally intense and wild-faced version of [b]torogao[/b]. (Ahegao is most easily recognized by the presence of [[eye roll]] and [[tongue out]] features.)\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[ahegao]]\r\n* [[looking pleasured]]"
