        {
          "tag": "sounding_rod",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1224,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3914854 thumb #3575207 thumb #4917466 thumb #4816882 thumb #2558520 thumb #5449614\n\nA [b]sounding rod[/b] (also called \"urethral sound\", \"urethral bougie\" or \"urethral dilator\"), is a rod, usually made of either stainless steel or silicone rubber, that is intended for [[urethral]] stimulation. They can be rigid to stimulate along the shaft of the penis (or for [[pussy sounding]]), or flexible if the intent is to move deeper for [[prostate penetration]] or [[bladder penetration]]. They are a common add-on on [[chastity cage|chastity cages]], where they are usually hollow to let [[cum]] and [[urine]] flow through.\n\nThe name is unrelated to noise, and instead comes from French \"sonde urinaire\" (lit. \"urinary probe\"), which is a term for urethral catheters.\n\nIn gynecology and urology, there are also special types of rods with characteristic shapes used in various circumstances. Among the common ones are: \n* Rosebud dilator (thin straight rod with a bullet at the end)\n* Van Buren dilator (thick rod that curves upwards towards the end)\n* Hegar dilator (thick rod with slight S-shape)\n* Guyon dilator (thick rod that curves down and then back up into somewhat of a hook shape)\n* Brooks dillator (thin rod with two right angle bends and a bullet at the end)\n* Amplatz dilator (tube going down the urethra to the bladder that allows other instruments to easily move through for more complex operations, usually targeting the kidneys)\n\n\nh4. Related tags\n\n* [[urethral]]\n** [[object_in_urethra]]\n** [[pussy_sounding]]\n** [[anal_beads_in_urethra]]"
