          "wiki_body": "thumb #4821785 thumb #3445948 thumb #3042404 thumb #1681859 thumb #3472903\r\n\r\n[b]Iridescence[/b] is a colorful shimmering effect that causes something to appear to change color as the angle of view/lighting changes. Iridescence is most commonly associated with soap [[bubble]]s, [[feathers]] and [[scales]], [[lepidopteran wings|butterfly wings]], [[opal_(gem)|opal]], and [[seashell]]s.\r\n\r\nThis effect is sometimes also referred to as \"holographic\", due to the use of holographic foil to replicate it in clothing and accessories.\r\n\r\nThe iridescent effect can vary in intensity greatly:\r\nthumb #4524417 thumb #3431116\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[glistening]]\r\n* [[glowing]]\r\n* [[rainbow]]\r\n* [[sparkles]]\r\n* [[translucent]]"
