        {
          "tag": "count",
          "kor": "카운트",
          "count": 1112,
          "wiki_body": "A [b]count[/b] is a value that represents a running total or quantity of something. This tag is usually [[number|numerical]] in nature to avoid overlap with [[tally marks]], and has restrictions to how it should be used.\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=General guidelines]\r\n\r\nh5. Good applications\r\n\r\n- Quantities that appear on a [[screen]], excluding monetary amounts.\r\n- Counts that appear as part of a [[video game]] interface.\r\n- Counts that track viewer counts, or patron / customer counts.\r\n- Counts that take the format: `<icon>:<quantity>` or `<icon>x<quantity>`\r\n- Counts that contribute to the context of the image. These are usually displayed prominently on the image.\r\n- Counts that track orgasms, or other sexual activity. This does not include tally marks.\r\n\r\nh4. Things to avoid\r\n\r\n- [[Tally marks]], or things that function like tally marks\r\n- Any value that might be measured in fractional amounts: temperature, weight, volume, etc.\r\n- Most values related to money or time (excludes days, weeks, months, years). See [[time period]]\r\n- Pagination* See [[page_number]]\r\n- Videogame / roleplaying [[stats]]: attack, defense, strength stats, etc.\r\n- Videogame [[score]] totals, points, or experience values\r\n- [[Counting]], or other sequential themes that doesn't refer to something specific such as a day count.\r\n\r\n[sub]* Page totals are allowed, but the current page number should not use this tag. The same rule also applies to chapter numbers.[/sub]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. List of count tags\r\n\r\n* [[day_count]]\r\n* [[hit_count]]\r\n* [[orgasm_count]]\r\n* [[viewer_count]]\r\n"
