          "tag": "urban",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1084,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3547365 thumb #3978098 thumb #2728075 thumb #1605696 thumb #3459115\r\n\r\n[b]Urban[/b] describes a scene set within a [[town]] or [[city]] — more specifically a densely constructed outdoor area (as opposed to a low density residential area of a city, or a scene in a city park) such as storefronts along a main street of a town, an alleyway in a large city, or a crosswalk bordered by large buildings.  \r\n\r\nUrban scenes are determined by their background elements, an urban scene may focus on a character in front of a single building, without showing the rest of the surrounding city or town area, or the focus may be primarily on a single character, with \"urban elements\" suggesting their location. \r\n\r\nUrban scenes may be \"grungy\" with focus on litter, graffiti, damaged walls or surfaces. [[Cyberpunk]] art often depicts urban scenes.\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[alley]]\r\n* [[skate park]] \r\n* [[rooftop]]\r\n* [[detailed background]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[tag_group:locations]]\r\n* [[city]]\r\n** [[cityscape]] - a broad view of a city setting, similar to a landscape\r\n* [[town]]\r\n\r\n"
