        {
          "tag": "under_shade",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 887,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1983368  thumb #1356833 thumb #151925 thumb #2270082  thumb #3201767 \r\n\r\nA character under [[shadow]] cast from blocked [[sunlight]] or, very rarely, a different [[bright]] [[light]] source. Shade is often sought for some relief from intense sunlight to hopefully allow one's body to cool down, particularly their head.\r\n\r\nSome objects and structures are intended to provide shade and other mild relief from the elements, like a [[beach umbrella]] or [[awning]], but a character can use anything for improvised shade, like a large shadow from a [[tree]] or [[building]] or even a [[size_difference|larger character]].\r\n\r\nh5. Tagging Guidance\r\n\r\nThe art does not need to depict the thing casting shade, but the [[detailed_background|setting]], direction of [[lighting]], and [[shadow]] patterns should at least convey:\r\n\r\n* an area that is exposed to a bright, major light source with...\r\n* a character within that area who [i]would be[/i] completely exposed to that light, but...\r\n* that character is meaningfully screened from that light somehow.\r\n\r\nNote that a [[backlighting|backlit]] character may appear [i]under shade[/i] when their body blocks a bright light source behind them and casts a shadow toward the viewer, but that character likely is not themself [i]under shade[/i].\r\n\r\nSemantically, the [[inside|interior contents of buildings]] are not usually considered to provide shade. A possible exception is a character lingering around a [[doorway]] or [[cave]] entrance [i]just before the reach of direct sunlight[/i]. Another exception is [[window shade]] casting a significant shadow on a character while still permitting some light inside.\r\n\r\nthumb #884113 thumb #2668579 \r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Shade sources]\r\n* [[against_surface]] that casts shade\r\n* [[awning]]\r\n* [[building]]\r\n* [[bus_stop]]\r\n* [[cave]] entrance\r\n* [[gazebo]]\r\n* [[shelter]]\r\n* [[size_difference]]\r\n** larger_*\r\n* [[tent]]\r\n* [[tree]]\r\n** [[canopy]] of a forest or cluster of trees\r\n** [[under_tree]]\r\n* [[umbrella]]\r\n** [[beach_umbrella]]\r\n** [[leaf_umbrella]]\r\n** [[parasol]]\r\n* [[wall_(structure)]]\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Shade themes]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Character]\r\n* [[exhausted]]\r\n* [[heat_(temperature)]]\r\n** [[overheated]]\r\n* [[lounge_chair]]\r\n* [[lying]]\r\n* [[picnic]]\r\n* [[relaxing]] / [[resting]]\r\n* [[shading_eyes]]\r\n* [[sunbathing]]\r\n* [[sun_hat]]\r\n* [[sweat]]\r\n* [[tired]]\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Light]\r\n[[light]]\r\n* [[bright]]\r\n* [[dappled_light]]\r\n* [[day]]\r\n* [[lens_flare]]\r\n* [[lighting]]\r\n* [[sun]]\r\n* [[sunlight]]\r\n** [[sunbeam]]\r\n* [[sunny]]\r\n* [[window_shade]]\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Places]\r\n* [[beach]]\r\n* [[desert]]\r\n* [[detailed_background]]\r\n* [[field]]\r\n* [[forest]]\r\n* [[outside]]\r\n* [[park]]\r\n* [[patio]]\r\n* [[porch]]\r\n[/section]"
