          "tag": "weight_difference",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 756,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1312573 thumb #4863006 thumb #5011051 thumb #4488877\r\n\r\n[b]Weight Difference[/b] describes a post containing two or more characters that have visible differences in the amount of body fat between one another — in simple terms: how \"fat\" or \"thin\" they are. \r\n\r\n[quote][b]Not to be confused with a single character being depicted at different weights, see [[weight gain]] or [[weight loss]].[/b][/quote]\r\n\r\nh5. Tagging Notes\r\n[b]This tag should be applied when the differences in weight are immediately and visually obvious[/b] \r\n\r\n* Most commonly this applies to an [[overweight]], [[slightly chubby]], or [[obese]] character depicted alongside a [[skinny]], [[athletic]] or [[muscular]] character\r\n* This tag may apply to cases where two \"fat\" characters are of obviously different \"levels\" of overweight, such as a slightly chubby character and an obese character depicted together\r\n* Weight differences frequently overlap with overall [[size difference]] between characters, this may involve a short fat character and tall thin character, or a character that is larger than average and overweight as well, paired with normal sized characters.\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Other \"Difference\" Tags\r\n[section=Body Parts Size Difference]\r\n* [[anus size difference]]\r\n* [[ball size difference]]\r\n* [[belly size difference]]\r\n* [[breast size difference]]\r\n* [[butt size difference]]\r\n* [[genital size difference]]\r\n* [[muscle size difference]]\r\n* [[nipple size difference]]\r\n* [[penis size difference]]\r\n* [[wing size difference]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[weight gain]]/[[weight loss]]\r\n* [[weight conscious]]"
