          "wiki_body": "[b]Glint[/b] is a property of reflective surfaces when a strong light bounces off the surface in such a way that the luminosity of the light is reflected along with the light image. This will give the appearance that an object is emitting light.\r\n\r\nThis tag should be used for light artifacts that represent glint such as sparkle shapes (concave diamonds, and crosses), or localized glow near the surface of an object. If the entire object has a glow, it is most likely emitting light, and should be tagged [[glowing]] instead.\r\n\r\nh4. Categories\r\n\r\n* [[armor_glint]]\r\n** [[shield_glint]]\r\n* [[eye_glint]]\r\n* [[eyewear_glint]]\r\n* [[gem_glint]]\r\n* [[jewelry_glint]]\r\n* [[piercing_glint]]\r\n* [[weapon_glint]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[glistening]] - Glistening is the tag for general shine across a surface. It refers to the light image itself.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[reflection]]\r\n* [[sparkles]]"
