          "kor": "",
          "count": 664,
          "wiki_body": "A [b]level number[/b] is a stat in many roleplaying games to indicate the progression status of the player. In a tiered leveling system, a player increases their level by accumulating experience points beyond the experience cap for whatever tier they are currently at.\r\n\r\nh4. Related themes\r\n\r\n* [[level_difference]]\r\n* [[level_drain]]\r\n* [[level_up]] - The process of achieving the next level tier.\r\n\r\nh4. Games with level mechanics\r\n\r\n* [[pokémon]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[gameplay_mechanics]]\r\n* [[stats]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "low_poly",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 661,
          "wiki_body": "Low poly, short for \"low polygon\" is a term that refers to computerized 3D models of basic shape. The surface of 3D models are made up of triangles and squares, referred to as polygons, so the more polygons a 3D model has, the smoother it looks. Conversely, the less polygons a 3D model has, the blockier and edgier it looks. By having less polygons or points to record, a 3D model takes up less file space.\r\n\r\nLow poly models are known for their often use in older video games, because of file space constraints, but they have also been used for newer retro style games and ironic/ absurd humor memes."
        },
        {
          "tag": "stasis_chamber",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 661,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #908911 thumb #1390777 thumb #48673\r\n\r\nA common sight in [[mad scientist]] [[laboratory|laboratories]], a [b]stasis chamber[/b] is a large [[container]] of some liquid used to preserve creatures in stasis or just [[contained|contain]] them, [[transformation|modify them]] using large quantities of a liquid formula or some other method, perform other \"[[scientific experiment|scientific experiments]]\" on them, or any combination of the above. Most typically the characters in stasis chambers are unconscious or barely conscious, but not necessarily.\r\n\r\nA stasis chamber may also be non-technological, and for example, biological in nature. Such are cases where monsters create stasis chambers for their prey to sustain them, either as incubators for their young, or as food to be eaten later.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[containment_tube]]\r\n"
        },
        {
          "tag": "falling_leaves",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 659,
          "wiki_body": "A tag describing one or many [[leaf|leaves]] falling from [[tree|trees]], typically signals that an image is set during [[Autumn]]."
