        {
          "tag": "tennis_racket",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 658,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1267826\r\n\r\nA [b]tennis racket[/b] is a sports implement consisting of a handled frame with an open hoop across which a network of strings or catgut is stretched tightly. It is used for striking a [[tennis_ball|ball]] in [[tennis]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[Tennis]]\r\n* [[tag_group:sports|Tag Group: Sports]][[tag_group:sports#equip| - Equipment]]\r\n\r\nh4. External:\r\n\r\n* \"Wikipedia - Racket (sports_equipment)\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Racket_%28sports_equipment%29#Tennis"
        },
        {
          "tag": "polyamory",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 658,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #4413650 thumb #3738667 thumb #2958571 thumb #4687151\r\n\r\n[b]Polyamory[/b] is a term used for consensual romantic relationships involving more than two partners. These relationships may be open - allowing the partners to have other partners outside the relationship, or they may be closed - being just as dedicated as a typical monogamous relationship. Not all partners have to be romantically involved with each other, \"V\" shaped relationships are still polyamorous.\r\n\r\nGenerally speaking, this tag should only be used if there is evidence in the post to suggest the characters are in a romantic relationship, and should not just be used for general [[group sex]] scenarios. [[Romantic ambiance]] or just generally \"loving\" shows of affection should be shown.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n* [[polyamory_pride_colors]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[bisexual]]\r\n* [[group_sex]]\r\n* [[harem]]\r\n* [[infidelity]]\r\n* [[romantic_couple]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "habit",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 658,
          "wiki_body": "Distinctive long, loose religious uniforms worn by clergy.\r\n\r\nh6.Full-length clothing\r\n* [[cassock]]\r\n* [[gown]]\r\n* [[mantle]]\r\n* [[robe]]\r\n* [[scapular]]\r\n\r\nh6.[[Headwear]]\r\n* [[veil]]\r\n\r\nh6.[[Topwear]]\r\n* [[hood]]\r\n** [[cowl]]\r\n* [[tunic]]\r\n\r\nh6.[[Legwear]]\r\n* [[hakama]]\r\n\r\nh6.Other\r\n* [[belt]]\r\n** [[cincture]]\r\n* [[clerical_collar]]\r\n* [[sash]]\r\n\r\nh5.See also\r\n* [[monk]]\r\n* [[nun]]\r\n* [[priest]]\r\n* [[religious_clothing]]\r\n* [[shrine_maiden]]"
