        {
          "tag": "hiccuping",
          "kor": "딸꾹질",
          "count": 630,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Hiccuping[/b] are involuntary contractions of the diaphragm that may repeat several times per minute, which causes a closure of the vocal cords with each contraction, resulting in repeat \"hic\" or \"hiccup\" sounds. Hiccuping is most often caused by rapid eating or swallowing excess amounts of air, it is often associated with a character being drunk, or having eaten a large amount of food.\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[burping]]\r\n* [[fart]]\r\n\r\n\r\n"
        },
        {
          "tag": "alternating_focus",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 630,
          "wiki_body": "Use when the prominent focus of a character in one frame / panel changes to the prominent focus of another character in the next/adjacent frame / panel.\r\n\r\nThis tag primarily targets [[comic|comics]], but it may have applications in non-comic material, especially content that highlights the reaction of two or more characters in separate frames.\r\n\r\nh4. General guidelines\r\n\r\n* The change in focus is usually deliberate, and meaningful to the scene. There may be arbitrary changes in focus that would not be a great fit for this tag.\r\n* Consider adding only if the zoom/crop level doesn't change too drastically between the frames."
        },
        {
          "tag": "keikogi",
          "kor": "케이코기",
          "count": 629,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #934056\r\n\r\n[b]Keikogi[/b] (or simply [b]gi[/b]) is a [[uniform]] used for training in martial arts derived from Japan.\r\n\r\nh4. External:\r\n\r\n* \"Wikipedia - Keikogi\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keikogi"
        },
        {
          "tag": "garage",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 628,
          "wiki_body": "A room to park and repair vehicles in, especially cars.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[tag_group:locations]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "younger_ambiguous",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 628,
          "wiki_body": "An [[ambiguous gender]] character depicted with another character who is visibly [i]older[/i] than them; making that ambiguous character [i]younger[/i] than the other character. Note that this tag does [b][i]not[/i][/b] indicate that the ambiguous character is [[young]], this tag can apply to an adult ambiguous character who is younger than an older, mature or elderly adult.\r\n\r\nh6. For the \"opposite age\", see [[older ambiguous]]\r\n\r\nh5. [[Age Difference]] Tags:\r\n\r\n[section= Older]\r\nA character that is older than another within the same scene. This doesn't mean the character is necessarily mature, middle aged, or elderly, these tags merely compare them to another character in the same image. If the character is middle aged use the appropriate mature_* tags,  (see the mature section in \"see also\" below).\r\n\r\n* [[older ambiguous]]\r\n* [[older female]]\r\n* [[older male]]\r\n* [[older intersex]]\r\n** [[older andromorph]]\r\n** [[older gynomorph]]\r\n** [[older herm]]\r\n** [[older maleherm]]\r\n\r\n[/section] \r\n\r\n[section= Younger]\r\nA character that is younger than another within the same scene. This doesn't mean the \"younger\" character is necessarily [[young]], a [[child]], or [[cub]], these tags merely compare them to the other character in the same image.\r\n\r\n* [b]younger ambiguous[/b]\r\n* [[younger female]]\r\n* [[younger male]]\r\n* [[younger intersex]]\r\n** [[younger andromorph]]\r\n** [[younger gynomorph]]\r\n** [[younger herm]]\r\n** [[younger maleherm]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Related:\r\n\r\n[section= Mature]\r\n[b]Mature[/b] describes characters that are \"middle aged\" - in human terms, this is generally around ages 45-65, however, this tag is more concerned with the visual appearance of the character rather than strict definitions of chronological age. If a mature character is in an image with a younger character, the post should also be tagged with the appropriate older_* and younger_* tags above.\r\n\r\n* [[mature ambiguous]]\r\n* [[mature female]]\r\n* [[mature male]]\r\n* [[mature intersex]]\r\n** [[mature andromorph]]\r\n** [[mature gynomorph]]\r\n** [[mature herm]]\r\n** [[mature maleherm]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also: \r\n\r\n* [[age difference]]\r\n* [[young]]\r\n* [[old]]\r\n* [[aged down]]\r\n* [[aged up]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "overweight_top",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 627,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #5414498 thumb #4677113 thumb #4390385\n\nWhen an [[overweight]] character is the \"top\" and/or is penetrating during sexual activity.\n\nh4. Related Tags:\n* [[overweight_dom]] - If the top is also the dominant partner. [i]May not always apply.[/i]\n* [[overweight_sub]] - If the top is also [[submissive]] (eg. [[service_top]])\n\nh4. See Also:\n* [[muscular]]\n** [[muscular_bottom]]\n** [[muscular_top]]\n* [[overweight]]\n** [[overweight_bottom]]\n** [b]overweight_top[/b]"
