          "tag": "yandere",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 621,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #4625884 thumb #4371477 thumb #3390323 thumb #238611 thumb #145272\r\n\r\n[b]Yandere[/b] is a Japanese character archetype involving a character with feelings of love and attraction that are so intense they become mentally unstable, leading the character to become inclined towards stalking and violence. Yandere characters are extremely possessive and will often threaten or harm anyone who gets in the way of them and their object of affection. In order for this tag to apply, a post must depict clear and obvious yandere behavior.\r\n\r\nThe term yandere is derived from [i]yanderu[/i] (ヤンデル, mentally unstable), and [i]deredere[/i] (デレデレ, lovestruck).\r\n\r\n[quote]\r\nh5. Common ways to depict yandere characters\r\n* Possessive and controlling behavior, i.e. \"you will be mine\"\r\n* [[Heart eyes]] juxtaposed with blood splatters, weapons, and threats\r\n* Violent outbursts towards their love interest or perceived \"threats\"\r\n* Physically restraining the object of their obsession\r\n* \"Crazed\" facial expressions, in combination with other elements\r\n* The phrase \"love me\", especially repeated\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\nThese things should not inherently be tagged yandere.\r\n* [[jealous]]\r\n* [[possessive]]\r\n* [[sadism]]\r\n* [[yandere_trance]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[gurokawa]]\r\n* [[jirai_kei]]\r\n* [[menhera]]"
