          "wiki_body": "thumb #1528680 thumb #3831943 thumb #3756486\n\nExtreme thinness from absence of body fat and lack of muscle — a character that is essentially \"skin and bones\", [[skinny]] to an extreme and, oftentimes, unhealthy degree. \n\nAn emaciated character's [[ribs]] or entire rib cage will be visible under their skin, their pelvic bones may be visible as well, their abdomen concave, and their limbs thin and bony; the character's cheeks and eye sockets may even be concave. \n\n\"Emaciation\" by definition is a sign of malnutrition and/or disease — however, some characters, especially ones intended to appear monstrous, are \"naturally emaciated\" in appearance without necessarily being starved or diseased. \n\n[b]This tag can also be used to describe apparently healthy, but [i]extremely skinny[/i] characters — e.g. the third example image above. [/b] A \"healthy\" emaciated character will typically only have thin limbs, a narrow torso, and visible ribs.\n\nh4. See Also\n* [[anorexia]]\n* [[tag group:figures]]\n** [[skinny]]\n\nh4. Tagging Projects\n* Correctly label emaciated posts mistagged as [[skinny]] or other figures.\n* {{emaciated -emaciated_*}}: Tag forms and gender where possible."
