          "tag": "ashtray",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 586,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #5026475 thumb #3368187 thumb #4294201 thumb #4984244\r\n\r\nAn [b]ashtray[/b] is a container designed to hold [[tobacco]] [[ashes]], and incidentally [[cigarette]] and [[cigar]] butts.\r\n\r\nThe best-known small-scale models are for domestic use. However, there are also larger models, called \"outdoor ashtrays\", which can be placed on the ground or fixed to a [[wall (structure)|wall]] [i](in public places, [[airport|airports]], etc)[/i].\r\n\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashtray\r\n\r\nFor a form of [[degradation]] where a character is used as one, see [[living_ashtray]].\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[ashes]]\r\n* [[smoking]]\r\n** [[cigar]]\r\n** [[cigarette]]\r\n** [[hookah]]\r\n** [[kiseru]]\r\n** [[smoking_pipe]]"
