        {
          "tag": "rumbling",
          "kor": "울부짖음",
          "count": 585,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Rumbling[/b] is a continuous low-toned sound represented by the [[onomatopoeia]] \"rumble\", or \"grumble\". The actual sound for the tone may vary.\r\n\r\nThis tag is most consistently used if restricted to sounds based on the onomatopoeic terms. Other sound effects such as \"gurgle\", or \"groan\" such as those that fall under [[rumbling_stomach]] may not fit a general purpose rumbling tag, but depending on if there is a need for a 'rumbling' variant for other body parts, this tag could serve as a base.\r\n\r\n[b]Sound effect forms:[/b] \"Rumble\", \"Grumble\", \"Rmmbll\", \"Grmmbll\", \"Rrrbll\", \"Rmmb\"\r\n\r\nh4. Tagging notes\r\n\r\n* Rumble packs are named for the sounds they make. If there are only [[motion lines]], tag as [[vibrating]] instead.\r\n* Despite being heavily associated with stomach noises, this is general purpose sound effect.\r\n\r\nh4. Related themes\r\n\r\n* [[bodily_noises]] - This theme applies to rumbling that applies to digestion, or hunger.\r\n* [[hungry]]\r\n* [[rumbling_stomach]]\r\n\r\nh4. Similar forms\r\n\r\n* Sound effect forms such as \"Growl\", \"Groan\", \"Grr\", or \"Grrrnnn\" should be tagged as [[rumbling_stomach]] instead.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:sound_effects]]\r\n\r\n* [[sound_effects]]\r\n* [[vibrating]]"
