          "wiki_body": "[b]Glurk[/b] is a common [[sound_effects|sound effect]] associated with [[swallowing]], and the [[digestion|digestive]] process. It is almost always depicted in the reduced form \"Glrk\". This sound may be an indication of [[gagging]] rather than swallowing in [[deep throat]] images.\r\n\r\n[b]Sound effect forms:[/b] \"Glurk\", \"Glork\", \"Glrk\", \"Grk\"\r\n\r\n- \"Glk\", and \"Gluk\" are tagged as shortened forms of [[gluck]] instead.\r\n\r\nh4. Related themes\r\n\r\n* [[digestion]]\r\n** [[digestion_noises]]\r\n* [[gagging]]\r\n* [[swallowing]]\r\n** [[swallowing_sound_effect]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[shortened_sound_effect]] - If it is \"Glrkk\", it should be tagged as [[sound_effect_variant]] instead.\r\n* [[vowelless_sound_effect]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:sound_effects]]\r\n\r\n* [[sound_effects]]\r\n** [[gluck]] (\"Glk\")\r\n** [[glunk_(sound_effect)]]\r\n** [[glup]]\r\n** [b]glurk[/b]\r\n** [[slurk]]"
