          "tag": "hissing",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 573,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Hissing[/b] refers to the production of a long, repeated 'S', or 'Sh' sound either audibly, or as a [[sound_effects|sound effect]]. It is represented by the onomatopoeia \"Hiss\".\r\n\r\nh4. Common applications\r\n\r\n* Certain animals make hissing noises, and artists may choose to use hissing sounds to make a creature appear more provocative, and dangerous. The [[animal_noises]] tag should be used anytime a character produces this sound.\r\n* This is the sound of escaping air, as from an [[inflatable]].\r\n* [[Sizzling]], a boiling sound effect, usually makes a hissing sound. Hissing will appear in [[digestion]] themes.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[extended_sound_effect]] - As long as it is more than just 'S\", this tag should be used when there are extra letters.\r\n* [[vowelless_sound_effect]] - Non-onomatopoeic forms of this sound are probably going to fall under this concept. \r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[psssh]] - A closely related sound representation of running water, and sometimes escaping gas.\r\n* [[shush]] - \"Shh\""
