        {
          "tag": "stylus",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 561,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1106296 thumb #2361914\r\n\r\nA stylus is a pen-shaped instrument a computer or console can detected and use as a input device. They are often used to assist in navigating or providing more precision when using touchscreens. examples include the [[https://web.archive.org/web/20230912222229/https://www.nintendo.com/en-ca/store/products/stylus-black-105213| Nintendo DS stylus]] and [[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Pencil|Apple Pencil]]. This tag usually refers to a narrow elongated staff, similar to a modern ballpoint pen. \r\n\r\nh4. Also known as:\r\n* Active pen\r\n* Digital pen\r\n* Light pen - An input device invented in 1951, predating the modern stylus pen.\r\n* Stylus pen\r\n\r\nh5. Not to be confused with...\r\n* [[stylus (object)]] - Ancient writing implement that predates the Light pen.\r\n* [[tablet_pen]] - A computer input device paired with a drawing tablet used to make art & animations.\r\n\r\nh4. External:\r\n\r\n* \"Wikipedia - Stylus\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stylus_(computing))"
