          "tag": "mantle_(mollusk)",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 511,
          "wiki_body": "The [b]mantle[/b] is a part of the anatomy of [[mollusk|mollusks]]. It is the outer body wall which covers the internal flesh of the mollusc, and often also can have protruding [[frill|frills]]. It is most commonly seen in [[cephalopod|cephalopods]], where it is often the most noticeable, and is often perceived by the average viewer as the \"head\" or \"[[skull]]\" of the creature. In some mollusks (usually [[gastropod|gastropods]]), the skin on the mantle secretes calcium carbonate and conchiolin, and creates a [[shell]], however for simplification's sake these are just tagged as shell.\r\n\r\nh4. Related\r\n\r\n* [[mollusk]]\r\n** [[cephalopod]]\r\n* [[shell]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[hole_(anatomy)]]\r\n* [[pouch_(anatomy)]]\r\n* [[siphon_(anatomy)]]"
