        {
          "tag": "front_and_back",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 498,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1257930 thumb #2237263 thumb #3084740 thumb #3731669\r\n\r\n[b]Front and back[/b] describes an image depicting a single character from a [[front view]] and a [[rear view]]. Front and back images are common for [[dakimakura design|dakimakura designs]] and [[model sheet|model sheets]].\r\n\r\n\r\nh5. Features of a Front and Back Image\r\n\r\n* The two views of the character are typically side-by-side\r\n* Many `front_and_back` images depict the character in the same pose, from the same angle, and are framed in the same way (e.g. two full length images of the character)\r\n* Some `front_and_back` images can show different poses and framing of the character, (e.g. a [[full length portrait]] front view, and a closer cropped, [[butt focus|butt focused]] rear view)\r\n\r\n\r\nh5. Tagging Notes\r\n\r\n* These two views should be [b]the focus of the image[/b], not incidental to a comic, sequence or sketch page\r\n* This tag should not apply to an animation depicting a character from the front and rear, use [[multiple angles]] instead\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[front view]]\r\n* [[rear view]]\r\n* [[three-quarter view]]\r\n* [[multiple angles]]\r\n* [[multiple poses]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* Similar concepts:\r\n** [[before and after]]\r\n** [[off/on]] "
