          "tag": "popping",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 490,
          "wiki_body": "This term has two meanings:\r\n\r\n- The sudden loss of internal pressure of an [[inflatable]], or something physically behaving like an inflatable caused by a sharp object (i.e. a needle, a pin, etc.) puncturing it, direct contact with hot surfaces or sources of heat, sitting, straddling or lying on it until it pops, overinflating, etc.\r\n\r\nh5. Tagging notes\r\n\r\nPopping should be seen as the less gruesome cousin to the bursting fetish. All living creatures that are having their bodies rupture by an internal pressure should be tagged [[bursting]]. Examples that lack the anticipated [[gore]] that follows such an event may be tagged as both `bursting`, and `popping`. Inanimate objects such as balloons, and pool toys should only use `popping`.\r\n\r\n- Activities that are recognized, and named after the sound produced from a sudden internal expansion (think popping corn). This is a less viable interpretation of the `popping` definition.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[bursting_out]]\r\n* [[button_pop]]\r\n\r\nh4. Popping concepts\r\n\r\n* [[balloon_popping]] - Subconcept to `popping`\r\n* [[popping_bubble|bubble_popping]] - Subconcept to `popping`\r\n* [[cork_popping]] - Might be a subconcept to `popping`\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[pop_(sound_effect)]]\r\n* [[popped_balloon]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[deflating]]\r\n* [[inflating]]\r\n** [[inflating_balloon]]"
