          "wiki_body": "thumb #3184021\r\n\r\n[b][i]Canada[/i][/b] is a federation of ten provinces and three territories comprising most of northern North America, it is a parliamentary democracy and a constitutional monarchy. The country is known for [[maple syrup]], [[poutine]], [[hockey|ice hockey]], the [[Royal Canadian Mounted Police]] (or \"Mounties\"), stereotypical politeness of its populace, as well as its vast unspoiled wilderness and national parks.\r\n\r\nAnimals endemic to and associated with Canada include [[beaver|beavers]] (the national animal), [[moose]], [[canada goose|Canada Geese]], [[Canadian Lynx]], and [[polar bear|Polar Bears]]\r\n\r\nThis tag is for posts depicting Canadian characters, characters wearing clothing related to Canada, the [[Canadian flag]], Canadian symbols, locations or [[landmark|landmarks]] in Canada, or other images associated with Canada/Canadian culture.\r\n\r\nh4. Additional Notes\r\n* Canada's capital city is [[Ottawa]], and largest city is [[Toronto]] — other major cities include [[Montreal]], Vancouver, Calgary, Edmonton, Quebec City, and Halifax. \r\n* Canada is the second largest [[tag group:countries|country]] on [[Earth]] (after [[Russia]])  \r\n** As much of the nation's north is a vast hinterland of taiga and tundra, it is sparsely populated, most of Canada's 40 million citizens reside in southern parts of the country. \r\n* Canada is an officially bilingual country, with an [[English]] speaking majority, and a large [[French]] speaking minority\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* [[canadian flag]]\r\n** [[canadian flag bikini]]\r\n* [[canada day]]\r\n* [[maple leaf]]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[tag group:countries]]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n"
