          "wiki_body": "thumb #1698838 thumb #1535564 thumb #236007 thumb #231739\r\n\r\nFor posts with directly and deliberately contrasting themes or imagery. Sometimes the duality is purely aesthetic, but often it suggests deeper meaning. Such themes include:\r\n\r\n* light and dark\r\n* red and blue\r\n* hot and cold\r\n* happy and sad\r\n* good and evil\r\n* peace and destruction\r\n* human and animal\r\n* female and male\r\n* inhibition and zeal\r\n* outward facade and inner feeling\r\n* reality and a heartfelt wish\r\n* normality and insanity\r\n\r\nIdeally, the dual themes compete with, offset, or reflect each other and combine to make a greater whole, often communicating with the viewer some truth, secret, or desire. \r\n\r\nh5.Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[altered_reflection]]\r\n* [[altered_shadow]]\r\n* [[alternate_form]]\r\n* [[alternate_species]]\r\n* [[dual_persona]]\r\n* [[split_screen]]\r\n* [[square_crossover]]\r\n\r\nh5.See also\r\n\r\n* [[yin_yang]]"
