          "kor": "나노",
          "count": 376,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1816303 thumb #2782871 thumb #2998817\n\n[b]Nano[/b] describes characters that are [b]extremely [/b]small, smaller than even an average [[micro]] character, their height is best measured by micrometres (they should not exceed 1-2 mm tall), and sometimes even smaller units of size. At 1-2 mm tall, a character would be about a thousandth the height of a human, making them about a billionth the mass and volume, fitting with the metric prefix \"nano\". Nano characters size can be directly compared to small bugs, or microscopic organisms such as [[tardigrade|tardigrades]] depending on the size of the character involved.\n\nDo not use this tag if there are nothing within the frame suggesting the scale of the creature in question. Common traits of nano posts include the nano characters being too small for macro characters to [[unaware|notice]], having to navigate forests of [[carpet]] or the \"terrain\" of normal sized characters' bodies (such as ridges or wrinkles in their skin, a [[pawscape]], a \"forest\" of fur, hair, feathers, etc), being smaller than drops of water etc.\n\nNano is the inverse of [[giga]], in the same way that [[micro]] is the inverse of [[macro]].\n\nh4. See also: \n\n* [[giga]] (antonym)\n** [[macro]] (moderate antonym)\n** [[terra_macro|tera]] (very extreme antonym)\n* [[micro]] (moderate)\n* [[extreme size difference]]"
