          "wiki_body": "To make forceful contact with something.\r\n\r\nh4. General guidelines \r\n\r\n- This tag is intended to be used for certain acts of [[violence]] such as [[punch|punches]], and [[kick|kicks]] that make direct contact with a character, or the immediate scene following such a contact.\r\n- This tag is more about the perceived impact. Even if a character sustains a wound by a slicing weapon, the presentation of the impact may still allow this tag to be used. \r\n- This tag may involve [[slap|slaps]], and other forms of [[spanking]].\r\n- Blunt weapon impacts are fine to use this tag. Slicing, and stabbing though are not the focus of this tag.\r\n- Body slams are a grey area, and full body impacts such as [[crush|crushing]] may not fit well in this tag.\r\n- Projectile impacts (bullets, arrows, etc.) probably shouldn't use this tag if the impact isn't a perceived focus."
