          "wiki_body": "thumb #857061 thumb #1148803 thumb #1759824\r\n\r\nA tankard is a form of drinkware consisting of a large, roughly cylindrical, drinking cup with a single handle.\r\n\r\nTankards are usually made of silver, pewter, or glass, but can be made of other materials, for example wood, ceramic or leather.\r\n\r\nA tankard may have a hinged lid, and tankards featuring glass bottoms are also fairly common. Tankards are shaped and used similarly to beer [[stein|steins]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[cup]]\r\n** [[drinking_glass]]\r\n*** [[champagne_glass]]\r\n*** [[cocktail_glass]]\r\n*** [[shot_glass]]\r\n*** [[whiskey_glass]]\r\n*** [[wine_glass]]\r\n** [[mug]]\r\n*** [[stein]]\r\n*** [b]tankard[/b]"
