          "wiki_body": "thumb #2765830 thumb #5623056 Thumb #5606366\n\nA pride flag used to represent the entire LGBT+ community, as well as solidarity with trans and POC members of the community. It features the standard [[rainbow_pride_colors|rainbow flag]] with a chevron that includes the [[transgender pride colors]], as well as a brown and black stripe to represent LGBT+ POC, as taken from [[Philadelphia rainbow pride colors|Philadelphia's eight-striped variant of the rainbow pride colors]]. This flag was released by Daniel Quasar in June 2018.\n\nIn 2021, [[intersex-inclusive_progress_pride_colors|a new variant of this flag]] was made by Valentino Vecchietti of Intersex Equality Rights UK, adding a yellow triangle with a purple circle in it (as taken from the [[intersex pride colors|intersex pride flag]]) to the chevron to add representation for intersex individuals."
