          "tag": "oculama",
          "kor": "안구",
          "count": 345,
          "wiki_body": "The cartoon science of substitutions for eyes to convey an expression. This tag is used for when the entire structure of the eyes is swapped out for a symbol, or pattern. It is a form of [[symbol-shaped_eyes]].\r\n\r\nThere should be nothing that can be identified as a sclera, or [[iris]] for this tag to apply. For example, a heart symbol replacing the iris of a character should be tagged [[<3_eyes|heart_eyes]], not [[heart_oculama]].\r\n\r\nh4. Oculama tags\r\n\r\n* [[heart_oculama]]\r\n* [[spiral_oculama]]\r\n* [[star_oculama]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[symbol-shaped_pupils]]"
