        {
          "tag": "gambling",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 344,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Gambling[/b] is placing [[money]], or some other thing of value on the outcome of a game of chance, or sporting event. A place specifically oriented for gambling is known as a [[casino]]. Images that clearly shows characters playing a game of chance at a casino, or operating a gaming machine associated with such facilities may be tagged gambling without evidence that a transaction has occurred. \r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[betting]]\r\n* [[card_game]]\r\n* [[playing_card]]\r\n* [[poker]]\r\n** [[strip_poker]]\r\n* [[poker_chip]]\r\n* [[slot_machine]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "potato",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 344,
          "wiki_body": "A potato is the edible tuber (Modified root stalk) of a nightshade plant. The flesh is starchy and nutritious. It takes the unprepossessing form of a brown or reddish lump. Potatoes are a very versatile foodstuff, with several uses including in soups, beverages, and by itself. It is also used in the production of plastic and biodegradeable packaging."
        },
        {
          "tag": "gorget",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 344,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3232672 thumb #1848583 thumb #3597037\r\n\r\nA [b]gorget[/b] is a piece of [[armor]] designed to protect the wearer's throat.\r\n\r\nh4.It can come in three forms:\r\n* A collar made out of protective material such as [[metal collar|metal]], [[leather collar|leather]] or kevlar.\r\n* A series of metal bands that cover the length of the neck,\r\n* Or a [[bib]]-like metal plate with a neck collar.\r\n\r\nThis armor piece is often worn together with other armor pieces as part of a suit of [[plate armor]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n* [[Bevor]] - Another type of neck armor that extends up to the wearer's jaw.\r\n* [[Armor]]\r\n\r\nh4. External:\r\n* \"Wikipedia - Gorget\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gorget"
        },
        {
          "tag": "black_hole",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 343,
          "wiki_body": "A black hole is an astronomical object with intense mass and gravitational pull. \r\n\r\nThey appear as an invisible sphere, bending light behind it around the corners of the object, however, in artworks, they can appear differently due to artistic representation. Some artworks may represent them as literally black, with most adding in hot glowing gases being pulled in or spiraling around the object. Some artworks may also add an astrophysical jet, which looks like a beam of light jetting out along the black hole's axis of rotation.\r\n\r\nThe effect that black holes have bending light around the edges is due to the intense gravitational pull, pulling light in towards itself, before letting go as it gets out of range."
        },
        {
          "tag": "hazard_stripes",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 343,
          "wiki_body": "A slanted yellow and black stripe pattern used to symbolize that a location or an object is hazardous. Often used in industrial areas where potentially harmful (lethal even) various machinery and locations are everywhere as well as on crime scenes and restricted areas where unauthorized personnel aren't allowed to cross. This pattern is usually painted on surfaces or printed on [[barricade tape]].\r\n\r\nIn character design this pattern is often used on certain characters to signal to the audience they that may prove to be harmful to those around them in some way, is somehow related to industrial related activities (such as a construction robot), or simply because the artist thought hazard stripes on characters look cool.\r\n\r\nh4.See Also\r\n* [[Barricade Tape]]"
        },
