        {
          "tag": "record",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 342,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #133339\r\n\r\nA [b]gramophone record[/b] ([b]phonograph record[/b]), commonly known as a [b]vinyl record[/b] or simply [b]vinyl[/b] or [b]record[/b], is an analog sound storage medium in the form of a flat polyvinyl chloride (previously shellac) disc with an inscribed, modulated spiral groove. The groove usually starts near the periphery and ends near the center of the disc.\r\n\r\nh4. Related:\r\n\r\n* [[record_player]]\r\n** [[gramophone]]\r\n** [[turntable_(decks)]]\r\n** [[turntable_(record_player)]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[disk]]\r\n\r\nh4. External:\r\n\r\n* \"Wikipedia - Gramophone record\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gramophone_record"
