          "tag": "identical_twins",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 336,
          "wiki_body": "Identical twins, scientifically known as [i]\"Monozygotic Twins\"[/i], are [[twins_(lore)|twins]] who share 100% of their DNA, having nearly identical or completely identical physical traits.\r\nthumb #3886540 thumb #951225 thumb #4369056\r\n\r\nIdentical twins are the result of one [[ovum|egg cell]] being fertilized by one [[sperm cell]], after which it successfully implanted in the [[uterus|womb]] before undergoing cell division and separating completely into two [[fetus|embryos]].\r\nBoth siblings share 100% of their DNA as a result. This means the resulting siblings are essentially two copies of the same person. They are always the same gender, and outside of hairstyle, they look extremely similar visually. Physical differences between them form much later in development, such as minor differences between their fingerprints.\r\n\r\nDuring development, both [[fetus|embryos]] share the same placenta and amniotic sac.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[twins (lore)]]: Tag for characters that are twins, regardless of how much DNA they share.\r\n* [[fraternal twins]]: Tag for characters that share 50% of their DNA.\r\n* [[half-identical twins]]: Tag for characters that share 75% of their DNA.\r\n* \"Monozygotic (identical) twins\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twin#Monozygotic_(identical)_twins: Information about Monozygotic twins."
