          "tag": "pedipalps",
          "kor": "발가락 촉수",
          "count": 318,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Pedipalps[/b], also known as palps or palpi, are a pair of facial/mouth appendages in [i]Chelerate[/i] [[arthropod|arthropods]], found on the front of their bodies past their first pair of legs, and to the side of their [[chelicerae]].\r\n\r\nPedipalps can vary from species to species, such as in [[scorpion|scorpions]], where their pedipalps carry their [[pincers]]. They can also come in more prehensile forms, acting as small arms of sorts. Similar to [[maxilliped|maxillipeds]] seen in animals like [[crustacean|crustaceans]], these more prehensile mouthparts are generally used to assist with feeding, though some like the [[spider|spider's]] also are used for the ejection of [[sperm]] in [[sex|reproduction]].\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[mandibles]], similar mouthparts seen in other arthropods such as [[myriapod|myriapods]] and [[crustacean|crustaceans]].\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:feral_anatomy]]\r\n* [[arthropod]]\r\n* [[chelicerae]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "donation_drive",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 318,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #5024538 thumb #4595275 thumb #4072555\n\nA [b]donation drive[/b] art piece is where the artist has stated monetary goals which the audience are able contribute to by donations and or social engagement.\n\nThere are usually incentives for reaching goals with the release of additional content. Current progress of the donation drive is usually shown by a donation bar.\n\nFollowing the '[[tag what you see]]' rule, this excludes additional content rewards not containing indicators of a donation drive such as stated goals or donation progress.\n\nh4. See Also:\n* [[interaction_drive]]\n* [[milestone_celebration]]"
