        {
          "tag": "corridor",
          "kor": "복도",
          "count": 233,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3894886 thumb #3502882 thumb #4532194\r\n\r\nA [b]corridor[/b] [i](\"Synonym\":http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synonym of \"[[aisle]]\" and \"[[hallway]]\")[/i] is a narrow passageway providing access to different areas.\r\n\r\n[b]Corridors[/b] vary in size: some are much longer, some shorter, some high, some small, some low-lit at the end, some with [[light]] on the [[wall (structure)|wall]].\r\n\r\nMaterials of the sides can also vary: [[brick wall|brick]], [[stone wall|stone]]...  Walls can be [[broken wall|broken]] or not, or covered with [[graffiti]], etc.\r\n\r\nh4.Related Tags\r\n* [[inside]]/[[outside]]\r\n* [[wall_(structure)]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also \r\n* [[aisle]]\r\n* [[hallway]]\r\n* [[tunnel]]"
