        {
          "tag": "saber",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 229,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1668935 thumb #1687925 thumb #1108909\r\n\r\nA saber is a type of [[sword]] with a curved blade associated with the light cavalry of the early modern and Napoleonic periods. Originally associated with Central European cavalry such as the hussars, the saber became widespread in Western Europe during the Thirty Years' War. Lighter sabers also became popular with infantry of the early 17th century. In the 19th century, models with less curving blades became common and were also used by heavy cavalry.\r\n\r\n* For the type of tooth, use [[sabertooth_(anatomy)]]. \r\n* For a \"saber-toothed tiger/cat\", use [[machairodontine]].\r\n* For the fictional squirrel species from [[Ice Age (series)]], use [[Saber-toothed_squirrel]]."
