          "kor": "",
          "count": 227,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #705687\r\n\r\n[b]Buruma[/b] is an English to Japanese to English recursive transliteration of bloomer, usually identifying an over-panty or public garment, whose purpose is to cover the panty and crotch area while leaving the maximum maneuvering room.\r\n\r\nTypically this is used as part of a gym uniform, paired up with a [[shirt|t-shirt]]. Though in real life they are rarely part of a gym uniform these days since they're considered old-fashioned, they still show up in anime since they are fetishized by otaku. They've become a feature internationally in women's track and field uniforms.\r\n\r\nContrast with [[bloomers]], which are a type of underwear constructed much like boxer shorts worn by women.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:clothes]]\r\n\r\n* [[bloomers]]\r\n* [[boy_shorts]]\r\n* [[gym_uniform]]\r\n* [[hotpants]]"
