          "wiki_body": "thumb #57783 thumb #1751499 thumb #1256671\r\n\r\nThe M16 rifle is the standard-issue [[assault rifle]] of the United States military, adapted from the ArmaLite [[AR-15]] and introduced in 1964, during the Vietnam War.\r\n\r\nIt has since been widely-exported around the world, and a large number of variants exists in both military service and the civilian market.\r\n\r\nh4.Tagging Info:\r\nThe M16 rifle can be distinguished from the shorter M4 carbine by the long handguard area toward the front of the weapon.\r\n\r\nIn order to avoid an excess of tags, please tag all M16/AR-15 variants with a long forend as M16.\r\n\r\nh4.See also:\r\n* [[tag group:weapons]]\r\n* [[m4 carbine]], a shortened version of the M16 rifle\r\n* [[assault rifle]]\r\n* [[ranged weapon]]\r\n\r\nh4. External:\r\n\r\n* \"Wikipedia - M16 rifle\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M16_rifle"
