          "count": 188,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1006220\r\n\r\n[b]Pit organs[/b] are specialized pits located on the faces of some [[snake]] species. Specifically, they can be found on [[pit viper|pit vipers]], some [[boa (snake)|boas]], and some [[python|pythons]]. These organs are an adaptation that allows for these snakes to sense infrared, effectively being able to sense the heat radiated from their prey.\r\n\r\nThe most visible type, and often most commonly portrayed and known, of pit organs are the [[labial pit|labials]], found on boas and pythons. There can be up to 13 pairs of these pits on a snake, appearing as a group of holes or depressions found on their upper or lower jaws.\r\n\r\nThe other type of pit organ, often the more subtle type, are known as [[loreal pit|loreals]]. These are found in single pairs on pit vipers, one on each side of the face, in between the eye and nose.\r\n\r\nh4. Types\r\n\r\n* [[labial_pit]]\r\n* [[loreal_pit]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:feral_anatomy]]\r\n* [[hole_(anatomy)]]\r\n* [[snake]]"
