          "wiki_body": "thumb #3027591 thumb #1344860 thumb #771939\r\n\r\nA [b]paint can[/b] is a resealable [[can]] primarily used for storing [[paint]]. Paint cans are designed with an attached pail handle giving them the same functionality as a [[bucket]] when unsealed. Although not all cans of this design store paint, if it isn't obvious what is in the container, it is safe to assume that it contains paint. Smaller paint cans exist that do not have attached handles.\r\n\r\nSometimes other types of [[bucket|buckets]] will be used to store paint. The term paint bucket might be used to describe any [[bucket]] that contains paint, but only the resealable containers should be considered as a can, or referred to as a paint can for that matter.\r\n\r\nh4. General guidelines\r\n\r\n* A paint can may be considered as both a [[can]], and a [[bucket]]. Smaller ones should only be tagged as [[can]]. See example below.\r\n\r\nthumb #2952375\r\n\r\n* [[Spray paint]] is stored in a different type of can known as a [[spray can]]. "
