          "tag": "fairy_dust",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 168,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1025784 thumb #787378 thumb #1809713 thumb #1135408 thumb #1724315\r\n\r\nA twinkling, [[sparkles|sparkling]], [[glowing]] [[particles|grain-sized substance]] imbued with [[magic|magical]] properties that is often seen around [[fairy|fairies]]. [i]Fairy dust[/i] may be seen constantly emanating, trailing, or falling from a fairy's body, sometimes localized to their [[wings]] (similar to the powdery scales of moth and butterfly wings). Further, a fairy's body or clothing may sparkle or [[glitter]], which strongly suggests [i]fairy dust[/i] that has not yet fallen loose. Also called pixie dust.\r\n\r\nWhen depicted with magical effect, [i]fairy dust[/i] may passively fall from a fairy and incidentally alter things in the fairy's wake (e.g., spontaneous plant growth). [i]Fairy dust[/i] can be [[jar|jarred]] or [[belt_pouch|bagged]] and later sprinkled on people or objects or perhaps mixed into [[potion|potions]]. A fairy casting a [[spell]] may have their magical [[energy|energies]] depicted with sparkling [i]fairy dust[/i], perhaps issuing from a [[wand]] or hand. Characters other than fairies can possess or use [i]fairy dust[/i], but proving that such substances are specifically [i]fairy dust[/i] and not some other generic magical item or effect is exceedingly unlikely for tagging purposes (see post #2834770).\r\n\r\nLike magic in general, [i]fairy dust[/i] magic on e621 can seemingly be used for anything imaginable although it lends itself well to [[transformation]], but classical effects involve[sup]1[/sup]:\r\n\r\n* application to the eyes causing temporary blindness, inducing [[sleeping|sleep]], or influencing [[dream|dreams]]\r\n* granting the ability to see supernatural creatures or phenomena hidden from normal human sight\r\n* granting access to \"dreamland\" or \"fairyland\"\r\n* granting the ability to fly, seen from [i][[peter_pan|Peter Pan's]][/i] [[tinker_bell_(disney)|Tinker Bell]]\r\n\r\n1. \"A History of Fairy Dust\":https://writinginmargins.weebly.com/home/a-history-of-fairy-dust"
