          "kor": "",
          "count": 163,
          "wiki_body": "Not to be confused with [[draw_over]], this tag refers to the presence of artistic tools such as Pens, Pencils, Erasers, Drawing tablets, styluses, etc. For the specific use of editing a another character(s) or element of the scene in the work as part of the work.\r\nThis could be as simple as erasing or drawing clothes, to as complex as completely redrawing a character's body. The character doing the drawing can be anything from another character in-fiction, to a disembodied hand of the artist.\r\n\r\nUnlike [[body_writing]] or [[bodypaint]], this tag requires in some physical change in a character, object, or both, and may be done through a proxy object such as a sketch pad, picture, or voodoo doll rather than being directly on the subject's form.\r\nBody Writing or Body Painting that induce a physical change count as this tag, while also counting as their respective tags. For situations such a dying clothes or a character's fur a different color, unless clearly shown through dialogue, visuals, or allusion to be in some form magical or meta-textual, it does not count as this tag.\r\n\r\nThis tag pairs well with [[transformation]], but does not imply it."
