          "count": 145,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #552223 thumb #2250904 thumb #2989850\r\n\r\n[b]Grade[/b] means \"to evaluate or rank,\" like teachers who grade their students or a food inspector who grades a crop, determining whether it is \"food-grade.\"\r\n\r\nMost typical grading is the alphabet based, where A-grade is the best and further down the alphabet the worse the quality/performance/grade is. At school, grading is often A-F.\r\n\r\nNumbers are also often used for grading. Equivalent to the alphabet grading is the use of \"1st class\", \"2nd class/2nd rate\", etc. Also the reverse is very common with numbers. 100% or 5/5 being the best and 0% or 0/5 being the worst.\r\n\r\nFor [[dialogue]] related to one's grade, use the [[stated_grade]] tag.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n* [[graded_condom]]\r\n* [[graded_dildo]]\r\n* [[graded_penis]]\r\n* [[graded_throat]]\r\n* [[graded_torso]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[number]]\r\n* [[text]]"
