          "tag": "dough",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 143,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Dough[/b] is a thick, malleable, sometimes elastic paste made from grains or from leguminous or chestnut crops. Dough is typically made by mixing flour with a small amount of water or other liquid and sometimes includes yeast or other leavening agents, as well as ingredients such as fats or flavorings.\r\n\r\nMaking and shaping dough begins the preparation of a wide variety of [[food]] products, particularly [[bread]] and bread-based items, but also including \"biscuits\":/wiki_pages/45230, [[cake]]s, [[cookie]]s, [[dumplings]], [[flatbread]]s, [[noodles]], [[pasta]], [[pastry]], [[pizza]], [[pie]]crusts, and similar items. Dough can be made from a wide variety of flour, commonly wheat and rye but also maize, rice, legumes, almonds, and other cereals or crops.\r\n\r\n\"Dough - From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dough"
