          "tag": "c.a.m.",
          "kor": "c.a.m.",
          "count": 132,
          "wiki_body": "The C.A.M. (Canadian, American, and Mexican) Special Operation Forces is an elite military unit of soldiers from Canada, the United States, and Mexico to protect North America.\n\nHistory:\n3 Months after the United States joined World War II, the US and Mexico formed a special forces team named the United States and Mexican Special Operatives. The USMSO would deploy in Germany and Japan for secret missions, infiltrating governments and gathering any information needed. A part of the team would also protect the Gulf of Mexico from U-boats sinking merchant ships. On August 15, 1950, the United States managed to have Canada join the special forces team. The USMSO was renamed to C.U.M. Five days later, it was renamed to C.A.M. Special Operation Forces. The C.A.M. has had combat during World War II, the Korean War, the Cold War, the Iran-Iraq War, the Militares Uniformizados da América do Sul War, the Gulf War, and the Mexican Drug War.\n\nC.A.M. was created by SoppyCastle9 for his comic universe for Prototype 9"
