          "tag": "fantasy_slur",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 123,
          "wiki_body": "A [b]fantasy slur[/b] is an offensive term targeted at a group on bases such as race, gender, or age. Compared to typical [[slur]]s, a fantasy slur is either invented or used in such a way that only has utility in a fantasy setting.\n\nA fantasy slur will commonly allude to real-world racial slurs by way of rhymes or similar etymology, especially when related to primates like [[monkey]]s:\n* The [[Warhammer 40,000]] book \"Codex: [[aeldari|Eldar]]\" (third edition) defined \"mon-keigh\" as a pejorative for any inferior species, especially humans.\n* [[Dragon Ball Super]] character [[Zamasu]] is frequently observed calling mortals \"ningen\" (Japanese for \"human\"/\"person\"), which has since become a meme in English.\n* Furry fiction occasionally uses \"skinnie\" or \"skinny\" as a human-centric counterpart to \"furry\", sometimes as a slur, and sometimes as a [[reverse furry]] who likes fictional humans.\n* Furry fiction occasionally addresses humans as \"[[ape]]s\", as in a tailless primate."
