          "count": 121,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #4027454 thumb #2972127\r\n\r\nArt created by digitally painting over top of an existing image, including a drawn sketch, 3d rendered image, photograph, or even a previously coloured image.\r\n\r\nThis may be done to simply render the subject, add greater detail, or alter the subject.\r\n\r\nA paintover of previously uncoloured piece of art isn't simply a [[color edit]] of [[lineart]] or a [[sketch]], but involves adding painted detail, complex lighting, texture, and sometimes a background that didn't exist in the sketch/lineart. A paintover of a sketch or lineart will often obscure or entirely cover the lines, creating a softer and more realistic looking image. Paintovers of finished artwork may done as [[collaboration]] between two artists.\r\n\r\nh5. Paintover Applications\r\n\r\n* Painting over a screenshot to create an [[edited screenshot]]\r\n* Painting over a figure posed using [[source_film_maker|SFM]], [[Blender]] or other [[3d (artwork)|3d rendered images]]\r\n** This may be done to add details to a rendered figure or be a full paintover of a 3d rendered image using the 3d art as a base\r\n* Paintover is a key part of [[photobashing]]\r\n\r\n[section=Before and After Examples of Paintovers]\r\nthumb #2320386thumb #2522641 thumb #3669705thumb #3677215 \r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[photo manipulation]]\r\n** [[photomorph]]\r\n* [[photobashing]]\r\n* [[color edit]]"
