          "count": 114,
          "wiki_body": "The [b]naginata[/b] (なぎなた, 薙刀) is one of several varieties of traditionally made [[Japanese]] blades (nihonto) in the form of a [[polearm|pole weapon]]. Naginatas were originally used by the [[samurai ]]class of feudal [[Japan]], as well as by ashigaru (foot soldiers) and sōhei (warrior monks). The naginata is the iconic weapon of the onna-bugeisha-archetype; a type of female warrior belonging to the Japanese nobility.\r\n\r\nA naginata consists of a wooden pole with a curved single-edged blade on the end; it is similar to the [[Chinese]] [[guandao]] and the European [[glaive]]. Similar to the [[katana]], naginata often have a round handguard (tsuba) between the blade and shaft, when mounted in a koshirae. The 30 cm to 60 cm long naginata blade is forged in the same manner as traditional Japanese swords. The blade has a long tang (nakago) which is inserted in the shaft.\r\n\r\nh4.See Also:\r\n* [[polearm]]\r\n** [b]naginata[/b]\r\n** [[guandao]]\r\n** [[glaive]]\r\n** [[swordstaff]]\r\n** [[spear]]"
