          "tag": "dating_sim",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 112,
          "wiki_body": "Posts emulating the look and feel of a typical dating simulator, a [[video_games|video game]] genre about romancing a character among a cast of other characters.\r\n\r\nh4. Elements\r\nHere are some elements and [[gameplay_mechanics]] commonly found in a dating sim game:\r\n* A dating sim-esque [[title screen]]. (A cutesy title font, lots of hearts, the datable characters on display, etc.)\r\n*  A static character avatar that switches from a set of expressions and poses.\r\n* A set of stock backgrounds that is repeatedly used throughout the game.\r\n* A prominent [[dialogue box]].\r\n* [[dialogue choice|Dialogue choices]].\r\n* A gifting system that boosts your relationship with a character.\r\n* Several [[progress bar|progress bars]] displaying various gameplay information such as relationship meters, mood meters, energy/action meters, completion percentage, and many others.\r\n* [[notification|Notification icons]] displaying how your choices and actions have affected the playthrough.\r\n* A \"skinship\" mechanic where you use a [[disembodied hand]] or two to physically interact with a character's body.\r\n* A special unique scene that shows up in place of the static avatars and stock backgrounds as a reward for players.\r\n* An overworld map displaying different locations and where the characters are currently at.\r\n* A clock and calendar system that passes every time the player makes an action.\r\n* A dating minigame where you must choose the right words and actions to accumulate points in a limited time.\r\n\r\nh4.Tagging notes\r\nBe mindful of the [[Tag What You See]] guideline. This tag is for posts that look like a dating sim gameplay screenshot or posts of characters playing a dating sim game. Having dating sim characters, official video game assets and promotional advertisements for a real dating sim game in the post doesn't necessarily warrant this tag.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[gameplay_mechanics]]"
