          "count": 106,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #926918\r\n\r\nA [b]tobacco pipe[/b], often called simply a [b]pipe[/b], is a device specifically made to [[smoking|smoke]] tobacco. It comprises a chamber (the bowl) for the tobacco from which a thin hollow stem (shank) emerges, ending in a mouthpiece (the bit). Pipes can range from very simple machine-made briar models to highly prized hand-made artisanal implements made by renowned pipemakers, which are often very expensive collector's items. Pipe smoking is the oldest known traditional form of tobacco smoking.\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[Smoking Pipe]]\r\n\r\nh4. External:\r\n\r\n* \"Wikipedia - Tobacco pipe\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tobacco_pipe"
