          "tag": "floppy_disk",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 103,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #499382 thumb #1533271 thumb #1090545 thumb #2287602\r\n\r\nA \"floppy disk\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floppy_disk, also called a floppy, diskette or just disk, is a type of disk storage composed of a disk of thin and flexible magnetic storage medium, sealed in a square plastic enclosure lined with fabric that removes dust particles. Floppy disks are read and written by a floppy disk drive (FDD).\r\n\r\nThese disks came most popularly known in their 3.5 inch and 5.25 inch formats, but were predated by an 8 inch format too. The two bigger formats were almost all black in colour with a sticker label in the corner, whereas the 3.5 inch version came mostly in blue, very often in black and additionally in several other colours.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[vinyl_record]]\r\n* [[blu-ray]]\r\n* [[cassette_tape]]\r\n* [[cd]]\r\n* [[dvd]]\r\n* floppy_disk"
