        {
          "tag": "mecha_musume",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 101,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #52751 thumb #29159 thumb #3229927 thumb #1769804 thumb #4654170\r\nA [b]mecha musume[/b] is a [[female]] character who is wearing [[clothing]], [[accessory|accessories]], [[armor]], and/or [[cybernetics]] that are themed after a particular [[machine]] such as a [[mecha]], a [[robot]], a [[vehicle]], an [[appliance]] or [[electronics]]. The machine in question can either be something from real life (from a [[sports car]] model to a kitchen appliance) or from a particular copyrighted work (such as a famous [[spacecraft]] or mech).\r\n\r\nIn other interpretations mecha musume can also refer to female characters donning armor evoking a typical Japanese mecha aesthetic with no reference to an original machine and is just a stand alone design.\r\n\r\nh4.Not to be confused with\r\n* [[Humanoidized]] - The machine is depicted with humanoid traits. Difference between this and mecha musume is that this one is basically a humanoid robot while the other one is clothed/armored like the original machine.\r\n* [[Living Machine]] - Basically an anthropomorphic form of the original machine. Similar in concept to an [[anthro]].\r\n\r\nh4.See Also\r\n* [[robot]]\r\n* [[mecha]]\r\n* [[cyborg]]\r\n** [[cybernetics]]\r\n* [[armor]]\r\n** [[power armor]]\r\n* [[personification]]\r\n\r\nh4.External\r\n* http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mecha_musume"
