          "tag": "older_ambiguous",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 220,
          "wiki_body": "An [[ambiguous gender]] character depicted with another character who is visibly [i]younger[/i] than them; making that ambiguous character [i]older[/i] than the other character. Note that this tag does [b][i]not[/i][/b] indicate that the ambiguous character is [[old]] or [[mature ambiguous ]], this tag can apply to an teenaged or adult ambiguous character who is merely older than a child or teenager, respectively. However, if a character is middle aged or elderly, remember to tag [[mature ambiguous ]] or [[elderly ambiguous]] as well.\r\n\r\nh6. For the \"opposite age\" see [[younger ambiguous]]\r\n\r\nh5. [[Age Difference]] Tags:\r\n\r\n[section= Older]\r\nA character that is older than another within the same scene. This doesn't mean the character is necessarily mature, middle aged, or elderly, these tags merely compare them to another character in the same image. If the character is middle aged use the appropriate mature_* tags,  (see the mature section in \"see also\" below).\r\n\r\n* [b]older ambiguous[/b]\r\n* [[older female]]\r\n* [[older male]]\r\n* [[older intersex]]\r\n** [[older andromorph]]\r\n** [[older gynomorph]]\r\n** [[older herm]]\r\n** [[older maleherm]]\r\n\r\n[/section] \r\n\r\n[section= Younger]\r\nA character that is younger than another within the same scene. This doesn't mean the \"younger\" character is necessarily [[young]], a [[child]], or [[cub]], these tags merely compare them to the other character in the same image.\r\n\r\n* [[younger ambiguous]]\r\n* [[younger female]]\r\n* [[younger male]]\r\n* [[younger intersex]]\r\n** [[younger andromorph]]\r\n** [[younger gynomorph]]\r\n** [[younger herm]]\r\n** [[younger maleherm]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Related:\r\n\r\n[section= Mature]\r\n[b]Mature[/b] describes characters that are \"middle aged\" - in human terms, this is generally around ages 45-65, however, this tag is more concerned with the visual appearance of the character rather than strict definitions of chronological age. If a mature character is in an image with a younger character, the post should also be tagged with the appropriate older_* and younger_* tags above.\r\n\r\n* [[mature ambiguous]]\r\n* [[mature female]]\r\n* [[mature male]]\r\n* [[mature intersex]]\r\n** [[mature andromorph]]\r\n** [[mature gynomorph]]\r\n** [[mature herm]]\r\n** [[mature maleherm]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also: \r\n\r\n* [[age difference]]\r\n* [[young]]\r\n* [[old]]\r\n* [[aged down]]\r\n* [[aged up]]"
