          "count": 69143,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #467791 thumb #270630 thumb #1405530 thumb #492271\r\n\r\nPhysical or narrative representation of a character's breath. \r\n\r\nUse this tag when a character's breath is visible, or it appears obvious from the image that a character's breathing is labored ([[huff|huffing]], [[panting]]), or characterized by an emphasized exhalation ([[sigh]]). Breathing effects may take the form of a puff, or cloud, appear as a fog / mist surrounding a character, or depicted using [[sound effects]].\r\n\r\nOther breathing effects such as the chest moving in and out might be better tagged as [[breathing]] instead of breath.\r\n\r\nBreath's visibility in art generally attempts to convey a significant difference between the breather's internal body temperature and the ambient temperature of their surroundings. Thus, breath is often seen in [[cold]] environments and during or after physical exertion (e.g., [[sex]], [[exercise]], [[tired]], etc.).\r\n\r\nh4. Features\r\n\r\n* [[breath_cloud]]\r\n* [[breathing_noises]] - Sound effect words such as [i]huff, pant, puff, sigh, snort[/i].\r\n\r\nh5. Categories\r\n\r\n* [[gasp]]\r\n* huff (defunct)\r\n* [[panting]]\r\n* [[sigh]]\r\n* [[snort]]\r\n* [[wheeze]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[breathing]]\r\n* [[smoke_from_nose]]\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[steam]] - visible evaporation of water from boiling, although the tag does not require boiling. In art, [[sweat]] may evaporate into steam. For tagging purposes, steam is not exhaled from the mouth or nose."
