          "wiki_body": "thumb #3831851 thumb #2839080\r\n\r\nHigh heels are a type of [[footwear]] that raises the heel of the wearer's foot higher than the toes. When both the heel and the toes are raised equal amounts, as in a [[platform_footwear |platform shoe]], it is technically not considered to be a high heel; however, there are also high-heeled platform shoes. High heels come in a wide variety of styles, and tend to give the aesthetic illusion of longer, more slender legs. \r\n\r\nh4. Tags about high heels\r\n\r\n[section=Design features]\r\n\r\nh4. [[ankle_strap_heels]]\r\nSecured to the foot with strap(s) that go around the ankle\r\nthumb #2707920 thumb #1363792\r\n\r\nh4. [[ballet_high_heels]]\r\nFeature extremely high heel, forcing the wearer to tiptoe like a [[ballerina]]\r\nthumb #2994890 thumb #2180817\r\n\r\nh4. [[block_heels]]\r\nFeature a thick, square heel.\r\nthumb #3269494 thumb #2834121\r\n\r\nh4. [[cutout_heels]]\r\nPumps and high heeled boots that feature cutout(s). Note that toe cutout should be tagged separately as toeless_heels.\r\nthumb #1518982 thumb #2634635\r\n\r\nh4. [[digitigrade_heels]]\r\nDesigned to fit on [[digitigrade]] feet\r\nthumb #2850978 thumb #3036798\r\n\r\nh4. [[heelless_heels]]\r\nDon't feature a heel but still raise wearer's foot\r\nthumb #97779 thumb #3538607\r\n\r\nh4. [[high_heeled_boots]]\r\n[[Boots]] with a high heel\r\nthumb #1960026 thumb #3881248\r\n\r\nh4. [[high_heeled_sandals]]\r\n[[Sandals]] with a high heel\r\nthumb #1227322 thumb #1740534\r\n\r\nh4. [[high_heeled_sneakers]]\r\n[[Sneakers]] with a high heel\r\nthumb #3663733 thumb #2150770\r\n\r\nh4. [[hoof_heels]]\r\nDesigned to fit on [[hooves]]\r\nthumb #2932875 thumb #2987231\r\n\r\nh4. [[mary_janes]]\r\nPumps that feature strap(s) across the top\r\nthumb #375667 thumb #4555834\r\n\r\nh4. [[mule_heels]]\r\nDo not feature straps, fasteners, heel guard, or anything else that could secure them to the foot, like [[slippers]]\r\nthumb #1444981 thumb #144762