          "tag": "mane",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 55999,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Mane[/b] is a term referring to thick hair or fur that extends down the back of the neck of certain species such as [[horse|horses]], and [[lion|lions]], but also accurately describes the fur of other species such as [[hyaenid|hyenas]], and [[furred_dragon|furred dragons]].\r\n\r\nh4. [[horse|Horse]]\r\n\r\nthumb #2211677 thumb #328170\r\n\r\nThe mane is the hair that grows from the top of the neck of a horse or other equine, reaching from the poll to the withers, and includes the forelock or foretop. It is thicker and coarser than the rest of the horse's coat, and naturally grows to roughly cover the neck. Heredity plays a role, giving some horses a longer, thicker mane, and others a shorter, thinner one.\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. [[lion|Lion]]\r\n\r\nthumb #370018 thumb #2221560 thumb #825050\r\n\r\nThe mane of the adult male lion, unique among cats, is one of the most distinctive characteristics of the species. It takes the form of a thick mass of hair covering from the top of the head, and fully around the neck.\r\n\r\n[section=Extra info]\r\nA mane makes the lion appear larger, providing an excellent intimidation display; this aids the lion during confrontations with other lions and with the species' chief competitor in Africa, the spotted hyena. The presence, absence, colour, and size of the mane is associated with genetic precondition, sexual maturity, climate, and testosterone production; the rule of thumb is the darker and fuller the mane, the healthier the lion. Sexual selection of mates by lionesses favors males with the densest, darkest mane. Research in Tanzania also suggests mane length signals fighting success in male–male relationships. Darker-maned individuals may have longer reproductive lives and higher offspring survival, although they suffer in the hottest months of the year. In prides including a coalition of two or three males, it is possible that lionesses solicit mating more actively with the males who are more heavily maned.\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Other\r\n\r\nthumb #2346696 thumb #2349053 thumb #2098380\r\n\r\nAny creature depicted with thick fur or hair lining the back of the neck.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with\r\n\r\n* [[ruff]] - A lining of [[feathers]], or [[fur]] surrounding the neck.\r\n\r\nh4. Tags About Manes\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=General]\r\n\r\nh6. Variants\r\n\r\n* [[back_mane]]\r\n* [[mane_hair]]\r\n* [[pseudo_mane]]\r\n** [[ethereal_mane]]\r\n*** [[cosmic_mane]]\r\n** [[feather_mane]]\r\n** [[flaming_mane]]\r\n* [[tail_mane]]\r\n\r\nh6. Traits\r\n\r\n* [[flowing_mane]]\r\n* [[fluffy_mane]]\r\n* [[glowing_mane]]\r\n* [[long_mane]]\r\n* [[messy_mane]]\r\n* [[wavy_mane]]\r\n* [[wet_mane]]\r\n\r\nh6. Other\r\n\r\n* [[cum_on_mane]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\n[section,expanded=Mane Colors]\r\n\r\n* [[black_mane]]\r\n* [[blonde_mane]]\r\n* [[blue_mane]]\r\n* [[brown_mane]]\r\n* [[cream_mane]]\r\n* [[gold_mane]]\r\n* [[green_mane]]\r\n* [[grey_mane]]\r\n* [[orange_mane]]\r\n* [[pink_mane]]\r\n* [[purple_mane]]\r\n* [[red_mane]]\r\n* [[tan_mane]]\r\n* [[teal_mane]]\r\n* [[white_mane]]\r\n\r\n* [[monotone_mane]]\r\n* [[multicolored_mane]]\r\n** [[rainbow_mane]]\r\n** [[two_tone_mane]]\r\n\r\n* [[dark_mane]]\r\n* [[light_mane]]\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[fur]]\r\n* [[hair]]"
