          "wiki_body": "A [b]bell[/b] is a simple sound-making device. The bell is a percussion instrument and an idiophone. Its form is usually a hollow, cup-shaped object, which resonates upon being struck. The striking implement can be a tongue suspended within the bell, known as a clapper, a small, free sphere enclosed within the body of the bell or a separate mallet or hammer.\n\nElectric bells (such as often found in schools, some fire alarm systems, etc.) are electrically rung by an electromagnet that makes a metal hammer vibrate, striking the bell.\n\nThis tag includes the [[jingle_bell|round \"bells\"]] often seen attached to collars and [[Christmas]] hats.\n\nh4. Types\n\n* [[bell_accessory]]\n** [[bell_piercing]]\n*** [[bell_earrings]]\n** [[hair_bell]]\n** [[horn_bell]]\n** [[nipple_bell]]\n** [[tail_bell]]\n* [[bell_bow]]\n* [[bell_collar]]\n* [[bell_harness]]\n* [[bell_hat]]\n* [[call_bell]]\n* [[cowbell]]\n* [[doorbell]] - This refers to a sound/sound effect.\n* [[handbell]]\n* [[jingle_bell]]\n** [[jingle_bell_harness]]\n* [[soothe_bell]] (Pokémon item)\n\nh4. Related themes\n\n* [[jingling]]\n* [[ringing_bell]]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[bow_(feature)]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "jingle_bell",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 4176,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1042272\n\nA [b]jingle bell[/b] or [b]sleigh bell[/b] is a type of [[bell]] which produces a distinctive 'jingle' sound, especially in large numbers. They find use in many areas as a percussion [[musical_instrument|instrument]], including the classic sleigh bell sound and morris dancing. They are typically used as a cheaper alternative to small 'classic' bells.\n\nThe simplest jingle bells are produced from a single piece of sheet metal bent into a roughly spherical shape to contain a small ball bearing or short piece of metal rod. This method of production results in the classic two- or four-leaved shape. Two halves may also be crimped together, resulting in a ridge around the middle. A glass marble may also be used as the ringer on larger bells.\n\nh4. Further reading:\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jingle_bell\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[bell]]\n** [[bell_accessory]]\n*** [[bell_collar]]\n*** [[bell_piercing]]\n**** [[bell_earrings]]\n*** [[hair_bell]]\n*** [[nipple_bell]]\n*** [[tail_bell]]\n** [[bell_hat]]\n** [[call_bell]]\n** [[cowbell]]\n** [b]jingle_bell[/b]\n*** [[jingle_bell_harness]]\n** [[soothe_bell]] (Pokémon item)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "crown",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 42936,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #2192506 thumb #2828931 thumb #3713494 thumb #1662248\r\n\r\nA [b]crown[/b] is the traditional symbolic form of headgear worn by a monarch or by a deity, for whom the crown traditionally represents power, legitimacy, immortality, righteousness, victory, triumph, resurrection, honour and glory of life after death. In art the crown may be shown being offered to those on Earth by angels. Apart from the traditional form, crowns also may be made of, for example, flowers, stars, oak leaves or [[thorns]] and be worn by others, representing what the coronation part aims to symbolize with the specific crown. They often contain jewels.\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n* [[circlet]]\r\n* [[headgear]]\r\n* [[tiara]]\r\n* [[jewelry]]\r\n* [[flower]]\r\n* [[thorns]]\r\n* [[leaf]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "tiara",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 8106,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3354624 thumb #3505042 thumb #1408453 thumb #3428225\r\n\r\nA [b]tiara[/b] is a type of headwear resembling a small [[crown]], usually worn by women. Tiaras are typically a semi-circle made of gold or silver, with engravings and jewels, they may be worn atop the head, or around the forehead. In simplified depictions they may merely be a gold band, or a set of spikes. \r\n\r\nWhile wearing a tiara can denote [[royalty]] or nobility, tiaras are more often worn by characters as a fashion statement rather than as a symbol of authority, especially in the case of \"forehead tiaras\". \r\n\r\n[section=Not to be confused with...]\r\n\r\nh5. [[Circlet]]\r\n\r\nthumb #3354971 thumb #3221332 thumb #3480299\r\n\r\nWhile sometimes similar to tiaras worn across the forehead (especially when the wearer's hair obscures most of it), circlets and tiaras should not be confused:\r\n* a circlet is a full circle, tiaras are only semi-circles\r\n* circlets may be a thin gold or silver hoop that goes around the wearer's entire head, or take the form of a chain or string, with jewels or beads worn atop the wearer's head, or around it, a tiara will always be a solid object.\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[headwear]]\r\n** [[crown]]\r\n** [[circlet]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "super_crown",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 2962,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1659678\r\n\r\nAn exclusive powerup item for [[Toadette]] that made its debut on [i]\"New Super Mario Bros. U Deluxe\"[/i]. It transforms her into a [[Princess Peach]] lookalike known as [[Peachette]]. It is a golden crown with [[dot eyes]] and a puffy pink, white polka dotted headgear in the middle, reminiscent of Toadette's mushroom caps. Once Toadette dons it and transforms into her Peachette form it changes in size and shape to fit her new self. It is also officially stated that only Toadette can harness the power of the crown. Anyone else who wears it will find that nothing happens.\r\n\r\nh2.The Super Crown Meme\r\nSince its debut fans have speculated what would happen if anyone else wore the super crown. Especially so when the game was yet to be released and little information was available apart from the trailers. Canonically, nothing will happen. In fan works, however, it will also transform anyone (and sometimes even anything) into a Princess Peach lookalike. This what-if idea quickly gained popularity among fan artists and spawned an art meme which eventually led to the creation of numerous Super Crowned [[fan character|fan characters]]. Popular among them is [[bowsette meme|Bowsette]]; who is basically just [[Bowser]] under the effects of the crown and [b]Booette[/b];A [[boo_(mario)|boo]] wearing the crown.\r\n\r\nh2.See Also\r\n* [[humanoidized]]\r\n* [[bowsette meme]]\r\n* [[transformation]]"
