          "kor": "낭만적",
          "count": 40734,
          "wiki_body": "A broad concept concerning the nature of [[love]], [[dating]], and the pursuit of [[romantic_couple|relationships]]. This tag can be used for any concept with an inherent romantic theme to it, but usually these themes will contain other more specific concepts that should also be tagged.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:romance]]\r\n\r\nh5. Major concepts\r\n\r\n* [[intimate]]\r\n** [[embrace]]\r\n** [[hug]]\r\n** [[kissing]]\r\n* [[love]]\r\n* [[passion]]\r\n* [[romantic_ambiance]]\r\n* [[romantic_couple]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "romantic_couple",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 34643,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #380816 thumb #812501 thumb #173823\r\n\r\nPosts that depict two characters who are clearly in love with each other. Do not tag by outside information. It does not matter how much of a canon couple it is, this tag only applies if the couple is currently showing it.\r\n\r\nThis includes content such as two lovers walking together through the park, [[hand_holding|holding hands]] and watching a sunset, watching a movie while cuddling, or, yes, engaging in graphically depicted [[penetration|sexual intercourse]]. \r\n\r\nFor clarification, this is not an appropriate tag for any and all pairs of sexually engaged characters. Do not tag if such sex scenes are indistinguishable from one-night stands. This tag should not be used if there is no indication from either the artist or the character owners that the characters shown in the art are a couple. The [[romantic_ambiance]] tag can be used instead.\r\n\r\nThis tag is somewhat subjective, but a reasonable guideline is that there should be obvious visible affection, not just lust.\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with:\r\n\r\n* [[canon_couple]] - Romantic couple does not apply if the characters aren't currently acting romantically.\r\n* [[duo]]\r\n* [[happy_sex]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[<3]]\r\n* [[cuddling]]\r\n* [[date]]\r\n* [[embrace]]\r\n* [[entwined_tails]]\r\n* [[eye_contact]]\r\n* [[face_to_face]]\r\n* [[hand_holding]]\r\n* [[hug]] \r\n* [[kissing]]\r\n* [[love]]\r\n* [[nose_to_nose]]\r\n* [[romantic_ambiance]] - for romantic locations/backgrounds\r\n* [[wedding]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n\r\n* forum #187937 - Tag Implication: romantic_couple -> romantic (Mar. 2016)\r\n* [[tag group:romance]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "romantic_ambiance",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 8688,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #146469 thumb #31453 thumb #250912 \r\n\r\nPosts that depict romantic scenes and settings. \r\n\r\nWhat counts as romantic ambiance is somewhat subjective, but it often involves elements such as candlelight dinner, dim lighting, filtered light, soft music, flowers, sunset, moonlit skies, et cetera. Red and pink colors are often associated with romance.\r\n\r\nIf the post is sexual in nature, it should emphasize the romantic aspect over erotic. Not all sex is romantic, so don't use this tag on all sex-containing artwork. Romantic aspects need to be taken into account such as cuddling, kissing, dialogue, eye contact and facial expressions.\r\n\r\nSometimes the presence of romantically involved characters may make this difficult to tag objectively. As a rule of thumb, consider this: would you still describe the scene as romantic if the characters were not present? If so, romantic ambiance applies.\r\n\r\nNote that this tag can apply even when the character(s) aren't romantically involved, as long as the setting and props are sufficiently romantic.\r\n\r\nh4. Not to be confused with:\r\n\r\n* [[seductive]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[cuddling]]\r\n* [[romantic_couple]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[tag group:romance]]\r\n* forum #197001"
