          "kor": "컷어웨이",
          "count": 36569,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #4352477 thumb #4276723 thumb #3046150\n\nA [b]cutaway[/b], or more descriptively an \"inset panel\" is a small panel within a larger image that depicts something within the same scene that is unseen in the larger view. \n\nh5. Cutaway Examples\n\n* An [[expression cutaway]] showing a character's face in a panel or bubble reacting to something within the scene\n** This can show the face of a character whose back is to the viewer's point of view, or the reaction of an otherwise offscreen character\n* An [[internal]] within a small panel — showing the inside of a character's body, with the larger scene depicting an external view of the same character, typically seen in sexual situations with [[internal vaginal]] or [[internal anal]], and especially in [[vore]] content showing an [[inside stomach|internal view of the stomach]]\n* A [[close-up]] within a smaller panel\n** [[sex shot|\"sex shots\"]], close-up close cropped views of genitalia during sexual activities, are often seen within a cutaway panel\n** [[butt shot|butt shots]] are commonly seen through cutaway panels, with the main part of the image showing the character's front\n\nh4. Categories\n\n* [[expression_cutaway]]\n* [[internal]] - Not exclusively a cutaway, but usually one.\n\nh4. Forms\n\n* [[dripping_cutaway]]\n* [[heart_cutaway]]\n* [[inward_tail_cutaway]]\n\nh4. Related tags\n\n* [[close-up]]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[expression_avatar]]"
