          "tag": "crop_top",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 34754,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3802672 thumb #3409120 thumb #2757195 thumb #2762134\r\n\r\n[b]Crop top[/b] describes any kind of [[shirt]] that is made to only cover the upper torso, revealing the wearer's [[midriff]].\r\n\r\nCrop tops can take a wide variety of forms, meaning a single garment can be tagged (ideally) as both `crop_top` and another tag describing the specific type of shirt, e.g. [[tank top]], [[camisole]], [[polo shirt]], [[t-shirt]] etc. \r\n\r\nThe amount a \"top\" is \"cropped\" can also vary, from only giving a peek of the wearer's [[navel]] when the crop top is very long, to being cropped extremely high, showing off the [[under boob|underside of the wearer's breasts]] or chest. Crop tops may be worn with [[high waisted bottomwear|shorts or pants with a very high waist]], partially or fully covering what would otherwise be bared by the crop top.\r\n\r\n[quote]\r\n\r\nh5. [color=yellow]Important Tagging Notes[/color]\r\n\r\n* [b]`crop_top` should NOT be applied to...[/b]\r\n** [[bandeau]]\r\n** [[bikini top|bikini tops]]\r\n** [[bra|bras]]\r\n** [[tube top|tube tops]]\r\n** [[sports bra|sports bras]]\r\n** [[tied shirt|tied shirts]] \r\n\r\n* Bandeau inherently — and tube tops [i]almost[/i] always — involve a bared midriff, they are not \"cropped\" tops \r\n* Bikini tops, bras, and sports bras are not shirts\r\n* Tied shirts are full length shirts that are tied off to expose the midriff, they are not cropped\r\n\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n[i]Other cropped topwear[/i]\r\n* [[cropped jacket]]\r\n* [[cropped hoodie]]\r\n* [[cropped sweater]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[tag_group:clothes]]\r\n* [[topwear]]"
