          "kor": "",
          "count": 34380,
          "wiki_body": "Images or animations depicting a character taking control of another character's mind by some means, most commonly [[hypnosis]]. \n\nThe exact methods used in mind control images and sequences vary wildly, from artificial machines meant to induce a state of suggestibility, to magical spells and potions, to a character's natural ability, to old-fashioned watches swinging back and forth before the victim's eyes.\n\nDue to its nature, mind control can be difficult to tag based on [[Tag What You See]]. The most common visual markers are special eye effects such as the following:\n* [[ringed eyes]]\n* [[spiral eyes]]\n* [[spiral pupils]]\n\nh4. Types of [[manipulation]]\n* [[blackmail]]\n** [[failed blackmail]]\n* [[brainwashing]]\n** [[conditioning]]\n** [[reprogramming]]\n* [[bribery]]\n** [[bribery for sex]]\n** [[bribery with sex]]\n** [[failed bribery]]\n* [[deception]]\n** [[impersonation]]\n* [[exploitation]]\n* [b]mind control[/b]\n** [[hypnosis]]\n* [[peer pressure]]\n* [[taunting]]\n* [[threat]]\n** [[coercion]] – using threat to obtain control of another's actions\n** [[extortion]] – using threat to obtain items, money, or status\n\nh4. See also\n* [[body control]]\n* [[mind break]]\n* [[mindfuck]]\n* [[mind wipe]]"
