          "tag": "tribal",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 14294,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1656640 thumb #1018318 thumb #1616041 thumb #2693177 thumb #1617930\r\n\r\nTribal, as a tag, is used to describe characters who have an aesthetic and/or outfit that implies belonging to a primitive hunter-gatherer society, or of a more developed agricultural civilization with Bronze Age or Iron Age level technology. A character doesn't need to be of an ancient society or of an actual tribe to fall under this tag, a character with a tribal look may inhabit a purely [[fantasy]] setting with any kind of technology or magic.\r\n\r\nWhat exactly creates \"tribal clothing\" or a \"tribal aesthetic\" can vary, in anthropomorphic art \"tribal\" looking characters are usually a part of a fantasy world or non-specific culture inspired by real world tribal societies. \r\n\r\n[b]Ideally a character wearing the traditional clothing of a real world culture that is or was tribal should be tagged with that culture's name rather than \"tribal\".[/b]\r\n\r\n[quote]h5.  \"Tribal\" Elements\r\n\r\n* clothing is generally [[skimpy]], outside of characters in very cold settings (who will wear layers of furs and animal pelts)\r\n** [[loincloth|loincloths]] are an extremely common unisex part of \"tribal\" outfits\r\n** female characters are often shown wearing [[bandeau]] or some sort of cropped top or bra-like topwear\r\n** male characters are overwhelmingly bare chested, but are sometimes depicted wearing loose topwear (often baring their midriff and/or chest), simple sleeveless shirts, tunics, vests etc.\r\n* clothing may consist of furs, animal hide, feather, bone, beads, grass, gemstones, or handcrafted textiles\r\n* \"tribal\" patterns on clothing\r\n\r\n* items which are handcrafted from flint, bone, wood, stone or smelted metals \r\n* weapons such as daggers, clubs, staffs, bows and arrows, and spears\r\n* armour may be leather and/or feature metal plates\r\n* use of primitive tools to hunt or live in a natural environment\r\n* [[tribal markings]] — tattoos or bodypaint that fit this aesthetic[/quote]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n* These character archetypes often have a tribal aesthetic:\r\n** [[barbarian]]\r\n** [[caveman]]\r\n** [[shaman]]\r\n** [[warrior]]\r\n* Specific tribal elements\r\n** [[tribal markings]]\r\n** [[tribal jewelry]]\r\n** [[tribal armor]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[medieval]]\r\n* [[fantasy]]\r\n"
