          "count": 178,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #543048  thumb #2786567  thumb #2229463\r\n\r\nA smaller head attached to the body of a [[multi_head|multi-headed]] creature with one primary head that is larger than all other heads. These ancillary heads typically have a long, [[serpentine]] body but do not have any limbs of their own. Typically the primary head is attached where the head of a single-headed creature would attach, with multiple ancillary head attached in a group from one part of the body (i.e. the base of the neck or the scalp of the primary head).\r\n\r\nThe replacement of an existing limb or extremity with a singular head (i.e. [[tail_head]] or [[head_hands]]) is not considered an ancillary head per this tag, however a replacement of a limb with multiple heads can be considered applicable to this tag (i.e. [[sylene_(blissey1)]]).\r\n\r\nAn ancillary head must be a full head, not just a mouth/maw. For this reason, [[snake_hair]] does not imply ancillary_head as some examples of snake hair only have mouths, although most posts tagged with snake_hair do fit the ancillary_head tag."
