          "tag": "destruction",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 8473,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3356322 thumb #3391056 thumb #3419171 thumb #3594330 thumb #2272497 thumb #3155450\r\n\r\n[b]A character causing destruction.[/b]\r\n\r\nMore specifically, a character actively, or having [i]just[/i] caused, notable damage to something inanimate — possibly entirely destroying the target of their destruction. This tag should not be used for [i]\"scenes of destruction\"[/i] that lack a character or force that clearly and directly caused the devastation around them.\r\n\r\nh5. What Counts As Destruction?\r\n\r\nThis tag is most often used for [[macro]] content, where the giant character is shown damaging buildings, biting, smashing or crushing vehicles, causing destruction of nature or natural features, levelling entire cities in their rampage or even destroying entire planets. It can also be seen in [[body size transformation]] and [[expansion]] content where the character's growth, or growth of a specific body part, causes or has caused damage to furniture, fixtures, or the room they are presently in. \r\n\r\nHowever, this is a broad tag and doesn't require a character to grow, expand or be giant to cause damage. Destruction can apply to a character actively using their body to destroy something (punching, kicking, jumping onto, butt slamming, ramming etc.) or passively (their weight/size causing them to crush or damage a seat, surface, or vehicle by sitting on it or leaning on it). It can apply to characters directly using weapons, magic, or supernatural powers to destroy objects (e.g. a character with laser vision cutting a car in half, a character using [[fire manipulation]] to burn a building, a character using a missile launcher to blow up a structure), \r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n\r\nh6. Subcategories of destruction\r\n* [[vehicle destruction]]\r\n* [[building destruction]]\r\n* [[planet destruction]]\r\n\r\nh6. Object, furniture, and interior/minor building damage\r\n* [[crushed object]]\r\n* [[broken bed]]\r\n* [[broken door]]\r\n* [[broken window]]\r\n* [[damaged ceiling]]\r\n* [[damaged floor]]\r\n* [[damaged wall]]\r\n\r\nh6. General tags for damage to an object or surface\r\n* [[cracks]]\r\n* [[crater]]\r\n\r\nh6. Aftermath of destruction\r\n* [[crushed vehicle]]\r\n* [[damaged building]]\r\n* [[damaged vehicle]]\r\n* [[destroyed building]]\r\n* [[burning building]]\r\n* [[ruins]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[butt slam]]\r\n* [[crush]]\r\n** [[butt crush]]\r\n** [[foot crush]]\r\n* [[stomping]]\r\n* [[trampling]]\r\n\r\n"
        },
        {
          "tag": "building_destruction",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1237,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #589521 thumb #3061924 thumb #1601783\r\n\r\n[b]Building destruction[/b] describes a [[building]] [i][b]actively[/b][/i] being damaged or destroyed. For a building that has already been damaged, use [[damaged building]] (if it is mostly still standing) or [[ruins]] (if most of the building has been destroyed).\r\n\r\nThis tag is by far most commonly used for [[macro]] characters smashing into, stepping on, punching, sitting on, or otherwise using their body to damage buildings around them. It can also apply to a character destroying a building through [[body size growth]], or through [[expansion]] of specific body parts. This tag can also apply to characters using heavy weapons, magic or superpowers to destroy a building.\r\n\r\nNote: Damage that is entirely localized to internal structures should use more specific tags instead such as [[damaged wall]], [[damaged ceiling]], or [[damaged floor]].\r\n\r\n[quote]\r\n\r\nh5. \"Building Destruction\" vs \"Damaged Building\"\r\n\r\nWhile easily confused, these two tags are intended to describe related but distinct concepts:\r\n\r\nh6. Building Destruction\r\nA character or force actively causing a building to be notably damaged, especially in a way that compromises the building's structural integrity, or completely destroys it\r\n\r\nh6. [[Damaged Building]] \r\nA building that has sustained any amount of damage. This tag can be more specifically used for posts where the act that caused the damage is not seen, or the aftermath of building destruction is shown after the act — e.g. a house in the background of a scene, with a large hole in the roof; a comic where a character breaks through the roof, followed by an exterior shot of the building with a hole in its roof.\r\n\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags\r\n\r\n* [[burning building]]\r\n* [[city destruction]] — widespread destruction in an urban environment, an entire city destroyed\r\n* [[ruins]] — a building or set of buildings that may have been destroyed, or simply fallen into disrepair, and have since been left abandoned\r\n\r\nh6. Macro Related Tags\r\n* [[building sex]] — giant characters using buildings as sex toys, usually causing building destruction\r\n** [[building insertion]]\r\n** [[building penetrated]]\r\n* [[holding building]]\r\n* [[sitting on building]]\r\n* [[rampage]]\r\n* [[crush]]\r\n\r\nh6. Cosmetic/Internal Damage\r\n* [[cracks]]\r\n* [[broken window]]\r\n* [[damaged wall]]\r\n* [[damaged ceiling]]\r\n* [[damaged floor]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[destruction]]\r\n** [[city destruction]]\r\n** [[planet destruction]]\r\n** [[vehicle destruction]]"
        },
