        {
          "tag": "fly_agaric",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 106,
          "wiki_body": "[i]Amanita muscaria[/i], commonly known as the [b]fly agaric[/b] or [b]fly amanita[/b], from the [i][[Amanitaceae]][/i] family and genus [i][[Amanita]][/i], is a species of [[mushroom]].\r\n\r\nIt is arguably one of the most iconic toadstool species, being hugely recognizable and often portrayed in popular culture such as in media focused around forested areas. The mushroom is large with white gills and [[white spots]], and the main fruited body is mostly red.\r\n\r\nDue to its common usage in popular media and folklore, it is often associated with [[gnome|gnomes]] or gnome-like beings such as [[smurf|smurfs]] as well as [[fairy|fairies]]. Fly agarics have also been portrayed in video games, inspiring the [[super mushroom]] from the [[mario bros|Mario Brothers series]].\r\n\r\nh4. External links\r\n\r\n* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amanita_muscaria\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[fungus]]\r\n** [[mushroom]]\r\n*** [[amanitaceae]]\r\n**** [[amanita]]\r\n***** [b]fly_agaric[/b]\r\n* [[mario_bros]]\r\n** [[super_mushroom]]"
