          "tag": "tally_marks",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 6614,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Tally marks[/b] are marks used to keep track of a value, such as points in a game or occurrences of some event. Every mark represents '1' and they are drawn in groups of 5.\n\nIn many Western countries, counting to 5 in tally marks looks like this: 𝍩 𝍪 𝍫 𝍬 卌 (or, the mark for 5 \"looks like this\":http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tally_marks-Five-bar_Gate.svg)\nIn some Asian countries, counting to 5 in tally marks looks like this: 𝍲 𝍳 𝍴 𝍵 𝍶 (or, the mark for 5 looks like this: 正 )\n\nTally marks are common in [[public_use]] pictures as [[body_writing]] or [[graffiti]] to (presumably) imply how many times other characters have ejaculated in/on them.\n\nAny use of \"tally_marks\" should also be tagged with one of these three:\n* [[western_tally_marks]] — for Western-style marks\n* [[cjk_tally_marks]] — for Asian-style marks\n** (note: [[japanese_tally_marks]], [[chinese_tally_marks]], and [[korean_tally_marks]] are all aliased to [[cjk_tally_marks]])\n* [[unusual_tally_marks]] — for any tally system that differs from the 2 above (including [[unary_tally_marks]] which are un-grouped, ...or versions of tally marks with groupings other than groups of 5).\n\n\nh4. Related tags\n\n* [[bodypaint]]\n* [[body_writing]]\n* [[graffiti]]\n* [[public_use]]\n* [[pregnancy_tally]]\n\nh4. See also\n\n* [[count]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "western_tally_marks",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 5268,
          "wiki_body": "A set of symbols used in many Western countries to count to five: 𝍩𝍪𝍫𝍬𝍸 (or, the mark for 5 looks like \"this\":http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tally_marks-Five-bar_Gate.svg)\r\nWhen they're not in groups of five (or are in some other grouping system), tag with [[unusual_tally_marks]] as well.\r\n\r\nFor the tally marks used in some Asian countries, where the mark for 5 looks like 正 , see [[cjk_tally_marks]].\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n* [[cjk_tally_marks]]\r\n* [[unusual_tally_marks]]\r\n* [[tally_marks]]"
        },
