          "wiki_body": "thumb #3183887\r\n\r\nA [b]Rosary[/b] or Rosary beads refer to a type of [[prayer beads]] used by Catholics to count prayers during the reciting of the Rosary (which gives its name to the beads used). Rosaries are often shown worn as [[necklace|necklaces]] or [[bracelet|bracelets]], and usually feature a [[Cross]] pendant, they may alternatively, or also include a small medallion with images of saints or of the Virgin Mary. Rosary beads are frequently shown worn by [[nun|nuns]], when a character is reciting the Rosary, they may be shown with [[hands_together|praying hands]], and the beads clasped in their hands. \r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n* [[cross necklace]]\r\n* [[religious symbols]]\r\n* [[Christianity]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also: \r\n* [[praying]] \r\n* [[prayer beads]]\r\n* [[bead necklace]]\r\n* [[pearl necklace]]"
