          "tag": "drone",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 4789,
          "wiki_body": "[b][u]Definition 1[/u][/b]\r\nthumb #2211088 thumb #1822172 thumb #1494165 thumb #1443074\r\n\r\nA specific form of [[hypnosis]] that reprograms the subject's brain to have little or no thoughts, emotions, personality, or bodily function other than to be obedient and/or turn other people into servants with mechanical efficiency. Likely involves an inescapable [[rubber suit]], [[goo transformation|coat of goo]], [[hypnotic visor|mind control devices]], [[symbiote|symbiotic entities]], [[robotization]], etc. \r\n\r\nIt is likely that the concept of the Drones in this capacity originates from the Television Series [i][[Star Trek: The Next Generation]][/i]. The Season 2 Episode \"Q Who\" who introduced a hostile alien race known as The [[Borg]]. The Borg operated in somewhat Eusocial Hierarchy, with a Borg Queen and much of the collective populations being referred to as Drones. The Borg's Goal was to obtain perfection by assimilating all other life forms (their knowledge, and technology, civilization, and physical capabilities) into their own collective. They did so by infecting non assimilated species with a subjecting them to lengthy surgical procedures or infecting them with nanoprobes to cybernetically augment the individual and take away their freewill from the collective.\r\n\r\n\r\n[b][u]Definition 2[/u][/b]\r\nthumb #2057543\r\nA drone may also refers to an [i]unmanned aerial vehicle[/i] (UAV) that is controlled remotely with no pilot inside of it. For this definition, use [[drone_(vehicle)]] instead.\r\n\r\n[b][u]Definition 3[/u][/b]\r\nthumb #3161745\r\nA drone may also refer to a type of small hovering/flying robot that follows orders rather than directly controlled. For this definition, use [[robot]] instead.\r\n\r\n[b][u]Definition 4[/u][/b]\r\nA drone may also refer to a specific class from a colonial [[species]]. Also referred to as a [i]\"worker drone\"[/i]. They do all the manual labor in a colony as opposed to the warriors (who fights) and the queen (who breeds).\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[goo_transformation]]\r\n* [[hypnosis]]\r\n* [[lock_symbol]]\r\n* [[null_bulge]]\r\n* [[rubber_suit]]\r\n* [[drone_(vehicle)]]\r\n* [[robot]]"
