          "tag": "sculpture",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 4543,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Sculpture[/b] is a 3 dimensional art form primarily based on solid form. Normally the process of sculpture involves carving away at a large, solid substance like stone, or wood, or molding a malleable substance to form an image of some sort. The sizes can range from massive statues, to small forms that easily fit in one's hand. \r\n\r\nFor purposes of tagging, this includes molding with clay, carving stone, wood, welding (as in, welding objects to make art, not welding metal together to make a machine).\r\n\r\nIf there is an [[artist]] in the image, be sure to tag [[artist]], as well as [[creating_art]] if applicable.\r\n\r\n* For actual sculptures in [[real]] photography, use [[sculpture_(artwork)]].\r\n\r\nh4. Categories\r\n\r\n* [[ice_sculpture]]\r\n* [[sand_sculpture]]\r\n* [[snow_sculpture]]\r\n* [[statue]]\r\n\r\nh4. General guidelines\r\n\r\n* Non-living sculptures do not count towards the character count, but [[animate inanimate]] examples do.\r\n* For both living, and non-living examples a species sculpture tag should be used. For instance, if it is a statue featuring a [[fox]], tag [[fox sculpture]]. The fox tag would only be reserved for animate inanimate examples.\r\n* Regardless of living status, copyrighted species (think [[pokemon_(species)|Pokémon]]) always get their fictional species tag, as well as a sculpture tag.\r\n* Only non-living sculptures in the shape of creatures (no matter how primitive) shall get the [[inanimate_object]] tag.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[miniature_model]]\r\n** [[figurine]]\r\n* [[petrification]]\r\n* [[statue]]\r\n\r\n-----This page is part of [[Tag Group:Art]]-----"
