          "tag": "guts",
          "kor": "내장",
          "count": 3236,
          "wiki_body": "While gut can be used to refer to the stomach or belly, it's more commonly used to describe the internal [[organs]] of a character or creature.\r\n\r\nMost frequently, 'guts' refers to the digestive tract--stomach and intestines, though other internal organs may be featured as well.  Generally speaking, the guts are what is normally hidden inside of a person.\r\n\r\nOften, when guts are featured, there is [[gore]] and [[blood]].\r\n\r\nNot to be confused with [[guts_(berserk)|Guts]], the protagonist of the incredibly violent manga [i]Berserk[/i], or the children's action competition TV series [i][[Nickelodeon GUTS]][/i].\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[blood]]\r\n* [[exposed_bone]]\r\n* [[exposed_muscle]]\r\n* [[gore]]\r\n* [[wounded]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[disembowelment]]\r\n* [[organs]]"
