        {
          "tag": "medium_truck",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 892,
          "wiki_body": "Vehicles such as box trucks, buses, small semi trucks, maintenance vehicles, delivery vans, and tow trucks, among others. In the United States, they are classified as trucks that can carry between 8,501 to 26,000 pounds (3,856 to 11,793 kilograms) worth of cargo on themselves (not counting how much they can tow).\r\n\r\nh4. Related:\r\n\r\n* [[box_truck]]\r\n* [[bus]]\r\n** [[school_bus]]\r\n* [[semi-trailer_truck]]\r\n* [[delivery_van]]\r\n** [[multi-stop_van]]\r\n* [[tow_truck]]\r\n* [[ambulance]]\r\n* [[food_truck]]"
        },
        {
