        {
          "tag": "small_head",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 2449,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #4028097 thumb #2615801 thumb #2832276 thumb #2978932\r\n\r\nWhen a character has a head that is noticeably disproportionately small in comparison to the rest of their body. \r\n\r\n* Normally proportioned adult characters usually have heads that are 1/7th or 1/8th of their total height\r\n** ...that means 7-8 of the character's heads \"lined up on top of each other\" would equal the character's full height \r\n* For a character to fall under `small_head`, their head should be smaller than 1/10th of their height.\r\n** ...for an example edge case, this image just barely does not quality because she is just under 10 heads tall: post #2932344\r\n\r\n\r\nWhile \"small head\" may imply a comment on art quality, or be seen as comical, this is almost always done as an intentional choice by the artist, and usually doesn't appear unnatural to most viewers. Characters are often drawn with smaller than usual heads to emphasize their height and/or size, to give the impression that the character is very tall; small heads are also frequently seen with characters who have [[hyper muscles]] or have exaggeratedly [[curvy figure|curvy figures]] to underline their extreme proportions.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n* [[big head]] (antonym)\r\n* [[huge head]] (extreme antonym)\r\n* [[tiny head]] (extreme)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "tiny_head",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 233,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #184431 thumb #3429302 thumb #2869574 thumb #4679998 thumb #1527305\r\nThe extreme version of [[small head]]. Posts tagged tiny head should also be tagged [[small head]].\r\nCharacters with heads that are disproportionately tiny compared to their body.\r\nFor fully grown adults, the head is usually 1/7th or 1/8th of their total height. This tag is for heads vastly smaller than this, under 1/20th of the height.\r\n\r\nThis is frequently, but not always, indicative of a character being extremely tall. This is the inverse of very short characters having a [[big head]] to emphasize their shortness.\r\n\r\nh4. See also:\r\n\r\n* [[Big Head]] (moderate antonym)\r\n* [[Huge Head]] (antonym)\r\n* [[Small Head]] (moderate)\r\n* [[Very Tiny Head]] (extreme)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "delivery_(commerce)",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 2392,
          "wiki_body": "[i]For other uses, see [[delivery_(disambiguation)]].[/i]\r\n\r\nIn commerce, [b]delivery[/b] is the transportation of goods from one location to another. Deliveries can take place between a business and a consumer, such as with retail purchases or fast food, between businesses or organizations, or internally within an organization.\r\n\r\nIn theory, any form of transportation or propulsion can be used to make a delivery, including motorized vehicles such as [[car|cars]] or [[aircraft]], animals such as [[horse|horses]], or even \"catapults\":https://web.archive.org/web/20110130043830/http://www.popsci.com/diy/article/2011-01/mexican-authorities-seize-homemade-marijuana-hurling-catapult-border. Cartoons often feature unusual delivery methods.\r\n\r\nSituations involving deliverypersons are common in pornography, as it can invoke multiple kinks such as [[casual sex]], [[exhibitionism]]/[[voyeur|voyeurism]], and [[infidelity]], among others. The premise has become so widespread and well-known that it is often ridiculed in popular culture."
