          "tag": "chart",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 2281,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #422913 thumb #4490983 thumb #4478653 thumb #2895433\r\n\r\nAlso known as a \"graph\", a [b]chart[/b] is a graphical representation for data visualization, a way to compile, compare and present data in a readable and easily understandable way. \r\n\r\n\r\nThis tag includes both charts that exist within a scene, such as an eye chart being used by a doctor to test a character's sight, as well as posts that are charts themselves. \r\nThe latter is more common on this site, with charts often comparing features of different characters or species.\r\n\r\nh3. Related Tags\r\n\r\nh5. Types of Chart\r\nForms of chart, sometimes describing a physical chart within a scene\r\n\r\n* [[flow chart]]\r\n* [[pie chart]]\r\n* [[height chart]]\r\n* [[eye chart]]\r\n\r\nh5. Charts by Content\r\nTags that describe what data the chart is presenting\r\n\r\n* [[age chart]]\r\n* [[alignment chart]]\r\n* [[bust chart]]\r\n* [[evolution chart]]\r\n* [[penis chart]]\r\n* [[size chart]]\r\n* [[waifu chart|waifu chart meme]]\r\n\r\nh5. [[Comparison|Comparisons]]\r\n\r\n* [[comparing_breasts]]\r\n* [[comparing_butts]]\r\n* [[comparing_muscles]]\r\n* [[comparing_penis]]\r\n* [[version_comparison]]\r\n\r\nh4. See Also\r\n\r\n* [[diagram]]\r\n* [[expression_sheet]]\r\n* [[model_sheet]]"
