          "tag": "heat_(temperature)",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 2046,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #3142700 thumb #161394 thumb #3363230 thumb #3300014\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe tag describes characters experiencing and reacting to hot conditions, which can be defined as temperatures well above \"[i]room temperature[/i]\" (20 Celsius/70 Fahrenheit), however, the character may be hot themselves from warm clothing or being in a hot room, rather than reacting to ambient temperatures. This tag can also apply to scenes that convey a sense of heat through visual elements. \r\n\r\nDepictions of a character experiencing heat almost always involve the character [[sweat|sweating]]. frequently [[blush|flushed]], looking tired, and/or unhappy with the heat; they may also verbally express their discomfort. Characters may be shown unbuttoning, unzipping, or pulling at their clothing to allow air to cool their body, fanning themselves, holding a cold object to their head or body, or standing in front of a fan or air conditioner.  Characters experiencing heat may be shown in varying states of undress. \r\n\r\nA \"hot scene\" may be hazy, feature clouds of [[steam]], and the pallet may use bright, warm colours to convey the sense of heat to the viewer.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote]\r\n[b]Note:[/b] This tag is not to be confused with a character being [[in heat]], although a character may be experiencing both at the same time\r\n[/quote]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n* [b]Reactions to Heat:[/b]\r\n** [[sweat|sweating]]\r\n*** [[sweat stain]]\r\n** [[fanning]]\r\n*** [[fanning self]]\r\n** [[panting]]\r\n* [b]Clothing Related:[/b]\r\n** [[topwear pull]]\r\n** [[shirt lift]]\r\n** [[open shirt]]\r\n** [[topless]]\r\n** [[bottomless]] \r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n* [[cold]]\r\n* [[overheated]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "animal_noises",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 2029,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Animal noises[/b] is an umbrella tag for any vocalization attributed to an animal species such as [i]purr[/i], [i]woof[/i], [i]oink[/i], [i]neigh[/i], and [i]squeak[/i] in certain circumstances, to name a few. Many of these sounds have their own tags that should be used along with this tag.\r\n\r\nThis tag can be used for [[sound|audio]], and textual sources ([[sound effects]]). Animal noises are sometimes used as a form of [[ambient_noises|ambient sound]] in animations.\r\n\r\nh4. Animal noise tags\r\n\r\nKeep in mind that some of these tags may not be purely used for the sound if the sound itself is associated with a well recognized posture mannerism. The [[howl]] tag may not always contain a howling sound for example. Most textual examples will count as [[onomatopoeia]], but some may have exceptions. [[Purring]] may be either an approximated sound, or an onomatopoeia.\r\n\r\n* Bird noises\r\n** [[cawing]]\r\n** [[chirping]]\r\n** [[peep_(sound_effect)]]\r\n** [[quacking]]\r\n** [[squawking]]\r\n* [[bleating]]\r\n* Cat noises\r\n** [[meow]] - Nya, and mewing are probably included\r\n** [[nya]]\r\n** [[purring]]\r\n* Dog noises\r\n** [[arf]]\r\n** [[barking]]\r\n** [[woof_(sound_effect)]]\r\n* [[croaking]]\r\n* [[hissing]] - Conditionally an animal sound.\r\n* [[howl]], [[awoo]]\r\n* [[mooing]]\r\n* [[neigh]]\r\n* [[oink]] / [[oinking]]\r\n* [[squeaking]] - Conditionally an animal sound\r\n* [[whinny]]\r\n\r\nh4. Animal cry tags\r\n\r\nAn animal cry is not specific to any one animal, but are generic sounds that animals are known to make.\r\n\r\n* [[growling]]\r\n* [[roaring]]\r\n* [[snarling]]\r\n* [[whimper]]\r\n* [[whining]]\r\n* [[yipping]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[tag_group:sound_effects]]\r\n\r\n* [[sound_effects]]"
