          "wiki_body": "thumb #5634525 thumb #3456970 thumb #1687690 thumb #1846196 thumb #2505482 thumb #3530004\n\nImages with a focus on sexual orientation, particularly a mismatch of one's identity with the activity going on in the image. Often involves play surrounding denial, homophobia, bicuriosity, conversion or other topics.\n\nThis tag is often misused as a way to tag pictures that conflict with canon sexualities, which goes against TWYS.\n\n[section,expanded=Tagging guidelines]\nh5. Things that count as orientation play:\n* A character proclaiming they aren't gay while engaging in sexual activity with the same sex. ([[no homo]])\n* A character discovering that they're sexually attracted to a gender they believed they weren't originally.\n* A character attempting to seduce someone who says they're straight/gay, or succeeding.\n* Trying to \"convert\" a character's sexuality.\n* Experimenting and exploring sexually with a different gender.\n* A character engaging in sexual activity with a gender they aren't usually attracted to, provided there is visual evidence to the orientation, such as a visible pride flag.\n* Mistaken gender in regards to attraction.\n\nh5. Things that DON'T count as orientation play:\n* Images with no reference to sexual orientation, regardless of the character's canon sexuality. For example, a lesbian with a man, with no reference in the image to the character being a lesbian.\n* Bisexual encounters with no reference to orientation.\n* Posts with a story in the description related to orientation play.\n[/section]\n\nh4. Related tags\n* [[accidentally_gay]]\n* [[accidentally_straight]]\n* [[bicurious]]\n* [[no_homo]]\n* [[questioning_sexuality]]\n* [[sexuality_change]]\n** [[straight_to_gay]]\n** [[gay_to_straight]]\n*** [[lesbian_correction]]\n* [[stated_sexuality]]\n** [[stated_asexuality]]\n** [[stated_bisexuality]]\n** [[stated_heterosexuality]]\n** [[stated_homosexuality]]\n\nh4. See also\n* [[bisexual]]\n* [[gender_confusion]]\n* [[homophobia]]\n* [[mind_control]]\n* [[misgendering]]\n* [[mistaken_identity]]"
