        {
          "tag": "pentacle",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1533,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #390153 thumb #748624 thumb #499431\r\n\r\nA [b]pentacle[/b] originally described a [[pentagram]] surrounded by a circular outline. The definition has evolved to refer to any type of insignia surrounded by a circular outline. It may not always be a pentagram, but this tag will be mostly of the pentagram variety.\r\n\r\n[section=Extra information]\r\nThe pentacle is an ancient symbol of a five pointed star ([[pentagram]]) within a circle. In Chinese and Japanese religions the points represent the four elements (fire, water, earth, and air) and ether (spirit) and the circle represents eternity. In Christianity, the five points represent the five wounds of Jesus, and the symbol was used as the city seal of Jerusalem. Inverted pentacle has been used by satanists and neo-pagans to represent materialism, the opposite of spiritualism.\r\n\r\nNowadays, it is commonly associated with occultism and satanism.\r\n\r\n[/section]\r\n\r\nh4. Types\r\n\r\n* [[heart_pentacle]]\r\n* [[inverted_pentacle]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[heartagram]]\r\n* [[pentagram]]\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[demon]]\r\n* [[magic_circle]]\r\n* [[star]]\r\n** [[pentagram]]\r\n* [[symbol]]\r\n"
        },
        {
          "tag": "inverted_pentacle",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 556,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #182659\r\n\r\nUpside-down [[pentacle]]. Used in various types of witchcraft and hermetic magic, but most commonly associated with Satanism, where it is meant to represents the head of a goat: the two upward-facing points resemble horns, sideway-facing points ears, and the downward-facing point a muzzle.\r\n\r\nIf the symbol is painted on floor (see [[magic circle]]), it is usually impossible to tell which way it is facing. Default to [[pentacle]] in such cases.\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags:\r\n\r\n* [[heartagram]]\r\n* [[sigil_of_baphomet]] - official seal of the Church of Satan"
        },
        {
          "tag": "swim_ring",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1524,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #900360\r\n\r\nA [b]swim ring[/b] (also known as a [b]swim tube[/b], [b]rubber ring[/b], [b]water donut[/b]) is a ring-shaped inflatable [[pool toy]]. Some have animal features which should be tagged as [[animal swim ring]].\r\n\r\nh4. Categories\r\n\r\n* [[life_ring]] - A type of swim ring designed to save individuals from drowning.\r\n\r\nh4. Tagging notes\r\n\r\n- A swim ring is a type of [[inner tube]] designed for use in the water.\r\n- Swim rings are typically a type of [[pool toy]]. In most cases, it is okay to tag them as a pool toy.\r\n\r\nh4. External links\r\n\r\n* \"Wikipedia - Swim ring\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swim_ring"
        },
        {
          "tag": "life_ring",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 169,
          "wiki_body": "A [b]life ring[/b] is a donut-shaped [[flotation device]] used in water rescue to save a character from [[drowning]]. These are usually smaller than a [[swim ring]], and can be identified by their white on red color pattern.\r\n\r\nthumb #1824372 thumb #41844 thumb #919603\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\n* [[lifeguard]]\r\n* [[water]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "dice",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1514,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #172334\r\n\r\n[b]Dice[/b] (singular form: [b]die[/b]) are small throwable objects with multiple resting positions, used for generating random numbers. Dice are used in gambling games, tabletop games, [[board game|board games]], certain [[card game|card games]], and others.\r\n\r\nDice can be any shape (usually a regular polyhedron) and have any number of sides, but the most common is a [[cube]] (sometimes called a D6).\r\n\r\nh5. Specific dice shape tags:\r\n* [[d4]]\r\n* [[d6]]\r\n* [[d8]]\r\n* [[d10]]\r\n* [[d12]]\r\n* [[d20]]"
        },
