        {
          "tag": "noodles",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1410,
          "wiki_body": "A strip, ring, or tube of pasta or a similar dough, typically made with egg and usually eaten with a sauce or in a soup.\r\n\r\nh4. See Also:\r\n*  [[food]]\r\n*  [[ramen]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "ramen",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 733,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #2577718 thumb #4916650 thumb #3689130 thumb #4727215 thumb #5098090\r\n\r\n[b]Ramen[/b] (拉麺, ラーメン or らあめん, rāmen) is a [[Japan|Japanese]] noodle dish, typically served in a broth with meat and vegetables. It is usually served as either restaurant cuisines or instant noodle cups. It also has roots in [[China|Chinese]] noodle dishes.\r\n\r\nIn [[Korea]], ramen is known as its original name (라멘), in addition to a variation of the dish, ramyeon (라면). In China, ramen is called rìshì lāmiàn (日式拉麵 \"Japanese-style lamian\"). Ramen, both its traditional and instant counterparts, also has a huge market in Western restuaraunts and stores, respectively.\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[eating]]\r\n* [[food]]\r\n* [[noodles]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "stated_age",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1313,
          "wiki_body": "When a character's age is specifically given through [[dialogue]], written on something within the scene (e.g. an identification card), or by other text in the post, which commonly seen in [[model sheet|model sheets]].\n\nIn some cases, the character's stated age may conflict with their appearance, if the character appears adult but is given an age younger than 18, tag [[young (lore)]]. If a character that appears underage is given an adult age, use [[adult (lore)]], the [[young]] tag should also be added.\n\nh4. Related tags:\n* [[stated adult]]\n* [[stated young]]\n\nh4. See also\n* [[stated incest]]\n* [[stated pedophilia]]\n* [[stated sexuality]]\n* [[stated virginity]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "stated_young",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 481,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #4212127 thumb #5045417\n\nA character whose age is directly or indirectly stated to be [[young]] through dialogue or other text, symbols or numbers.\n\nThis is regardless of the whether the character appears young or not. Dialogue can reveal that a character is not an adult and younger than they appear, or contrast the young character's age with the older age of another character, the viewer, etc.\n\nNot to be confused with the [[young_(lore)]] tag, in which the artist describes a character as young when they do not physically appear to look young.\n\nh4. Related Tags:\n* [[stated age]]\n** [[stated adult]]\n\nh4. See Also\n* [[stated sexuality]]\n* [[stated virginity]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "stated_adult",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 452,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #4694233 thumb #4444665\n\nWhen a character is specifically stated through [[dialogue]], written on something within the scene (e.g. an identification card), or by other text in the post (commonly seen in [[model sheet|model sheets]]) to be an adult.\n\nIn some cases, this may conflict if they have a [[young]] appearance. If a character that appears underage is given an adult age, use [[adult (lore)]] per [[Tag What You See]]. The [[young]] tag should also be added if appropriate.\n\nh4. Related Tags:\n* [[stated age]]\n** [[stated young]]\n\nh4. See Also\n* [[stated sexuality]]\n* [[stated virginity]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "roller_skates",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 1251,
          "wiki_body": "[b]Roller skates[/b] are any shoes, boots, or other footwear that enable the wearer to roll on wheels. \r\n\r\nh4. Types of roller skates\r\n\r\nh5. [[quad skates]]\r\nthumb #1095839 \r\n— wheels arranged in a 2 by 2 layout \r\n\r\nh5. [[inline skates]] \r\nthumb #52340 \r\n— wheels arranged in a straight line\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[carhop]]\r\n* [[motorized skates]]\r\n* [[roller rink]]\r\n* [[skating]]\r\n\r\nh4. External\r\n\r\n* \"Wikipedia - Roller skates\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roller_skates"
        },
        {
          "tag": "quad_skates",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 672,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #145903 thumb #2025115 thumb #379234\r\n\r\n[b]Quad skates[/b] are a type of [[roller skates]] with wheels arranged in a 2 by 2 layout, similar to the wheels of a typical car. For stopping, quad skates commonly feature a toe brake, though rear brakes also exist. Brakes may also be omitted entirely, and toe stop brakes may be replaced with shorter [[jam plugs]] for dance forms of [[skating]].\r\n\r\nNot to be confused with [[inline skates]] — which instead have wheels arranged in a straight line.\r\n\r\nh5. Types of quad skates\r\n* [[high-top quad skates]]\r\n* [[low-top quad skates]]\r\n\r\nh5. See also\r\n\r\n* [[carhop]]\r\n* [[roller skates]]\r\n* [[skating]]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "inline_skates",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 566,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #267 thumb #1562294 thumb #511997 thumb #2104802\r\n\r\n[b]Inline skates[/b] are a type of [[roller skates|roller skate]] with two to five wheels arranged in a single line. If a brake is present, it is positioned on the rear end of the skate.\r\n\r\nNot to be confused with [[quad skates]], which have wheels arranged in a 2 by 2 layout (and featuring toe stop brakes), inline skates always have their wheels in a single line.\r\n\r\nh5. Subtypes of inline skates\r\n* [[aggressive skates]]\r\n* [[big wheeled inline skates]]\r\n\r\nh5. See also\r\n\r\n* [[ice skates]]\r\n* [[skating]]\r\n\r\nh5. Trivia\r\n* While inline skates are sometimes referred to as \"rollerblades\", this is an incorrect naming as [[Rollerblade]] is a brand of skate.\r\n\r\nh5. External\r\n* \"Wikipedia - Inline skates\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inline_skates"
        },
