          "count": 1154,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #2720992 thumb #2909267 thumb #3201767\r\n\r\n[b]Trap[/b] can either describe:\r\n\r\n* A device designed to catch and retain a person or animal\r\n* A situation where a character is, or is about to become, captured, ambushed, bound, restrained or imprisoned by another character.\r\n\r\nThis can also be applied if the viewer is being lured into a trap by a character.\r\n\r\nh5. Types of traps\r\n* [[bear trap]]\r\n* [[booby trap]]\r\n* [[mouse trap]]\r\n* [[snare trap]]\r\n* [b][[net]][/b]\r\n** [[fishing net]]\r\n** [[trapped in net]]\r\n\r\n\r\nh4. Related Tags:\r\n* [[trapped]] - a character who has been caught in a trap\r\n* [[bound]] - being tied to prevent movement\r\n* [[restrained]] - being held by another to prevent movement \r\n* [[imminent danger]] - relevant if a character is about to fall into a trap\r\n* [[ambush]]\r\n* [[attack]]"
