        {
          "tag": "tarot",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 955,
          "wiki_body": "thumb #1561088\r\n\r\n[b]Tarot[/b] (rhymes with \"arrow\", [i]not[/i] \"carrot\") refers to activities done with [[tarot_card|tarot cards]].\r\n\r\nOriginally, tarot (also tarok, tarocchi, etc.) was nothing more than playing card games with tarot cards, just as today's standard poker deck is used.  Many countries, especially in Europe, still play card games with tarot cards.\r\n\r\nHowever, ever since 1781, when a Swiss clergyman named \"Antoine Court de Gébelin\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antoine_Court_de_Gebelin erroneously claimed tarot cards had their origins in ancient Egyptian mysticism, tarot conjures up images of [[fortune_telling|fortune telling]] and the occult in the English-speaking world.  On e621, this is the most likely way a viewer will encounter anything tarot-related.\r\n\r\nh4. More Information:\r\n* \"Tarot (Wikipedia)\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarot\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n* [[major_arcana]]\r\n* [[minor_arcana]]\r\n* [[tarot_card]]\r\n* [[tarot_(housepets!)]] - A character named Tarot."
        },
        {
          "tag": "major_arcana",
          "kor": "",
          "count": 663,
          "wiki_body": "The [b]major arcana[/b] are a set of 22 cards complementing the [[minor_arcana|minor arcana]] in the [[tarot_card|tarot card]] deck.  They are commonly used in either [[fortune_telling|fortune telling]] or playing card games depending on country.  On e621, viewers are far more likely to encounter the former than the latter.\r\n\r\nThe major arcana typically feature custom-made art, often rich with symbolism, and cards can have a different name depending on deck. The most common names (based on the Rider-Waite-Smith deck) are listed below. The major arcana of [[playing_card|playing card]] versions of the [[tarot]] deck are instead called [[trump_(tarot)|trumps]] and only name a few of the cards, such as [[the_fool_(tarot)|The Fool]] and [[the_world_(tarot)|The World]].\r\n\r\nh4. The Major Arcana\r\n* 0: [[the_fool_(tarot)|The Fool]]\r\n* I: [[the_magician_(tarot)|The Magician]]\r\n* II: [[the_high_priestess_(tarot)|The High Priestess]]\r\n* III: [[the_empress_(tarot)|The Empress]]\r\n* IV: [[the_emperor_(tarot)|The Emperor]]\r\n* V: [[the_hierophant_(tarot)|The Hierophant]]\r\n* VI: [[the_lovers_(tarot)|The Lovers]]\r\n* VII: [[the_chariot_(tarot)|The Chariot]]\r\n* VIII: [[strength_(tarot)|Strength]]\r\n* IX: [[the_hermit_(tarot)|The Hermit]]\r\n* X: [[wheel_of_fortune_(tarot)|Wheel of Fortune]]\r\n* XI: [[justice_(tarot)|Justice]]\r\n* XII: [[the_hanged_man_(tarot)|The Hanged Man]]\r\n* XIII: [[death_(tarot)|Death]]\r\n* XIV: [[temperance_(tarot)|Temperance]]\r\n* XV: [[the_devil_(tarot)|The Devil]]\r\n* XVI: [[the_tower_(tarot)|The Tower]]\r\n* XVII: [[the_star_(tarot)|The Star]]\r\n* XVIII: [[the_moon_(tarot)|The Moon]]\r\n* XIX: [[the_sun_(tarot)|The Sun]]\r\n* XX: [[judgement_(tarot)|Judgement]]\r\n* XXI: [[the_world_(tarot)|The World]]\r\n\r\nh4. More info:\r\n* \"Tarot (Wikipedia)\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarot\r\n* \"Tarot Card Games (Wikipedia)\":http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarot,_tarock_and_tarocchi_games\r\n* \"Image showing the Major Arcana (right here on e621)\":http://e621.net/post/show/21273"
